{'copyright': 'Copyright (c) 2020 The New York Times Company. All Rights Reserved.', 'response': {'docs': [{'abstract': 'In “Phantom,” a Soviet submarine captain dispatched on a final cold war mission confronts a handful of K.G.B. radicals intent on deploying the sub’s nuclear missile.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/01/movies/phantom-a-thriller-directed-by-todd-robinson.html', 'snippet': 'In “Phantom,” a Soviet submarine captain dispatched on a final cold war mission confronts a handful of K.G.B. radicals intent on deploying the sub’s nuclear missile.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Claiming that Todd Robinson’s cold war howler “Phantom” was inspired by actual events is like locating the source of the Superman mythology in the red underwear of one of its creators. In this case the basis for the film’s confusing, cliché-stuffed plot is the mysterious sinking of a Soviet submarine in 1968 — an event around which Mr. Robinson spins a yarn of unpardonable monotony.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/01/arts/01RDP_PHANTOM_SPAN/01RDP_PHANTOM_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 348, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/01/arts/01RDP_PHANTOM_SPAN/01RDP_PHANTOM_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 348}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/01/arts/01RDP_PHANTOM_SPAN/01RDP_PHANTOM_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 594, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/01/arts/01RDP_PHANTOM_SPAN/01RDP_PHANTOM_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1188, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 's