amines hunger in America, where almost 50 million people rely on food stamps.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Stepping lightly and carrying a very small stick, “A Place at the Table” documents hunger in America with studied politeness. Revealing little that a moderately informed viewer will not already know, the film shies away from the outrage and bare-knuckle journalism that this shameful topic deserves.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/01/arts/01RDP_PLACE_SPAN/01RDP_PLACE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/01/arts/01RDP_PLACE_SPAN/01RDP_PLACE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/01/arts/01RDP_PLACE_SPAN/01RDP_PLACE_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 577, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/01/arts/01RDP_PLACE_SPAN/01RDP_PLACE_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1079, 'width': 1914, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/01/arts/01RDP_PLACE_SPAN/01RDP_PLACE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/01/arts/01RDP_PLACE_SPAN/01RDP_PLACE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/01/arts/01RDP_PLACE_SPAN/01RDP_PLACE_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': '