rtime protections for home care workers are not approved by the Obama administration.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/01/opinion/home-care-rules-in-the-home-stretch.html', 'snippet': 'It will be a great injustice if minimum-wage and overtime protections for home care workers are not approved by the Obama administration.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over a year ago, President Obama announced that new Labor Department rules would guarantee home care workers minimum-wage and overtime-pay protections. The move would undo a nearly 40-year-old rule that defines home care workers as “companions,” a label that exempts employers from having to pay them the minimum wage and time and a half for overtime. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Home Care Rules in the Home Stretch', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Home Care Rules in the Home Stretch', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Home Health Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minimum Wage', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Care', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-01T02:11:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1e86df2-c681-58ea-b5d4-9d7d3d7778cc', 'word_count': 316, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1e86df2-c681-58ea-b5d4-9d7d3d7778cc'}, {'abstract': 'Antibiotic overuse in Chinese pig farms poses a potential worldwide human health risk.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/01/opinion/breeding-bad-bugs.html', 'snippet': 'Antibiotic overuse in Chinese pig farms poses a potential worldwide human health risk.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Study after study has found that the practice of feeding subtherapeutic doses of antibiotics to livestock to enhance growth is a threat to public health because it can lead to the breeding of antibiotic-resistant organisms, rendering essential drugs useless against disease-carrying organisms. Now there is alarming new evidence that unchecked antibiotic use in Chinese livestock farming has led to antibiotic-resistant genes in bacteria. China produces and uses more antibiotics than any other country, and nearly half the antibiotics it uses are fed to livestock. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Breeding Bad Bugs', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Breeding Bad Bugs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTIBIOTICS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factory Farming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Livestock', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-01T02:15:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/295d44b6-432d-5409-be53-5c5875ae2dd2', 'word_count': 277, 'uri': 'nyt://article/295d44b6-432d-5409-be53-5c5875ae2dd2'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Reynolds, who at the time of the theft was known to the police as a burglar well-connected in the London underworld, referred to the heist in a 1996 interview as “my Sistine Chapel.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/01/world/europe/bruce-reynolds-leader-of-great-train-robbery-dies-at-81.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Reynolds, who at the time of the theft was known to the police as a burglar well-connected in the London underworld, referred to the heist in a 1996 interview as “my Sistine Chapel.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bruce Reynolds, the chief architect of one of 20th-century Britain’s most notorious crimes, the caper known as the Great Train Robbery, died on Thursday in England. He was 81. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/01/world/REYNOLDS3-obit/REYNOLDS3-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1260, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/01/world/REYNOLDS3-obit/REYNOLDS3-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1260}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/01/world/REYNOLDS3-obit/REYNOLDS3-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 488, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/01/world/REYNOLDS3-obit/REYNOLDS3-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 976, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/01/world/REYNOLDS3-obit/REYNOLDS3-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/01/world/REYNOLDS3-obit/REYNOLDS3-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/01/world