ne}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d21840d7-4f58-5a1b-941c-abfa89bec5c3', 'word_count': 938, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d21840d7-4f58-5a1b-941c-abfa89bec5c3'}, {'abstract': 'Speaker John A. Boehner seems to have decided that he may have more to lose by negotiating with the White House over spending cuts that begin Friday than by letting them happen.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/01/us/politics/house-republicans-cheer-boehners-refusal-to-negotiate-on-cuts.html', 'snippet': 'Speaker John A. Boehner seems to have decided that he may have more to lose by negotiating with the White House over spending cuts that begin Friday than by letting them happen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Speaker John A. Boehner, the man who spent significant portions of the last Congress shuttling to and from the White House for fiscal talks with President Obama that ultimately failed twice to produce a grand bargain, has come around to the idea that the best negotiations are no negotiations.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/01/us/JP-BOEHNER/JP-BOEHNER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 376, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/01/us/JP-BOEHNER/JP-BOEHNER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 376}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/01/us/JP-BOEHNER/JP-BOEHNER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 642, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/01/us/JP-BOEHNER/JP-BOEHNER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1285, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/01/us/JP-BOEHNER/JP-BOEHNER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/01/us/JP-BOEHNER/JP-BOEHNER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/01/us/JP-BOEHNER/JP-BOEHNER-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Boehner Halts Talks on Cuts, and House G.O.P. Cheers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Boehner’s Halt\r\nTo Fiscal Talks\r\nCheers G.O.P.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Aid (US)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-01T03:35:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d720ced-1aeb-51fb-8338-3e89594dd038', 'word_count': 1159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d720ced-1aeb-51fb-8338-3e89594dd038'}, {'abstract': 'A German television crew filming in a village near Beijing was assaulted by men in four vehicles who tried to run the crew’s minivan off the road, said one of the correspondents.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/01/world/asia/china-german-journalists-say-they-were-assaulted-for-filming.html', 'snippet': 'A German television crew filming in a village near Beijing was assaulted by men in four vehicles who tried to run the crew’s minivan off the road, said one of the correspondents.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A German television crew filming in a village near Beijing was assaulted on Wednesday by a group of men in four vehicles who tried to run the crew’s minivan off the road and then smashed its windshield with baseball bats, said one of the correspondents. No injuries were reported. One witness later told the journalists that at least one of the vehicles belonged to the local Communist Party chief. The German crew, working for the broadcaster ARD, said the episode took place in Sanhe, a city in Hebei Province, roughly 30 miles east of Beijing. The attackers rammed the minivan, forcing it to stop. Two men then smashed it with bats as two police officers stood by. After more officers arrived they led the journalists to a police station. The five journalists were questioned for 16 hours, said Christine Adelhardt, an ARD correspondent. A police officer later suggested that the attackers had been “offended” because the crew had filmed without permission. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China: German Journalists Say They Were Assaulted for Filming', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China: German Journalists Say They Were Assaulted for Filming', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assaults', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-01T03:38:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Jacobs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jacobs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/61ecd7ce-0667-505c-928a-b20dabb2b3f6', 'word_count': 161, 'uri': 'nyt://article/61ecd7ce-0667-505c-928a-b20dabb2b3f6'}, {'abstract': 'With Rick Nash, Ryan McDonagh and Michael Del Zotto back from injuries, the Rangers completed a three-game, season-series sweep of the Lightning.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/01/sports/hockey/rangers-beat-lightning-to-end-losing-streak.html', 'snippet': 'With Rick Nash, Ryan McDonagh and Michael Del Zotto back from injuries, the Rangers completed a three-game, season-series sweep of the Lightning.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Everything lined up perfectly for the Rangers on Thursday at Madison Square Garden. Rick Nash, Ryan McDonagh and Michael Del Zotto returned from injuries, the Tampa Bay Lightning were the opponent, and the Rangers snapped their four-game losing streak with a 4-1 victory.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/01/sports/sub-rangers/sub-rangers-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 415, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/01/sports/sub-rangers/sub-rangers-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 415}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/01/sports/sub-rangers/sub-rangers-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 708, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/01/sports/sub-rangers/sub-rangers-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1416, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/01/sports/sub-rangers/sub-rangers-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/01/sports/sub-rangers/sub-rangers-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/01/sports/sub-rangers/sub-rangers-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Nash Looks Like Himself, and the Rangers Get Back on Track, Too', 'kicker': 'Rangers 4, Lightning 1', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nash Looks Like Himself, and the Rangers Get Back on Track, Too', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klein, Jeff Z', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Rangers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tampa Bay Lightning', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McDonagh, Ryan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nash, Rick', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Del Zotto, Michael', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-01T03:40:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f3c7599f-663b-5ab0-b001-48279c06afb1', 'word_count': 748, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f3c7599f-663b-5ab0-b001-48279c06afb1'}, {'abstract': 'Congress approved an accord with Iran to create a fact-finding commission of foreign legal experts to investigate the bombing of a Buenos Aires Jewish center in 1994.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/01/world/americas/argentina-congress-supports-deal-with-iran-to-investigate-1994-blast.html', 'snippet': 'Congress approved an accord with Iran to create a fact-finding commission of foreign legal experts to investigate the bombing of a Buenos Aires Jewish center in 1994.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Congress on Thursday approved an accord with Iran to create a fact-finding commission of foreign legal experts to investigate the bombing of a Buenos Aires Jewish center in 1994. The agreement was approved over the protests of Jewish leaders and some of the victims’ relatives. Nearly 19 years ago, a suicide bomber drove a van full of explosives into the headquarters of the Argentine-Israeli Mutual Association headquarters, killing 85 people and wounding about 300. An Argentine prosecutor has accused Hezbollah, the Lebanese group with ties to Iran and Syria, of carrying out the bombing and senior Iranian officials of planning and financing it. Iran has refused extradition requests for nine suspects. The agreement will allow Argentine prosecutors to interrogate suspects in Tehran. Iran’s Parliament is said to be examining the proposal. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Argentina: Congress Supports Deal With Iran to Investigate 1994 Blast', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Argentina: Congress Supports Deal With Iran to Investigate 1994 Blast', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Buenos Aires (Argentina)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hezbollah', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-01T03:46:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily Schmall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schmall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/0de8eb4e-71ac-5848-8b84-f4e0a6de2e5a', 'word_count': 131, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0de8eb4e-71ac-5848-8b84-f4e0a6de2e5a'}, {'abstract': 'New York City has yet to explain what led to the wrongful convictions of five teenagers in the Central Park jogger case.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/01/nyregion/awaiting-end-to-new-york-citys-silence-in-central-park-jogger-case.html', 'snippet': 'New York City has yet to explain what led to the wrongful convictions of five teenagers in the Central Park jogger case.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A senior lawyer for New York City complained last week that “The Central Park Five,” a documentary film on the Central Park jogger case, was a “one-sided” version of events.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After 24 Years, Awaiting End to the Silence', 'kicker': 'About New York', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After 24 Years, Awaiting End To the Silence', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dwyer, Jim', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Central Park Jogger Case (1989)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'False Arrests, Convictions and Imprisonments', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reyes, Matias', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Central Park (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Central Park Five (Movie)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-01T03:47:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Dwyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dwyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/94c610c6-e5ae-5147-818f-0269db42c2f8', 'word_count': 752, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94c610c6-e5ae-5147-818f-0269db42c2f8'}, {'abstract': 'A vacationing employee of the United States Department of State, Victoria Tcaciuc, 38, was found strangled in a Rio de Janeiro hotel, the police said Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/01/world/americas/brazil-us-state-department-employee-strangled-at-hotel.html', 'snippet': 'A vacationing employee of the United States Department of State, Victoria Tcaciuc, 38, was found strangled in a Rio de Janeiro hotel, the police said Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A vacationing employee of the United States Department of State was found strangled in a Rio de Janeiro hotel, the police said Thursday. The victim was identified as Victoria Tcaciuc, 38, and said she was killed Feb. 20, said Rivaldo Barbosa, chief of the Rio police homicide division. The police have arrested a suspect who is seen in security camera video entering the hotel in Rio’s Copacabana neighborhood, Mr. Barbosa said. The press office of the United States Consulate in Rio said Ms. Tcaciuc was a contract employee of the State Department. Citing privacy act considerations, the consulate did not provide her hometown or other information. The arrested man, identified as Alessandro Rufino Oliveira Carvalho, has acknowledged that he was with Ms. Tcaciuc in the room but denies killing her, Mr. Barbosa said. (AP)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Brazil: U.S. State Department Employee Strangled at Hotel', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Brazil: U.S. State Department Employee Strangled at Hotel', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-01T03:50:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/23a64b45-9ec6-5c9f-86d5-6f26f641f832', 'word_count': 134, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23a64b45-9ec6-5c9f-86d5-6f26f641f832'}, {'abstract': 'The United States government has petitioned the Irish High Court to extradite an Algerian man living in Ireland on terrorism charges relating to a plot to kill a Swedish artist.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/01/world/europe/ireland-suspect-in-terrorism-case-faces-extradition-to-us.html', 'snippet': 'The United States government has petitioned the Irish High Court to extradite an Algerian man living in Ireland on terrorism charges relating to a plot to kill a Swedish artist.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The United States government has petitioned the Irish High Court to extradite an Algerian man living in Ireland on terrorism charges relating to a plot to assassinate a Swedish artist, officials said Thursday. The United States alleges that the man, Ali Charaf Damache, planned to set up terrorist training camps and kill several Europeans, including a Swedish artist, Lars Vilks, whose sketch of the Prophet Muhammad’s head on a dog, published in 2007, had enraged the Islamic world. On Wednesday, Mr. Damache pleaded guilty in the Waterford Circuit Court to making a menacing phone call to an American peace activist, a charge for which he was arrested and detained in 2010. The judge sentenced him to time served and released him, but Mr. Damache was immediately rearrested on the American extradition warrant. Mr. Damache arrived in Ireland in 2000 and married an Irish woman in 2002. The relationship ended in 2008 and he then married an American citizen, Jamie Paulin Ramirez. Ms. Ramirez has pleaded guilty in the United States to charges of conspiring with Colleen LaRose, also known as Jihad Jane, to support and train terrorists. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ireland: Suspect in Terrorism Case Faces Extradition to U.S.', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ireland: Suspect in Terrorism Case Faces Extradition to U.S.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ireland', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Extradition', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Damache, Ali Charaf', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assassinations and Attempted Assassinations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vilks, Lars', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-01T03:53:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Douglas Dalby', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Douglas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dalby', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b649021-1b9b-5f44-9280-416cdb943e47', 'word_count': 187, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b649021-1b9b-5f44-9280-416cdb943e47'}, {'abstract': 'The State University of New York released a music video as part of its effort to attract applicants, but not everyone was a fan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/01/nyregion/suny-adds-a-hip-hop-anthem-to-its-marketing-set-list.html', 'snippet': 'The State University of New York released a music video as part of its effort to attract applicants, but not everyone was a fan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The video begins with some generic hip-hop imagery — beautiful fans, a D.J. with serious headphones — and moves quickly to a college setting, where a young man in a varsity jacket walks through a crowd of cheerleaders. Raising his eyes to meet the camera’s gaze, he delivers a message previously unheard in the annals of rap music: “Let ’em know you go to S-U-N-Y,” he says. “When you go to SUNY, you’re on the right road, so if you want to dream, then come and join the team.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/01/nyregion/suny/suny-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 334, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/01/nyregion/suny/suny-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 334}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/01/nyregion/suny/suny-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 570, 'width': 1