stitutional. Opponents, taking judicial care not to talk about future cases, would surely take the justice to task for his more unpopular decisions.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'State’s Justices Forced to Face Pull of Politics', 'kicker': 'The Texas Tribune', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'State’s Justices Forced to Face Pull of Politics', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-01T05:52:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Ramsey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ramsey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8fe3b3a-a020-5287-81ba-3574611e63de', 'word_count': 729, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8fe3b3a-a020-5287-81ba-3574611e63de'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/01/arts/television/whats-on-friday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '11:30 P.M. (MLB Network) 2013 WORLD BASEBALL CLASSIC National teams from Australia and Taiwan face off at the Taipei Intercontinental Baseball Stadium in Taichung, Taiwan, in the opening match of this tournament. Team USA, with a roster that includes Mark Teixeira of the Yankees and David Wright of the Mets, will play its first game against Mexico next Friday. Bob Costas, Tom Verducci and Matt Yallof are among the announcers. The network will also offer studio programming like “World Baseball Classic Today,” which has its premiere at 11 a.m. on Saturday, and “International Talk,” a live show during each game of the championship round, which ends on March 19.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Friday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-01T06:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/891a9d3c-d83a-552f-b037-55205265fbb1', 'word_count': 732, 'uri': 'nyt://article/891a9d3c-d83a-552f-b037-55205265fbb1'}, {'abstract': 'Republican senators in Texas have proposed adding $100 million to a state-run primary care program specifically for women’s health services, an effort that could help avoid a political fight.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/01/us/texas-may-restore-some-family-planning-budget-cuts.html', 'snippet': 'Republican senators in Texas have proposed adding $100 million to a state-run primary care program specifically for women’s health services, an effort that could help avoid a political fight.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The fight to restore family-planning financing that was cut from the Texas budget in the last legislative session has taken a turn toward primary care. Republican state senators have proposed adding $100 million to a state-run primary care program specifically for women’s health services, an effort that could help avoid a political fight over subsidizing specialty family-planning clinics. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/01/us/01ttHealth1/01ttHealth1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 353, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/01/us/01ttHealth1/01ttHealth1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 353}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/01/us/01ttHealth1/01ttHealth1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 602, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/01/us/01ttHealth1/01ttHealth1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1205, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/01/us/01ttHealth1/01ttHealth1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/01/us/01ttHealth1/01ttHealth1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/01/us/01ttHealth1/01ttHealth1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Restoring Family-Planning Cuts Without Ruffling Feathers', 'kicker': 'The Texas Tribune', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Restoring Family-Planning Cuts Without Ruffling Feathers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Control and Family Planning', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'ma