ion arrived in Beijing in November 2011, under the guidance of Orville Schell, a veteran journalist and observer of China who is now director of the Center on U.S.-China Relations at the Asia Society. That delegation had names familiar to anyone steeped in American high culture and popular culture of recent decades: Yo-Yo Ma, Meryl Streep, Joel Coen, Damian Woetzel, Alice Waters and Amy Tan all seized the chance to engage with Chinese counterparts and foreigners in the city.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/02/28/arts/28artsbeat-schell/28artsbeat-schell-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 760, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/02/28/arts/28artsbeat-schell/28artsbeat-schell-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 760}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/02/28/arts/28artsbeat-schell/28artsbeat-schell-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 889, 'width': 702, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/02/28/arts/28artsbeat-schell/28artsbeat-schell-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 889, 'width': 702, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/02/28/arts/28artsbeat-schell/28artsbeat-schell-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/02/28/arts/28artsbeat-schell/28artsbeat-schell-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/02/28/arts/28artsbeat-schell/28artsbeat-schell-thumbLa