: 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/26683524-0e70-50fa-9bc9-44106dec296c', 'word_count': 1081, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26683524-0e70-50fa-9bc9-44106dec296c'}, {'abstract': 'The documentary “A Place at the Table,” featuring Jeff Bridges, opens on Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/01/film-on-childhood-hunger-opens/', 'snippet': 'The documentary “A Place at the Table,” featuring Jeff Bridges, opens on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One out of every two children today will be on food stamps at some point. Children are not hungry because of a shortage of food, but because of poverty. Those are some of the points made in “A Place at the Table,” a film that opens today that examines how hunger poses economic, social and cultural implications for the country. The directors of the documentary, Kristi Jacobson and Lori Silverbush, and the founder of Share Our Strength, Bill Shore, took part in a TimesTalk discussion this week about how they made the project. Also participating were the chef Tom Colicchio, who was the film’s executive producer, and Jeff Bridges, the actor and activist who appears in the film.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Film on Hunger in America Opens', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bridges, Jeff', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Colicchio, Tom', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Silverbush, Lori', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-01T15:50:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/50f5739d-592d-5abe-944e-9e9225666826', 'word_count': 152, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50f5739d-592d-5abe-944e-9e9225666826'}, {'abstract': 'From the left, the right, and the D.C. housing market.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/01/three-arguments-for-the-sequester/', 'snippet': 'From the left, the right, and the D.C. housing market.', 'lead_paragraph': 'First, Matt Yglesias, from the left:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Three Arguments for the Sequester', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-01T15:52:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cbf4d098-83a2-54f4-8b49-f1210cd23353', 'word_count': 757, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cbf4d098-83a2-54f4-8b49-f1210cd23353'}, {'abstract': 'The ex-basketball star said he “loved” Kim Jong-un.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/01/no-comment-necessary-dennis-rodman-in-north-korea/', 'snippet': 'The ex-basketball star said he “loved” Kim Jong-un.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The ex-basketball star Dennis Rodman watched an exhibition game in Pyongyang, North Korea on Thursday. He sat next to Kim Jong-un, the country’s authoritarian leader, and later had sushi with him. Apparently he enjoyed his trip.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Comment Necessary: Dennis Rodman in North Korea', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Jong-un', 'rank