n “The Christmas Candle.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/01/susan-boyle-gets-a-movie-role/', 'snippet': 'The singer will make her film debut in “The Christmas Candle.”', 'lead_paragraph': ' Susan Boyle, the Scottish singer with the big voice who enjoyed a period of international fame in 2009 after appearing on a British talent show, has landed a part in a Christmas movie, Reuters reported.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Susan Boyle Gets a Movie Role', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boyle, Susan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Isle of Man', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-01T16:01:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5392d7a-505e-5448-8fab-0f09ee6b21e7', 'word_count': 317, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5392d7a-505e-5448-8fab-0f09ee6b21e7'}, {'abstract': 'The Times has announced that the Europe-based paper will reflect a new global strategy.', 'web_url': 'https://publiceditor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/01/for-international-herald-tribune-romance-gives-way-to-reality/', 'snippet': 'The Times has announced that the Europe-based paper will reflect a new global strategy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Musings while pondering Pfc. Bradley Manning’s phone call to a previous public editor’s voice mail line:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For International Herald Tribune, Romance Gives Way to Reality', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Benedict XVI', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-01T16:05:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaret Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/468e854d-ef47-517d-9b55-ee3a3500dcb9', 'word_count': 542, 'uri': 'nyt://article/468e854d-ef47-517d-9b55-ee3a3500dcb9'}, {'abstract': 'The college basketball coach with 902 victories says that the worst word in the English language is “hope.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/03/magazine/coach-bobby-knight-on-why-hes-so-unpleasant.html', 'snippet': 'The college basketball coach with 902 victories says that the worst word in the English language is “hope.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Your book, “The Power of Negative Thinking,” presents what could be considered an anti-Pollyanna vision of the world. I have to agree that eternally optimistic positive thinkers are incredibly annoying.  When I first started coaching, one of the worst things that I think I heard was “It will be O.K.” I would wonder, How the hell is it going to be O.K.? The worst word in the English language is “hope.”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/magazine/03talk/03talk-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 363, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/magazine/03talk/03talk-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1335, 'width': 473, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/magazine/03talk/03talk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/03/magazine/03talk/03talk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/magazine/03talk/03talk-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Coach Bobby Knight on Why He’s So Unpleasant', 'kicker': 'Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘If I Didn’t Enjoy It, I Wouldn’t Have Done It.’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goldman, Andrew', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indiana University', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Knight, Bob (1940- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Power of Negative Thinking (Book)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball (College)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coaches and Managers', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-01T16:09:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'Interview by Andrew Goldman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Interview', 'middlename': 'Andrew', 'lastname': 'Goldman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interview', '_id': 'nyt://article/2da2a39c-d8a1-54f3-ae55-5305455bb1ba', 'word_count': 716, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2da2a39c-d8a1-54f3-ae55-5305455bb1ba'}, {'abstract': 'The “edible promise of a better world.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/03/magazine/who-made-that-sliced-bread.html', 'snippet': 'The “edible promise of a better world.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1928, a full-page newspaper ad announced the first presliced loaf of bread. It included instructions: 1) “Open wrapper at one end”; 2) “Pull out pin”; 3) “Remove as many slices as desired.” At the time, as everyone knew, cut bread quickly went stale. Anticipating consumers’ fears, Otto Rohwedder, a Missouri-based inventor, inserted a U-shaped pin at both ends of his presliced loaf to hold the bread together inside the resealable bag, creating an illusion of wholeness that signified freshness.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/magazine/03wmt1/03wmt1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 453, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/03/magazine/03wmt1/03wmt1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 453}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/magazine/03wmt1/03wmt1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 773, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/magazine/03wmt1/03wmt1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1037, 'width': 1373, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/magazine/03wmt1/03wmt1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/03/magazine/03wmt1/03wmt1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/magazine/03wmt1/03wmt1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Made That Sliced Bread?', 'kicker': 'Innovation', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Who Made That? (Sliced Bread)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bread', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kennedy, Pagan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inventions and Patents', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Missouri', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bakeries and Baked Products', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rohwedder, Otto', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bench, Frank', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-01T16:13:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pagan Kennedy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pagan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kennedy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/68df50a5-1238-5a01-8648-59378551190f', 'word_count': 495, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68df50a5-1238-5a01-8648-59378551190f'}, {'abstract': 'My father couldn’t get far enough away from Italy, but the family business drew me back in.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/03/magazine/bound-together-by-blood-and-wine.html', 'snippet': 'My father couldn’t get far enough away from Italy, but the family business drew me back in.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Once, when I was 15, I passed my grandfather on Queens Boulevard and pretended not to know him. He was over six feet tall, wearing his giant leather boots and weighed down with bags of cured meats, fresh loaves of bread, probably anchovies and what I considered exotic produce at the time (escarole, artichokes and Swiss chard), food of his native Piedmont, Italy. I was with a friend and embarrassed by his Old World ways.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '58', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/magazine/03lives/mag-03Lives-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 604, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/03/magazine/03lives/mag-03Lives-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 604}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/magazine/03lives/mag-03Lives-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 993, 'width': 986, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/magazine/03lives/mag-03Lives-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 993, 'width': 986, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/magazine/03lives/mag-03Lives-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/03/magazine/03lives/mag-03Lives-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/magazine/03lives/mag-03Lives-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bound Together by Blood and Wine', 'kicker': 'Lives', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Family Vine', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Foglino, Annette', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Family Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grandparents', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-01T16:13:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Annette Foglino', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Annette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Foglino', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/68ff4268-ec33-5811-a37d-f5653cabc95f', 'word_count': 772, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68ff4268-ec33-5811-a37d-f5653cabc95f'}, {'abstract': 'Readers respond.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/03/magazine/the-2-17-13-issue.html', 'snippet': 'Readers respond.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAN THE G.O.P. BE SAVED FROM OBSOLESCENCE?', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The 2.17.13 Issue', 'kicker': 'Reply All | Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Can The G.O.P. Be Saved From Obsolescence?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-01T16:13:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/e6640b26-ac1a-5387-b54e-c1eca296e9d3', 'word_count': 777, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e6640b26-ac1a-5387-b54e-c1eca296e9d3'}, {'abstract': 'Source material; parking lottery.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/03/magazine/the-journalist-and-the-moneymaker.html', 'snippet': 'Source material; parking lottery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I recently read a nonfiction book detailing the lives of ordinary people living in extreme poverty abroad. The book has enjoyed great commercial success in the United States. The author no doubt received an advance and funding to spend time following these people’s lives. My question is this: Is she ethically obligated to share her profits with the people whose stories have made this book what it is? KATE MCMAHON, BROOKLYN', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/magazine/ethicist/ethicist-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1316, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/02/02/magazine/ethicist/ethicist-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1316}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/magazine/ethicist/ethicist-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 467, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/magazine/ethicist/ethicist-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 934, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/magazine/ethicist/ethicist-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/02/02/magazine/ethicist/ethicist-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/magazine/ethicist/e