wly minted president, than in well over a decade.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI — Last year it seemed the death penalty might be on the way out in India. But in just the past two months, since the new president, Pranab Mukherjee, took office, it is being enforced again. Two men have already been hanged, and Mukherjee rejected the petitions for clemency of five death-row inmates.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'India’s Mr. Death', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime Rates', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mukherjee, Pranab', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court of India', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-01T16:23:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hartosh Singh Bal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hartosh', 'middlename': 'Singh', 'lastname': 'Bal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca5a8524-b325-52c2-b7d3-5e9688ed3d7e', 'word_count': 660, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca5a8524-b325-52c2-b7d3-5e9688ed3d7e'}, {'abstract': 'This week, Emily Bazelon talks about “Sticks and Stones,” her new book about bullying; Phillip Lopate discusses the craft of essay writing; and Gregory Cowles has best-seller news. Sam Tanenhaus is the host.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2013/03/01/books/review/03books_pod.html', 'snippet': 'This week, Emily Bazelon talks about “Sticks and Stones,” her new book about bullying; Phillip Lopate discusses the craft of essay writing; and Gregory Cowles has best-seller news. Sam Tanenhaus is the host.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week, Emily Bazelon talks about “Sticks and Stones,” her new book about bullying; Phillip Lopate discusses the craft of essay writing; and Gregory Cowles has best-seller news. Sam Tanenhaus is the host.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Book Review Podcast', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Podcasts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-01T16:27:38+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/563894ad-091c-529c-9fd9-3ae494a28dcd', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/563894ad-091c-529c-9fd9-3ae494a28dcd'}, {'abstract': 'Lance Armstrong was hit with two more lawsuits on Thursday, including one by an insurance company that paid him $3 million in bonuses for his first three Tour victories.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/02/sports/cycling/lance-armstrong-is-facing-another-lawsuit.html', 'snippet': 'Lance Armstrong was hit with two more lawsuits on Thursday, including one by an insurance company that paid him $3 million in bonuses for his first three Tour victories.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the wake of his doping confession, Lance Armstrong is facing two more lawsuits, including one filed by an insurance company that paid him $3 million in bonuses for his first three Tour de France victories.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, '