: None, 'lastname': 'Bishop', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/81c37f90-4cf7-5d38-b227-d49f09333926', 'word_count': 1195, 'uri': 'nyt://article/81c37f90-4cf7-5d38-b227-d49f09333926'}, {'abstract': 'In these intertwined essays, Cynthia Zarin reflects on love, work and the surprises of time’s passing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/03/books/review/an-enlarged-heart-by-cynthia-zarin.html', 'snippet': 'In these intertwined essays, Cynthia Zarin reflects on love, work and the surprises of time’s passing.', 'lead_paragraph': '“An Enlarged Heart” is a collection of personal essays written mostly over the past decade by the poet Cynthia Zarin. I assume the book is labeled a “personal history” for the same reason that collections of short stories are sometimes called “linked stories” or even “novels in stories,” which is that the reading public apparently prefers unified, book-length narratives to such hodgepodge. This is a superficial point, and the packaging decision was almost certainly out of Zarin’s hands, but I mention it up front for a couple of reasons.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/books/review/0303-Beha-Sub/0303-Beha-Sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 729, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/03/books/review/0303-Beha-Sub/0303-Beha-Sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 729}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/books/review/0303-Beha-Sub/0303-Beha-Sub-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 844, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'c