andfills globally by 40 percent per vehicle from 2011 levels. In 2016, the company said, Ford would be producing just 13.4 pounds of waste a vehicle at its operations around the world, down from 38 pounds in 2007, 22.7 pounds in 2011 and 20.3 pounds this year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Automakers Work to Achieve Zero-Waste Goals', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recycling of Waste Materials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Waste Materials and Disposal', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chrysler Group LLC', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ford Motor Co', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Honda Motor Co Ltd', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nissan Motor Co', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Toyota Motor Corporation', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Volkswagen AG', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-01T19:13:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Motavalli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Motavalli', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/be6c1e5d-7603-5750-83d7-e4fe3d9983dd', 'word_count': 645, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be6c1e5d-7603-5750-83d7-e4fe3d9983dd'}, {'abstract': 'Speaking to reporters after meeting with Congressional leaders, Pr