ublican lawmakers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama is obviously sick and tired of the widely peddled notion that the sequester and all other budget failures are ultimately his fault because he’s the president. His frustration made for a surprisingly lively news conference this morning, and gave the public a brief reminder that there are real limits to the power of the White House.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Limits of Executive Power', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-01T19:25:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Firestone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Firestone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5827ca1-144b-5885-9d7b-3ff73ac8433f', 'word_count': 588, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5827ca1-144b-5885-9d7b-3ff73ac8433f'}, {'abstract': 'After Li Junyun, a Korean citizen, disappeared in Queens last week, her friends tried several times to report her missing. Ms. Li’s death is now being investigated.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/01/before-a-tourists-body-was-found-rebuffed-efforts-to-report-her-missing/', 'snippet': 'After Li Junyun, a Korean citizen, disappeared in Queens last week, her friends tried several times to report her missing. Ms. Li’s death is now being investigated.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Li Junyun, 46, arrived in New York last month with a tourist visa and a single suitcase, “hoping to see what America was like,” a friend said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/01/nyregion/01li-cityroom/01li-cityroom-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 670, 'width': 502, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/01/nyregion/01li-cityroom/01li-cityroom-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 670, 'width': 502, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/01/nyregion/01li-cityroom/01li-cityroom-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/01/nyregion/01li-cityroom/01li-cityroom-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/01/nyregion/01li-cityroom/01li-cityroom-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Before a Tourist’s Body Was Found, Rebuffed Efforts to Report Her Missing', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Missing Persons', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Flushing (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-01T19:28:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeffrey E. Singer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeffrey', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Singer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0486ffb9-0409-5bf8-a8d3-3c4179a1501f', 'word_count': 596, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0486ffb9-0409-5bf8-a8d3-3c4179a1501f'}, {'abstract': 'Lawsuits in New Orleans over snowball patents and trademarks involving equipment and flavors are finally settled.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/01/new-orleans-snowball-wars-come-to-an-end/', 'snippet': 'Lawsuits in New Orleans over snowball patents and trademarks involving equipment and flavors are finally settled.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Snowballs are as integral to New Orleans life as beignets. But hard-core loyalties have cleaved the community of shaved-ice enthusiasts and vendors, as seen by the three decades of lawsuits that have just come to an end. Channel 4 in New Orleans has the story. The lawsuits involved disputes over trademarks and patents for the equipment used to make the snowballs, and also which companies could use which names for flavors like “King Cake,” “Cajun Red Hot,” “Orchid Cream Vanilla” and “Hurricane.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Orleans Snowball Wars Come to an End', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Orleans (La)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-01T19:30:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/950ed8d4-1d44-5462-83a7-3be6f95247f2', 'word_count': 82, 'uri': 'nyt://article/950ed8d4-1d44-5462-83a7-3be6f95247f2'}, {'abstract': 'A bill broadening protections for news publishers was approved by German lawmakers, but critics said the measure did not go far enough.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/02/technology/german-copyright-law-targets-google-links.html', 'snippet': 'A bill broadening protections for news publishers was approved by German lawmakers, but critics said the measure did not go far enough.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — German lawmakers approved legislation on Friday that grants publishers the right to charge search engines and other online aggregators for reproducing their content but continues to allow the free use of text in links and brief summaries.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'German Copyright Law Targets Google Links', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'German Copyright Law Takes Aim at Google Links', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eddy, Melissa', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search Engines', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Copyrights and Copyright Violations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-01T19:30:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Eddy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eddy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/18a5db52-7494-557d-a4e5-e485ef342a94', 'word_count': 679, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18a5db52-7494-557d-a4e5-e485ef342a94'}, {'abstract': 'Root vegetables make a colorful and satisfying winter meal, writes Martha Rose Shulman in this week’s Recipes for Health.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/01/a-rainbow-of-root-vegetables/', 'snippet': 'Root vegetables make a colorful and satisfying winter meal, writes Martha Rose Shulman in this week’s Recipes for Health.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week’s Recipes for Health is as much a treat for the eyes as the palate. Colorful root vegetables from bright orange carrots and red scallions to purple and yellow potatoes and pale green leeks will add color and flavor to your table.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/02/27/science/recipehealthpromo/recipehealthpromo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 406, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/02/27/science/recipehealthpromo/recipehealthpromo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 406}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/02/27/science/recipehealthpromo/recipehealthpromo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 694, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/02/27/science/recipehealthpromo/recipehealthpromo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1387, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/02/27/science/recipehealthpromo/recipehealthpromo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/02/27/science/recipehealthpromo/recipehealthpromo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/02/27/science/recipehealthpromo/recipehealthpromo-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Rainbow of Root Vegetables', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-01T19:31:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Parker-Pope', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker-Pope', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1f40178-b27d-5998-a5fc-5e4ff664469f', 'word_count': 335, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1f40178-b27d-5998-a5fc-5e4ff664469f'}, {'abstract': 'A 10-hour mini-series, “The Bible,” begins on Sunday on History and will rerun on Monday nights on Lifetime.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/03/arts/television/with-the-bible-the-mini-series-goes-back-to-the-beginning.html', 'snippet': 'A 10-hour mini-series, “The Bible,” begins on Sunday on History and will rerun on Monday nights on Lifetime.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For as long as there has been filmed entertainment there have been producers and directors retelling the dramatic stories from the 66 books of the Old and New Testaments. But the cable channel History’s coming 10-hour mini-series, “The Bible,” might be the first to include an angel skilled in Chinese martial arts.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/arts/03THEBIBLE1_SPAN/03THEBIBLE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/03/arts/03THEBIBLE1_SPAN/03THEBIBLE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/arts/03THEBIBLE1_SPAN/03THEBIBLE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/arts/03THEBIBLE1_SPAN/03THEBIBLE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/arts/03THEBIBLE1_SPAN/03THEBIBLE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/03/arts/03THEBIBLE1_SPAN/03THEBIBLE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/arts/03THEBIBLE1_SPAN/03THEBIBLE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'With ‘The Bible,’ the Mini-Series Goes Back to the Beginning', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mini-Series Goes Back to the Beginning', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jensen, Elizabeth', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bible', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'History Channel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burnett, Mark', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-01T19:33:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/24dbf9e7-9584-50c8-965d-a7b7f621ad5c', 'word_count': 1050, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24dbf9e7-9584-50c8-965d-a7b7f621ad5c'}, {'abstract': 'Jane Campion’s TV mini-series “Top of the Lake,” the first TV show to be screened at Sundance, was well-received — not surprising, given how TV watching is changing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/03/arts/television/a-day-of-watching-tv-at-sundance.html', 'snippet': 'Jane Campion’s TV mini-series “Top of the Lake,” the first TV show to be screened at Sundance, was well-received — not surprising, given how TV watching is changing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARK CITY, Utah — Jane Campion has spent decades traveling the festival circuit, listening to countless audiences react to her films, like “The Piano” or “Bright Star.” Still, nothing prepared her for the response during a showing in the Egyptian Theater during the Sundance Film Festival in January. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/arts/03LAKE1_SPAN/03LAKE1_SPAN-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/03/arts/03LAKE1_SPAN/03LAKE1_SPAN-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/arts/03LAKE1_SPAN/03LAKE1_SPAN-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 488, 'width': 732, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/arts/03LAKE1_SPAN/03LAKE1_SPAN-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 488, 'width': 732, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/arts/03LAKE1_SPAN/03LAKE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/03/arts/03LAKE1_SPAN/03LAKE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/arts/03LAKE1_SPAN/03LAKE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Day of Watching TV at Sundance', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Day of Watching TV at Sundance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sundance Film Festival (Park City, Utah)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Campion, Jane', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-01T19:33:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dade Hayes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dade', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hayes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dc260b91-ab3a-5a52-8bd8-6ec88cf78bd5', 'word_count': 1038, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dc260b91-ab3a-5a52-8bd8-6ec88cf78bd5'}, {'abstract': 'Financial woes are forcing cutbacks and closings in government-owned hotels known as paradors, many of which occupy striking historic buildings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/03/travel/spains-paradors-face-an-uncertain-future.html', 'snippet': 'Financial woes are forcing cutbacks and closings in government-owned hotels known as paradors, many of which occupy striking historic buildings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We crisscrossed Europe in the family car when I was a child. My father, a sports columnist based in Paris in the 1960s, was always testing tips he had gotten from Grand Prix racecar drivers. My mother, no surprise, was constantly telling him to slow down. In the back seat, my sisters and I were usually hungry, tired or fighting. But we saw amazing things: castles, cathedrals, villages slapped up against cliffs to protect them from Roman invaders, beaches still scarred with the wreckage of World War II battles.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/travel/03PARADORES4/03PARADORES4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 384, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/03/travel/03PARADORES4/03PARADORES4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 384}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/travel/03PARADORES4/03PARADORES4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 656, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/travel/03PARADORES4/03PARADORES4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1312, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/travel/03PARADORES4/03PARADORES4-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/03/travel/03PARADORES4/03PARADORES4-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/travel/03PARADORES4/03PARADORES4-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Spain’s Paradors Face an Uncertain Future', 'kicker': 'Update', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Fond Past With an Uncertain Future', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Daley, Suzanne', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and Sites', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hotels and Travel Lodgings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-01T19:33:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Suzanne Daley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Suzanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Daley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ec9b1da1-a665-5bc4-b029-71a2c804fdac', 'word_count': 1861, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ec9b1da1-a665-5bc4-b029-71a2c804fdac'}, {'abstract': 'A spicy, zingy pickle alleviates the root vegetable doldrums of winter.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/06/dining/pickled-radishes-provide-a-crunchy-end-to-winter.html', 'snippet': 'A spicy, zingy pickle alleviates the root vegetable doldrums of winter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'By March I’ve had my fill of root vegetables. All winter long, I gratinéed them, puréed them, roasted and sautéed them. I savored them in soups, blanketed them with cheese and cream and shaved them sensibly into lean, crisp salads.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Crunchy End to Winter', 'kicker': 'A Good Appetite', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Crunchy End to Winter', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clark, Melissa', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pickles and Relishes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radishes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kimchi (South Korean Food)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-01T19:34:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/55525c94-3af3-5db0-a001-60f217f3efa9', 'word_count': 392, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55525c94-3af3-5db0-a001-60f217f3efa9'}, {'abstract': 'The 22-year-old Russian model and face of Christian Dior talks to T about music, beauty and more.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/01/model-diary-daria-strokous/', 'snippet': 'The 22-year-old Russian model and face of Christian Dior talks to T about music, beauty and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was no surprise that Daria Strokous, a face in Christian Dior’s current advertising campaign, was on the runway today in a Raf Simons-designed frock. The 22-year-old Russian model lives in New York and is currently bopping around Paris to hip-hop music on her iPod.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Model Diary | Daria Strokous', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Models (Professional)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'na