print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-01T22:21:56+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'ABC', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/68b927fc-8b66-5c78-8672-75e4f4a1da8f', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/68b927fc-8b66-5c78-8672-75e4f4a1da8f'}, {'abstract': 'A high-priced Westchester village with a top-rated school system has acquired a slightly more diverse population.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/03/realestate/bronxville-ny-traditions-change-even-here.html', 'snippet': 'A high-priced Westchester village with a top-rated school system has acquired a slightly more diverse population.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Seven years ago, when Irina Sher, a native of Yerevan, Armenia, first set foot in the southern Westchester suburb of Bronxville and saw its wooded hillsides inset with substantial Tudor, Shingle-style and Victorian homes, she was captivated. When she learned about its top-rated public school, her decision was made: “I knew right away I had to raise my children here, whatever the cost.”', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/realestate/03LIVING_SPAN/03LIVING_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/03/realestate/03LIVING_SPAN/03LIVING_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/realestate/03LIVING_SPAN/03LIVING_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/realestate/03LIVING_SPAN/03LIVING_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/realestate/03LIVING_SPAN/03LIVING_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/03/realestate/03LIVING_SPAN/03LIVING_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/realestate/03LIVING_SPAN/03LIVING_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Traditions Change, Even Here', 'kicker': 'Living In | Bronxville, N.Y.', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Traditions Change, Even Here', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Eastchester (NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronxville (NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-01T22:23:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elsa Brenner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elsa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brenner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6861004d-7490-5e62-a28d-463a55e89f62', 'word_count': 507, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6861004d-7490-5e62-a28d-463a55e89f62'}, {'abstract': 'Several businesses in Red Hook have reopened.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/01/fairway-market-comes-back-after-sandy/', 'snippet': 'Several businesses in Red Hook have reopened.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In another sign that the region is recovering from Sandy’s devastation, the Fairway Market and other businesses in Red Hook on Brooklyn’s waterfront reopened today. Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg and Senator Charles E. Schumer were some of the first customers to order from the Fairway deli counter.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fairway Market Comes Back After Sandy', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-01T22:23:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/784cff1c-1b6c-529e-8918-0ab0cf28f16c', 'word_count': 47, 'uri': 'nyt://article/784cff1c-1b6c-529e-8918-0ab0cf28f16c'}, {'abstract': 'The goal: a pure look. the makeup artist Aaron de Mey achieved this by giving the models a dewy, shimmery complexion.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/01/backstage-beauty-report-chalayan/', 'snippet': 'The goal: a pure look. the makeup artist Aaron de Mey achieved this by giving the models a dewy, shimmery complexion.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Hussein is doing something very elevated with his collection, so I wanted the girls to appear very pure,” said the makeup artist Aaron de Mey backstage at Chalayan. To accomplish this, he first worked M.A.C. Mineralize Charged Water Moisture Gel onto the skin to lay the groundwork for a dewy complexion. He then mixed together two shimmery hues of M.A.C. Cream Color Base, Pearl and Luna, and applied them “where the sun hits your face” — cheekbones, bridge of nose, cupid bow, chin — “to give the face dimension.” The look was stark and clean but not severe thanks to the iridescence in the product.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Backstage Beauty Report | Chalayan', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-01T22:35:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Moroz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moroz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/92856785-fc43-5e52-991b-4184badab5ee', 'word_count': 105, 'uri': 'nyt://article/92856785-fc43-5e52-991b-4184badab5ee'}, {'abstract': 'Rihanna’s costume designer, who worked with her on the Rihanna for River Island collection, is sharing the spotlight.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2013/03/03/fashion/20130303-SELMAN.html', 'snippet': 'Rihanna’s costume designer, who worked with her on the Rihanna for River Island collection, is sharing the spotlight.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rihanna’s costume designer, who worked with her on the Rihanna for River Island collection, is sharing the spotlight.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/fashion/20130303-SELMAN-slide-XUIB/20130303-SELMAN-slide-XUIB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1010, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/03/fashion/20130303-SELMAN-slide-XUIB/20130303-SELMAN-slide-XUIB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1010}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'image