odel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 2012 Honda Civic was a goof: a dull all-new car that wasn’t better, in any significant way, than the one it replaced. Goofs are fixable, however — just ask NASA.', 'print_section': 'AU', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/automobiles/CIVICsilo/CIVICsilo-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 328, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/03/automobiles/CIVICsilo/CIVICsilo-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 328}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/automobiles/CIVICsilo/CIVICsilo-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 561, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/automobiles/CIVICsilo/CIVICsilo-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1121, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/automobiles/CIVICsilo/CIVICsilo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/03/automobiles/CIVICsilo/CIVICsilo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/automobiles/CIVICsilo/CIVICsilo-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Well-Done Do-Over Raises the Final Grade', 'kicker': 'Behind the Wheel | 2013 Honda Civic', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Well-Done Do-Over\r\nRais