ganization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ab3f3c5-4cd4-5648-939d-b6b93b3e5802', 'word_count': 1117, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ab3f3c5-4cd4-5648-939d-b6b93b3e5802'}, {'abstract': 'Elements of American show business and North Korean propaganda came together when the former basketball star Dennis Rodman said in Pyongyang that North Koreans “love” their new leader, Kim Jong-un.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/01/with-rodman-stunt-american-reality-tv-and-north-korean-propaganda-fuse/', 'snippet': 'Elements of American show business and North Korean propaganda came together when the former basketball star Dennis Rodman said in Pyongyang that North Koreans “love” their new leader, Kim Jong-un.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, Sunday, 11:21 p.m. Elements of American show business and North Korean propaganda briefly fused on Friday, when the former basketball star Dennis Rodman told reporters in Pyongyang that North Koreans “love” their new leader, Kim Jong-un. “And guess what?” the athlete turned reality TV star added, “I love him — the guy’s awesome.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With Rodman Stunt, American Reality TV and North Korean Propaganda Fuse', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reality Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Jong-un', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rodman, Dennis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pyongyang (North Korea)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-01T22:39:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstnam