, 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Devil Wants a Sequel', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Last Exorcism: Part II', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gass-Donnelly, Ed', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-01T23:14:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Webster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Webster', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/4082703f-71eb-5f3f-a14a-5ec2e7ecbbea', 'word_count': 290, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4082703f-71eb-5f3f-a14a-5ec2e7ecbbea'}, {'abstract': 'One the Waterfront, in New Rochelle, underwent a renovation last year and returned with a refreshed menu of mainly seafood, with a smattering of traditional pub fare.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/03/nyregion/a-review-of-on-the-waterfront-in-new-rochelle.html', 'snippet': 'One the Waterfront, in New Rochelle, underwent a renovation last year and returned with a refreshed menu of mainly seafood, with a smattering of traditional pub fare.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One cold, windy evening, I found myself yearning, somewhat perversely, for a seafood dinner served on a deck overlooking the water. Though that’s really a summertime treat, I went in search of the closest thing I could find in these waning weeks of winter.', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/nyregion/03DINEWE2_SPAN/03DINEWE2_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 731, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2