, 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef2ae6d3-20e6-5c06-a6ce-5c29e7d7b8d3', 'word_count': 382, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef2ae6d3-20e6-5c06-a6ce-5c29e7d7b8d3'}, {'abstract': 'For the Tony Award-winning producer Daryl Roth, Sunday is a day to sit on a bench in the park, see a morning movie or visit the cast and crew of her shows.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/03/nyregion/for-daryl-roth-sundays-include-taking-cookies-and-hugs-to-the-theater.html', 'snippet': 'For the Tony Award-winning producer Daryl Roth, Sunday is a day to sit on a bench in the park, see a morning movie or visit the cast and crew of her shows.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even on Sundays, the theater takes center stage for the Tony Award-winning producer Daryl Roth. With her newest production, the musical “Kinky Boots,” starting previews at the Al Hirschfeld Theater this Sunday, a visit with its cast and crew is a priority. But Ms. Roth, 68, who has produced seven Pulitzer Prize-winning plays and serves as artistic director of her two Off Broadway theaters, also makes time for the other joys in her life, which include her grandchildren and her dog. She lives on the Upper East Side with her husband, Steven, 71, the chairman of Vornado Realty Trust, and their 14-year-old Lowchen, Lucy.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/nyregion/03ROUTINE1_SPAN/03ROUTINE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/03/nyregion/03ROUTINE1_SPAN/03ROUTINE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/nyregion/03ROUTINE1_SPAN/03ROUTINE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_nam