le/162fc168-f095-56cd-87ac-8771aa8da03d', 'word_count': 593, 'uri': 'nyt://article/162fc168-f095-56cd-87ac-8771aa8da03d'}, {'abstract': 'Brian Rose and Edward Fausty documented the neighborhood, concentrating not so much on the people, but on the structures and shapes that made up the local landscape.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/03/nyregion/brian-rose-and-edward-faustys-images-of-the-lower-east-side.html', 'snippet': 'Brian Rose and Edward Fausty documented the neighborhood, concentrating not so much on the people, but on the structures and shapes that made up the local landscape.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Toward the end of 1979, Brian Rose and Edward Fausty began roaming the Lower East Side of Manhattan with a Japanese view camera attached to a tripod. New York City’s fiscal crisis was a fresh memory, and gentrification had not yet arrived. Tenements seemed to burn daily. But the frontierlike nature of the neighborhood and the availability of cheap rent encouraged an explosion of creativity.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/nyregion/20130303LESss-slide-GG50/20130303LESss-slide-GG50-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 476, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/03/nyregion/20130303LESss-slide-GG50/20130303LESss-slide-GG50-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 476}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/nyregion/20130303LESss-slide-GG50/20130303LESss-slide-GG50-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 813, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/nyregion/20130303LESss-slide-GG50/20130303LESss-slide-GG50-superJumbo.jpg', 'heigh