'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/02/sports/hockey/nhls-request-for-video-rights-creates-quandary-for-olympics.html', 'snippet': 'As talks continue over whether N.H.L. players will go to the Sochi Games, there is concern that other leagues may ask the I.O.C. for the same concessions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Talks between the N.H.L. and the International Olympic Committee over whether the league will send its players next year to Sochi, Russia, hinge on one overarching issue: if the I.O.C. grants the N.H.L. concessions for shutting down its business at midseason, other leagues that send players to the Olympics may ask for the same.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'N.H.L.’s Request for Video Rights Creates Quandary for Olympics', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'N.H.L.’s Request for Video Rights Creates Quandary for Olympics', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2014)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Olympic Committee', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bettman, Gary', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "National Hockey League Players' Assn", 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-02T05:11:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6298008-ba44-5a6c-b246-6606219de1fa', 'word_count': 573, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6298008-ba44-5a6c-b246-6606219de1fa'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/02/arts/television/whats-on-saturday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '9 P.M. (Starz) THE AMAZING SPIDER-MAN (2012) Five years after “Spider-Man 3,” the director Marc Webb rebooted the franchise with new stars — Andrew Garfield, above, as Peter Parker; Emma Stone as his girlfriend, Gwen Stacy; and Martin Sheen and Sally Field as Uncle Ben and Aunt May — and an updated origin story centered on a bioengineering company, Oscorp. And along comes a spider. “The latest post-atomic-age Spider-Man has been updated with a skateboard and a hoodie, but it’s unclear whom he speaks to (beyond Sony’s shareholders), and for what reason,” Manohla Dargis wrote in The New York Times. “Mr. Garfield and Ms. Stone are by far the movie’s greatest assets and when they’re together on screen, they add warmth and a believable closeness to the industrial mix.” Still, “this ‘Spider-Man’ feels like one of those unnecessary software versions, more Spider-Man 1.5 than Spider-Man reborn,” she said. “Spider-Man’s ethos remains — with great power comes great responsibility — but these days you can’t see his superhero heart and soul for his branding.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Saturday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-02T06:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/e877c169-556f-5a38-ad91-89107634b40d', 'word_count': 766, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e877c169-556f-5a38-ad91-89107634b40d'}, {'abstract': 'President Benigno S. Aquino III made the plea a day after the group lost several members in a violent clash with Malaysian police officers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/03/world/asia/aquino-calls-for-surrender-of-filipino-group-in-malaysia.html', 'snippet': 'President Benigno S. Aquino III made the plea a day after the group lost several members in a violent clash with Malaysian police officers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — The Philippine president, Benigno S. Aquino III, called on Saturday for the surrender of an armed Muslim clan that took over a Malaysian village, making the plea a day after the group lost several members in a violent clash with Malaysian police officers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Philippine Leader Calls for Surrender of Group in Malaysia', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Philippine Leader Calls for Surrender of Group in Malaysia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Aquino, Benigno S III', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philippines', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Malaysia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-02T09:26:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gerry Mullany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gerry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mullany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5cbb5291-7ba6-5d2a-af84-a7a6a8f6db7d', 'word_count': 270, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5cbb5291-7ba6-5d2a-af84-a7a6a8f6db7d'}, {'abstract'