jamin Netanyahu of Israel received a two-week extension to form a governing coalition, a situation complicated by an unexpected alliance of two rising political stars.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/03/world/middleeast/in-israel-netanyahu-expects-extension-to-form-coalition.html', 'snippet': 'Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu of Israel received a two-week extension to form a governing coalition, a situation complicated by an unexpected alliance of two rising political stars.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — Israel’s president on Saturday granted Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu a two-week extension to form a governing coalition, a task complicated by mathematics and chemistry. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Israeli Premier Gets Extension to Form a Coalition but Faces Turmoil', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Israeli Premier, Facing Unlikely Alliance, Is Given More Time to Form a Coalition', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Netanyahu, Benjamin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lapid, Yair', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bennett, Naftali', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Likud Party (Israel)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-02T15:15:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Isabel Kershner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kershner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6bec2c6-bafd-565a-88af-17f9fa65bd7e', 'word_count': 847, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6bec2c6-bafd-565a-88af-17f9fa65bd7e'}, {'abstract': 'Viktor & Rolf presented a fall show on Saturday that was minimal on tricks, and also minimal on lengths.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/02/viktor-rolf-in-black-and-white/', 'snippet': 'Viktor & Rolf presented a fall show on Saturday that was minimal on tricks, and also minimal on lengths.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Continuing in the restrained direction of their last collection, the designers Viktor Horsting and Rolf Snoeren of Viktor & Rolf presented a fall show on Saturday that was minimal on tricks, and also minimal on lengths. The only thing that caused a ruckus was the arrival of the actress Jessica Chastain in the front row.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Viktor & Rolf in Black and White', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Horsting, Viktor', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Snoeren, Rolf', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Viktor & Rolf', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-02T15:32:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b77d48c-e3f5-51cc-9cd3-85f1e94345a7', 'word_count': 248, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b77d48c-e3f5-51cc-9cd3-85f1e94345a7'}, {'abstract': 'Wasting taxpayer money is OK, as long as it’s on corporations.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/02/welfare-for-the-medical-industrial-complex/', 'snippet': 'Wasting taxpayer money is OK, as long as it’s on corporations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Stephen Brill’s long piece about medical costs has brought forth a mixture of praise and annoyance from health-care economics experts, including Aaron Carroll and Uwe Reinhardt; they’ve been screaming for years that our medical system charges too much, and so they’re both gratified and annoyed to see a major-media piece confirming what they’ve been saying all along.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Welfare for the Medical-Industrial Complex', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-02T15:34:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d04801c-be0e-5159-a856-526d72c3b62d', 'word_count': 375, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d04801c-be0e-5159-a856-526d72c3b62d'}, {'abstract': 'Virginia’s economy will be among the hardest hit by the federal government’s $85 billion in spending cuts to military and domestic programs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2013/03/03/us/virginia.html', 'snippet': 'Virginia’s economy will be among the hardest hit by the federal government’s $85 billion in spending cuts to military and domestic programs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Virginia’s economy will be among the hardest hit by the federal government’s $85 billion in spending cuts to military and domestic programs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sequestration’s Impact', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None,