lling for similarly rigorous studies of other popular diets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This is a watershed moment in the field of nutrition, medical experts say. For the first time, researchers have shown that a diet can have an effect as powerful as drugs in preventing what really matters to patients — heart attacks, and strokes and deaths from cardiovascular disease. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/us/HEART-1/HEART-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/03/us/HEART-1/HEART-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/us/HEART-1/HEART-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/us/HEART-1/HEART-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/us/HEART-1/HEART-1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/03/us/HEART-1/HEART-1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/us/HEART-1/HEART-1-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Experts Want More Studies of Diet’s Role for the Heart', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Experts Want More Studies Of Diet’s Role For the Heart', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kolata, Gina', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Heart', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Journal of Medicine', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-02T16:44:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gina Kolata', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kolata', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/433fe8e6-61d8-568c-9976-c9c4463c6371', 'word_count': 1262, 'uri': 'nyt://article/433fe8e6-61d8-568c-9976-c9c4463c6371'}, {'abstract': 'Bernard Lagat, the holder of several American track records, discusses his preparations for his first long-distance road race, the 13.1-mile NYC Half, on March 17.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/03/sports/bernard-lagat-training-for-nyc-half.html', 'snippet': 'Bernard Lagat, the holder of several American track records, discusses his preparations for his first long-distance road race, the 13.1-mile NYC Half, on March 17.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bernard Lagat has been so successful on the track for so long that he has been able to delay running road races, a transition that Mo Farah of Britain and other middle-distance specialists have been making. In February, Lagat, 38, set an American indoor two-mile record at the Millrose Games, adding to his many national records. But days later, Lagat announced that he would run his first long-distance road race, the 13.1-mile NYC Half, on March 17. He spoke recently by telephone from his home in Tucson, where he trains with the distance runner Abdi Abdirahman. KEN BELSON ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/sports/dogSECONDS/dogSECONDS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 720, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/03/sports/dogSECONDS/dogSECONDS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 720}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/sports/dogSECONDS/dogSECONDS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 853, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/sports/dogSECONDS/dogSECONDS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1819, 'width': 1515, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/sports/dogSECONDS/dogSECONDS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/03/sports/dogSECONDS/dogSECONDS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/sports/dogSECONDS/dogSECONDS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'With Bernard Lagat', 'kicker': '30 Seconds ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Middle-Distance Star Prepares to Go Long', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lagat, Bernard', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Track and Field', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Running', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-02T16:57:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/b4bd9383-7981-5745-ad6e-e4bdebf0bf55', 'word_count': 546, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b4bd9383-7981-5745-ad6e-e4bdebf0bf55'}, {'abstract': 'The Braves’ Craig Kimbrel is a hitter’s nightmare: his fastball, reaching into the upper 90s, has an extra gear. Last season, he struck out more than half the batters he faced.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/03/sports/baseball/craig-kimbrels-stare-is-menacing-but-his-fastball-is-most-feared.html', 'snippet': 'The Braves’ Craig Kimbrel is a hitter’s nightmare: his fastball, reaching into the upper 90s, has an extra gear. Last season, he struck out more than half the batters he faced.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KISSIMMEE, Fla. — It cannot be detected by a radar gun, and it would not make sense to a physicist. But to the sharpened eyes of a major league hitter, one pitcher’s 98-mile-per-hour fastball can behave much differently from another’s. And when that pitcher is Craig Kimbrel of the Atlanta Braves, it does not seem fair.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/02/sports/dog-jp-kimbrel/dog-jp-kimbrel-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 415, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/02/sports/dog-jp-kimbrel/dog-jp-kimbrel-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 415}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': Non