cut’s public employee retirement plans brought a class-action lawsuit against Amgen, one of the world’s largest biotechnology companies, accusing it of securities fraud. Last week, in a 6-to-3 decision affirming a ruling by the United States Court of Appeals for the Ninth Circuit, the Supreme Court allowed the suit to proceed, giving the retirement plans the chance to prove their case. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Class Action in the Public Interest', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Class Action in the Public Interest', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMGEN INC', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Securities and Commodities Violations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pensions and Retirement Plans', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-02T18:17:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1a9812b-852d-5b9d-bc0f-6f33fb23640e', 'word_count': 440, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1a9812b-852d-5b9d-bc0f-6f33fb23640e'}, {'abstract': 'Companies will need to finesse their policies on telecommuting by employees.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/03/opinion/sunday/working-from-home-vs-the-office.html', 'snippet': 'Companies will need to finesse their policies on telecommuting by employees.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Marissa Mayer, chief executive at Yahoo, may not have set out to start a national conversation about working from home when she decided that employees at that Internet company must come into the office. But she has done just that. In a memo, Ms. Mayer’s top human resources executive wrote: “Speed and quality are often sacrificed when we work from home. We need to be one Yahoo!, and that starts with physically being together.” ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Location, Location, Location', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Location, Location, Location', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yahoo! Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telecommuting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Productivity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mayer, Marissa', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Silicon Valley (Calif)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-02T18:18:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a14e170-26a6-521a-ad9a-70dca18a7062', 'word_count': 534, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a14e170-26a6-521a-ad9a-70dca18a7062'}, {'abstract': 'A new advocacy group debases the presidency by trolling for unlimited corporate money.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/03/opinion/sunday/the-white-house-joins-the-cash-grab.html', 'snippet': 'A new advocacy group debases the presidency by trolling for unlimited corporate money.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is tempting to applaud the nonprofit group now spending nearly $100,000 on ads to pressure Republican lawmakers to accept gun-control measures. The group is fighting a well-financed and powerful corporate gun lobby that has never hesitated to spend millions to get its way in Congress.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The White House Joins the Cash Grab', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The White House Joins the Cash Grab', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Organizing for Action', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Action Committees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lobbying and Lobbyists', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-02T18:19:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a94da72-001a-573b-82cd-d34d44ebd35f', 'word_count': 640, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a94da72-001a-573b-82cd-d34d44ebd35f'}, {'abstract': 'Texas officials said that so far they had found no reason to file criminal charges against the adoptive mother of a Russian boy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/03/world/europe/russians-renew-fury-after-death-of-adopted-boy-in-texas-is-ruled-accidental.html', 'snippet': 'Texas officials said that so far they had found no reason to file criminal charges against the adoptive mother of a Russian boy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — Supporters of a Russian law banning adoptions by Americans reacted with renewed fury and derision on Saturday after Texas officials said that so far they had found no reason to file criminal charges against the adoptive mother of a 3-year-old boy from Russia who died under mysterious circumstances in January. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/world/03adopt_337/03adopt_337-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/03/world/03adopt_337/03adopt_337-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/world/03adopt_337/03adopt_337-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/world/03adopt_337/03adopt_337-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/world/03adopt_337/03adopt_337-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/03/world/03adopt_337/03adopt_337-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/world/03adopt_337/03adopt_337-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Russians Renew Fury After Death o