'nyt://article/145869b2-d22d-5430-a94c-b89dd1e9280a', 'word_count': 1145, 'uri': 'nyt://article/145869b2-d22d-5430-a94c-b89dd1e9280a'}, {'abstract': 'Washington State is the latest college to enter the meat market, offering premium beef, alongside its longtime staple, Cougar Gold, cheese in a can.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/03/us/how-about-a-university-steak-with-your-sweatshirt.html', 'snippet': 'Washington State is the latest college to enter the meat market, offering premium beef, alongside its longtime staple, Cougar Gold, cheese in a can.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PULLMAN, Wash. — Tongs in hand, you lean over to take in the smoky sizzle of a steak on the grill, and your thoughts naturally turn to ... your alma mater?', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/us/MEAT-1/MEAT-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 397, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/03/us/MEAT-1/MEAT-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 397}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/us/MEAT-1/MEAT-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 677, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/us/MEAT-1/MEAT-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1354, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/us/MEAT-1/MEAT-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/03/us/MEAT-1/MEAT-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/us/MEAT-1/MEAT-1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A University Steak to Go With That Sweatshirt?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A University Steak to Go With That Sweatshirt?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Kirk', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Meat', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington State University', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-02T18:47:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kirk Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kirk', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b5f0a775-e600-512e-838a-0fae44a82228', 'word_count': 1073, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5f0a775-e600-512e-838a-0fae44a82228'}, {'abstract': 'Luigi Murenu used wispy double braids to create a windblown, schoolgirl hairstyle.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/02/backstage-beauty-report-viktor-rolf/', 'snippet': 'Luigi Murenu used wispy double braids to create a windblown, schoolgirl hairstyle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Luigi Murenu, the global creative director for John Frieda, evoked the “age of innocence” with the windblown, schoolgirl hairstyle he created for Viktor & Rolf on Saturday. John Frieda Luxurious Volume Volume Building Mousse (for a slight oomph), a messy middle part, and double braids (crossed and pinned along the bottom of the hairline) were the foundation. Murenu then put his palm right at the top of the model’s head and made a turntable motion to purposefully free a few strands and create extra wispiness. He likened this look to evoking meadows of wheat, and indeed it felt fresh from the fields.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Backstage Beauty Report | Viktor & Rolf', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-02T18:48:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Moroz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moroz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9588fedb-1830-5169-aeb6-e302e4e662fa', 'word_count': 102, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9588fedb-1830-5169-aeb6-e302e4e662fa'}, {'abstract': 'An obsessive drive to win is often cited as a trait of those who reach the pinnacle. But perhaps LeBron James has a better model: the happy athlete.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/03/sports/basketball/lebron-james-is-making-the-case-for-the-happy-athlete.html', 'snippet': 'An obsessive drive to win is often cited as a trait of those who reach the pinnacle. But perhaps LeBron James has a better model: the happy athlete.', 'lead_paragraph': "Is anyone having more fun these days than LeBron James? As he demolishes his opposition nightly, the N.B.A.'s resident megastar has bearhugged a fan who drained a halfcourt shot, elevated the pregame dunk line into an art form and joined his Miami Heat teammates in putting together their own version of a Harlem Shake video. (James is the shirtless one wearing the crown.)", 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 