', '_id': 'nyt://article/249e2a17-4b37-5dbb-86a5-d145f7ad1093', 'word_count': 1184, 'uri': 'nyt://article/249e2a17-4b37-5dbb-86a5-d145f7ad1093'}, {'abstract': 'In the widening world of classes taught online, new technologies are helping to ensure that students on distant laptops are doing their own work.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/03/technology/new-technologies-aim-to-foil-online-course-cheating.html', 'snippet': 'In the widening world of classes taught online, new technologies are helping to ensure that students on distant laptops are doing their own work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MILLIONS of students worldwide have signed up in the last year for MOOCs, short for massive open online courses — those free, Web-based classes available to one and all and taught by professors at Harvard, Duke, M.I.T. and other universities. ', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Keeping an Eye on Online Test-Takers', 'kicker': 'Novelties', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Keeping an Eye On Online Test-Takers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Learning', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cheating', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests and Examinations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Coursera Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ProctorU Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Software Secure', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-02T19:11:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anne Eisenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eisenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/07af064c-f026-579c-9d53-da573e2f1ad9', 'word_count': 924, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07af064c-f026-579c-9d53-da573e2f1ad9'}, {'abstract': 'In a new book, Benn Steil describes in detail the intellectual back-and-forth that played out in 1944 at the Bretton Woods monetary conference.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/03/business/bretton-woods-monetary-agreement-examined-in-a-new-book.html', 'snippet': 'In a new book, Benn Steil describes in detail the intellectual back-and-forth that played out in 1944 at the Bretton Woods monetary conference.', 'lead_paragraph': '“DOWNTON ABBEY” has tapped our inner Anglophile on a wide front. But Americans were not so besotted with Britain in the first half of the 20th century, when it was a powerhouse of international trade. Until World War II, Britain ran international finance to its liking, and Americans were thirsting to chop it down to size. We need to understand that to grasp the importance of the Bretton Woods monetary conference.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/business/03-SHELF/03-SHELF-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 882, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/03/business/03-SHELF/03-SHELF-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 882}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/business/03-SHELF/03-SHELF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 697, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/business/03-SHELF/03-SHELF-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1393, 'subType': 'superJumbo