stments, JPMorgan pressures brokers to sell the bank’s own products, current and former employees say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Everything is scripted for the brokers in an elite group at JPMorgan Chase: the sales pitches; the personal voice mail message; even the preferred desk candy, Glitterati Fruit & Berry.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Selling the Home Brand: A Look Inside an Elite JPMorgan Unit', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Selling the Home Brand: A Look Inside an Elite JPMorgan Unit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Financial Brokers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JPMorgan Chase & Company', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-02T22:56:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susanne Craig and Jessica Silver-Greenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Craig', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jessica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver-Greenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc808c93-11ee-58fd-a1cf-da7ca87a6a63', 'word_count': 1474, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc808c93-11ee-58fd-a1cf-da7ca87a6a63'}, {'abstract': 'Blurbing books with Samuel A. Donaldson.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/02/seven-blurbs-for-seven-biographies/', 'snippet': 'Blurbing books with Samuel A. Donaldson.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SUNDAY’S PUZZLE — One of the more interesting parts of the writing process is trying to find people who are willing to write what is called a blurb for your book. Blurbs are those quotes you see on the back cover that rave about what readers will find inside, and one trick to publishing a successful book — other than being J.K. Rowling — is to find people in the literary world who are impressive enough to help you move merchandise and are willing to say nice things about what you wrote. It’s not as easy as it looks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Seven Blurbs for Seven Biographies', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-02T23:00:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/203f63af-1429-585e-b91a-37c8dcff6ed3', 'word_count': 282, 'uri': 'nyt://article/203f63af-1429-585e-b91a-37c8dcff6ed3'}, {'abstract': 'The model transforms with makeup by Pat McGrath and hair by Luigi Murenu.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/02/model-morphosis-kremi-otashliyska-for-viktor-rolf/', 'snippet': 'The model transforms with makeup by Pat McGrath and hair by Luigi Murenu.', 'lead_paragraph': "(function($) {var data = chameleonData[0];var beforeAfterContainer = $('#nytmm_beforeAfter_wrapper4 .nytmm_beforeAfter_container');var options = {leftImage: data.images.left.leftImage,rightImage: data.images.right.rightImage,showFooter: data.footer.showFooter,leftCredit: data.images.left.leftCredit,rightCredit: data.images.right.rightCredit,caption: data.footer.caption,startPoint: data.images.startPoint,showButton: data.footer.button.showButton,leftButtonText: data.footer.bu