 presented at the M.I.T. Sloan and Sports Analytics Conference showcases a method for assessing basket protection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOSTON — For many basketball traditionalists, defense has been the go-to factor when denouncing the importance of basketball’s advanced statistics revolution. Hard to concretely quantify as an individual skill, defense and the metrics that would define it have lagged\xa0as numerous new-age offensive statistics have become more and more a part of day-to-day player evaluation. Kirk Goldsberry and Eric Weiss acknowledged as much in a research paper presented here at the annual M.I.T. Sloan and Sports Analytics Conference.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Searching for a New Way to Measure Defensive Production', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Statistics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Howard, Dwight', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'van Gundy, Stan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-03T06:04:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jake Appleman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jake', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Appleman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0bd56117-f60b-52d7-b9c5-bfca739d4170', 'word_count': 710, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0bd56117-f60b-52d7-b9c5-bfca739d4170'}, {'abstract': 'Best of long-form journalism this week.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/03/newswallah-long-reads-edition-19/', 'snippet': 'Best of long-form journalism this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Down to Earth, Alok Gupta analyzes the damaging effect violence has had on Bihar’s efforts to empower women and advance self-governance. The article argues that although the Bihar government announced a 50 percent quota for women in the panchayat (village council) in 2006, it has not helped in bringing about true empowerment for women. Instead, men force their homemaker wives to contest elections as the husbands continue to make all the decisions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Newswallah: Long Reads Edition', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jamaat-e-Islami', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tehelka', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bihar (India)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kashmir and Jammu (India)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-03T08:40:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neha Thirani Bagri', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neha', 'middlename': 'Thirani', 'lastname': 'Bagri', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dbc75423-b96c-5229-9894-ab91ee08c802', 'word_count': 672, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dbc75423-b96c-5229-9894-ab91ee08c802'}, {'abstract': 'A man and his pregnant wife were on the way to a doctor when they were fatally injured in a Brooklyn collision, but their son was delivered.', 'web_url': 'https://