& Style', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': "Women's Runway", 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/846b1528-a73c-5070-ac64-5e8b563d0c7e', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/846b1528-a73c-5070-ac64-5e8b563d0c7e'}, {'abstract': 'So where am I now, 13 years after my 2½-year-old son, Jacob, died because of a brain tumor? One thing I can say is that my junk mail has no idea where I am.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/03/a-high-functioning-bereaved-parent/', 'snippet': 'So where am I now, 13 years after my 2½-year-old son, Jacob, died because of a brain tumor? One thing I can say is that my junk mail has no idea where I am.', 'lead_paragraph': 'So where am I now, 13 years after my 2½-year-old son, Jacob, died because of a brain tumor? One thing I can say is that my junk mail has no idea where I am. The other day I threw out yet another letter offering to give us advice on Jacob’s college career, as well as a solicitation to re-subscribe to Highlights magazine. Obviously, Jacob is not going to college. And my surviving children are 11 and 13, a bit out of the Highlights demographic.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A High-Functioning Bereaved Parent', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Brain Cancer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Death and Dying', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-03T14:31:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy Shatan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shatan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f72d44cd-746c-5fd8-bf6e-5b982987ad0a', 'word_count': 918, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f72d44cd-746c-5fd8-bf6e-5b982987ad0a'}, {'abstract': 'Here, the private sector does it worse.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/03/government-and-medical-costs-continued/', 'snippet': 'Here, the private sector does it worse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ve spent some more time going through Steven Brill’s magnum opus on medical prices, and am even more amazed at (a) the quality of the reporting (b) his weird refusal to draw the obvious conclusion.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Government and Medical Costs, Continued', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-03T14:36:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7ea9f4b-a3e9-5c5e-962c-d92d98304159', 'word_count': 301, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7ea9f4b-a3e9-5c5e-962c-d92d98304159'}, {'abstract': 'Shirley MacLaine will reprise her role as the outspoken Martha Levinson in Season 4 of “Downton Abbey,” and several new characters will join the series. But one more star of the PBS/”Masterpiece” period drama has announced her exit.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/03/shirley-maclaine-will-return-to-downton-abbey-but-others-are-leaving-the-series/', 'snippet': 'Shirley MacLaine will reprise her role as the outspoken Martha Levinson in Season 4 of “Downton Abbey,” and several new characters will join the series. But one more star of the PBS/”Masterpiece” period drama has announced her exit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The revolving door of casting continues to spin at “Downton Abbey” as the popular PBS/”Masterpiece” period drama prepares for its fourth season. After a year in which the series lost the actors Dan Stevens, who played Matthew Crawley, and Jessica Brown Findlay, who played Lady Sybil (for reasons that the “Downton Abbey” creator Julian Fellowes explained here), PBS announced over the weekend that some new faces would join the series and that a familiar one was returning. But another well-known co-star has also announced her exit.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/arts/downton/downton-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 309, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/03/arts/downton/downton-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 309}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/arts/downton/downton-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 680, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/arts/downton/downton-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 680, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/03/arts/downton/downton-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/03/arts/downton/downton-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type':