//article/01836c58-4190-5cbf-9e89-87d5fbf5b43a'}, {'abstract': 'In Jean-Jacques Annaud’s “Day of the Falcon” warring Arab leaders in the early 20th century agree to a peace sealed with a buffer zone, but their pact is threatened by oil discovered there.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/04/movies/jean-jacques-annauds-day-of-the-falcon.html', 'snippet': 'In Jean-Jacques Annaud’s “Day of the Falcon” warring Arab leaders in the early 20th century agree to a peace sealed with a buffer zone, but their pact is threatened by oil discovered there.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Opened on Friday in New York; Los Angeles; Chicago; Detroit; Cincinnati; Orlando, Jacksonville and Tallahassee, Fla.; Kansas City, Mo.; and Charlotte, N.C.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/04/movies/04falcon/04falcon-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 367, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/04/movies/04falcon/04falcon-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 367}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/04/movies/04falcon/04falcon-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 626, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/04/movies/04falcon/04falcon-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1251, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/04/movies/04falcon/04falcon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/04/movies/04falcon/04falcon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/04/movies/04falcon/04falcon-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Blood Spills Over Black Gold', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Day of the Falcon', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Day of the Falcon (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANNAUD, JEAN-JACQUES', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-03T22:27:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Webster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Webster', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/53f7de2e-37e3-5151-a210-a9d63c718fcf', 'word_count': 282, 'uri': 'nyt://article/53f7de2e-37e3-5151-a210-a9d63c718fcf'}, {'abstract': 'Boy made a belated New York City debut on Friday; its album, “Mutual Friends,” is newly released here but has been available in Europe since 2011.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/04/arts/music/boy-joined-by-deniz-erarslan-at-joes-pub.html', 'snippet': 'Boy made a belated New York City debut on Friday; its album, “Mutual Friends,” is newly released here but has been available in Europe since 2011.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Of course, in 2013, a group called Boy is a duo of women: Valeska Steiner, from Zurich, and Sonja Glass, from Hamburg, Germany. But any subterfuge ends there. Boy writes and sings tuneful, friendly, forthright pop-folk songs about life and relationships. The songs detail small milestones: moving into a new apartment, working as a waitress, partying, flirting, fending off unwanted advances, savoring friendship and love. The lyrics are in idiomatic American English, cradled by melodies with a comfortable lilt and by Ms. Steiner’s sweet, unfailingly precise lead vocals. Boy’s songs make sleek craftsmanship sound guileless. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/04/arts/BOY/BOY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 304, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/04/arts/BOY/BOY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 304}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/04/arts/BOY/BOY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 519, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/04/arts/BOY/BOY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1038, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/04/arts/BOY/BOY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/04/arts/BOY/BOY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/04/arts/BOY/BOY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Life’s Minor Milestones, Served in Lush Detail', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Life’s Minor Milestones, Served in Lush Detail', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-03T22:31:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/09d9a1ab-dbf9-52a9-bd6b-8715ac1109b8', 'word_count': 384, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09d9a1ab-dbf9-52a9-bd6b-8715ac1109b8'}, {'abstract': '“The Staircase 2: Last Chance” is Jean-Xavier de Lestrade’s sequel to his eight-part documentary “The Staircase,” an examination of a sensational murder trial in Durham, N.C.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/04/arts/television/the-staircase-2-last-chance-on-sundance-channel.html', 'snippet': '“The Staircase 2: Last Chance” is Jean-Xavier de Lestrade’s sequel to his eight-part documentary “The Staircase,” an examination of a sensational murder trial in Durham, N.C.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A decade ago the French filmmaker Jean-Xavier de Lestrade spent a reported 650 hours filming his eight-part documentary “The Staircase,” an examination of a sensational murder trial in Durham, N.C. It was a highly accomplished true-crime thriller that also functioned as an evisceration of the American legal system and a “what can you do?” evocation of Southern cronyism and small-mindedness for a European audience.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/04/arts/staircase/staircase-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 507, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/04/arts/staircase/staircase-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 507}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/04/arts/staircase/staircase-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 865, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/04/arts/staircase/staircase-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1232, 'width': 1458, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/04/arts/staircase/staircase-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/04/arts/staircase/staircase-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/04/arts/staircase/staircase-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Unresolved Feelings Long After a Murder Trial’s End', 'kicker': 'Television Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Unresolved Feelings Long After a Murder Trial’s End', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sundance Channel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Lestrade, Jean-Xavier', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-03T22:36:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Hale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef08ea8e-d0ec-552b-8285-9006f6e2e70e', 'word_count': 493, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef08ea8e-d0ec-552b-8285-9006f6e2e70e'}, {'abstract': 'The indie singer-songwriter Ingrid Michaelson offered her take on love during an evening at Lincoln Center’s American Songbook series.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/04/arts/music/ingrid-michaelson-in-american-songbook-at-allen-room.html', 'snippet': 'The indie singer-songwriter Ingrid Michaelson offered her take on love during an evening at Lincoln Center’s American Songbook series.', 'lead_paragraph': '“No one’s gonna wait for you/so do it now.” That statement may sound like a slogan spouted by a motivational speaker, but as sung at the Allen Room on Saturday evening by the gifted indie singer-songwriter Ingrid Michaelson it conveyed the warmth and encouragement of a close friend sitting beside you in the back of a bus when you’re feeling discouraged. “Do It Now” was one of 16 originals she performed at the Allen Room as part of Lincoln Center’s American Songbook series. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/04/arts/INGRID/INGRID-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 362, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/04/arts/INGRID/INGRID-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 362}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/04/arts/INGRID/INGRID-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 618, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/04/arts/INGRID/INGRID-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1236, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}