is post, winning a hard-fought election against a candidate from the party of Prime Minister Yingluck Shinawatra.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BANGKOK — Defying predictions by pollsters, the incumbent governor of Bangkok retained his post on Sunday, winning a hard-fought election against a candidate from the party of Prime Minister Yingluck Shinawatra. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bangkok’s Governor Re-elected, Signaling Thailand’s Political Split', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bangkok’s Governor Re-elected, Signaling Thailand’s Political Split', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bangkok (Thailand)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yingluck Shinawatra', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-03T22:54:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Fuller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fuller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f2d18c3-ae82-5ad2-b461-128ffa63159f', 'word_count': 268, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f2d18c3-ae82-5ad2-b461-128ffa63159f'}, {'abstract': 'Before the main event at the 2nd Copenhagen Bridge Invitational over the weekend, there was a pro-am event for 52 pairs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/04/crosswords/bridge/bridge-2nd-copenhagen-bridge-invitational.html', 'snippet': 'Before the main event at the 2nd Copenhagen Bridge Invitational over the weekend, there was a pro-am event for 52 pairs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before the main event at the 2nd Copenhagen Bridge Invitational over the weekend, there was a pro-am event for 52 pairs. The winners could not really be termed pro-am, because the “am” was Helle Rasmussen, who has played four times on the Danish women’s team. Her partner was Michael Barel from Israel, who also won the invitational pair event with Yaniv Zack from Israel.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/04/crosswords/bridge/04card/04card-jumbo.gif', 'height': 500, 'width': 270, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/04/crosswords/bridge/04card/04card-superJumbo.gif', 'height': 500, 'width': 270, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/04/crosswords/bridge/04card/04card-thumbStandard.gif', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/04/crosswords/bridge/04card/04card-thumbStandard.gif', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/04/crosswords/bridge/04card/04card-thumbLarge.gif', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '2nd Copenhagen Bridge Invitational', 'kicker': 'Bridge', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bridge (Card Game)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cards and Card Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-03T22:55:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'subsection_name': 'Bridge', 'byline': {'original': 'By Phillip Alder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Phillip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3021b314-4677-55ad-a0a4-95ac9c7242aa', 'word_count': 306, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3021b314-4677-55ad-a0a4-95ac9c7242aa'}, {'abstract': 'Kent Tritle conducted a student presentation of Mendelssohn’s “Elijah” at the Manhattan School of Music.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/04/arts/music/elijah-at-the-manhattan-school-of-music.html', 'snippet': 'Kent Tritle conducted a student presentation of Mendelssohn’s “Elijah” at the Manhattan School of Music.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Happily, there are more ways than one to enjoy Mendelssohn’s “Elijah.” The most satisfying, perhaps, is to be swept along by a powerful bass or baritone in the title role of the combative prophet, as he roars through the work like the “mighty wind” of the text that “rent the mountains around.” Characterizations by the likes of Benjamin Luxon, Thomas Quasthoff and Bryn Terfel blaze in the memory.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/04/arts/ELIJIAH/ELIJIAH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 552, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/04/arts/ELIJIAH/ELIJIAH-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 552}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/04/arts/ELIJIAH/ELIJIAH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 943, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/04/arts/ELIJIAH/