9f-5c21-a0fa-c2baea4c2a98', 'word_count': 1455, 'uri': 'nyt://article/31f7bb09-739f-5c21-a0fa-c2baea4c2a98'}, {'abstract': 'Mrs. Obama may have been criticized for handing out the Best Picture award at the Oscars, but her appearance on NBC’s “Late Night With Jimmy Fallon” has been immensely popular.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/03/michelle-obamas-mom-dancing-on-jimmy-fallon-is-a-youtube-hit/', 'snippet': 'Mrs. Obama may have been criticized for handing out the Best Picture award at the Oscars, but her appearance on NBC’s “Late Night With Jimmy Fallon” has been immensely popular.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Michelle Obama may have drawn some criticism, especially in conservative circles, for showing up a week ago to hand out the Best Picture award at the Oscars. But interest in the first lady is surely intense, as proved by the continuing phenomenon of her guest appearance on NBC’s “Late Night With Jimmy Fallon.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'First Lady’s Dance Moves Catch Fire on the Web', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-04T02:33:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Media', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By BILL CARTER', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'CARTER', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0b0f5ab-c4f7-576e-8841-f97093dbfad9', 'word_count': 447, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0b0f5ab-c4f7-576e-8841-f97093dbfad9'}, {'abstract': 'Where the top scorers were successful on the field.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2013/03/03/sports/soccer/goals.html', 'snippet': 'Where the top scorers were successful on the field.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Where the top scorers were successful on the field.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shots and Goals from the Premier League’s Top Scorers This Season', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-04T02:37:21+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/a1dcc213-539f-5d8b-9664-e305be415ca1', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/a1dcc213-539f-5d8b-9664-e305be415ca1'}, {'abstract': 'Regulators need to crack down on payday lenders’ raiding checking accounts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/04/opinion/bleeding-the-borrower-dry.html', 'snippet': 'Regulators need to crack down on payday lenders’ raiding checking accounts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York is one of 15 states that have banned the predatory, high-interest loans that payday lenders commonly use to pillage low-income borrowers. But offshore lenders increasingly get around state laws by issuing predatory loans over the Internet. Worse still, as the Times’s Jessica Silver-Greenberg reported recently, banks in the state are profiting from the loans by allowing the Internet lenders to automatically withdraw payments from the borrower’s account, in some cases without his or her permission. When the borrowers — or their lenders — overdraw on the accounts, the banks get to collect fat overdraft fees. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bleeding the Borrower Dry', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bleeding the Borrower Dry', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Payday Loans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-04T02:38:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8844a2b-1eba-5650-9e53-19f77a8998e1', 'word_count': 576, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8844a2b-1eba-5650-9e53-19f77a8998e1'}, {'abstract': 'After a successful showing in last week’s election, Beppe Grillo, a comedian turned activist, is being courted by Italy’s traditional political players, with whom he has refused to play ball.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/04/world/europe/beppe-grillo-italys-gadfly-reflects-a-movement.html', 'snippet': 'After a successful showing in last week’s election, Beppe Grillo, a comedian turned activist, is being courted by Italy’s traditional political players, with whom he has refused to play ball.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — A populist with wild hair, a booming voice and untucked shirts, Beppe Grillo now holds the fate of Italy — and to some extent Europe — in his hands.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/04/world/europe/ITALY/ITALY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 404, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/04/world/europe/ITALY/ITALY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 404}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images