cted by the Oscar-winning filmmakers Karen Goodman and Kirk Simon and featuring sessions between acclaimed artists and students, focuses on Mr. Guare (above) — the author of plays including “A Free Man of Color,” “The House of Blue Leaves” and “Six Degrees of Separation” — as he advises writers at a workshop in Rome. Their assignment is to wander the city for inspiration and then compose a monologue drawing on their experiences in the voice of an imagined character, all while being encouraged by Mr. Guare to pursue “weird vibes” and “go into the darkness.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Monday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-04T05:15:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/e3c03a71-8c7f-5eea-ba1c-84a51ed7a307', 'word_count': 723, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e3c03a71-8c7f-5eea-ba1c-84a51ed7a307'}, {'abstract': 'A young churchgoer watches a Pentecostal minister slowly become more accepting of gays.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/04/booming/dont-ask-dont-tell-in-the-black-church.html', 'snippet': 'A young churchgoer watches a Pentecostal minister slowly become more accepting of gays.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’d been assigned to write a story for Loop21.com, an online African-American publication, about how pastors at black churches were handling homosexuality with their congregations. I’d picked one of my friend’s father to interview, a Pentecostal minister in Chicago.', 'source': 'The 