, 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf3acc73-1b16-544c-bf09-3e28ac11a7e4', 'word_count': 1117, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf3acc73-1b16-544c-bf09-3e28ac11a7e4'}, {'abstract': 'Riccardo Tisci’s Givenchy show on Sunday was very affecting, with a firm grasp of the Givenchy woman: a layered personality and plenty of grit.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/04/givenchys-layers-of-emotion/', 'snippet': 'Riccardo Tisci’s Givenchy show on Sunday was very affecting, with a firm grasp of the Givenchy woman: a layered personality and plenty of grit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Paris collections are giving women — and anyone who monitors fashion as closely as the Vatican and the N.F.L. draft — a lot to obsess over. That’s quite a change from Milan, where many of us were wishing the Italians could get their shows done in fewer days. (When people are discussing the schedule, and not the clothes, you know there’s a problem.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Givenchy’s Layers of Emotion', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tisci, Riccardo', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Givenchy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-04T11:56:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b958da2a-2108-5d02-8b2b-d7f64a72e244', 'word_count': 394, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b958da2a-2108-5d02-8b2b-d7f64a72e244'}, {'abstract': 'I thought it would fast-track me to adulthood, but what Adderall gave me was nothing compared to what it took away.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/04/the-last-all-nighter/', 'snippet': 'I thought it would fast-track me to adulthood, but what Adderall gave me was nothing compared to what it took away.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first time I took Adderall I didn’t think twice. It was 2007. I was in my last year at U.C.L.A., where I had come down with a bad case of senioritis, and found myself cramming for finals. I bought it from a gangly kid with yellow skin and bags under his eyes who lived in the dorms. His hair was stringy. There were papers on the floor and piles of clothes on all the furniture in the room. Above his desk was a poster of John Belushi from “Animal House,” chugging a bottle of Jack Daniels and wearing a sweatshirt that read COLLEGE. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Last All-Nighter', 'kicker': 'Anxiety', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADDERALL (DRUG)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Anxiety and Stress', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fear (Emotion)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-04T12:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Miller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Miller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/70024a28-6688-5dff-89d4-b638277553cc', 'word_count': 1689, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70024a28-6688-5dff-89d4-b638277553cc'}, {'abstract': 'The author of one of the magazine’s features this week talks about his voyages on Amtrak.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/04/behind-the-story-nathaniel-rich-on-kooky-train-travelers-and-why-he-always-shaves-before-reporting/', 'snippet': 'The author of one of the magazine’s features this week talks about his voyages on Amtrak.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nathaniel Rich wrote a feature article in this past weekend’s Voyages issue about long-distance train travel. Rich is the author of the novel “The Mayor’s Tongue”; his second novel will be published by Farrar, Straus & Giroux this spring. Last year he wrote cover stories for the magazine about a Japanese scientist who studies jellyfish and the Lower Ninth Ward in New Orleans.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/03/26/magazine/26-nathanielrichphoto/26-nathanielrichphoto-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/03/26/magazine/26-nathanielrichphoto/26-nathanielrichphoto-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/03/26/magazine/26-nathanielrichphoto/26-nathanielrichphoto-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/03/26/magazine/26-nathanielrichphoto/26-nathanielrichphoto-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2000, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/03/26/magazine/26-nathanielrichphoto/26-nathanielrichphoto-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'heig