oration and production.', 'lead_paragraph': '8:55 p.m. | Updated  The Hess truck may be going in a yard sale.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hess to Sell Gas Stations as Part of a Shift in Strategy', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hess to Sell Gas Stations As Part of Strategy Shift', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hess, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Elliott Management Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hess Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Relational Investors LLC', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-04T13:39:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6f67944-00a6-51e4-ab1f-d6ce30f4df4b', 'word_count': 694, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6f67944-00a6-51e4-ab1f-d6ce30f4df4b'}, {'abstract': 'Vice magazine was behind Dennis Rodman’s high-profile trip to North Korea; “The Walking Dead” is killing networks in the ratings; and a photojournalists in Oakland, Calif., have become victims of a rash of robberies.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/04/the-breakfast-meeting-how-rodman-wound-up-in-north-korea-and-amc-lurches-ahead-in-ratings/', 'snippet': 'Vice magazine was behind Dennis Rodman’s high-profile trip to North Korea; “The Walking Dead” is killing networks in the ratings; and a photojournalists in Oakland, Calif., have become victims of a rash of robberies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Vice, a print magazine that is producing a TV newsmagazine that will debut on HBO in April, made international news by arranging a basketball game featuring flamboyant former N.B.A. player Dennis Rodman and three Harlem Globetrotters players before Kim Jong-un, in North Korea, Brian Stelter writes. Mr. Rodman and Vice’s film crew are the first Americans to meet the North Korean ruler since he inherited power from his father in 2011. Pundits debated on television and online over who gained more from the interaction, Vice or the North Korean government, and reporters at the State Department wanted to know why Mr. Rodman, who has returned to the United States, was not debriefed about his visit with Mr. Kim, whom he called a “friend.” Vice had no assurance that Mr. Kim would watch the game, but were familiar with his love of basketball, especially the Chicago Bulls.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting: How Rodman Wound Up in North Korea, and AMC Lurches Ahead in Ratings', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-04T13:41:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel E. Slotnik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Slotnik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/adb5af50-c6e9-59e9-87f2-1a93e5321205', 'word_count': 650, 'uri': 'nyt://article/adb5af50-c6e9-59e9-87f2-1a93e5321205'}, {'abstract': 'More than 40 Syrian soldiers who had sought temporary safety in Iraq were killed on Monday in an ambush, in the most serious spillover of violence into Iraq since the Syrian conflict began.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/05/world/middleeast/fighting-escalates-in-syrian-city-opposition-says.html', 'snippet': 'More than 40 Syrian soldiers who had sought temporary safety in Iraq were killed on Monday in an ambush, in the most serious spillover of violence into Iraq since the Syrian conflict began.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BAGHDAD — More than 40 Syrian soldiers who had sought temporary safety in Iraq from rebel fighters along the border were killed on Monday in an attack by unidentified gunmen as the Iraqi military was transporting the soldiers back to Syria in a bus convoy, the Iraqi government said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/world/middleeast/05syria_cnd/05syria_cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/05/world/middleeast/05syria_cnd/05syria_cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/world/middleeast/05syria_cnd/05syria_cnd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/world/middleeast/05syria_cnd/05syria_cnd-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/world/middleeast/05syria_cnd/05syria_cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/05/world/middleeast/05syria_cnd/05syria_cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnail