de with its 100th anniversary, the manufacturer of luxurious leather furniture has officially inaugurated its museum in central Italy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To coincide with its 100th anniversary, Poltrona Frau, the manufacturer known for its luxurious leather furniture, has officially inaugurated its museum in the central Italian town of Tolentino, its headquarters since the early 1960s. Designed by Michele De Lucchi, the Milan architect who was a key figure in radical design movements like Memphis, the Poltrona Frau Museum presents both the company’s history and the processes involved in making its products.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sitting Pretty | The Poltrona Frau Museum', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chairs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Leather and Leather Goods', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-04T14:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pilar Viladas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pilar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Viladas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5081090d-0626-56f6-ae4a-40837a992e3e', 'word_count': 176, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5081090d-0626-56f6-ae4a-40837a992e3e'}, {'abstract': '“Bull,” a drama about office politics by the British playwright Mike Bartlett (“The Cockfight Play”), will have its New York premiere in the Brits Off Broadway festival at 59E59 Theaters.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/04/brits-off-broadway-adds-bull-to-slate/', 'snippet': '“Bull,” a drama about office politics by the British playwright Mike Bartlett (“The Cockfight Play”), will have its New York premiere in the Brits Off Broadway festival at 59E59 Theaters.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Bull,” a drama about office politics by the British playwright Mike Bartlett (“The Cockfight Play”), will have its New York premiere in the Brits Off Broadway festival at 59E59 Theaters, the theater is to announce on Monday. The play, which is to begin performances on April 25, recently completed a run at the Crucible Studio in Sheffield, England, where it received good reviews. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Brits Off Broadway Adds ‘Bull’ to Slate', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Brits Off Broadway Festival', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bartlett, Mike', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': '59E59 THEATERS', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-04T14:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven McElroy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McElroy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/74bb2a00-d6a1-52d2-a480-94d4ceb615b7', 'word_count': 243, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74bb2a00-d6a1-52d2-a480-94d4ceb615b7'}, {'abstract': 'The infant had been delivered prematurely after his mother and father were killed in a car crash in Brooklyn.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/05/nyregion/baby-whose-parents-were-killed-in-crash-also-dies.html', 'snippet': 'The infant had been delivered prematurely after his mother and father were killed in a car crash in Brooklyn.', 'lead_paragraph': 