tion': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/da5e0d46-590a-5f55-8e73-d8540e93b21e', 'word_count': 275, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da5e0d46-590a-5f55-8e73-d8540e93b21e'}, {'abstract': 'A group considered what, if anything, a fellow business owner could do to address a dissatisfying experience with a software supplier at a late stage.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/04/when-software-vendors-take-their-time/', 'snippet': 'A group considered what, if anything, a fellow business owner could do to address a dissatisfying experience with a software supplier at a late stage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the last meeting of the She Owns It business group, Susan Parker talked about the frustrating process of switching to new software to run her company, Bari Jay. After more than a year, the project, which was supposed to take three months, is still unfinished — although she hopes the new software will be live within a month. Although she likes the software, with hindsight she says that she would never work with this particular software development company again. But where does that leave her now?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Software Vendors Take Their Time', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-04T16:00:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adriana Gardella', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adriana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gardella', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://ar