r', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/94c673c6-38c1-51ec-ac65-8a3fb345220c', 'word_count': 479, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94c673c6-38c1-51ec-ac65-8a3fb345220c'}, {'abstract': 'A quick and easy bread with a rich and nutty taste.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/07/health/whole-wheat-irish-soda-bread-recipes-for-health.html', 'snippet': 'A quick and easy bread with a rich and nutty taste.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you have ever been to Ireland you have tasted soda bread, a moist, easy to make bread that is rich and nutty tasting when made with whole wheat flour. It is a very quick and easy bread to make as long as you are willing to get your hands sticky. When you pull the bread from the oven wrap it loosely in a kitchen towel and allow to cool. This softens the crust and makes it easier to cut.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/science/07recipehealth/07recipehealth-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 407, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/05/science/07recipehealth/07recipehealth-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 407}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/science/07recipehealth/07recipehealth-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 695, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/science/07recipehealth/07recipehealth-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1389, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/science/07recipehealth/07recipehealth-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/05/science/07recipehealth/07recipehealth-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/science/07recipehealth/07recipehealth-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Whole Wheat Irish Soda Bread With Bulgur', 'kicker': 'Recipes for Health', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-04T17:28:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martha Rose Shulman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martha', 'middlename': 'Rose', 'lastname': 'Shulman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'recipe', '_id': 'nyt://article/188fcdda-54ad-57dd-8a77-30882d6d04e6', 'word_count': 558, 'uri': 'nyt://article/188fcdda-54ad-57dd-8a77-30882d6d04e6'}, {'abstract': 'Seen at Paris Fashion Week: ladylike hemlines were coupled with bulky knits at Celine, Dries Van Noten and Jil Sander.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/04/threes-a-trend-skirts-and-sweaters/', 'snippet': 'Seen at Paris Fashion Week: ladylike hemlines were coupled with bulky knits at Celine, Dries Van Noten and Jil Sander.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Paris, designers modernized their approach to ladylike hemlines with skirts hitting just at the calf. Pairing them with bulky knits appeared fresh instead of frumpy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Three’s a Trend | Skirts and Sweaters', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-04T17:34:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/18114221-7b9d-5f68-9429-5fe59450bab5', 'word_count': 26, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18114221-7b9d-5f68-9429-5fe59450bab5'}, {'abstract': 'A simple skillet supper with a savory mixture of mushrooms and spinach.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/08/health/bulgur-with-middle-eastern-seasoning-recipes-for-health.html', 'snippet': 'A simple skillet supper with a savory mixture of mushrooms and spinach.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This is a simple skillet supper, a bowl of bulgur topped with a savory mixture of mushrooms and spinach. It gets a final flourish of dukkah, a Middle Eastern seasoning made with toasted nuts (or in some places chickpea flour), seeds and spices that is as much a snack as it is a seasoning; a favorite way to eat dukkah is to dip vegetables or bread into olive oil and then into the dukkah. There are many versions of the mix. Ana Sortun, a chef at Oleana in Cambridge, Mass., and the author of “Spices: Flavors of the Eastern Mediterranean,” adds coconut to hers. The recipe for the dukkah makes more than you will need for this meal, but it keeps well (I keep mine in the freezer) and it is great to have on hand.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/science/08recipehealth/08recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/05/science/08recipehealth/08recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/science/08recipehealth/08recipehealth-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/science/08recipehealth/08recipehealth-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/science/08recipehealth/08recipehealth-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/05/science/08recipehealth/08recipehealth-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/science/08recipehealth/08recipehealth-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bulgur Bowl With Spinach, Mushrooms and Middle Eastern Nut and Spice Seasoning', 'kicker': 'Recipes for Health', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wheat', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Spinach', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mushrooms', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-04T17:39:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martha Rose Shulman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martha', 'middlename': 'Rose', 'lastname': 'Shulman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'recipe', '_id': 'nyt://article/bae58760-2f5a-50ca-a06a-175be46d36e5', 'word_count': 806, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bae58760-2f5a-50ca-a06a-175be46d36e5'}, {'abstract': 'A selection of events for this week.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/04/dining-calendar-7/', 'snippet': 'A selection of events for this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bento Boxes', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dining Calendar', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-04T17:42:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bao Ong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bao', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/567b9f62-660b-5ea4-bebe-8989fcefaa92', 'word_count': 577, 'uri': 'nyt://article/567b9f62-660b-5ea4-bebe-8989fcefaa92'}, {'abstract': 'If you lose a dispute over negative information in your credit report, you can still include a short statement on the report explaining the circumstances.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/04/tips-for-disputing-credit-report-errors/', 'snippet': 'If you lose a dispute over negative information in your credit report, you can still include a short statement on the report explaining the circumstances.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Checking the accuracy of your credit report is important, given recent reports that 5 percent of consumers may have errors in their reports that can result in higher interest rates on a loan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tips for Disputing Credit Report Errors', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Scores', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AnnualCreditReport.com', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Equifax Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Experian Group Ltd', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TransUnion LLC', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-04T17:46:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/73ffd554-d75a-5dfb-b3f4-9ae80521a1ff', 'word_count': 564, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73ffd554-d75a-5dfb-b3f4-9ae80521a1ff'}, {'abstract': 'Karl Ove Knausgaard’s beautiful, meditative essay in this past weekend’s issue suggests nothing of the controversy that surrounded the publication of his novel in Norway.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/04/northern-exposure/', 'snippet': 'Karl Ove Knausgaard’s beautiful, meditative essay in this past weekend’s issue suggests nothing of the controversy that surrounded the publication of his novel in Norway.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The essay that accompanies Simon Norfolk’s photographs of the northern lights in this past weekend’s Voyages issue was written by the Norwegian novelist Karl Ove Knausgaard. A beautiful, meditative piece, it suggests nothing of the controversy that surrounded the publication of Knausgaard’s six-volume autobiographical novel in Norway. Lauded by critics as a literary feat (the first volume appeared in English last summer), the book played less well among Knausgaard’s own family members. Part fiction, part memoir, “Min Kamp,” or “My Struggle” as it is known in English, included not just unflinching descriptions of his father’s alcoholism and grandmother’s incontinence but also revealing details about his ex- and his current wife. Some took revenge (the ex made a radio documentary); others sued (the uncle succeeded in getting his family members’ names changed before publication). As The Guardian noted last March, the question of whether Knausgaard had crossed a line became a national obsession:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/04/magazine/04-karl-ove/04-karl-ove-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 715, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/04/magazine/04-karl-ove/04-karl-ove-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 715}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/04/magazine/04-karl-ove/04-karl-ove-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 860, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/04/magazine/04-karl-ove/04-karl-ove-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1719, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/04/magazine/04-karl-ove/04-karl-ove-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/04/magazine/04-karl-ove/04-karl-ove-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/04/magazine/04-karl-ove/04-karl-ove-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Northern Exposure', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Knausgaard, Karl Ove', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-04T17:51:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sheila Glaser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sheila', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Glaser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ab86163-2d8d-5289-9144-06ff6ef863b1', 'word_count': 283, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ab86163-2d8d-5289-9144-06ff6ef863b1'}, {'abstract': 'Tony Vaccaro, who took as many as 8,000 photographs during World War II, was one of about 50 veterans honored along with Holocaust survivors on Sunday. “I felt the world had to see it,” he said.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/04/viewing-world-war-ii-through-a-soldiers-camera-lens/', 'snippet': 'Tony Vaccaro, who took as many as 8,000 photographs during World War II, was one of about 50 veterans honored along with Holocaust survivors on Sunday. “I felt the world had to see it,” he said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tony Vaccaro wanted to become a foreign correspondent, but after being raised in Italy, he returned to the United States less than proficient in English. One of his teachers at Isaac E. Young High School in New Rochelle, N.Y., suggested he become a photographer instead. (He joined a camera club begun by his science teacher, Bertram L. Lewis.) He worked as a caddy to afford a $47.50 American-made Argus C2 camera, intent on taking it with him when he went to war.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/nyregion/04cityroom-photog/04cityroom-photog-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 442, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/05/nyregion/04cityroom-photog/04cityroom-photog-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 442}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/nyregion/04cityroom-photog/04cityroom-photog-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 755, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/nyregion/04cityroom-photog/04cityroom-photog-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1509, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/nyregion/04cityroom-photog/04cityroom-photog-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/05/nyregion/04cityroom-photog/04cityroom-photog-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/nyregion/04cityroom-photog/04cityroom-photog-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Viewing World War II Through a Soldier’s Camera Lens', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-04T17:54:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Roberts', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roberts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/905788d6-877c-5f2b-805d-7151e8af432e', 'word_count': 657, 'uri': 'nyt://article/905788d6-877c-5f2b-805d-7151e8af432e'}, {'abstract': 'Wrongfully foreclosed on? We want to hear from you.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/04/are-you-a-member-of-the-military-who-illegally-lost-your-home-to-foreclosure/', 'snippet': 'Wrongfully foreclosed on? We want to hear from you.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jessica Silver-Greenberg and Ben Protess have a shocking story in the Times today about how, in the course of their foreclosure review, the big bank servicing departments discovered they had foreclosed on at least 700 members of the military, in clear violation of the Servicemembers Civil Relief Act.\xa0The story also reported that some two dozen homeowners lost their homes in foreclosure proceedings despite being current on their mortgages.\xa0(The story also describes, in damning detail, the pathetically weak settlement recently negotiated – if you can call it that – by the Office of the Comptroller of the Currency, the nation’s top bank regulator.\xa0But let’s leave that for another day.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Are You a Member of the Military Who Illegally Lost Your Home to Foreclosure?', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub'