013/03/04/false-modesty-in-decline-in-european-bank-bonuses/', 'snippet': 'One might have expected European bank bosses to show more contrition in the year that the Libor scandal erupted, the author writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'European banks were asking for a slap when new rules on pay were unveiled last week. Just consider this year’s bonus round. Lower payouts had been predicted, reflecting the relative weakness of the business environment. In fact, pay for the average investment bank employee at Europe’s top four firms fell just 2 percent last year, to $313,000. Deferred awards cloud the picture, but there’s little sign of pay restraint.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'False Modesty in Decline in European Bank Bonuses', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bonuses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Libor (London Interbank Offered Rate)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-04T18:22:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dominic Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dominic', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/52c41c0f-512b-5ab6-a0fa-71db4da393d9', 'word_count': 384, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52c41c0f-512b-5ab6-a0fa-71db4da393d9'}, {'abstract': 'Mark Sanford, who turned the phrase “hiking the Appalachian Trail” into a euphemism for an affair, is one of 18 candidates vying for a Congressional seat in South Carolina.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/20