e Gloss from the outer corner of the eye outward toward the temples, in a thick stripe that tapered toward the hairline, for “a high-gloss finish.” To add a bit of unexpected sparkle, Garland dabbed the same gloss lightly upon the cupid’s bow, following the M of the upper lip. “You don’t really see it, but it’s making the mouth feel fuller,” she said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Backstage Beauty Report | Giambattista Valli', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-04T20:28:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Moroz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moroz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe1ca615-cc9e-569a-8d14-e99f3781a072', 'word_count': 89, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe1ca615-cc9e-569a-8d14-e99f3781a072'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama’s cabinet choices on environment and energy reflect his middle-path approach to governing.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/04/obamas-all-of-the-above-energy-and-environment-nominees/', 'snippet': 'President Obama’s cabinet choices on environment and energy reflect his middle-path approach to governing.', 'lead_paragraph': '7:06 p.m. | See addendum for sample of Twitter commentary |', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama’s ‘All of the Above’ Energy and Environment Nominees', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Pollution', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coal', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 