deadline, a steep drop from the 21 players who were tagged last season. The decline is likely an indication that even with a modest rise in the salary cap this year, most teams – many of which have gone on a wave of restructuring contracts in recent days to create cap space — found it too expensive to use the tag on any but the most critical players. This came a year after tag numbers that were reduced from the pre-lockout years were considered more palatable.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Eight Teams Use Franchise Tag', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-04T22:20:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judy Battista', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Battista', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/26f92c1a-59e4-5cd0-a3b0-228122e84f83', 'word_count': 442, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26f92c1a-59e4-5cd0-a3b0-228122e84f83'}, {'abstract': 'Brian Cashman sustained his first injury from one of his adventurous extracurricular activities when he broke his right fibula jumping out of a plane for charity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/05/sports/baseball/yankees-cashman-breaks-ankle-after-jumping-out-of-plane.html', 'snippet': 'Brian Cashman sustained his first injury from one of his adventurous extracurricular activities when he broke his right fibula jumping out of a plane for charity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TAMPA, Fla. — Brian Cashman has often said that being the general manager of the Yankees is much harder than any of the high-altitude, thrill-seeking challenges he has undertaken in rece