d', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/efb1359a-7d5d-5f7a-a049-e1b805e35a24', 'word_count': 968, 'uri': 'nyt://article/efb1359a-7d5d-5f7a-a049-e1b805e35a24'}, {'abstract': 'Not my finest hour.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/04/urk-charlie-rose-edition/', 'snippet': 'Not my finest hour.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Well, we’ll see how it comes out after editing, but I feel that I just had my Denver debate moment: I was tired, cranky, and unready for the blizzard of misleading factoids and diversionary stuff (In 1997 you said that the aging population was a big problem! When Social Security was founded life expectancy was only 62!) Oh, and I wasn’t prepared for Joe Scarborough’s slipperiness about what he actually advocates (he’s for more spending in the near term? Who knew?)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Urk, Charlie Rose Edition', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-04T22:47:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aae943eb-0613-55a0-a92a-b7cd1eae7bf7', 'word_count': 125, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aae943eb-0613-55a0-a92a-b7cd1eae7bf7'}, {'abstract': 'China Gansu Dance Theater, from northwest China, brings a Silk Road tale to the Koch Theater.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/05/arts/dance/china-gansu-dance-theater-tells-a-silk-road-story.html', 'snippet': 'China Gansu Dance Theater, from northwest China, brings a Silk Road tale to the Koch Theater.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Mogao caves near the oasis of Dunhuang, in the deserts of the northwestern Chinese province of Gansu, are one of the world’s great sites of Buddhist art. By a junction of the ancient Silk Road, they are testament to China’s engagement with cultures to its west. “Silk Road,” the dance drama presented by the China Gansu Dance Theater at the David H. Koch Theater last week, is an example of the specific way that some Chinese artists can turn their great culture into kitsch. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/arts/GANSU/GANSU-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 353, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/05/arts/GANSU/GANSU-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 353}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/arts/GANSU/GANSU-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 603, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/arts/GANSU/GANSU-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1206, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/arts/GANSU/GANSU-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/05/arts/GANSU/GANSU-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/arts/GANSU/GANSU-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Back and Forth Along an Ancient Trade Route', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Back and Forth Along an Ancient Trade Route', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-04T22:48:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Seibert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Seibert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/8fd50d1e-40d4-5dd7-8509-b9d178b1e413', 'word_count': 507, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8fd50d1e-40d4-5dd7-8509-b9d178b1e413'}, {'abstract': 'Twitter photos from rallies at Oberlin College after a series of racist, antigay and anti-Semitic incidents on campus.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/04/photos-of-oberlin-college-students-rallying-against-hate-incidents/', 'snippet': 'Twitter photos from rallies at Oberlin College after a series of racist, antigay and anti-Semitic incidents on campus.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As my colleague Richard Pérez-Peña reports, Oberlin College in Ohio canceled classes Monday for a “day of solidarity” after a person wearing what appeared to be a Ku Klux Klan-style white hood and robe was spotted on campus early Monday near the college’s Afrikan Heritage House.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Photos of Oberlin College Students Rallying Against Hate Incidents', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oberlin College', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ohio', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-04T22:48:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5859ac57-e558-5a80-b0aa-8328005642d1', 'word_count': 570, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5859ac57-e558-5a80-b0aa-8328005642d1'}, {'abstract': 'The Stella McCartney woman is unleashing her inner tomboy for fall.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/04/the-daily-do-stella-mccartney/', 'snippet': 'The Stella McCartney woman is unleashing her inner tomboy for fall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Armed in a voluminous overcoat with pinstripes and baseball cap, the Stella McCartney woman is unleashing her inner tomboy for fall. The borrowed from the boy look is complete with hair that requires zero effort — a simple low ponytail. The message in hair this week is: the less maintenance, the better.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Daily Do | Stella McCartney', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-04T22:49:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Malina Joseph Gilchrist', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Malina', 'middlename': 'Joseph', 'lastname': 'Gilchrist', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2447c18-7b94-5a45-9dd4-48a3d38e7369', 'word_count': 52, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2447c18-7b94-5a45-9dd4-48a3d38e7369'}, {'abstract': 'Will act for herring: The director of “Breakfast at Tiffany’s,” coming to Broadway, is facing predictable challenges in casting — and rehearsing — the onstage cat.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/05/theater/herding-cats-in-breakfast-at-tiffanys-on-broadway.html', 'snippet': 'Will act for herring: The director of “Breakfast at Tiffany’s,” coming to Broadway, is facing predictable challenges in casting — and rehearsing — the onstage cat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Four days before previews, the cast and crew of the new Broadway version of “Breakfast at Tiffany’s” were putting the finishing touches on the show’s blocking, lighting and costumes. But on this final day of February, there remained one gaping hole: the director still hadn’t cast the role of Holly Golightly’s cat. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/arts/BREAKFAST/BREAKFAST-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 367, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/05/arts/BREAKFAST/BREAKFAST-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 367}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/arts/BREAKFAST/BREAKFAST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 627, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/arts/BREAKFAST/BREAKFAST-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1253, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/arts/BREAKFAST/BREAKFAST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/05/arts/BREAKFAST/BREAKFAST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/arts/BREAKFAST/BREAKFAST-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Like Herding Cats? Well, Try It on Broadway', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Like Herding Cats? Well, Try It on Broadway', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clifford, Stephanie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cats', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "Breakfast at Tiffany's (Play)", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mathias, Sean', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greenberg, Richard', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-04T22:49:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Clifford', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clifford', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e95e741-054e-5881-8d35-0fd36ef6cd0c', 'word_count': 1315, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e95e741-054e-5881-8d35-0fd36ef6cd0c'}, {'abstract': 'In this installment of Jennifer Koh’s Bach and Beyond series — in which she assesses Bach’s impact on other artists — she played a Bach sonata and partita, as well as work by Phil Kline and Bartok.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/05/arts/music/jennifer-koh-in-bach-and-beyond-at-92nd-street-y.html', 'snippet': 'In this installment of Jennifer Koh’s Bach and Beyond series — in which she assesses Bach’s impact on other artists — she played a Bach sonata and partita, as well as work by Phil Kline and Bartok.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The six unaccompanied Sonatas and Partitas for violin that Bach composed during the first two decades of the 18th century have long represented an Everest that every serious violinist feels compelled to climb. The challenges are considerable, not least because Bach provides few explicit interpretive directions. And for some players, Bach’s monumental set is less a peak to be surmounted than a journey that warrants return excursions and encourages consideration of manifold paths. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/arts/05KOH/05KOH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 353, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/05/arts/05KOH/05KOH-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 353}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/arts/05KOH/05KOH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 602, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/arts/05KOH/05KOH-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1203, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/arts/05KOH/05KOH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/05/arts/05KOH/05KOH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/arts/05KOH/05KOH-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'S