ey once dominated.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/05/science/particle-physicists-in-us-worry-about-being-left-behind.html', 'snippet': 'American scientists are wondering what role, if any, they will play in the future in high-energy physics — the search for the fundamental particles and forces of nature — a field they once dominated.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Are the glory days of American physics over?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Particle Physicists in U.S. Worry About Being Left Behind', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Particle Physicists in U.S. Worry About Being Left Behind', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Particle Accelerators', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Higgs Boson', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Large Hadron Collider', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Physics', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-05T00:37:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dennis Overbye', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dennis', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Overbye', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/67c9c75d-7fc3-5a65-9956-e1b606ade278', 'word_count': 1130, 'uri': 'nyt://article/67c9c75d-7fc3-5a65-9956-e1b606ade278'}, {'abstract': 'It will take more work and analysis before physicists have the cold numbers that clinch the case that the new particle announced last July is in fact the long-lost Higgs boson.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/05/science/all-signs-point-to-higgs-boson-but-still-waiting-for-scientific-certainty.html', 'snippet': 'It will take more work and analysis before physicists have the cold numbers that clinch the case that the new particle announced last July is in fact the long-lost Higgs boson.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In their bones, physicists feel it is the long-lost Higgs boson, but in science, feelings take second place to data. So these same physicists admit that it will take more work and analysis before they will have the cold numbers that clinch the case that the new particle announced on July 4 last year is in fact the exact boson first predicted by Peter Higgs and others in 1964 to be the arbiter of mass and cosmic diversity. “Personally, I have no problems calling this a Higgs boson,” said Joe Incandela, a professor at the University of California, Santa Barbara, and spokesman, or leader, of one of the teams, known as CMS, that reported the new particle last July. “If it’s not, I won’t mind eating my words, because it would be so much more interesting.”', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'All Signs Point to Higgs, but Scientific Certainty Is a Waiting Game', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'All Signs Point to Higgs, but Scientific Certainty Is a Waiting Game', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Higgs Boson', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dark Matter (Astronomy)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Large Hadron Collider', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CERN', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Particle Accelerators', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Physics', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-05T00:37:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dennis Overbye', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dennis', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Overbye', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organizati