e World Baseball Classic, but that excitement is tempered by concerns about the future of the national team.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HAVANA — On Sunday, the morning after Cuba’s 5-2 triumph against Brazil in Fukuoka, Japan, its opening game in this year’s World Baseball Classic, Sigfredo Barros ventured to the tree-lined Central Park here to partake in the musings of La Peña del Parque Central, a group of men who gather each day to debate baseball.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/sports/CUBA4/CUBA4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 531, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/05/sports/CUBA4/CUBA4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 531}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/sports/CUBA4/CUBA4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 906, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/sports/CUBA4/CUBA4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1812, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/sports/CUBA4/CUBA4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/05/sports/CUBA4/CUBA4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/sports/CUBA4/CUBA4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'High Hopes