ions and interrogation techniques is to be released on Tuesday called on the United States to publicly account for the policy and said that failure to prosecute those responsible would breach international law. The investigator, Ben Emmerson, whose report was to be presented to the United Nations Human Rights Council in Geneva, added that although President Obama had clearly repudiated “the unlawful actions carried out by the Bush-era C.I.A., many of the facts remain classified and no public official has been brought to justice.” Mr. Emmerson, a British human rights lawyer working for the United Nations, also called for the publication of a report by the Senate Intelligence Committee on rendition and interrogation programs “to the fullest extent possible.” The C.I.A. declined to comment. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Inquiry on C.I.A. Detentions to Be Unveiled', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | United Nations', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Inquiry on C.I.A. Detentions to Be Unveiled', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central Intelligence Agency', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Emmerson, Ben', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-05T01:47:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Cumming-Bruce', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cumming-Bruce', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b5d4a05-ade1-5d28-b6c9-a91f0db16619', 'word_count': 138, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b5d4a05-ade1-5d28-b6c9-a91f0db16619'}, {'abstract': 'The F.D.A.’s committee members said both medicines offered only marginal benefit, reducing the number of hot flashes by only about one a day compared to a placebo.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/05/business/fda-panel-advises-against-two-medicines-to-treat-hot-flashes.html', 'snippet': 'The F.D.A.’s committee members said both medicines offered only marginal benefit, reducing the number of hot flashes by only about one a day compared to a placebo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Menopausal women looking for an approved alternative to hormones to treat hot flashes will probably not be getting immediate relief. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'F.D.A. Panel Advises Against Two Medicines to Treat Hot Flashes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'F.D.A. Panel Advises Against Two Medicines to Treat Hot Flashes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pollack, Andrew', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Menopause', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gabapentin (Drug)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Estrogen', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-05T01:48:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Pollack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pollack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/41f18081-88f8-564f-af53-20555e0eabfa', 'word_count': 817, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41f18081-88f8-564f-af53-20555e0eabfa'}, {'abstract': 'On Monday, there were further indications that Abdelhamid Abu Zeid, a leader of Al Qaeda in the Islamic Maghreb, had been killed last week in northern Mali.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/05/world/africa/mali-more-weight-to-reports-of-militants-death.html', 'snippet': 'On Monday, there were further indications that Abdelhamid Abu Zeid, a leader of Al Qaeda in the Islamic Maghreb, had been killed last week in northern Mali.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Monday, there were further indications that Abdelhamid Abu Zeid, a leader of Al Qaeda in the Islamic Maghreb, had been killed last week in northern Mali, in the Adrar des Ifoghas mountains, where French and Chadian troops were hunting down Islamist fighters. A Mauritanian news Web site, Sahara Media, which has close contacts with Abu Zeid’s group, cited an Islamist source as confirming that he had been killed in a French airstrike. But the same unnamed Islamist source denied reports of the death of Mokhtar Belmokhtar, another militant leader, who Chad’s military said had been killed by its soldiers in Mali last week. The source claimed that Mr. Belmokhtar was alive and operating to the southwest, close to the Malian town of Gao. France’s chief of the defense staff, Adm. Édouard Guillaud, told Europe 1 radio Monday morning that it was probable that Abu Zeid had been killed. “It is likely, but only likely,” he said. “We don’t have any certainty for the moment. It would be good news.” Abu Zeid is said to have abducted more than 20 Western hostages since 2008 for ransom, some of which went to Al Qaeda. He is believed to have killed a British hostage, Edwin Dyer, in 2009, and a 78-year-old Frenchman, Michel Germaneau, in 2010. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mali: More Weight to Reports of Militant’s Death', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Africa', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mali: More Weight to Reports of Militant&#8217;s Death', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Abu Zeid, Abdelhamid', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Al Qaeda in the Islamic Maghreb', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mali', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-05T01:51:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Erlanger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erlanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/412770bd-98a5-5b35-989e-612094ee1add', 'word_count': 214, 'uri': 'nyt://article/412770bd-98a5-5b35-989e-612094ee1add'}, {'abstract': 'Mayor Cory A. Booker of Newark, who is running for Senate, pledged to put forth a full accounting of his outside earnings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/05/nyregion/booker-says-he-donated-speaking-fees-to-charity.html', 'snippet': 'Mayor Cory A. Booker of Newark, who is running for Senate, pledged to put forth a full accounting of his outside earnings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEWARK — Mayor Cory A. Booker has earned about $1 million from public speaking engagements during his seven years in office, as he has built his position at City Hall into a national brand. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/nyregion/Y-BOOKER/Y-BOOKER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 409, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/201