'By Malia Wollan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Malia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wollan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/85d387d7-4fb1-52c6-b291-e04566403e7f', 'word_count': 933, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85d387d7-4fb1-52c6-b291-e04566403e7f'}, {'abstract': 'If confirmed, this would be the first time a person has been cured with simple drug treatments, making a lifetime of antiviral therapy unnecessary.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/05/opinion/the-intriguing-case-of-a-baby-cured-of-hiv.html', 'snippet': 'If confirmed, this would be the first time a person has been cured with simple drug treatments, making a lifetime of antiviral therapy unnecessary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Doctors have apparently cured a baby infected with H.I.V., the virus that causes AIDS, with an aggressive treatment of drugs starting a day after the baby was born. If confirmed by further analysis, this would be the first time a person has been cured with simple drug treatments, making a lifetime of antiviral therapy unnecessary.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Intriguing Case of a Baby Cured of H.I.V.', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Intriguing Case of a Baby Cured of H.I.V.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies and Infants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Acquired Immune Deficiency Syndrome', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-05T02:20:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6484e6a-a44f-5aec-b943-1d0f108fc2cb', 'word_count': 379, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6484e6a-a44f-5aec-b943-1d0f108fc2cb'}, {'abstract': 'Seventeen new pardons are a step in the right direction but are still disappointing for a president whose clemency record is woeful.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/05/opinion/president-obamas-timid-use-of-the-pardon-power.html', 'snippet': 'Seventeen new pardons are a step in the right direction but are still disappointing for a president whose clemency record is woeful.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week, President Obama pardoned 17 people who had been convicted of felonies. An Na Peng, a Chinese citizen living in Hawaii, is the first person convicted of an immigration crime to be pardoned in many years. With the pardon, she can now become an American citizen. Lynn Marie Stanek, convicted in a minor drug deal, told her Oregon newspaper that the pardon would allow her to “move beyond my past in a tangible, legal and personally meaningful way.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Timid Use of the Pardon Power', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Timid Use of the Pardon Power', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Amnesties, Commutations and Pardons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mandatory Sentencing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-05T02:22:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/7fa08101-0cd2-51ff-af42-0fa27829c18c', 'word_count': 333, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7fa08101-0cd2-51ff-af42-0fa27829c18c'}, {'abstract': 'In nominating Gina McCarthy to head the E.P.A. and Ernest J. Moniz for the Energy Department, President Obama showed his intent to use all the tools at his disposal to tackle climate change.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/05/us/politics/obama-names-2-to-fill-epa-and-energy-posts.html', 'snippet': 'In nominating Gina McCarthy to head the E.P.A. and Ernest J. Moniz for the Energy Department, President Obama showed his intent to use all the tools at his disposal to tackle climate change.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Obama on Monday named two people to his cabinet who will be charged with making good on his threat to use the powers of the executive branch to tackle climate change and energy policy if Congress does not act quickly.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/us/jp-ENERGY/jp-ENERGY-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 495, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/05/us/jp-ENERGY/jp-ENERGY-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 495}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/us/jp-ENERGY/jp-ENERGY-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 844, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/us/jp-ENERGY/jp-ENERGY-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1689, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/us/jp-ENERGY/jp-ENERGY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width':