early 12 weeks after undergoing cancer surgery, a government official said Monday. “There is a worsening of the respiratory function related to the state of immunodepression corresponding to his clinical situation,” said Information Minister Ernesto Villegas in a 10 p.m. broadcast. He added that Mr. Chávez was suffering from “a new and severe infection.” Officials previously said the president had overcome a lung infection, and it was not clear from the statement whether the new infection was also in the lungs. Mr. Villegas said Mr. Chávez had been receiving “chemotherapy of strong impact” and characterized his condition as “very delicate.” Monday’s health update was one of the bleakest since Mr. Chávez’s surgery. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Venezuela: Chávez’s Condition Worsens, Official Says', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Venezuela: Chávez’s Condition Worsens, Official Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Venezuela', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chavez, Hugo', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-05T03:57:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Neuman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Neuman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/685c15e1-2442-5941-9e10-5b0b16bf8b6e', 'word_count': 123, 'uri': 'nyt://article/685c15e1-2442-5941-9e10-5b0b16bf8b6e'}, {'abstract': 'Private industry is blooming in Detroit, even as the city’s municipal finances have descended into wreckage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2013/03/04/us/DETROIT.html', 'snippet': 'Priv