cisions, according to a new report.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/05/us/lax-policing-of-doctor-and-pharmacy-conflicts-is-found-in-medicare-coverage-decisions.html', 'snippet': 'The federal Medicare agency had not clearly defined “conflict of interest” and did not enforce standards to prevent such conflicts from influencing coverage decisions, according to a new report.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Deciding which drugs will be covered by Medicare can influence huge amounts of spending, but government officials do little to police conflict of interest among doctors and pharmacists who make those decisions, federal investigators said Monday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lax Policing of Doctor and Pharmacy Conflicts Is Found in Medicare Coverage Decisions', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lax Policing of Doctor and Pharmacy Conflicts Is Found in Medicare Coverage Decisions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pear, Robert', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicaid', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conflicts of Interest', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tavenner, Marilyn B', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Health and Human Services Department', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-05T05:11:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Pear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pear', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa317dc4-73d5-58af-aebc-5fce0810a910', 'word_count': 768, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa317dc4-73d5-58af-aebc-5fce0810a910'}, {'abstract': 'Russia has no intentions of getting involved again in Afghanistan. Yet the Central Asian republics, especially Uzbekistan, now fear instability on their borders as NATO’s 100,000-strong presence ends.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/05/russias-concerns-about-afghanistan-after-nato/', 'snippet': 'Russia has no intentions of getting involved again in Afghanistan. Yet the Central Asian republics, especially Uzbekistan, now fear instability on their borders as NATO’s 100,000-strong presence ends.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the United States winds down its combat mission in Afghanistan, Russia is looking on, not with Schadenfreude but with extreme concern.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/06/blogs/06rdv-page-two-nato-dempsey/06rdv-page-two-nato-dempsey-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 503, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/06/blogs/06rdv-page-two-nato-dempsey/06rdv-page-two-nato-dempsey-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 503}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/06/blogs/06rdv-page-two-nato-dempsey/06rdv-page-two-nato-dempsey-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 858, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/06/blogs/06rdv-page-two-nato-dempsey/06rdv-page-two-nato-dempsey-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1458, 'width': 1740, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/06/blogs/06rdv-page-two-nato-dempsey/06rdv-page-two-nato-dempsey-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/06/blogs/06rdv-page-two-nato-dempsey/06rdv-page-two-nato-dempsey-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/06/blogs/06rdv-page-two-nato-dempsey/06rdv-page-two-nato-dempsey-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia’s Concerns About Afghanistan After NATO', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-05T05:35:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judy Dempsey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dempsey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fee74a81-ca62-59fd-b607-ca2436f62934', 'word_count': 360, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fee74a81-ca62-59fd-b607-ca2436f62934'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/05/arts/television/whats-on-tuesday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '8 P.M. (Sundance) THE GIRL WITH THE DRAGON TATTOO (2010) Michael Nyqvist stars as a crusading Swedish journalist hired by a wealthy industrialist (Sven-Bertil Taube) to investigate the disappearance of his niece 40 years earlier. Noomi Rapace, above with Mr. Nyqvist, is Lisbeth Salander, the vulnerable yet ruthlessly competent computer hacker who helps him solve the mystery in this original Swedish film adaptation of the Stieg Larsson novel, directed by Niels Arden Oplev. “Though Ms. Rapace is a fine professional scowler, with cheekbones that thrust like knives and a pout that’s mostly pucker, she tends to register as an intriguing idea instead of a thoroughly realized character,” Manohla Dargis wrote in The New York Times. “She more or less looks the part that the filmmakers don’t let her fully play.” Ms. Dargis added: “\xa0‘The Girl With the Dragon Tattoo’ was originally published as ‘Men Who Hate Women,’ which apparently wasn’t sexy enough for English-language bookshelves. The title change certainly spices things up, no matter how commonplace body art is, at least outside of Stockholm, and it plays down its overarching theme, which the movie only does further. Just as significant is the substitution in the title of ‘girl’ for ‘women,’ a categorical displacement (and diminution) that also shifts the emphasis from the crime (and criminals) and places it on Salander’s slender back. It’s an attractive back in the movie, as is the tattoo adorning it, even if, like all the prettily photographed winter landscapes, the dragon covers up something the filmmakers seem loath to reveal and simultaneously eager to exploit.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Tuesday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-05T06:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/b61874fc-c694-5b8c-bf84-d2ceb8a4f161', 'word_count': 788, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b61874fc-c694-5b8c-bf84-d2ceb8a4f161'}, {'abstract': 'In the Brahmaputra River system, planners face a Hobson’s choice between the twin goals of climate change adaptation and mitigation.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/05/brahmaputra-dams-promise-prosperity-but-at-a-big-cost/', 'snippet': 'In the Brahmaputra River system, planners face a Hobson’s choice between the twin goals of climate change adaptation and mitigation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROTTUNG, Arunachal Pradesh—I’m standing, weak-kneed, midway across the gorge of the Siang River, one of the three tributaries that converge to form the Brahmaputra River. Treading slowly over a bamboo suspension footbridge 300-odd meters long and just a meter wide, I marvel at this premodern engineering by the Adi Minyong tribe that dominates this section of Arunachal Pradesh.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/04/world/asia/4-brahmaputra-IndiaInk/4-brahmaputra-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/04/world/asia/4-brahmaputra-IndiaInk/4-brahmaputra-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/04/world/asia/4-brahmaputra-IndiaInk/4-brahmaputra-IndiaInk-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/04/world/asia/4-brahmaputra-IndiaInk/4-brahmaputra-IndiaInk-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'sub