 falls can be exceeded by the morbid fear associated with going to the ground.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My 84-year-old father-in-law is a “flogger.” That’s the moniker his son gave him because Dad keeps a written record of every fall my 83-year-old mother-in-law takes. She has Parkinson’s disease, and the “flog” (fall log) of her spills has helped her doctors monitor her disease progression and adjust her therapy. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fear of Falling', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bones', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Falls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jong, Erica', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Centers for Disease Control and Prevention', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-05T10:45:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harley A. Rotbart, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harley', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Rotbart', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/69282279-608a-548a-bc7c-b8d9f5c5dd15', 'word_count': 959, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69282279-608a-548a-bc7c-b8d9f5c5dd15'}, {'abstract': 'If you’re a high school junior, this is the part of your college search that does not have a lot of specific deadlines. It does, however, have a lot of things you need to do to stay on track and set yourself up for the best experience.', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/05/counselors-calendar-march-juniors/', 'snippet': 'If you’re a high school junior, this is the part of your college search that does not have a lot of specific d