ut you do not have to use an Apple-branded model.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Q&A: Keyboarding With an Apple TV', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Using a Keyboard\r\nWith an Apple TV', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bluetooth Wireless Technology', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Software', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Logitech International SA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-05T12:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By J.d. Biersdorfer', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ea11a8e-d361-5838-b1a8-62574cfdb50a', 'word_count': 212, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ea11a8e-d361-5838-b1a8-62574cfdb50a'}, {'abstract': 'Carol Miller, 62, began her radio D.J. career in 1973 and is continuing over the years to solidly promote classic rock.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/05/booming/what-makes-this-radio-dj-roll.html', 'snippet': 'Carol Miller, 62, began her radio D.J. career in 1973 and is continuing over the years to solidly promote classic rock.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Carol Miller, who is 62, began her New York radio career as a disc jockey at WNEW-FM in 1973. These days she can be heard weeknights on Q104.3 FM and on Sirius/XM’s Classic Rewind channel. Get the Led Out, her widely syndicated show chronicling the history of Led Zeppelin, began in 1984. (That’s not a misprint; it’s Ms. Miller’s commitment to rock ’n’ roll forever) In her recently published memoir titled "Up All Night: My Life and Times in Rock Radio" (Ecco/Harper Collins), she describes her relationships with some of the greatest rock stars of the time. Paul McCartney and Robert Plant dropped by the studio to chat; she dated Aerosmith’s Steven Tyler and Paul Stanley of Kiss. And through it all, she has battled cancer — for 40 years now. This interview has been condensed and edited.  ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/02/19/booming/19dj-booming4/19dj-booming4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 427, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/02/19/booming/19dj-booming4/19dj-booming4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 427}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/02/19/booming/19dj-booming4/19dj-booming4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 729, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/02/19/booming/19dj-booming4/19dj-booming4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1055, 'width': 1482, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/02/19/booming/19dj-booming4/19dj-booming4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/02/19/booming/19dj-booming4/19dj-booming4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/02/19/booming/19dj-booming4/19dj-booming4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Makes This Radio D.J. Roll?', 'kicker': 'The Creative Mid-Life', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baby Boomers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radio', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sirius XM Radio Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-05T12:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Booming', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jo Maeder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jo', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Maeder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7fd446e-7a68-51d3-ae66-76dd23c02621', 'word_count': 1539, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7fd446e-7a68-51d3-ae66-76dd23c02621'}, {'abstract': 'A technical assistance Web site reviewed more than 720,000 support requests to determine which phones had the highest complaint ratios.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/05/how-users-rate-their-phones/', 'snippet': 'A technical assistance Web site reviewed more than 720,000 support requests to determine which phones had the highest complaint ratios.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you are phone-shopping and wonder about the reliability of various brands, you are in luck. FixYa, a volunteer technical assistance Web site, has analyzed more than 720,000 support requests to come up with complaint-per-phone ratios, which the company said represent reliability.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Users Rate Their Phones', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-05T12:00:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roy Furchgott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Furchgott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/82700309-c665-5569-aca9-9de3800272fd', 'word_count': 431, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82700309-c665-5569-aca9-9de3800272fd'}, {'abstract': 'When we started H.Bloom, we would hire a candidate based exclusively on e-mail interactions, a phone screen and in-person interviews. After a couple of early mistakes, we realized that we needed to make a change.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/05/you-have-identified-the-candidates-how-do-you-pick-the-right-one/', 'snippet': 'When we started H.Bloom, we would hire a candidate based exclusively on e-mail interactions, a phone screen and in-person interviews. After a couple of early mistakes, we realized that we needed to make a change.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In my last two posts, I talked about the process we use at H.Bloom to run a recruiting campaign: defining the role, targeting the right profile of candidates, building a list of potential candidates and presenting them with a persuasive pitch. This process is meant to yield viable candidates for a position.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'You Have Identified the Candidates. How Do You Pick the Right One?', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burkhart, Bryan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-05T12:00:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bryan Burkhart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bryan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burkhart', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d356a7e-32d9-53bf-a54d-1ae3e7e378f9', 'word_count': 1086, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d356a7e-32d9-53bf-a54d-1ae3e7e378f9'}, {'abstract': 'A New York Times/CBS News poll has found that American Catholics had less positive views of the leadership of Pope Benedict XVI than of Pope John Paul II.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/06/us/in-poll-us-catholics-mixed-on-benedicts-papacy.html', 'snippet': 'A New York Times/CBS News poll has found that American Catholics had less positive views of the leadership of Pope Benedict XVI than of Pope John Paul II.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Looking back on the papacy of Pope Benedict XVI, most Roman Catholics in the United States offered mixed reviews of his leadership, a new New York Times/CBS News poll found.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Catholics Give Mixed Reviews of Benedict’s Papacy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Benedict XVI', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date':