'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/05/fashion/runway-womens/chanel_fall13-slide-ECDE/chanel_fall13-slide-ECDE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/fashion/runway-womens/chanel_fall13-slide-ECDE/chanel_fall13-slide-ECDE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/fashion/runway-womens/chanel_fall13-slide-ECDE/chanel_fall13-slide-ECDE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/fashion/runway-womens/chanel_fall13-slide-ECDE/chanel_fall13-slide-ECDE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/05/fashion/runway-womens/chanel_fall13-slide-ECDE/chanel_fall13-slide-ECDE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/fashion/runway-womens/chanel_fall13-slide-ECDE/chanel_fall13-slide-ECDE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Chanel: Fall 2013 RTW', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-05T13:44:06+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Fashion & Style', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': "Women's Runway", 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/1720cc91-a3e7-52b8-a825-d5a1f69caad9', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/1720cc91-a3e7-52b8-a825-d5a1f69caad9'}, {'abstract': 'Most important: He is running the magazine’s Twitter account this week.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/05/some-things-you-may-not-have-known-about-adam-davidson/', 'snippet': 'Most important: He is running the magazine’s Twitter account this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you read Adam Davidson’s “It’s the Economy” column, you might think that he is a pretty smart guy who knows a lot about how the exchange of money and ideas shapes\xa0our thinking. What you wouldn’t know, however, is that Adam isn’t interested in only beer mergers or finding a nanny for his 1-year-old. He also likes to sing Kelly Clarkson songs at the top of his lungs, make henna designs and watch endless loops of “Full House” reruns. He also wore only green clothing for an entire year when he was 38.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/04/magazine/04-adam-davidson-twitter/04-adam-davidson-twitter-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 153, 'width': 480, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/04/magazine/04-adam-davidson-twitter/04-adam-davidson-twitter-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 153, 'width': 480, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/04/magazine/04-adam-davidson-twitter/04-adam-davidson-twitter-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/04/magazine/04-adam-davidson-twitter/04-adam-davidson-twitter-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/04/magazine/04-adam-davidson-twitter/04-adam-davidson-twitter-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Some Things You May Not Have Known About Adam Davidson', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davidson, Adam', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-05T13:55:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Kelly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kelly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb2d7545-532a-5c56-b4a9-51baf3707b18', 'word_count': 170, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb2d7545-532a-5c56-b4a9-51baf3707b18'}, {'abstract': 'Sticky question, sticky answer.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/05/why-dont-we-have-deflation/', 'snippet': 'Sticky question, sticky answer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Whenever you see a piece suggesting that the US economy has entered a “new normal” of slow growth, you’re likely to see someone making the argument that if the economy actually had lots of excess capacity, we should be seeing deflation. And the question of why we don’t have deflation is a good one. It is, however, a question that people like me have answered repeatedly; unfortunately, it seems that this analysis hasn’t been making it to, say, a number of current and former Fed officials.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Don’t We Have Deflation?', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-05T13:59:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/86f5d80c-99d9-58a3-b90f-825e2b22899f', 'word_count': 546, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86f5d80c-99d9-58a3-b90f-825e2b22899f'}, {'abstract': 'Ungaro’s new designer hits some high notes.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/05/a-promising-debut-at-ungaro/', 'snippet': 'Ungaro’s new designer hits some high notes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ever since Emanuel Ungaro retired, in 2005, and the Avenue Montaigne house was sold to Asim Abdullah, an affable Silicon Valley entrepreneur with no experience in fashion, the company has floundered. Five or six designers have come and gone (I’m not sure whether to count Lindsay Lohan, who laughably served as artistic adviser). The most recent was Giles Deacon, a London designer, who initially seemed a good choice but couldn’t make anything happen.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Promising Debut at Ungaro', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lohan, Lindsay', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ungaro, Emanuel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-05T14:02:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/94523fdd-3940-5228-a4c8-fa0a4de936e7', 'word_count': 198, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94523fdd-3940-5228-a4c8-fa0a4de936e7'}, {'abstract': 'British officials were too focused on containing the financial crisis to analyze information connected to potential interest-rate manipulation, an audit by the Financial Services Authority said on Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/03/05/audit-faults-british-regulators-response-to-libor-scandal/', 'snippet': 'British officials were too focused on containing the financial crisis to analyze information connected to potential interest-rate manipulation, an audit by the Financial Services Authority said on Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON – British authorities failed to spot interest-rate manipulation by big banks because they were narrowly focused on responding to the financial crisis, according to an internal review by the country’s financial watchdog released on Tuesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'British Regulators Slow to Respond to Libor Scandal, Audit Says', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Libor (London Interbank Offered Rate)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Financial Services Authority', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-05T14:10:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8960f1fa-753b-5eab-a4b3-b83e20ad6556', 'word_count': 365, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8960f1fa-753b-5eab-a4b3-b83e20ad6556'}, {'abstract': 'A 20 percent stake in an offshore field being sold by Anadarko and Videocon could lead to a breakthrough for development of the country’s considerable energy resources.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/06/business/global/anadarko-and-videocon-to-sell-mozambique-gas-stakes.html', 'snippet': 'A 20 percent stake in an offshore field being sold by Anadarko and Videocon could lead to a breakthrough for development of the country’s considerable energy resources.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Anadarko Petroleum of the United States and Videocon of India have put 20 percent of an important natural gas field off the coast of Mozambique up for sale, according to Videocon’s chairman and others with direct knowledge of the matter.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Anadarko and Videocon to Sell Mozambique Gas Stakes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Anadarko and Videocon to Sell Natural Gas Stake in Mozambique', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reed, Stanley', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ANADARKO PETROLEUM CORP', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Natural Gas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mozambique', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Offshore Drilling and Exploration', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Videocon Industries Ltd', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-05T14:24:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stanley Reed', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stanley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/880bd180-835a-55f2-852a-95dbfe29c33e', 'word_count': 658, 'uri': 'nyt://article/880bd180-835a-55f2-852a-95dbfe29c33e'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/05/what-were-reading-642/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Town & Country: The urbane maître d’hôtel of Daniel, John Winterman, bemoans the unsightly legions of “baggy trench coats, oversized shopping bags and damp umbrellas” cluttering his dining room, as more customers refuse to check their belongings. — Pete Wells', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-05T14:32:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9089dbc-4247-5737-be35-12cec9c2d7bd', 'word_count': 317, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9089dbc-4247-5737-be35-12cec9c2d7bd'}, {'abstract': 'Television pilots are moving from networks to streaming services online, Fox plans to take on ESPN with Fox Sports 1 and San Francisco becomes a center for innovative advertisers.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/05/the-breakfast-meeting-tv-pilots-move-to-the-web-and-fox-prepares-to-take-on-espn/', 'snippet': 'Television pilots are moving from networks to streaming services online, Fox plans to take on ESPN with Fox Sports 1 and San Francisco becomes a center for innovative advertisers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TV shows like “House of Cards,” “Hemlock Grove” and the latest iteration of “Arrested Development” are debuting regularly on streaming services like Netflix, signaling a departure from traditional networks and a sea change in the way television is viewed, Brian Stelter writes. Amazon.com and Microsoft are also commissioning original shows for their millions of subscribers. The shows’ production values now rival those of network television, and their proliferation is seen as a good thing for viewers that may inflame cable companies’ concerns about cutting the cord.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting: TV Pilots Move to the Web and Fox Prepares to Take On ESPN', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-05T14:33:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel E. Slotnik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Slotnik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd90a278-bd77-5b23-a2e3-6b2c046f5824', 'word_count': 502, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd90a278-bd77-5b23-a2e3-6b2c046f5824'}, {'abstract': 'There are concerns about whether the forces that have driven the market rally — government spending and banner corporate profits — will be sufficient to push it higher.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/06/business/daily-stock-market-activity.html', 'snippet': 'There are concerns about whether the forces that have driven the market rally — government spending and banner corporate profits — will be sufficient to push it higher.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The economy may be struggling to recover, but by one closely watched measure the fear that not long ago paralyzed the markets has lifted.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Fears Recede, Dow Industrials Hit a Milestone', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Fears Recede, Dow Industrials Hit a Milestone', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dow Jones Stock Average', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eavis, Peter', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-05T14:35:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Eavis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eavis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7bb1a86e-21e1-5c14-b8e1-e65b3d56f7d6', 'word_count': 1240, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7bb1a86e-21e1-5c14-b8e1-e65b3d56f7d6'}, {'abstract': 'Definitely a wow moment.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/05/the-life-expectancy-zombie/', 'snippet': 'Definitely a wow moment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'So, one of the moments in my debate with JoScar — which wasn’t as bad as I felt, but should have gone much better — was my “wow” when JS raised the old line that life expectancy was 62 when Social Security started, so the program was no big deal.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Life Expectancy Zombie', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-05T14:46:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/820f9d68-479b-51d0-8749-75ef0422d9f7', 'word_count': 415, 'uri': 'nyt://article/820f9d68-479b-51d0-8749-75ef0422d9f7'}, {'abstract': 'T plucks the best shoes right off the runway. Today’s pick: a four-buckle studded motorcycle boot.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/05/the-daily-shoe-saint-laurent-2/', 'snippet': 'T plucks the best shoes right off the runway. Today’s pick: a four-buckle studded motorcycle boot.', 'lead_paragraph': 'T plucks the best shoes right off the runway. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Daily Shoe | Saint Laurent', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paris Fashion Week', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shoes and Boots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Slimane, Hedi', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yves Saint Laurent', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-05T14:53:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Malina Joseph Gilchrist', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Malina', 'middlename': 'Joseph', 'lastname': 'Gilchrist', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a35a337-12cc-5c50-ab19-2a48dc1df552', 'word_count': 63, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a35a337-12cc-5c50-ab19-2a48dc1df552'}, {'abstract': 'The unemployment rate for people in their 20s with college degrees was 5.7 percent in late 2011. For those with only a high school education, it was 16.2 percent.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/05/yes-even-young-college-graduates-have-low-unemployment/', 'snippet': 'The unemployment rate for people in their 20s with college degrees was 5.7 percent in late 2011. For those with only a high school education, it was 16.2 percent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ve written recently about the job prospects for college graduates versus those without bachelor’s degrees, noting that the unemployment rate for college graduates is about half that for workers with no more than a high school diploma (3.7 percent versus 8.1 percent as of January). Several readers wrote me to take issue with the fact that I was looking at the whole universe of workers with these credentials, rather than just the recently graduated. Perhaps college graduates from generations past are more protected than those just entering the work force, they wrote, and it is misleading to say that young graduates are equally secure.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yes, Even Young College Graduates Have Low Unemployment', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-05T15:00:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c3df48ac-c147-519b-9f04-3e2591f45584', 'word_count': 417, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c3df48ac-c147-519b-9f04-3e2591f45584'}, {'abstract': 'Men’s basketball has another No. 1, but the women’s game is all about Baylor, Notre Dame, Connecticut — and Brittney Griner.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/06/sports/in-womens-basketball-a-season-of-powerhouses-leading-off.html', 'snippet': 'Men’s basketball has another No. 1, but the women’s game is all about Baylor, Notre Dame, Connecticut — and Brittney Griner.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If there was ever a year when men’s and women’s college basketball were more different, well, it’s hard to remember it, and Monday summed it up in one nice little package. The women’s game is all about powerhouses, about Baylor’s Brittney Griner’s being one in and of herself, scoring 50 points and dunking on Kansas State; about Notre Dame elbowing Connecticut out of its usual spot atop the Big East hill; about UConn hyperventilating because it hasn’t won a national title in three whole years. Gasp.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/06/sports/ncaabasketball/06leadingpic/06leadingpic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 873, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/06/sports/ncaabasketball/06leadingpic/06leadingpic-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 873}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/06/sports/ncaabasketball/06leadingpic/06leadingpic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 704, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/06/sports/nc