e, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Census', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Commuting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Census Bureau', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-05T15:05:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Roberts', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roberts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5af4c18-6e16-5f65-8b59-44161789f1a3', 'word_count': 295, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5af4c18-6e16-5f65-8b59-44161789f1a3'}, {'abstract': 'We’re tracking America’s corporate family leave policies.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/05/what-parental-leave-does-your-employer-offer/', 'snippet': 'We’re tracking America’s corporate family leave policies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Between Marissa Mayer’s new full-time face-time policy at Yahoo, new numbers showing America’s support for breast-feeding — as long as we don’t have to pay for it — yet more news regarding the dismal state of family leave in the United States, and now, a discussion of whether even graduate schools support new mothers (let alone new parents), family leave has been a big topic here in the past few weeks. With no national paid leave policy (and only 40 percent of employees eligible for unpaid leave under the Family Medical Leave Act), whether workers have access to leave depends largely on where and for whom they work.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Parental Leave Does Your Employer Offer?', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject