n be fuzzy.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/05/the-costs-of-underconfidence/', 'snippet': 'There is a cost to being underconfident as much as there is to being overconfident. Finding the line between the two can be fuzzy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Carl Richards is a certified financial planner in Park City, Utah, and is the director of investor education at The BAM Alliance. His book, “The Behavior Gap,” was published this year. His sketches are archived\xa0on the Bucks blog.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Costs of Underconfidence', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Asset Allocation (Personal Finances)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-05T15:38:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Richards', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Richards', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ad3dd31-2d7f-51f0-a9a2-3451582258a8', 'word_count': 527, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ad3dd31-2d7f-51f0-a9a2-3451582258a8'}, {'abstract': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/05/the-gun-report-march-5-2013/', 'snippet': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the problems with guns is that there are too many people who simply don’t take seriously their killing potential. Either that or they don’t care. Last Friday, for instance, a woman named Mary Frances Alday, 61, went into a Walmart in Crawfordville, Fla., and when she got to the checkout line, demanded that the store redeem a “dollar off” coupon she procured online. She became furious when told the store would not honor Internet coupons, and after lashing out at the store clerk and other Walmart employees – and hurling a shopping cart at them – she went to her car, where she pulled out a loaded Smith & Wesson .38 Special and waved it in the direction of the Walmart staff. After she fled the parking lot, Alday was pulled over by the sheriff’s department and charged with four counts of aggravated assault with a deadly weapon.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Gun Report: March 5, 2013', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Richmond (Va)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Jose (Calif)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tennessee', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (State)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-05T15:41:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Nocera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nocera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b055fc77-45fb-5dda-9b70-490ec38e5abf', 'word_count': 751, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b055fc77-45fb-5dda-9b70-490ec38e5abf'}, {'abstract': 'Germans with little or no direct memory of the Berlin Wall are demanding the preservation of what’s left of it, even if it’s fake.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/05/dont-tear-down-this-wall/', 'snippet': 'Germans with little or no direct memory of the Berlin Wall are demanding the preservation of what’s left of it, even if it’s fake.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — One quarter of a century after Ronald Reagan called on Mikhail Gorbachev to tear down the Berlin Wall, a new generation of Berliners is taking to the streets to preserve it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Don’t Tear Down This Wall', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Berlin Wall', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Buildings (Structures)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cold War Era', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gorbachev, Mikhail S', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ide, Robert', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reagan, Ronald Wilson', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Berlin Wall Memorial', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Checkpoint', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Berlin (Germany)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Germany', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-05T15:44:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lucian Kim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lucian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b745f6b-f4bd-5d6c-b35d-da7ed05d99d5', 'word_count': 527, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b745f6b-f4bd-5d6c-b35d-da7ed05d99d5'}, {'abstract': 'The story of Alex Johnson, one of the youngest soldiers in the famed 54th Massachusetts.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/05/colonel-shaws-drummer-boy/', 'snippet': 'The story of Alex Johnson, one of the youngest soldiers in the famed 54th Massachusetts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'African-American volunteers poured into the ranks of the 54th Massachusetts Infantry from across the Bay State during the early months of 1863; conspicuous among the patriotic towns that sent their black sons off to war was New Bedford. The seafaring city, with its large population of escaped slaves, had been targeted early on as a prime spot for recruits, and among those who enrolled in the new regiment was Alex Johnson, a 16-year-old sailor with a passion for percussion.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Colonel Shaw’s Drummer Boy', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shaw, Robert Gould', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Massachusetts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-05T15:45:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ronald S. Coddington', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ronald', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Coddington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d5237c9-0f35-5837-b7eb-73fb6027fa18', 'word_count': 1319, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d5237c9-0f35-5837-b7eb-73fb6027fa18'}, {'abstract': 'Despite reforms in Myanmar, many grievances remain and the downtrodden are less and less afraid to express them.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/05/occupy-rice-paddy/', 'snippet': 'Despite reforms in Myanmar, many grievances remain and the downtrodden are less and less afraid to express them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALWAN SOK, Myanmar — “Nostalgia” is one way to translate the name of this small farming village 25 kilometers south of Yangon. Nostalgia is also one way to describe the way the farmers who live here feel about their land and the time, many years ago, when they were sure it was theirs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Occupy Rice Paddy', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Investments', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Irrigation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Land Use Policies', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thein Sein', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Myanmar', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-05T15:45:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Swe Win', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Swe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Win', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/76be489f-5193-555c-8f16-dd3e3c72ca88', 'word_count': 774, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76be489f-5193-555c-8f16-dd3e3c72ca88'}, {'abstract': 'A court in Prague rules that Randy Blythe is not guilty of causing the death of a 19-year-old fan at a concert in 2010.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/05/lamb-of-god-singer-acquitted-in-fans-death/', 'snippet': 'A court in Prague rules that Randy Blythe is not guilty of causing the death of a 19-year-old fan at a concert in 2010.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A municipal court in Prague on Tuesday acquitted the lead singer of the heavy metal band Lamb of God of causing a teenage fan’s death at a concert in the Czech Republic, The Associated Press reported. A court spokeswoman, Marketa Puci, said that the court had ruled that what Mr. Blythe did was not a crime and that the concert organizers were to blame for the incident.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lamb of God Singer Acquitted in Fan’s Death', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blythe, Randy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lamb of God', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Prague (Czech Republic)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-05T15:53:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2bd6d353-d294-5cb0-b79d-c6a3f85101bd', 'word_count': 196, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2bd6d353-d294-5cb0-b79d-c6a3f85101bd'}, {'abstract': 'Laser’s concept for the namesake art fair, now in its 100th year, will turn the show on its head by focusing on the visitors as the subject.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/05/liz-magic-lasers-armory-show-souvenirs/', 'snippet': 'Laser’s concept for the namesake art fair, now in its 100th year, will turn the show on its head by focusing on the visitors as the subject.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The European avant-garde crashed onto American shores with the 1913 Armory Show, introducing New York’s art-going public to many of today’s most revered modern painters, among them Cézanne, Kandinsky, Matisse and Picasso. With radical works like Marcel Duchamp’s “Nude Descending a Staircase,” the exhibition both fascinated and disturbed; many visitors regarded the paintings, with their brash colors, warped perspectives and semi-abstract figures, as assaults on the virtues of classical beauty.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Liz Magic Laser’s Armory Show Souvenirs', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARMORIES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-05T16:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kareem Estefan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kareem', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Estefan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/530b3b1b-fccd-5c86-9c5a-b1c83422a6c7', 'word_count': 410, 'uri': 'nyt://ar