tract': 'Punk is back in the fall collections, which is not surprising given that the impact of the punk movement in fashion is the subject of an upcoming Costume Institute exhibition. Here are excerpts from a conversation with Vivienne Westwood about punk, and continuing to push buttons:', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/05/vivienne-westwood-at-71-still-not-done-provoking/', 'snippet': 'Punk is back in the fall collections, which is not surprising given that the impact of the punk movement in fashion is the subject of an upcoming Costume Institute exhibition. Here are excerpts from a conversation with Vivienne Westwood about punk...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Punk is back in the fall collections — spikes at Donatella Versace and Anthony Vaccarello, garbage bag dresses at Gareth Pugh — which is not surprising given that the impact of the punk movement in fashion is the subject of an upcoming Costume Institute exhibition. It all goes back to Vivienne Westwood, who designed for the Sex Pistols and whose collaborations with Malcolm McLaren in the 1970s will feature prominently at the Met. At 71, she remains as provocative as ever while continuing to design collections shown in London and Paris. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vivienne Westwood: At 71, Still Not Done Provoking', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Westwood, Vivienne', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Costume Institute', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Museum of Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-05T18:20:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 