he bully in all of us.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Next Monday I’m scheduled to be on a panel at the South by Southwest mediafest in Austin, discussing the ways in which our digital culture is changing how our children grow up. My role is apparently to make the more expert members of the panel – Emily Bazelon of Slate, Danah Boyd of Microsoft Research and Jason Rzepka of MTV – look brilliant by comparison. Given Bazelon’s timely new book on bullying, I expect that much of the conversation will explore whether the Internet contributes to a rising tide of meanness.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Bullying Pulpit', 'kicker': 'Bill Keller', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bazelon, Emily', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-05T18:44:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Keller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/06bf13ca-48f9-52e2-9e8d-f158b4dc11d4', 'word_count': 824, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06bf13ca-48f9-52e2-9e8d-f158b4dc11d4'}, {'abstract': 'Jazz at Lincoln Center is asking fans to vote for their favorite artists from a list of 10 nominees chosen by a panel of experts.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/05/jazz-hall-of-fame-opens-voting-to-fans-online/', 'snippet': 'Jazz at Lincoln Center is asking fans to vote for their favorite artists from a list of 10 nominees chosen by a panel of experts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As part of a broader effort to harness the Internet to engage more jazz fans, Jazz at Lincoln Center is inviting the general public to vote online for the 2013 inductees to the Nesuhi Ertegun Jazz Hall of Fame.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jazz Hall of Fame Opens Voting to Fans Online', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Halls of Fame', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jazz at Lincoln Center', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-05T18:45:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad6f780c-a4da-5fc8-ab1d-299113e85111', 'word_count': 369, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad6f780c-a4da-5fc8-ab1d-299113e85111'}, {'abstract': 'About 17 percent of car title loans incur repossession fees of about $400.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/05/consumer-groups-urge-scrutiny-of-car-title-loans/', 'snippet': 'About 17 percent of car title loans incur repossession fees of about $400.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As payday loans come under more scrutiny, consumer advocates are also urging a closer look at a similar type of short-term loan often marketed to the poor: car title loans.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Consumer Groups Urge Scrutiny of Car Title Loans', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Car Title Loans\r\nGet Scrutiny', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'nam