 [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Central Park (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Upper West Side (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-05T19:53:54+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Real Estate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/04a27970-bf9a-54f7-bdc9-dc5bfaf01aef', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/04a27970-bf9a-54f7-bdc9-dc5bfaf01aef'}, {'abstract': 'A necklace of fine architecture, strung between clasps — Columbus Circle to the south, Frederick Douglass Circle to the north — with barely any storefronts, unless you count doctors’ offices.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/10/realestate/central-park-west-eye-candy-in-structure-and-nature.html', 'snippet': 'A necklace of fine architecture, strung between clasps — Columbus Circle to the south, Frederick Douglass Circle to the north — with barely any storefronts, unless you count doctors’ offices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Architectural grandeur lines one side, 1.32 square miles of natural splendor the other; in these you have the virtues that validate Central Park West’s pride of place among city attractions. It certainly isn’t the shopping — there is no sidewalk-level retail on the entire 51-block stretch, beyond a dry cleaner, a tax preparer and a deli (unless you count doctors’ offices). ', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/06/realestate/10livingin-span/10livingin-span-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/06/realestate/10livingin-span/10living