d_count': 355, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe5f7096-e20f-5cd6-8f1b-2a5e14910899'}, {'abstract': 'Recipe Lab, a new feature, invites you to join cookbook authors to discuss their recipes in a live video chat.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/05/making-pasta-with-nigella-lawson/', 'snippet': 'Recipe Lab, a new feature, invites you to join cookbook authors to discuss their recipes in a live video chat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It takes just two good recipes for a new cookbook to earn a place on my shelf. But which recipes to try first? In Recipe Lab, a new monthly online feature, I make the book’s author choose its essential recipes for us. I’ll select one for you, our readers, to make at home. As you cook — or even if you don’t — you’ll be able to post comments and questions for the author here on Diner’s Journal. The author will then join me, and three of you, in a live video chat that everyone can watch. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Making Pasta With Nigella Lawson', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Chance to Cook With Nigella Lawson', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-05T21:22:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Moskin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moskin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/02305423-b215-5896-a106-c43de0bd929b', 'word_count': 589, 'uri': 'nyt://article/02305423-b215-5896-a106-c43de0bd929b'}, {'abstract': 'The British pianist Stephen Hough played the New York premiere of his own Piano Sonata No. 2 on Monday at Carnegie Hall.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/06/arts/music/stephen-hough-at-carnegie-hall.html', 'snippet': 'The British pianist Stephen Hough played the New York premiere of his own Piano Sonata No. 2 on Monday at Carnegie Hall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is hard for concertgoers today to imagine what it must have been like in the early decades of the 20th century, when towering composers who were also extraordinary pianists, like Rachmaninoff, Prokofiev and Bartok, performed their own works. We have some invaluable recordings, of course. But hearing these composers playing their music when it was new must have been overwhelming. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/06/arts/06HOUGH/06HOUGH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 393, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/06/arts/06HOUGH/06HOUGH-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 393}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/06/arts/06HOUGH/06HOUGH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 671, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/06/arts/06HOUGH/06HOUGH-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1343, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/06/arts/06HOUGH/06HOUGH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/06/arts/06HOUGH/06HOUGH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/06/arts/06HOUGH/06HOUGH-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 