eele and Colleen Hill of the Museum at the Fashion Institute of Technology meticulously chronicle the world of fancy footwear in their new book.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/05/head-over-heels/', 'snippet': 'Valerie Steele and Colleen Hill of the Museum at the Fashion Institute of Technology meticulously chronicle the world of fancy footwear in their new book.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function jsonSlideshowCallback(response){data = response;}NYTD.options = {source: data,cropType: \'blog480\',appendTo: \'fullScreenSlideShow\',showHeadLine: \'false\', renderstyle: "embeddedSlideShowTmag"}', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Head Over Heels', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shoes and Boots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Steele, Valerie', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fashion Institute of Technology', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-05T21:30:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Azadeh Ensha', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Azadeh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ensha', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e64603b-ba8b-586f-9832-b0a7c7eb9cdc', 'word_count': 342, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e64603b-ba8b-586f-9832-b0a7c7eb9cdc'}, {'abstract': 'As the spring tourism season nears, the White House said it would cease offering tours starting on Saturday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/06/us/politics/white-house-suspending-tours-over-budget-cuts.html', 'snippet': 'As the spring tourism season nears, the White House said it would cease offering tours starting on Saturday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Obama administration told members of Congress on Tuesday that it was canceling all White House tours beginning on Saturday because of the $85 billion in across-the-board spending cuts that went into effect last week.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'White House Tours Halted Over Cuts; Congress Says, ‘We’re Open’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'White House Tours Halted Over Cuts; Congress Says, ‘We’re Open’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'White House (Washington, DC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-05T21:31:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9138ad0-46fe-5b0d-bf76-34c0634ade32', 'word_count': 634, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9138ad0-46fe-5b0d-bf76-34c0634ade32'}, {'abstract': 'Henry A. Kissinger, the former secretary of state, was admitted to NewYork-Presbyterian/Weill Cornell hospital on Tuesday and released later in the day.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/05/kissinger-briefly-hospitalized-after-fall/', 'snippet': 'Henry A. Kissinger, the former secretary of state, was admitted to NewYork-Presbyterian/Weill Cornell hospital on Tuesday and released later in the day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Henry A. Kissinger, the former secretary of state, was admitted to NewYork-Presbyterian/Weill Cornell hospital on Tuesday after a fall at his home on the East Side of Manhattan. Mr. Kissinger, 89, was released Tuesday afternoon, the hospital said. No details were released about his injuries. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/nyregion/05kissinger-cityroom/05kissinger-cityroom-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/05/nyregion/05kissinger-cityroom/05kissinger-cityroom-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/nyregion/05kissinger-cityroom/05kissinger-cityroom-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/nyregion/05kissinger-cityroom/05kissinger-cityroom-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 403, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/05/nyregion/05kissinger-cityroom/05kissinger-cityroom-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 403}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/nyregion/05kissinger-cityroom/05kissinger-cityroom-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 687, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/nyregion/05kissinger-cityroom/05kissinger-cityroom-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1375, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Kissinger Briefly Hospitalized After Fall', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kissinger, Henry A', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-05T21:36:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2319f370-77b7-5e79-925e-8a3b6e7016ad', 'word_count': 46, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2319f370-77b7-5e79-925e-8a3b6e7016ad'}, {'abstract': 'A new report, based on 80 surveys, suggests that 60 percent of the forest elephants in Africa were killed between 2002 to 2011.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/06/science/surveys-quantify-loss-of-african-elephants-for-ivory-trade.html', 'snippet': 'A new report, based on 80 surveys, suggests that 60 percent of the forest elephants in Africa were killed between 2002 to 2011.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sixty percent of the forest elephants in Africa were killed from 2002 to 2011, scientists reported on Monday, putting a number to the rampant slaughter of both forest and savannah elephants for their ivory.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/07/science/07elephant/07elephant-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/07/science/07elephant/07elephant-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/07/science/07elephant/07elephant-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo'