36', 'word_count': 510, 'uri': 'nyt://article/acf49eb9-17e4-53fe-9596-732916c6f236'}, {'abstract': 'Gary Gensler, head of the Commodity Futures Trading Commission, is assuring officials that he plans to remain in the Obama administration through at least December even as he weighs other options, according to people briefed on the matter.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/03/05/gensler-said-to-pledge-to-stay-in-administration/', 'snippet': 'Gary Gensler, head of the Commodity Futures Trading Commission, is assuring officials that he plans to remain in the Obama administration through at least December even as he weighs other options, according to people briefed on the matter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gary Gensler, one of the top regulators of Wall Street, is assuring officials that he plans to remain in the Obama administration through at least December even as he weighs other options, according to three people briefed on the matter.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Futures Agency’s Leader Is Expected to Remain', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Futures Agency’s Leader Is Expected to Remain', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gensler, Gary S', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Meister, David', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Commodity Futures Trading Commission', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-06T00:54:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Protess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/213b0d8b-2297-5a49-9ba5-20711c9dfd1f', 'word_count': 514, 'uri': 'nyt://article/213b0d8b-2297-5a49-9ba5-20711c9dfd1f'}, {'abstract': 'When Geneva rolls around on the international auto salon calendar each March, consider the styling envelope about to be folded, spindled and mutilated.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/05/geneva-notebook-the-revenge-of-the-customizers/', 'snippet': 'When Geneva rolls around on the international auto salon calendar each March, consider the styling envelope about to be folded, spindled and mutilated.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GENEVA — If the Hollywood director Tim Burton designed cars, he would save his most twisted creations for the Geneva motor show. When Geneva rolls around on the international auto salon calendar each March, consider the styling envelope about to be folded, spindled and mutilated. To tell a designer with something on display here that his work is wildly impractical would be to bestow the highest sort of compliment.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Geneva Notebook: The Revenge of the Customizers', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Geneva International Motor Show', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burton, Tim', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Land Rover', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Toyota Motor Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-06T00:58:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jerry Garrett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jerry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garrett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e36ebe35-8d4d-517e-9cac-bf1363cf8909', 'word_count': 601, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e36ebe35-8d4d-517e-9cac-bf1363cf8909'}, {'abstract': 'Though his ill-fated design became a synonym for bad ideas, Mr. Brown was proud of it and drove one into his 90s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/06/business/roy-brown-jr-edsel-designer-dies-at-96.html', 'snippet': 'Though his ill-fated design became a synonym for bad ideas, Mr. Brown was proud of it and drove one into his 90s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Roy Brown Jr., a car designer for Ford Motor whose signature creation, the supposedly futuristic but ultimately ill-fated Edsel, became a synonym for bold, bad ideas not long after it was introduced in 1957, died on Feb. 24 in Michigan. He was 96.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/06/business/BROWN-obit/BROWN-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 447, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/06/business/BROWN-obit/BROWN-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 447}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/06/business/BROWN-obit/BROWN-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 763, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/06/business/BROWN-obit/BROWN-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1478, 'width': 1983, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtyp