e': 'subject', 'value': 'Memorabilia and Souvenirs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Archives and Records', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-06T01:46:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hillel Kuttler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hillel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kuttler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c7935d3-36e2-5127-b7f7-d77ba232ab5c', 'word_count': 1346, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c7935d3-36e2-5127-b7f7-d77ba232ab5c'}, {'abstract': 'Hugo Chávez’s death appeared to be welcomed directly and indirectly by some top figures in American politics in Washington, but some statements celebrated aspects of his leadership in whole or in part.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/05/hugo-chavez-death-reactions-obama-carter-royce-serrano/', 'snippet': 'Hugo Chávez’s death appeared to be welcomed directly and indirectly by some top figures in American politics in Washington, but some statements celebrated aspects of his leadership in whole or in part.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Not long after the death of Hugo Chávez was announced in Venezuela, a variety of major figures in American politics in Washington and beyond released statements offering their reactions. While his death was welcomed by some, others praised the Venezuelan leader for his efforts to help the poor. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Condemnation but Some Praise for Chávez From Washington', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carter, Jimmy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chavez, Hugo', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Royce, Edward R', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Serrano, Jose E', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Venezuela', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-06T01:49:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Roston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4f34aa9-b3dc-51d9-8d43-c82938d4f932', 'word_count': 428, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4f34aa9-b3dc-51d9-8d43-c82938d4f932'}, {'abstract': 'Some of the 30 companies in the Dow Jones industrial average are still down from their peaks, reflecting a move in financial power.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/06/business/economy/dows-premier-companies-have-not-recovered-evenly.html', 'snippet': 'Some of the 30 companies in the Dow Jones industrial average are still down from their peaks, reflecting a move in financial power.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Behind the bull market that drove the Dow Jones industrial average to a record high on Tuesday is a startling gulf in the fortunes of some of the nation’s largest corporations. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/06/business/DOW/DOW-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 376, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/06/business/DOW/DOW-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 376}}, {'rank': 0,