a historic outpouring of responses from opponents and supporters of gun control.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/06/nyregion/2-conflicting-agendas-arise-from-gun-safety-task-force-in-connecticut.html', 'snippet': 'Democratic and Republican leaders said gun legislation had proved extraordinarily complex, given a historic outpouring of responses from opponents and supporters of gun control.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HARTFORD — A week past their original goal for passing gun legislation, Democratic and Republican members of a legislative task force on Tuesday released competing gun-safety agendas in response to the massacre at Sandy Hook Elementary School.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '2 Conflicting Legislative Agendas Arise From Gun Safety Task Force in Connecticut', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '2 Conflicting Legislative Agendas Arise From Gun Safety Task Force in Connecticut', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Applebome, Peter', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newtown, Conn, Shooting (2012)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-06T01:57:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Applebome', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Applebome', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cac7e8d8-d2c1-5c6b-a760-5bb3aa04b144', 'word_count': 650, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cac7e8d8-d2c1-5c6b-a760-5bb3aa04b144'}, {'abstract': 'Creative thinking is needed to break the endless cycle of punishments and threats in order to disrupt the North’s nuclear program.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/06/opinion/another-round-of-sanctions-on-north-korea.html', 'snippet': 'Creative thinking is needed to break the endless cycle of punishments and threats in order to disrupt the North’s nuclear program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'China’s decision to join the United States in proposing tougher sanctions on North Korea is a welcome step. The new resolution, introduced at the United Nations on Tuesday, would seek to curtail North Korea’s nuclear and missile programs by making it more difficult for that country to move money around the world and explicitly banning the sale of items coveted by its elite, like yachts. It would also increase scrutiny of North Korea’s diplomats.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Another Round of Sanctions on North Korea', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Another Round of Sanctions on North Korea', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Tests', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-06T01:58:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/e34dc1da-30c2-5cf8-80dc-282b468171ca', 'word_count': 398, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e34dc1da-30c2-5cf8-80dc-282b468171ca'}, {'abstract': 'A British man who spent nearly two decades hiding in the United States after driving off with an armored van with $1.5 million in England was sentenced Tuesday in London to five years in jail.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/06/us/missouri-jail-after-years-of-hiding.html', 'snippet': 'A British man who spent nearly two decades hiding in the United States after driving off with an armored van with $1.5 million in England was sentenced Tuesday in London to five years in jail.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A British man who spent nearly two decades hiding in the United States after driving off with an armored van with $1.5 million in England was sentenced Tuesday in London to five years in jail. Edward J. Maher was a guard for a security company in 1993 when he took off with the van as a colleague was making a delivery. He was arrested in Ozark, Mo., in 2012 on a tip from his estranged daughter-in-law. In the United States, Mr. Maher often used a brother’s name or the alias Stephen King. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Missouri: Jail After Years of Hiding', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Midwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Missouri: Prison After Years of Hiding', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burns, John F', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ozark (Mo)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maher, Edward J', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-06T01:59:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By John F. Burns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Burns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/789e2fc4-6fb5-5299-830c-d14537de5db9', 'word_count': 92, 'uri': 'nyt://article/789e2fc4-6fb5-5299-830c-d14537de5db9'}, {'abstract': 'It is heartening to see an appellate court block the anti-solicitation provision of Arizona’s immigration law, calling it unconstitutional.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/06/opinion/free-speech-for-day-laborers.html', 'snippet': 'It is heartening to see an appellate court block the anti-solicitation provision of Arizona’s immigration law, calling it unconstitutional.', 'lead_paragraph': 'They trim trees, mow lawns, care for the elderly, clean up and rebuild after hurricanes and floods — and they defend the Constitution, too. Immigrant day laborers, who are so often the targets of local laws meant to sweep them off street corners, keep battling in court to defend their right to seek work, and they keep winning. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Free Speech on the Street Corner', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Free Speech on the Street Corner', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigrants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Day Laborers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-06T01:59:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/b397e9b3-e681-5381-872b-be21462d8f56', 'word_count': 322, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b397e9b3-e681-5381-872b-be21462d8f56'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama made the first trip of his second term, and the 12th of his presidency, to Walter Reed National Military Medical Center.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/05/obama-visits-wounded-as-afghanistan-casualties-continue/', 'snippet': 'President Obama made the first trip of his second term, and the 12th of his presidency, to Walter Reed National Military Medical Center.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama is winding down the war in Afghanistan, but the casualties continue. So on Tuesday afternoon, he made the first trip of his second term, and the 12th of his presidency, to visit wounded service men and women at Walter Reed National Military Medical Center.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Visits Wounded as Afghanistan Casualties Continue', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Reed, Walter, National Military Medical Center', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-06T01:59:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jackie Calmes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jackie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Calmes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0cb17374-1597-56bf-bcc2-735962f693ad', 'word_count': 145, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0cb17374-1597-56bf-bcc2-735962f693ad'}, {'abstract': 'This short documentary follows a 15-year-old from Stamford, N.Y., in the Catskills, as he hunts his first deer in the state’s first Youth Firearms Deer Hunt.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/06/opinion/shoot-one-please.html', 'snippet': 'This short documentary follows a 15-year-old from Stamford, N.Y., in the Catskills, as he hunts his first deer in the state’s first Youth Firearms Deer Hunt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last October, New York State for the first time held a three-day season for 14- and 15-year-olds to use guns to hunt deer. The State Department of Environmental Conservation had proposed the Youth Firearms Deer Hunt as a way to engage more young people in nature and outdoor recreation and to protect against deer overpopulation. The number of hunting licenses sold in New York has fallen by about one-quarter since peaking in the 1980s, the department said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/06/opinion/video-opdoc-shoot/video-opdoc-shoot-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/06/opinion/video-opdoc-shoot/video-opdoc-shoot-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/06/opinion/video-opdoc-shoot/video-opdoc-shoot-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/06/opinion/video-opdoc-shoot/video-opdoc-shoot-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1080, 'width': 1920, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 's