ww.nytimes.com/2013/03/06/nyregion/assigning-blame-after-boy-is-killed-by-truck.html', 'snippet': 'The death of Amar Diarrassouba, 6, has provided a window into how elected officials and pedestrian safety advocates in New York City navigate the complex politics of a tragedy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For years, the debate over the safety of New York City’s streets has roiled without pause, from the highest corridors of elected office to the zealous corners of social media, inflamed whenever a pedestrian is fatally struck by a vehicle.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fingers Are Pointed After Truck Kills Boy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fingers Are Pointed After Truck Kills Boy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Transportation Department (NYS)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Diarrassouba, Amar', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Transportation Alternatives', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stringer, Scott M', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-06T03:07:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Flegenheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flegenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/21a881b9-c083-5a5c-abd0-e3bc509b1d87', 'word_count': 869, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21a881b9-c083-5a5c-abd0-e3bc509b1d87'}, {'abstract': 'Notable properties that h