giant camel, with a shoulder height of perhaps nine feet, in Canada’s frigid high Arctic.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Canada’s North, Home to Bears, and Once, Camels', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Canada’s North, Home to Bears, And Once, Camels', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Camels', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Austen, Ian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fossils', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nature Communications (Journal)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ellesmere Island (Canada)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paleontology', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-06T03:17:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4ca763c-b301-5a9f-8072-712ab22e956f', 'word_count': 350, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4ca763c-b301-5a9f-8072-712ab22e956f'}, {'abstract': 'Reactions from Venezuelans and people around the world after the death of President Hugo Chávez.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/05/on-social-networks-mourning-and-division-after-chavezs-death/', 'snippet': 'Reactions from Venezuelans and people around the world after the death of President Hugo Chávez.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With expressions of mourning and calls for peace and stability, Venezuelans took to the streets and social networks on Tuesday after the announcement of the death of President Hugo Chávez. Messages came from all over the country and around the world, as supporters and critics of Mr. Chávez grappled with the news and tried to figure out what was next for the deeply divided country.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Social Networks, Mourning and Division After Chávez’s Death', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chavez, Hugo', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Venezuela', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-06T03:21:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elias E. Lopez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elias', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Lopez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/75fbedc0-d4e7-5d51-9d72-d1d4e017ce6d', 'word_count': 561, 'uri': 'nyt://article/75fbedc0-d4e7-5d51-9d72-d1d4e017ce6d'}, {'abstract': 'Some international couples are marrying by proxy over the Internet, a practice so new that immigration authorities say they do not typically watch for it in their efforts to detect fraud.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/06/nyregion/internet-marriages-on-rise-in-some-immigrant-communities.html', 'snippet': 'Some international couples are marrying by proxy over the Internet, a practice so new that immigration authorities say they do not typically watch for it in their efforts to detect fraud.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With a red embroidered veil draped over her dark hair, Punam Chowdhury held her breath last month as her fiancé said the words that would make them husband and wife. After she echoed them, they were married. Guests erupted in applause; the bride and groom traded bashful smiles.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank':