there is a long-term trend of shifting the cost of higher education from the public onto students and their families.', 'lead_paragraph': 'State and local financing for higher education declined 7 percent in fiscal 2012, to $81.2 billion, according to the annual report of the State Higher Education Executive Officers Association, and per-student support dropped 9 percent from the previous year, to $5,896, in constant dollars, the lowest level in at least 25 years. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Financing for Colleges Declines as Costs Rise', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Financing For Colleges Declines As Costs Rise', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Higher Education Executive Officers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tuition', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Financial Aid (Education)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-06T05:11:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tamar Lewin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tamar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lewin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/01407cd7-5960-5c7e-ab86-f62ac855a53b', 'word_count': 449, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01407cd7-5960-5c7e-ab86-f62ac855a53b'}, {'abstract': 'A report by Stuart W. Bowen Jr., the special inspector general for Iraq reconstruction, covers the more than $60 billion in American aid that was used to carry out projects in Iraq.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2013/03/06/world/