ws_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Choe Sang-Hun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Choe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sang-Hun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8fd25b3a-f880-590e-9a26-91ad1a6de4fa', 'word_count': 433, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8fd25b3a-f880-590e-9a26-91ad1a6de4fa'}, {'abstract': 'President Hugo Chávez of Venezuela dies; a dancer and two other men have confessed to an acid attack on the Bolshoi’s artistic director; Italian politics dominate the discussion at the Geneva auto show; Michael Haneke’s opera; and a World Cup problem that won’t go away.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/06/iht-quick-read-march-6/', 'snippet': 'President Hugo Chávez of Venezuela dies; a dancer and two other men have confessed to an acid attack on the Bolshoi’s artistic director; Italian politics dominate the discussion at the Geneva auto show; Michael Haneke’s opera; and a World Cup prob...', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEWS President Hugo Chávez of Venezuela died Tuesday afternoon after a struggle with cancer, the government announced, leaving behind a bitterly divided nation in the grip of a political crisis that grew more acute as he languished for weeks, silent and out of sight, in hospitals in Havana and Caracas. William Neuman reports from Caracas.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/timestopics/06rdv-chavez/topics_chavez_190-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 438, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/05/timestopics/06rdv-chavez/topics_chavez_190-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 438}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'ima