Toronto in September 2011 and photographed her odometer. She had driven just over 22,000 miles — more than four times the distance across Canada. Ms. Harris, a self-described “professional hobo,” had traveled the country in a car she bought on eBay, taking portraits of people she met along the way. Having lived in the United States for many years, she was seeking to capture her beloved homeland, asking herself an all-too-common question:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Oh, Canada?', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALBERTA (CANADA)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'British Columbia (Canada)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Newfoundland (Canada)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Saskatchewan (Canada)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Toronto (Ontario)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-06T10:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kerri MacDonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kerri', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MacDonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/80e99fe9-5084-5a5b-ad76-9a28cd6577f2', 'word_count': 840, 'uri': 'nyt://article/80e99fe9-5084-5a5b-ad76-9a28cd6577f2'}, {'abstract': 'If you could have any achievement, in sports or elsewhere, caught on camera for the world to see, what would it be?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/06/whats-the-most-impressive-sports-moment-youve-seen/', 'snippet': 'If you could have any achievement, in sports or elsewhere, caught on camera for the world to see, what would it be?', 'lead_paragraph': 'A leaping catch in the back of the end zone. A bottom-of-the-ninth, come-from-behind grand slam. A perfect landing off the balance beam. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s the Most Impressive Sports Moment You’ve Seen?', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-06T10:00:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Gonchar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonchar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/542a26f6-d305-5e5c-a8a1-dd6cc192f436', 'word_count': 320, 'uri': 'nyt://article/542a26f6-d305-5e5c-a8a1-dd6cc192f436'}, {'abstract': 'Northern Badakshan Province is far from insurgent strongholds and had been generally peaceful until recent months.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/07/world/asia/taliban-kill-17-afghan-soldiers.html', 'snippet': 'Northern Badakshan Province is far from insurgent strongholds and had been generally peaceful until recent months.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — Taliban insurgents killed as many as 17 Afghan National Army soldiers in a single episode in northern Badakhshan Province, an area that has been generally quiet and far from insurgent strongholds until recent months, according to accounts from Afghan officials on Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/07/world/07afghan_map/07afghan_map-jumbo.png', 'height': 211, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'jumbo'