nionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/06/crowd-funding-clean-energy/', 'snippet': 'There are plenty of recent signs that we may be witnessing the coming of age of solar power.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you wanted to get large numbers of people actively engaged in helping to solve global warming, how might you go about it? For years, the main approach in the environmental movement has been to sound the alarm bell and implore people to consume less, switch to green products, recycle, and speak up to companies and politicians. It hasn’t always been an easy sell. However, if the approach of a promising Oakland-based start-up takes hold, there may be another line of action that could become available to ordinary people: directly financing renewable energy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Crowdfunding Clean Energy', 'kicker': 'Fixes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alternative and Renewable Energy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Solar Energy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Buffett, Warren E', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rabobank', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-06T14:00:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Bornstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bornstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0aae893-c1e9-5c25-928c-e916d08ef6d6', 'word_count': 1970, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0aae893-c1e9-5c25-928c-e916d08ef6d6'}, {'abstract': 'Girls and boys alike teamed up in similar colors, patterns and styles to make people-watching an event o