section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e066cbf1-73a8-5d33-a9a4-ac8cce7c2b0b', 'word_count': 317, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e066cbf1-73a8-5d33-a9a4-ac8cce7c2b0b'}, {'abstract': 'The French national rail company SNCF is starting an economy high-speed rail service called Ouigo.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/06/high-speed-lower-price/', 'snippet': 'The French national rail company SNCF is starting an economy high-speed rail service called Ouigo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The French national rail company SNCF is starting an economy high-speed rail service called Ouigo on April 2. It will operate between the Paris suburb Marne-la-Vallée (home to Disneyland Paris) to points south, including Lyon, Marseille and Montpellier. Fares for the single-class, no-frills service (with no food or drink) range from 10 to 85 euros (about $12.50 to $107).', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'High Speed, Lower Price', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rail: High Speed, Lower Price', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'SNCF', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-06T16:00:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tanya Mohn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tanya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mohn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4774b47-4b0c-5043-8732-477a32097cb3', 'word_count': 59, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4774b47-4b0c-5043-8732-477a32097cb3'}, {'abstract': 'Under the direction of Mr. Mendes, “Skyfall” — which featured an Academy Award-winning title song performed by Adele and a regrettable title — sold more than $1.1 billion in tickets worldwide.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/06/sam-mendes-says-he-wont-direct-next-james-bond-movie/', 'snippet': 'Under the direction of Mr. Mendes, “Skyfall” — which featured an Academy Award-winning title song performed by Adele and a regrettable title — sold more than $1.1 billion in tickets worldwide.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With any luck, the next James Bond movie will have a better title than “Skyfall” — yes, “Skyfall” — the 23rd official entry in that long running spy-thriller franchise, which featured an Academy Award-winning title song performed by Adele, the detachable jaw of Javier Bardem and Albert Finney in a supporting role that seemed almost surely designed for Sean Connery.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/06/arts/skyfall/skyfall-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/06/arts/skyfall/skyfall-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/06/arts/skyfall/skyfall-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 433, 'width': 650, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/06/arts/skyfall/skyfall-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 433, 'width': 650, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/06/arts/skyfall/skyfall-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/06/arts/skyfall/skyfall-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sam Mendes Says He Won’t Direct Next James Bond Movie', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-06T16:00:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d3f279e-fa16-5dbb-9366-6fdf6cace20c', 'word_count': 304, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d3f279e-fa16-5dbb-9366-6fdf6cace20c'}, {'abstract': 'In a letter to Defense Secretary Chuck Hagel, five former deputy defense secretaries suggest using the budget cuts as an opportunity to re-examine military strategy, personnel numbers and weapons purchases.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/06/former-defense-officials-urge-using-budget-cuts-to-shape-military-strategy/', 'snippet': 'In a letter to Defense Secretary Chuck Hagel, five former deputy defense secretaries suggest using the budget cuts as an opportunity to re-examine military strategy, personnel numbers and weapons purchases.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the across-the-board spending cuts now a reality, a group of five former deputy defense secretaries has written to the new Pentagon chief, Chuck Hagel, urging that he make the best of a bad situation by using the budget cuts as an opportunity to re-examine military strategy, personnel numbers and weapons purchases.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Former Defense Officials Urge Using Budget Cuts to Shape Military Strategy', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headlin