atabase Marketing', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Journal of the American Medical Informatics Assn', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-06T17:31:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Markoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Markoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8df9c1aa-b82a-5962-9fea-8994a75f622a', 'word_count': 775, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8df9c1aa-b82a-5962-9fea-8994a75f622a'}, {'abstract': 'Virginia’s Signature Theater will stage an adaptation of the 1985 novel that also spawned the 1988 film, but at this point “Wind Beneath My Wings” won’t be part of the score.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/06/beaches-musical-finds-a-home/', 'snippet': 'Virginia’s Signature Theater will stage an adaptation of the 1985 novel that also spawned the 1988 film, but at this point “Wind Beneath My Wings” won’t be part of the score.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The wind beneath the wings of the musical adaptation of the film “Beaches” has landed the show a home. This week the Signature Theater in Arlington, Va., announced that it would produce the show as part of its 2013-14 season. Eric Schaeffer, Signature’s artistic director, will direct the production, which has been talked about for a Broadway run. Casting is still to be announced.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Musical Version of ‘Beaches’ Finds a Home', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Austin, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dart, Iris Rainer', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thomas, Thom', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Signature Theater (Arlington, Va)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-06T17:37:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7226009f-3080-5391-a423-acb88f865e1f', 'word_count': 653, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7226009f-3080-5391-a423-acb88f865e1f'}, {'abstract': 'Dereck Whittenburg, an analyst for ESPN, discusses North Carolina State’s national championship in 1983 and what to look for in the Metro Atlantic Athletic Conference tournament, among other things in a question-and-answer session.', 'web_url': 'https://thequad.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/06/talking-n-c-state-and-the-m-a-a-c-tournament/', 'snippet': 'Dereck Whittenburg, an analyst for ESPN, discusses North Carolina State’s national championship in 1983 and what to look for in the Metro Atlantic Athletic Conference tournament, among other things in a question-and-answer session.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thirty years ago, Dereck Whittenburg won a national basketball championship as a player at North Carolina State. More recently he coached at Wagner and Fordham, where he was fired midseason in December 2009.\xa0 Whittenburg still lives in the New York area and works for ESPN as a television analyst. Among the games he covers are those played in the Metro Atlantic Athletic Conference.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/07/sports/ncaabasketball/07dereck/07dereck-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 873, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'