ations', 'value': 'Fordham University', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metro Atlantic Athletic Conference', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-06T17:43:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Styczynski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Styczynski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4683621-e99d-5df7-b8c7-005d36b977f6', 'word_count': 577, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4683621-e99d-5df7-b8c7-005d36b977f6'}, {'abstract': 'Access Industries, a holding company owned by Len Blavatnik, the Russian-born billionaire investor, is one of several parties investing $60 million in Daisy, a planned service by Beats Electronics, Beats announced late Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/06/warner-music-owner-bets-on-competing-digital-services/', 'snippet': 'Access Industries, a holding company owned by Len Blavatnik, the Russian-born billionaire investor, is one of several parties investing $60 million in Daisy, a planned service by Beats Electronics, Beats announced late Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Len Blavatnik, the Russian-born billionaire investor who bought the Warner Music Group two years ago, has placed big bets on multiple digital music services as the streaming model grows around the world.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Warner Music Owner Bets on Competing Digital Services', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blavatnik, Leonard', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Iovine, Jimmy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizatio