'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/847ed0e2-c2a9-53c0-9c7c-96c6b4cc6fef', 'word_count': 972, 'uri': 'nyt://article/847ed0e2-c2a9-53c0-9c7c-96c6b4cc6fef'}, {'abstract': 'Perhaps the most intriguing wine event in a month full of them was Rieslingfeier.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/06/german-rieslings-turn-in-the-spotlight/', 'snippet': 'Perhaps the most intriguing wine event in a month full of them was Rieslingfeier.', 'lead_paragraph': 'La Paulée de New York, Daniel Johnnes’s adaptation of the Meursault harvest festival, begins this week, signifying the apogee of a remarkable month of wine in the city. La Paulée, a mélange of seminars, discussions and tastings culminating in a grand dinner in which producers and collectors share precious bottles, has been so successful that it has inspired similar events celebrating other wines.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'German Riesling’s Turn in the Spotlight', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Riesling (Wine)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Galloni, Antonio', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnnes, Daniel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wine and Spirits', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-06T17:52:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Asimov', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Asimov', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36ea14b1-3678-5cc8-ae89-877aea1d9aa0', 'word_count': 668, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36ea14b1-3678-5cc8-ae89-877aea1d9aa0'}, {'abstract': 'Other than Robinson Cano, question marks abound among the top 10 second basemen and beyond.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/06/fantasy-baseball-second-base-preview/', 'snippet': 'Other than Robinson Cano, question marks abound among the top 10 second basemen and beyond.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Justin Sablich is one half of the Sablich brothers, who provide fantasy sports advice on nytimes.com and on Twitter at @5thDownFantasy. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fantasy Baseball: Second Base Preview', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fantasy Sports', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cano, Robinson', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-06T17:56:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Justin Sablich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Justin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sablich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a564b66-100a-5c87-8345-f81db02e2c12', 'word_count': 220, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a564b66-100a-5c87-8345-f81db02e2c12'}, {'abstract': 'When The International Herald Tribune is rebranded as The International New York Times this fall, one of the great names in American journalism will fade away.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/06/fondly-recalling-a-paper-that-punched-the-times-in-the-nose/', 'snippet': 'When The International Herald Tribune is rebranded as The International New York Times this fall, one of the great names in American journalism will fade away.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ghostly vestiges of the gothic Herald Tribune logo still survive on the eastern facade of 230 West 41st Street in Midtown Manhattan, camouflaged by a faded Group Health Insurance emblem, and, more recently, dwarfed by the towering headquarters of The New York Times next door.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/06/nyregion/06cityroom-trib4/06cityroom-trib4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/06/nyregion/06cityroom-trib4/06cityroom-trib4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/06/nyregion/06cityroom-trib4/06cityroom-trib4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 426, 'width': 640, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/06/nyregion/06cityroom-trib4/06cityroom-trib4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 426, 'width': 640, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/06/nyregion/06cityroom-trib4/06cityroom-trib4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/06/nyregion/06cityroom-trib4/06cityroom-trib4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/06/nyregion/06cityroom-trib4/06cityroom-trib4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'heigh