 for military service and establishing policies to carry out those obligations, engaging government, the private sector, vetera...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Stand on the corner of H Street and Vermont Avenue in Washington, D.C., and in every direction you’ll see the ways and means of American government — the White House in front, the Treasury to the left and the huge Office of Management and Budget building down the street and to the right. This vista is both symbolic of — and essential to running — our system of governance “by the people, for the people.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Call for a National Strategy on Veterans', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coolidge, Calvin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lincoln, Abraham', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Syracuse University', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Veterans Affairs Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-06T19:33:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Haynie and Nicholas Armstrong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haynie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Armstrong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cef32a7c-b