/', 'snippet': 'Senator Rand Paul is speaking on the Senate floor to extend debate on John Brennan’s nomination. When he gets tired, the real filibuster will start.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As of 3:30 p.m. Wednesday, Senator Rand Paul of Kentucky has been speaking on the Senate floor for about three-and-a-half hours, self-indulging in an old-school filibuster against John Brennan, President Obama’s choice to run the C.I.A. At 3 p.m., Senator Mike Lee of Utah jumped in to help him, asking Mr. Paul questions so he could keep the floor. Then Ted Cruz of Texas and Jerry Moran of Kansas joined in the tirade. It’s a C-Span spectacle, but make no mistake: this isn’t the real filibuster of Mr. Brennan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obstruct and Delay', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Filibusters and Debate Curbs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Halligan, Caitlin Joan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Rand', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-06T20:31:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Firestone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Firestone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a374b11-fe53-5607-94f7-b61ae32ff87b', 'word_count': 392, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a374b11-fe53-5607-94f7-b61ae32ff87b'}, {'abstract': 'A minimalist house in a suburb of Athens is on the market for $4.4 million.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2013/03/06/greathomesanddestinations/20130306-GH-IHH.html', 'snippet': 'A minimalist house in a suburb of Athens is on the market for $4.4 million.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A minimalist house 