r the proceeds on a costly makeover.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Vodafone Should Head for a Verizon Exit', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telephones and Telecommunications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Verizon Communications Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vodafone Group Plc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-06T20:42:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Quentin Webb', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quentin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Webb', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b0a3c8a-d27a-5d8c-9279-3b1763fef75e', 'word_count': 396, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b0a3c8a-d27a-5d8c-9279-3b1763fef75e'}, {'abstract': 'Call it basketball diplomacy or stunt journalism. But the bromance between Dennis Rodman and Kim Jong-un was simply bizarre.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/07/fashion/a-traveling-violation.html', 'snippet': 'Call it basketball diplomacy or stunt journalism. But the bromance between Dennis Rodman and Kim Jong-un was simply bizarre.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Call it basketball diplomacy or stunt journalism. But the bromance between former National Basketball Association star Dennis Rodman and Kim Jong-un,\xa0the repressive leader of North Korea, was simply bizarre. Mr. Rodman’s less-than-eloquent appearance on ABC’s “This Week” did little to shed light on the North Korean trip. Twitter users, luckily, had more to say.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{