_paragraph': ' The Stone’s weekly briefing of notable philosophy-related issues and ideas from around the Web.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Is Poetry Good For Pigs?', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-06T20:52:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.c. Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/45423ba8-2f6d-543f-b2e2-0c4f12393f77', 'word_count': 501, 'uri': 'nyt://article/45423ba8-2f6d-543f-b2e2-0c4f12393f77'}, {'abstract': 'The fresh-faced models at Vionnet got a hint of sheen on the eyes and lips.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/06/backstage-beauty-report-vionnet/', 'snippet': 'The fresh-faced models at Vionnet got a hint of sheen on the eyes and lips.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was all about M.A.C. Silver Dusk Iridescent Powder for extra sheen on the fresh-faced models at Vionnet. The makeup artist Charlotte Tilbury dusted some over the T-zone, “taking one brush and literally going straight down” from the bridge of the nose to the cupid’s bow, and then lightly over the lips. The iridescent powder was also used as a highlighter in the corner of the eyes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Backstage Beauty Report | Vionnet', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beauty', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cosmetics and Toiletries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paris F