epublicans filibustered the confirmation of Caitlin J. Halligan to become a federal appeals court judge in the District of Columbia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Senate Republicans on Wednesday blocked the confirmation of Caitlin J. Halligan, a prominent New York lawyer, to become a federal appeals court judge in the District of Columbia, the second time in two years Republicans have filibustered her nomination.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Republicans Block Judicial Nominee’s Confirmation for a Second Time', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Republicans Block Judicial Nominee’s Confirmation for a Second Time', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Halligan, Caitlin Joan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Filibusters and Debate Curbs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appeals Courts (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-06T21:58:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/797b968f-5ebb-5e3c-9813-738460297165', 'word_count': 605, 'uri': 'nyt://article/797b968f-5ebb-5e3c-9813-738460297165'}, {'abstract': 'The Chilean playwright Guillermo Calderón discusses his play “Neva,” which opens at the Public Theater in its English-language debut.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/10/theater/guillermo-calderon-writer-and-director-of-neva.html', 'snippet': 'The Chilean playwright Guillermo Calderón discusses his play “Neva,” which opens at the Public Theater in its English-language debut.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Neva” may be set in a Russia on the verge of explosion, but the Chilean playwright Guillermo Calderón still calls it “my American play” because “it was born here.” As a graduate student in film at the City University of New York a decade ago he prowled Manhattan’s bookstores, where he found Janet Malcolm’s “Reading Chekhov,” which stimulated an interest in Russian culture and politics that led him to “A People’s Tragedy: The Russian Revolution 1891-1924” by Orlando Figes. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/10/arts/10CALDERON1_SPAN/10CALDERON1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 410, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/10/arts/10CALDERON1_SPAN/10CALDERON1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 410}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/10/arts/10CALDERON1_SPAN/10CALDERON1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 700, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/10/arts/10CALDERON1_SPAN/10CALDERON1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1400, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/10/arts/10CALDERON1_SPAN/10CALDERON1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/10/arts/10CALDERON1_SPAN/10CALDERON1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, '