dia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'House Tells Postal Service to Keep Six-Day Delivery', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Postal Service (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-06T22:04:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ron Nixon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nixon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5ac8774-e104-5989-94a1-371bb574f944', 'word_count': 480, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5ac8774-e104-5989-94a1-371bb574f944'}, {'abstract': 'Only vehicles sold or registered in 20 salt-belt states and the District of Columbia are affected.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/06/ford-recalling-196500-minivans-for-corrosion-problem/', 'snippet': 'Only vehicles sold or registered in 20 salt-belt states and the District of Columbia are affected.', 'lead_paragraph': '4:44 p.m., March 7 | Updated Ford is recalling about 196,500 of its 2004-7 Ford Freestar and Mercury Monterey minivans to fix a corrosion problem that prevents the fold-down third-row seats from locking safely into place, Kelli Felker, a spokeswoman for the automaker, said today.', 'print_section': 'AU', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ford Recalling 196,500 Minivans for Corrosion Problem', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ford Recalling Minivans For Corrosion Problem', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minvans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recalls and Bans of Products', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Center for Auto Safety', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ford Motor Co', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Highway Traffic Safety Administration', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-06T22:06:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f72f542-29ce-5ad9-ad19-c77a419733cb', 'word_count': 422, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f72f542-29ce-5ad9-ad19-c77a419733cb'}, {'abstract': 'This week, Doyle New York will auction off more than 400 objects belonging to the Southern decorator Charlotte Moss.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/06/going-once-going-twice/', 'snippet': 'This week, Doyle New York will auction off more than 400 objects belonging to the Southern decorator Charlotte Moss.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you are one of the many individuals who has been mourning the loss of Charlotte Moss’s treasure trove of design gems ever since she shuttered her Upper East Side town house store in 2008, you can now rejoice a bit. On Thursday at 10 a.m., Doyle New York will auction off “The Charlotte Moss Collection,” which includes over 400 objects belonging to the Southern decorator, including leftover inventory from the retail space as well as other design items she’s collected along the way. Pieces range from signed 18th-century art to a set of De Gournay hand-painted Indian tea paper wallpaper panels with an estimated price tag somewhere between $2,000 and $4,000, and the comprehensive catalog is available at doylenewyork.com leading up to the auction.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Going Once, Going Twice', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Doyle New York', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-06T22:06:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alainna Lexie Beddie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alainna', 'middlename': 'Lexie', 'lastname': 'Beddie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/715b9f9d-5be5-5f8c-bd5e-182a87b281f3', 'word_count': 125, 'uri': 'nyt://article/715b9f9d-5be5-5f8c-bd5e-182a87b281f3'}, {'abstract': 'Using a smartphone or your computer to get rid of gifts and block any traces of past loves.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/07/fashion/apps-and-web-sites-that-go-with-a-breakup.html', 'snippet': 'Using a smartphone or your computer to get rid of gifts and block any traces of past loves.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Breaking up has always been excruciating, but at least in the old days lovers could split, move on and retain their dignity. Now, in the age of social media, extrication is nearly impossible. The pain of a breakup is nourished by an endless real-time stream of Facebook status updates, Instagram photos and tweets about one’s ex. ', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/07/fashion/07ZAPPS1_SPAN/07ZAPPS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 403, 'width': 600, 'subType': 