nnequins, Then and Now', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mannequins (Dummies)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klein, William', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-06T22:30:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Moroz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moroz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2a35245-2e69-5e81-a4cf-3f33fa33380f', 'word_count': 349, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2a35245-2e69-5e81-a4cf-3f33fa33380f'}, {'abstract': 'The opening night gala for the Paul Taylor Dance Company’s three-week season at Lincoln Center included a work from 1956 and one world premiere.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/07/arts/dance/paul-taylor-dance-company-at-david-h-koch-theater.html', 'snippet': 'The opening night gala for the Paul Taylor Dance Company’s three-week season at Lincoln Center included a work from 1956 and one world premiere.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Paul Taylor has often seemed the greatest of today’s choreographers, the most imaginative and disconcerting in any genre. Tuesday’s opening night gala of his dance company’s three-week season at Lincoln Center didn’t demonstrate enoughof that top quality, but its four works — spanning from 1956 to a world premiere — represented an intelligent retrospective. They showed his diversity, from offbeat idiosyncrasy to poetic orthodoxy and from comic pratfalls to dark, wild force. They also included costumes and designs by Alex Katz and Robert Rauschenberg, and scores from jazz to Offenbach. The season that follows contains 17 other works, many of which are among Mr. Taylor’s most singular masterpieces. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/07/arts/07TAYLORjp2/07TAYLORjp2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/07/arts/07TAYLORjp2/07TAYLORjp2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/07/arts/07TAYLORjp2/07TAYLORjp2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/07/arts/07TAYLORjp2/07TAYLORjp2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/07/arts/07TAYLORjp2/07TAYLORjp2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/07/arts/07TAYLORjp2/07TAYLORjp2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/07/arts/07TAYLORjp2/07TAYLORjp2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Order and Disorder, as Dawn Casts a Glow Over a Funereal March', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Order and Disorder, as Dawn Casts a Glow Over a Funereal March', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizatio