d to be taunting the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hugo Chávez dominated Venezuelan politics for 14 years with his charismatic personality, populist policies and authoritarian methods before his death this week. His redistributionist policies brought better living conditions to millions of poor Venezuelans. But his legacy is stained by the undermining of democratic institutions and the embrace of malevolent foreign leaders like Bashar al-Assad of Syria and Mahmoud Ahmadinejad of Iran.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hugo Chávez', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hugo Chávez', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chavez, Hugo', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Venezuela', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maduro, Nicolas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T01:52:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/63eb74f9-480c-5179-9eba-ea0cc78971ff', 'word_count': 360, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63eb74f9-480c-5179-9eba-ea0cc78971ff'}, {'abstract': 'China’s voracious appetite for ivory continues to devastate Africa’s elephants.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/07/opinion/death-of-the-elephants.html', 'snippet': 'China’s voracious appetite for ivory continues to devastate Africa’s elephants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Day after day, the slaughter of the elephants continues at a record pace — 25,000 killed in 2011, conservationists say, and more than 30,000 last year. A study from the Wildlife Conservation Society shows that 60 percent of all African forest elephants (a slightly smaller subspecies of the African savanna elephant) have been killed in the last decade for their ivory, leaving about 80,000 in their primary habitats in Western and Central Africa. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Death in the Forests', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Death in the Forests', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ivory', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elephants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endangered and Extinct Species', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poaching (Wildlife)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T01:52:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c90b815-3f28-5382-9ba0-a8b1284c0ca9', 'word_count': 400, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c90b815-3f28-5382-9ba0-a8b1284c0ca9'}, {'abstract': 'At a time when Republicans are divided on many social issues, the budget wars are one of the few things that unite them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/07/opinion/from-one-budget-fight-to-the-next.html', 'snippet': 'At a time when Republicans are divided on many social issues, the budget wars are one of the few things that unite them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Unable to stop the sequester’s job-killing spending cuts, President Obama now says he wants to move past the endless wars of budget attrition. Though he still wants a long-term deficit deal, he said last week, it is time to turn to immigration, gun control, universal preschool, a higher minimum wage and voting reform.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From One Budget Fight to the Next', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From One Budget Fight to the Next', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T01:57:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/db6a5d39-d314-5922-a413-03b2ddf5db86', 'word_count': 523, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db6a5d39-d314-5922-a413-03b2ddf5db86'}, {'abstract': 'The Gunnison sage grouse, only recently known to science, is going extinct, right before our eyes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/07/opinion/the-plight-of-the-gunnison-sage-grouse.html', 'snippet': 'The Gunnison sage grouse, only recently known to science, is going extinct, right before our eyes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ITHACA, N.Y.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/07/opinion/0306OPEDroumieu/0306OPEDroumieu-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 650, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/07/opinio