cs out “of duty, and only because it is for France.” His remarks will be published in a center-right magazine, Valeurs Actuelles, whose editors said they had not spoken directly with Mr. Sarkozy but with close associates, who presumably did so with his encouragement. Mr. Sarkozy, 58, who narrowly lost his attempt at re-election in May, said that politics “bores him to death,” but that “sadly, there may come a moment when the question is no longer, ‘Do you want to?’ but, ‘Do you have a choice?’\xa0” He predicted a “social crisis” and a “financial crisis of an uncommon violence.” Mr. Sarkozy’s comments were greeted with pleasure by his supporters and derision by his critics. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'France: Sarkozy Dips a Toe Back In', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'France: Sarkozy Dips a Toe Back In', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sarkozy, Nicolas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Erlanger, Steven', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T02:54:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Erlanger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erlanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/9847a7ed-d70f-5461-b978-acecfd07f99c', 'word_count': 144, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9847a7ed-d70f-5461-b978-acecfd07f99c'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on March 7, 2013.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/07/pageoneplus/corrections-march-7-2013.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on March 7, 2013.', 'lea