'uri': 'nyt://article/7d425954-866c-5164-b137-5bdc10d7fc19'}, {'abstract': 'The senator from Kentucky staged a filibuster over the government’s use of lethal drone strikes, forcing the Senate to delay the expected confirmation of John O. Brennan to lead the C.I.A.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/06/rand-paul-does-not-go-quietly-into-the-night/', 'snippet': 'The senator from Kentucky staged a filibuster over the government’s use of lethal drone strikes, forcing the Senate to delay the expected confirmation of John O. Brennan to lead the C.I.A.', 'lead_paragraph': '1:27 a.m. | Updated WASHINGTON — A small group of Republicans, led by Senator Rand Paul of Kentucky, stalled the Senate on Wednesday by waging a nearly 13-hour old-school, speak-until-you-can-speak-no-more filibuster over the government’s use of lethal drone strikes — forcing the Senate to delay the expected confirmation of John O. Brennan to lead the Central Intelligence Agency.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Republicans, Led by Rand Paul, Finally End Filibuster', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drones (Pilotless Planes)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Filibusters and Debate Curbs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brennan, John O', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Rand', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central Intelligence Agency', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T03:01:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Parker', 'person': 