Against the Bobcats, the Nets Receive Another Chance to Start Over', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Nets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Charlotte Bobcats', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T03:24:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zach Schonbrun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zach', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schonbrun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cdf93c8a-c17b-565b-b087-f0a2d97f6e90', 'word_count': 686, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cdf93c8a-c17b-565b-b087-f0a2d97f6e90'}, {'abstract': 'Detroit’s City Council voted on Wednesday to challenge state plans to assign an outside emergency manager to shore up the city’s troubled finances.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/07/us/michigan-detroit-council-resists-state-plan-for-emergency-manager.html', 'snippet': 'Detroit’s City Council voted on Wednesday to challenge state plans to assign an outside emergency manager to shore up the city’s troubled finances.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Detroit’s City Council voted on Wednesday to challenge state plans to assign an outside emergency manager to shore up the city’s troubled finances, even as Mayor Dave Bing announced that he would take no part in a challenge. “We need to end the drama and infighting and understand that whether we like it or not, an emergency financial manager is coming to Detroit,” Mr. Bing said. In a hearing planned for Tuesday, the City Council, which would lose authority with state intervention, is expected to argue that although Detroit’s financial circumstances are indeed dire, the city has a plan for repairing them. Gov. Rick Snyder, who last week deemed an outside manager a necessity for the city, would be asked to reconsider, a possibility Mr. Bing and others view as remote. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Michigan: Detroit Council Resists State Plan for Emergency Manager', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Midwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Michigan: Detroit Council Resists State Plan For Emergency Manager', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Detroit (Mich)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'City Councils', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bing, Dave', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Michigan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T03:34:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Monica Davey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Monica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/779f72c6-1436-56d5-9b46-76b7edda3830', 'word_count': 131, 'uri': 'nyt://article/779f72c6-1436-56d5-9b46-76b7edda3830'}, {'abstract': 'Animals suffer. So what excuse is there for treating them badly? Is “culture” a reason?', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/06/amid-suffering-animal-welfare-legislation-still-far-off-in-china/', 'snippet': 'Animals suffer. So what excuse is there for treating them badly? Is “culture” a reason?', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — About animals, “The question is not, ‘Can they reason?’ nor, ‘Can they talk?’ but, ‘Can they suffer?’” So wrote Jeremy Bentham, the English philosopher, more than 200 years ago.', 'source': 'The New York Tim