who has been jailed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — The lead defender of Ukraine’s jailed former prime minister, Yulia V. Tymoshenko, was stripped of his seat in the Ukrainian Parliament on Wednesday by the country’s top administrative court, despite stern warnings by Western officials who said the case was a matter of political retribution. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ex-Premier’s Ally Expelled From Ukraine Parliament', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ex-Premier’s Ally Expelled From Ukraine Parliament', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tymoshenko, Yulia V', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vlasenko, Sergey', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T04:51:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By David M. Herszenhorn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/78a072e5-de56-5282-841c-3262c4055d95', 'word_count': 262, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78a072e5-de56-5282-841c-3262c4055d95'}, {'abstract': 'Neatly tailored and to the knee, all manner of coats this season offer a sharp measure of austerity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/07/t-magazine/straight-to-the-point.html', 'snippet': 'Neatly tailored and to the knee, all manner of coats this season offer a sharp measure of austerity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Neatly tailored and to the knee, all manner of coats this season offer a sharp measure of austerity.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Straight to the Point', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T05:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TDesign', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Magazine', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/65997f98-10e9-5812-b044-5e350f745df3', 'word_count': 18, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65997f98-10e9-5812-b044-5e350f745df3'}, {'abstract': 'Do we need to change the rules about healthful eating?', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/07/eat-your-heart-out/', 'snippet': 'Do we need to change the rules about healthful eating?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the last several decades, it has become accepted wisdom that consuming saturated fat, the type found in meat and butter, is bad for you. Starting in the 1960s, studies showed convincingly that saturated fat raises cholesterol levels and that these elevated levels, especially of low-density lipoprotein cholesterol, or LDL (the so-called bad cholesterol), increase heart disease. Studies also showed that consuming polyunsaturated fats — safflower, corn and soybean oils — reduced people’s levels of overall cholesterol and LDL and should be encouraged.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/05/health/05well_column/05well_column-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 661, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/05/health/05well_column/05well_column-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 661}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'captio