ocations', 'value': 'Philippines', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Golan Heights', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T05:44:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Cowell and Hania Mourtada', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cowell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Hania', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mourtada', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b224099-30a4-5ba5-bbcb-84460e5bea24', 'word_count': 759, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b224099-30a4-5ba5-bbcb-84460e5bea24'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/07/arts/television/whats-on-thursday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '10 P.M. (Sundance) MARATHON MAN (1976) Dustin Hoffman (above, with Marthe Keller) portrays Babe, a Columbia graduate student who unwittingly finds himself in a mysterious plot involving diamonds and a Nazi war criminal named Szell (Laurence Olivier, in an Oscar-nominated role) with a penchant for dentistry in this thriller from John Schlesinger, adapted by William Goldman from his novel. “Is it safe?” Szell asks. “Is what safe?” Babe replies. “Is it safe?” Szell asks again before fiddling with a live nerve in one of Babe’s teeth. “High-level conspiracies really aren’t that interesting unless we can get a fix on who is doing what to whom, which is never clear here,” Vincent Canby wrote in The New York Times. “Yet the individual details of ‘Marathon Man,’ the performances, and the attention given to its physical settings — in New York, Paris and South America — keep one’s belief willingly suspended by a wickedly thin thread.” The film “hasn’t a real idea in its head,” he added. “It just wants to scare the hell out of you — and it does.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Thursday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T06:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/57a240cd-f02a-5f4f-b237-bd11bdee9969', 'word_count': 675, 'uri': 'nyt://article/57a240cd-f02a-5f4f-b237-bd11bdee9969'}, {'abstract': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/07/news-quiz-march-7-2013/', 'snippet': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'See what you know about the news below. To prepare, you might scan the articles or summaries on today’s paper. Good luck!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News Quiz | March 7, 2013', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T06:30:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anastasia Economides', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anastasia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Economides', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization':