eople who would like to dip a toe into the American Crossword Puzzle Tournament is “I wouldn’t feel comfortable. I don’t know anyone.” The other is “How exactly does Dan Feyer do that?”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A.C.P.T. 2013: How to Have Fun', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T08:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d18bf7d5-f61a-5e5f-861a-8b04a50b7dec', 'word_count': 966, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d18bf7d5-f61a-5e5f-861a-8b04a50b7dec'}, {'abstract': 'On melding political and social themes in art and more.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/07/a-conversation-with-video-artist-nalini-malani/', 'snippet': 'On melding political and social themes in art and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nalini Malani is a pioneering video and installation artist who lives and works in Mumbai. Born in Karachi in 1946, she came to India as a refugee of the partition of India, an experience that deeply informs her art practice. Her piece at the Kochi-Muziris Biennale, “In Search of Vanished Blood (2012)”, is a “video play” that melds Greek and Indian myths with the revolutionary poetry of Faiz Ahmed Faiz through projection, sound and hand-drawn animation. The effect is a multilayered commentary on social fracturing, gender violence and the echoes of American hegemony.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Conversation With: Video Artist Nalini Malani', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T09:03:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Meara Sharma and Henry Peck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Meara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sharma', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Henry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Peck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/964d3806-b2fd-5da1-9ec7-1b5f68de3aa1', 'word_count': 1090, 'uri': 'nyt://article/964d3806-b2fd-5da1-9ec7-1b5f68de3aa1'}, {'abstract': 'Can you identify the literary device found in the sentence?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/07/test-yourself-english-march-7-2013/', 'snippet': 'Can you identify the literary device found in the sentence?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The question was written by Shannon Doyne. It comes from the article “Chasing the Higgs Boson.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Test Yourself | English, March 7, 2013', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T09:27:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/56698052-d5f9-5b94-a3cc-97a86cec9636', 'word_count': 45, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56698052-d5f9-5b94-a3cc-97a86cec9636'}, {'abstract': 'A week after Pope Benedict XVI formally retired, cardinals gathered in Rome to choose his successor went into a fourth day of soundings and deliberations on Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/08/world/europe/cardinals-conclave-pope.html', 'snippet': 'A week after Pope Benedict XVI formally retired, cardinals gathered in Rome to choose his successor went into a fourth day of soundings and deliberations on Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VATICAN CITY — A week after Pope Benedict XVI formally retired, cardinals assembled in here to choose his successor went into a fourth day of soundings and deliberations on Thursday without reaching a decision so far on a date to begin the secret papal balloting known as a conclave, a Vatican spokesman said. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cardinals Hold 4th Day of Talks on New Pope', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cardinals Hold 4th Day of Talks on New Pope', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cardinals (Roman Catholic Prelates)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rome (Italy)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Benedict XVI', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T09:27:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Donadio and Alan Cowell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Donadio', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cowell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab57aa28-7893-5e2c-9489-d64102db4785', 'word_count': 342, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab57aa28-7893-5e2c-9489-d64102db4785'}, {'abstract': 'How many LED white lights are included in the public art sculpture?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/07/led-light-sculpture-makes-bay-bridge-a-glowing-attraction/', 'snippet': 'How many LED white lights are included in the public art sculpture?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In “Long Stuck in Obscurity, Bay Bridge Will Go From Drab Gray to Glowing,” Malia Wollan writes about the Bay Bridge’s transformation into a 1.8-mile light sculpture.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'LED Light Sculpture Makes Bay Bridge a Glowing Attraction', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T09:30:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Gonchar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonchar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/432d9188-990f-50b9-bd92-42581aa8b669', 'word_count': 128, 'uri': 'nyt://article/432d9188-990f-50b9-bd92-42581aa8b669'}, {'abstract': 'The rejection at a major international conference  highlighted the difficulties of reaching a global consensus on protecting many kinds of endangered wildlife.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/08/world/asia/proposal-to-ban-trade-in-polar-bear-parts-is-rejected.html', 'snippet': 'The rejection at a major international conference  highlighted the difficulties of reaching a global consensus on protecting many kinds of endangered wildlife.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BANGKOK — A proposal to ban international trade in polar bear parts was rejected on Thursday at a major conference on wildlife trade, highlighting the difficulties of reaching a global consensus on protecting many kinds of endangered wildlife. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Proposal to Ban Trade in Polar Bear Parts Is Rejected', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Proposals to Protect Polar Bears Fail', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endangered and Extinct Species', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polar Bears', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Thailand', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T09:51:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bettina Wassener', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bettina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wassener', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/496970ef-d3ac-51aa-8b6d-5e4a7dd314e3', 'word_count': 242, 'uri': 'nyt://article/496970ef-d3ac-51aa-8b6d-5e4a7dd314e3'}, {'abstract': 'The Federal Reserve must stop its internal wrangling and impose more effective control over the biggest banks, and Sheila Bair is the kind of strong regulator to lead the effort, an economist writes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/07/filling-a-fed-vacuum-in-bank-supervision/', 'snippet': 'The Federal Reserve must stop its internal wrangling and impose more effective control over the biggest banks, and Sheila Bair is the kind of strong regulator to lead the effort, an economist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Simon Johnson, former chief economist of the International Monetary Fund, is the Ronald A. Kurtz Professor of Entrepreneurship at the M.I.T. Sloan School of Management and co-author of “White House Burning: The Founding Fathers, Our National Debt, and Why It Matters to You.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Filling a Fed Vacuum in Bank Supervision', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bair, Sheila C', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T10:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Simon Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Simon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/59184123-49fe-5ee7-95ea-b71346920c31', 'word_count': 1805, 'uri': 'nyt://article/59184123-49fe-5ee7-95ea-b71346920c31'}, {'abstract': 'Mikel Aristregi went to Mongolia to document street children. Instead, he found homeless alcoholics living underground among the pipes that run beneath the streets of Ulan Bator.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/07/underground-and-off-the-radar-in-ulan-bator/', 'snippet': 'Mikel Aristregi went to Mongolia to document street children. Instead, he found homeless alcoholics living underground among the pipes that run beneath the streets of Ulan Bator.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2004, Mikel Aristregi documented street children in Cambodia, fascinated by the bonds they forged among themselves, a coping mechanism against an onslaught of threats along the harsh landscape of Phnom Penh’s boulevards. So when he learned of children living in the sewers of Ulan Bator, Mongolia, he went there in pursuit of a similar project. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Way Down and Out in Ulan Bator', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alcohol Abuse', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Temperature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Health Organization', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mongolia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T10:00:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt McCann', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McCann', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2370906-59be-51fb-9cd6-adb2419e38d7', 'word_count': 770, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2370906-59be-51fb-9cd6-adb2419e38d7'}, {'abstract': 'You may not remember the last time Gareth Bale and Tottenham faced Inter Milan, but fans of both clubs will never forget.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/07/the-last-time-inter-saw-gareth-bale/', 'snippet': 'You may not remember the last time Gareth Bale and Tottenham faced Inter Milan, but fans of both clubs will never forget.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Champions League has a pretty sexy first four for its quarterfinals — Real Madrid, Dortmund, Paris Saint-Germain and Juventus — but Thursday is the Europa League’s day, and it has at least one matchup no one will want to miss: Inter Milan against Tottenham at White Hart Lane (Fox Soccer, 3 p.m. ET). ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Last Time Inter Saw Gareth Bale', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bale, Gareth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Inter Milan (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tottenham Hotspur (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T10:00:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Das', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Das', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e56e837-ea7f-5084-b6a2-9230a55c8d0e', 'word_count': 387, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e56e837-ea7f-5084-b6a2-9230a55c8d0e'}, {'abstract': 'Are many seniors so “underscheduled” that the year is a waste and might be better spent in an internship, or going to college early? Or, does senior year play an important emotional role in college readiness?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/07/should-students-be-allowed-to-skip-senior-year-of-high-school/', 'snippet': 'Are many seniors so “underscheduled” that the year is a waste and might be better spent in an internship, or going to college early? Or, does senior year play an important emotional role in college readiness?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Is senior year just about partying? If so, should prepared students be allowed to skip it and spend a year volunteering, or go on to college early? Or, does senior year play an key role in helping students transition emotionally to being on their own?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption'