ee5cac6-3c90-5add-bd39-c79f5ed2da40'}, {'abstract': 'Is there life after caregiving, and if so what it is like?', 'web_url': 'https://newoldage.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/07/after-the-caregiving-ends/', 'snippet': 'Is there life after caregiving, and if so what it is like?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In January, the 93-year-old mother of my oldest friend died in a Chicago suburb. Suzy was exceptionally close to her mother, and had long dreaded saying a final goodbye. But when it came time to do so — after a year in which her mother struggled with illness and increasing disability — my friend was surprisingly at peace.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After the Caregiving Ends', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elder Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T15:05:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judith Graham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Graham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/97df1122-ac23-504a-afe5-7354c806e14f', 'word_count': 1212, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97df1122-ac23-504a-afe5-7354c806e14f'}, {'abstract': "The Times's Scott Shane says a classified report poses risks for John O. Brennan, the nominee to lead the C.I.A.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/us/100000002105477/challenges-for-brennan.html', 'snippet': "The Times's Scott Shane says a classified report poses risks for John O. Brennan, the nominee to lead the C.I.A.", 'lead_paragraph': "The Times's Scott Shane says a classified report poses risks for John O. Brennan, the nominee to lead the C.I.A.", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/07/us/video-tc-130307/video-tc-130307-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/07/us/video-tc-130307/video-tc-130307-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/07/us/video-tc-130307/video-tc-130307-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/07/us/video-tc-130307/video-tc-130307-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/07/us/video-tc-130307/video-tc-130307-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Challenges for Brennan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central Intelligence Agency', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brennan, John O', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T15:11:15+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'Ben Werschkul, Channon Hodge and Pedro Rafael Rosado', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Werschkul', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Channon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hodge', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Pedro', 'middlename': 'Rafael', 'lastname': 'Rosado', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/37a89a3f-4778-5571-8ba0-c7ce87531efc', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/37a89a3f-4778-5571-8ba0-c7ce87531efc'}, {'abstract': 'Michel Gondry’s film “The We and the I” captures the chaos, glee and heartache of the last day of school for a group of boisterous South Bronx high school students.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/08/movies/the-we-and-the-i-directed-by-michel-gondry.html', 'snippet': 'Michel Gondry’s film “The We and the I” captures the chaos, glee and heartache of the last day of school for a group of boisterous South Bronx high school students.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Any adult who has ridden public transportation in New York around 3 o’clock on a weekday afternoon will find the opening scenes of “The We and the I” familiar, perhaps dismayingly so. At certain stops the bus or subway car will suddenly be flooded with adolescents releasing their pent-up energies in a confined space. Their loudness, their rudeness, the lack of consideration they display as they flirt, fight, tease and shout can be overwhelming, and can cause even tolerant old-timers to think grouchy thoughts. What’s the matter with kids these days?', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Last Stop, Adulthood, the Bronx', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Last Stop, Adulthood, The Bronx', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gondry, Michel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T15:14:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf20e059-6783-5cf5-ba5e-325705d8033e', 'word_count': 830, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf20e059-6783-5cf5-ba5e-325705d8033e'}, {'abstract': 'His new, posthumous memoir sheds light on the Saturday Night Massacre.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/07/the-bilious-robert-bork/', 'snippet': 'His new, posthumous memoir sheds light on the Saturday Night Massacre.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The late Robert Bork became infamous long before the Senate rejected his nomination for the Supreme Court in 1987. Fourteen years before, to be exact, when President Richard Nixon ordered Mr. Bork to fire the Watergate Special Prosecutor Archibald Cox, and Mr. Bork complied—the so-called Saturday Night Massacre.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Bilious Robert Bork', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Watergate Affair', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bork, Robert H', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cox, Archibald', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T15:14:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lincoln Caplan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lincoln', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caplan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/10627c3a-a761-5105-9792-58da93d25305', 'word_count': 378, 'uri': 'nyt://article/10627c3a-a761-5105-9792-58da93d25305'}, {'abstract': 'The two new comedy shows, “The Spoils of Babylon,” a comedy serial produced by Will Ferrell and Adam McKay, and “The Birthday Boys,” a variety show produced by Ben Stiller and Bob Odenkirk, would make their debuts on IFC this year.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/07/ifc-orders-new-comedy-shows-from-will-ferrell-ben-stiller-and-bob-odenkirk/', 'snippet': 'The two new comedy shows, “The Spoils of Babylon,” a comedy serial produced by Will Ferrell and Adam McKay, and “The Birthday Boys,” a variety show produced by Ben Stiller and Bob Odenkirk, would make their debuts on IFC this year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Will Ferrell, Adam McKay, Ben Stiller and Bob Odenkirk aren’t just the stars and producers of comedy films and television series that will live in perpetuity on DVD players, DVRs and cable-TV programming lineups. They’re also among the creative talent responsible for two new comedy series that IFC said Thursday it had picked up.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'IFC Orders New Comedy Shows from Will Ferrell, Ben Stiller and Bob Odenkirk', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ferrell, Will', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McKay, Adam', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Odenkirk, Bob', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Piedmont, Matt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stiller, Ben', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Independent Film Channel', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Monty Python's Flying Circus", 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T15:22:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b7b6d6f-ce65-5794-8421-d425a016ffe8', 'word_count': 345, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b7b6d6f-ce65-5794-8421-d425a016ffe8'}, {'abstract': 'Goldman Sachs has lured away Kate Richdale, Morgan Stanley’s chief of investment banking in Asia, to be Goldman’s head of investment banking services for Asia, excluding Japan.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/03/07/goldman-hires-a-top-executive-in-asia/', 'snippet': 'Goldman Sachs has lured away Kate Richdale, Morgan Stanley’s chief of investment banking in Asia, to be Goldman’s head of investment banking services for Asia, excluding Japan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Goldman Sachs has lured away Morgan Stanley’s chief of investment banking in Asia. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Goldman Hires a Top Executive in Asia', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Morgan Stanley', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Thomson Reuters Corporation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Far East, South and Southeast Asia and Pacific Areas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hong Kong', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T15:35:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a275fc6-623c-55be-901a-0dae6d0260d6', 'word_count': 226, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a275fc6-623c-55be-901a-0dae6d0260d6'}, {'abstract': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/07/the-gun-report-march-7-2013/', 'snippet': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You read the items in today’s gun report, and you know what your first thought is? Thank goodness no children died. But rare is the day when no children are shot. Today we have two examples – a 16-year-old shot near a high school in Northern California and a 5-year-old boy shot in the knee while leaving a daycare center.\xa0In both cases, you wonder about the lingering aftereffects, both physically and emotionally.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Gun Report: March 7, 2013', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Antioch (Calif)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARLINGTON (TEX)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colorado', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Holyoke (Mass)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Miami (Fla)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Phoenix (Ariz)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pittsburgh (Pa)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T15:41:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Nocera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nocera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ca2d406-9f61-5935-af1b-73ea9ae28101', 'word_count': 591, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ca2d406-9f61-5935-af1b-73ea9ae28101'}, {'abstract': 'There is a lot of talk about a lot of victories in the N.H.L. and N.B.A. (and a lot of points by the Lakers).', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/08/sports/hawks-heat-and-streaks-leading-off.html', 'snippet': 'There is a lot of talk about a lot of victories in the N.H.L. and N.B.A. (and a lot of points by the Lakers).', 'lead_paragraph': 'Midway through the N.H.L. season and roughly midway through the N.B.A. slog, we have been greeted with a full blast of streak mania, conveniently being played out on a hype machine near you. Having the Chicago Blackhawks on a 24-game points streak and the Miami Heat on a 16-game winning streak at the same time is wonderfully easy fodder for the screaming TV types who can mindlessly compare the two, ad nauseam. It is also cause for the conga line that has formed in the N.H.L. offices, which cannot believe its good fortune to be mentioned in the same sentence as the N.B.A. Lockout? What lockout? What concussion epidemic? How ‘bout them ‘Hawks!!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/sports/golf/08leadingpic/08leadingpic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 497, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/08/sports/golf/08leadingpic/08leadingpic-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 497}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/sports/golf/08leadingpic/08leadingpic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 849, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/sports/golf/08leadingpic/08leadingpic-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1697, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/sports/golf/08leadingpic/08lead