583-00745e669cc0'}, {'abstract': 'O.D. Anosike, last season’s national rebounding leader, discusses his career at Siena and what the future might hold for him in a question-and-answer session.', 'web_url': 'https://thequad.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/07/top-rebounder-nears-end-of-college-career/', 'snippet': 'O.D. Anosike, last season’s national rebounding leader, discusses his career at Siena and what the future might hold for him in a question-and-answer session.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last season, Siena’s O. D. Anosike won the national rebounding crown, and this season, as his team limps into the Metro Atlantic Athletic Conference tournament with a 7-23 record, he is locked in a tight battle with Colorado’s Andre Roberson to defend that title.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Top Rebounder Nears End of College Career', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'NCAA Basketball Championships (Men)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metro Atlantic Athletic Conference', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Collegiate Athletic Assn', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T16:13:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Styczynski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Styczynski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/87615520-4d6d-5bdc-9eec-f7b665d0de3b', 'word_count': 849, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87615520-4d6d-5bdc-9eec-f7b665d0de3b'}, {'abstract': 'Two bars at the Waldorf-Astoria:  Peacock Alley, which is  festive, and the Bull and Bear, a little less so.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/07/booming/peacock-alley-a-bar-that-lives-up-to-its-name-and-setting.html', 'snippet': 'Two bars at the Waldorf-Astoria:  Peacock Alley, which is  festive, and the Bull and Bear, a little less so.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sometimes, a cocktail bar in a landmark hotel really can be as impressive as its setting, and Peacock Alley at the Waldorf-Astoria is, happily, one of them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/07/booming/07drink-booming-waldorf3/07drink-booming-waldorf3-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 441, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/07/booming/07drink-booming-waldorf3/07drink-booming-waldorf3-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 441}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/07/booming/07drink-booming-waldorf3/07drink-booming-waldorf3-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 752, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/07/booming/07drink-booming-waldorf3/07drink-booming-waldorf3-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 964, 'width': 1312, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/07/booming/07drink-booming-waldorf3/07drink-booming-waldorf3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/07/booming/07drink-booming-waldorf3/07drink-booming-waldorf3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/07/booming/07drink-booming-waldorf3/07drink-booming-waldorf3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Peacock Alley, a Bar that Lives Up to  Its Name and Setting', 'kicker': 'A Quiet Drink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baby Boomers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bars and Nightclubs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T16:28:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Booming', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Reddicliffe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reddicliffe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/45b3dda4-8cd3-5c78-b574-2b453f50fcc1', 'word_count': 919, 'uri': 'nyt://article/45b3dda4-8cd3-5c78-b574-2b453f50fcc1'}, {'abstract': 'Expectations were soaring for two new pieces from the choreographers Alexei Ratmansky and Christopher Wheeldon at the Royal Ballet. But after the premiere, the reviews were, for the most part, far from sky high.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/07/high-stakes-for-2-royal-ballet-premieres/', 'snippet': 'Expectations were soaring for two new pieces from the choreographers Alexei Ratmansky and Christopher Wheeldon at the Royal Ballet. But after the premiere, the reviews were, for the most part, far from sky high.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Alexei Ratmansky and Christopher Wheeldon are, with reason, frequently referred to as the most important ballet choreographers working today. A new ballet by either is reason for excitement, so it was quite a coup for the Royal Ballet — and a shot in the arm for the company’s new director, Kevin O’Hare — when the company announced last year that two commissions were in the bag, on a single program.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/07/blogs/07rdv-ballet07a/07rdv-ballet07a-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 533, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/07/blogs/07rdv-ballet07a/07rdv-ballet07a-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 533}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/07/blogs/07rdv-ballet07a/07rdv-ballet07a-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 909, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/07/blogs/07rdv-ballet07a/07rdv-ballet07a-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1819, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/07/blogs/07rdv-ballet07a/07rdv-ballet07a-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/07/blogs/07rdv-ballet07a/07rdv-ballet07a-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/07/blogs/07rdv-ballet07a/07rdv-ballet07a-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'High Stakes for 2 Royal Ballet Premieres', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Britten, Benjamin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ratmansky, Alexei', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wheeldon, Christopher', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN BALLET THEATER', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Ballet', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Royal Ballet', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Royal Opera House', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Apollo (Ballet)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T16:35:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roslyn Sulcas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roslyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sulcas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/86f6d1c1-88fb-594b-be36-782f6d5a2f31', 'word_count': 529, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86f6d1c1-88fb-594b-be36-782f6d5a2f31'}, {'abstract': 'Employers are shifting more of the cost of health care to workers.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/07/workers-share-of-health-costs-is-likely-to-continue-rising/', 'snippet': 'Employers are shifting more of the cost of health care to workers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Workers are paying a greater share of their health care costs, and that trend is likely to continue over the next several years, a new report on employer-based health plans finds.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Workers’ Share of Health Costs Is Likely to Continue Rising', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Medical Plans:\r\nA Bigger Bite', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T16:45:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e3caf259-a939-555c-a300-aed34f81d2d1', 'word_count': 322, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e3caf259-a939-555c-a300-aed34f81d2d1'}, {'abstract': 'Kickstarter is successful and popular. You know that. I want to talk about what it has done to my brain, and may soon do to yours: Kickstarter is turning me into an investor.', 'web_url': 'https://open.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/07/this-is-my-brain-on-kickstarter/', 'snippet': 'Kickstarter is successful and popular. You know that. I want to talk about what it has done to my brain, and may soon do to yours: Kickstarter is turning me into an investor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'These days, Kickstarter is close to a household name, raising nearly $500 million for books, movies, podcasts, design objects, food items and anything else someone might come up with. I just helped a coffee shop in Oakland buy a roaster. I helped Ze Frank bring back his transcendent video show. I backed my favorite menswear video series and blog. I backed an animation made of engraved wooden tiles. And yes, I backed the Pebble.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'This Is My Brain on Kickstarter', 'kicker': 'Open', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T16:46:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andre Behrens', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andre', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Behrens', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6ec665e-0f41-503a-ab88-ecd88868ed84', 'word_count': 1267, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6ec665e-0f41-503a-ab88-ecd88868ed84'}, {'abstract': 'Doug McDermott, a two-time Missouri Valley Conference player of the year, could be a dynamic player in the N.C.A.A. tournament, but first Creighton has to get there.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/08/sports/ncaabasketball/creighton-has-mvcs-best-player-in-doug-mcdermott-but-no-guarantee.html', 'snippet': 'Doug McDermott, a two-time Missouri Valley Conference player of the year, could be a dynamic player in the N.C.A.A. tournament, but first Creighton has to get there.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The moves. The smoothness. The deadeye release. Even on television, almost everything that Doug McDermott of Creighton used to score 41 points against Wichita State on Saturday appeared so familiar to Ed Schilling that he had to smile.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/sports/ncaabasketball/08creighton-pic/08creighton-pic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/08/sports/ncaabasketball/08creighton-pic/08creighton-pic-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/sports/ncaabasketball/08creighton-pic/08creighton-pic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/sports/ncaabasketball/08creighton-pic/08creighton-pic-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1361, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/sports/ncaabasketball/08creighton-pic/08creighton-pic-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/08/sports/ncaabasketball/08creighton-pic/08creighton-pic-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/sports/ncaabasketball/08creighton-pic/08creighton-pic-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Creighton Star Seeking a Bigger Stage', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Junior at Creighton Has Worked to Become a Star; Now He Needs a Stage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Borzi, Pat', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball (College)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McDermott, Doug', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Creighton University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Missouri Valley Conference', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'NCAA Basketball Championships (Men)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T16:49:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pat Borzi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pat', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borzi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9111c677-96a0-5805-afe4-60242512d31c', 'word_count': 1174, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9111c677-96a0-5805-afe4-60242512d31c'}, {'abstract': 'Why are people on the F.B.I.’s terrorist watch list legally entitled to buy guns?', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/07/the-terror-loophole/', 'snippet': 'Why are people on the F.B.I.’s terrorist watch list legally entitled to buy guns?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The law that requires background checks on gun buyers is full of loopholes, some big and some small, but the most egregious loophole of all may be the fact that people on the F.B.I.’s terrorist watch list are legally entitled to buy firearms and explosives. And they have been doing so at an alarming rate. Between February 2004 and December 2010, individuals whose names turned up on the list were cleared to purchase firearms or explosives a total of 1,321 times, according to the General Accounting Office. Felons, illegal immigrants and mentally ill applicants are barred on the obvious grounds that they could present a heightened risk of violence. Not so, terrorist suspects — an anomaly that congress has occasionally tsk-tsked over since the 9/11 atrocities, but done nothing substantial to repair.Senator Frank Lautenberg, Democrat of New Jersey, has reintroduced a worthy measure to close this “terror gap”— eight years after his initial attempt failed. It would give the Attorney General authority to stop a firearm or explosive sale when a background check reveals the buyer is a known or suspected terrorist who the Attorney General reasonably believes may be planning mayhem. The National Rifle Association opposed the measure in the past because the terrorist watch list has been shown to contain errors. That’s hardly a justification for extending carte blanche to terrorist suspects. Besides, the Lautenberg bill includes written guidelines and due process safeguards that would permit individuals to challenge denials. There’s really no good reason for inaction, unless of course fear of the gun lobby counts as an excuse.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Terror Loophole', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lautenberg, Frank R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T16:50:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Francis X. Clines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Francis', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Clines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/027e3517-ee23-5d21-a82d-a8f42d5cd482', 'word_count': 261, 'uri': 'nyt://article/027e3517-ee23-5d21-a82d-a8f42d5cd482'}, {'abstract': 'At times, I have to admit, there is absolutely no response to my cancer that seems acceptable to me, probably because the cancer isn’t.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/07/living-with-cancer-for-the-birds/', 'snippet': 'At times, I have to admit, there is absolutely no response to my cancer that seems acceptable to me, probably because the cancer isn’t.', 'lead_paragraph': '“There’s nothing makes us feel so much alive as to see others die,” exclaims a dying Ralph Touchett in Henry James’s “Portrait of a Lady.” At my most snarky, it seems to me that there’s nothing makes some people so invigorated as to see others debilitated by cancer or by medical responses to it. To my beloved friends, I hiss what must be tedious recriminations against off-the-wall reactions to my continuing treatments. But here I’ll simply wing it. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/07/health/07well_gubar/07well_gubar-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 218, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/07/health/07well_gubar/07well_gubar-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 218}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/07/health/07well_gubar/07well_gubar-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 372, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/07/health/07well_gubar/07well_gubar-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 745, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/07/health/07well_gubar/07well_gubar-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/07/health/07well_gubar/07well_gubar-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/07/health/07well_gubar/07well_gubar-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Living With Cancer: For the Birds', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cancer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T16:57:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susan Gubar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gubar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c2e79d7-d084-5380-9101-e335de3f8729', 'word_count': 844, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c2e79d7-d084-5380-9101-e335de3f8729'}, {'abstract': 'Syrian rebels released video on Thursday showing six of the 21 Filipino United Nations peacekeepers they abducted the day before in the Golan Heights.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/07/video-of-captive-u-n-peacekeepers-in-syria/', 'snippet': 'Syrian rebels released video on Thursday showing six of the 21 Filipino United Nations peacekeepers they abducted the day before in the Golan Heights.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last Updated, 8:19 p.m. One day after Syrian rebels seized 21 United Nations peacekeepers from the Philippines in the Golan Heights, a part of Syria held by Israel since the 1967 war, all of the captives appeared in a series of video clips released by an opposition group.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/07/world/middleeast/07lede_philbatt/07lede_philbatt-articleLarge.png', 'height': 354, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/07/world/middleeast/07lede_philbatt/07lede_philbatt-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 354}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/07/world/middleeast/07lede_philbatt/07lede_philbatt-jumbo.png', 'height': 604, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/07/worl