-b3fd-5380-ad53-1538927b44c6', 'word_count': 371, 'uri': 'nyt://article/331b1a6e-b3fd-5380-ad53-1538927b44c6'}, {'abstract': 'Virginia Rometty, the chief executive of I.B.M., is delivering a speech on Thursday evening at the Council on Foreign Relations that addresses the management challenges posed by the spread of Big Data technologies. Her speech comes five years after her predecessor, Samuel Palmisano, used the same setting to sketch out the benefits to business and society of exploiting advances in computer intelligence. That concept became I.B.M.’s successful Smarter Planet campaign.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/07/i-b-m-s-rometty-on-the-data-challenge-to-the-culture-of-management/', 'snippet': 'Virginia Rometty, the chief executive of I.B.M., is delivering a speech on Thursday evening at the Council on Foreign Relations that addresses the management challenges posed by the spread of Big Data technologies. Her speech comes five years afte...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Five years ago, Samuel J. Palmisano, then chief executive of I.B.M., gave a speech at the Council on Foreign Relations on the big opportunity ahead for modern computing technology to help businesses, government agencies and other institutions operate more intelligently. His remarks captured an emerging trend that opened the way to a large, lucrative business for I.B.M.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/07/technology/07bits-ibm/07bits-ibm-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 342, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/07/technology/07bits-ibm/07bits-ibm-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 342}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/07/technology/07bits-ibm/07bits-ibm-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 584, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/07/technology/07bits-ibm/07bits-ibm-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1169, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/07/technology/07bits-ibm/07bits-ibm-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/07/technology/07bits-ibm/07bits-ibm-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/07/technology/07bits-ibm/07bits-ibm-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'I.B.M.’s Rometty on the Data Challenge to the Culture of Management', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Enterprise Computing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rometty, Virginia M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Council on Foreign Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Business Machines Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T17:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Lohr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lohr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/98de3e6b-9fc0-5a0f-9052-4e018b045823', 'word_count': 650, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98de3e6b-9fc0-5a0f-9052-4e018b045823'}, {'abstract': 'The only way to survive in the confines of New York: compromise.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/07/staying-sane-in-small-spaces/', 'snippet': 'The only way to survive in the confines of New York: compromise.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I was born and grew up in the late ’80s in a one-bedroom apartment on the Upper West Side. In New York, apartments can be appealing for three reasons: size, location and cost. You hope to score in one of these categories. Sometimes you’re lucky enough to find a place with two. Three is unimaginable. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Staying Sane in Small Spaces', 'kicker': 'Townies', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T17:00:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jessica Soffer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jessica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Soffer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f02f047-235d-5d11-beef-5d1740d023eb', 'word_count': 1417, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f02f047-235d-5d11-beef-5d1740d023eb'}, {'abstract': 'Scenes from the Paris Fashion Week photo diary of Schohaja.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/07/photos-of-the-moment-louis-vuitton-13/', 'snippet': 'Scenes from the Paris Fashion Week photo diary of Schohaja.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function jsonSlideshowCallback(response){data = response;}NYTD.options = {source: data,cropType: \'blog480\',appendTo: \'fullScreenSlideShow\',showHeadLine: \'false\', renderstyle: "embeddedSlideShowTmag"}', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Photos of The Moment | Louis Vuitton', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paris Fashion Week', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vuitton, Louis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T17:01:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Schohaja', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Schohaja', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3fc36262-6749-503e-93c2-ceb716067704', 'word_count': 33, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3fc36262-6749-503e-93c2-ceb716067704'}, {'abstract': 'Efforts like creating school-run law firms are trying to address the glut of heavily indebted graduates with no clients and a vast number of Americans unable to afford a lawyer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/08/education/law-schools-look-to-medical-education-model.html', 'snippet': 'Efforts like creating school-run law firms are trying to address the glut of heavily indebted graduates with no clients and a vast number of Americans unable to afford a lawyer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TEMPE, Ariz. — When Douglas J. Sylvester, dean of the law school at Arizona State University, was visiting the Mayo Clinic in Minnesota a couple of years ago he mentioned the shifting job market for his students — far fewer offers and a new demand for graduates already able to draft documents and interact with clients.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/education/08lawschools-cnd/08lawschools-cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 385, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/08/education/08lawschools-cnd/08lawschools-cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 385}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/education/08lawschools-cnd/08lawschools-cnd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 658, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/education/08lawschools-cnd/08lawschools-cnd-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1315, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'To Place Graduates, Law Schools Are Opening Firms', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Place Graduates, Law Schools Are Opening Firms', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legal Profession', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bronner, Ethan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law Schools', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T17:02:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ethan Bronner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ethan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bronner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4b657277-d870-552f-af70-b8d425648747', 'word_count': 1232, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4b6