aption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/sports/tennis/08gulbis/08gulbis-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 575, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/sports/tennis/08gulbis/08gulbis-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1151, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/sports/tennis/08gulbis/08gulbis-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/08/sports/tennis/08gulbis/08gulbis-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/sports/tennis/08gulbis/08gulbis-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Gulbis, a Fast Climb After a Steep Fall', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T17:34:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By BEN ROTHENBERG', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'ROTHENBERG', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a38a843-a485-59f0-af42-8f6d547bfcf4', 'word_count': 2839, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a38a843-a485-59f0-af42-8f6d547bfcf4'}, {'abstract': '“Oz the Great and Powerful,” starring James Franco and Michelle Williams, is Disney’s prequel to the original story.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/08/movies/oz-the-great-and-powerful-starring-james-franco.html', 'snippet': '“Oz the Great and Powerful,” starring James Franco and Michelle Williams, is Disney’s prequel to the original story.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Can the major studios still make magic? From the looks of “Oz the Great and Powerful,” a dispiriting, infuriating jumble of big money, small ideas and ugly visuals, the answer seems to be no — unless, perhaps, the man behind the curtain is Martin Scorsese or James Cameron. The Walt Disney Company is the studio lurking behind “Oz,” and, as usual, it is banking that it can leverage this 3-D prehistory of the Wizard of Oz (James Franco) for its wonderful world of cross-promotional marketing and ancillary revenue streams. With so much riding on this “Oz” it’s a surprise that the results are so uninspired — or given Disney’s recent run with the likes of “Alice in Wonderland,” maybe not.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'That Man, Before the Curtain, and Before Dorothy, Too', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'That Man, Before the Curtain, and Before Dorothy, Too', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Walt Disney Company', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Raimi, Sam', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Franco, James', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'WILLIAMS, MICHELLE', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kunis, Mila', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weisz, Rachel', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T17:36:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/494f1817-5b73-5193-b571-6e8209094e7e', 'word_count': 1353, 'uri': 'nyt://article/494f1817-5b73-5193-b571-6e8209094e7e'}, {'abstract': 'The new season in the Chinese Super League begins on Friday highlighted by the departure and arrival of new players from abroad.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/07/a-new-season-in-chinese-super-league/', 'snippet': 'The new season in the Chinese Super League begins on Friday highlighted by the departure and arrival of new players from abroad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEOUL, South Korea — With the arrival of Nicolas Anelka and Didier Drogba at Shanghai Shenhua last season, the international news media hailed the Chinese Super League as one to watch and talked of a shift in the global goalposts. It is not surprising then that the departure of the two players has led to the lifting of that particular label.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/07/sports/soccer/lippi/lippi-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 605, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/07/sports/soccer/lippi/lippi-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 605}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/07/sports/soccer/lippi/lippi-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1017, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/07/sports/soccer/lippi/lippi-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2000, 'width': 1985, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', '