 two alternatives to the proposed buyout of Dell, Carl C. Icahn is hoping to make the computer maker’s board blink first.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Let’s face it, our lives would be much less interesting without Carl C. Icahn, whom I have previously referred to as a genius version of Wile E. Coyote. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Icahn, a Game of Chicken With Dell’s Board', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boards of Directors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shareholder Rights and Activism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dell, Michael S', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Icahn, Carl C', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dell Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T17:37:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Davidoff Solomon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': 'Davidoff', 'lastname': 'Solomon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d176d81b-a29a-52f4-b35c-c4f640cc9bec', 'word_count': 1321, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d176d81b-a29a-52f4-b35c-c4f640cc9bec'}, {'abstract': 'The company’s efforts to create an Internet radio service to compete with Pandora has been delayed by licensing negotiations with music companies, according to a number of people briefed on the talks.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/07/apples-internet-radio-service-said-to-be-delayed/', 'snippet': 'The company’s efforts to create an Internet radio service to compete with Pandora has been dela