ept unlimited donations from individuals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Organizing for Action, the pro-Obama advocacy group spun off from the president’s campaign machine, announced an important change today: It will not accept corporate contributions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Grassroots, Big Money', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Messina, Jim (1969- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Organizing for Action', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T18:34:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Firestone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Firestone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e5bb4d2-285c-5bae-8dd1-ea010834e1ca', 'word_count': 407, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e5bb4d2-285c-5bae-8dd1-ea010834e1ca'}, {'abstract': 'Mayfield, which opened in October in Crown Heights, Brooklyn, is broadly American in mission, with an occasional Southern twang.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/13/dining/reviews/hungry-city-mayfield-in-crown-heights-brooklyn.html', 'snippet': 'Mayfield, which opened in October in Crown Heights, Brooklyn, is broadly American in mission, with an occasional Southern twang.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is a dish that unfolds in panorama: on one end, a bowl of smoky collards, the leaves sweated until just soft, with hunks of bacon waiting to be flushed out of the undergrowth; then spoonbread, made with white cornmeal and given breath by whipped egg whites so it has the body of a soufflé and the heart of a pudding; and, last, quail, brined, soaked