ab4-197abc688061'}, {'abstract': 'Rock hunting goes awry in this debut thriller from Becky Masterman about a 59-year-old former undercover F.B.I. agent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/08/books/rage-against-the-dying-by-becky-masterman.html', 'snippet': 'Rock hunting goes awry in this debut thriller from Becky Masterman about a 59-year-old former undercover F.B.I. agent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Becky Masterman’s pulse-quickening debut thriller, “Rage Against the Dying,” starts with the genre’s standard-issue opening scene — almost. That’s the prologue in which somebody is violently killed so that the rest of the book can revolve around making sense of the crime. The scene’s two characters seem pretty familiar too. There is the oily-haired Gerald Peasil, the kind of guy who once smacked his mother across the chest with a skillet. And there’s the little old white-haired lady spied by Gerald as she pokes along the Arizona desert with a walking stick, looking for interesting rocks.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/arts/BOOKMASTERMAN/BOOKMASTERMAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 896, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/08/arts/BOOKMASTERMAN/BOOKMASTERMAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 896}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/arts/BOOKMASTERMAN/BOOKMASTERMAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 686, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/arts/BOOKMASTERMAN/BOOKMASTERMAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1372, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumb