val-explores-an-ugly-medical-chapter/', 'snippet': 'A new film about researchers injecting active hepatitis virus into healthy children with mental disabilities explores a dark chapter of medical history.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A film festival dedicated to stories about people with disabilities kicks off this week in New York City. The event, called “ReelAbilities,” is mostly a celebration of people with different abilities, but one troubling new film explores a particularly dark chapter of medical history.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/07/health/07well_willowbrook/07well_willowbrook-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 336, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/07/health/07well_willowbrook/07well_willowbrook-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 336}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/07/health/07well_willowbrook/07well_willowbrook-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 574, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/07/health/07well_willowbrook/07well_willowbrook-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 717, 'width': 1280, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/07/health/07well_willowbrook/07well_willowbrook-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/07/health/07well_willowbrook/07well_willowbrook-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/07/health/07well_willowbrook/07well_willowbrook-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Film Festival Explores an Ugly Medical Chapter', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disabilities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hepatitis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T20:09:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Barron H. Lerner, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Barron', 'middlename': 'H.', 'lastname': 'Lerner', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3bf73ae4-6c46-52ef-adae-fb1ffd4376b0', 'word_count': 889, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3bf73ae4-6c46-52ef-adae-fb1ffd4376b0'}, {'abstract': 'The Virgins’ newest album will be released on Cult Records, which is run by Julian Casablancas of the Strokes.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/07/born-again-virgins/', 'snippet': 'The Virgins’ newest album will be released on Cult Records, which is run by Julian Casablancas of the Strokes.', 'lead_paragraph': "It’s pretty neat to be the first act with an album out on a brand-new record label, but even more momentous when that label — in this case, Cult Records — is run by Julian Casablancas, of the Strokes. While lead singer Donald Cumming isn’t shying away from whatever halo effect that may cast on the Virgins‘ “Strike Gently,” which will be released March 12, mostly he’s excited to have the blessing of a fellow musician who understands both sides of the mixing board. “We all played the songs in the studio together,” Cumming said of the band. “You can really hear our instruments bleeding over each other.” The organic quality here lies in considerable contrast to the Virgins’ self-titled 2008 debut, whose rock ‘n’ roll was produced to within inches of bubble-gum pop on tracks like “Rich Girls” and “One Week of Danger.” Their new material is stripped down, a harmonic rumble of moonlight swagger and blue-rose tattoos. “I never aspired to hear someone sing my lyrics on ‘American Idol,'” Cumming explained. “I just wanted to make music that felt authentic to me.” Indeed, a lot has changed in the intervening five years: Cumming is the only original member left in the group; he’s married now, to the artist Aurel Schmidt; and he even taught himself to play the piano (think Schroeder from Peanuts, but with a Brechtian twist). “I don’t like to practice too much,” he admitted. “I like the discoveries I make to sound fresh.”", 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Born-Again Virgins', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Firing Up A New Label', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Casablancas, Julian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Strokes, The', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Virgins (Music Group)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T20:15:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Powers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Powers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ec914dde-40e5-51e8-8c3e-3f64654c688a', 'word_count': 262, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ec914dde-40e5-51e8-8c3e-3f64654c688a'}, {'abstract': 'The State Labor Department, in a new report, said the rate was 9.1 percent, up from 8.8 percent in December.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/08/nyregion/new-york-city-jobless-rate-hit-9-1-percent-in-january.html', 'snippet': 'The State Labor Department, in a new report, said the rate was 9.1 percent, up from 8.8 percent in December.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York City’s unemployment rate rose back above 9 percent at the start of 2013, even though the city started the year with more jobs than it had ever had, according to reports released on Thursday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'City’s Jobless Rate in January Hit 4-Month High', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jobless Rate For City Back Above 9%, New Data Say', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McGeehan, Patrick', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T20:16:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick McGeehan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGeehan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72c6f7ec-ed23-5397-9dc5-06b2f257f5fe', 'word_count': 473, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72c6f7ec-ed23-5397-9dc5-06b2f257f5fe'}, {'abstract': 'Just after the avalanche, Ron Pankey and Tim Carlson discover the debris pile.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/multimedia