orney General Eric Holder said that some banks are too big to jail.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the same Wednesday judiciary committee meeting where Attorney General Eric Holder hemmed and hawed before acknowledging that the president cannot authorize a drone strike on American soil, against an American terrorist suspect posing no imminent threat, he explained why the Justice Department has failed to bring criminal charges against a single Wall Street bank. Mr. Holder suggested, as a Financial Times headline put it this morning, that some banks are “too big to jail.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Banks Above the Law', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grassley, Charles E', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holder, Eric H Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'HSBC Holdings PLC', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T21:09:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Juliet Lapidos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Juliet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lapidos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7bbe7884-5a05-5a06-8b94-baae9750d311', 'word_count': 323, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7bbe7884-5a05-5a06-8b94-baae9750d311'}, {'abstract': 'From a single magazine, Time, a giant media conglomerate was built. With the planned spinoff, the dismantling of the empire is now nearly complete.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/03/07/a-grand-history-of-mergers-told-in-magazines/', 'snippet': 'From a single magazine, Time, a giant media conglomerate was built. With the planned spinoff, the dismantling of the empire is now nearly complete.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The brief history of Time Inc. is a truly epic M.&A. tale. The gold standard of American magazine publishing proved the foundation for a giant media conglomerate. Time Warner’s decision on Wednesday to spin off the legacy of Henry Luce’s 1920s vision represents the last step in dismantling the empire.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Grand History of Mergers, Told in Magazines', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Magazines', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Luce, Henry Robinson', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AOL', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Time (Magazine)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Time Inc.', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Time Warner Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T21:12:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeffrey Goldfarb', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeffrey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldfarb', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/58734552-0eb1-5638-8e16-d862dae3b736', 'word_count': 427, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58734552-0eb1-5638-8e16-d862dae3b736'}, {'abstract': 'Carl C. Icahn, the activist investor, does not want Dell to become a private company by selling to its founder, Michael S. Dell and the private equity firm Silver Lake Partners.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/03/07/icahn-said-to-have-floated-idea-of-15-a-share-tender-offe