les in the Italian wine tapestry, one of the wrinkliest is about as far northwest as you can go in Italy. There, tucked away in the Alps beneath looming Mont Blanc, the tallest peak in the chain, is the smallest Italian viticultural region, brimming with little-known wines capable of offering great pleasure.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/13/dining/13POUR/13POUR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/13/dining/13POUR/13POUR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/13/dining/13POUR/13POUR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/13/dining/13POUR/13POUR-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/13/dining/13POUR/13POUR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/13/dining/13POUR/13POUR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/13/dining/13POUR/13POUR-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Treasures of the Alps', 'kicker': 'Wines of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Treasures of the Alps', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Asimov, Eric', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALPS MOUNTAINS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T22:45:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'subsection_name': 'Dining & Wine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Asimov', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Asimov', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ce1b3ab-e46b-527e-96ca-ee50aee9313f', 'word_count': 1095, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ce1b3ab-e46b-527e-96ca-ee50aee9313f'}, {'abstract': 'Based on a Gothic thriller, “The Monk” traces the downfall of a sternly pious monk.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/08/movies/the-monk-directed-by-dominik-moll.html', 'snippet': 'Based on a Gothic thriller, “The Monk” traces the downfall of a sternly pious monk.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s a moment in “The Monk,” an adaptation of a notorious 1796 Gothic novel, when the shadows all but swallow the actor Vincent Cassel’s face. It’s an appropriately foreboding image for a heavily plotted tale of demons and men, God and the Devil that, in his influential review of the novel, Coleridge excoriated for combining “all that is most awfully true in religion with all that is most ridiculously absurd in superstition.” He conceded that the book had “much real merit” but also “impiety,” “abominations” and “libidinous minuteness.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/arts/08MONK_SPAN/08MONK_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 321, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/08/arts/08MONK_SPAN/08MONK_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 321}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/arts/08MONK_SPAN/08MONK_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 547, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/arts/08MONK_SPAN/08MONK_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1094, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/arts/08MONK_SPAN/MONK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/08/arts/08MONK_SPAN/MONK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/arts/08MONK_SPAN/MONK-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Holy Man or Hypocrite? A Low-Risk Devil’s Wager', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Holy Man or Hypocrite? A Low-Risk Devil’s Wager', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Monk (Movie)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moll, Dominik', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cassel, Vincent', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T22:45:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/434d621e-a01d-5b9c-b7e6-4f01142f4897', 'word_count': 470, 'uri': 'nyt://article/434d621e-a01d-5b9c-b7e6-4f01142f4897'}, {'abstract': 'Trout plucked from an icy mountain stream seems just right with wines from the Alps.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/13/dining/trout-bolstered-with-herbs-and-smoky-bacon.html', 'snippet': 'Trout plucked from an icy mountain stream seems just right with wines from the Alps.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There you are in the Alps. You take off your skis and you’re ready for a cool glass of local red alongside some fresh trout just plucked from an icy mountain stream. The wine promises lean, herbaceous, earthy, even flinty notes to accompany the meaty fish. No plans for skiing or fishing in Italy, or even the Gallatin River near Big Sky, Mont., or the in the Esopus Creek in the Catskills? Simply find a reliable fish market for the trout and bolster the whole fish with herbs and smoky bacon (or speck, the regional Italian version). You will not need black-diamond kitchen skills to put it on the table or to open that bottle of Valle d’Aosta.\xa0', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/13/dining/13PAIRING_SPAN/13PAIRING_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/13/dining/13PAIRING_SPAN/13PAIRING_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/13/dining/13PAIRING_SPAN/13PAIRING_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/13/dining/13PAIRING_SPAN/13PAIRING_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/13/dining/13PAIRING_SPAN/13PAIRING_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/13/dining/13PAIRING_SPAN/13PAIRING_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/13/dining/13PAIRING_SPAN/13PAIRING_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fish Bolstered With Herbs and Smoky Bacon', 'kicker': 'Pairings', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trout', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T22:46:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/abf9a7d8-ebeb-536e-a350-ae07f9d54b84', 'word_count': 118, 'uri': 'nyt://article/abf9a7d8-ebeb-536e-a350-ae07f9d54b84'}, {'abstract': '“Give them what they want” could be the motto of this year’s Armory Show, which has seen changes after a focus group and others weighed in.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/08/arts/design/the-armory-show-at-piers-92-and-94.html', 'snippet': '“Give them what they want” could be the motto of this year’s Armory Show, which has seen changes after a focus group and others weighed in.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few months ago, a focus group convened to discuss the 2013 Armory Show. Organized and videotaped by the fair’s official artist, Liz Magic Laser, it engaged art writers, curators, collectors and others in a lively discussion of the flagging Armory brand. It was a clever way of acknowledging things that art-worlders have been complaining about for years: That the Armory had become too big and too corporate under its owners, Merchandise Mart; that it took New York for granted; and, most recently, that it had been dealt a possible death blow by the upstart Frieze art fair.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/arts/08SUBARMORY/SUBJPARMORY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/08/arts/08SUBARMORY/SUBJPARMORY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/arts/08SUBARMORY/SUBJPARMORY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/arts/08SUBARMORY/SUBJPARMORY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/arts/08SUBARMORY/SUBJPARMORY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/08/arts/08SUBARMORY/SUBJPARMORY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/arts/08SUBARMORY/SUBJPARMORY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Homages, Giddy Humor and Less Clutter', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Homages, Giddy Humor and Less Clutter', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosenberg, Karen', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARMORY SHOW, THE INTERNATIONAL FAIR OF NEW ART (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-07T22:52:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/2bb7f86c-9b67-5291-82ab-c17a423fd85d', 'word_count': 1003, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2bb7f86c-9b67-5291-82ab-c17a423fd85d'}, {'abstract': 'More than half of the booths at the Art Show, the annual exhibition of the Art Dealers Association of America, are dedicated to single artists, a rarity in past years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/08/arts/design/art-dealers-association-show-at-park-avenue-armory.html', 'snippet': 'More than half of the booths at the Art Show, the annual exhibition of the Art Dealers Association of America, are dedicated to single artists, a rarity in past years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It would be hyperbolic to call it a revolution, but it is a significant development: Of the 72 vendors taking part in this year’s Art Dealers Association of America Art Show at the Park Avenue Armory, 40 have dedicated their booths to single artists. Last year’s featured 30 solo shows. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/arts/08DEALERS2/DEALERS2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 248, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/08/arts/08DEALERS2/DEALERS2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 248}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/arts/08DEALERS2/DEALERS2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 423, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/arts/08DEALERS2/DEALERS2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 846, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/arts/08DEALERS2/DEALERS2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/08/arts/08DEALERS2/DEALERS2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/arts/08DEALERS2/DEALERS2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Going Solo Has Its Day, in a Hodgepodge of Styles', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Going Solo Has Its Day, in a Hodgepodge of Styles', 'name