ations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-08T00:26:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liam Stack and Hania Mourtada', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Hania', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mourtada', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d269d06a-c393-51e8-be1c-c09a2312f87b', 'word_count': 965, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d269d06a-c393-51e8-be1c-c09a2312f87b'}, {'abstract': 'Matt Kroll and Catherine Kellogg went looking for a large one-bedroom on the Upper East Side.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/10/realestate/the-dog-stays-well-see-about-the-stuff.html', 'snippet': 'Matt Kroll and Catherine Kellogg went looking for a large one-bedroom on the Upper East Side.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Matt Kroll moved to the city after graduating from Colgate University, he lived with roommates in a three-bedroom duplex in the East 70s, paying $1,250 a month for a large bedroom with an en-suite bathroom and four closets. The situation, as well as the vast amount of space, “worked out seamlessly,” Mr. Kroll said.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/10/realestate/10HUNT5/Hunt5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 412, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/10/realestate/10HUNT5/Hunt5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 412}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/10/realestate/10HUNT5/Hunt5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 70