endo, the chief investment officer of the bailout program, is stepping down on Friday. He will be succeeded by Charmian Uy, who joined the department last summer.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/03/07/bailout-official-at-the-treasury-to-leave-post/', 'snippet': 'Matt Pendo, the chief investment officer of the bailout program, is stepping down on Friday. He will be succeeded by Charmian Uy, who joined the department last summer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After more than two years of long train rides and selling off more than $120 billion in assets, the chief investment officer of the Treasury Department’s bailout program is stepping down.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bailout Official at the Treasury to Leave Post', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bailout Official Is Leaving Post At the Treasury', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Treasury Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-08T00:29:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e4c3157-b29a-5b60-8a69-74864aa2c341', 'word_count': 387, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e4c3157-b29a-5b60-8a69-74864aa2c341'}, {'abstract': 'If the companies do not reach an agreement before April 8, Justice Jeffrey K. Oing of New York State Supreme Court will continue hearing the case.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/08/business/judge-sends-macys-penney-case-to-mediation.html', 'snippet': 'If the companies do not reach an agreement before April 8, Justice Jeffrey K. Oing of New York State Supreme Court will continue hearing the case.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After almost three weeks of testimony, the judge overseeing the lawsuits that Macy’s brought against J. C. Penney and Martha Stewart Living Omnimedia has sent the parties into mediation.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Justice Orders Mediation in Martha Stewart Case', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Justice Orders Mediation In Martha Stewart Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clifford, Stephanie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JC Penney Company Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Macy's Inc", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Martha Stewart Living Omnimedia Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stewart, Martha', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-08T00:32:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Clifford', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clifford', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6ac913c-ef1b-5bcc-a7af-6883bda40aea', 'word_count': 512, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6ac913c-ef1b-5bcc-a7af-6883bda40aea'}, {'abstract': 'Young women from around the world tell their stories of triumph over adversity in “Girl Rising,” a twist on the social issue documentary.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/08/movies/girl-rising-by-richard-e-robbins.html', 'snippet': 'Young women from around the world tell their stories of triumph over adversity in “Girl Rising,” a twist on the social issue documentary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If “Girl Rising” is wholly a vehicle furthering the cause of girls’ education across the globe, it’s more of a multicolored bus to worthy destinations than a pace car. In this twist on the social-issue documentary, girls act out stories adapted from their own lives by writers from their own countries, including Edwidge Danticat, Aminatta Forna and Manjushree Thapa. The hybrid results feature occasional bold strokes alongside ad-pitch eye candy and sleeve-tugging.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/arts/SUBGIRLRISING/SUBGIRLRISING-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/08/arts/SUBGIRLRISING/SUBGIRLRISING-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/arts/SUBGIRLRISING/SUBGIRLRISING-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/arts/SUBGIRLRISING/SUBGIRLRISING-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1080, 'width': 1919, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/arts/SUBGIRLRISING/SUBGIRLRISING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/08/arts/SUBGIRLRISING/SUBGIRLRISING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 