ortion ban in the country.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Arkansas’s Attack on Abortion', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Arkansas’s Attack on Abortion', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARKANSAS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pregnancy and Childbirth', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-08T02:36:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/4cf75202-5a45-5309-a353-5f7b1944f726', 'word_count': 432, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4cf75202-5a45-5309-a353-5f7b1944f726'}, {'abstract': 'Swiss measures are the newest and most far-reaching of the say-on-pay policies now in place or under consideration in many European nations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/08/opinion/shareholders-in-europe-demand-control-on-executive-pay.html', 'snippet': 'Swiss measures are the newest and most far-reaching of the say-on-pay policies now in place or under consideration in many European nations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Voters in Switzerland this week overwhelmingly approved a referendum to give shareholders a binding say on executive pay. The Swiss measures are the latest and most far-reaching of various say-on-pay policies now in place or under consideration in many European nations. Denmark, Norway, Sweden and the Netherlands all have some form of voting on binding pay.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shareholders in Europ