ype_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/da3479d4-1e79-53d3-b533-1bdcad01d44a', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/da3479d4-1e79-53d3-b533-1bdcad01d44a'}, {'abstract': 'The newly confirmed C.I.A. chief should commit to making a Senate report on torture public.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/08/opinion/john-brennans-excuse-on-torture-report.html', 'snippet': 'The newly confirmed C.I.A. chief should commit to making a Senate report on torture public.', 'lead_paragraph': 'John Brennan, the newly confirmed chief of the Central Intelligence Agency, has been at the agency for most of 25 years. He had two counterterrorism jobs during the administration of George W. Bush. In one, he compiled intelligence reports from 20 agencies (including the C.I.A.) for Mr. Bush’s morning briefing. He was President Obama’s\xa0counterterrorism adviser in his first term and an architect of the Obama administration’s targeted killings policy.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mr. Brennan’s Excuse', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mr. Brennan’s Excuse', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brennan, John O', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, George W', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Torture', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central Intelligence Agency', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-08T02:47:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/e033fc74-017b-5328-96fa-c1c3a3d0b70d', 'word_count': 545, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e033fc74-017b-5328-96fa-c1c3a3d0b70d'}, {'abstract': 'In Texas, a state dominated by Republicans, conservatives are pushing two constitutional amendments that would limit most statewide officeholders.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/08/us/texas-term-limit-proposals-revived-20-years-later.html', 'snippet': 'In Texas, a state dominated by Republicans, conservatives are pushing two constitutional amendments that would limit most statewide officeholders.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Texas conservatives were pushing for term limits 20 years ago, in an effort easy to dismiss as an attempt to flush Democrats out of the Legislature, the Congressional delegation and even some executive offices. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Conservatives Revive Proposals for Term Limits', 'kicker': 'The Texas Tribune', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Conservatives Revive Proposals For Term Limits', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Term Limits (Political Office)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-08T02:51:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Ramsey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ramsey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5aba9d84-ae5f-5c8d-b43f-b9d1ed01df0a', 'word_count': 736, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5aba9d84-ae5f-5c8d-b43f-b9d1ed01df0a'}, {'abstract': 'House Bill 1608 would require Texas law enforcement agencies to obtain warrants and prove probable cause of illegal activity before obtaining cellphone records in their investigations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/08/us/cellphone-records-officer-in-texas-you-may-soon-need-a-warrant.html', 'snippet': 'House Bill 1608 would require Texas law enforcement agencies to obtain warrants and prove probable cause of illegal activity before obtaining cellphone records in their investigations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Seeking to regulate the use of cellphone records in investigations by law enforcement, Texas lawmakers are considering a bill that would require police officers and prosecutors to have a warrant before obtaining such records.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Cellphone Records, Officer? You May Soon Need a Warrant', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Cellphone Records, Officer? You May Soon Need a Warrant', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-08T02:52:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maurice Chammah', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maurice', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chammah', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/689c77b8-7fce-5bc4-9f88-91cc88276946', 'word_count': 488, 'uri': 'nyt://article/689c77b8-7fce-5bc4-9f88-91cc88276946'}, {'abstract': 'In a grouping of the top three players in the world, only Tiger Woods posted a luminous score in the first round of the World Golf Championship event. Rory McIlroy and Luke Donald struggled.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/08/sports/golf/rory-mcilroy-struggles-but-tiger-woods-soars-at-doral.html', 'snippet': 'In a grouping of the top three players in the world, only Tiger Woods posted a luminous score in the first round of the World Golf Championship event. Rory McIlroy and Luke Donald struggled.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DORAL, Fla. — The featured group at the Cadillac Championship on Thursday was like a marquee with one light burned out and another flickering. In a grouping of the top three players in the world, only one posted a luminous score. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/sports/GOLF/GOLF-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/08/sports/GOLF/GOLF-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/sports/GOLF/GOLF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 676, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/sports/GOLF/GOLF-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1353, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/sports/GOLF/GOLF-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/08/sports/GOLF/GOLF-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/sports/GOLF/GOLF-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'McIlroy Struggles, but Woods Soars at Doral', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Power Group, Long Faces and One Low Score', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McIlroy, Rory', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woods, Tiger', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Donald, Luke', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-08T02:55:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/93933dba-ba1a-5ef1-bcc2-f2eace777252', 'word_count': 884, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93933dba-ba1a-5ef1-bcc2-f2eace777252'}, {'abstract': 'As the Supreme Court reviews a section of the landmark Voting Rights Act, arguments for and against election monitoring are again being batted about in New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/08/nyregion/calls-to-end-voting-rights-act-stir-debate-in-the-bronx.html', 'snippet': 'As the Supreme Court reviews a section of the landmark Voting Rights Act, arguments for and against election monitoring are again being batted about in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Emerging from the bloody protests in Selma, Ala., the Voting Rights Act was initially heralded as a declaration that the federal government would no longer tolerate the open racism of the segregated South. But this narrow mandate to monitor elections in six Southern states grew quietly over the years, extending to unexpected corners of the country, including the Bronx.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source