s-the-blackhawks-on-top/', 'snippet': 'A look at the players who are behind the Chicago Blackhawks’ 21-0-3 record.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At 21-0-3, the Chicago Blackhawks have roared through half of their schedule without a regulation loss. Their 24-game run has shattered the previous N.H.L. record for longest season-opening point streak (16 games, by Anaheim in 2006-7) and is second to the overall single-season mark (35 games, by Philadelphia in 1979-80).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Depth Puts the Blackhawks on Top', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Blackhawks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-08T04:29:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/db509d9d-9198-59b9-b117-2807b37cc37e', 'word_count': 96, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db509d9d-9198-59b9-b117-2807b37cc37e'}, {'abstract': 'With Carmelo Anthony sitting out, J. R. Smith had 36 points to keep the Knicks competitive. He came up short, though, and the Thunder won.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/08/sports/basketball/knicks-fall-to-thunder.html', 'snippet': 'With Carmelo Anthony sitting out, J. R. Smith had 36 points to keep the Knicks competitive. He came up short, though, and the Thunder won.', 'lead_paragraph': 'J. R. Smith is not Carmelo Anthony. He is a little shorter, a little lighter, slightly younger. He does not have the All-Star credentials or the gold medals or the fame. Where Anthony celebrates h