aph': 'About half of the runners registered for last year’s New York City Marathon, which was canceled after Hurricane Sandy, chose to have their entry fee refunded, and the other half chose to run in a coming marathon or half marathon, New York Road Runners said in a letter to runners.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Half of New York City Marathon Entrants Opt for a Refund', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Half of Registrants Opt for a Refund', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Running', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York City Marathon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Road Runners Club', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-08T04:46:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/44caad92-304a-5c9c-9074-eb4ff4fc25b8', 'word_count': 268, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44caad92-304a-5c9c-9074-eb4ff4fc25b8'}, {'abstract': 'The Hanford nuclear cleanup project in Richland, Wash., has been hit by leaking waste, layoffs and delays; now more trouble is ahead.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/08/us/struggling-hanford-site-awaits-new-cuts.html', 'snippet': 'The Hanford nuclear cleanup project in Richland, Wash., has been hit by leaking waste, layoffs and delays; now more trouble is ahead.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RICHLAND, Wash. — Here in the place where plutonium production for the nation’s bomb arsenal was elevated to industrial scale, in the rollin