: 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Pogrebin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogrebin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb19152b-48f7-546a-8423-1789aea14786', 'word_count': 1537, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb19152b-48f7-546a-8423-1789aea14786'}, {'abstract': 'Behind the scenes at the shoot for the cover story of the Men’s Fashion issue.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/08/t-magazine/on-the-set-with-matthias-schoenaerts.html', 'snippet': 'Behind the scenes at the shoot for the cover story of the Men’s Fashion issue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the rain poured down on the drive from downtown Miami to the Ocean Queen Motel in Hollywood, the actor Matthias Schoenaerts, marking his first visit to Florida, said this isn’t how he imagined the Sunshine State. Schoenaerts was right on time for a 7:30 a.m. pickup from the Eden Roc Hotel, despite having arrived from Brussels only hours before. Once everyone got to the motel, to shoot the Men’s issue cover, the photo crew worked tirelessly to keep the breakfast catering out of the rain, while Schoenaerts stood on the motel balcony smoking hand-rolled cigarettes and taking iPhone photos of the Atlantic.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On the Set With Matthias Schoenaerts', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-08T05:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TDesign', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lauren Tabach-Bank', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lauren', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tabach-Bank', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_