-read-march-8/', 'snippet': 'New sanctions for North Korea; Berlusconi convicted and sentenced to prison; Malaysian troops in Borneo kill 31 Filipino gunmen; and in rugby, the struggles of Les Bleus.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEWS Ignoring threats of retaliation, the United Nations Security Council ordered new economic sanctions against North Korea on Thursday for its third nuclear test last month, unanimously approving a resolution that the United States negotiated with China, the North’s greatest protector. Rick Gladstone reports from New York, and David E. Sanger from Washington.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/world/asia/08korea/08korea-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 372, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/08/world/asia/08korea/08korea-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 372}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/world/asia/08korea/08korea-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 636, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/world/asia/08korea/08korea-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1271, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/world/asia/08korea/08korea-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/08/world/asia/08korea/08korea-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/world/asia/08korea/08korea-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'IHT Quick Read: March 8', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-08T07:58:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By The International Herald Tribune', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The International Herald Tribune'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c05e814-5d98-50bd-8115-407db382e320', 'word_count': 493, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c05e814-5d98-50bd-8115-407db382e320'}, {'abstract': 'Syrian rebels holding a group of peacekeepers from the Philippines in the Golan Heights region were pressing for a redeployment of Syrian government forces nearby, the Filipino authorities said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/09/world/middleeast/syria-developments.html', 'snippet': 'Syrian rebels holding a group of peacekeepers from the Philippines in the Golan Heights region were pressing for a redeployment of Syrian government forces nearby, the Filipino authorities said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The United Nations said Friday that an agreement had been reached to secure the release of the 21 Filipino peacekeepers seized two days earlier by Syrian insurgents in the disputed Golan Heights region between Syria and Israel. But it was unclear when the captives, the first international troops to become entangled in Syria’s civil war, would be freed.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/09/world/syria/syria-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/09/world/syria/syria-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600,