s-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1333, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/10/magazine/10lives/10lives-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/10/magazine/10lives/10lives-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/10/magazine/10lives/10lives-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Public Apology for My Sofa', 'kicker': 'Lives', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Moving Violation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bry, Dave', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Moving and Moving Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-08T15:49:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Bry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/010347f8-d12b-5de2-9599-4adf09d17cfc', 'word_count': 782, 'uri': 'nyt://article/010347f8-d12b-5de2-9599-4adf09d17cfc'}, {'abstract': 'The difference between what is reasonable and what is “right.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/10/magazine/should-i-pay-for-a-gas-station-attendants-mistake.html', 'snippet': 'The difference between what is reasonable and what is “right.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I go to the local gas station, I always give the attendant $20 and request that he provide me with that specific value of fuel (which always changes because of fluctuating gas prices). I repeat my request three times and show the attendant the $20 in my hand. During a recent visit, I glanced over to the pump to see that the attendant had made a mistake and exceeded our $20 agreement. I beeped my horn and waved my arms. Once I got out of my car, he came forward and realized his error. Because the amount of $20 was stated before the gas being pumped, should I stand my ground and agree to pay only $20? Or should I pay the difference (because I will obviously use the extra gas at some point in the future)? VINCENT MAZZOLLA, NORTH ARLINGTON, N.J.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/magazine/ethicist/ethicist-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1316, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/02/02/magazine/ethicist/ethicist-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1316}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/magazine/ethicist/ethicist-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 467, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/magazine/ethicist/ethicist-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 934, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/magazine/ethicist/ethicist-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/02/02/magazine/ethicist/ethicist-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailw