 90 comedians, from Bill Hader to Reggie Watts (above) to Maggie Maye. The event not to miss: an air sex competition. Remember when air guitar was cool?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Calendar: Coming Events in Austin, Tex.; London; Eisenach, Germany', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-08T18:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/30a4ae75-ada3-504d-9311-c2c58f98c9a2', 'word_count': 292, 'uri': 'nyt://article/30a4ae75-ada3-504d-9311-c2c58f98c9a2'}, {'abstract': 'There is a strong possibility that there will be three teams from Germany’s Bundesliga in the semifinals of the UEFA Champions League.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/08/champions-leagues-german-accent/', 'snippet': 'There is a strong possibility that there will be three teams from Germany’s Bundesliga in the semifinals of the UEFA Champions League.', 'lead_paragraph': 'By the middle of next week, there is a good chance that for the first time since 1998 there will be three German teams, of the eight remaining, in the quarterfinals of the UEFA Champions League. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Champions League’s German Accent', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'UEFA Champions League (Soccer)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bayern Munich (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Borus