t': 'The combined effect of payroll tax increases and automatic budget cuts could suppress monthly hiring by more than last year’s average monthly gain, economists say.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/08/federal-austeritys-bite-on-job-growth/', 'snippet': 'The combined effect of payroll tax increases and automatic budget cuts could suppress monthly hiring by more than last year’s average monthly gain, economists say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The latest jobs report could have been even better. Employers added 236,000 jobs in February, evidence that the economy is gaining strength, but analysts generally agree that the number would have been higher if the federal government had not increased payroll tax rates in January.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Federal Austerity’s Bite on Job Growth', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gross Domestic Product', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-08T18:11:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Binyamin Appelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Binyamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Appelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8d7b94f-eb93-53b8-ad68-5a634acf483f', 'word_count': 465, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8d7b94f-eb93-53b8-ad68-5a634acf483f'}, {'abstract': 'A jury ordered $8.3 million in damages in the first of some 10,000 lawsuits tied to a now-recalled implant.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nyti