Kim Jong-un, inspected military units.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/08/north-koreans-fond-of-leader-state-tv-suggests/', 'snippet': 'North Korean state television producers appeared to outdo themselves with a report on the frenzied reaction from the populace Thursday as the nation’s young leader, Kim Jong-un, inspected military units.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As The Lede has reported previously, displays of official joy are quite common in North Korea, even before Rodmania swept the nation. On Thursday, though, the producers of state television’s news bulletins appeared to outdo themselves with a long report on the frenzied reaction from the populace as the nation’s young leader, Kim Jong-un, inspected military units deployed near the country’s disputed maritime border with South Korea. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'North Koreans Fond of Leader, State TV Suggests', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Jong-un', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-08T18:15:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f77595bb-9f96-52fc-a7c5-b04ce4f0f0cb', 'word_count': 121, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f77595bb-9f96-52fc-a7c5-b04ce4f0f0cb'}, {'abstract': 'Inside the Sistine Chapel, the final preparations for the meetings to decide the next Pope are underway.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/08/video-of-preparations-inside-the-sistine-chapel-for-conclave/', 'snippet': 'Inside the Sistine Chapel, the final preparations for the meetings to decide the next Pope are underway.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Vatican officials announced Friday that the 115 cardinals from around the world will officially begin their conclave, the official process used to elect the successor of Pope Benedict XVI, on Tuesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video of Preparations Inside the Sistine Chapel for Conclave', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cardinals (Roman Catholic Prelates)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Popes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Benedict XVI', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rome (Italy)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-08T18:23:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eaa77fb9-2a69-5d54-ace1-fac5e0a8a5ba', 'word_count': 304, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eaa77fb9-2a69-5d54-ace1-fac5e0a8a5ba'}, {'abstract': 'Yoselyn Ortega, who is accused of fatally stabbing two children on the Upper West Side last October, is still undergoing a psychological evaluation to determine whether she is fit to stand trial.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/08/nanny-charged-with-murder-appears-in-court/', 'snippet': 'Yoselyn Ortega, who is accused of fatally stabbing two children on the Upper West Side last October, is still undergoing a psychological evaluation to determine whether she is fit to stand trial.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Yoselyn Ortega, a nanny charged with fatally stabbing two children she cared for on the Upper West Side last October, appeared in State Supreme Court in Manhattan on Friday for the first time since her arrest. Ms. Ortega, 50, who had been unable to attend several prior court dates, was taken to court from the prison ward for psychiatric patients at Elmhurst Hospital Center in Queens. A psychiatric exam to evaluate her fitness to stand trial has not been completed. A large scar on her throat could be seen above the gray jumpsuit she wore. The authorities have said she turned a knife on herself after attacking Lucia Krim, 6, and Leo Krim, 2, in the bathtub of their apartment. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nanny Charged With Murder Appears in Court', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ortega, Yoselyn', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-08T18:23:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c73b90f6-8467-5c60-99bd-448a064ff65a', 'word_count': 121, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c73b90f6-8467-5c60-99bd-448a064ff65a'}, {'abstract': 'The police in Ottawa, say an organized crime ring is operating in the city. What leads them to this conclusion: a surge in thefts of older model minivans.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/08/wheelies-the-can-crime-get-more-dull-edition/', 'snippet': 'The police in Ottawa, say an organized crime ring is operating in the city. What leads them to this conclusion: a surge in thefts of older model minivans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In which we bring you motoring news from around the Web:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wheelies: The ‘Can Crime Get More Dull?’ Edition', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nascar Sprint Cup Series', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newtown, Conn, Shooting (2012)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-08T18:29:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b92c8728-d81a-5908-9413-adb0ebe6febd', 'word_count': 606, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b92c8728-d81a-5908-9413-adb0ebe6febd'}, {'abstract': "The agency cut its rating on Italy's credit by a notch, saying political gridlock could deepen the slump in a pivotal euro zone economy.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/09/business/global/09iht-fitch09.html', 'snippet': "The agency cut its rating on Italy's credit by a notch, saying political gridlock could deepen the slump in a pivotal euro zone economy.", 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — The Fitch ratings agency cut its assessment of Italy’s sovereign credit by a notch on Friday, citing the abrupt emergence of fresh political turmoil that could push one of the euro zone’s most pivotal economies, already in a deep slump, into a further slowdown.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fitch Downgrades Italian Debt, Citing Political Turmoil', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fitch Cuts Italy’s Rating,\r\nCiting Political Turmoil', 'name': N