': 'subject', 'value': 'Wearable Computing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Memoto AB', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-08T19:47:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jenna Wortham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jenna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wortham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0f50d624-8d26-58b9-92ad-f328ce306108', 'word_count': 665, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0f50d624-8d26-58b9-92ad-f328ce306108'}, {'abstract': 'David Tanis, a former chef at Chez Panisse, on what was lost when fire destroyed part of the restaurant early this morning.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/08/the-porch-is-gone-the-memories-remain/', 'snippet': 'David Tanis, a former chef at Chez Panisse, on what was lost when fire destroyed part of the restaurant early this morning.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To encounter the remains of a destructive fire, like the one that ravaged a portion of Chez Panisse in Berkeley, Calif., early Friday morning, is a traumatic experience, even if no one was injured. As a longtime member of the Chez Panisse family —\xa0I was the chef there on and off from the mid-1980s through 2011 — my heart goes out to Alice Waters and the staff. It is especially traumatic for those who know the history of the place. In the wake of such an accident, memories are everywhere. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/dining/dj-chezporch/dj-chezporch-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 417, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/08/dining/dj-chezporch/dj-chezporch-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 417}}, {'rank': 0, 'subt