y down and striking his genitals, sat quietly as the judge addressed them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The three teenage boys sat up straight, eyes ahead, in a criminal courtroom in the Bronx on Friday morning. They wore dress shirts and ties. On a wooden bench behind them sat their supporters: More young men, in khakis, corduroys and other preppy attire; one wore brown leather boat shoes with no socks, even though it was snowing outside.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Students in Hazing Case Make Court Appearance', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Three Bronx Students Accused of Hazing Go Before a Judge', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hazing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bronx High School of Science', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Diallo, Boubacar', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berkmans, Pier', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brady, Thomas', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-08T22:51:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Al Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Al', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c15f4f7e-b512-5ac0-abb8-f3672ba7e522', 'word_count': 618, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c15f4f7e-b512-5ac0-abb8-f3672ba7e522'}, {'abstract': 'The Bates Motel, the setting for Alfred Hitchcock’s “Psycho” and a new A&E series, doesn’t see a lot of customers these days.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/10/arts/television/spending-the-night-inside-bates-motel.html', 'snippet': 'The Bates Motel, the setting for Alfred Hitchcock’s “Psycho” and a new A&E series, doesn’t see a lot of customers these days.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALDERGROVE, BRITISH COLUMBIA — Say what you will about Norma Bates’s notorious motel and her unusually vigilant child-rearing practices. The woman makes a darn good breakfast.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/10/arts/10BATES5/10BATES5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/10/arts/10BATES5/10BATES5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/10/arts/10BATES5/10BATES5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/10/arts/10BATES5/10BATES5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/10/arts/10BATES5/10BATES5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/10/arts/10BATES5/10BATES5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/10/arts/10BATES5/10BATES5-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Norman, Show Our Guest His Room', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Norman, Show Our Guest His Room', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Psycho (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARTS & ENTERTAINMENT NETWORK', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-08T22:57:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ba7dde0-1d6b-5291-b934-b85cfd083cdd', 'word_count': 1517, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ba7dde0-1d6b-5291-b934-b85cfd083cdd'}, {'abstract': 'Devendra Banhart shows maturity on his new album, “Mala,” following in the footsteps of other freak-folk acts like Joanna Newsom and Grizzly Bear.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/10/arts/music/devendra-banharts-mala-and-changes-in-freak-folk.html', 'snippet': 'Devendra Banhart shows maturity on his new album, “Mala,” following in the footsteps of other freak-folk acts like Joanna Newsom and Grizzly Bear.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On his latest release, “Mala,” the hippie-redux singer-songwriter Devendra Banhart can still be as loopy as he was on his first albums a decade ago. He calls himself a “low-bottom bottle-fed baby” and sings about a nun who quits an abbey to work as a V.J. (For those who don’t recall when MTV played videos, that abbreviation stands for “videodisc jockey.”) Reflecting his mother’s Venezuelan background and his time spent there as a child, Mr. Banhart croons two songs in Spanish.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/10/arts/10BANHART1_SPAN/10BANHART1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/10/arts/10BANHART1_SPAN/10BANHART1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/10/arts/10BANHART1_SPAN/10BANHART1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/10/arts/10BANHART1_SPAN/10BANHART1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/10/arts/10BANHART1_SPAN/10BANHART1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/10/arts/10BANHART1_SPAN/10BANHART1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/10/arts/10BANHART1_SPAN/10BANHART1_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Freak Folk Courts the Plain Folk', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Freak Folk Courts the Plain Folk', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Banhart, Devendra', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-08T22:58:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Browne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Browne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/993af575-296a-5c78-82ab-c0248b547b9c', 'word_count': 1273, 'uri': 'nyt://article/993af575-296a-5c78-82ab-c0248b547b9c'}, {'abstract': 'This month we feature a wonderfully diverse array of men, all admirable in distinct and varied ways.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/08/editors-letter-in-the-company-of-men/', 'snippet': 'This month we feature a wonderfully diverse array of men, all admirable in distinct and varied ways.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is a particular pleasure, as a woman, to get to edit a men’s issue. In fact, it is the great pleasure of journalism — and by extension of being a reader — to be able to step outside one’s own world and dive into another as an interested outsider. This month we feature a wonderfully diverse array of men, all admirable in distinct and varied ways.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '40', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In the Company of Men', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In The Company Of Men', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-08T23:00:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deborah Needleman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deborah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Needleman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/34c5bfc8-9ae1-5597-b37d-5fa40e8509b1', 'word_count': 468, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34c5bfc8-9ae1-5597-b37d-5fa40e8509b1'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Shultz, who was the secretary of state, labor and the Treasury, urged lawmakers to support the development of hydraulic fracturing, also known as fracking, and alternative energy.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/08/george-shultz-presses-congress-to-act-on-climate-change/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Shultz, who was the secretary of state, labor and the Treasury, urged lawmakers to support the development of hydraulic fracturing, also known as fracking, and alternative energy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'George P. Shultz, a former Republican cabinet secretary, seems an unlikely figure to fight for climate change, which is largely the political turf of Democrats.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'George Shultz Presses Congress to Act on Climate Change', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alternative and Renewable Energy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Energy and Power', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hydraulic Fracturing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shultz, George P', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-08T23:01:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Southall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Southall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b513eb4-f557-521c-a10a-3a64a1f50413', 'word_count': 447, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b513eb4-f557-521c-a10a-3a64a1f50413'}, {'abstract': 'The Commodity Futures Trading Commission announced on Friday that its general counsel, Dan M. Berk