material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/66406b03-7c54-5f8d-ab2b-42df00e6d10c', 'word_count': 894, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66406b03-7c54-5f8d-ab2b-42df00e6d10c'}, {'abstract': 'Our latest issue highlights the rise of the well-dressed man and the importance of male friendships.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/08/now-online-t-mens-fashion-spring-2013/', 'snippet': 'Our latest issue highlights the rise of the well-dressed man and the importance of male friendships.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The actor Matthias Schoenaerts, photographed by Bruce Weber, is the cover subject of the spring men’s fashion issue of T. Learn how the Belgian import is dealing with becoming an American sensation. Inside: read Guy Trebay’s essay about how the average male is shedding schlumpiness for style, meet five exceptionally talented young poets (and read their work) and visit the Stockholm studio of the perfumer Ben Gorham. Additional highlights from the magazine include “Sporting Goods,” a round-up of athletic gear, “The Male Bond,” in which Andrew O’Hagan ruminates on male friendships, and “The Modern Man,” a primer on the frank irony to dressing stylishly today. See all from the issue >> ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'T Men’s Fashion Spring 2013', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-09T00:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Editors', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c7aca6b9-2130-59a4-9b4a-5df527ed4d6c', 'word_count': 112, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c7aca6b9-2130-59a4-9b4a-5df527ed4d6c'}, {'abstract': 'At Hummus Elite, in Englewood, one owner supplies the enthusiasm, and one is the source of the knowledge and technical skills that elevate hummus and other dishes beyond the ordinary.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/10/nyregion/a-review-of-hummus-elite-in-englewood.html', 'snippet': 'At Hummus Elite, in Englewood, one owner supplies the enthusiasm, and one is the source of the knowledge and technical skills that elevate hummus and other dishes beyond the ordinary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even though Hummus Elite is mostly about hummus and has only 10 tables, a friend urged me to try it. I did, and was enchanted by almost every dish I ate. In the hummus category, these dishes included hummus with beef, hummus with eggplant, plain hummus and hummus with mushrooms and truffle oil. In the nonhummus category, they consisted of silky, roasted eggplant; ground beef-and-lamb kebabs fragrant with coriander; and, most surprising of all, an eight-ounce hamburger that, like the best backyard burgers, tasted as if it had been cooked over charcoal instead of just gas. ', 'print_section': 'NJ', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/10/nyregion/10DINENJ3/10DINENJ3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 417, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/10/nyregion/10DINENJ3/10DINENJ3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 417}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/10/nyregion/10DINENJ3/10DINENJ3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 712, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/10/nyregion/10DINENJ3/10DINENJ3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1425, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0,