da A&M University students now charged with manslaughter in the hazing death of a drum major plans to plead guilty in the hope of receiving a more lenient sentence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of a dozen Florida A&M University students now charged with manslaughter in the hazing death of a drum major plans to plead guilty in the hope of receiving a more lenient sentence, his lawyer said Friday. The student, Caleb Jackson, 24, who is in the Leon County Jail on a probation violation, was on the bus where the drum major, Robert Champion, was beaten in 2011. Mr. Jackson is expected to plead guilty next month in an Orlando court. Chuck Hobbs, his lawyer, said Mr. Jackson was not one of the students who beat Mr. Champion, 26. The guilty plea comes in response to a decision by Jeff Ashton, the newly elected state attorney for Orange and Osceola Counties, to add manslaughter charges to existing felony hazing charges. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Florida: Guilty Plea Expected in Hazing Death of Drum Major', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Florida: Guilty Plea Expected In Hazing Death of Drum Major', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Alvarez, Lizette', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hazing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Champion, Robert', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Florida A&M University', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-09T00:28:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lizette Alvarez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lizette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alvarez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1caad5a-1a8b-5a7f-baf0-64510bdd0d4a', 'word_count': 129, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1caad5a-1a8b-5a7f-baf0-64510bdd0d4a'}, {'abstract': 'Subjects include the opening of Fairway in Brooklyn, a brightly painted school and a St. Patrick’s Day parade in the Rockaways.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/08/the-week-in-pictures-for-march-8/', 'snippet': 'Subjects include the opening of Fairway in Brooklyn, a brightly painted school and a St. Patrick’s Day parade in the Rockaways.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here is a slide show of photographs from the past week in New York City and the region. Subjects include the opening of Fairway in Brooklyn, a brightly painted school and a St. Patrick’s Day parade in the Rockaways.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Week in Pictures for March 8', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parades', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "St Patrick's Day", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fairway Supermarkets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-09T00:30:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2afda3b-1a42-5cd2-a670-80b411cbc6c1', 'word_count': 129, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d2afda3b-1a42-5cd2-a670-80b411cbc6c1'}, {'abstract': 'Many of the accouterments of the White Horse Country Pub and Restaurant pay homage to England, but its offerings extend far beyond shepherd’s pie and Yorkshire pudding.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/10/nyregion/a-review-of-the-white-horse-country-pub-and-restaurant-in-marbledale-conn.html', 'snippet': 'Many of the accouterments of the White Horse Country Pub and Restaurant pay homage to England, but its offerings extend far beyond shepherd’s pie and Yorkshire pudding.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Its position along the Aspetuck River on a remote stretch of Route 202 in Marbledale, Conn., a few miles north of New Milford, makes the White Horse very much a country pub. ', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/10/nyregion/10DINECT2/10DINECT2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 391, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/10/nyregion/10DINECT2/10DINECT2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 391}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/10/nyregion/10DINECT2/10DINECT2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 668, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/10/nyregion/10DINECT2/10DINECT2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1335, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/10/nyregion/10DINECT2/10DINECT2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/10/nyregion/10DINECT2/10DINECT2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/10/nyregion/10DINECT2/10DINECT2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Old World Décor, and a Cosmopolitan Menu', 'kicker': 'Connecticut Dining | Marbledale', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Old World Décor, and a Cosmopolitan Menu', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Marbledale (Conn)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'White Horse Country Pub and Restaurant (Marbledale, Conn)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-09T00:31:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Brooks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/272f67cd-ba5d-56f1-9f77-2b2c72ea4b79', 'word_count': 746, 'uri': 'nyt://article/272f67cd-ba5d-56f1-9f77-2b2c72ea4b79'}, {'abstract': 'The F.B.I. is investigating racist and antigay messages left around Oberlin College in the past month and the possible sighting of someone wearing a Ku Klux Klan-type outfit.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/09/education/ohio-fbi-enters-inquiry-at-oberlin.html', 'snippet': 'The F.B.I. is investigating racist and antigay messages left around Oberlin College in the past month and the possible sighting of someone wearing a Ku Klux Klan-type outfit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The F.B.I. is investigating racist and antigay messages left around Oberlin College in the past month and the possible sighting of someone wearing a Ku Klux Klan-type outfit, a college spokesman said on Friday. A student newspaper, The Oberlin Review, reported that the college removed two students last week in connection with the vandalism; Oberlin would not comment on that report. The newspaper also reported that the recent incidents were probably linked to online racist messages dating back almost a year. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ohio: F.B.I. Enters Inquiry at Oberlin', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Midwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ohio: F.B.I. Enters Inquiry at Oberlin', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Investigation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oberlin College', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ku Klux Klan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ohio', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-09T00:37:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Pérez-Peña', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pérez-Peña', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b65e617-a00d-54cc-b3b1-64df7a37dfb8', 'word_count': 81, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b65e617-a00d-54cc-b3b1-64df7a37dfb8'}, {'abstract': 'The dishes at Coriander, compared with those at most Indian restaurants, seem lighter, but each dish’s flavors and complexities remain in full force.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/10/nyregion/a-review-of-coriander-in-larchmont.html', 'snippet': 'The dishes at Coriander, compared with those at most Indian restaurants, seem lighter, but each dish’s flavors and complexities remain in full force.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In these days of trendy fusion this and fusion that, diners often have to guess what lies ahead when a restaurant claims modernity. In the case of Coriander, in Larchmont, several factors combine to create a modern feel. The décor is low key: a contemporary beige and charcoal color scheme, brightened by a row of charming white lanterns in the aisle that leads to the dining room. A small handful of cross-legged mustachioed Rajasthani figurines and a dramatic Shiva as Nataraja the cosmic dancer set the Indian theme.', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/10/nyregion/10DINEWE2/10DINEWE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 522, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/10/nyregion/10DINEWE2/10DINEWE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 522}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/10/nyregion/10DINEWE2/10DINEWE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 891, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/10/nyregion/10DINEWE2/10DINEWE2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1781, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/10/nyregion/10DINEWE2/10DINEWE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/10/nyregion/10DINEWE2/10DINEWE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/10/nyregion/10DINEWE2/10DINEWE2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Indian Flavors, Cool, Minimalist and Modern', 'kicker': 'Westchester Dining | Larchmont', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Indian Flavors, Cool, Minimalist and Modern', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Larchmont (NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Coriander Modern Indian (Larchmont, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-09T00:41:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By M. H. Reed', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c7cd4924-475e-5363-919d-adf62dc51d60', 'word_count': 639, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c7cd4924-475e-5363-919d-adf62dc51d60'}, {'abstract': 'Performers from Questlove to Elvis Costello celebrated the music of Prince.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2013/03/08/arts/music/20130309PRINCE.html', 'snippet': 'Performers from Questlove to Elvis Costello celebrated the music of Prince.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Performers from Questlove to Elvis Costello celebrated the music of Prince.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/arts/artsspecial/20130309PRINCE-slide-TZFA/20130309PRINCE-slide-TZFA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/08/arts/artsspecial/20130309PRINCE-slide-TZFA/20130309PRINCE-slide-TZFA-articleLarge.jp