 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/3a51afd4-22db-5caa-a8f0-a755837d17e5'}, {'abstract': 'Tim Howard’s English club, Everton, announced that he had two broken bones in his back, and he is unlikely to play in two important World Cup qualifiers later this month.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/08/howard-has-broken-bones-in-back-likely-out-for-qualifiers/', 'snippet': 'Tim Howard’s English club, Everton, announced that he had two broken bones in his back, and he is unlikely to play in two important World Cup qualifiers later this month.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Goalkeeper Tim Howard has two broken bones in his back, his English club, Everton, announced Friday, an injury that will almost certainly rule him out of two important World Cup qualifiers for the United States national team later this month.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Howard Has Broken Bones in Back; Likely Out for Qualifiers', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Starting Goalkeeper Injured,\r\nThreatening U.S. Cup Hopes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Howard, Tim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Everton (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "United States Men's National Soccer Team", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-09T00:54:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Das', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Das', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dbc20b56-c3aa-5ac5-803e-f4e9d6d5ad28', 'word_count': 326, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dbc20b56-c3aa-5ac5-803e-f4e9d6d5ad28'}, {'abstract': 'Ballet Flamenco de Andalusia opened a short season at City Center on Wednesday night.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/09/arts/dance/ballet-flamenco-de-andalusia-at-city-center.html', 'snippet': 'Ballet Flamenco de Andalusia opened a short season at City Center on Wednesday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Wednesday night Ballet Flamenco de Andalusia opened a short season at City Center. When the music was live, it was wretchedly overamplified; often the dancers and singers performed to a taped orchestral accompaniment that sounded less like Andalusia than like a Hollywood idea of Spanish sounds. Two star dancers, Pastora Galván and Rubén Olmo, exuded absurd mannerism far more than they did flamenco rhythms. And the third, Rocío Molina, though a marvelous dancer, performed in an idiom that came across as pretentious. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/09/arts/09ANDALUCIA/09ANDALUCIA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 604, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/09/arts/09ANDALUCIA/09ANDALUCIA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 604}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/09/arts/09ANDALUCIA/09ANDALUCIA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1018, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/09/arts/09ANDALUCIA/09ANDALUCIA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2035, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/09/arts/09ANDALUCIA/09ANDALUCIA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/09/arts/09ANDALUCIA/09ANDALUCIA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/09/arts/09ANDALUCIA/09ANDALUCIA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When Each Stylized Flourish Proclaims Itself', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When Each Stylized Flourish Proclaims Itself', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ballet Flamenco de Andalusia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Center Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-09T00:56:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/69f0d180-1a39-5588-9b7c-633a39d2962c', 'word_count': 657, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69f0d180-1a39-5588-9b7c-633a39d2962c'}, {'abstract': '“The Music of Prince” brought a wide range of performers, including Elvis Costello, Bilal and the Blind Boys of Alabama, to Carnegie Hall on Thursday evening.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/09/arts/music/the-music-of-prince-tribute-at-carnegie-hall.html', 'snippet': '“The Music of Prince” brought a wide range of performers, including Elvis Costello, Bilal and the Blind Boys of Alabama, to Carnegie Hall on Thursday evening.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One concert could hardly contain the multiplicity of Prince’s enormous songwriting catalog over the 35 years since he released his debut album, “For You,” in 1978. “The Music of Prince,” a tribute concert on Thursday night at Carnegie Hall, tried hard. The program strove to capture a broad swath of Prince’s work, through funk and rock and pop, from lust to spirituality to apocalypse to partying. It included hits, rarities and even some of Prince’s dance moves (but alas, no leaping splits). It was the ninth annual “Music of” concert produced by Michael Dorf, the owner of City Winery, to benefit music programs for underprivileged children. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/09/arts/09PRINCE/09PRINCE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 392, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/09/arts/09PRINCE/09PRINCE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 392}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/09/arts/09PRINCE/09PRINCE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 670, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/09/arts/09PRINCE/09PRINCE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1339, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/09/arts/09PRINCE/09PRINCE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/09/arts/09PRINCE/09PRINCE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': N