ing sense of chaos and lawlessness in Egypt, where opposition to President Mohamed Morsi has been newly energized in recent days by anticipation of a second round of verdicts over the deaths of more than 70 soccer fans in a stadium riot in Port Said last year. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Police Strike, Egypt Tensely Awaits Verdicts in Soccer Riot', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Port Said (Egypt)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-09T02:04:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liam Stack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2eb0cbe0-2451-5748-8dd2-b80653d95b93', 'word_count': 991, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2eb0cbe0-2451-5748-8dd2-b80653d95b93'}, {'abstract': 'Lawmakers need to work with President Obama on a diplomatic solution to the nuclear dispute in Iran.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/09/opinion/congress-gets-in-the-way-on-iran.html', 'snippet': 'Lawmakers need to work with President Obama on a diplomatic solution to the nuclear dispute in Iran.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If there is any hope for a peaceful resolution of the nuclear dispute with Iran, President Obama needs Congress to support negotiations. But negotiations and compromise are largely anathema in Washington, with many lawmakers insisting that any deal with Iran would be unacceptable — a stance that would make military action by Israel and the United States far more likely.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Congress Gets in the Way', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Congress Gets in the Way', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-09T02:05:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b7b8f6d-cd22-51c8-9e94-f74637584ca0', 'word_count': 411, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b7b8f6d-cd22-51c8-9e94-f74637584ca0'}, {'abstract': 'Turning roadkill into dinner is common in parts of rural America, and state lawmakers are starting to take notice.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/09/opinion/doubling-back-for-the-roadkill.html', 'snippet': 'Turning roadkill into dinner is common in parts of rural America, and state lawmakers are starting to take notice.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Squirrel gravy is such a delicacy in Appalachia that there is a RoadKill Cook-off each year in the hollows of West Virginia. Lawmakers in Montana get the drift. The lower house of the Montana Legislature recently approved a measure that would allow citizens to salvage fresh roadkill and take it home for dinner. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Doubling Back for the Roadkill', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Doubling Back for the Roadkill', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Roadkill', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Montana', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-09T02:09:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b256541-9068-538f-81c5-924fad558f48', 'word_count': 258, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b256541-9068-538f-81c5-924fad558f48'}, {'abstract': 'Research suggests that sports fans, even zealous ones, are less prone to depression and alienation than nonfans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/09/sports/one-way-to-cheer-up-cheer-harder.html', 'snippet': 'Research suggests that sports fans, even zealous ones, are less prone to depression and alienation than nonfans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You probably think rabid sports fans are a bunch of lonely, disoriented souls who try to fill the holes in their lives by attaching themselves to a team. And you’re probably wrong.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/09/sports/YFANS/YFANS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/09/sports/YFANS/YFANS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None