 'uri': 'nyt://article/dca243f6-70ef-511a-a857-9cd7e82a1191'}, {'abstract': 'Representative Gregory W. Meeks, who had a little-known but significant relationship with Hugo Chávez, was part of a small United States delegation to Venezuela.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/09/nyregion/meeks-new-york-congressman-attends-chavez-funeral.html', 'snippet': 'Representative Gregory W. Meeks, who had a little-known but significant relationship with Hugo Chávez, was part of a small United States delegation to Venezuela.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Representative Gregory W. Meeks, a New York Democrat who developed a little-known but significant relationship with President Hugo Chávez of Venezuela over the last decade, attended Mr. Chávez’s funeral on Friday as part of a small United States delegation. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Queens Congressman Attends Chávez Funeral', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Queens Congressman Attends Chávez Funeral', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hernandez, Raymond', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Meeks, Gregory W', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chavez, Hugo', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Funerals and Memorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Delahunt, William D', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Venezuela', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-09T02:34:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Raymond Hernandez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Raymond', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hernandez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c51c1a9-05c1-58d9-8aed-5e0fff2fa109', 'word_count': 418, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c51c1a9-05c1-58d9-8aed-5e0fff2fa109'}, {'abstract': 'The vast majority of foreign aid is going to territory controlled by President Bashar al-Assad while the small amount reaching opposition-held areas is all but invisible.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/09/world/middleeast/in-syrias-rebel-strongholds-foreign-aid-yields-anger.html', 'snippet': 'The vast majority of foreign aid is going to territory controlled by President Bashar al-Assad while the small amount reaching opposition-held areas is all but invisible.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAWRAN, Syria — The United States and other international donors are spending hundreds of millions of dollars on humanitarian aid for Syrians afflicted by the civil war. But here in the rebel-controlled north, where the deprivation is most acute, that money has bought mostly anger and resentment: the vast majority of aid is going to territory controlled by President Bashar al-Assad, and the small amount reaching opposition-held areas is all but invisible.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/09/world/middleeast/RELIEF/RELIEF-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 416, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/09/world/middleeast/RELIEF/RELIEF-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 416}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/09/world/middleeast/RELIEF/RELIEF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 710, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', '