ial milestone today.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SATURDAY’S PUZZLE — This was a very interesting puzzle on quite a few levels: for one thing, with today’s puzzle, co-written by David Steinberg and Barry C. Silk, Mr. Steinberg has hit for the cycle after only his ninth puzzle published in The New York Times. Mr. Steinberg, who is in his mid-teens, has had at least one puzzle published in The Times on each day of the week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gets in a Lather', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-09T03:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/00d153df-c9dd-579e-8beb-cd222e73a95d', 'word_count': 297, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00d153df-c9dd-579e-8beb-cd222e73a95d'}, {'abstract': 'The Schoolhouse Theater’s production of Jon Robin Baitz’s “Ten Unknowns” opened on Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/10/nyregion/ten-unknowns-opens-at-the-schoolhouse-theater.html', 'snippet': 'The Schoolhouse Theater’s production of Jon Robin Baitz’s “Ten Unknowns” opened on Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most people don’t like Malcolm Raphelson. Even in his 70s, he is a menacing, arrogant, womanizing, narcissistic artist who has never forgiven Jackson Pollock and the other Abstract Expressionists for stealing his thunder in the 1940s and ’50s. Raphelson has an appetite for destruction, including his own.', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 