cruised past the Wizards.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Deron Williams’s night began quietly, with a 3-pointer from the left wing that whipped through the net about 90 seconds after the opening tip. Fans were still settling in their seats, and the Nets’ main concern was stopping Washington’s John Wall, a pesky guard who could cause them headaches.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/09/sports/NETS/NETS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 720, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/09/sports/NETS/NETS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 720}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/09/sports/NETS/NETS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 854, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/09/sports/NETS/NETS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1707, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/09/sports/NETS/NETS-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/09/sports/NETS/NETS-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/09/sports/NETS/NETS-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Williams Electrifies From Long Distance', 'kicker': 'Nets 95, Wizards 78', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Williams Electrifies From Long Distance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Nets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Wizards', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Deron', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carlesimo, P J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Evans, Reggie', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-09T03:31:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zach Schonbrun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zach', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schonbrun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e537acd-83c2-59a4-a2e2-35dc6385656f', 'word_count': 718, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e537acd-83c2-59a4-a2e2-35dc6385656f'}, {'abstract': 'A manager who turned around Germany’s national railway and second largest airline took over the company behind the construction of Berlin’s new international airport on Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/09/world/europe/germany-airport-project-reorganized.html', 'snippet': 'A manager who turned around Germany’s national railway and second largest airline took over the company behind the construction of Berlin’s new international airport on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A tough manager who turned around Germany’s national railway and second largest airline took over the company behind the construction of Berlin’s new international airport on Friday. “We will do everything to speed up the completion of the airport,” said the new leader, Hartmut Mehdorn, 70. Embarrassing budgetary and technical problems have repeatedly pushed the opening of the Berlin-Brandenburg Willy Brandt Airport further from its original target of last June, pushed costs to $5.2 billion, turned the project into a national joke, and cost the last manager, Rainer Schwarz, his job. Mr. Mehdorn brought the national railway, Deutsche Bahn, into profitability as its head from 1999 to 2009 and then helped return Air Berlin to competitiveness before leaving as its chief executive in January. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Germany: Airport Project Reorganized', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Germany: Airport Project Reorganized', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eddy, Melissa', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRPORTS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Berlin-Brandenburg International Airport', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Berlin (Germany)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-09T03:35:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Eddy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eddy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/540dce3c-bf4f-5687-beac-66bb80adc137', 'word_count': 124, 'uri': 'nyt://article/540dce3c-bf4f-5687-beac-66bb80adc137'}, {'abstract': 'While their Yankee teammates were on the other side of Florida, the aging stars Derek Jeter, Mariano Rivera and Andy Pettitte moved closer to playing together again.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/09/sports/baseball/derek-jeter-mariano-rivera-and-andy-pettitte-quietly-get-ready-for-season.html', 'snippet': 'While their Yankee teammates were on the other side of Florida, the aging stars Derek Jeter, Mariano Rivera and Andy Pettitte moved closer to playing together again.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TAMPA, Fla. — A team of aspiring Yankees played in a spring training game on the other side of Florida on Friday. Meanwhile, three of the most revered Yankees in team history had their run of the team’s quiet complex, preparing for what is likely to be their last season together after two immensely successful decades.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/09/sports/YANKEES/YANKEES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 421, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/09/sports/YANKEES/YANKEES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 421}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/09/sports/YANKEES/YANKEES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 443, 'width': 632, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/09/sports/YANKEES/YANKEES-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 443, 'width': 632, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/09/sports/YANKEES/YANKEES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/09/sports/YANKEES/YANKEES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/09/sports/YANKEES/YANKEES-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Three Men at Work, Quietly, While Yankees Are Elsewhere', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Three Men at Work, Quietly, While Yankees Are Elsewhere', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Waldstein, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rivera, Mariano', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jeter, Derek', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pettitte, Andy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-09T03:35:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e893a63-8fc1-5f7a-b68d-8076d0f3a096', 'word_count': 878, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e893a63-8fc1-5f7a-b68d-8076d0f3a096'}, {'abstract': 'Four former public officials pleaded guilty Friday to illegally selling information to the Rupert Murdoch-owned tabloid, The Sun.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/09/world/europe/britain-4-plead-guilty-in-selling-information-to-tabloids.html', 'snippet': 'Four former public officials pleaded guilty Friday to illegally selling information to the Rupert Murdoch-owned tabloid, The Sun.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the latest of dozens of criminal cases stemming from the phone-hacking scandal that led to the closure in 2011 of Rupert Murdoch’s News of the World tabloid, four former public officials pleaded guilty Friday to illegally selling information to another Murdoch-owned tabloid, The Sun. One, Alan Tierney, a former police constable, admitted to selling information in 2009 about the shoplifting arrests of the mother and mother-in-law of the soccer star John Terry. He also admitted selling another story that year about how the Rolling Stones guitarist Ron Wood had been arrested on suspicion of beating up a girlfriend. Mr. Tierney, who prosecutors said was paid $2,600, will be sentenced on March 27. Another defendant, Richard Trunkfield, a former prison officer at a high-security facility, admitted to receiving $5,000 for information about a “high-profile prisoner” in 2010. The two other defendants cannot be named because their alleged co-conspirators have yet to face trial. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Britain: 4 Plead Guilty in Selling Information to Tabloids', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Britain: 4 Plead Guilty in Selling Information to Tabloids', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lyall, Sarah', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wiretapping and Other Eavesdropping Devices and Methods', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News of the World', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sun, The (British Newspaper)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-09T03:39:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Lyall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lyall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/2361bf70-b705-55cc-9af5-a4bbb5264fb0', 'word_count'