e': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': 'Weddings', 'byline': {'original': 'Samantha Stark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Samantha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/93680f43-12bc-5a27-9593-a2305621918e', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/93680f43-12bc-5a27-9593-a2305621918e'}, {'abstract': 'The military had planned to hand over control of the prison on Saturday, but remarks President Hamid Karzai made about releases may have caused a reversal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/09/world/asia/us-cancels-transfer-of-bagram-prison-to-afghans.html', 'snippet': 'The military had planned to hand over control of the prison on Saturday, but remarks President Hamid Karzai made about releases may have caused a reversal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — A ceremony in which the American military had planned to hand over full control of the Bagram Prison to Afghanistan was canceled Saturday, throwing into doubt an agreement between the two countries on custody of the remaining Afghan prisoners still being held by American forces.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Cancels Transfer of Bagram Prison to Afghans', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Cancels Transfer of Bagram Prison to Afghans', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bagram Air Base (Afghanistan)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karzai, Hamid', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-09T05:04:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rod Nordland', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rod', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nordland', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a03672a5-9382-5fc2-9601-e1374c95d3eb', 'word_count': 540, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a03672a5-9382-5fc2-9601-e1374c95d3eb'}, {'abstract': 'The band Moshiach Oi!, part of an emerging strand of Jews defined by religion and rebellion, is in a documentary, “Punk Jews.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/10/nyregion/moshiach-oi-merges-orthodox-judaism-and-punk-rock.html', 'snippet': 'The band Moshiach Oi!, part of an emerging strand of Jews defined by religion and rebellion, is in a documentary, “Punk Jews.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'At age 6, he was a budding yeshiva student, in white shirt and black hat, with little contact outside the Orthodox Jewish world. At 16, he discovered some things he liked better, punk rock and drugs: marijuana, LSD, eventually crack and heroin. At 26, on the Thursday before the holiday of Purim last month, he was back among the faithful, sort of: side curls flailing, knees jackknifing up around his torso, leaping, crouching, shouting a Scriptural message from the Book of Ramones: “Avraham was a punk rocker.”', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/10/nyregion/10JEWS1_SPAN/10JEWS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/10/nyregion/10JEWS1_SPAN/10JEWS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/10/nyregion/10JEWS1_SPAN/10JEWS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 679, 'width': 1024, 's