aragraph': 'WASHINGTON — One morning in late September 2011, a group of American drones took off from an airstrip the C.I.A. had built in the remote southern expanse of Saudi Arabia. The drones crossed the border into Yemen, and were soon hovering over a group of trucks clustered in a desert patch of Jawf Province, a region of the impoverished country once renowned for breeding Arabian horses. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/10/world/10awlaki_511/10awlaki_511-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 250, 'width': 511, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/10/world/10awlaki_511/10awlaki_511-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 250, 'width': 511, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/10/world/10awlaki_511/10awlaki_511-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/10/world/10awlaki_511/10awlaki_511-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How a U.S.\r\n    Citizen Came to\r\n    Be in America’s\r\n    Cross Hairs', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A U.S. Citizen, in America’s Cross Hairs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Awlaki, Anwar al-', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mazzetti, Mark', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Savage, Charlie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Targeted Killings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drones (Pilotless Planes)', 'rank': 6