doing damage control, and will be featured on almost all of this week’s Sunday shows.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Former Gov. Jeb Bush of Florida made headlines in the past week after acknowledging he would be open to a run for the White House in 2016. But the renewed attention on Mr. Bush has been mixed. His book on immigration reform is dividing a Republican Party that is trying to connect with Latino voters. Mr. Bush is doing damage control, and will be featured on almost all of this week’s Sunday shows.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sunday Breakfast Menu, March 10', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-09T23:06:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jada F. Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jada', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2abf597c-89f3-53e0-b768-60b7fc0a56e9', 'word_count': 550, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2abf597c-89f3-53e0-b768-60b7fc0a56e9'}, {'abstract': 'Perhaps the most prominent self-described progressive with doubts about the current version of affirmative action is Richard D. Kahlenberg. He argues that the current race-focused version of affirmative action can be unfair, is inconsistent with many of the program’s original goals and has lost the support of the public.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/09/the-leading-liberal-against-affirmative-action/', 'snippet': 'Perhaps the most prominent self-described progressive with doubts about the current version of affirmative action is Richard D. Kahlenberg. He argues that the current race-focused version of affirmative action can be unfair, is inconsistent with m...', 'lead_paragraph': 'My Capital Ideas column this week looks at liberals who would see some upsides if the Supreme Court made substantial changes to affirmative-action programs. The justices heard arguments in such a case in October — Fisher v. the University of Texas — and are expected to issue their decision between March 18 and late June.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Leading Liberal Against Affirmative Action', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AFFIRMATIVE ACTION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kahlenberg, Richard D', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Texas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-09T23:06:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d98b31c-e16d-5d5a-9bcf-2b91c180c1e3', 'word_count': 564, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d98b31c-e16d-5d5a-9bcf-2b91c180c1e3'}, {'abstract': 'Over the long term, investors in equity mutual funds have underperformed the S.&.P. 500.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2013/03/10/business/Buying-High-and-Selling-Low.html', 'snippet': 'Over the long term, investors in equity mutual funds have underperformed the S.&.P. 500.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the long term, investors in equity mutual funds have underperformed the S.&.P. 500.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [