ne}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-10T10:48:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c5a4b0a-1f3d-5077-8095-117699022ba8', 'word_count': 11, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c5a4b0a-1f3d-5077-8095-117699022ba8'}, {'abstract': 'Tales of Osbornia.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/10/the-imf-on-the-austerity-trap/', 'snippet': 'Tales of Osbornia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The IMF has just released a new paper on austerity that is kind of heavy going (unnecessarily, I think), but ends up making a simple but important point. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The IMF on the Austerity Trap', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-10T11:05:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/98cde6dc-6e78-5af7-a070-9534b1ceff8f', 'word_count': 364, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98cde6dc-6e78-5af7-a070-9534b1ceff8f'}, {'abstract': 'If confirmed, the attack could be the first U.S. strike in Waziristan in two months — one of the longest operational pauses since the drone campaign started in earnest in mid-2008.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/11/world/asia/drone-strike-reported-in-pakistan.html', 'snippet': 'If confirmed, the attack could be the first U.S. strike in Waziristan in two months — one of the longest operational pauses since the drone campaign started in earnest in mid-2008.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PESHAWAR, Pakistan — Two people suspected of being militants were killed Sunday morning in the volatile North Waziristan tribal region by what Pakistani and Taliban officials said was a drone strike. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Attack, Said to Be Drone Strike by U.S., Kills 2 in Pakistan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Attack, Said to Be Drone Strike By U.S., Kills 2 in Pakistan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Khan, Ismail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drones (Pilotless Planes)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Waziristan (Pakistan)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-10T11:49:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ismail Khan and Declan Walsh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ismail', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Khan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Declan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Walsh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1ca027b-974d-5af3-9b12-308fe34ff322', 'word_count': 395, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1ca027b-974d-5af3-9b12-308fe34ff322'}, {'abstract': 'If my family history taught me anything, it was that hospitals meant death. So when my newborn son contracted a dangerous disease, I braced for the worst.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/10/intensive-care/', 'snippet': 'If my family history taught me anything, it was that hospitals meant death. So when my newborn son contracted a dangerous disease, I braced for the worst.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Our son was born healthy, large and pink-skinned, with a newborn assessment score of a perfect 10, but an hour after his birth, a nurse told us that something was wrong. He was jaundiced. It was not a typical case of jaundice; his bilirubin levels kept increasing at an alarming rate. I’d only seen him for a few moments — he’d been delivered by C-section, then whisked away for the usual tests and procedures — but now, as I was moved to a recovery room, the doctors couldn’t tell me when I might see my baby again.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Intensive Care', 'kicker': 'Anxiety', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies and Infants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nursing and Nurses', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-10T12:00:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margo Rabb', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margo', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rabb', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f009dcc9-de32-51ae-810b-99b2ad9126ac', 'word_count': 1389, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f009dcc9-de32-51ae-810b-99b2ad9126ac'}, {'abstract': 'Christine C. Quinn, the New York City Council speaker, visited all five boroughs on Sunday as she officially began her mayoral campaign.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/11/nyregion/quinn-declares-her-candidacy-for-nyc-mayor.html', 'snippet': 'Christine C. Quinn, the New York City Council speaker, visited all five boroughs on Sunday as she officially began her mayoral campaign.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the bus driver in the Bronx called out her name, Christine C. Quinn did not hesitate. The City Council speaker — and, as of Sunday, official candidate for mayor — bounded up the vehicle’s steps and gave him a warm handshake as passengers, unbothered by the delay, began to applaud.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With a Tour of the City, Quinn Declares Her Candidacy for Mayor', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With a Tour of the City, Quinn Declares Her Candidacy for Mayor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quinn, Christine C', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-10T12:40:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael M. Grynbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/33a91d2e-83ec-53d2-8550-568194c27b5f', 'word_count': 955, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33a91d2e-83ec-53d2-8550-568194c27b5f'}, {'abstract': 'Kim Jong-un and Uncle Sam face off.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/10/opinion/global/north-korea-and-the-un-sanctions.html', 'snippet': 'Kim Jong-un and Uncle Sam face off.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kim Jong-un and Uncle Sam face off.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/10/opinion/global/10iht-edheng10/10iht-edheng10-articleLarge.jpg', 