ubsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/1e18d9a3-13a7-521b-8e99-18e81af3b00c', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/1e18d9a3-13a7-521b-8e99-18e81af3b00c'}, {'abstract': 'In “Sticks and Stones” Emily Bazelon wants nothing less than for her readers, and her nation, utterly to rethink bullying.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/11/books/sticks-and-stones-by-emily-bazelon.html', 'snippet': 'In “Sticks and Stones” Emily Bazelon wants nothing less than for her readers, and her nation, utterly to rethink bullying.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Emily Bazelon was in eighth grade, her friends “fired” her. She had loved them; now they rejected her — an act, she recalls, that left her “crawling with insecurity and self-doubt.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/11/arts/BOOK/BOOK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 833, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/11/arts/BOOK/BOOK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 833}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/11/arts/BOOK/BOOK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 738, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/11/arts/BOOK/BOOK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1475, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/11/arts/BOOK/BOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/11/arts/BOOK/BOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/11/arts/BOOK/BOOK-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Words That Hurt and Kill: Lessons for Society From Bullying and Its Psychic Toll', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Words That Hurt and Kill: Lessons for Society From Bullying and Its Psychic Toll', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bazelon, Emily', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bullies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-10T22:06:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Schwartz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwartz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/acadf767-1dff-50cc-b2b6-291d2d347e34', 'word_count': 968, 'uri': 'nyt://article/acadf767-1dff-50cc-b2b6-291d2d347e34'}, {'abstract': 'Big oil plays the bad guy in “Ring of Fire,” on Reelz, and its drilling in an unsafe manner seems to annoy the Earth itself.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/11/arts/television/ring-of-fire-on-reelz.html', 'snippet': 'Big oil plays the bad guy in “Ring of Fire,” on Reelz, and its drilling in an unsafe manner seems to annoy the Earth itself.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The cast of “Ring of Fire,” a two-part disaster movie served up by Reelz on Monday and Tuesday, deserves credit for putting some effort into the film rather than sleepwalking through it, as actors often do in these collect-a-paycheck jobs. The script is decent enough too, for the first half. But the closer the world gets to ending, the more wearyingly formulaic “Ring of Fire” becomes.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Drilling Earth Seems to Get It Annoyed', 'kicker': 'Television Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Drilling Earth Seems to Get It Annoyed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ReelzChannel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Quinn, Terry", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Lauren Lee', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vartan, Michael', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-10T22:20:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2c4f49f-924e-51b3-aa5f-6b46c07c33fc', 'word_count': 349, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2c4f49f-924e-51b3-aa5f-6b46c07c33fc'}, {'abstract': 'As part of the Stripped/Dressed series at the Harkness Dance Festival, a discussion of Liz Gerring’s “she dreams in code” precedes a performance.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/11/arts/dance/liz-gerring-dance-company-at-the-92d-street-y.html', 'snippet': 'As part of the Stripped/Dressed series at the Harkness Dance Festival, a discussion of Liz Gerring’s “she dreams in code” precedes a performance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s not unusual to see small-scale modern-dance performances in which the choreographer and dancers return to the stage for a question-and-answer session. But the Stripped/Dressed series of this year’s Harkness Dance Festival at the 92nd Street Y has the choreographer and dancers explain things first. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/11/arts/GERRING/GERRING-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 341, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/11/arts/GERRING/GERRING-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 341}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/11/arts/GERRING/GERRING-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 582, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/11/arts/GERRING/GERRING-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1164, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/11/arts/GERRING/GERRING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/11/arts/GERRING/GERRING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/11/arts/GERRING/GERRING-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dissecting the Dance Even Before It Begins', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dissecting the Dance Even Before It Begins', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gerring, Liz, Dance Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gerring, Liz', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-10T22:23:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/375e4a4f-0cf1-5551-bbf1-3d352480ed38', 'word_count': 713, 'uri': 'nyt://article/375e4a4f-0cf1-5551-bbf1-3d352480ed38'}, {'abstract': 'First Book, a nonprofit that promotes literacy among children in low-income communities, will give two awards through its Stories for All project to publishers offering multicultural books.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/10/2-awards-given-to-promote-multicultural-childrens-books/', 'snippet': 'First Book, a nonprofit that promotes literacy among children in low-income communities, will give two awards through its Stories for All project to publishers offering multicultural books.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A month ago a nonprofit called First Book, which promotes literacy among children in low-income communities, announced the Stories for All project, a program intended to prod publishers to print more multicultural books. Kyle Zimmer, First Book’s chief executive, says that part of the motivation was the “chasm” between the number of people who want such books and what is available.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '2 Awards Given to Promote Multicultural Children’s Books', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '2 Awards for Multicultural Books', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Book Trade and Publishing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zimmer, Kyle', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'First Book', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'HarperCollins Publishers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'LEE & LOW BOOKS', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-10T22:26:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Leslie Kaufman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Leslie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaufman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/60eafc78-8658-5eb4-8520-9ae4cbc5ce20', 'word_count': 395, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60eafc78-8658-5eb4-8520-9ae4cbc5ce20'}, {'abstract': 'After the Night of the Stars charity pro-am event at the Richmond Bridge Club in London on Feb. 28 the players received a booklet.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/11/crosswords/bridge/bridge-night-of-the-stars-at-the-richmond-bridge-club.html', 'snippet': 'After the Night of the Stars charity pro-am event at the Richmond Bridge Club in London on Feb. 28 the players received a booklet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After the Night of the Stars charity pro-am event at the Richmond Bridge Club in London on Feb. 28 the players received a booklet. This contained copies of the deals with bidding and play predictions by various experts from around the world. And to give Jason Hackett from England credit, he did mention the unusual contract reached when Shivam Shah sat South, partnering Azad Mahomed.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type'