 at the South by Southwest festival.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/10/new-arrested-development-episodes-arent-enough-for-some-fans/', 'snippet': 'Mitch Hurwitz, the show’s creator, and two of its stars, Will Arnett and Jeffrey Tambor, talked about fans’ demand for a film at the South by Southwest festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AUSTIN, Tex. — For years after the cult series “Arrested Development” went off the air, the question was whether a movie about the demented Bluth family would follow. Now that the show, which ended in 2006, is getting new life with 14 more episodes on Netflix this spring, that was still the question of the hour at a South by Southwest festival Q&A session with Mitch Hurwitz, the show’s creator, and two of its stars, Will Arnett and Jeffrey Tambor.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New ‘Arrested Development’ Episodes Aren’t Enough for Some Fans', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Arrested Development (TV Program)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'South by Southwest Music and Media Conference', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hurwitz, Mitch', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-10T23:03:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d683b021-a914-5935-a6a0-d9c5ba7a9afa', 'word_count': 246, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d683b021-a914-5935-a6a0-d9c5ba7a9afa'}, {'abstract': 'Comic books went digital long ago, but Marvel Comics upped the ante significantly by unveiling a superhero-size slate of mobile and online initiatives.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/10/marvel-comics-introduces-redesigned-apps-and-new-video-programming/', 'snippet': 'Comic books went digital long ago, but Marvel Comics upped the ante significantly by unveiling a superhero-size slate of mobile and online initiatives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Like the rest of the publishing industry, comic books went digital long ago. You can catch up on Batman via mobile app and unfurl Wolverine’s claws from your laptop. But Marvel Comics upped the ante significantly on Sunday, unveiling a superhero-size slate of new and expanded mobile and online initiatives.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Marvel Comics, a Renewed Digital Mission', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Marvel Comics, A Renewed Digital Mission', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comic Books and Strips', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'South by Southwest Music and Media Conference', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Marvel Comics', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-10T23:25:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c5f12f6-e8cc-56aa-ace9-a1426e0b2697', 'word_count': 344, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c5f12f6-e8cc-56aa-ace9-a1426e0b2697'}, {'abstract': 'A committee in Saudi Arabia has recommended that “because of the scarcity of swordsmen and their unavailability in a number of regions” the princes who govern provinces should be free to use firing squads.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/11/world/middleeast/saudis-consider-firing-squads-for-executions.html', 'snippet': 'A committee in Saudi Arabia has recommended that “because of the scarcity of swordsmen and their unavailability in a number of regions” the princes who govern provinces should be free to use firing squads.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — After centuries of public beheadings, the kingdom of Saudi Arabia is considering firing squads as an alternative means of execution.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Saudis Consider Firing Squads for Executions', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Saudis Consider Firing Squads for Executions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kirkpatrick, David D', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Saudi Arabia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Swords', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-10T23:25:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By David D. Kirkpatrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/73b03279-c4a0-5eb8-bebf-8cad2ae3025c', 'word_count': 281, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73b03279-c4a0-5eb8-bebf-8cad2ae3025c'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Jan Brewer and her advisers are working to win o