 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mandhana, Niharika', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suicides and Suicide Attempts', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality and Misconduct', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-11T11:51:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Heather Timmons and Niharika Mandhana', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Heather', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Timmons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Niharika', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mandhana', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/55f0e9fe-5ab4-54c1-95b3-e5631951a4bc', 'word_count': 614, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55f0e9fe-5ab4-54c1-95b3-e5631951a4bc'}, {'abstract': 'Joe Nocera examines how Goldman Sachs handled the eToys I.P.O. | Erin Callan, former C.F.O. of Lehman Brothers, expresses regret over how career choices affected her personal life. | British lawmakers raise concerns over proposed legislation intended to protect the financial services sector.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/03/11/competing-interests-in-an-i-p-o/', 'snippet': 'Joe Nocera examines how Goldman Sachs handled the eToys I.P.O. | Erin Callan, former C.F.O. of Lehman Brothers, expresses regret over how career choices affected her personal life. | British lawmakers raise concerns over proposed legislation inten...', 'lead_paragraph': 'When it comes to hot initial public offerings, there is a long-running debate over the obligations of the underwriter. In one classic case, the 1999 I.P.O. of eToys, a cache of documents newly unearthed by Joe Nocera of The New York Times offers insight into the way one Wall Street firm, Goldman Sachs, has approached these deals. In a lawsuit that is still going on, lawyers for an eToys creditors’ committee claimed that Goldman purposely set a low price to create a first-day pop in the stock for institutional investors, at the expense of the company itself.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Competing Interests in an I.P.O.', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-11T11:53:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/78256fe8-201b-58d0-9b5b-b0901b77b85c', 'word_count': 2106, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78256fe8-201b-58d0-9b5b-b0901b77b85c'}, {'abstract': 'Avoiding “single supplements” while traveling, myths about the flu vaccine, Wi-Fi in every room and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/11/monday-reading-avoiding-single-surcharge-while-traveling/', 'snippet': 'Avoiding “single supplements” while traveling, myths about the flu vaccine, Wi-Fi in every room and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Monday Reading: Avoiding ‘Single’ Surcharge While Traveling', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-11