ading.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Melanie Thernstrom wrote this week’s cover article about a doctor who is trying to cure children of their dangerous food allergies. Thernstrom is the author, most recently, of “The Pain Chronicles.” She last wrote for the magazine about twiblings.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/magazine/08-melanie/08-melanie-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 640, 'width': 426, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/magazine/08-melanie/08-melanie-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 640, 'width': 426, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/magazine/08-melanie/08-melanie-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/08/magazine/08-melanie/08-melanie-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/08/magazine/08-melanie/08-melanie-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Behind the Cover Story: Melanie Thernstrom on Untangling the Mystery of Food Allergies', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALLERGIES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thernstrom, Melanie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-11T12:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Nolan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nolan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e3818fc2-26d2-5812-93fe-3e780434031b', 'word_count': 878, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e3818fc2-26d2-5812-93fe-3e780434031b'}, {'abstract': 'Nintendo’s Shigeru Miyamoto discusses sales of the company’s Wii U, violence and video games, and the games at the Museum of Modern Art.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/12/arts/video-games/shigeru-miyamoto-of-nintendo-on-wii-u-sales-and-game-violence.html', 'snippet': 'Nintendo’s Shigeru Miyamoto discusses sales of the company’s Wii U, violence and video games, and the games at the Museum of Modern Art.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since helping to invent the modern video-game industry in 1981 with his design of Donkey Kong, Nintendo’s Shigeru Miyamoto has repeatedly reinvented it, most notably with the Nintendo Entertainment System in the 1980s — it introduced Super Mario Bros. and the Legend of Zelda to American households — and in the 2000s with the Wii, whose arm-waving motion controls started yet another widely imitated video-game craze.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/12/theater/12nintendo-web/12nintendo-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/12/theater/12nintendo-web/12nintendo-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/12/theater/12nintendo-web/12nintendo-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption':