source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Roadside Bomb Kills 3 Soldiers in Pakistan Tribal District', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Roadside Bomb Kills 3 Soldiers in Pakistan Tribal District', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Improvised Explosive Devices', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tehrik-e-Taliban', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-11T12:38:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ihsanullah Tipu Mehsud', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ihsanullah', 'middlename': 'Tipu', 'lastname': 'Mehsud', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/34b7f91c-aa1d-5f4d-b417-7ca447741932', 'word_count': 181, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34b7f91c-aa1d-5f4d-b417-7ca447741932'}, {'abstract': '“The Bachelor” regains high ratings, Martha Stewart Living Omnimedia might be better off private and copyright issues have arisen for “Harlem Shake.”', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/11/the-breakfast-meeting-the-bachelor-draws-viewers-and-martha-stewarts-need-for-privacy/', 'snippet': '“The Bachelor” regains high ratings, Martha Stewart Living Omnimedia might be better off private and copyright issues have arisen for “Harlem Shake.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'ABC’s romance reality show “The Bachelor” has experienced a rare resurgence after a downswing that lasted several seasons\xa0, Amy Chozick and Bill Carter report. The show, which pairs a hunky man with dozens of heavily made-up women until he picks one as his fiancée, has become the unlikely exception in a television season when almost every other show on ABC and its competitors has declined. The audience has increased to 8.8 million viewers, 3.3 million of whom are 18 to 49 years old, the most attractive group for advertisers. The show is especially popular among women, particularly those in households that make more than $100,000 a year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting: ‘The Bachelor’ Draws Viewers, and Martha Stewart’s Need for Privacy', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Harvard University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Martha Stewart Living Omnimedia Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-11T12:52:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel E. Slotnik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Slotnik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/013d7657-0eb1-5814-94d2-ffa59d0cd4d7', 'word_count': 661, 'uri': 'nyt://article/013d7657-0eb1-5814-94d2-ffa59d0cd4d7'}, {'abstract': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/11/the-gun-report-march-11-2013/', 'snippet': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On February 27, we included in our gun report\xa0the murder of two officers in Santa Cruz, Calif., who were shot while following up on a sexual assault claim. The gunman, Jeremy Goulet, who was killed by police, was an Army veteran who had been accused of raping two military officers in 2006. Instead of jail time, a plea bargain allowed him to walk away with a less than honorable discharge. Former Defense Secretary Leon Panetta, who once represented Santa Cruz in Congress, spoke at the slain officers’ memorial service and suggested that this slap on the wrist paved the way for Goulet’s final, horrific crime.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Gun Report: March 11, 2013', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kansas City (Mo)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nashville (Tenn)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oklahoma City (Okla)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Santa Cruz (Calif)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tulsa (Okla)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Whitefish (Mont)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-11T13:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Mascia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mascia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8e8bb3b-16ac-5757-8821-4aa4d77ac1a5', 'word_count': 693, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8e8bb3b-16ac-5757-8821-4aa4d77ac1a5'}, {'abstract': 'Carl C. Icahn said on Monday that he had signed a confidentiality agreement with Dell Inc., potentially heading off a confrontation over its $24.4 billion sale.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/03/11/icahn-signs-confidentiality-agreement-with-dell/', 'snippet': 'Carl C. Icahn said on Monday that he had signed a confidentiality agreement with Dell Inc., potentially heading off a confrontation over its $24.4 billion sale.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dell Inc. has agreed to open its books to the activist investor Carl C. Icahn, signaling a possible truce on one front in the battle over the computer maker’s proposed $24.4 billion buyout.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dell Agrees to Open Its Books to Icahn', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dell Agrees To Show Financials To Icahn', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dell, Michael S', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Icahn, Carl C', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dell Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-11T13:00:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd7bb982-8031-5cbc-926d-2cc646449e77', 'word_count': 636, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd7bb982-8031-5cbc-926d-2cc646449e77'}, {'abstract': 'Hageled, too.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/11/breitbarted/', 'snippet': 'Hageled, too.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OK, I’m an evil person — and my scheming has paid off.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Breitbarted', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-11T13:13:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb117ea7-747c-5206-be21-b44161bea063', 'word_count': 101, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb117ea7-747c-5206-be21-b44161bea063'}, {'abstract': 'Sanctions do nothing but hurt those who have no say.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/11/opinion/global/leave-iran-to-its-own-devices.html', 'snippet': 'Sanctions do nothing but hurt those who have no say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Iran should be left alone with its nuclear ambitions. Sanctions do nothing more than hurt those who have nothing to say about anything in their own country. Just tell the Iranians this: If you detonate one of the weapons outside of your country, your country will cease to exist.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Leave Iran to Its Own Devices', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-11T13:17:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Global Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb9f1c15-99ba-50b3-9f95-cf5e155d5e4a', 'word_count': 53, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb9f1c15-99ba-50b3-9f95-cf5e155d5e4a'}, {'abstract': 'Thousands including women and children demand action against the rising pollution in the river.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/11/massive-march-for-yamuna-river-nears-delhi/', 'snippet': 'Thousands including women and children demand action against the rising pollution in the river.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI —Tens of thousands of villagers are marching toward Delhi to pressure the central government to save the Yamuna River, in one of the biggest protests against river pollution in India.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/11/world/asia/11-Yamuna-IndiaInk/11-Yamuna-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 410, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/11/world/asia/11-Yamuna-IndiaInk/11-Yamuna-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 410}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/11/world/asia/11-Yamuna-IndiaInk/11-Yamuna-IndiaInk-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 700, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/11/world/asia/11-Yamuna-IndiaInk/11-Yamuna-IndiaInk-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1400, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/11/world/asia/11-Yamuna-IndiaInk/11-Yamuna-IndiaInk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/11/world/asia/11-Yamuna-IndiaInk/11-Yamuna-IndiaInk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/11/world/asia/11-Yamuna-IndiaInk/11-Yamuna-IndiaInk-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline'