'nyt://article/7b75c6ac-0ff4-53cc-ae93-1c4f2c588266'}, {'abstract': 'When the stock market hits new highs or lows, investors often question whether they should be making changes to their original investment plan.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/11/market-milestones-can-lead-to-false-assumptions/', 'snippet': 'When the stock market hits new highs or lows, investors often question whether they should be making changes to their original investment plan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Any time the stock market hits a new milestone, whether it’s going up or down, we start to hear a lot of noise. And the chatter seems to be focused on this idea of what it all means.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Market Milestones Can Lead to False Assumptions', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Avoiding False Assumptions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-11T14:34:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Richards', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Richards', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc2d5847-69a0-5751-9919-7d58ff669f9c', 'word_count': 366, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc2d5847-69a0-5751-9919-7d58ff669f9c'}, {'abstract': 'Participants at SXSW may not read print newspapers much, but they love quality information', 'web_url': 'https://publiceditor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/11/for-the-tech-crowd-a-taste-of-newspaper-talk/', 'snippet': 'Participants at SXSW may not read print newspapers much, but they love quality information', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here in Austin, Tex., where I’m attending the digital media extravaganza known as South by Southwest, or SXSW, the arrival of the local newspaper at the hotel room door each morning seems almost otherworldly. Amid this gathering of techie (not to say geeky, because that would be a bit unfair), mostly young, mostly male participants, where plaid flannel is the de rigueur fashion note and Google glasses are the accessory of choice, The Austin American-Statesman feels like an unfamiliar visitor from the distant past. (It’s a good paper, by the way, with Pulitzer Prizes in its history and a lively local report each day.) To put it mildly, this is not a print newspaper kind of crowd.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For the Tech Crowd, a Taste of Newspaper Talk', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'South by Southwest Music and Media Conference', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-11T14:37:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaret Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b44b9799-a79c-5954-8b30-d51d68fc1f8e', 'word_count': 447, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b44b9799-a79c-5954-8b30-d51d68fc1f8e'}, {'abstract': "The Times's Adam Liptak on the growing advantage less populated states enjoy in the Senate.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/us/politics/100000002111367/reasonable-representation.html', 'snippet': "The Times's Adam Liptak on the growing advantage less populated states enjoy in the Senate.", 'lead_paragraph': "The Times's Adam Liptak on the growing advantage less populated states enjoy in the Senate.", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtyp