{'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/12/nyregion/12qanda/12qanda-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/12/nyregion/12qanda/12qanda-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Your Guide to New York’s Soda Ban', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beverages', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coffee', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soft Drinks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-11T15:46:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivian Yee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1df4be2-9de0-5c74-be2f-28c4345b0cf0', 'word_count': 783, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1df4be2-9de0-5c74-be2f-28c4345b0cf0'}, {'abstract': 'The Supreme Court’s Prize Cases decision and the apogee of Lincoln’s executive powers.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/11/abraham-lincoln-war-president/', 'snippet': 'The Supreme Court’s Prize Cases decision and the apogee of Lincoln’s executive powers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Throughout the Civil War, the federal courts made little attempt to curb the wide executive war powers claimed by President Abraham Lincoln. Judges issued few pronouncements on the legality of the president’s most controversial measures, one way or the other. This included the Supreme Court – with one critical exception: the ruling in the so-called Prize Cases in early 1863, involving the blockade of Southern ports. The justices, along narrow lines, validated Lincoln’s broad claim, under the war powers, to confiscate goods found aboard blockade runners, in perhaps the court’s most important decision during the entire war.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Abraham Lincoln, War President', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitution (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Habeas Corpus', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lincoln, Abraham', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-11T15:57:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Greenbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f89ac1c8-11fd-5a89-899f-8e56d5d40490', 'word_count': 1607, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f89ac1c8-11fd-5a89-899f-8e56d5d40490'}, {'abstract': 'The moves are the latest in a series of steps by taken by both Congress and the administration to expand the S.B.A.’s reach by making more businesses eligible for the agency’s programs.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/11/s-b-a-proposes-rule-changes-to-lure-borrowers/', 'snippet': 'The moves are the latest in a series of steps by taken by both Congress and the administration to expand the S.B.A.’s reach by making more businesses eligible for the agency’s programs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Concerned, apparently, that not enough businesses are taking advantage of government-guaranteed loans, the Small Business Administration recently proposed changing some of its lending rules. If adopted, the new rules could make the agency’s loan programs accessible and popular enough that they could reach their legal limits on lending — something the programs have seldom ever done. Oddly enough, this is happening at the same time the prospective “sequester” budget cuts may force the agency to make fewer loans.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'S.B.A. Proposes Rule Changes to Lure Borrowers', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mills, Karen', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Small Business Administration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-11T16:00:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robb Mandelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mandelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/622e326b-7ac4-5897-9d67-25e8d42e639b', 'word_count': 1203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/622e326b-7ac4-5897-9d67-25e8d42e639b'}, {'abstract': "The Times's Michael M. Grynbaum on Christine C. Quinn's bid to be New York City's first female and openly gay mayor.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/nyregion/100000002111441/th