lf-conscious new parent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s unusual for me to interview the author of a novel, rather than a nonfiction book on parenting. But then, “The Sunshine When She’s Gone,” by Thea Goodman, is an unusual book. Ms. Goodman’s main characters, the new parents Veronica and John, find themselves in that strange, sleep-deprived dream state of new parenthood, and then act on escape fantasies that will seem familiar to anyone who has been there. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/11/style/motherlode-sunshine-when-shes-gone/motherlode-sunshine-when-shes-gone-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 282, 'width': 186, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/11/style/motherlode-sunshine-when-shes-gone/motherlode-sunshine-when-shes-gone-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 282, 'width': 186, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/11/style/motherlode-sunshine-when-shes-gone/motherlode-sunshine-when-shes-gone-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/11/style/motherlode-sunshine-when-shes-gone/motherlode-sunshine-when-shes-gone-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/11/style/motherlode-sunshine-when-shes-gone/motherlode-sunshine-when-shes-gone-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Q. and A. With Thea Goodman, Author of ‘The Sunshine When She’s Gone’', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kick