rity.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a Facebook post on Sunday, ’ino announced that it had closed. When the shoebox-shaped and nearly shoebox-size panini shop opened on Bedford Street 15 years ago, there was nothing quite like it in New York, a restaurant that kept things simple and kept prices low, serving flavorful food in a room that was just adorable enough that you could decide, midmeal, that maybe the two of you squeezed into the counter were there on a date, and not just grabbing a bite. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '’Ino Helped Usher In Simpler, Freer Fare', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "'Ino (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Village (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-11T17:58:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Oliver Strand', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Oliver', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Strand', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b89315d-5e6e-56e7-8ed7-a46216ae503d', 'word_count': 586, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b89315d-5e6e-56e7-8ed7-a46216ae503d'}, {'abstract': 'A breakdown of the junk foods that readers said they have a love-hate relationship with.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/11/the-junk-food-pile/', 'snippet': 'A breakdown of the junk foods that readers said they have a love-hate relationship with.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What emerged from the 1,300-plus comments posted by readers in response to Michael Moss’s article, “The Extraordinary Science of Addictive Junk Food,” was not only a debate over t