urant ready for Valentine’s Day, and an owner shoveling out her business after a heavy snow storm.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Small Picture: Capturing the Soul of Your Business', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-11T21:06:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': "By You're the Boss Editors", 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d32da84d-d6d2-5516-9a64-b9ea9cc5fd63', 'word_count': 184, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d32da84d-d6d2-5516-9a64-b9ea9cc5fd63'}, {'abstract': 'Marty Mornhinweg, the new offensive coordinator for the Jets, stressed the importance of competition at the quarterback position.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/11/mornhinweg-is-assessing-jets-quarterbacks/', 'snippet': 'Marty Mornhinweg, the new offensive coordinator for the Jets, stressed the importance of competition at the quarterback position.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GLEN RIDGE, N.J. – Mark Sanchez threw four interceptions in a must-win December game at Tennessee. He committed 26 turnovers overall, and for the second straight season. He was also benched twice. But it seems increasingly apparent that Sanchez will begin training camp as the Jets’ starting quarterback, regardless of how the team addresses the position through free agency and the draft, or in a potential trade.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mornhinweg Is Assessing Jets Quarterbacks', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jets Sign Garrad', '