, Andrew M', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klein, Jeffrey D', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Silver, Sheldon', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Skelos, Dean G', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-11T22:34:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Kaplan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaplan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ccc34434-79f6-5d1a-8f90-a6f102f19590', 'word_count': 582, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ccc34434-79f6-5d1a-8f90-a6f102f19590'}, {'abstract': 'The S.E.C. said that Oppenheimer had inflated the value of the largest investment in its fund. The false valuation raised the fund’s internal rate of return.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/03/11/oppenheimer-settles-s-e-c-s-accusations-it-misled-investors/', 'snippet': 'The S.E.C. said that Oppenheimer had inflated the value of the largest investment in its fund. The false valuation raised the fund’s internal rate of return.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Oppenheimer & Company will pay nearly $3 million to settle accusations by federal and state regulators that it misled investors about the performance of one of its private equity funds, in a case that signals stepped-up scrutiny of the buyout industry and how it values its holdings.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Oppenheimer Settles S.E.C.’s Accusations It Misled Investors', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Oppenheimer Settles Accusations of Misleading Investors', 'n