b2e-58c6-a70f-c04bea5ae557'}, {'abstract': 'Even among the supporters of gun rights who packed the Connecticut State Capitol, many appeared resigned to greater restrictions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/12/nyregion/gun-rights-backers-rally-in-hartford.html', 'snippet': 'Even among the supporters of gun rights who packed the Connecticut State Capitol, many appeared resigned to greater restrictions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HARTFORD — More than 1,000 supporters of gun rights, most wearing red stickers reading “N.R.A. Stand and Fight,” packed the atrium of the State Capitol on Monday as Connecticut’s protracted negotiations on new gun laws seemed to be lurching toward a resolution.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/12/nyregion/Y-CTGUNS1/Y-CTGUNS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/12/nyregion/Y-CTGUNS1/Y-CTGUNS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/12/nyregion/Y-CTGUNS1/Y-CTGUNS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/12/nyregion/Y-CTGUNS1/Y-CTGUNS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/12/nyregion/Y-CTGUNS1/Y-CTGUNS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/12/nyregion/Y-CTGUNS1/Y-CTGUNS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/12/nyregion/Y-CTGUNS1/Y-CTGUNS1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Gun-Rights Allies Rally in Hartford Against New Rules ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gun-Rights Allies Rally in Hartford Against New Rules', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Applebome, Peter', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hartford (Conn)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-12T00:26:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Applebome', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Applebome', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c819411-40d5-5b01-bd8f-f782d202b400', 'word_count': 416, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c819411-40d5-5b01-bd8f-f782d202b400'}, {'abstract': 'A federal judge has upheld all but one aspect of an Arizona law prohibiting school districts from offering courses taught from a specific racial or ethnic perspective.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/12/education/most-of-arizona-law-on-ethnic-studies-is-upheld.html', 'snippet': 'A federal judge has upheld all but one aspect of an Arizona law prohibiting school districts from offering courses taught from a specific racial or ethnic perspective.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A federal judge has upheld all but one aspect of an Arizona law prohibiting school districts from offering courses taught from a specific racial or ethnic perspective, which targeted the Mexican-American studies program at some Tucson public schools. The ruling Friday, by Judge A. Wallace Tashima of the United States Court of Appeals for the Ninth Circuit, came in a lawsuit brought by teachers and students at the Tucson Unified School District against Arizona’s school superintendent, John Huppenthal, and other state officials. The plaintiffs say the law is too broad to be constitutional. The law, signed in 2010, prohibits public schools from offering courses that promote the overthrow of the United States government, advocate ethnic solidarity and foster resentment toward a race or class of people. In Tucson, students studied history and literature from a Mexican-American perspective. Opponents said the curriculum encouraged students to resent white people. Judge Tashima ruled, however, that banning classes tailored specifically to students of a particular ethnicity is unconstitutional. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Arizona: Most of Law on Ethnic Studies Is Upheld', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Southwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Arizona: Most of Law On Ethnic Studies Is Upheld', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santos, Fernanda', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-12T00:35:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fernanda Santos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fernanda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/04724d89-23f8-531e-b6eb-102bd80de8c8', 'word_count': 164, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04724d89-23f8-531e-b6eb-102bd80de8c8'}, {'abstract': 'Students at the Pontifical North American College in Rome have the rare opportunity to watch a papal transition up close.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/12/world/europe/us-seminarians-in-rome-have-ringside-seat-for-conclave.html', 'snippet': 'Students at the Pontifical North American College in Rome have the rare opportunity to watch a papal transition up close.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — Morning prayers, chanted in Latin, had just ended at the Benedictine monastery in France, where a few American seminarians were on retreat. A monk quietly approached one of them, James Platania, who was walking through the cloister to the refectory, and asked if he had heard the news. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/12/world/SEMINARIANS/SEMINARIANS-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/12/world/SEMINARIANS/SEMINARIANS-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/12/world/SEMINARIANS/SEMINARIANS-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': No