ion-of-the-day-for-tuesday-mar-12-2013.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the day for Tuesday, Mar. 12, 2013.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I’ve got to defend my children, and yours, and do what’s right to save lives. Obesity kills. There’s no question it kills.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day for Tuesday, Mar. 12, 2013', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-12T01:55:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/56ea1ee0-4a55-5f20-b4bf-7af3423033bc', 'word_count': 42, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56ea1ee0-4a55-5f20-b4bf-7af3423033bc'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on March 12, 2013.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/12/pageoneplus/corrections-march-12-2013.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on March 12, 2013.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRONT PAGE', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: March 12, 2013', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-12T02:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/298d9b1b-2e4f-5781-8725-1410ac586c00', 'word_count': 491, 'uri': 'nyt://article/298d9b1b-2e4f-5781-8725-1410ac586c00'}, {'abstract': '“Neva” is a Guillermo Calderón play set in 1905 Russia and centering on Chekhov’s widow, Olga Knipper.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/12/theater/reviews/neva-by-guillermo-calderon-at-the-public-theater.html', 'snippet': '“Neva” is a Guillermo Calderón play set in 1905 Russia and centering on Chekhov’s widow, Olga Knipper.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I am beginning to think that all an aspiring (or established) dramatist needs to do to draw notice is to billboard some connection to Chekhov in his or her work, so august has the Russian author’s name become. “Neva,” a new play written and directed by the Chilean writer Guillermo Calderón that is having its English-language premiere at the Public Theater, is a turgid and repetitive meditation on love, theater and politics, but it has already been widely seen on international stages, possibly because Olga Knipper, Chekhov’s widow, has a central role.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/12/arts/12NEVAjp/12NEVAjp-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/12/arts/12NEVAjp/12NEVAjp-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/12/arts/12NEVAjp/12NEVAjp-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 679, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/12/arts/12NEVAjp/12NEVAjp-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1358, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/12/arts/12NEVAjp/12NEVAjp-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/12/arts/12NEVAjp/12NEVAjp-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, '