/12/world/americas/falkland-islanders-vote-to-remain-part-of-britain.html', 'snippet': 'All but three voters in the south Atlantic archipelago, which Argentina claims, cast ballots in favor of remaining an overseas territory of Britain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BUENOS AIRES — All but three voters in the Falkland Islands, the south Atlantic archipelago, cast ballots Sunday and Monday in favor of remaining an overseas territory of Britain. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Falkland Islanders Vote to Remain Part of Britain', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Falkland Islanders Vote to Remain Part of Britain', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Referendums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Falkland Islands', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARGENTINA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-12T03:55:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily Schmall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schmall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea0ad625-7b00-534d-852b-947266825703', 'word_count': 222, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea0ad625-7b00-534d-852b-947266825703'}, {'abstract': 'About 130 people had gathered in East Flatbush and were marching toward the 67th Police Precinct station house when about two dozen protesters splintered off and grew rowdy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/12/nyregion/violence-breaks-out-in-brooklyn-at-vigil-for-teenager-killed-by-the-police.html', 'snippet': 'About 130 people had gathered in East Flatbush and were marching toward the 67th Police Precinct station house when about two dozen protesters splintered off and grew rowdy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A vigil for an armed Brooklyn teenager who was fatally shot by police officers turned violent Monday night when a small group broke off from the gathering and began throwing bottles at a local police precinct station house and knocking food off a bodega stand, the authorities said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vigil for Brooklyn Teenager Fatally Shot by the Police Turns Violent', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Brooklyn Vigil For Teenager Turns Violent', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ruderman, Wendy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gray, Kimani', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Attacks on Police', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-12T03:55:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Wendy Ruderman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Wendy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ruderman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4e6e59b-aa9e-5d1b-8347-ee58861d74bd', 'word_count': 354, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4e6e59b-aa9e-5d1b-8347-ee58861d74bd'}, {'abstract': 'This word has appeared in 25 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/12/word-of-the-day-unimpeachable/', 'snippet': 'This word has appeared in 25 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'unimpeachable •\\ˌən-im-ˈpe-chə-bəl\\• adjective', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Word of the Day | unimpeachable', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-12T04:04:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2709f746-47f2-5616-b280-1fb078c7173f', 'word_count': 280, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2709f746-47f2-5616-b280-1fb078c7173f'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/12/arts/television/whats-on-tuesday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '1:15 P.M. (MoreMax) LOLA VERSUS (2012) After Lola (Greta Gerwig, above), a graduate student in New York, is dumped by her fiancé, Luke (Joel Kinnaman), as her 30th birthday approaches, she tries to pull her life together with the help of her best friends, the wacky Alice (Zoe Lister-Jones) and the sensitive Henry (Hamish Linklater). But somehow Luke can’t let go of Lola entirely, and she can’t help longing to get back together with him. Debra Winger and Bill Pullman play Lola’s mostly supportive parents. The film, directed by Daryl Wein from a script he wrote with Ms. Lister-Jones, who are a couple in real life, “very much wants to be a funny, affectionate portrait of a young woman in crisis,” A. O. Scott wrote in The New York Times. “\xa0‘Lola Versus,’ unfortunately, is a dismayingly conventional exploration of the vicissitudes of romance. In spite of its scruffy look and slack pacing, it often rings as false as any of the big, shiny and soft studio rom-coms (starring Kate Hudson or Katherine Heigl, say) of the last decade.” Lola, he added, “deserves better.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Tuesday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-12T05:00:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/583a534e-1059-5fe5-8514-59a5171bc523', 'word_count': 777, 'uri': 'nyt://article/583a534e-1059-5fe5-8514-59a5171bc523'}, {'abstract': 'As anger bubbles up about pollution in China, online posters are altering a sacrosanct image of Chairman Mao to channel their frustration into humor.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/12/mao-zedongs-anti-pollution-face-mask/', 'snippet': 'As anger bubbles up about pollution in China, online posters are altering a sacrosanct image of Chairman Mao to channel their frustration into humor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — With air readings of “hazardous” or “very unhealthy” seemingly the new normal, antipollution face masks are becoming a common sight on the streets of China. Even Mao Zedong has donned one. At least his image has, in doctored photos circulating online to widespread amusement (Mao, of course, died in 1976.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/12/global-home/12rdv-mao/12rdv-mao-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 270, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/12/global-home/12rdv-mao/12rdv-mao-articleLa