nization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a37c60f7-da37-5191-88a0-142770457a4d', 'word_count': 1691, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a37c60f7-da37-5191-88a0-142770457a4d'}, {'abstract': 'Broke and without work, Daniel Rodrigues had to sell his photo gear to pay the bills. Then one good frame gave him another shot at photojournalism.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/12/good-luck-and-good-light/', 'snippet': 'Broke and without work, Daniel Rodrigues had to sell his photo gear to pay the bills. Then one good frame gave him another shot at photojournalism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Daniel Rodrigues is a 26-year-old freelance photographer based in Porto, Portugal. After graduating from the Portuguese Institute of Photography in 2010, he was an intern for the newspaper Correio da Manhã and worked for the photo agency Global Imagens. Two years later, Rodrigues was broke. That was when a stroke of good luck — and good light — changed his fortunes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Good Luck and Good Light', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Press Photo Foundation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guinea', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-12T09:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jesse Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jesse', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2d69a81-f8ec-5182-9789-908e0b041958', 'word_count': 575, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2d69a81-f8ec-5182-9789-908e0b041958'}, {'abstract': 'How much stuff have you accumulated over the years? Are there things you own that you don’t need?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/12/does-buying-and-accumulating-more-and-more-stuff-make-us-happier/', 'snippet': 'How much stuff have you accumulated over the years? Are there things you own that you don’t need?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Americans love to buy things: tech gadgets, clothing, sneakers, jewelry, you name it. We love to accumulate what we buy too, so it overflows our rooms, closets, garages, basements and yards. And then we throw some of it away and buy more.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/10/sunday-review/10NOTHING-LN/10NOTHING-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/10/sunday-review/10NOTHING-LN/10NOTHING-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/10/sunday-review/10NOTHING-LN/10NOTHING-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/10/sunday-review/10NOTHING-LN/10NOTHING-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/10/sunday-review/10NOTHING-LN/10NOTHING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/0