fetime of sex offenses.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/13/world/europe/british-report-says-police-failed-to-pursue-savile-sex-charges.html', 'snippet': 'A report released Tuesday found a catalog of police failures that allowed Jimmy Savile, a television personality, to avoid investigation for a lifetime of sex offenses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Police failures over five decades allowed Jimmy Savile, one of Britain’s best-known television personalities, to escape investigation for a lifetime of sex offenses dating back to the early 1960s, according to a report published on Tuesday by a police oversight agency.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'British Oversight Unit Says Police Failed to Pursue Sex Accusations Against Savile', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'British Oversight Unit Says Police Failed to Pursue Sex Accusations Against Savile', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Castle, Stephen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Savile, Jimmy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-12T11:52:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Castle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Castle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f14fd955-e0f5-5d70-8c97-f08e3f1a21a1', 'word_count': 735, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f14fd955-e0f5-5d70-8c97-f08e3f1a21a1'}, {'abstract': 'A summary of what’s on today’s editorial page.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/12/opinion-report-access-to-the-polls/', 'snippet': 'A summary of what’s on today’s editorial page.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From the editorial page', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Opinion Report: Access to the Polls', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-12T11:57:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a33cc85e-8cfd-556e-88cb-fca3ff99efc0', 'word_count': 82, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a33cc85e-8cfd-556e-88cb-fca3ff99efc0'}, {'abstract': 'Attorney General Eric H. Holder Jr.’s statement that prosecuting big banks could harm the financial system raises a lot of questions. | Mary Jo White, the nominee to head the S.E.C., goes before the Senate Banking Committee. | Michael S. Dell gave a rare interview about his effort to buy Dell Inc. | Federal regulators accused Illinois of misleading investors about the condition of its public pension system.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/03/12/to-indict-or-not-to-indict/', 'snippet': 'Attorney General Eric H. Holder Jr.’s statement that prosecuting big banks could harm the financial system raises a lot of questions. | Mary Jo White, the nominee to head the S.E.C., goes before the Senate Banking Committee. | Michael S. Dell gave...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some banks may have become too big to prosecute, Attorney General Eric H. Holder Jr. said last week in testimony before the Senate Judiciary Committee. That comment — an acknowledgment, for the first time, that Mr. Holder has not pursued big bank prosecutions out of fear of possibly harming the financial system — raises a variety of questions, Andrew Ross Sorkin writes in the DealBook column. “Does this mean that our banks are still too big to fail? Should we prosecute corporations? Should the size of an institution or its systemic importance influence the decision of prosecutors? What’s the right policy?”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'To Indict, or Not to Indict', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-12T11:59:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/27782eb3-f46a-515d-bd80-ec22ae09e73f', 'word_count': 1883, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27782eb3-f46a-515d-bd80-ec22ae09e73f'}, {'abstract': 'This week’s grab bag of grammar, style and other missteps, compiled with help from colleagues and readers', 'web_url': 'https://afterdeadline.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/12/in-a-word-2/', 'snippet': 'This week’s grab bag of grammar, style and other missteps, compiled with help from colleagues and readers', 'lead_paragraph': 'The file is overflowing, so we’ll go straight to this week’s grab bag of grammar, style and other missteps from recent editions of The Times, compiled with help from colleagues and readers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In a Word', 'kicker': 'After Deadline', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-12T12:00:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Times Topics', 'byline': {'original':