nyt://article/1bac8cc0-b306-5089-b2f3-e76aff3734a9'}, {'abstract': 'Could the treatment of transgenders become the brightest spot in Vietnam’s bleak record on human rights?', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/12/vietnam-a-leader-on-l-g-b-t-rights-in-asia/', 'snippet': 'Could the treatment of transgenders become the brightest spot in Vietnam’s bleak record on human rights?', 'lead_paragraph': 'HO CHI MINH CITY — In the video, a transgender Vietnamese in a stringy, low-cut top entertains a crowd by balancing three fiery batons in her hands and on her head. A while later, other transgenders talk about the daily challenges of being at odds with your sex of birth, ranging from which restroom to use to bickering with the police over the gender stipulated on your official I.D.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Engendering Law', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transgender and Transsexual', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vietnam', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-12T12:36:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lien Hoang', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d3d92f6-addf-5c43-9888-caea612cbfcf', 'word_count': 777, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d3d92f6-addf-5c43-9888-caea612cbfcf'}, {'abstract': 'A recent renovation has transformed the Cliveden House, a sprawling Italianate manse overlooking the Thames, into an aristo fantasy camp.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/12/sleeping-beauty/', 'snippet': 'A recent renovation has transformed the Cliveden House, a sprawling Italianate manse overlooking the Thames, into an aristo fantasy camp.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cliveden House, a sprawling Italianate manse overlooking the Thames, was once the home of the Waldorf Astors, who entertained a varied lot, including their pro-fascist aristocratic friends — known as “the Cliveden Set” — before World War II. It was also the backdrop of the Profumo Affair, the political sex scandal that brought down Prime Minister Harold Macmillan’s government 50 years ago. A recent renovation has transformed the manor, located an hour outside of London, into an aristo fantasy camp, complete with 38 Edwardian rooms and a storybook riverside cottage that comes with its own butler, on request. Owned by the National Trust, the luxury hotel and spa overlooks 376 acres of forests and meadows. There’s a garden maze, a 19th-century parterre and a full range of anachronistic amusements — from snooker to archery to a lazy river cruise on an electric canoe that Lady Astor had built for herself in the 1920s.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sleeping Beauty', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Trust', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-12T13:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dana Thomas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thomas', 'qualifier': 