ue': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kandahar (Afghanistan)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Security Assistance Force', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Helicopters', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-12T14:27:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0e92620-e95b-56df-9057-af676e2ccee1', 'word_count': 220, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0e92620-e95b-56df-9057-af676e2ccee1'}, {'abstract': 'Anquan Boldin, who helped the Ravens beat the 49ers in the Super Bowl, was traded to San Francisco, which is in an arms race with Seattle.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/13/sports/ravens-trade-boldin-after-winning-super-bowl-leading-off.html', 'snippet': 'Anquan Boldin, who helped the Ravens beat the 49ers in the Super Bowl, was traded to San Francisco, which is in an arms race with Seattle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the N.F.L. kicks off its annual personnel swap meet, better known as the free-agency signing period, it has gotten an early jump on baring its business side to the masses. That happened in a flurry of pre-free-agency moves, most notably the one in which the Super Bowl champion shipped one of its key players (receiver Anquan Boldin) to another team (its Super Bowl opponent, no less: the San Francisco 49ers) for the football equivalent of a case of shoe polish (a sixth-round draft pick). All this was done before Ravens fans could say, “Wha. ...?”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/13/sp