5dbe-a7eb-02a3252f799c', 'word_count': 1149, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69b9674e-6da4-5dbe-a7eb-02a3252f799c'}, {'abstract': 'Guest blogger Seema Jilani writes about a Pakistani girl who, after being shot alongside Malala Yousafzai last year, is struggling under threats from the Taliban.', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/12/the-other-malala/', 'snippet': 'Guest blogger Seema Jilani writes about a Pakistani girl who, after being shot alongside Malala Yousafzai last year, is struggling under threats from the Taliban.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was one of the most ruthless attacks of our time: three Pakistani schoolgirls were on their way home when the Taliban shot them. Their crime? Pursuit of an education. Malala Yousafzai was shot in the head and two other young women sustained injuries to their arms. “We are all Malala,” roared the world. \xa0Protestors marched and lit candlelight vigils. Malala was nominated for a Nobel Peace Prize and became an iconic symbol for young women’s educational struggles.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Forgotten Malala', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-12T17:32:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Seema Jilani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Seema', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jilani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a20cd2b-7916-54b9-8aab-559d41cb43d9', 'word_count': 1056, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a20cd2b-7916-54b9-8aab-559d41cb43d9'}, {'abstract': 'Tibetan exiles in Dharamsala, Himachal Pradesh, commemorate Tibetan Women’s Uprising Day.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/12/image-of-the-day-march-12-2/', 'snippet': 'Tibetan exiles in Dharam