ives-release-carbon-emissions-tax-plan/', 'snippet': 'The proposal imposes a fee on greenhouse gas emissions from power plants, factories, refineries and other major sources.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Almost exactly four years after unveiling his doomed cap-and-trade proposal to deal with global warming, Representative Henry Waxman, Democrat of California, released a new plan on Tuesday to address climate change and federal budget woes: a tax on carbon emissions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lawmakers Release Carbon Emissions Tax Plan', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-12T18:47:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By John M. Broder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/553be47e-93ea-5760-80fd-1b8db0659be4', 'word_count': 419, 'uri': 'nyt://article/553be47e-93ea-5760-80fd-1b8db0659be4'}, {'abstract': 'A day after a judge derailed his planned restrictions, Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg forcefully defended them in an appearance at a restaurant whose owner said he was adopting the limits on his own.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/12/bloomberg-again-blasts-court-ruling-on-large-sugary-drinks/', 'snippet': 'A day after a judge derailed his planned restrictions, Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg forcefully defended them in an appearance at a restaurant whose owner said he was adopting the limits on his own.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 3:41 p.m. | A day after a judge struck down his administration’s impending limits on large sugary drinks, Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg appeared at a Manhattan cafe on Tuesday that was never