52e6766db40', 'word_count': 954, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b26e5866-6324-5805-bc4a-852e6766db40'}, {'abstract': 'Allison M. Macfarlane, the chairwoman of the Nuclear Regulatory Commission, said in a speech that nuclear safety was a moving target.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/13/science/earth/head-of-us-nuclear-watchdog-emphasizes-unknown.html', 'snippet': 'Allison M. Macfarlane, the chairwoman of the Nuclear Regulatory Commission, said in a speech that nuclear safety was a moving target.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Appealing for a shift in emphasis on nuclear safety, the new head of the Nuclear Regulatory Commission warned a gathering of more than 3,000 industry executives, experts and government regulators on Tuesday against relying too heavily on their ability to predict the future, and suggested that when it comes to commercial reactors, the industry and the government should be ready to deal with the unknown.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Head of U.S. Nuclear Watchdog Emphasizes Preparing for Unknown', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Energy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Wastes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nuclear Regulatory Commission', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Macfarlane, Allison M', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Speeches and Statements', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fukushima Daiichi Nuclear Power Plant (Japan)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-13T01:00:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d56a8b7-f886-544e-aed5-cab6d4963a46', 'word_count': 537, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d56a8b7-f886-544e-aed5-cab6d4963a46'}, {'abstract': 'The city has a chance to do something on Fulton Street that would benefit us all.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/12/a-food-market-for-new-york/', 'snippet': 'The city has a chance to do something on Fulton Street that would benefit us all.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is nothing like a grand urban food market, which can anchor a neighborhood and even a city. Think of the 120-year-old Reading Terminal Market in Philadelphia; the Ferry Building in San Francisco, which 10 years ago helped revitalize the Embarcadero; and the ever-popular Pike Place Market in Seattle. Even much-maligned Los Angeles has a permanent mid-city market, in business since 1934. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Food Market for New York', 'kicker': 'Mark Bittman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Area Planning and Renewal', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fulton Fish Market (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Amsterdam Market', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-13T01:00:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Bittman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bittman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0