ld War', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Preventing An Arctic Cold War', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARCTIC REGIONS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law of the Sea (UN Convention)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fishing, Commercial', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-13T01:02:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Arthur Berkman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': 'Arthur', 'lastname': 'Berkman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/52a791ec-f8b4-5a14-b6db-b0cc5c5df37b', 'word_count': 758, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52a791ec-f8b4-5a14-b6db-b0cc5c5df37b'}, {'abstract': 'Senator John D. Rockefeller IV proposed an overhaul and update of the E-Rate fund, which uses money collected on consumers’ phone bills to subsidize Internet connections for schools.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/13/technology/fund-that-subsidizes-internet-for-schools-should-expand-a-senator-says.html', 'snippet': 'Senator John D. Rockefeller IV proposed an overhaul and update of the E-Rate fund, which uses money collected on consumers’ phone bills to subsidize Internet connections for schools.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The $2.3 billion federal E-Rate program, which subsidizes basic Internet connections for schools and libraries, should be overhauled and expanded to provide those community institutions with new, lightning-fast connections to the Web, the chairman of a Senate committee that oversees the F.C.C. said Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/13/business/FCC-2/FCC-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/13/business/FCC-2/FCC-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/13/business/FCC-2/FCC-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/13/business/FCC-2/FCC-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 813, 'width': 1219, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/13/business/FCC-2/FCC-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/13/business/FCC-2/FCC-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/13/business/FCC-2/FCC-2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fund That Subsidizes Internet for Schools Should Expand, a Senator Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fund That Subsidizes Internet for Schools Should Expand, a Senator Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wyatt, Edward', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Communications Commission', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rockefeller, John D IV', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-13T01:02:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wyatt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wyatt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ac0d46c-3c89-5c0d-9323-c62d44515d2f', 'word_count': 808, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ac0d46c-3c89-5c0d-9323-c62d44515d2f'}, {'abstract': 'In his return to Miami, Jose Reyes homered to help the Dominican Republic overcome a 4-0 deficit and defeat Italy in the first game of the World Baseball Classic’s second round.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/13/sports/baseball/dominican-republic-rallies-to-beat-italy-in-wbc.html', 'snippet': 'In his return to Miami, Jose Reyes homered to help the Dominican Republic overcome a 4-0 deficit and defeat Italy in the first game of the World Baseball Classic’s second round.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MIAMI — Robinson Cano touched home plate, and the party started. His Dominican Republic teammates rushed out of the dugout. They mobbed him, patted his head and danced, as if their three-run seventh inning had won the game, as if this were the Little League World Series, not the second round of the World Baseball Classic. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/13/sports/WBC1/WBC1-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 432, 'wi