.nytimes.com/2013/03/13/opinion/mayor-bloombergs-anti-obesity-campaign.html', 'snippet': 'There are better ways for the mayor to use his time and resources to combat obesity in New York City than to ban giant sugary drinks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A state judge ruled Monday that Mayor Michael Bloomberg’s ban on servings of sugary drinks larger than 16 ounces was “arbitrary and capricious,” blocking the limits one day before they were to take effect. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mayor Bloomberg’s Anti-Obesity Campaign', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mayor Bloomberg’s Anti-Obesity Campaign', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Obesity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soft Drinks', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-13T01:08:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/9931f42e-eccd-5df5-8dd2-326682e0cadd', 'word_count': 333, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9931f42e-eccd-5df5-8dd2-326682e0cadd'}, {'abstract': 'Finding solutions to the epidemic of sexual violence in the armed forces is urgently needed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/13/opinion/sexual-assaults-and-military-justice.html', 'snippet': 'Finding solutions to the epidemic of sexual violence in the armed forces is urgently needed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Senate Armed Services subcommittee is scheduled to hold a hearing on sexual assaults in the military on Wednesday, the first Senate hearing on the issue in nearly a decade. There will certainly be a lot to talk about.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sexual Assaults and Military Justice', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sexual Assaults and Military Justice', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilkerson, James', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-13T01:08:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/2eea7167-7f11-592f-bf1c-616fa5e7c0e7', 'word_count': 450, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2eea7167-7f11-592f-bf1c-616fa5e7c0e7'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama is trying to charm a party that clings to calcified ideas on spending and taxes. Just look at the latest from Representative Paul Ryan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/13/opinion/the-worst-of-paul-ryans-budgets.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama is trying to charm a party that clings to calcified ideas on spending and taxes. Just look at the latest from Representative Paul Ryan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s nothing wrong with President Obama speed-dating members of Congress. Meeting face to face over food and wine, as Mr. Obama has recently done with several groups of lawmakers from both parties, may ease the demonizing politics of the last four years — along with the president’s well-earned reputation for aloofness. And given how little some Republicans know about his budget proposals — one senator confessed he had no idea what Mr. Obama wanted to cut before last week’s dinner — the shared meals were probably overdue.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Worst of the Ryan Budgets', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Worst of the Ryan Budgets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-13T01:17:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/bee1c528-bb35-5826-b5d7-5c1599959fa1', 'word_count': 509, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bee1c528-bb35-5826-b5d7-5c1599959fa1'}, {'abstract': 'As Arabs and Israelis book look inward, the chance for a New Peace emerges — not lofty declarations, but a pragmatic, gradual process that advances mutual needs and interests.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/13/opinion/the-old-peace-is-dead-but-a-new-peace-is-possible.html', 'snippet': 'As Arabs and Israelis book look inward, the chance for a New Peace emerges — not lofty declarations, but a pragmatic, gradual process that advances mutual needs and interests.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KFAR SHMARYAHU, Israel', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Old Peace Is Dead, but a New Peace Is Possible', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Is Any Hope Left for Mideast Peace?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shavit, Ari', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-13T01:17:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ari Shavit', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ari', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shavit', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/b427dabe-3868-56df-9761-d4a3637929f6', 'word_count': 898, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b427dabe-3868-56df-9761-d4a3637929f6'}, {'abstract': 'Here are a few questions the president might ask on his visit to Israel next week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/13/opinion/friedman-mr-obama-goes-to-israel.html', 'snippet': 'Here are a few questions the president might ask on his visit to Israel next week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In case you haven’t heard, President Obama leaves for Israel next week. It is possible, though, that you haven’t heard because it is hard for me to recall a less-anticipated trip to Israel by an American president. But there is a message in that empty bottle: Little is expected from this trip — not only because little is possible, but because, from a narrow U.S. point of view, little is necessary. Quietly, with nobody announcing it, the Israeli-Palestinian conflict has shifted from a necessity to a hobby for American diplomats. Like any hobby — building model airplanes or knitting sweaters — some days you work on it, some days you don’t. It depends on your mood, but it doesn’t usually matter when that sweater gets finished. Obama worked on this hobby early in his first term. He got stuck as both parties rebuffed him, and, therefore, he adopted, quite rationally in my view, an attitude of benign neglect. It was barely noticed.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mr. Obama Goes to Israel', 'kicker': 'Op-