me': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of California', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-13T01:27:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tamar Lewin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tamar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lewin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd246af8-b255-53e2-a67f-dd73bb32f633', 'word_count': 1154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd246af8-b255-53e2-a67f-dd73bb32f633'}, {'abstract': 'Sara Volz, of Colorado Springs, cultivated populations of algae under her loft bed for her winning project in the Intel Science Talent Search.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/12/science/colorado-student-receives-100000-intel-first-prize.html', 'snippet': 'Sara Volz, of Colorado Springs, cultivated populations of algae under her loft bed for her winning project in the Intel Science Talent Search.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A high school senior who cultivated populations of algae under her loft bed won first place and $100,000 in the Intel Science Talent Search on Tuesday night.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Colorado Student Receives $100,000 Intel First Prize', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Science | High School Senior’s Research Wins $100,000 Prize', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Intel Science Talent Search', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hauser, Ethan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Contests and Prizes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-13T01:30:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ethan Hauser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ethan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hauser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/41f69369-8a3c-587c-854c-2fcacda0748d', 'word_count': 371, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41f69369-8a3c-587c-854c-2fcacda0748d'}, {'abstract': 'Is a purely physical, scientific account of subjective experience possible?', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/12/mary-and-the-zombies-can-science-explain-consciousness/', 'snippet': 'Is a purely physical, scientific account of subjective experience possible?', 'lead_paragraph': 'We trust science because its claims are based on experience. But experience itself is a subjective reality that seems to elude the objectivity of scientific understanding. We know that our experiences—of seeing red, feeling pain, falling in love and so forth—depend on physical systems like the brain that science can, in principle, exhaustively explain. But it’s hard to make sense of the idea that experiences themselves could be physical. No doubt experiences correlate with objective physical facts, but, as subjective phenomena, how could they be such facts? When I feel intense pain, scientists may be able to observe brain-events that cause my pain, but they cannot observe the very pain that I feel. What science can observe is public and objective; what I feel is private and subjective.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mary and the Zombies: Can Science Explain Consciousness?', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Brain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Color', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-13T01:30:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gary Gutting', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gutting', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/45ddc078-03a8-54cf-8d3b-3d3f35d5855f', 'word_count': 1118, 'uri': 'nyt://article/45ddc078-03a8-54cf-8d3b-3d3f35d5855f'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Mirante is a principal of the Canadian commercial real estate company Avison Young and the president of its Tri-State division, which was established last year in New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/13/realestate/commercial/the-30-minute-interview-arthur-j-mirante-ii.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Mirante is a principal of the Canadian commercial real estate company Avison Young and the president of its Tri-State division, which was established last year in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mr. Mirante, 69, is a principal of the Canadian commercial real estate company Avison Young and the president of its Tri-State division, which was established last year in New York. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/13/business/Interview/Interview-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 934, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/13/business/Interview/Interview-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 934}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/13/business/Interview/Interview-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 659, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/13/business/Inter