major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-13T02:45:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/5df49197-7164-55e3-812d-c9f5413c50dd', 'word_count': 171, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5df49197-7164-55e3-812d-c9f5413c50dd'}, {'abstract': 'Venezuela will create a scientific panel to investigate the illness of Hugo Chávez, after an accusation by the interim president that the former president’s cancer was caused by his enemies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/13/world/americas/venezuela-panel-will-investigate-roots-of-cancer-that-killed-chavez.html', 'snippet': 'Venezuela will create a scientific panel to investigate the illness of Hugo Chávez, after an accusation by the interim president that the former president’s cancer was caused by his enemies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Venezuela will create a scientific panel to investigate the illness of Hugo Chávez, after an accusation by the interim president last week that the former president’s cancer was mysteriously caused by his enemies. “We have this intuition that our Commander Chávez was poisoned by dark forces that wanted to get rid of him to destroy the Bolivarian revolution and strike at Latin America and the Caribbean,” Nicolás Maduro, the interim president, said Monday night. Mr. Chávez, a charismatic leftist, died last week after 14 years in office. The government has refused to say what type of cancer Mr. Chávez had, but Mr. Maduro said that it had behaved in a very unusual way. Mr. Maduro said that the United States and other countries had developed programs in the 1940s and 1950s to experiment with intentionally causing cancer, but he added, “I’m not accusing the United States at this moment.” He did not say when the scientific panel would be created or who would be on it.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/13/world/BRIEFS/BRIEFS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 719, 'width': 470, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/13/world/BRIEFS/BRIEFS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 719, 'width': 470, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/13/world/BRIEFS/BRIEFS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/13/world/BRIEFS/BRIEFS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/13/world/BRIEFS/BRIEFS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Venezuela: Panel Will Investigate Roots of Cancer That Killed Chávez', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Venezuela: Panel Will Investigate Roots of Cancer That Killed Chávez', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Venezuela', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chavez, Hugo', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maduro, Nicolas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-13T02:50:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Neuman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Neuman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/dbabba75-6caa-5ff9-a669-c69767376f6e', 'word_count': 166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dbabba75-6caa-5ff9-a669-c69767376f6e'}, {'abstract': 'France has told fellow United Nations Security Council members it intends to introduce a resolution this month that would authorize a replacement peacekeeping force in Mali.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/13/world/africa/mali-france-will-seek-un-force-to-replace-french-led-coalition.html', 'snippet': 'France has told fellow United Nations Security Council members it intends to introduce a resolution this month that would authorize a replacement peacekeeping force in Mali.', 'lead_paragraph': ' France has told fellow United Nations Security Council members it intends to introduce a resolution this month that would authorize a peacekeeping force in Mali to replace the current contingents of African and French soldiers deployed in that country, diplomats said Tuesday. France, which has said publicly it wants to scale down its forces in Mali, plans to schedule a vote on such a resolution in April, with the goal of transferring peacekeeping responsibilities by July, the diplomats said. French forces intervened two months ago in Mali, a former French colony, to stop Islamist militants occupying the northern part of the country from expanding into the south. Since then, a combination of soldiers from France, Mali and neighboring African countries has helped drive the militants out of northern Malian cities deep into the hinterlands, but they remain a threat. The exact size of a United Nations peacekeeping force for Mali has yet to be determined, but France’s foreign minister, Laurent Fabius, was quoted by Agence France-Presse as telling lawmakers in Paris it could be as many as 10,000 soldiers.  ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mali: France Will Seek U.N. Force to Replace French-Led Coalition', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Africa', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mali: France Will Seek U.N. Force To Replace French-Led Coalition', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mali', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Security Council (UN)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fabius, Laurent', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-13T02:52:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/173a9bd0-a78e-55d4-afeb-360b2db554a4', 'word_count': 179, 'uri': 'nyt://article/173a9bd0-a78e-55d4-afeb-360b2db554a4'}, {'abstract': 'Police Commissioner Raymond W. Kelly appeared before the council to outline the Police Department’s budget, but council members seized the chance to discuss civil rights topics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/13/nyregion/kelly-questioned-on-stop-and-frisk-tactic-at-council-budget-meeting.html', 'snippet': 'Police Commissioner Raymond W. Kelly appeared before the council to outline the Police Department’s budget, but council members seized the chance to discuss civil rights topics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just before spring, Police Commissioner Raymond W. Kelly fulfills an annual ritual, appearing before the City Council to outline his department’s preliminary budget.', 'print_section': 'A', 'prin