leave the Republican Party and run as an independent for governor this year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/13/us/virginia-bolling-decides-not-to-run-for-governor.html', 'snippet': 'Lt. Gov. Bill Bolling announced Tuesday that he would not leave the Republican Party and run as an independent for governor this year.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Lt. Gov. Bill Bolling announced Tuesday that he would not leave the Republican Party and run as an independent for governor this year. “I was not confident I could raise enough money to run a winning campaign,” Mr. Bolling said in a message posted online and sent to supporters. In November, Mr. Bolling said he would not run for the Republican nomination, clearing the way for Kenneth T. Cuccinelli II, the state attorney general. He cited the state party’s nominating process, which would favor the more conservative Mr. Cuccinelli. Mr. Bolling has withheld an endorsement for either Mr. Cuccinelli or Terry McAuliffe, the Democratic Party’s leading candidate. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Virginia: Bolling Decides Not to Run for Governor', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Virginia: Bolling Decides Not To Run For Governor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Governors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wheaton, Sarah', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bolling, Bill', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuccinelli, Kenneth T II', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-13T04:15:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Wheaton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wheaton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ecb777a-b8cf-5c79-999d-a03ab77071a3', 'word_count': 107, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ecb777a-b8cf-5c79-999d-a03ab77071a3'}, {'abstract': 'State Attorney General Pam Bondi sought a court order on Tuesday to allow the exhumation of bodies thought to be buried at the Dozier School for Boys in Marianna, which closed in 2011.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/13/us/florida-exhumations-sought-at-reform-school.html', 'snippet': 'State Attorney General Pam Bondi sought a court order on Tuesday to allow the exhumation of bodies thought to be buried at the Dozier School for Boys in Marianna, which closed in 2011.', 'lead_paragraph': ' State Attorney General Pam Bondi sought a court order on Tuesday to allow the exhumation of bodies thought to be buried at the Dozier School for Boys in Marianna, which closed in 2011. The reform school was dogged by reports that the staff beat, neglected and mistreated boys for decades. Forensic anthropologists have spent the past year using radar in the Boot Hill cemetery and have found 50 possible graves. Families of some of the dead boys have asked for exhumations so they can bring their bodies home and resolve questions about their deaths. The boys died between 1900 and 1952. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Florida: Exhumations Sought at Reform School', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Florida: Exhumations Sought at Reform School', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dozier, Arthur G, School for Boys', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Alvarez, Lizette', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 