ue': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Workplace Environment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burkhart, Bryan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bonobos.com', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Thrillist.com', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Warby Parker', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ZocDoc Inc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-13T11:40:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bryan Burkhart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bryan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burkhart', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba652c97-da25-597d-aba0-3306e1a45bd3', 'word_count': 1168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba652c97-da25-597d-aba0-3306e1a45bd3'}, {'abstract': 'Mary Jo White would face significant challenges as leader of the S.E.C. | Hostess Brands struck a $410 million deal to save Twinkies and Ding Dongs. | A corporate spinoff can present a tempting opportunity to offload liabilities. | The Carlyle Group is lowering the bar for investors to participate in its private equity buyouts.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/03/13/challenges-facing-next-s-e-c-chief/', 'snippet': 'Mary Jo White would face significant challenges as leader of the S.E.C. | Hostess Brands struck a $410 million deal to save Twinkies and Ding Dongs. | A corporate spinoff can present a tempting opportunity to offload liabilities. | The Carlyle Gro...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mary Jo White got a friendly reception during testimony before the Senate Banking Committee on Tuesday, moving closer to becoming the next leader of the Securities and Exchange Commission. But even her supporters on Capitol Hill highlighted the significant challenges that would await her in that role, DealBook’s Ben Protess writes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Challenges Facing Next S.E.C. Chief', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-13T11:48:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cbb5499e-b92d-536c-9c53-247db0318853', 'word_count': 1741, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cbb5499e-b92d-536c-9c53-247db0318853'}, {'abstract': 'The antitax group is looking to set up primary challenges to Republican incumbents who it believes have compromised on conservative principles.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/13/club-for-growth-leads-conservative-charge-sometimes-at-republicans/', 'snippet': 'The antitax group is looking to set up primary challenges to Republican incumbents who it believes have compromised on conservative principles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Representative Adam Kinzinger, Republican of Illinois, would seem to be just the kind of promising politician his party needs at this stage: a telegenic, 35-year-old former Air Force pilot, close to members of the House leadership and an effective campaigner who won easily in both 2010 and 2012.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Club for Growth Leads Conservative Charge, Sometimes at Republicans', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Group Leads a Charge For Conservative Ideals', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'nam