s', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Art Direction', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Space to Mix Things Up', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-13T17:02:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooke Hodge', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooke', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hodge', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72da260a-de0f-59b3-942c-67d5dac20963', 'word_count': 300, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72da260a-de0f-59b3-942c-67d5dac20963'}, {'abstract': 'Brooks and Collins argue about Sheryl Sandberg, “The Bachelor” and the papal election.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/13/having-none-of-having-it-all/', 'snippet': 'Brooks and Collins argue about Sheryl Sandberg, “The Bachelor” and the papal election.', 'lead_paragraph': 'David Brooks:\xa0 As opinionators, this is the late winter of our discontent. The world just hasn’t thrown up that many topics to generate passionate debate. I’m not counting the new episodes of “The Bachelor.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Having None of Having It All', 'kicker': 'The Conversation', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vatican Bank', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-13T17:08:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Brooks and Gail Collins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Gail', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0fa68601-b13d-534a-8b5d-c3ba4b4721b1', 'word_count': 1322, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0fa68601-b13d-534a-8b5d-c3ba4b4721b1'}, {'abstract': 'Deportations reached a record 1.5 million people during President Obama’s first term. John Moore sought to put a face on this story, photographing deported — or soon-to-be-deported — immigrants.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/13/detained-deported-and-determined/', 'snippet': 'Deportations reached a record 1.5 million people during President Obama’s first term. John Moore sought to put a face on this story, photographing deported — or soon-to-be-deported — immigrants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Almost every day of the week in places like Mesa, Ariz., federal authorities send planes filled with deportees back to Central America. Originally arrested for anything from traffic offenses to murder, they end up patted down and shackled with 100 others who had been in this country illegally. Even more are deported by land across the Mexican border.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Detained, Deported and Determined', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Arizona Immigration Law (SB 1070)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deportation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigrants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration Detention', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moore, John', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nogales (Ariz)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-13T17:10:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Moore', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/49e7ed5e-4f02-5a42-a883-8c44d2bf5ab3', 'word_count': 471, 'uri': 'nyt://article/49e7ed5e-4f02-5a42-a883-8c44d2bf5ab3'}, {'abstract': 'The president’s meeting with House Republicans served only to reinforce the divisions that have created a cycle of deadline-driven short-term fiscal policy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/14/us/politics/obama-to-meet-with-house-gop-over-budget.html', 'snippet': 'The president’s meeting with House Republicans served only to reinforce the divisions that have created a cycle of deadline-driven short-term fiscal policy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Obama’s meeting with a restive and resistant House Republican majority on Wednesday underscored their deep divisions over fiscal policy as both sides acknowledged that an overarching budget compromise was in doubt despite a new push by the White House.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'typ