93, 'uri': 'nyt://article/400bb768-0dec-5bc3-8785-e32e6f99783c'}, {'abstract': 'Paula Champa’s new novel, “The Afterlife of Emerson Tang,” may be the first whose theme is the reunification of a vintage car with its original engine.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/13/an-automotive-love-story-reuniting-a-car-with-its-engine/', 'snippet': 'Paula Champa’s new novel, “The Afterlife of Emerson Tang,” may be the first whose theme is the reunification of a vintage car with its original engine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cars play major roles in many important novels, like F. Scott Fitzgerald’s “The Great Gatsby” and Stephen King’s “Christine.” In a novel published this week, a car and an engine take center stage.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Automotive Love Story: Reuniting a Car With Its Engine', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fitzgerald, F Scott', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, Stephen', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Houghton Mifflin Harcourt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-13T18:58:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Phil Patton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Phil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Patton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d8d342e-04f7-593e-873a-70e17dee903c', 'word_count': 410, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d8d342e-04f7-593e-873a-70e17dee903c'}, {'abstract': 'Express train service from Beijing cuts hours off of travel time to some of China’s most popular tourist sites.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/13/speeding-through-china/', 'snippet': 'Express train service from Beijing cuts hours off of travel time to some of China’s most popular tourist sites.', 'lead_paragraph': 'China recently began express train service from Beijing to Guangzhou, Xi’an and Luoyang, making it easier to visit the terra-cotta warriors, the Buddhist carvings at the Longmen Grottoes, and Hong Kong. The new rail service takes five and a half hours to Xi’an and four hours to Luoyang, which cuts travel time to each city from Beijing by more than six hours. A journey from Beijing to Hong Kong that previously took about 22 hours now takes half that on the new Beijing-Guangzhou express line. ', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Speeding Through China', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rail: Speeding Through China', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beijing (China)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guangzhou (China)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hong Kong', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-13T19:00:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tanya Mohn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tanya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mohn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/30a59964-961e-556c-8f20-0db0f8dad756', 'word_count': 86, 'uri': 'nyt://article/30a59964-961e-556c-8f20-0db0f8dad756'}, {'abstract': 'A reader responds to a recent review of “Going to Tehran.”', 'web_url': 