bStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/14/arts/20130314SXSW-slide-ASV2/20130314SXSW-slide-ASV2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/arts/20130314SXSW-slide-ASV2/20130314SXSW-slide-ASV2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Scenes From South by Southwest Music', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'South by Southwest Music and Media Conference', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-13T20:35:49+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Arts', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/1a396dfb-53e6-5ba0-83d7-e9ca572dceca', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/1a396dfb-53e6-5ba0-83d7-e9ca572dceca'}, {'abstract': 'Life on the tube, as written by London’s literati and cultural tastemakers, now in a box set.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/13/subway-reads/', 'snippet': 'Life on the tube, as written by London’s literati and cultural tastemakers, now in a box set.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The sight of subway commuters with their noses buried in books is one that transcends iPods, Angry Birds and any number of technological and cultural advances. It’s only appropriate, then, that Penguin has teamed with Transport for London to create a series of 12 books, each inspired by a different tube line, to commemorate the 150th anniversary of the London Underground. The publisher tasked a select group of straphangers — pulling from the city’s literati and cultural tastemakers — with sharing their experiences of the English capital in 15,000 words or less.', 'source': 'The New York 