n of North, Central American and Caribbean Association Football (CONCACAF)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "United States Men's National Soccer Team", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-13T20:39:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Bell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca3f2af3-f2bd-5bfe-b72a-52c6a0ebd531', 'word_count': 550, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca3f2af3-f2bd-5bfe-b72a-52c6a0ebd531'}, {'abstract': 'The child was critically injured in the fall from an eighth-floor window on Bradhurst Avenue shortly before 3:30 p.m., the authorities said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/14/nyregion/mother-dies-in-leap-from-harlem-building.html', 'snippet': 'The child was critically injured in the fall from an eighth-floor window on Bradhurst Avenue shortly before 3:30 p.m., the authorities said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A woman leapt out an eighth-floor window with her infant son in Harlem on Wednesday, killing herself and critically injuring him, the police said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '33', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mother Leaps With an Infant and Dies', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mother Leaps With an Infant and Dies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suicides and Suicide Attempts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Harlem (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-13T20:39:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman and Randy Leonard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Randy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8a36ed0-7ec3-59f6-9636-a198a0f835f2', 'word_count': 122, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8a36ed0-7ec3-59f6-9636-a198a0f835f2'}, {'abstract': 'A slide show of images from the music festival.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/13/scenes-from-south-by-southwest-music/', 'snippet': 'A slide show of images from the music festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A  slide show of images from the festival in Austin.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Scenes From South by Southwest Music', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-13T20:40:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Josh Haner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Josh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/97dd5e81-2651-5d4b-8fba-fb26177a8950', 'word_count': 11, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97dd5e81-2651-5d4b-8fba-fb26177a8950'}, {'abstract': 'The City Council in Portland, Ore., has passed a law that will enable many employees there to earn up to five paid sick days a year.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/13/portland-ore-approves-earned-sick-leave-policy/', 'snippet': 'The City Council in Portland, Ore., has passed a law that will enable many employees there to earn up to five paid sick days a year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Sheryl Sandberg’s “Lean In,” she declares the problem of women’s advancement in the workplace to be a “classic chicken-and-egg problem.” The chicken — her concern — is the impact of the choices women make that make career advancement harder. The egg is the impact of policies and society that push back, on women and all parents, as we work to both raise our families and financially support them. Without progress on both fronts, Ms. Sandberg argues, we’ll never see workplace equality.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Portland, Ore., Approves Earned Sick Leave Policy', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Family Leaves', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paid Time Off', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's Rights", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DeLauro, Rosa', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harkin, Tom', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quinn, Christine C', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Steinem, Gloria', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-13T20:42:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36cfddf3-1011-5b97-af8d-5be6cc313ee9', 'word_count': 417, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36cfddf3-1011-5b97-af8d-5be6cc313ee9'}, {'abstract': 'Bob Dylan will become an honorary member of the American Academy of Arts and Letters.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/13/bob-dylan-to-be-honored-by-american-academy-of-arts-and-letters/', 'snippet': 'Bob Dylan will become an honorary member of the American Academy of Arts and Letters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The American Academy of Arts and Letters will go electric (sort of ) in May when it welcomes Bob Dylan as an honorary member at a ceremony at its Upper Manhattan headquarters. If he shows up, Mr. Dylan — the first rock musician honored by the group — will also be serenaded in words by the novelist Michael Chabon, who was elected as a regular member last year and is scheduled to give an address titled “Rock ‘n’ Roll.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bob Dylan to Be Honored by American Academy of Arts and Letters', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chabon, Michael', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dylan, Bob', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Galgut, Damon', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Just, Ward', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tuttle, Richard', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tuymans, Luc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Winters, Terry', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN ACADEMY OF ARTS AND LETTERS', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-13T20:44:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Schuessler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': N