d from the novel about a boy who appears to have Asperger’s syndrome, has opened at the Apollo Theater in London.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/14/theater/reviews/curious-incident-of-the-dog-in-the-night-time-in-london.html', 'snippet': '“The Curious Case of the Dog in the Night-Time,” a play adapted from the novel about a boy who appears to have Asperger’s syndrome, has opened at the Apollo Theater in London.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — You need blinkers to navigate a big city, something to screen out the teeming surplus of ambient sights and sounds. Christopher Boone — the 15-year-old hero of the thrillingly staged adaptation of “The Curious Incident of the Dog in the Night-Time” at the Apollo Theater — has no such apparatus at all. And on his first day in London, it’s a lack that threatens to pulverize him.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/arts/14CURIOUS/14CURIOUS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 359, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/14/arts/14CURIOUS/14CURIOUS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 359}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/arts/14CURIOUS/14CURIOUS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 612, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/arts/14CURIOUS/14CURIOUS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1120, 'width': 1873, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/arts/14CURIOUS/14CURIOUS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/14/arts/14CURIOUS/14CURIOUS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/arts/14CURIOUS/14CURIOUS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Unnerved, Like All of Us, by Life’s Strangeness', 'kicker': 'Theater Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Unnerved, Like All of Us, by Life’s Strangeness', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stephens, Simon', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Haddon, Mark', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'APOLLO THEATER', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Treadaway, Luke', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-13T21:11:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Brantley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brantley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/50286654-6d33-5dc8-b68b-4a96fd36ba4f', 'word_count': 1035, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50286654-6d33-5dc8-b68b-4a96fd36ba4f'}, {'abstract': 'SandRidge Energy said it would expand its board by four seats, giving the new positions to TPG-Axon Capital Management. The company also said it would decide by June 30 whether to remove its chief executive, Tom L. Ward.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/03/13/sandridge-settles-fight-with-activist-investor/', 'snippet': 'SandRidge Energy said it would expand its board by four seats, giving the new positions to TPG-Axon Capital Management. The company also said it would decide by June 30 whether to remove its chief executive, Tom L. Ward.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SandRidge Energy announced on Wednesday that it had settled with a hedge fund that had been calling for the removal of the oil company’s chairman and chief executive, Tom L. Ward.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'SandRidge Settles Fight With Hedge Fund', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boards of Directors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'SandRidge Energy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TPG-Axon Capital Management LP', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-13T21:11:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/99a066b9-781c-5b88-951b-6cbd1f7a69c4', 'word_count': 260, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99a066b9-781c-5b88-951b-6cbd1f7a69c4'}, {'abstract': 'Students overhearing a one-sided conversation had more trouble solving puzzles than those within earshot of two people talking in the same room.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/13/study-adds-to-evidence-of-cellphone-distraction/', 'snippet': 'Students overhearing a one-sided conversation had more trouble solving puzzles than those within earshot of two people talking in the same room.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you have just read the same paragraph 12 times because the person sitting next to you on the bus is chatting on her cellphone, feel free to show her this: scientists have found another piece of evidence that overheard cellphone conversations are far more distracting and annoying than a dialogue between two people nearby.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/us/PHONE/PHONE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 379, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/14/us/PHONE/PHONE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 379}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/us/PHONE/PHONE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 647, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/us/PHONE/PHONE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1293, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/us/PHONE/PHONE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/14/us/PHONE/PHONE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/us/PHONE/PHONE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cellphones as a Modern Irritant', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cellphone Talkers Proved To Be Irritants, Study Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cellular Telephones', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-13T21:12:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Douglas Quenqua', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Douglas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Quenqua', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc53f8d8-1fb3-5298-aa74-08aa34b93ec0', 'word_count': 990, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc53f8d8-1fb3-5298-aa74-08aa34b93ec0'}, {'abstract': 'Members of Congress are struggling to agree on a new stopgap measure to fund the government.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/13/continuing-resolution-continuing-dysfunction/', 'snippet': 'Members of Congress are struggling to agree on a new stopgap measure to fund the government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The “continuing resolution,” now a seemingly permanent method of paying for the United States government, is also a continuing symbol of Congressional dysfunction. Lawmakers resort to C.R.’s (as they are known) when they are unable to agree on a year’s worth of new spending priorities, and so simply keep what is already in effect, along with a few tweaks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Continuing Resolution, Continuing Dysfunction', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-13T21:12:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', '