ount': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/466dd9a1-0970-5ce5-870e-1ac7932a4b19'}, {'abstract': '“Love Songs,” performed by Tim Rushton’s Danish Dance Theater as part of the Joyce Theater’s Ice Hot: A Nordic Dance Festival, has a problem: It’s lukewarm.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/14/arts/dance/love-songs-performed-by-danish-dance-theater.html', 'snippet': '“Love Songs,” performed by Tim Rushton’s Danish Dance Theater as part of the Joyce Theater’s Ice Hot: A Nordic Dance Festival, has a problem: It’s lukewarm.', 'lead_paragraph': 'During “Love Songs,” a work by the British choreographer Tim Rushton, dancers dressed in everyday clothes swoop onto the stage like beams of light and swivel into deep lunges. Off-kilter steps send bodies gliding from one side of the stage to the other. The chief partnering motif involves a woman — often, the diminutive Maxim-Jo Beck McGosh — running at full speed into the arms of a man. It’s athletic to the point of being clinical. Never once does your heart get caught in your throat. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/arts/danishdance/danishdance-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 774, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/14/arts/danishdance/danishdance-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 774}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/arts/danishdance/danishdance-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 795, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/arts/danishdance/danishdance-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1589, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/arts/danishdance/danishdance-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/14/arts/danishdance/danishdance-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/arts/danishdance/danishdance-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Racing Leap Into Rhythms and Romance', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Racing Leap Into Rhythms And Romance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Danish Dance Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-13T21:21:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/a9163b0e-f6e2-5fa1-b66f-16b20e0d61b4', 'word_count': 464, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a9163b0e-f6e2-5fa1-b66f-16b20e0d61b4'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama named Melissa Rogers to replace a clergyman in an office that has long grappled with First Amendment issues.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/13/obama-appoints-church-state-law-expert-to-head-faith-based-office/', 'snippet': 'President Obama named Melissa Rogers to replace a clergyman in an office that has long grappled with First Amendment issues.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the world watched the Vatican for an announcement of a new leader for the Roman Catholic faithful, the White House quietly made a leadership appointment of its own on Wednesday, to the office responsible for outreach to religious organizations: Melissa Rogers will be the new director of the Office of Faith-Based and Neighborhood Partnerships. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Appoints Church-State Law Expert to Head Faith-Based Office', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Director Is Chosen For Faith-Based Agency', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Faith-Based Initiatives', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion-State Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rogers, Melissa', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'White House Office of Faith-Based and Neighborhood Partnerships', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-13T21:24:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Wheaton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wheaton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/862b2110-8a20-5347-9dec-62c099705b5b', 'word_count': 559, 'uri': 'nyt://article/862b2110-8a20-5347-9dec-62c099705b5b'}, {'abstract': 'Readers respond to the announcement that Cardinal Jorge Mario Bergoglio, the archbishop of Buenos Aires, is the new pope.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/14/opinion/the-day-the-world-met-pope-francis-i.html', 'snippet': 'Readers respond to the announcement that Cardinal Jorge Mario Bergoglio, the archbishop of Buenos Aires, is the new pope.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Day the World Met Pope Francis', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Day the World Met Pope Francis', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Francis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-13T21:25:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1b90bb5-0045-5ace-875c-43c270b468fe', 'word_count': 477, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1b90bb5-0045-5ace-875c-43c270b468fe'}, {'abstract': 'A contained Vladimir Jurowski led the London Philharmonic Orchestra in two concerts at Avery Fisher Hall.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/14/arts/music/london-philharmonic-at-avery-fisher-hall.html', 'snippet': 'A contained Vladimir Jurowski led the London Philharmonic Orchestra in two concerts at Avery Fisher Hall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In England, Vladimir Jurowski, the 40-year-old principal conductor of the London Philharmonic Orchestra, is revered in equal measure for the fierce elegance of his conducting and the meticulously thought-out programs he puts together. At Royal Festival Hall in London last December he paired Mahler’s Fifth Symphony with “Quatre Chants Pour Franchir le Seuil,” an apocalyptic song cycle by Gérard Grisey; in November he contextualized Beethoven’s emancipatory Fifth with Holocaust-darkened works by Schoenberg and Nono.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit':