imes.com/2013/03/13/after-a-divorce-creeping-around-happiness/', 'snippet': 'After a divorce, a mother looks for an honest conversation about what really makes us happy — and it’s hard to find.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lately I’ve become a “creeper.” I didn’t even know what this word meant until about a month ago, when my ninth-grade students enlightened me. We had just started reading “Lord of the Flies,” and on our first day of discussion, one student raised her hand. “What are all these creepers all over the place?” she asked. Other students chimed in with echoes of confusion. She continued: “I mean, like, I thought there weren’t any other people on this island? I don’t get it.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After a Divorce, Creeping Around Happiness', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Divorce, Separations and Annulments', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emotions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Happiness', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-13T21:46:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Lawton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lawton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5e4c238-392f-56e3-9536-5b5718d08264', 'word_count': 741, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5e4c238-392f-56e3-9536-5b5718d08264'}, {'abstract': 'The lawsuit filed on Wednesday in Delaware state court.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interact