e': 'persons', 'value': 'Larsen, Elizabeth Foy', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-13T22:08:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Great Homes & Destinations', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Kurutz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kurutz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/04d555c7-f1e4-5803-99ad-26d13dc874c3', 'word_count': 710, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04d555c7-f1e4-5803-99ad-26d13dc874c3'}, {'abstract': 'Using a kind of brinkmanship that has become commonplace in contract negotiations of symphony orchestras, the musicians of the San Francisco Symphony went on strike on Wednesday, a week before a scheduled appearance at Carnegie Hall.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/13/san-francisco-symphony-musicians-go-on-strike/', 'snippet': 'Using a kind of brinkmanship that has become commonplace in contract negotiations of symphony orchestras, the musicians of the San Francisco Symphony went on strike on Wednesday, a week before a scheduled appearance at Carnegie Hall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Using a kind of brinkmanship that has become commonplace in contract negotiations of symphony orchestras, the musicians of the San Francisco Symphony went on strike on Wednesday, a week before a scheduled appearance at Carnegie Hall. The orchestra announced the cancellation of a concert at its home auditorium, Louise M. Davies Symphony Hall, that was scheduled for Thursday afternoon. The musicians’ contract expired in November but was extended to February when, by mutual agreement, the musicians continued talking and playing. On Wednesday the union rejected the administration’s latest proposal for a three-year contract that, according to the administration, “would have kept the musicians among the three highest-paid orchestras in the country” (the others being the Chicago Symphony and the Los Angeles Philharmonic). The current average salary of the musicians is $165,000, the administration said. In addition to higher salaries, the musicians are seeking increases in benefits and pension contributions. A spokesman for the players could not immediately be reached. The administration said it had already notified the players that it would present a revised proposal on Thursday. It plans to go ahead with the presentation, it said, in hopes that San Francisco concerts can resume on Friday and an East Coast tour can proceed.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'San Francisco Symphony Musicians Go on Strike', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'San Francisco Symphony Musicians Go on Strike', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Strikes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Francisco Symphony', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-13T22:09:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James R. Oestreich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Oestreich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/64e6be81-5331-560f-a6ee-5eac7356f8cb', 'word_count': 204, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64e6be81-5331-560f-a6ee-5eac7356f8cb'}, {'abstract': 'When baseball retired Jackie Robinson’s No. 42 in 1997, the 13 major leaguers with No. 42 were allowed to keep wearing it. Mariano Rivera will be the last.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/14/sports/baseball/mariano-rivera-carries-banner-for-final-42s-and-for-jackie-robinson.html', 'snippet': 'When baseball retired Jackie Robinson’s No. 42 in 1997, the 13 major leaguers with No. 42 were allowed to keep wearing it. Mariano Rivera will be the last.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mariano Rivera’s decision to retire after the 2013 season represents the end of an era for several reasons. The major leagues’ career leader in saves, he has been a cornerstone of the Yankees since winning his first championship ring with them, in 1996, and given his remarkable consistency and distinct lack of histrionics, he will be difficult, if not impossible, to replace.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/sports/baseball/14mariano-1/14mariano-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 379, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/14/sports/baseball/14mariano-1/14mariano-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 379}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/sports/baseball/14mariano-1/14mariano-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 646, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/sports/baseball/14mariano-1/14mariano-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1293, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/sports/baseball/14mariano-1/14mariano-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/14/sports/baseball/14mariano-1/14mariano-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/sports/baseball/14mariano-1/14mariano-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rivera Is Taking Robinson’s 42 to Its Last Stop', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rivera Is Taking Robinson’s 42 To Its Last Stop', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rivera, Mariano', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Robinson, Jackie', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-13T22:13:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b5f684b-261d-52a1-a00c-978b837ee3a6', 'word_count': 630, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b5f684b-261d-52a1-a00c-978b837ee3a6'}, {'abstract': 'Notes on an unexpected pontiff.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/13/pope-francis-i/', 'snippet': 'Notes on an unexpected pontiff.', 'lead_paragraph': 'So the oddsmakers were wrong, and we have an Argentine Jesuit as pope. This is one of those moments when humility is the better part of punditry: Despite having been the runner-up to Joseph Ratzinger in the last papal conclave, Cardinal Jorge Mario Bergoglio was no more on my radar screen over the last two weeks than he was on (almost) anyone else’s, and it would be folly for me to pretend to know what his elevation portends. His age would suggest a kind of caretaker pope, but his name (evoking not only Francis of Assisi but the great Jesuit Francis Xavier as well) suggests a mix of humility and purifying zeal; his rich biography, meanwhile, offers enough material for multiple narratives, multiple hopes, and (of course) multiple lines of attack from the church’s many critics.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pope Francis I', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Francis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-13T22:13:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d923d037-70ab-5eb1-99cf-08715fb4bda2', 'word_count': 477, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d923d037-70ab-5eb1-99cf-08715fb4bda2'}, {'abstract': 'A Brooklyn designer’s latest creation is a twist on an old watering can.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/14/garden/a-creative-turn-for-watering.html', 'snippet': 'A Brooklyn designer’s latest creation is a twist on an old watering can.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Paul Loebach, a Brooklyn-based industrial designer, has produced furniture, accessories, lighting and even wallpaper, but says that his latest creation, the X3 watering can for Kontextür, beats them all. Like much of Mr. Loebach’s work, the can, which won the award for product-design excellence at the Accent on Design show in January, celebrates a vintage industrial aesthetic while looking new. It gets its name from a trick in its construction: a single metal tube is bent three times to create the handle and spout, then soldered onto the body. The X3 will be available in late April in solid copper ($99.95) and in white-, green-, blue- or red-painted steel ($49.95). Information: (614) 818-1446 or wabnitzeditions.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/garden/14GOODS/14CURR5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/14/garden/14GOODS/14CURR5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/garden/14GOODS/14CURR5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/garden/14GOODS/14CURR5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/garden/14GOODS/14CURR5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/14/garden/14GOODS/14CURR5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/garden/14GOODS/14CURR5-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Creative Turn for Watering', 'kicker': 'Currents | Goods', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Creative Turn for Watering', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Loebach, Paul', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hirst, Arlene', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gardens and Gardening', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kontextur', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-13T22:15:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Arlene Hirst', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Arlene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hirst', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0695e10-c897-5e4d-8aab-39e7735294f5', 'word_count': 115, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0695e10-c897-5e4d-8aab-39e7735294f5'}, {'abstract': 'Uruguay’s market has slowed, primarily because of concerns about the economy in neighboring Argentina.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/14/greathomesanddestinations/real-estate-in-uruguay.html', 'snippet': 'Uruguay’s market has slowed, primarily because of concerns about the economy in neighboring Argentina.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A CONTEMPORARY WITH FOUR BEDROOMS AND OCEAN VIEWS IN EL CHORRO, URUGUAY', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/13/greathomesanddestinations/13-GH-IHH-SPAN/13-GH-IHH-SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/13/greathomesanddestinations/13-GH-IHH-SPAN/13-GH-IHH-SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/13/greathomesanddestinations/13-GH-IHH-SPAN/13-GH-IHH-SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': No