pet': 'An obscure tax strategy is the latest technique that private equity firms are using to extract money from their companies well after completing an initial public offering.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the Berry Plastics Group, a container and packaging company, went public last October, it generated up to $350 million in tax savings. But the company won’t collect the bulk of the benefits. Rather, Berry Plastics will hand over 85 percent of the savings, in cash, to its former private equity owners.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Squeezing Out Cash Long After the I.P.O.', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Private Equity Squeezes Out Cash Long After Its Exit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corporate Taxes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Equity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Berry Plastics Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-13T22:26:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynnley Browning', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynnley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Browning', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9228e0cc-e9bd-5331-8af7-97e0e68634cb', 'word_count': 847, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9228e0cc-e9bd-5331-8af7-97e0e68634cb'}, {'abstract': 'Las Supper, which blends hip-hop and soul, tried out some songs from its first album, “Back to the Future,” at the Blue Note.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/14/arts/music/las-supper-and-big-daddy-kane-at-the-blue-note.html', 'snippet': 'Las Supper, which blends hip-hop and soul, tried out some songs from its first album, “Back to the Future,” at the Blue Note.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last September, at the inaugural concert at the Barclays Center in Brooklyn, Jay-Z brought out just one guest, Big Daddy Kane. It was the student offering the spotlight to the teacher: a show of respect, of civic pride (like Jay-Z, Big Daddy Kane is from Brooklyn) and a compliment. It was also an opportunity, one that Big Daddy Kane took advantage of, showing in just a few minutes why he was worthy of the gesture, and the stage.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/arts/SUPPER/SUPPER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 362, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/14/arts/SUPPER/SUPPER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 362}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/arts/SUPPER/SUPPER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 618, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/arts/SUPPER/SUPPER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1237, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/arts/SUPPER/SUPPER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/14/arts/SUPPER/SUPPER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/arts/SUPPER/SUPPER-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'cr