assing sensible gun-control measures is so difficult.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Americans puzzled by the growing gap between popular support for gun controls and Washington lawmakers’ obeisance to the gun lobby should know about the Congressional Sportsmen’s Foundation. It is a private charity that enjoys considerable tax-deductible support from the firearms industry and has very close ties to more than 250 members of the Senate and the House of Representatives, those who make up the separate Congressional Sportsmen’s Caucus. A good part of its clout comes from Washington dinners, gala “shootouts” and junkets with lawmakers. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Pro-Gun Charity’s Capitol Influence', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Pro-Gun Charity’s Capitol Influence', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Congressional Sportsmen's Foundation", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lobbying and Lobbyists', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-14T01:06:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/61e58444-fc88-522f-b9b1-60dfe8203213', 'word_count': 271, 'uri': 'nyt://article/61e58444-fc88-522f-b9b1-60dfe8203213'}, {'abstract': 'In order to replace the dismal and inadequate Pennsylvania Station, the massive sports arena should not be given a new lease. It should move.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/14/opinion/madison-square-gardens-overreach.html', 'snippet': 'In order to replace the dismal and inadequate Pennsylvania Station, the massive sports arena should not be given a new lease. It should move.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For decades now, New Yorkers have yearned for a grand entranceway to New York City to replace the dismal and inadequate Pennsylvania Station. One major obstacle has always been Madison Square Garden, the massive sports arena that is perched on top of the station and whose presence makes almost any rational redesign of the waiting rooms and tracks below virtually impossible. Architects, designers and a few visionary politicians have been trying to persuade the Garden’s owners to move so that reconstruction can begin. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Madison Square Garden’s Overreach', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Madison Square Garden’s Overreach', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Madison Square Garden', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pennsylvania Station (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stadiums and Arenas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-14T01:06:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/48f7ea43-fecf-54cf-9a2d-25d32ed7f6a0', 'word_count': 364, 'uri': 'nyt://article/48f7ea43-fecf-54cf-9a2d-25d32ed7f6a0'}, {'abstract': 'Kenya’s decision to elect a president charged with crimes against humanity poses a challenge for the West.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/14/opinion/kenyas-awkward-choice-for-president.html', 'snippet': 'Kenya’s decision to elect a president charged with crimes against humanity poses a challenge for the West.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kenya’s apparent decision to elect a president charged by the International Criminal Court at The Hague for crimes against humanity is deeply unsettling. But if Uhuru Kenyatta withstands an expected legal challenge by his opponent Raila Odinga, the United States and Europe are going to have to find a way to work with the new government, given Kenya’s standing as a vital security ally and a regional economic power.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Awkward Choice in Kenya', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Awkward Choice in Kenya', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kenya', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kenyatta, Uhuru Muigai', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Odinga, Raila', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-14T01:10:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/4bcc4aec-aa7e-50d1-a3e0-e10f771960c6', 'word_count': 443, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4bcc4aec-aa7e-50d1-a3e0-e10f771960c6'}, {'abstract': 'You know, that conclave process works so well in selecting new popes, I wonder if it could help out our fearless lawmakers on Capitol Hill.', 'web_url': 'https://ww