 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/49cedd62-26d6-5168-a065-66c7cf19cca5', 'word_count': 1094, 'uri': 'nyt://article/49cedd62-26d6-5168-a065-66c7cf19cca5'}, {'abstract': 'Citizens are stepping forward in favor of comprehensive legislation that would include a quick and direct path to citizenship for 11 million people living in the country illegally.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/14/us/politics/us-citizens-join-illegal-immigrants-in-pressing-lawmakers-for-change.html', 'snippet': 'Citizens are stepping forward in favor of comprehensive legislation that would include a quick and direct path to citizenship for 11 million people living in the country illegally.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — On her trip to Washington to push for an overhaul of immigration laws, Cindy Garcia on Wednesday went straight to the office of Senator Marco Rubio, Republican of Florida, to tell him about how the looming deportation of her husband had affected her family. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/us/IMMIG-1/IMMIG-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 372, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/14/us/IMMIG-1/IMMIG-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 372}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/us/IMMIG-1/IMMIG-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 636, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/us/IMMIG-1/IMMIG-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1271, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/us/IMMIG-1/IMMIG-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/14/us/IMMIG-1/IMMIG-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/us/IMMIG-1/IMMIG-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Citizens Join Illegal Immigrants in Pressing Lawmakers for Change', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Citizens Join Illegal Immigrants In Pressing Lawmakers for Change', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Preston, Julia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigrants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Citizenship and Naturalization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-14T03:05:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5ee1aa6-e1eb-5044-b36b-c19f979e9698', 'word_count': 1083, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5ee1aa6-e1eb-5044-b36b-c19f979e9698'}, {'abstract': 'People in the crowds filling St. Peter’s Square gave their first impressions of Pope Francis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/14/world/europe/pope-francis-bowing-to-crowds-wins-hearts.html', 'snippet': 'People in the crowds filling St. Peter’s Square gave their first impressions of Pope Francis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'They filled St. Peter’s Square on Wednesday night, thousands of people who endured steady rain and cold temperatures, awaiting the naming of the new pope of the Roman Catholic Church. When Pope Francis was introduced, the people responded to history in the making: the first pope from Latin America and the first non-European pope in centuries. Out in the crowds, people sang, shouted the name of the new pope and spoke about the significance of the moment. GAIA PIANIGIANI', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pope Francis, Bowing to Crowds, Wins Hearts', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Bow From a Balcony Captures Many Hearts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Francis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-14T03:07:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gaia Pianigiani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gaia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pianigiani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/861c1526-7bc1-5058-8ede-220844d357a5', 'word_count': 642, 'uri': 'nyt://article/861c1526-7bc1-5058-8ede-220844d357a5'}, {'abstract': 'Three ways of defining poverty suggest three different approaches to relief.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/13/who-is-poor/', 'snippet': 'Three ways of defining poverty suggest three different approaches to relief.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are three ways of defining poverty\xa0in America: the official\xa0Census\xa0Bureau\xa0method,\xa0which\xa0uses\xa0a set of income thresholds\xa0that vary by family size and composition;\xa0an experimental income-based method\xa0called the\xa0Supplemental Poverty Measure\xa0that\xa0factors in\xa0government programs designed to help people with low incomes; and a consumption-based method\xa0that\xa0measures\xa0what households actually spend.By defining\xa0poverty\xa0according to different criteria, these three methods\xa0capture\xa0surprisingly different populations of men, women and children. In a perfect world, these three methods would all tell us to do the same thing to alleviate poverty, but it’s not like that. Each method\xa0suggests a different approach toward how our government should direct its poverty-fighting resources.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Is Poor?', 'kicker': 'Thomas B. Edsall', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poverty', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Welfare (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Edin, Kathryn', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Munnell, Alicia H', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brookings Institution', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Center for Economic and Policy Research', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Opinion Research Center', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-14T03:12:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas B. Edsall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c39de12-ff2c-5236-b278-20ac16fc5142', 'word_count': 2338, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c39de12-ff2c-5236-b278-20ac16fc5142'}, {'abstract': 'Pontiac, Mich., once a healthy blue-collar city, has been guided by emergency managers for the last four years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/14/us/lessons-for-detroit-in-pontiacs-years-of-emergency-oversight.html', 'snippet': 'Pontiac, Mich., once a healthy blue-collar city, has been guided by emergency managers for the last four years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PONTIAC, Mich. — The mayor here has no decision-making power. The City Council still holds meetings every Thursday night, though no official business can be conducted. Afterward, the council members are locked out of City Hall until morning, escorted from the building by a janitor.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/us/jp-PONTIAC-1/jp-PONTIAC-1-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/14/us/jp-PONTIAC-1/jp-PONTIAC-1-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/us/jp-PONTIAC-1/jp-PONTIAC-1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/us/jp-PONTIAC-1/jp-PONTIAC-1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/us/jp-PONTIAC-1/jp-PONTIAC-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/14/us/jp-PONTIAC-1/jp-PONTIAC-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/us/jp-PONTIAC-1/jp-PONTIAC-1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lessons for Detroit in a City’s Takeover', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lessons for Detroit in a City’s Takeover', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yaccino, Steven', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pontiac (Mich)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Detroit (Mich)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schimmel, Louis H', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-14T03:16:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Yaccino', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yaccino', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a86c7de-3a9c-5c93-9952-e274ce974879', 'word_count': 1237, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a86c7de-3a9c-5c93-9952-e274ce974879'}, {'abstract': 'A report on the international travel industry has ranked Egypt the least safe of 140 tourist destinations, evidence of the toll that unrest has taken on the country’s tourist industry.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/14/world/middleeast/egypt-last-place-on-tourism-list.html', 'snippet': 'A report on the international travel industry has ranked Egypt the least safe of 140 tourist destinations, evidence of the toll that unrest has taken on the country’s tourist industry.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A report on the international travel industry has ranked Egypt the least safe and secure of 140 tourist destinations, putting it behind Pakistan, Yemen and Chad, evidence of the toll that two years of near-constant unrest has taken on the country’s once-lucrative tourist industry. Tourism — which has accounted for 11 percent of Egypt’s gross domestic product, economists say — has suffered more than any other industry from the street protests and political turmoil that have prevailed since the ouster of President Hosni Mubarak two years ago. The report, released by the nonprofit World Economic Forum and publicized around the world, is unlikely to help. A Tourism Ministry official said the results were not a surprise, given the turmoil and the survey’s methodology, which relied heavily on a survey of executives as well as statistics like traffic accidents. Both government and industry officials say, however, that there are signs of recovery, although mainly because of bargain-hunting Red Sea beachgoers, rather than the more profitable Sphinx-and-Pyramids circuit. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egypt: Last Place on Tourism List', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Egypt: Last Place on Tourism List', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kirkpatrick, David D', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mubarak, Hosni', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Economic Forum', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-14T03:21:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By David D. Kirkpatrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e6a1e75-bedb-5d0f-85a5-cc4ed7534e50', 'word_count': 166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e6a1e75-bedb-5d0f-85a5-cc4ed7534e50'}, {'abstract': 'Iranian oil shipments to foreign customers increased in February, a report said Wednesday, despite a new regimen of American sanctions over Iran’s disputed nuclear program.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/14/world/middleeast/iran-oil-exports-rose-report-says.html', 'snippet': 'Iranian oil shipments to foreign customers increased in February, a report said Wednesday, despite a new regimen of American sanctions over Iran’s disputed nuclear program.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Iranian oil shipments to foreign customers increased in February, a widely followed monthly report said Wednesday, despite a new regimen of American sanctions over Iran’s disputed nuclear program intended to further limit the country’s ability to sell petroleum, its most important export. The monthly report, by the International Energy Agency, a 28-nation group of oil-importing nations, said Iran’s exports rose to 1.28 million barrels a day, from 1.13 million barrels a day in January, suggesting that the impact of the new sanctions was either negligible or had not yet begun to be felt. Under an American sanctions law provision that took effect on Feb. 6, any country that buys Iranian oil must put the purchase money into a local bank account. Iran cannot repatriate the money and can only use it to buy goods within that country. Violators of the provision risk severe penalties in doing business with the United States. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iran: Oil Exports Rose, Report Says', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iran: Oil Exports Rose, Report Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Energy Agency', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-14T03:25:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/cbef6de5-914d-5f55-b7d8-f75eb5c77307', 'word_count': 151, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cbef6de5-914d-5f55-b7d8-f75eb5c77307'}, {'abstract': 'The monarch population has declined with extreme weather and a lack of the milkweed that the butterflies feed on, experts say.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/14/science/earth/monarch-migration-plunges-to-lowest-level-in-decades.html', 'snippet': 'The monarch population has declined with extreme weather and a lack of the milkweed that the butterflies feed on, experts say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The number of monarch butterflies that completed an annual migration to their winter home in a Mexican forest sank this year to its lowest level in at least two decades, due mostly to extreme weather and changed farming practices in North America, the Mexican government and a conservation alliance reported on Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/us/MONARCH/MONARCH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 704, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/14/us/MONARCH/MONARCH-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 704}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/us/MONARCH/MONARCH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 873, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/us/MONARCH/MONARCH-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1284, 'width': 1094, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/us/MONARCH/MONARCH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/14/us/MONARCH/MONARCH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/us/MONARCH/MONARCH-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Monarch Migration Plunges to Lowest Level in Decades', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': No