photo of the most interesting one you’ve seen. It could be yours. It could be your neighbor’s. (We won’t scold you for coveting.) If you send us the picture by March 22, your work could be featured in the magazine. (The last time around, we asked to see your rooftops. We will also run a larger selection of images online.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/13/magazine/13lawn-photos/13lawn-photos-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 379, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/13/magazine/13lawn-photos/13lawn-photos-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 379}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/13/magazine/13lawn-photos/13lawn-photos-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 648, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/13/magazine/13lawn-photos/13lawn-photos-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1295, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/13/magazine/13lawn-photos/13lawn-photos-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/13/magazine/13lawn-photos/13lawn-photos-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/13/magazine/13lawn-photos/13lawn-photos-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Full Frontal: Send Us Photos of Front-Yard Finery', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-14T14:17:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Staff', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Staff'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ecd2cd28-8b21-577a-815c-54060df91b51', 'word_count': 91, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ecd2cd28-8b21-577a-815c-54060df91b51'}, {'abstract': 'Wes Welker’s departure comes as little surprise to anyone who has watched the Patriots treat players like disposable napkins through the Bill Belichick era.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/14/leading-off-the-patriot-highway/', 'snippet': 'Wes Welker’s departure comes as little surprise to anyone who has watched the Patriots treat players like disposable napkins through the Bill Belichick era.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You do have to hand it to the Patriots. Because if there is going to be trend of heartlessly cutting the players your fans have grown attached to, well, the Patriots are going to be out in front of that. The most productive receiver in football wanted to come back for a reasonable salary? Gone. What, Tom Brady isn’t happy either? The all-world quarterback who just restructured his contract, essentially returning armored trucks full of money to his team so it could sign guys like Welker, his football soul mate? Pffffttt.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/15/sports/football/15leadingpic/15leadingpic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/15/sports/football/15leadingpic/15leadingpic-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image',