r Mix Diskerud is hoping to get off to a strong start with Rosenborg when Norway’s Tippeligaen season opens this weekend.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/14/diskerud-stays-in-norway-but-still-has-u-s-on-his-mind/', 'snippet': 'U.S. national team midfielder Mix Diskerud is hoping to get off to a strong start with Rosenborg when Norway’s Tippeligaen season opens this weekend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the 2013 Tippeligaen season opens this weekend in Norway, midfielder Mix Diskerud will be looking to help bring Rosenborg BK back to the elite level of European soccer. But he will also be looking to attract the attention of the United States national team coaching staff.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Diskerud Stays in Norway but Still Has U.S. on His Mind', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-14T15:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Sciaretta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sciaretta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fab19dd2-49c3-5186-a581-b1a64e5796e1', 'word_count': 833, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fab19dd2-49c3-5186-a581-b1a64e5796e1'}, {'abstract': 'In her memoir, the daughter of the irascible New York City cook Kenny Shopsin chronicles a year filled with drama yet also strange moments of grace.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/14/the-wander-years/', 'snippet': 'In her memoir, the daughter of the irascible New York City cook Kenny Shopsin chronicles a year filled with drama yet also strange moments of grace.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The irascible New York City cook Kenny Shopsin never met a curse word he didn’t love, and the tirades from his cramped restaurants are the stuff of legend. His daughter Tamara, a graphic designer and sometime chef in the family kitchens, has inherited his fondness for the profane but she’s also a romantic, and she shows these twin sides in her memoir, “Mumbai New York Scranton.” Through terse prose and charming illustrations, Tamara chronicles a year filled with drama yet also strange moments of grace, taking her from the rickshaw-clogged Indian city of Kochi to a hospital bed in New York to her unlikely second home in the Rust Belt: “I’m not sure what the people of Scranton do for a living. I know there is a ring-pop factory.” Scribner, $25.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Wander Years', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shopsin, Kenny', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-14T15:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ethan Hauser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ethan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hauser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b53e445-6748-56ad-8d1c-7f0a203249e9', 'word_count': 131, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b53e445-6748-56ad-8d1c-7f0a203249e9'}, {'abstract': '“Spectacle: the Music Video,” celebrating the short films made for the music of artists like Devo, Madonna, Peter Gabriel, Beastie Boys and Bjork, will come to the Museum of the Moving Image on April 3.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/14/i-want-my-music-videos-the-art-form-gets-its-own-museum-exhibition/', 'snippet': '“Spectacle: the Music Video,” celebrating the short films made for the music of artists like Devo, Madonna, Peter Gabriel, Beastie Boys and Bjork, will come to the Museum of the Moving Image on April 3.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Long before party-goers at New Jersey beaches and dudes who shock themselves with Taser guns were deemed worthy of their own television series, there was the music video: an art form so prolific and diverse that there were whole television channels that ran almost nothing but these short musical films, nearly 24 hours a day.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'I Want My Music Videos: The Art Form Gets Its Own Museum Exhibition', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bjork', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cash, Johnny', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gabriel, Peter', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARCADE FIRE', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Beastie Boys', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Devo', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MTV Networks', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Museum of the Moving Image', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Radiohead', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Astoria (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}], 'p