_paragraph': 'On April 15, 2013, we will deprecate our New York State Legislature API. We’re doing this for several reasons, but what influenced our decision most is that there is a better source for this information: the Open States Project, run by the Sunlight Foundation. The Open States Project has an excellent API and also offers bulk downloads of legislative data for many states, including New York. If you’re interested in state legislative data, you can contribute.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Deprecating the New York State Legislature API', 'kicker': 'Open', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-14T16:12:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Derek Willis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Derek', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Willis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/438582d5-ab08-50d8-b734-8702b3f97dd4', 'word_count': 209, 'uri': 'nyt://article/438582d5-ab08-50d8-b734-8702b3f97dd4'}, {'abstract': 'Both sides in the Civil War used ciphers and other forms of cryptography to send messages.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/14/the-codes-of-war/', 'snippet': 'Both sides in the Civil War used ciphers and other forms of cryptography to send messages.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Years ago, when I was working on my master’s degree in history at Louisiana Tech University, an acquaintance allowed me to use the Civil War diary of Joseph W. Ely as the basis for my thesis. Ely, a corporal in the 19th Michigan Infantry, was captured at Thompson’s Station, Tenn., and spent time in the infamous Libby Prison before being exchanged. He had his left ring finger shot off in the Atlanta Campaign and survived the March to the Sea and the Carolinas Campaign to return home and live well into the 20th century.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Codes of War', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cryptography, Codes and Ciphers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage and Intelligence Services', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-14T16:15:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Terry L. Jones', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Terry', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Jones', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6b8e8fd-6c52-5b5c-9001-22e52d3cf5e7', 'word_count': 2835, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6b8e8fd-6c52-5b5c-9001-22e52d3cf5e7'}, {'abstract': 'The model steps out in a mod striped turtleneck and skirt.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/14/look-of-the-moment-karolina-kurkova-2/', 'snippet': 'The model steps out in a mod striped turtleneck and skirt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Look: Opposites Attract. A mod striped turtleneck balances out a flouncy mini. Booties with contrasting colored heels add a subdued edge.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Look of the Moment | Karolina Kurkova', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-14T16:23:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reporte