the appeal of evangelicalism there?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/roomfordebate/2013/03/14/does-pope-franciss-election-signal-a-catholic-comeback-for-latin-america/', 'snippet': 'Now under the first pope from Latin America, what can the Catholic Church do to compete with the appeal of evangelicalism there?', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Catholic Comeback for Latin America?', 'kicker': 'Room for Debate', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-14T16:42:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e7a182a-b639-5d47-95b7-fd8cb3eec1a8', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e7a182a-b639-5d47-95b7-fd8cb3eec1a8'}, {'abstract': 'Punk lives at South by Southwest: across generations, genders, wardrobes and skill sets.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/14/sxsw-music-punks-not-dead/', 'snippet': 'Punk lives at South by Southwest: across generations, genders, wardrobes and skill sets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Punk lives at South by Southwest: across generations, genders, wardrobes and skill sets. As Dr. Seuss never wrote, you can do it in a suit, you can do it in a dress, you can play it quite precisely, you can play it like a mess. Much of my Wednesday at SXSW was a blast of punk old and new, a testament both to indie-rock’s archival pride and to the enduring alchemy of frustration and loud guitars.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/15/arts/music/15CAVE/15CAVE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/15/arts/music/15CAVE/15CAVE-articleLarge