stname': 'Berenstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 4}, {'firstname': 'Alyssa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 5}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/8c1cd447-0778-5f26-b906-a70bc2b56c3a', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/8c1cd447-0778-5f26-b906-a70bc2b56c3a'}, {'abstract': 'Tim Duncan’s statistics per 36 minutes underscore his remarkable consistency over the years, and win shares highlight Tony Parker and Manu Ginobili’s value to the Spurs.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/14/keeping-score-winning-is-just-another-constant-for-the-spurs/', 'snippet': 'Tim Duncan’s statistics per 36 minutes underscore his remarkable consistency over the years, and win shares highlight Tony Parker and Manu Ginobili’s value to the Spurs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The San Antonio Spurs will enter Thursday night’s matchup against the Dallas Mavericks one win short of 50 victories for the season. This is nothing new for the Spurs, who have won 50 or more games for the past 13 seasons, the longest such streak in N.B.A. history.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Keeping Score: Winning Is Just Another Constant for the Spurs', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duncan, Tim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ginobili, Manu', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Parker, Tony', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Antonio Spurs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-14T16:58:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Justin Kubatko', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Justin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kubatko', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a47eb4e-63fb-5c9e-b46a-c6ec5b10bd81', 'word_count': 574, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a47eb4e-63fb-5c9e-b46a-c6ec5b10bd81'}, {'abstract': 'Lots of small-business owners are maintaining more expensive financing arrangements then they need.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/14/are-you-sticking-with-expensive-financing-too-long/', 'snippet': 'Lots of small-business owners are maintaining more expensive financing arrangements then they need.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I am currently involved in two loan transactions where the small-business owner stands to save substantial money by changing lenders. In both instances, these are relatively young companies that have been working with expensive private money lenders and factors, and their companies have grown to the point where they can now work with the asset-based lending departments at Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation-insured banks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Are You Sticking With Expensive Financing Too Long?', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Deposit Insurance Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Small Business Administration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-14T17:00:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ami Kassar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ami', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kassar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba23d2d7-d790-5b03-afd4-9711244ed610', 'word_count': 474, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba23d2d7-d790-5b03-afd4-9711244ed610'}, {'abstract': 'Judy Battista, the N.F.L. reporter for The Times, will answer questions from readers.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/14/have-n-f-l-questions-judy-battista-has-answers-13/', 'snippet': 'Judy Battista, the N.F.L. reporter for The Times, will answer questions from readers.', 'lead_paragraph': '5:04 p.m. | Updated Anquan Boldin to the 49ers? Wes Welker to the Broncos? Darrelle Revis to…where, exactly? Judy Battista, the N.F.L. reporter for The Times, will answer questions from readers. Put your questions in the comments field and answers will appear on The Fifth Down next week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Have N.F.L. Questions? Judy Battista Has Answers', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boldin, Anquan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Revis, Darrelle', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Welker, Wes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Denver Broncos', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Francisco 49ers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-14T17:06:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c22a36ff-06aa-52a7-aa40-dd0270448327', 'word_count': 54, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c22a36ff-06aa-52a7-aa40-dd0270448327'}, {'abstract': 'Performers will bring a range of styles from two continents to the “Vocal Electrofolk: Africa to New York” concert.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/15/nyregion/vocal-electrofolk-africa-to-new-york-in-soho.html', 'snippet': 'Performers will bring a range of styles from two continents to the “Vocal Electrofolk: Africa to New York” concert.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We live increasingly, so the Miser is assured, in a remix culture, an age when new digital media and the Internet have conspired to collapse time and space. But doesn’t it seem as if most of this mashing up were done by machines, issued as recordings, and consumed in private? It’s a rare privilege to encounter performers musically skilled and culturally sympathetic enough to synthesize a global range of styles and periods before a live audience in real time and in an intimate space. “Vocal Electrofolk: Africa to New York,” a concert on Saturday night at the radio station WQXR’s Jerome L. Greene Space in the South Village, could be such an occasion. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/15/arts/15MISER/15MISER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 393, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/15/arts/15MISER/15MISER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 393}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/15/arts/15MISER/15MISER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 671, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/15/arts/15MISER/15MISER-superJumbo.jpg', 'heigh