gazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/14/six-things-sagmeister-walsh/', 'snippet': 'Can we make ourselves happier? A New York-based designer explores the question in his show at the Jewish Museum.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the past 10 years, the Austrian-born, New York-based designer Stefan Sagmeister has explored an appealing subject: happiness. Is it possible, he asks, to train our minds the same way we train our bodies? Can we make ourselves happier? His latest findings, the product of a collaboration with his recently acquired partner, Jessica Walsh, are presented in “Six Things: Sagmeister & Walsh,” an exhibition that opens tomorrow at the Jewish Museum and runs through Aug. 4.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Six Things: Sagmeister & Walsh’', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sagmeister, Stefan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jewish Museum (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-14T17:15:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anna Carnick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carnick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d2aec19-6dfa-5034-bcae-470ff1f55a53', 'word_count': 274, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d2aec19-6dfa-5034-bcae-470ff1f55a53'}, {'abstract': 'Instead of mourning the Big East, consider that it might be a better conference without the football schools.', 'web_url': 'https://thequad.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/14/a-new-big-east-is-a-better-big-east/', 'snippet': 'Instead of mourning the