 that some dinosaurs and related reptiles long ago seemed to be marvelous four-winged creatures, seemingly on standby at some runway for takeoff in flight as early birds.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Some Primitive Birds Flew With 4 Wings, Study Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Some Primitive Birds Flew With 4 Wings, Study Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilford, John Noble', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paleontology', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fossils', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Science (Journal)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-14T18:01:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Noble Wilford', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'Noble', 'lastname': 'Wilford', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d057f19a-76be-5d8b-abb2-1b98a3766f59', 'word_count': 709, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d057f19a-76be-5d8b-abb2-1b98a3766f59'}, {'abstract': 'Not since Benghazi has the G.O.P. seemed this intent on second-guessing the Obama administration.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/14/white-house-tour-outrage/', 'snippet': 'Not since Benghazi has the G.O.P. seemed this intent on second-guessing the Obama administration.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Not since Benghazi — no, not since Fast and Furious has the G.O.P. seemed this intent on second-guessing the Obama administration. I refer, of course, to the matter of White House public tours.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'White House Tour Outrage', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gohmert, Louis B Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stewart, Chris', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-14T18:06:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Juliet Lapidos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Juliet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lapidos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f17917b0-6c10-5cde-8c66-d5169ccb057b', 'word_count': 400, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f17917b0-6c10-5cde-8c66-d5169ccb057b'}, {'abstract': 'Haruhiko Kuroda, a Finance Ministry veteran and lover of Greek philosophy, has been charged with turning around an institution reviled for its monetary policy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/15/business/global/kuroda-a-critic-of-japans-central-bank-takes-on-task-of-redirecting-it.html', 'snippet': 'Haruhiko Kuroda, a Finance Ministry veteran and lover of Greek philosophy, has been charged with turning around an institution reviled for its monetary policy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOKYO — In the late 1990s, in the thick of the Asian financial crisis, a top Japanese Finance Ministry official turned to his protégé and found him engrossed not in policy documents, but in a chunky volume of the works of Aristotle.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/15/business/KURODA/KURODA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/15/business/KURODA/KU