: 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-14T19:52:28+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/e83d8981-1b67-5be5-9d38-30643fc74fe6', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/e83d8981-1b67-5be5-9d38-30643fc74fe6'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from Darwin Deez, Emicida and the English singer and songwriter Charli XCX.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/14/a-few-stray-sxsw-thoughts/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from Darwin Deez, Emicida and the English singer and songwriter Charli XCX.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The best lost-love song with advanced-physics puns has to be “Redshift” by Darwin Deez, whose mission as a songwriter seems to involve merging the guitar-scrubbing light funk of the 1970’s with the musicianly twists–gnarled harmonies, leaping and twisting melodies–of Frank Zappa. “You loved all of my little quarks, so what went wrong?/Don’t superstring me along,” he lamented in a semblance of an R&B ballad. “Wave or particle, I can’t be both.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Few Stray SXSW Thoughts', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'South by Southwest Music and Media Conference', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-14T19:52:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/436fb4fe-0f1d-56dd-a8fc-4d881285e793', 'word_count': 336, 'uri': 'nyt://article/436fb4fe-0f1d-56dd-a8fc-4d881285e793'}, {'abstract': 'Living aboard a 100-foot boat, exploring a mostly uninhabited region spread out over 250 miles in the Andaman Sea.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/17/travel/setting-sail-among-myanmars-islands-of-mystery-explorer.html', 'snippet': 'Living aboard a 100-foot boat, exploring a mostly uninhabited region spread out over 250 miles in the Andaman Sea.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I arrived on a chaotic pier in the border town of Ranong, Thailand, feeling as if I was about to throw up as I watched three-story fishing boats chug by. I had persuaded my two younger brothers and eight girlfriends to fly across the world and pool a large chunk of money so we could charter a live-aboard boat. The plan was to sail for six days through the Mergui Archipelago, a chain of 800 islands off Myanmar’s coast that’s become the holy grail of sublime, empty beaches. ', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/17/travel/17EXPLORER1_SPAN/17EXPLORER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/17/travel/17EXPLORER1_SPAN/17EXPLORER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 500}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/17/travel/17EXPLORER1_SPAN/17EXPLORER1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 854, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/17/travel/17EXPLORER1_SPAN/17EXPLORER1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1707, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013