serious — analysis about the future of the Roman Catholic Church, and about what it would mean for the church’s profile in the Americas. But in other corners of the Internet, there were also some less serious discussions, too.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Vatican, the New Boss Is a Soccer Fan', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-14T20:23:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Das', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Das', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1fc5bdaa-e780-59ac-bcfa-f881223ca030', 'word_count': 459, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1fc5bdaa-e780-59ac-bcfa-f881223ca030'}, {'abstract': '“Spring Breakers” delves into a deeply American topic: the pursuit of happiness taken to nihilistic extremes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/15/movies/spring-breakers-directed-by-harmony-korine.html', 'snippet': '“Spring Breakers” delves into a deeply American topic: the pursuit of happiness taken to nihilistic extremes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just before the candy-colored apocalypse comes to Harmony Korine’s “Spring Breakers” you hear the peaceable murmurings of a beach, of lapping water, calling gulls and playing children. They’re nice, these sounds of summer, promises of carefree, youthful pursuits like building sand castles and shrieking at waves. The first image of what looks like a beach party keeps the happy vibe going. Dozens, hundreds of gyrating, dancing young women and men are basking in the honeyed light — as the beat goes on and the smiles sour into sneers — though it becomes evident that they’re also marinating in a tsunami of beer.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Debauchery and the American Experience (Woo-Hoo!)', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Debauchery and the American Experience (Woo-Hoo!)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Korine, Harmony', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gomez, Selena', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Franco, James', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hudgens, Vanessa Anne', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Spring Breakers (Movie)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Korine, Rachel', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Benson, Ashley', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-14T20:31:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/478a714f-39c6-5424-876c-3974a885f0af', 'word_count': 1401, 'uri': 'nyt://article/478a714f-39c6-5424-876c-3974a885f0af'}, {'abstract': 'The New York Philharmonic presented Bach’s Mass in B minor with New York Choral Artists on Wednesday, part of the Bach Variations festival.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/15/arts/music/new-york-philharmonic-at-avery-fisher-hall.html', 'snippet': 'The New York Philharmonic presented Bach’s Mass in B minor with New York Choral Artists on Wednesday, part of the Bach Variations festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a video introducing the New York Philharmonic’s monthlong Bach Variations festival, Alan Gilbert, the orchestra’s music director, describes himself as not at all a Bach specialist. That is exactly why it was a fresh idea for Mr. Gilbert to oversee this initiative. The major offering came on Wednesday night, when he conducted the first of four performances of Bach’s Mass in B minor at Avery Fisher Hall. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/15/arts/JPPHIL1/JPPHIL1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/15/arts/JPPHIL1/JPPHIL1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/15/arts/JPPHIL1/JPPHIL1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/15/arts/JPPHIL1/JPPHIL1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1472, 'width': 1962, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/15/arts/JPPHIL1/JPPHIL1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/15/arts/JPPHIL1/JPPHIL1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/15/arts/JPPHIL1/JPPHIL1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Celebrating Voices as Instruments', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'c