e tried to find a slur for white Americans as evocative and offensive as the N-word is for African-Americans. And, frankly, there aren’t many classics to choose from. Honky, whitey, cracker, hillbilly: they all fall flat. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Theater Talkback: How to Offend a White Person', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-14T21:19:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Greg Kalleres', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Greg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kalleres', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c09a2967-1261-5ddf-9b27-3537f12b999a', 'word_count': 846, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c09a2967-1261-5ddf-9b27-3537f12b999a'}, {'abstract': 'The characters in Jamie Quatro’s collection of short stories, “I Want to Show You More,” are preoccupied with five things: sex, running, God, illness and infidelity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/15/books/i-want-to-show-you-more-by-jamie-quatro.html', 'snippet': 'The characters in Jamie Quatro’s collection of short stories, “I Want to Show You More,” are preoccupied with five things: sex, running, God, illness and infidelity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The woman on the (terrible) dust jacket of Jamie Quatro’s first book, a collection of stories called “I Want to Show You More,” is wearing a dress made out of tin foil, as if she wanted to be baked like a sweet potato — or wants to protect her heart from electromagnetic fields or meddling influence of any sort.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimed