ideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/b195b7fb-fa5a-5d4d-b032-3da8e39ee0be', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/b195b7fb-fa5a-5d4d-b032-3da8e39ee0be'}, {'abstract': '“The Hugo Boss Prize 2012: Danh Vo I M U U R 2” at the Guggenheim Museum is a homage to an artist’s ambiguous cultural explorations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/15/arts/design/the-hugo-boss-prize-2012-danh-vo-works-at-the-guggenheim.html', 'snippet': '“The Hugo Boss Prize 2012: Danh Vo I M U U R 2” at the Guggenheim Museum is a homage to an artist’s ambiguous cultural explorations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The exhibition as cornucopia — as an overwhelming array of found objects selected and arranged by an artist — has become something of a trend. You could call it the return of the repressed: a way for stringent conceptually motivated sensibilities to re-engage with materials and objects.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/15/arts/15DANHVO2_SPAN/15DANHVO2_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 358, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/15/arts/15DANHVO2_SPAN/15DANHVO2_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 358}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/15/arts/15DANHVO2_SPAN/15DANHVO2_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 610, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/15/arts/15DANHVO2_SPAN/15DANHVO2_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1220, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/15/arts/15DANHVO2_SPAN/1