right.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/15/arts/music/mets-hd-broadcasts-success-but-at-what-cost.html', 'snippet': 'The Metropolitan Opera’s chief, Peter Gelb, is softening his assessment of the house’s HD broadcasts as cannibalizing ticket sales. But there are reasons to think he was right.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Peter Gelb, the general manager of the Metropolitan Opera, now says that it was not the most fortunate choice of words when he recently attributed a decline in attendance at the house to the “cannibalization” of the audience by the company’s high-definition broadcasts. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/15/arts/15SUBJPMETOPERA/15SUBJPMETOPERA-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/15/arts/15SUBJPMETOPERA/15SUBJPMETOPERA-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/15/arts/15SUBJPMETOPERA/15SUBJPMETOPERA-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/15/arts/15SUBJPMETOPERA/15SUBJPMETOPERA-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/15/arts/15SUBJPMETOPERA/15SUBJPMETOPERA-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/15/arts/15SUBJPMETOPERA/15SUBJPMETOPERA-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/15/arts/15SUBJPMETOPERA/15SUBJPMETOPERA-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Success in HD, but at What Cost?', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Success in HD, But at What Cost?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tommasini, Anthony', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gelb, Peter', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-14T21:47:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Tommasini', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tommasini', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8673d5a6-f789-51fc-aa3b-d4f5ce5abeb8', 'word_count': 1038, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8673d5a6-f789-51fc-aa3b-d4f5ce5abeb8'}, {'abstract': 'In “Ginger & Rosa,” a coming-of-age story directed by Sally Potter, the close friendship of two teenagers comes undone with an act of treachery.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/15/movies/ginger-rosa-starring-elle-fanning-and-alice-englert.html', 'snippet': 'In “Ginger & Rosa,” a coming-of-age story directed by Sally Potter, the close friendship of two teenagers comes undone with an act of treachery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ginger and Rosa are best friends. Vanguard baby boomers born in adjacent London hospital beds in 1945, they are teenagers in 1962, when most of Sally Potter’s ardent and intelligent film about the girls takes place. The air around them is charged with anxiety — about the threat of nuclear war, mostly — intellectual restlessness and sexual curiosity. Perhaps it always is that way for 17-year-olds, but every generation acts out its own particular pageant of rage, revolt and disillusionment.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ticking Bomb in Their Friendship', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ticking Bomb in Their Friendship', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fanning, Elle', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Potter, Sally', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Englert, Alice', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nivola, Alessandro', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hendricks, Christina', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'May, Jodhi', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-14T21:48:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/84c15f73-248c-5df5-8d5a-1c34f08ab9f8', 'word_count': 783, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84c15f73-248c-5df5-8d5a-1c34f08ab9f8'}, {'abstract': 'Matthew Keys, a 26-year-old social media editor, was charged with assisting the hacking collective Anonymous in an attack on The Los Angeles Times Web site.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/14/thomson-reuters-editor-indicted-on-charges-of-aiding-hackers-group/', 'snippet': 'Matthew Keys, a 26-year-old social media editor, was charged with assisting the hacking collective Anonymous in an attack on The Los Angeles Times Web site.', 'lead_paragraph': '8:30 p.m. | Updated Matthew Keys, a 26-year-old deputy social media editor at Thomson Reuters, has been charged with assisting the hacking collective Anonymous in an attack on the Web site of The Los Angeles Times, the Justice Department said Thursday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Thomson Reuters Editor Is Charged in Hacking of News Site', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Media Editor Is Charged In Hacking of News Site', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberattacks and Hackers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Times', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Thomson Reuters Corporation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tribune Co', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-14T21:51:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Chozick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chozick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b9884dd-e69f-56c8-a3df-917f29892768', 'word_count': 679, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b9884dd-e69f-56c8-a3df-917f29892768'}, {'abstract': 'The Foo Fighters frontman made an impassioned plea in his 45-minute keynote address.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/14/sxsw-music-dave-grohl-urges-musicians-to-discover-your-voice/', 'snippet': 'The Foo Fighters frontman made an impassioned plea in his 45-minute keynote address.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AUSTIN, Tex. — Recounting his rise from obscure punk rocker to mainstream rock star, Dave Grohl gave a impassioned defense of the importance of artistic freedom and a do-it-yourself ethic in keeping popular music vibrant, as he delivered the keynote address at the South by Southwest Music Festival on Thursday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/arts/14artsbeat-grohl/14artsbeat-grohl-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 403, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/14/arts/14artsbeat-grohl/14artsbeat-grohl-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 403}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/arts/14artsbeat-grohl/14artsbeat-grohl-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 688, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/arts/14artsbeat-grohl/14artsbeat-grohl-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1377, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/arts/14artsbeat-grohl/14artsbeat-grohl-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/14/arts/14artsbeat-grohl/14artsbeat-grohl-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'capt