le/cb7b1679-db62-5e57-8dac-700205536394'}, {'abstract': 'In “The Incredible Burt Wonderstone,” Steve Carell is a successful Las Vegas magician who faces a challenge from a take-no-prisoners newcomer played by Jim Carrey.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/15/movies/the-incredible-burt-wonderstone-with-steve-carrell.html', 'snippet': 'In “The Incredible Burt Wonderstone,” Steve Carell is a successful Las Vegas magician who faces a challenge from a take-no-prisoners newcomer played by Jim Carrey.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Is that Steve Carell or Will Ferrell? While watching “The Incredible Burt Wonderstone” you may be forgiven for confusing the two, since Mr. Carell’s title character, a vainglorious Las Vegas magician, is drawn straight from the Will Ferrell playbook. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sleepwalking Magician Pulls a New Self Out of a Hat', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sleepwalking Magician Pulls a New Self Out of a Hat', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carell, Steve', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Buscemi, Steve', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carrey, Jim', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ARKIN, ALAN', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilde, Olivia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gandolfini, James', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Incredible Burt Wonderstone (Movie)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-14T21:57:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ef8d296-f65c-5248-ac77-42f7333084a9', 'word_count': 614, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ef8d296-f65c-5248-ac77-42f7333084a9'}, {'abstract': '“If I Were You” is the story of a boozy middle-aged marketing executive who impulsively bonds with her husband’s girlfriend.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/15/movies/if-i-were-you-directed-by-joan-carr-wiggin.html', 'snippet': '“If I Were You” is the story of a boozy middle-aged marketing executive who impulsively bonds with her husband’s girlfriend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Buried in the bloat of Joan Carr-Wiggin’s interminable “If I Were You” are the seeds of what might have been a lean, snappy farce about duplicitous, adulterous games. The story of Madelyn (Marcia Gay Harden), a boozy middle-aged marketing executive who impulsively bonds with her husband’s girlfriend, has its goofy moments but lacks focus, precision and structure. The pace is sluggish and the humor spotty. Just when you think it might settle into a comfortable rhythm, it throws in unnecessary characters and takes a mystifying tangent. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/15/arts/IFIWERE1_SPAN/IFIWERE1_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 488, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/15/arts/IFIWERE1_SPAN/IFIWERE1_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 488}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/15/arts/IFIWERE1_SPAN/IFIWERE1_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 833, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image',