hurch.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2013/03/14/world/europe/pope-francis-reader-reactions.html', 'snippet': 'After Pope Francis was introduced in Vatican City, The Times asked readers to describe how they thought his papacy would affect the future of the Catholic Church.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After Pope Francis was introduced in Vatican City, The Times asked readers to describe how they thought his papacy would affect the future of the Catholic Church.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Readers Consider the Selection of a New Pope', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-14T23:10:16+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'World', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/5e39ecea-0448-529d-9254-e8d248cb2fdf', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/5e39ecea-0448-529d-9254-e8d248cb2fdf'}, {'abstract': 'The 1892 Sullivan Street Industrial School awaits a new mission.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/17/realestate/victorian-gothic-lifeline-for-children-of-the-street.html', 'snippet': 'The 1892 Sullivan Street Industrial School awaits a new mission.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the 1880s and 1890s the Children’s Aid Society built a dozen distinctive Victorian Gothic lodging houses and vocational schools, advancing its mission of rescuing young people from the evils of 19th-century New York. All were on the same model, red-brick Victorians with towers and gables, and six remain. ', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/17/realestate/17STREETS2_SPAN/17STREETS2_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height':