nged to spread more money to impoverished areas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Andrew Cuomo and state legislative leaders are hammering out the $142 billion state budget for the 2013-14 fiscal year, which must be approved by April 1. It is crucial that more financing be allocated to public schools, both in upstate areas and in New York City. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York’s Education Deficit', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New York’s Education Deficit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-15T01:06:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/bbd11452-bb55-5962-8945-f441bd39082c', 'word_count': 397, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bbd11452-bb55-5962-8945-f441bd39082c'}, {'abstract': 'With no definitive results from a messy election, Italy can’t push through the kind of radical changes it needs to grow its economy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/15/opinion/italy-in-search-of-a-government.html', 'snippet': 'With no definitive results from a messy election, Italy can’t push through the kind of radical changes it needs to grow its economy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Italy’s newly elected Parliament convenes on Friday with no clear governing majority. Only a government with a strong popular mandate can push through the kind of radical changes Italy really needs: sweeping labor market and tax reforms, tough anticorruption laws, electoral reform and a new fiscal bargain with euro-zone partners that replaces austerity with growth. All or most of that will now have to wait until new elections, probably later this year, can produce more definitive results. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Italy, in Search of a Government', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Italy, in Search of a Government', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grillo, Beppe', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-15T01:06:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/bec8f1c2-bb4d-5dd8-ad38-153a0f76bd3c', 'word_count': 368, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bec8f1c2-bb4d-5dd8-ad38-153a0f76bd3c'}, {'abstract': 'In Kenya, a rising middle class, educated but struggling, finds its hopes for reform repeatedly dashed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/15/opinion/why-kenyan-democracy-is-a-fragile-proposition.html', 'snippet': 'In Kenya, a rising middle class, educated but struggling, finds its hopes for reform repeatedly dashed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NAIROBI, Kenya', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Crushing of the Safari Ants', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor