every generation does better than the previous generation. This is no longer the case. This generation might have less.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day for Friday, Mar. 15, 2013', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-15T01:40:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/7356c440-620e-53a9-9c0b-bdcc3a2699a9', 'word_count': 40, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7356c440-620e-53a9-9c0b-bdcc3a2699a9'}, {'abstract': 'San Lorenzo de Almagro, an Argentine soccer team with holy beginnings, now has a supporter at the Vatican in Pope Francis I.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/15/world/americas/pope-francis-fan-of-saints-on-soccer-field-and-off.html', 'snippet': 'San Lorenzo de Almagro, an Argentine soccer team with holy beginnings, now has a supporter at the Vatican in Pope Francis I.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BUENOS AIRES — San Lorenzo de Almagro, a top-division soccer club here, has holy beginnings. It was created in 1908 by Lorenzo Massa, a priest. One of the team’s nicknames is Los Santos (the Saints), and the team’s colors, blue and red, are said to correspond to the colors of the Virgin Mary’s robe. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/15/world/jplorenzo/jplorenzo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 516, 'width': 569, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/15/world/jplorenzo/jplorenzo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 516, 'wid