e residents of Buenos Aires described an archbishop who had worked hard to change the lives of the poor, but others said he had done too little to challenge the country’s former dictatorship.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/15/world/americas/argentines-divide-over-selection-of-pope-francis.html', 'snippet': 'Some residents of Buenos Aires described an archbishop who had worked hard to change the lives of the poor, but others said he had done too little to challenge the country’s former dictatorship.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BUENOS AIRES — Pope Francis was celebrated here on Thursday by faithful congregants and priests in some of this capital city’s vast slums as he started his papacy on an austere note, shunning the throne reserved for him at the Vatican, but the praise was tempered by criticism of him for his hard-line conservative views on a range of issues, including gay rights and artistic expression. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Back Home a Pontiff Is Honored, if Not by All', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Back Home A Pontiff Is Honored, If Not by All', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARGENTINA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romero, Simon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Francis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-15T02:13:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Simon Romero', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Simon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Romero', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dda47a57-570f-50ab-927f