rom the United States and its allies shutting down the North’s Web sites, the country’s main tool of spreading propaganda abroad.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'North Korea Sees South and U.S. Behind Cyberstrikes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'North Korea Sees South and U.S. Behind Hacks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberattacks and Hackers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Propaganda', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-15T09:53:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Choe Sang-Hun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Choe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sang-Hun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b583c8b1-5911-5802-b4b9-5d799d02eba0', 'word_count': 620, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b583c8b1-5911-5802-b4b9-5d799d02eba0'}, {'abstract': 'Older veterans often are slow to recognize post-traumatic stress syndrome, even as it haunts many of them.', 'web_url': 'https://newoldage.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/15/no-end-to-trauma-for-some-older-veterans/', 'snippet': 'Older veterans often are slow to recognize post-traumatic stress syndrome, even as it haunts many of them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Who knew much about post-traumatic stress syndrome in 1945? The term didn’t enter the official manual of psychiatric diagnoses until 1980; effective treatments d