, 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Delhi (India)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-15T11:55:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hari Kumar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hari', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kumar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5feaa988-d292-5276-b618-ac633df8f5a0', 'word_count': 461, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5feaa988-d292-5276-b618-ac633df8f5a0'}, {'abstract': 'Congressional investigators on Thursday released a harsh portrait of the events surrounding JPMorgan Chase’s huge trading loss. | The Fed said Goldman Sachs and JPMorgan Chase were not strong enough to go ahead with plans to pay out billions of dollars to shareholders. | Bill Clinton may have spilled the beans about a new job for Marc Lasry of Avenue Capital. | Timothy F. Geithner is preparing to tell his side of what happened during the financial crisis and the recession.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/03/15/jpmorgan-faulted-over-trading-loss/', 'snippet': 'Congressional investigators on Thursday released a harsh portrait of the events surrounding JPMorgan Chase’s huge trading loss. | The Fed said Goldman Sachs and JPMorgan Chase were not strong enough to go ahead with plans to pay out billions of do...', 'lead_paragraph': 'JPMORGAN FAULTED OVER TRADING LOSS \xa0|\xa0 Congressional investigators on Thursday released a harsh portrait of the events surrounding JPMorgan Chase’s huge trading loss last year, saying the bank ignored internal risk controls while its chief executive, Jamie Dimon, briefly withheld some information from regulators. The 300-page report is sure to escalate the debate over policing Wall Street, and it may foreshadow a criminal case against employees at the center of the trading disaster, Jessica Silver-Greenberg and Ben Protess report in DealBook. Current and former JPMorgan executives, including Ina Drew, who led the office that oversaw the trades, are scheduled to testify at a hearing starting at 9:30 a.m., which DealBook will be live-blogging.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'JPMorgan Faulted Over Trading Loss', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-15T11:55:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2673762-7964-5aa6-a1e0-ce24b5d6e1e0', 'word_count': 1703, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2673762-7964-5aa6-a1e0-ce24b5d6e1e0'}, {'abstract': 'An owner petition prompts a Honda recall, why sore knees accompany middle age, younger generations lag in wealth building and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/15/friday-reading-owner-petition-prompts-honda-recall/', 'snippet': 'An owner petition prompts a Honda recall, why sore knees accompany middle age, younger generations lag in wealth building and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Friday Reading: Owner Petition Prompts Honda Recall', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-15T12:06:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original'