/03/17/arts/music/jerusalem-quartet-to-play-shostakovich-at-alice-tully-hall.html', 'snippet': 'The Jerusalem Quartet will perform the full cycle of Shostakovich’s 15 string quartets in a series presented by the Chamber Music Society of Lincoln Center.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like a man writing his own obituary Dmitri Shostakovich composed his String Quartet No. 8 as a requiem for himself, weaving it together with an autobiographical motif consisting of the letters D-S-C-H.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/17/arts/17INTO1_SPAN/17INTO1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/17/arts/17INTO1_SPAN/17INTO1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/17/arts/17INTO1_SPAN/17INTO1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/17/arts/17INTO1_SPAN/17INTO1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/17/arts/17INTO1_SPAN/17INTO1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/17/arts/17INTO1_SPAN/17INTO1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/17/arts/17INTO1_SPAN/17INTO1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'It’s Your Own Funeral, Shostakovich', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'It’s Your Own Funeral, Shostakovich', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schweitzer, Vivien', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shostakovich, Dmitri', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jerusalem Quartet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kam, Ori', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chamber Music Society of Lincoln Center', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-15T14:33:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivien Schweitzer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schweitzer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1d6bc1d-ebb4-5b36-823c-ba7a9fed2354', 'word_count': 930, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1d6bc1d-ebb4-5b36-823c-ba7a9fed2354'}, {'abstract': 'The ballet dancer Gemma Bond will unveil her work “Silent Titles,” which she choreographed, at Florence Gould Hall.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/17/arts/dance/gemma-bond-choreographs-ballet.html', 'snippet': 'The ballet dancer Gemma Bond will unveil her work “Silent Titles,” which she choreographed, at Florence Gould Hall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Gemma Bond was 14 and training at the Royal Ballet School in London she entered a choreographic competition. “It seems really silly now,” she said with the sort of half-embarrassed laughter that frequently trickles into her speech. “But I thought: ‘Well, I should have a go. Everyone else is trying.’\xa0” Her ballet, she added, wasn’t experimental in the least. “I just wanted it to be pretty.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/17/arts/17BOND2_SPAN/17BOND2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/17/arts/17BOND2_SPAN/17BOND2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/17/arts/17BOND2_SPAN/17BOND2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/17/arts/17BOND2_SPAN/17BOND2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/17/arts/17BOND2_SPAN/17BOND2_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/17/arts/17BOND2_SPAN/17BOND2_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/17/arts/17BOND2_SPAN/17BOND2_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Ballerina Makes Her Own Moves', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Ballerina Makes Her Own Moves', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN BALLET THEATER', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-15T14:34:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dbeba9bb-fbea-5186-b511-aeed7b783651', 'word_count': 1119, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dbeba9bb-fbea-5186-b511-aeed7b783651'}, {'abstract': 'Adam Leon explains how he came to make “Gimme the Loot,” a movie about two graffiti writers from the Bronx who want to tag the Mets’ home-run apple.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/17/movies/adam-leon-on-gimme-the-loot-and-learning-graffiti.html', 'snippet': 'Adam Leon explains how he came to make “Gimme the Loot,” a movie about two graffiti writers from the Bronx who want to tag the Mets’ home-run apple.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the past five years Adam Leon has gone from working for film festivals to being honored by them. After a stint on the payroll of the New York Film Festival he eventually took his love for film behind the camera, writing and directing a feature debut that got festival audiences buzzing and distributors calling. That movie is “Gimme the Loot,” about two young graffiti writers from the Bronx whose quest to tag the New York Mets home-run apple takes them on a lively adventure throughout New York City. It includes encounters with drug dealers, a little petty theft and walking shoeless through the city streets.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/17/arts/17SNAPSHOT/17SNAPSHOT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 859, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'cro