[{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed6455bc-b841-5aa5-8841-6e4f49304bf1', 'word_count': 619, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed6455bc-b841-5aa5-8841-6e4f49304bf1'}, {'abstract': 'A prominent Republican’s turnaround on gay marriage prompts questions.', 'web_url': 'https://bruni.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/15/portmans-progress/', 'snippet': 'A prominent Republican’s turnaround on gay marriage prompts questions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I suppose it’s a measure of how far the fight for gay equality has come that within minutes of Senator Rob Portman’s announcement that he now supports same-sex marriage, because he learned that his own son is gay, my inbox began filling with messages not of celebration, but of complaint. Readers, colleagues and friends wrote that they were pleased with his destination, but offended by the route there.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Portman’s Progress', 'kicker': 'Frank Bruni', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Portman, Rob', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-15T15:27:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Frank Bruni', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Frank', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bruni', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/17a2f6bf-7f7e-5e51-b410-93b19ba1