ype': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By James B. Stewart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1307d683-7f9e-51e2-9ed4-287ba92b398a', 'word_count': 1843, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1307d683-7f9e-51e2-9ed4-287ba92b398a'}, {'abstract': 'For his show in the Netherlands, American sculptor Keith Edmier chose to focus on an apt subject: tulip mania.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/15/now-showing-keith-edmier/', 'snippet': 'For his show in the Netherlands, American sculptor Keith Edmier chose to focus on an apt subject: tulip mania.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The American sculptor Keith Edmier got his start in Hollywood, so it’s not entirely surprising that his work is influenced by pop culture. Over the years he’s worked with at least a couple of recognizable actresses, using an adolescent, prefame Lena Dunham as the model for a cast of his childhood crush in 1997 and collaborating with the actress and artist Farrah Fawcett. The result is a body of autobiographical work that is relatable to different generations.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Now Showing | Keith Edmier', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Edmier, Keith', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Netherlands', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-15T17:17:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erika Allen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erika', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Allen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/603dd8fe-c983-506d-9a7b-b55e6d822b69', 'word_count': 466, 'uri': 'nyt://article/603dd8fe-c983-506d-9a7b-b55e6d822b69'}, {'abstract': 'Ennio Morricone, who has worked on four Quentin Tarantino films, told film students in Rome that he would never collaborate with the director again, saying he “places music in his films without coherence.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/15/django-composer-takes-aim-at-tarantino/', 'snippet': 'Ennio Morricone, who has worked on four Quentin Tarantino films, told film students in Rome that he would never collaborate with the director again, saying he “places music in his films without coherence.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Quentin Tarantino may have won an Oscar for “Django Unchained” (for best original screenplay), but he’s getting less than favorable reviews from the composer who supplied some whistle-heavy spaghetti western tracks for the movie’s soundtrack.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/15/movies/ennio/ennio-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/15/movies/ennio/ennio-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/15/movies/ennio/ennio-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/15/movies/ennio/ennio-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype':