 military in 1976, when he served under the man who was appointed pope this week.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/15/full-statement-from-jesuit-kidnapped-by-argentine-junta-on-new-pope/', 'snippet': 'An English translation of the statement released on Friday by Fr. Franz Jalics, a Jesuit priest who was kidnapped by the Argentine military in 1976, when he served under the man who was appointed pope this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last Updated, 5:03 p.m. BERLIN — The Vatican rejected accusations on Friday that the newly appointed Pope Francis had failed to stand up for two Jesuit priests who served under him when they were kidnapped by the military in 1976, during the so-called Dirty War in his home country of Argentina.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Full Statement From Jesuit Kidnapped by Argentine Junta on New Pope', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Francis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARGENTINA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-15T18:15:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kulish', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kulish', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/15271d54-6f13-53c3-b5ad-47119430cec2', 'word_count': 545, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15271d54-6f13-53c3-b5ad-47119430cec2'}, {'abstract': 'The stimulant DMAA is banned by numerous sports groups, but i