s and newspapers paid tribute to the victim, Parween Rahman, who was shot dead by unidentified assassins on Wednesday evening.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISLAMABAD, Pakistan — Concern over deteriorating law and order in Karachi, Pakistan’s largest city, continued to grow Friday as politicians and newspapers paid tribute to a celebrated social worker who was shot dead by unidentified assassins.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/world/0316BRIEFS/0316BRIEFS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/16/world/0316BRIEFS/0316BRIEFS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/world/0316BRIEFS/0316BRIEFS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/world/0316BRIEFS/0316BRIEFS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1359, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/world/0316BRIEFS/0316BRIEFS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/16/world/0316BRIEFS/0316BRIEFS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/world/0316BRIEFS/0316BRIEFS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Concern Over Violence Grows in Karachi as a Social Worker Is Mourned', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pakistan: Slain Activist Hailed\r\nFor Her Work With Karachi’s Poor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Karachi (Pakistan)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assassinations and Attempted Assassinations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-15T18:19:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Declan Walsh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Declan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Walsh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7c4cf1c-502f-5811-82c0-6cfcf60f28fa', 'word_count': 500, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7c4cf1c-502f-5811-82c0-6cfcf60f28fa'}, {'abstract': 'After a soldier died, his parents took aim at a dietary supplement — and the retail chain GNC, where he bought it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/17/business/a-soldiers-parents-take-aim-at-gnc-and-a-supplement-maker.html', 'snippet': 'After a soldier died, his parents took aim at a dietary supplement — and the retail chain GNC, where he bought it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EVERY morning as she gets dressed for her accounting job, Leanne Sparling hangs her son’s military dog tags and a photograph of him in uniform around her neck. She wears the tags on the outside of her clothes, hoping to prompt strangers to ask about him. “When I do tell them what happened,” she says, “they are in total disbelief.”', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'Th