y reshape the debate over what to do about gun violence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/16/us/politics/as-gun-bills-advance-spotlight-falls-on-reid.html', 'snippet': 'How four bills are presented to the full Senate — and which ones Senator Harry Reid chooses to promote — will probably reshape the debate over what to do about gun violence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON – For months, as gun control advocates and gun rights groups have held competing rallies, senators have debated and President Obama has implored Congress to act, one key player, Senator Harry Reid of Nevada, has remained largely on the sidelines of the national debate over guns.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Gun Measures Advance, Spotlight Falls on Reid', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reid, Harry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-15T18:36:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Steinhauer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b136914e-120b-5262-b2a2-e3f4727d586c', 'word_count': 927, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b136914e-120b-5262-b2a2-e3f4727d586c'}, {'abstract': 'M.L.S. and NBC are teaming up on Saturday to provide 10 uninterrupted hours of coverage of league games.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/15/wall-to-wall-m-l-s-on-nbc/', 'snippet': 'M.L.S. and NBC are teaming up on Saturday to provide 10 uninterrupted hours of coverage of league games.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This weekend’s slate of nine games in Major League Soccer is being called several things: Rivalry Day, the Breakaway, or maybe (a stretch perhaps) the GoalZone (with a bow at the waist to the N.F.L.’s RedZone channel).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wall-to-Wall M.L.S. on NBC', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Major League Soccer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-15T18:44:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Bell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c8b66654-1e91-584e-88ea-578c24089a99', 'word_count': 677, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c8b66654-1e91-584e-88ea-578c24089a99'}, {'abstract': 'Melissa DeRosa, who begins her new job April 1, has worked for  Eric T. Schneiderman since 2011 and has a long history in politics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/16/nyregion/cuomo-hires-melissa-derosa-from-attorney-generals-staff.html', 'snippet': 'Melissa DeRosa, who begins her new job April 1, has worked for  Eric T. Schneiderman since 2011 and has a long history in politics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Filling a key vacancy in his inner circle, Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo on Friday named one of Attorney General Eric T. Schneiderman’s top aides to serve as his new communications director.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cuomo Drafts Communications Director From Attorney General’s Staff', 'kicker':