id': 'nyt://article/6af79755-50e3-5e0a-bdf1-0b2195ab4c3c', 'word_count': 473, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6af79755-50e3-5e0a-bdf1-0b2195ab4c3c'}, {'abstract': '“Kick-Ass 2 Prelude: Hit-Girl” is No. 4 on the hardcover list this week.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/15/graphic-books-best-sellers-girl-power/', 'snippet': '“Kick-Ass 2 Prelude: Hit-Girl” is No. 4 on the hardcover list this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Coming in at No. 4 on the graphic books hardcover best-seller list this week is “Kick-Ass 2 Prelude: Hit-Girl,” written by Mark Millar and illustrated by John Romita Jr. The book, published by Icon, an imprint of Marvel, involves the further adventures of Dave Lizewski, a young man who decides to fight crime as Kick-Ass, and Mindy Macready, who was trained by her father to be the lethal force for justice known as Hit-Girl. The premise of “Kick-Ass” is based in reality (what would it be like if heroes existed?), but the violence is amped up a thousandfold. It is somehow more absurd than some regular superhero comics, but infinitely more entertaining than most of them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/15/books/15kick/15kick-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 402, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/15/books/15kick/15kick-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 402, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/15/books/15kick/15kick-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/15/books/15kick/15kick-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'head