5d979'}, {'abstract': 'At Om Bistro, nearly everything, including breads, sauces and desserts, is deftly prepared in-house, and nothing on the menu tops $19.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/17/nyregion/a-review-of-om-bistro-in-great-neck.html', 'snippet': 'At Om Bistro, nearly everything, including breads, sauces and desserts, is deftly prepared in-house, and nothing on the menu tops $19.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For almost a decade, I have been a fan of Richard Desmond. When he was cooking at Bliss in East Setauket from 2004 to 2006, I was there. When he went to Public House 49 in Patchogue in 2009, I followed him. In January he became the chef at Om Bistro in Great Neck, a new restaurant where he is also an owner. His partners there are Harjinder Singh, who is also a co-owner of Raga in East Setauket, and Sandeet Mehen.', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/17/nyregion/17DINELI2/17DINELI2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 397, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/17/nyregion/17DINELI2/17DINELI2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 397}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/17/nyregion/17DINELI2/17DINELI2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 678, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/17/nyregion/17DINELI2/17DINELI2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1356, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/17/nyregion/17DINELI2/17DINELI2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/17/nyregion/17DINELI2/17DINELI2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/17/nyregion/17DINELI2/17DINELI2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Arrangements by a Singing Chef', 'kicker': 'Long Island Dining | Great Neck', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Arrangements by a Singing Chef', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Neck (NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Om Bistro (Great Neck, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-15T22:18:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanne Starkey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Starkey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c78ab885-cffd-553a-8905-a2e0d61f3f47', 'word_count': 589, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c78ab885-cffd-553a-8905-a2e0d61f3f47'}, {'abstract': 'The technology reporters and editors of The New York Times scour the Web for important and peculiar items. For Friday, selections include a satirical dinner with a smartphone, changes to Amazon’s publishing business and a report of slow sales for Microsoft’s tablet.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/15/todays-scuttlebot-amazon-publishing-and-surface-sales/', 'snippet': 'The technology reporters and editors of The New York Times scour the Web for important and peculiar items. For Friday, selections include a satirical dinner with a smartphone, changes to Amazon’s publishing business and a report of slow sales for ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here are some of the more interesting items that the tech reporters and editors of The New York Times found on the Web recently. More Scuttlebot can be found here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 500, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Today’s Scuttlebot: Amazon Publishing and Surface Sales', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-15T22:26:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f27c3a3-eaf2-5946-89e9-99a83d7cd503', 'word_count': 110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f27c3a3-eaf2-5946-89e9-99a83d7cd503'}, {'abstract': '“Mindless Behavior,” a documentary, follows the group of the same name on its “#1 Girl Tour” and in countless public appearances across the country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/16/movies/mindless-behavior-all-around-the-world-a-documentary.html', 'snippet': '“Mindless Behavior,” a documentary, follows the group of the same name on its “#1 Girl Tour” and in countless public appearances across the country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Watching the quasi-documentary marketing tool “Mindless Behavior: All Around the World,” you would think that the boy band Mindless Behavior existed as a charity, so abundant are the platitudes about the members’ living for the fans, being positive, inspiring others and the self-actualization of the “mindless” state. Despite its title, the film, a record of the group’s “#1 Girl Tour,” follows this teenage R&B-lite foursome around the United States, interspersing concert footage with biographical tidbits, public appearances and countless images of screaming, swooning female tweens and adolescents. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/arts/16MINDLESS/16MINDLESS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 284, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/16/arts/16MINDLESS/16MINDLESS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 284}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/arts/16MINDLESS/16MINDLESS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 712, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/arts/16MINDLESS/16MINDLESS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 712, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/arts/16MINDLESS/16MINDLESS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/16/arts/16MINDLESS/16MINDLESS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/arts/16MINDLESS/16MINDLESS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'On the Road With Young Performers', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On the Road With Young Performers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mindless Behavior (Music Group)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-15T22:27:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Webster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Webster', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/65a2c9ce-3e22-525b-b372-bdae3be7a59f', 'word_count': 299, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65a2c9ce-3e22-525b-b372-bdae3be7a59f'}, {'abstract': 'DreamWorks Animation’s next movie may sell popcorn in theaters, but it took lots of hard-nosed computer processing to get there. DreamWorks has been thinking hard about technology and digital costs for the last several years, In the process it has become a marquee client for Intel and Hewlett-Packard, speaking to the oil industry and Wall Street.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/15/making-movie-magic-more-efficient/', 'snippet': 'DreamWorks Animation’s next movie may sell popcorn in theaters, but it took lots of hard-nosed computer processing to get there. DreamWorks has been thinking hard about technology and digital costs for the last several years, In the process it has...', 'lead_paragraph': '“The Croods” is a caveman movie from DreamWorks Animation that comes out March 22. The subject may be paleolithic, but the technology approach may well be cutting edge.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/15/technology/15bits-light1/15bits-light1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 592, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/15/technology/15bits-light1/15bits-light1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 592, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/15/technology/15bits-light1/15bits-light1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/15/technology/15bits-light1/15bits-light1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Making Movie Magic More Efficient', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANIMATED FILMS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'DreamWorks Animation SKG Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-15T22:29:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Quentin Hardy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quentin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hardy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b7f00f1-17e6-53e0-ad67-48c42e4afc77', 'word_count': 540, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b7f00f1-17e6-53e0-ad67-48c42e4afc77'}, {'abstract': 'Robert M. Morgenthau, 93, and two other prominent former prosecutors are asking the United States Supreme Court to take up the case of William Ernest Kuenzel, who has been on death row in Alabama for 24 years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2013/03/15/nyregion/15about-amicus-brief.html', 'snippet': 'Robert M. Morgenthau, 93, and two other prominent former prosecutors are asking the United States Supreme Court to take up the case of William Ernest Kuenzel, who has been on death row in Alabama for 24 years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Robert M. Morgenthau, 93, and two other prominent former prosecutors are asking the United States Supreme Court to take up the case of William Ernest Kuenzel, who has been on death row in Alabama for 24 years.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Legal Brief Filed on Behalf of William Ernest Kuenzel', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morgenthau, Robert M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kuenzel, William Ernest', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALABAMA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legal Profession', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-15T22:30:16+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'New York', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/4de35b3b-30cb-56af-bc1b-9be390d87033', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/4de35b3b-30cb-56af-bc1b-9be390d87033'}, {'abstract': 'To meet federal mandates, refiners trade ethanol credits, whose prices have jumped nearly tenfold since January, adding to costs at the pump, experts say.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/16/business/energy-environment/ethanol-glut-threatens-a-rise-in-gasoline-prices.html', 'snippet': 'To meet federal mandates, refiners trade ethanol credits, whose prices have jumped nearly tenfold since January, adding to costs at the pump, experts say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — A glut of ethanol in the gasoline supply is threatening to push up prices at the pump and may have exacerbated the growing cost gap between regular gasoline and premium, some oil experts say. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/business/Ethanol1/Ethanol1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 369, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/16/business/Ethanol1/Ethanol1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 369}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/business/Ethanol1/Ethanol1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 629, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/business/Ethanol1/Ethanol1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1258, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/business/Ethanol1/Ethanol1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/16/business/Ethanol1/Ethanol1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/business/Ethanol1/Ethanol1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ethanol Surplus May Lift Gas Prices', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ethanol Surplus May Lift Gas Prices', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethanol', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fuel Efficiency', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-15T22:32:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Energy & Environment ', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0374cf4-269e-5a13-b19d-aba538e1e1f2', 'word_count': 1159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0374cf4-269e-5a13-b19d-aba538e1e1f2'}, {'abstract': 'The E.P.A. fuel economy and emissions numbers for 2012 are preliminary, and based on sales estimates provided to the agency by automakers.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/15/fuel-economy-small-decline-in-2011-and-a-probable-climb-in-2012-e-p-a-says/', 'snippet': 'The E.P.A. fuel economy and emissions numbers for 2012 are preliminary, and based on sales estimates provided to the agency by automakers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An Environmental Protection Agency report issued on Friday offers a mixed picture of fleetwide fuel economy in the United States. It documents a minor decline in the 2011 model year to 22.4 miles per gallon, but projects “significant gains” to 23.8 m.p.g. for 2012, a 1.4 m.p.g. improvement over one year. The report said that the 2012 numbers, if confirmed, “would be all-time records and amongst the largest annual improvements since 1975.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fuel Economy: Small Decline in 2011 and a Probable Climb in 2012, E.P.A. Says', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Pollution', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fuel Efficiency', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-15T22:36:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Motavalli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Motavalli', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e8fb317-82f2-5114-9de9-c3c7938a5de7', 'word_count': 633, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e8fb317-82f2-5114-9de9-c3c7938a5de7'}, {'abstract': 'To prevent fire and smoke episodes, Boeing said, the lithium-ion batteries on the 787 will be sealed in a steel box as a fail-safe.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/16/business/boeing-details-its-fixes-for-787.html', 'snippet': 'To prevent fire and smoke episodes, Boeing said, the lithium-ion batteries on the 787 will be sealed in a steel box as a fail-safe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Boeing officials have detailed for the first time their proposed fixes for the lithium-ion batteries aboard its 787 planes, and the changes include better insulation between the eight cells in the battery, gentler charging to minimize stress and a 