 YouTube in Arabic and English.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Remembering the Start of Syria’s Uprising', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Idriss, Salim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Free Syrian Army', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALEPPO (SYRIA)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Damascus (Syria)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-15T23:42:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/90c3b41c-29cc-5a85-acbf-92d22a5a9627', 'word_count': 442, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90c3b41c-29cc-5a85-acbf-92d22a5a9627'}, {'abstract': 'The boy band Mindless Behavior is an African-American answer to British groups like the Wanted and One Direction. But its lack of success reflects how thoroughly black styles have been absorbed into pop.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/16/arts/music/mindless-behavior-an-old-style-boy-band.html', 'snippet': 'The boy band Mindless Behavior is an African-American answer to British groups like the Wanted and One Direction. But its lack of success reflects how thoroughly black styles have been absorbed into pop.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Judging by the old rules and metrics, the boy band has been severely debased in the last couple of years. Gone are the song-and-dance extravaganza groups of decades past. What we have now are the Wanted and One Direction, British imports whose nonchalance can feel like an undermining commentary on the traditional model.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/arts/16BOYBAND/16BOYBAND-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 327, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/16/arts/16BOYBAND/16BOYBAND-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 327}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/arts/16BOYBAND/16BOYBAND-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 558, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/arts/16BOYBAND/16BOYBAND-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1117, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/arts/16BOYBAND/16BOYBAND-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/16/arts/16BOYBAND/16BOYBAND-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/arts/16BOYBAND/16BOYBAND-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Old-Style Boy Band, With Modern Wooing', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Old-Style Boy Band, With Modern Wooing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mindless Behavior (Music Group)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-15T23:44:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b812135a-bf82-547a-bf5d-597a1462e823', 'word_count': 719, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b812135a-bf82-547a-bf5d-597a1462e823'}, {'abstract': 'I don’t need an ad campaign to tell me about the challenges of parenthood. I need support, not stereotypes and shame.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/16/opinion/i-was-a-teenage-mother.html', 'snippet': 'I don’t need an ad campaign to tell me about the challenges of parenthood. I need support, not stereotypes and shame.', 'lead_paragraph': '“EVERYTHING’S going to be O.K., mamita,” my mother said, before walking into her bedroom and crying her eyes out. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'I Was a Teenage Mother', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'I Was a Teenage Mother', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teenage Pregnancy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-15T23:58:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gloria Malone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gloria', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Malone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/9876801a-a4e6-58a7-b503-9e420ca5f7ec', 'word_count': 607, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9876801a-a4e6-58a7-b503-9e420ca5f7ec'}, {'abstract': 'As the National People’s Congress continued in Beijing, thousands of residents stood guard in the streets as the front lines in the government’s war against potential unrest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/16/world/asia/neighborhood-committees-keep-watch-over-beijing-during-peoples-congress.html', 'snippet': 'As the National People’s Congress continued in Beijing, thousands of residents stood guard in the streets as the front lines in the government’s war against potential unrest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — Dressed in a new crimson windbreaker, a red cap and an armband emblazoned with “Capital Public Security Patrol,” Gao Fengping sat in a child-sized pink chair and vigilantly watched the midday bustle of a narrow back street. If a protest or disturbance erupted, Ms. Gao, 58, a retired factory worker, was ready.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/world/16stability1/16stability1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/16/world/16stability1/16stability1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/world/16stability1/16stability1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/world/16stability1/16stability1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail'