cán, on a mountain called Sierra Chincua, where the branches of hundreds of fir trees were covered with butterflies that exploded into glorious flight when warmed by the sun. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/opinion/0316OPEDojala/0316OPEDojala-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 615, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/16/opinion/0316OPEDojala/0316OPEDojala-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 615}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/opinion/0316OPEDojala/0316OPEDojala-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/opinion/0316OPEDojala/0316OPEDojala-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/opinion/0316OPEDojala/0316OPEDojala-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/16/opinion/0316OPEDojala/0316OPEDojala-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/opinion/0316OPEDojala/0316OPEDojala-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Winter of the Monarch', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributors', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Winter of the Monarch', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Butterflies and Moths', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-16T00:10:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lincoln P. Brower and Homero Aridjis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lincoln', 'middlename': 'P.', 'lastname': 'Brower', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Homero', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Aridjis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/0761e5cc-74bb-54ec-b660-c27a4166d847', 'word_count': 820, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0761e5cc-74bb-54ec-b660-c27a4166d847'}, {'abstract': 'A judge struck down a law that allows the F.B.I. to secretly seize subscriber information from Internet companies and other communications service providers without a warrant.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/16/us/california-judge-strikes-down-law-on-national-security-letters.html', 'snippet': 'A judge struck down a law that allows the F.B.I. to secretly seize subscriber information from Internet companies and other communications service providers without a warrant.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A federal judge on Friday struck down a law that allows the Federal Bureau of Investigation to secretly seize subscriber information from Internet companies and other communications service providers without a court warrant. The ruling, by Judge Susan Illston of Federal District Court in San Francisco, struck down the law because it forbids companies from disclosing that they had received such an order, called a National Security Letter, making the statute “impermissibly overbroad” under the First Amendment, she wrote. She also struck down a statute on legal challenges by recipients of the security letters, but stayed her ruling to allow the government to appeal. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'California: Judge Strikes Down Law on National Security Letters', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | West', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'California: Judge Strikes Down Law On National Security Letters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Savage, Charlie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Investigation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search and Seizure', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Illston, Susan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-16T00:13:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/94992590-9fc9-5d93-80fe-7d63533c7cb4', 'word_count': 104, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94992590-9fc9-5d93-80fe-7d63533c7cb4'}, {'abstract': 'A leaked tape of a closed meeting of the private club for actors shows a membership unhappy with day-to-day operations and with the club’s executive director, John Martello.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/16/nyregion/players-club-director-survives-an-ouster-vote.html', 'snippet': 'A leaked tape of a closed meeting of the private club for actors shows a membership unhappy with day-to-day operations and with the club’s executive director, John Martello.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One thing to be said for theater people: they know drama. On Thursday night, more than 100 members of the Players, a private club founded for actors, crowded into the main dining room of its 1847 Greek Revival town house on Gramercy Park for a vote on whether to oust their longstanding executive director.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/nyregion/PLAYERS/PLAYERS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/16/nyregion/PLAYERS/PLAYERS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/nyregion/PLAYERS/PLAYERS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/nyregion/PLAYERS/PLAYERS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/nyregion/PLAYERS/PLAYERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/16/nyregion/PLAYERS/PLAYERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/nyregion/PLAYERS/PLAYERS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Players Club Stages a Real-Life Drama Over Whether to Oust Its Director', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Players Club Stages a Real-Life Drama Over Whether to Oust Its Director', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martello, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Players Club', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organizations, Societies and Clubs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gramercy Park (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-16T00:17:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Leland', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leland', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d314dbe4-c1e7-5260-9c34-ed155a097621', 'word_count': 901, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d314dbe4-c1e7-5260-9c34-ed155a097621'}, {'abstract': 'Fiamma Trattoria in Mamaroneck is old-fashioned, but not retro, with fresh, hand-cranked pasta, a robust tagliatelle Bolognese and delicate lobster manicotti.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/17/nyregion/a-review-of-fiamma-trattoria-in-mamaroneck.html', 'snippet': 'Fiamma Trattoria in Mamaroneck is old-fashioned, but not retro, with fresh, hand-cranked pasta, a robust tagliatelle Bolognese and delicate lobster manicotti.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On our first visit to Fiamma Trattoria, which hugs a corner in a modest neighborhood near the Metro-North tracks in Mamaroneck, we were greeted with an enthusiasm that all but raised suspicion. No indifferent hostess sized us up us at a lectern; instead, our waiter, Anthony, pulled out a couple of chairs and said, “Sit down, I’ll be with you in a minute.” And he was, returning in a jiffy to fill us in on details, as if we were his new best friends.', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/17/nyregion/17DINEWE2/17DINEWE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/17/nyregion/17DINEWE2/17DINEWE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/17/nyregion/17DINEWE2/17DINEWE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/17/nyregion/17DINEWE2/17DINEWE2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1359, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/17/nyregion/17DINEWE2/17DINEWE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/17/nyregion/17DINEWE2/17DINEWE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/17/nyregion/17DINEWE2/17DINEWE2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Honoring Italian-American Classics', 'kicker': 'Westchester Dining | Mamaroneck', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Honoring Italian-American Classics', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mamaroneck (NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fiamma Trattoria (Mamaroneck, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-16T00:21:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alice Gabriel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alice', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gabriel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e6094839-30e8-55ef-a1c0-3dc1444715bc', 'word_count': 700, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e6094839-30e8-55ef-a1c0-3dc1444715bc'}, {'abstract': 'A court grievance panel blocked Ivan S. Fisher from practicing in the Southern District of New York, saying he stole from a client.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/16/nyregion/ivan-fisher-barred-from-practicing-law-in-us-court-in-manhattan.html', 'snippet': 'A court grievance panel blocked Ivan S. Fisher from practicing in the Southern District of New York, saying he stole from a client.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ivan S. Fisher, a prominent criminal defense lawyer, has been barred from practicing law in Federal District Court in Manhattan, the site of many of his celebrated trials, including representing a New York mafia boss in the well-known pizza connection narcotics case in the 1980s. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Criminal Lawyer Is Barred From Working in U.S. Court', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Criminal Lawyer Is Barred From Working in U.S. Court', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fisher, Ivan S', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Institutional)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legal Profession', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'},