l', 'snippet': 'A new judge was named on Friday to preside over the trial of James (Whitey) Bulger, who faces 19 counts of murder, after another judge was removed over a possible perception of bias.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A judge who is relatively new to the federal bench was named on Friday to preside over the trial of James (Whitey) Bulger, Boston’s notorious crime boss who faces 19 counts of murder. The appointment of the judge, Denise J. Casper, comes a day after Judge Richard G. Stearns was removed because of a possible perception of bias. Ms. Casper, 45, a Harvard Law School graduate and former federal prosecutor, was appointed to the bench by President Obama in 2010. The court has not announced whether the trial, set to begin June 6, will be delayed to allow Ms. Casper to familiarize herself with the voluminous case material. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Massachusetts: New Judge for Bulger', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | New England', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Massachusetts: New Judge For Bulger', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bulger, James J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Casper, Denise J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stearns, Richard Gaylore', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Crime', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-16T00:28:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katharine Q. Seelye', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katharine', 'middlename': 'Q.', 'lastname': 'Seelye', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/295c5e51-345d-51d1-98a0-e385ca77b997', 'word_count': 108, 'uri': 'nyt://article/295c5e51-345d-51d1-98a0-e385ca77b997'}, {'abstract': 'A former player is finally able to sit down and watch baseball with his children.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/15/offspring-training/', 'snippet': 'A former player is finally able to sit down and watch baseball with his children.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I do not claim to know what my playing career meant in the grand scheme of baseball. All I know for sure is that I found a passion I could express on a diamond. For this I am eternally grateful. Yet after my career was over, I found myself adrift from the game. A post-retirement stasis of sorts. In a way, it also kept my new family from embracing baseball. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Offspring Training', 'kicker': 'Doug Glanville', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-16T00:30:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Doug Glanville', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Doug', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Glanville', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca24af08-09b6-57f9-a1a5-c5c5a138820d', 'word_count': 768, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca24af08-09b6-57f9-a1a5-c5c5a138820d'}, {'abstract': 'After Hurricane Sandy wiped out nearly all the cars in Howard Beach, Queens, residents bought new ones and provided tire thieves inviting targets.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/16/nyregion/the-storm-took-their-cars-then-thieves-disabled-the-new-ones.html', 'snippet': 'After Hurricane Sandy wiped out nearly all the cars in Howard Beach, Queens, residents bought new ones and provided tire thieves inviting targets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'First came the floodwater. Then the insurance checks. Then, just when things were looking up, more trouble, in the form of a sophisticated crew of thieves who work with precision, tools and, in a throwback to rougher times, heavy cinder blocks. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/nyregion/CRIMESCENE/CRIMESCENE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/16/nyregion/CRIMESCENE/CRIMESCENE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/nyregion/CRIMESCENE/CRIMESCENE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/nyregion/CRIMESCENE/CRIMESCENE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/nyregion/CRIMESCENE/CRIMESCENE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/16/nyregion/CRIMESCENE/CRIMESCENE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/nyregion/CRIMESCENE/CRIMESCENE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Storm Took Their Cars, Then Thieves Disabled the New Ones', 'kicker': 'Crime Scene', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Storm Took Their Cars, Then Thieves Disabled the New Ones', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilson, Michael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Howard Beach (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-16T00:32:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/41cbaf5f-3020-543f-9fb6-703261d7c588', 'word_count': 787, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41cbaf5f-3020-543f-9fb6-703261d7c588'}, {'abstract': 'Maryland is likely to become the 18th state to outlaw executions after lawmakers approved a measure abolishing the death penalty.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/16/us/maryland-repeal-of-death-penalty-awaits-governors-signature.html', 'snippet': 'Maryland is likely to become the 18th state to outlaw executions after lawmakers approved a measure abolishing the death penalty.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Maryland is likely to become the 18th state to outlaw executions after lawmakers approved a measure abolishing the death penalty. Gov. Martin O’Malley, a Democrat who has long pushed for the change, is expected to sign the bill when the legislative session ends in April. The House of Delegates passed the bill 82 to 56 on Friday, 10 days after the Senate approved it. The legislation would replace death sentences with life terms without the possibility of parole. It would not apply to the five inmates on death row in the state. Mr. O’Malley will decide whether to convert their sentences. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Maryland: Repeal of Death Penalty Awaits Governor’s Signature', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Mid-Atlantic', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Maryland: Repeal of Death Penalty Awaits the Governor’s Signature', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Maryland', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Malley, Martin J", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-16T00:33:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Southall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Southall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/5bba3bae-949d-54e2-9512-80a7c5082f74', 'word_count': 101, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5bba3bae-949d-54e2-9512-80a7c5082f74'}, {'abstract': 'Factional struggles in Beijing have spilled into Hong Kong, where tens of thousands of people have joined large street demonstrations against the Beijing-backed government.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/16/world/asia/friction-with-beijing-as-hong-kong-seeks-more-democracy.html', 'snippet': 'Factional struggles in Beijing have spilled into Hong Kong, where tens of thousands of people have joined large street demonstrations against the Beijing-backed government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — Looming over