ions of Americanness.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/16/arts/dance/paul-taylor-dance-company-at-lincoln-center.html', 'snippet': 'From the poet-renegade to the passing of generations, Paul Taylor’s offerings at Lincoln Center plumb notions of Americanness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many American artists have adapted the myths, themes and art of Europe to American settings. Shakespeare’s “Othello” has been told to Motown music (last year in “Mo(or)town Redux,” by the choreographer Doug Elkins); Mozart’s “Nozze di Figaro” has been set in an apartment in the Trump Tower (in Peter Sellars’s 1988 production). ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/arts/16CASCADE1/16CASCADE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 355, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/16/arts/16CASCADE1/16CASCADE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 355}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/arts/16CASCADE1/16CASCADE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 607, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/arts/16CASCADE1/16CASCADE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1213, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/arts/16CASCADE1/16CASCADE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/16/arts/16CASCADE1/16CASCADE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/arts/16CASCADE1/16CASCADE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dreamscape of America, Rollicking or Sublime', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dreamscape Of America, Rollicking Or Sublime', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taylor, Paul, Dance Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Koch, David H, Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-16T01:15:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/5484aab9-67cf-589c-a7b9-eec8b9202ed1', 'word_count': 719, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5484aab9-67cf-589c-a7b9-eec8b9202ed1'}, {'abstract': 'Their 2014 budget is a strong counterweight to the reckless House proposals from Paul Ryan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/16/opinion/senate-democrats-finally-take-a-stand.html', 'snippet': 'Their 2014 budget is a strong counterweight to the reckless House proposals from Paul Ryan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s been four years since the Democrats who control the Senate produced a budget. That has meant four missed opportunities to demonstrate what they stand for, in hard numbers and clear spending priorities. On Wednesday, the chamber’s leaders stiffened their spines and issued a 2014 budget. If the result isn’t quite a courageous resistance to political winds, it at least makes most of the right choices and is a solid rebuttal to the heartless collection of obsolete dogmas that is the House budget.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Senate Democrats Finally Take a Stand', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Senate Democrats Finally Take a Stand', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murray, Patty', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-16T01:16:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/bfdf6672-b7d4-52e3-8fc5-47e6cd4310bf', 'word_count': 497, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bfdf6672-b7d4-52e3-8fc5-47e6cd4310bf'}, {'abstract': 'New York Road Runners, which was criticized over its handling of the canceled New York City Marathon, has had fewer finishers at its races this year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/16/sports/new-york-road-runners-face-difficulty-months-after-marathon.html', 'snippet': 'New York Road Runners, which was criticized over its handling of the canceled New York City Marathon, has had fewer finishers at its races this year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The furor over New York Road Runners’ handling of its marathon last year has died down, but questions about the group’s future persist, including whether its dominance has started to erode because of rival race organizers and disaffected runners.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Road Runners Facing More Difficulty 4 Months After Marathon Uproar', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Road Runners Facing Difficulty Months After Marathon Uproar', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Road Runners Club', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lehren, Andrew W', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wittenberg, Mary', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Running', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York City Marathon', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marathon Running', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-16T01:16:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson and Andrew W. Lehren', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Lehren', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8413c8ac-5b2a-59ed-8222-db299ee6e7d7', 'word_count': 1279, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8413c8ac-5b2a-59ed-8222-db299ee6e7d7'}, {'abstract': 'With “Edwardian Opulence,” in New Haven, the curators Angus Trumble and Andrea Wolk Rager ask us to look anew at an era we feel we know well, thanks to plays, novels, film and television dramas.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/17/nyregion/a-review-of-edwardian-opulence-at-the-yale-center-for-british-art.html', 'snippet': 'With “Edwardian Opulence,” in New Haven, the curators Angus Trumble and Andrea Wolk Rager ask us to look anew at an era we feel we know well, thanks to plays, novels, film and television dramas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The three sumptuous objects, studded with gemstones and embellished with gold, are too large to be worn as jewelry; they’re too small to serve as display pieces. If they were boxes, they might hold stamps or face powder; but they don’t open. Their exquisite workmanship implies instead that they exist only to be beautiful. ', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/17/nyregion/17ARTSCT_1SPAN/17ARTSCT_1SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/17/nyregion/17ARTSCT_1SPAN/17ARTSCT_1SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/17/nyregion/17ARTSCT_1SPAN/17ARTSCT_1SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/17/nyregion/17ARTSCT_1SPAN/17ARTSCT_1SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1133, 'width': 1698, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/17/nyregion/17ARTSCT_1SPAN/17ARTSCT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/17/nyregion/17ARTSCT_1SPAN/17ARTSCT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'imag