 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/b5bc11dd-faca-5ec1-aa2a-fa1f4cfe9396', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/b5bc11dd-faca-5ec1-aa2a-fa1f4cfe9396'}, {'abstract': 'On Sunday, John C. Liu plans to announce his candidacy for mayor — a seemingly quixotic bid, given fraud charges against two associates, but one that he insists is still winnable.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/16/nyregion/despite-troubles-liu-keeps-moving-forward-in-mayoral-race.html', 'snippet': 'On Sunday, John C. Liu plans to announce his candidacy for mayor — a seemingly quixotic bid, given fraud charges against two associates, but one that he insists is still winnable.', 'lead_paragraph': 'John C. Liu is the most ubiquitous of New York City officeholders, with a voracious appetite for retail politics, ever smiling, hugging everyone he meets and sampling all the food along the way. He has been the brightest political hope of the city’s fast-growing Asian-American community, which propelled him first onto the City Council, and then to citywide office as comptroller.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York Mayoral Hopeful Forges Ahead, Undeterred', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Undeterred by Inquiry, a Mayoral Hopeful Forges Ahead', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chen, David W', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Liu, John C', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-16T01:18:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/53ccf026-a2ae-5a1a-93f0-88dfc43d6e45', 'word_count': 948, 'uri': 'nyt://article/53ccf026-a2ae-5a1a-93f0-88dfc43d6e45'}, {'abstract': 'Conflict over governing the University of Virginia has become a proxy war in a much larger struggle over control of the nation’s public universities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/16/education/university-of-virginia-crisis-reflects-wider-fight.html', 'snippet': 'Conflict over governing the University of Virginia has become a proxy war in a much larger struggle over control of the nation’s public universities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nine months after the University of Virginia removed its president, prompting a storm of protest, and then reinstated her, the university still cannot go more than a few days or weeks without some new reminder of that spectacle, or persisting tensions between the president and the trustee who ousted her.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'University of Virginia’s Crisis Reflects Wider Conflict', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'University’s Crisis Reflects Wider Conflict', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Virginia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sullivan, Teresa A', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Texas', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Wisconsin', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Oregon', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-16T01:18:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Pérez-Peña', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pérez-Peña', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e153526-9d21-5b98-8463-bfd455a184ac', 'word_count': 941, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e153526-9d21-5b98-8463-bfd455a184ac'}, {'abstract': 'Afghanistan’s president has shown his truly sinister side in demonizing the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/16/opinion/the-duplicity-of-afghanistans-president.html', 'snippet': 'Afghanistan’s president has shown his truly sinister side in demonizing the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Hamid Karzai of Afghanistan has been America’s faithless partner throughout the war. Despite corruption in his government and his own family, Washington has worked with him to hold the country together because it has had to.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Over the Line', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Over the Line', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karzai, Hamid', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-16T01:21:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/c7f5e360-5cba-55de-8f26-a41fce640772', 'word_count': 393, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c7f5e360-5cba-55de-8f26-a41fce640772'}, {'abstract': 'Bills that would allow check-cashing stores to enter the lending business and be exempt from the usury law are a bad idea.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/16/opinion/gouging-the-poor-in-new-york.html', 'snippet': 'Bills that would allow check-cashing stores to enter the lending business and be exempt from the usury law are a bad idea.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Andrew Cuomo of New York has warned debt collectors that they could face legal sanctions if they try to collect predatory loans that violate the state’s usury law, which prohibits loans with interest rates above 25 percent. The governor needs to take an equally forceful stand against pending bills that would encourage predatory lending by allowing check-cashing stores to enter the lending business and exempting them from the usury law. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gouging the Poor in New York', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gouging the Poor in New York', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Payday Loans', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-16T01:24:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization