erson': [{'firstname': 'Victoria', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burnett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Biography', '_id': 'nyt://article/64ec6ebb-f48a-531f-b095-2cbe21ae4d27', 'word_count': 1266, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64ec6ebb-f48a-531f-b095-2cbe21ae4d27'}, {'abstract': 'A question about the real Swing Street, on West 133rd in Harlem.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/17/nyregion/answers-to-questions-about-new-york.html', 'snippet': 'A question about the real Swing Street, on West 133rd in Harlem.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q. My father once mentioned that when he was a young man, he and friends would listen to jazz in speakeasies on 133rd Street in Harlem. Can you tell me about that stretch?', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Listening to Jazz on 133rd', 'kicker': 'F.Y.I.', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Harlem (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bars and Nightclubs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-16T02:13:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Pollak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pollak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e82a9d0-9a6c-5cae-8334-decd32b3ef37', 'word_count': 446, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e82a9d0-9a6c-5cae-8334-decd32b3ef37'}, {'abstract': 'Fifty years after the Supreme Court ruled in Gideon v. Wainwright, the promise of legal representation for all is not fully realized.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/16/us/16gideon.html', 'snippet': 'Fifty years after the Supreme Court ruled in Gideon v. Wainwright, the promise of legal representation for all is not fully realized.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ADEL, Ga. — Billy Jerome Presley spent 17 months in a Georgia jail because he did not have $2,700 for a child support payment. He had no prior jail record but also no lawyer. In Baltimore last fall, Carl Hymes, 21, was arrested on charges of shining a laser into the eyes of a police officer. Bail was set at $75,000. He had no arrest record but also no lawyer. In West Orange, N.J., last summer, Walter Bloss, 89, was served with an eviction notice from the rent-controlled apartment he had lived in for 43 years after a dispute with his landlord. He had gone to court without a lawyer.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/us/GIDEON/GIDEON-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 720, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/16/us/GIDEON/GIDEON-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 720}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/us/GIDEON/GIDEON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 854, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/us/GIDEON/GIDEON-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1707, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/us/GIDEON/GIDEON-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/16/us/GIDEON/GIDEON-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/us/GIDEON/GIDEON-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Right to Lawyer Can Be Empty Promise for Poor', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Right to Lawyer Can Be Empty Promise for Poor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bronner, Ethan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legal Aid for the Poor (Civil)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Southern Center for Human Rights', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Georgia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public Defenders and Court-Appointed Lawyers (Criminal)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legal Profession', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-16T02:18:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ethan Bronner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ethan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bronner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/66e96646-07dc-5ecc-addb-bd3fd85461a9', 'word_count': 1366, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66e96646-07dc-5ecc-addb-bd3fd85461a9'}, {'abstract': 'In the Gideon v. Wainwright decision, which held that states must provide legal representation for the poor in serious criminal cases, the Supreme Court unanimously overturned its own 1942 decision in the landmark case of Betts v. Brady.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2013/03/15/us/gideon-wainwright-original-times-article.html', 'snippet': 'In the Gideon v. Wainwright decision, which held that states must provide legal representation for the poor in serious criminal cases, the Supreme Court unanimously overturned its own 1942 decision in the landmark case of Betts v. Brady.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the Gideon v. Wainwright decision, which held that states must provide legal representation for the poor in serious criminal cases, the Supreme Court unanimously overturned its own 1942 decision in the landmark case of Betts v. Brady.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Times’s 1963 Article on the Gideon v. Wainwright Decision', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legal Aid for the Poor (Civil)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legal Profession', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-16T02:18:03+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/8cc30808-3608-58c3-909c-8d50f8bcca9a', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/8cc30808-3608-58c3-909c-8d50f8bcca9a'}, {'abstract': 'A lot is riding on the Texas Clean Energy Project. Its technology could be a climate-saver.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/16/opinion/nocera-texas-might-be-on-to-something.html', 'snippet': 'A lot is riding on the Texas Clean Energy Project. Its technology could be a climate-saver.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sometime this summer, in Odessa, Tex., the Summit Power Group plans to break ground on a $2.5 billion coal gasification power plant. Summi