nyt://article/808b760e-da34-52de-9413-34f1f7584691', 'word_count': 801, 'uri': 'nyt://article/808b760e-da34-52de-9413-34f1f7584691'}, {'abstract': 'An ethnic Uighur farmer has been detained and accused of killing five people and wounding seven in a knife attack on March 7 in Korla, according to a report on Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/16/world/asia/china-uighur-detained-in-attack.html', 'snippet': 'An ethnic Uighur farmer has been detained and accused of killing five people and wounding seven in a knife attack on March 7 in Korla, according to a report on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': ' An ethnic Uighur farmer has been detained and accused of killing five people and wounding seven in a knife attack on March 7 in Korla, a center of oil production in the western region of Xinjiang, according to a report on Friday on the Xinjiang government Web site that cited an article in the newspaper Xinjiang Daily. The farmer, Aizitiali Mamuti, 27, had been punished by the authorities for three previous knife attacks, the report said. Right before the attack, he had argued with relatives and had decided to take “revenge on society.” The attack raised questions about ethnic tensions in Korla; in Xinjiang, ethnic Uighurs often speak of discrimination by ethnic Han, who rule China. Four of the victims were Han and one was Hui; the attack also injured six Han and one Uighur. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China: Uighur Detained in Attack', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China: Uighur Detained in Attack', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Uighurs (Chinese Ethnic Group)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-16T02:25:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/861e4ddd-4c6c-5995-9188-ffb2d4b34e27', 'word_count': 135, 'uri': 'nyt://article/861e4ddd-4c6c-5995-9188-ffb2d4b34e27'}, {'abstract': 'Seven people, some of them members of a taxi union, were fatally shot in a bar in Cancún, several miles from the city’s popular beachfront resorts, the authorities said Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/16/world/americas/mexico-7-die-in-cancun-shooting.html', 'snippet': 'Seven people, some of them members of a taxi union, were fatally shot in a bar in Cancún, several miles from the city’s popular beachfront resorts, the authorities said Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Seven people, some of them members of a taxi union, were fatally shot in a bar in Cancún, several miles from the city’s popular beachfront resorts, the authorities said Thursday. The state prosecutor, Armando García Torres, told a local radio station that the motive was under investigation, and that the possibility of the involvement of organized crime gangs, which have targeted taxi workers in other states, had not been ruled out. The shooting took place in a working-class neighborhood not on the tourist circuit, but Mexico’s efforts to increase tourism have not been helped by recent episodes of crime near or in tourist spots, including the arrest last month of local police officers in the rape of an Italian woman in Playa del Carmen, near Cancún, and the sexual assault of six women from Spain last month at a beach house in Acapulco, on the Pacific coast.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mexico: 7 Die in Cancún Shooting', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mexico: 7 Die in Cancún Shooting', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cancun (Mexico)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxicabs and Taxicab Drivers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-16T02:29:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karla Zabludovsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zabludovsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d9861a9-9f97-5365-b912-82bddfe7eeb2', 'word_count': 147, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d9861a9-9f97-5365-b912-82bddfe7eeb2'}, {'abstract': 'The final conference tournament meeting between fierce rivals Syracuse and Georgetown took place in a dream matchup that lived up to the hype.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/16/sports/ncaabasketball/syracuse-defeats-georgetown-in-final-big-east-meeting.html', 'snippet': 'The final conference tournament meeting between fierce rivals Syracuse and Georgetown took place in a dream matchup that lived up to the hype.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Moments like these made the Big East tournament, made it less of a basketball culmination and more of a touchstone, complete with a distinct New York flavor. Take Friday. Here was Syracuse, and here was Georgetown, with every seat filled in Madison Square Garden, in a game that went into overtime, undecided until the final shot.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/sports/sub-georgetown-1/sub-georgetown-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 362, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/16/sports/sub-georgetown-1/sub-georgetown-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 362}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/sports/sub-georgetown-1/sub-georgetown-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 617, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/sports/sub-georgetown-1/sub-georgetown-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1235, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/sports/sub-georgetown-1/sub-georgetown-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/16/sports/sub-georgetown-1/sub-georgetown-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/sports/sub-georgetown-1/sub-georgetown-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Last, Long Goodbye at the Garden', 'kicker': 'Syracuse 58, Georgetown 55', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Last, Long Goodbye at the Garden', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball (College)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Georgetown University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Syracuse University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Big East Conference', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'NCAA Basketball Championships (Men)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-16T02:33:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Greg Bishop', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Greg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bishop', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0f96df3-7452-5945-99dd-1b76b288dcb5', 'word_count': 931, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0f96df3-7452-5945-99dd-1b76b288dcb5'}, {'abstract': 'On Sundays, the classical pianist Simone Dinnerstein and her 11-year-old son sometimes practice their instruments; her husband plays the radio.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/17/nyregion/at-simone-dinnersteins-home-music-plays-upstairs-and-downstairs.html', 'snippet': 'On Sundays, the classical pianist Simone Dinnerstein and her 11-year-old son sometimes practice their instruments; her husband plays the radio.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The classical pianist Simone Dinnerstein, 40, has a hectic international performance schedule, but in Park Slope her husband, Jeremy Greensmith, 46, and their son, Adrian Greensmith, 11, keep her grounded. While she plays her nine-foot Hamburg Steinway concert grand on the second floor, Adrian practices downstairs on an electric guitar for his band, the Animation, and Mr. Greensmith cooks dinner or plans lessons for his fifth-grade classes at Public School 321. Ms. Dinnerstein (her first name is pronounced “Simona”) has a new album, “Night,” with the singer-songwriter Tift Merritt, being released on Tuesday in the United States; she and Ms. Merritt are scheduled to perform at Merkin Concert Hall on Thursday.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/17/nyregion/17ROUTINE2/17ROUTINE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 457, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/17/nyregion/17ROUTINE2/17ROUTINE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 457}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/17/nyregion/17ROUTINE2/17ROUTINE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 779, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/17/nyregion/17ROUTINE2/17ROUTINE2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1558, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/17/nyregion/17ROUTINE2/17ROUTINE2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/17/nyregion/17ROUTINE2/17ROUTINE2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/17/nyregion/17ROUTINE2/17ROUTINE2-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Music Upstairs and Downstairs', 'kicker': 'Sunday Routine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Music Upstairs and Downstairs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dinnerstein, Simone', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Robbins, Liz', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Park Slope (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-16T02:36:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liz Robbins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robbins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b342295-1a34-58e2-9491-72b65df3a12c', 'word_count': 708, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b342295-1a34-58e2-9491-72b65df3a12c'}, {'abstract': 'An Army general and his wife, an Army colonel, talk about their 30 years of marriage, through two children and six deployments.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/15/still-together-30-years-and-6-deployments-later/', 'snippet': 'An Army general and his wife, an Army colonel, talk about their 30 years of marriage, through two children and six deployments.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Maj. Gen. Kenneth Dahl is a deputy commanding general for United States forces in Afghanistan, stationed in Kabul. His current assignment is to oversee the withdrawal of troops from the country, as well as to prepare for the removal of all military equipment and weaponry. From 2010 to 2011, he was stationed in Kandahar, and before that, from 2005 to 2006, he served in Iraq.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Still Together, 30 Years and 6 Deployments Later', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Military Academy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fort Dr