ml', 'snippet': 'Read an excerpt of the book.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Prologue1899', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Excerpt From ‘Fever’ by Mary Beth Keane', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Fever (Book)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-16T03:56:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mary Beth Keane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mary', 'middlename': 'Beth', 'lastname': 'Keane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/11f3bb1c-22b1-59ba-a4ef-4f26fad322c3', 'word_count': 4253, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11f3bb1c-22b1-59ba-a4ef-4f26fad322c3'}, {'abstract': 'In New York City, where the poverty rate has remained steady for a decade, Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg’s efforts to limit the size of sugary drinks ignore a much larger problem.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/17/nyregion/in-obesity-fight-poverty-is-patient-zero.html', 'snippet': 'In New York City, where the poverty rate has remained steady for a decade, Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg’s efforts to limit the size of sugary drinks ignore a much larger problem.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Under the category “Summer Rentals That Have Gone Terribly Wrong,” there are perhaps few parallels to the experience of Charles Henry Warren, a Manhattan banker who, in 1906, took a house in Oyster Bay on Long Island’s North Shore. By the end of the season, Mr. Warren’s young daughter had developed typhoid. She was soon followed in illness by Mr. Warren’s wife, a second daughter, two maids and a gardener. At the time, typhoid, a bacterial illness spread through contaminated food and water, was largely a disease of the urban poor. The property’s owner, George Thompson, concerned that the house, on which he relied for rental income, would become associated with tenement filth in the minds of wealthy New Yorkers, invited a sanitary engineer to determine the source of the outbreak.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/17/nyregion/17BIG_SPAN/17BIG-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/17/nyregion/17BIG_SPAN/17BIG-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/17/nyregion/17BIG_SPAN/17BIG-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/17/nyregion/17BIG_SPAN/17BIG-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/17/nyregion/17BIG_SPAN/17BIG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/17/nyregion/17BIG_SPAN/17BIG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/17/nyregion/17BIG_SPAN/17BIG-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Obesity Epidemic, Poverty Is an Ignored Contagion', 'kicker': 'Big City', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Obesity Fight, Poverty Is Patient Zero', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Obesity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poverty', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Fever (Book)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Typhoid', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soft Drinks', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-16T04:09:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ginia Bellafante', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ginia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bellafante', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/88b0c601-32d5-5a81-bbfe-d84148e07584', 'word_count': 856, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88b0c601-32d5-5a81-bbfe-d84148e07584'}, {'abstract': 'While flamenco remains a quintessential component of Spanish culture, its economic sustainability relies increasingly on foreigners, who flock to Andalusia to learn the dance and its music.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/16/world/europe/flamencos-foreign-saviors.html', 'snippet': 'While flamenco remains a quintessential component of Spanish culture, its economic sustainability relies increasingly on foreigners, who flock to Andalusia to learn the dance and its music.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEVILLE, Spain — Alicia Márquez raises her arms high above her head to get her students to look up while they stamp their feet. She claps her hands hard to keep them in rhythm. To teach flamenco these days here in the epicenter of the dance, she finds she must rely more on showing than telling: Though the 10 women in her class this morning are all accomplished dancers in their 20s and 30s, only one is Spanish.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Flamenco’s Foreign Saviors', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Outsiders Breathe Life Into a Spanish Art Form', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flamenco (Dance)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-16T04:10:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Raphael Minder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Raphael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Minder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/98832db5-6742-5b6d-bcc2-586b8099c8b3', 'word_count': 1089, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98832db5-6742-5b6d-bcc2-586b8099c8b3'}, {'abstract': 'Pope Francis’s past; snakes as Irish economic barometer; treason accusation in Russia; and Bolshoi director recovers.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/16/iht-quick-read-march-15-2/', 'snippet': 'Pope Francis’s past; snakes as Irish economic barometer; treason accusation in Russia; and Bolshoi director recovers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEWS Reacting with unusual swiftness, the Vatican on Friday rejected any suggestion that Pope Francis of Argentina was implicated in his country’s so-called Dirty War during the 1970s, tackling the issue just two days after the pontiff’s election. On a day when Francis delivered a warm address to his cardinals and continued to project humility, the Vatican seemed intent on quickly putting to rest questions about the pope’s past, dismissing them as opportunistic defamations from anticlerical leftists. Dan Wakin reports from Rome.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/world/europe/Vatican-1/Vatican-1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 372, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/14/world/europe/Vatican-1/Vatican-1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 372}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/world/europe/Vatican-1/Vatican-1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 635, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/world/europe/Vatican-1/Vatican-1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1271, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/world/europe/Vatican-1/Vatican-1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/14/world/europe/Vatican-1/Vatican-1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/14/world/europe/Vatican-1/Vatican-1-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'IHT Quick Read: March 15', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-16T04:22:50+0000', 'do