other has a promising future after workers agreed to concessions that many consider to be onerous.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AMIENS, France — This is a tale of two factories, across the road from each other in north Amiens, both owned by the same company, Goodyear Dunlop Tires France. But one, Goodyear, is scheduled to close after the union workers there refused to agree to new working conditions, which they argued were too harsh and benefited only the company. The other, Dunlop, has a promising future, and the company treats it very differently.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/17/world/FRANCE/FRANCE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 371, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/17/world/FRANCE/FRANCE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 371}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/17/world/FRANCE/FRANCE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 634, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/17/world/FRANCE/FRANCE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1267, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/17/world/FRANCE/FRANCE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/17/world/FRANCE/FRANCE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/17/world/FRANCE/FRANCE-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 