y needs a refresher course in counting, the diagramless puzzles don’t give me the satisfaction I look for in solving. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Variety: Do Your Diagramless', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-16T16:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/524890bb-ec28-5013-8f8c-651492f25cf8', 'word_count': 289, 'uri': 'nyt://article/524890bb-ec28-5013-8f8c-651492f25cf8'}, {'abstract': 'The new charter is meant to resolve some of the problems that have kept Zimbabwe mired in crisis, but critics say it leaves the president’s powers undiluted.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/17/world/africa/zimbabwe-votes-on-new-constitution.html', 'snippet': 'The new charter is meant to resolve some of the problems that have kept Zimbabwe mired in crisis, but critics say it leaves the president’s powers undiluted.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HARARE, Zimbabwe — Batsi Munyaka, 27, an unemployed mechanic, had not read the document that could govern his nation for decades to come. But he said he was tired of trying to cobble together a living with little ventures that did not add up to much, and he hoped that a new Constitution, whatever its provisions, could help get Zimbabwe’s economy on track. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '2 Years Late, Zimbabwe Votes on New Constitution', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '2 Years La