dolph, Eleanor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'QueensWay (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parks and Other Recreation Areas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Railroads', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-16T17:39:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eleanor Randolph', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eleanor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Randolph', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b52386d-761a-5cb9-bf22-c869a9310a11', 'word_count': 596, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b52386d-761a-5cb9-bf22-c869a9310a11'}, {'abstract': 'The Catholic Church is more persuasive on economic justice than on sexual morality. The new pope should put his focus there.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/17/opinion/sunday/bruni-beyond-the-bedroom.html', 'snippet': 'The Catholic Church is more persuasive on economic justice than on sexual morality. The new pope should put his focus there.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT was too much to hope that after the white smoke rose and the TV anchors began nervously filling time and the cameras lingered for what seemed an eternity on that balcony over St. Peter’s Square, the man who stepped onto it would be someone open to revisiting the most archaic, obsolete matters of Roman Catholic doctrine. The group electing him was assembled by the last two popes, both conservatives. Its choice was bound to be more carbon copy than new page.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit