Lakers as the only teams to record 21 or more wins in a row, the questions now become how long the team can keep the streak going.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/16/questions-of-vulnerability-as-heat-stay-hot/', 'snippet': 'With the Heat having joined the 2007-8 Rockets and the 1971-72 Lakers as the only teams to record 21 or more wins in a row, the questions now become how long the team can keep the streak going.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the Miami Heat to win their 21st consecutive game, they had to get through one of the few teams to win 20 in a row, the Milwaukee Bucks. Of course, the Bucks of this season are a far cry from the 1970-71 team that was led by a big three that rivals Miami’s: Lew Alcindor, Oscar Robertson and Bob Dandridge.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Questions of Vulnerability as Heat Stay Hot', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Payoff, And the Peril, Of Big Streaks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Heat', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-16T19:47:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Hoffman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoffman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ea02a30-575e-519f-b9ad-925db95314fb', 'word_count': 936, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ea02a30-575e-519f-b9ad-925db95314fb'}, {'abstract': 'People around the country celebrated the holiday with parades and green attire.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2013/03/16/us/20130317_PATRICKS.html', 'snippe