BERTS? Granted, I wasn’t big on Barbie dolls, but it seems like the kind of pop culture factoid I should have known.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Any Pun for Tennis?', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-16T22:00:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce148f61-69f8-5751-b571-4bf4c65b0fa7', 'word_count': 731, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce148f61-69f8-5751-b571-4bf4c65b0fa7'}, {'abstract': 'A new study found that a majority of high-achieving high school seniors from low-income families did not apply to any selective colleges.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2013/03/17/education/How-Top-Students-of-Different-Incomes-Apply-for-College.html', 'snippet': 'A new study found that a majority of high-achieving high school seniors from low-income families did not apply to any selective colleges.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new study found that a majority of high-achieving high school seniors from low-income families did not apply to any selective colleges.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Top Students of Different Incomes Apply for College', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-16T22:11:55+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_des