': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/17/g-o-p-leaders-unswayed-by-obamas-charm-offensive/', 'snippet': 'In television appearances, Republican leaders who hold the most sway over fiscal negotiations were holding firm in opposing President Obama’s proposal to raise new tax revenue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama appeared on Sunday to still be enjoying a bit of good karma from his extended outreach to Congress last week, but Republican leaders who hold the most sway over fiscal negotiations were holding firm in opposition to the president.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'G.O.P. Leaders Unswayed by Obama’s ‘Charm Offensive’', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-17T19:01:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Knowlton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Knowlton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/87a87092-3e31-5c68-8096-f02e4742d2db', 'word_count': 323, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87a87092-3e31-5c68-8096-f02e4742d2db'}, {'abstract': 'Empty brackets become a thing of the past today as the field of 68 is chosen for the 2013 men’s N.C.A.A. basketball tournament.', 'web_url': 'https://thequad.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/17/live-updates-and-analysis-selection-sunday/', 'snippet': 'Empty brackets become a thing of the past today as the field of 68 is chosen for the 2013 men’s N.C.A.A. basketball tournament.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Empty brackets become a thing of the past today as the field of 68 is chosen for the 2013 men’s N.C.A.A. basketball tournament. Mike Huguenin is providing live updates and analysis. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Highlights and Analysis: Selection Sunday', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'NCAA Basketball Championships (Men)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Collegiate Athletic Assn', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-17T19:08:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Huguenin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Huguenin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8a12c78-27c5-5c47-96b6-3394bf387aab', 'word_count': 2106, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8a12c78-27c5-5c47-96b6-3394bf387aab'}, {'abstract': 'Michael Moss’s “Salt Sugar Fat: How the Food Giants Hooked Us” looks at food manufacturers’ distortion of the American diet in favor of calorie-dense products that maximize “bliss.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/18/books/salt-sugar-fat-by-michael-moss.html', 'snippet': 'Michael Moss’s “Salt Sugar Fat: How the Food Giants Hooked Us” looks at food manufacturers’ distortion of the American diet in favor of calorie-dense products that maximize “bliss.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Americans eat 33 pounds of cheese and cheese products per year, per person, which is triple the consumption rate of the 1970s. Fans of Humboldt Fog and Cabot Clothbound Cheddar may hope this signals the return of the artisan producer, but Michael Moss gives all credit to mighty Kraft and the other food giants. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'cre