ame': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Mowbray', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mowbray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/da4325f4-9e5c-533c-9d0a-eda20b7eee34', 'word_count': 1131, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da4325f4-9e5c-533c-9d0a-eda20b7eee34'}, {'abstract': 'Alvin Ailey’s junior company, Ailey II, gamely performed its program “All New” in its first New York season under its new artistic director, Troy Powell.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/18/arts/dance/ailey-iis-all-new-at-the-ailey-citigroup-theater.html', 'snippet': 'Alvin Ailey’s junior company, Ailey II, gamely performed its program “All New” in its first New York season under its new artistic director, Troy Powell.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the Ailey Citigroup Theater last April, Troy Powell talked about having to fill a small woman’s big shoes. He was referring to his succeeding Sylvia Waters, who was stepping down after 38 years as the artistic director of Ailey II, Alvin Ailey American Dance Theater’s junior company. On Wednesday, when Ailey II opened its first New York season under Mr. Powell’s direction, he said that for himself and seven new dancers “everything is new, including my shoes.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/18/arts/ailey/ailey-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 378, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/18/arts/ailey/ailey-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 378}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/18/arts/ailey/ailey-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 644, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'l