South by Southwest festival, but lesser known acts still make up its core.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/18/arts/music/selling-stars-brands-and-baby-bands.html', 'snippet': 'Big names and big productions with corporate tie-ins were one thread at the South by Southwest festival, but lesser known acts still make up its core.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AUSTIN, Tex. — Two images linger from this year’s South by Southwest Music festival, which ended Sunday after five nights and days with hundreds of performances. One has been the major part of SXSW for all of its 27 years: sharing the crowded sidewalks with sleep-deprived but bright-eyed musicians toting their own equipment to the next gig. The other is more recent: a 62-foot-high outdoor stage built to resemble a snack-chip vending machine that turned into a six-story video billboard when it wasn’t showing live performances.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/18/arts/sxsw/sxsw-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 390, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/18/arts/sxsw/sxsw-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 390}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/18/arts/sxsw/sxsw-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 666, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/18/arts/sxsw/sxsw-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1332, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/18/arts/sxsw/sxsw-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/18/arts/sxsw/sxsw-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/18/arts/sxsw/sxsw-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Selling Stars, Brands and Baby Bands', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Selling Stars, Brands and Baby Bands', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'South by Southwest Music and Media Conference', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rap and Hip-Hop', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Austin (Tex)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-17T22:12:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b1c6285-3eea-5698-83c6-aab80ce5d527', 'word_count': 1328, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b1c6285-3eea-5698-83c6-aab80ce5d527'}, {'abstract': 'The New York theater company Clubbed Thumb has announced its lineup for the 18th annual Summerworks festival.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/18/theater/footnote.html', 'snippet': 'The New York theater company Clubbed Thumb has announced its lineup for the 18th annual Summerworks festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York theater company Clubbed Thumb has announced its lineup for the 18th annual Summerworks festival, which is set for May 24 to June 29 at the Wild Project in the East Village. The festival, which highlights original works by American playwrights, is to feature the three new plays; “Phoebe in Winter,” by Jen Silverman (“Crane Story”), “La Brea,” by Gregory S. Moss (“Billy Witch”) and Clare Barron’s “Baby Screams Miracle.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Footnote', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Footnote', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Clubbed Thumb', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-17T22:14:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2292bda-4160-58f9-9b5d-2a044fc5cd10', 'word_count': 72, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2292bda-4160-58f9-9b5d-2a044fc5cd10'}, {'abstract': 'After months and months of something passing for blessed calm in the euro zone, the bailout of Cypriot banks rekindles fears of instability in Italy and Spain.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/17/waiting-for-the-run-on-the-banks/', 'snippet': 'After months and months of something passing for blessed calm in the euro zone, the bailout of Cypriot banks rekindles fears of instability in Italy and Spain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The economics Nobel laureate Paul Krugman could not have been clearer about the dangers of forcing depositors in Cypriot banks to take a loss on their accounts. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/18/blogs/18RDV-cyprus-banks/18RDV-cyprus-banks-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 349, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/18/blogs/18RDV-cyprus-banks/18RDV-cyprus-banks-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 349}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/18/blogs/18RDV-cyprus-banks/18RDV-cyprus-banks-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 596, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/18/blogs/18RDV-cyprus-banks/18RDV-cyprus-banks-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1061, 'width': 1822, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/18/blogs/18RDV-cyprus-banks/18RDV-cyprus-banks-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/18/blogs/18RDV-cyprus-banks/18RDV-cyprus-banks-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/18/blogs/18RDV-cyprus-banks/18RDV-cyprus-banks-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Waiting for the Run on the Banks', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cyprus', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-17T22:20:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By The International Herald Tribune', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The International Herald Tribune'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/60a07320-714d-5776-b977-ac1d8ea353ff', 'word_count': 276, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60a07320-714d-5776-b977-ac1d8ea353ff'}, {'abstract': 'Concerns about the effects of the Federal Reserve’s stimulus policy can dilute the policy’s impact by causing investors to doubt that rates will remain low.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/18/business/economy/federal-reserve-expected-to-continue-stimulus-tries-to-reassure-investors.html', 'snippet': 'Concerns about the effects of the Federal Reserve’s stimulus policy can dilute the policy’s impact by causing investors to doubt that rates will remain low.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Each time in recent years that the Federal Reserve has paused in its efforts to stimulate the economy, it has come to regret the decision as premature. Its leading officials say the recovery has been slower as a consequence of those pauses. It is a mistake they do not want to repeat.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/18/business/fed/fed-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 397, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/18/business/fed/fed-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 397}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/18/business/fed/fed-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 678, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/18/business/fed/fed-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1355, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank'