'_id': 'nyt://article/e87fe875-51ed-5f45-9b18-1e3f52d8fac1', 'word_count': 1316, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e87fe875-51ed-5f45-9b18-1e3f52d8fac1'}, {'abstract': 'Talks with the musicians, who went on strike on Wednesday, mainly over wage issues, broke down on Sunday evening.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/17/san-francisco-symphonys-east-coast-tour-is-canceled-as-labor-talks-break-down/', 'snippet': 'Talks with the musicians, who went on strike on Wednesday, mainly over wage issues, broke down on Sunday evening.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The San Francisco Symphony has announced that negotiations over a new contract with its musicians have broken down with the players’ rejection of a federal mediator’s proposal for a cooling-off period. As a result, the orchestra’s East Coast tour, which was to have included concerts at Carnegie Hall on Wednesday and Thursday as well as concerts in Newark on Friday and Washington on Saturday, has been canceled.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'San Francisco Symphony’s East Coast Tour Is Canceled as Labor Talks Break Down', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Strikes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Francisco Symphony', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-18T00:35:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James R. Oestreich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Oestreich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b76ed7e5-29a7-5647-ae31-4e4c8925c260', 'word_count': 140, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b76ed7e5-29a7-5647-ae31-4e4c8925c260'}, {'abstract': 'As lawmakers struggle to narrow the government’s deficit, every dollar taken from a grant program counts as a budget cut, while every dollar taken from a tax credit is instead a tax increase.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/18/business/economy/taxes-or-spending-budget-fight-in-congress-focuses-on-a-distinction.html', 'snippet': 'As lawmakers struggle to narrow the government’s deficit, every dollar taken from a grant program counts as a budget cut, while every dollar taken from a tax credit is instead a tax increase.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — In a low-income neighborhood in Bozeman, Mont., taxpayers helped pay for the construction of a grocery store, Town and Country Foods. They are doing the same in New Orleans, with federal dollars helping to build new groceries, including a Whole Foods, in an area still suffering after Hurricane Katrina.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/18/business/jp-tax-1/jp-tax-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 392, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/18/business/jp-tax-1/jp-tax-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 392}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/18/business/jp-tax-1/jp-tax-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 669, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/18/business/jp-tax-1/jp-tax-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1339, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/18/business/jp-tax-1/jp-tax-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/18/business/jp-tax-1/jp-tax-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/18/business/jp-tax-1/jp-tax-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tax Credits or Spending? Labels, but in Congress, Fighting Words', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tax Credits or Spending? Labels. But in Congress, Fighting Words.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Credits, Deductions and Exemptions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lowrey, Annie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corporate Taxes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-18T00:39:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Annie Lowrey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Annie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lowrey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/99f99fee-cedc-5e9f-be48-c6025b8397cd', 'word_count': 1171, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99f99fee-cedc-5e9f-be48-c6025b8397cd'}, {'abstract': 'Louisville Coach Rick Pitino routinely reinforces one message: knock the ball away. The Cardinals’ trapping defense helped them earn the overall No. 1 seed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/18/sports/ncaabasketball/deflections-at-the-core-of-louisvilles-smothering-defense.html', 'snippet': 'Louisville Coach Rick Pitino routinely reinforces one message: knock the ball away. The Cardinals’ trapping defense helped them earn the overall No. 1 seed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Louisville Coach Rick Pitino has his assistants chart deflections whenever his team takes the court, whether for practice or for games. The totals are collected and posted, and Pitino reinforces the message every day, every hour, practically every minute through the season: stay active on defense, keep your hands busy, knock the ball away. At Louisville, deflections form the foundation for the team’s swarming defense.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/18/sports/MIDWESTlouisville/MIDWESTlouisville-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 393, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/18/sports/MIDWESTlouisville/MIDWESTlouisville-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 393}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/18/sports/MIDWESTlouisville/MIDWESTlouisville-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 671, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/18/sports/MIDWESTlouisville/MIDWESTlouisville-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1341, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/18/sports/MIDWESTlouisville/MID