Matt Flegenheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flegenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/97891a33-40db-5bc6-8b12-48b3c712ba07', 'word_count': 1111, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97891a33-40db-5bc6-8b12-48b3c712ba07'}, {'abstract': 'Even with the Helms amendment, foreign aid money could be used to provide abortions to victims of rape.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/18/opinion/abortion-and-women-overseas.html', 'snippet': 'Even with the Helms amendment, foreign aid money could be used to provide abortions to victims of rape.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Each year some 47,000 women around the world die as a result of unsafe abortions. Efforts to reduce that toll are severely hampered by the Helms amendment, which was originally enacted in 1973 and restricts the use of United States foreign aid money to finance abortions overseas, even in places where abortion is legal.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cruelty to Women Overseas', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cruelty to Women Overseas', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Aid', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-18T01:06:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/f96b5857-d1a4-56bb-98ad-9ee7f4109e9f', 'word_count': 322, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f96b5857-d1a4-56bb-98ad-9ee7f4109e9f'}, {'abstract': 'Thousands of people are needlessly dying of cholera while groups that promised to help, particularly the U.N., abdicate responsibility.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/18/opinion/a-worsening-haitian-tragedy.html', 'snippet': 'Thousands of people are needlessly dying of cholera while groups that promised to help, particularly the U.N., abdicate responsibility.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The aid group Doctors Without Borders said last Tuesday that the cholera crisis in Haiti was getting worse, for the most unnecessary and appalling of reasons: a lack of money and basic medical supplies. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Worsening Haitian Tragedy', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Worsening Haitian Tragedy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Haiti', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cholera', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Humanitarian Aid', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-18T01:06:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/6928d9f9-9303-5db8-a1e1-6d90007e7a23', 'word_count': 338, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6928d9f9-9303-5db8-a1e1-6d90007e7a23'}, {'abstract': 'South Korea’s security would not be improved by developing its own nuclear weapons.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/18/opinion/no-nukes-on-the-korean-peninsula.html', 'snippet': 'South Korea’s security would not be improved by developing its own nuclear weapons.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s little wonder that South Koreans are thinking about ways to defend themselves, given North Korea’s bizarre and dangerous behavior. The North has recently launched a long-range rocket and conducted its third nuclear test. It has also unleashed a barrage of apocalyptic threats, including potentially launching “pre-emptive nuclear strikes” on Seoul and the United States and declaring the 1953 Korean War armistice nullified. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Nukes on the Korean Peninsula', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Nukes on the Korean Peninsula', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-18T01:09:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e7bd42e-2142-5011-a316-4514e07c18e3', 'word_count': 415, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e7bd42e-2142-5011-a316-4514e07c18e3'}, {'abstract': 'Did we learn anything from Iraq?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/18/opinion/krugman-marches-of-folly.html', 'snippet': 'Did we learn anything from Iraq?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ten years ago, America invaded Iraq; somehow, our political class decided that we should respond to a terrorist attack by making war on a regime 