orrections appearing in print on March 18, 2013.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/18/pageoneplus/corrections-march-18-2013.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on March 18, 2013.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRONT PAGE', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: March 18, 2013', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-18T04:04:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/232b59d5-348b-5a76-85e7-bdff35f061b6', 'word_count': 285, 'uri': 'nyt://article/232b59d5-348b-5a76-85e7-bdff35f061b6'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the Day for Monday, March 18.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/18/pageoneplus/quotation-of-the-day-for-monday-march-18.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the Day for Monday, March 18.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I remember thinking, ‘Cops, I need the cops. He’s going to kill me in my own house. I’m going to die!’”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day for Monday, March 18', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-18T04:06:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/4fa8a91b-19be-5cf9-ae9b-7a2f76e74730', 'word_count': 33, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4fa8a91b-19be-5cf9-ae9b-7a2f76e74730'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/18/arts/television/whats-on-monday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '10 P.M. (TMC) MY LEFT FOOT (1989) Daniel Day-Lewis, in his first Oscar-winning role, portrays Christy Brown (1932-81), who was born in Dublin with cerebral palsy and learned to write and paint using the only limb he could control, his left foot. Brenda Fricker, who also won an Oscar, and Ray McAnally play Christy’s parents; Ruth McCabe (above, with Mr. Day-Lewis) is the young woman he falls in love with and eventually marries; and Fiona Shaw is the doctor who largely facilitates his education in what Vincent Canby, writing in The New York Times, called “an intelligent, beautifully acted adaptation” of Mr. Brown’s first book, directed by Jim Sheridan. But “though ‘My Left Foot’ is blunt and tough in its presentation of Christy’s handicaps, it avoids any direct criticism of the handicapped world into which he is born, one in which his mother spends most of her time being pregnant, in which poverty is as likely to make the spirit ugly as beautiful, and in which the church always has the last word.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Monday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-18T04:15:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/57890a6f-2470-56f5-acdb-dac8d7cb6f46', 'word_count': 731, 'uri': 'nyt://article/57890a6f-2470-56f5-acdb-dac8d7cb6f46'}, {'abstract': 'The slumping Rangers trail their metropolitan rivals, the Devils and the Islanders, while the Pittsburgh Penguins lead the Eastern Conference after beating Boston.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/18/sports/hockey/rangers-in-an-odd-place-with-penguins-in-first.html', 'snippet': 'The slumping Rangers trail their metropolitan rivals, the Devils and the Islanders, while the Pittsburgh Penguins lead the Eastern Conference after beating Boston.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After a trip that ended with three straight losses, the Rangers occupy 10th place in the Eastern Conference with only 21 games to play. They face two games in the next two nights from a perspective they have not seen in more than five years. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'While Sliding Rangers Look Up in Standings, the Surging Penguins Look Down', 'kicker': 'N.H.L. Roundup', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'While Sliding Rangers Look Up in Standings, the Surging Penguins Look Down', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klein, Jeff Z', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Rangers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Jersey Devils', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Islanders', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tortorella, John', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pittsburgh Penguins', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Bruins', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Capitals', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Buffalo Sabres', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-18T04:16:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4900a397-27ce-5170-924c-1176d2fe14b9', 'word_count': 652, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4900a397-27ce-5170-924c-1176d2fe14b9'}, {'abstract': 'The Dutch team’s pitchers are largely from the Netherlands, and its star position players come from Curaçao and Aruba.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/18/sports/baseball/netherlands-a-surprise-semifinalist-in-the-world-baseball-classic.html', 'snippet': 'The Dutch team’s pitchers are largely from the Netherlands, and its star position players come from Curaçao and Aruba.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO — The goal of the World Baseball Classic has never been to prove which nation is best at baseball. This is not that kind of sport. Small samples can yield misleading conclusions. The validity of World Series results comes largely from the six-month grind just to get there.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/18/sports/KEPNER/KEPNER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/18/sports/KEPNER/KEPNER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 402}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/18/sports/KEPNER/KEPNER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 686, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/18/sports/KEPNER/KEPNER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1371, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtyp