'abstract': 'Despite the march of time and civilization, small groups of Europeans still practice ancient pagan rites to mark the passing of seasons.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/18/where-the-wild-things-are/', 'snippet': 'Despite the march of time and civilization, small groups of Europeans still practice ancient pagan rites to mark the passing of seasons.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Charles Fréger was fascinated by what the human race lost over the millenniums when it evolved from hunter-gather to farmer and, eventually, urban dweller. After learning that there were Europeans who continued ancient pagan rites of celebrating the winter solstice and the beginning of spring, he set out to examine what traditions faded as people became more civilized. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Where the Wild Things Are', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pagans and Paganism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yossi Milo Gallery', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-18T09:00:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Estrin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Estrin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc9de106-7b19-518e-8c69-3b5156b09863', 'word_count': 449, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc9de106-7b19-518e-8c69-3b5156b09863'}, {'abstract': 'The Italian ambassador has been barred from traveling outside India for another week.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/18/indias-supreme-court-extends-restrictions-on-italian-ambassador/', 'snippet': 'The Italian amba