ies and Exchange Commission would be enough to cripple some hedge funds. But SAC saw the positive in the penalty, which settles two insider trading lawsuits brought by the government, DealBook’s Peter Lattman writes. The $15 billion hedge fund said in a statement that the settlements were “a substantial step toward resolving all outstanding regulatory matters.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'SAC Looks on the Bright Side', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-18T11:40:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7920ecb8-6e63-5181-9e76-db8733086875', 'word_count': 1652, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7920ecb8-6e63-5181-9e76-db8733086875'}, {'abstract': 'A summary of what’s on today’s editorial page.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/18/opinion-report-treating-alzheimers/', 'snippet': 'A summary of what’s on today’s editorial page.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From the editorial page', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Opinion Report: Treating Alzheimer’s', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-18T11:47:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id':