f Phuket, Thailand, offers privacy like no other.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/18/thai-modern/', 'snippet': 'A secluded new beach resort on the western coast of Phuket, Thailand, offers privacy like no other.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rather than rooms, the Naka hotel is made up of 94 minimalist glass-and-stone pods, elevated and scattered pell-mell among tropical almond trees in this secluded new beach resort on the western coast of Phuket, Thailand. Each unit comes with a private pool and a cantilevered bedroom that juts out 20 feet toward the Andaman Sea. Rates from about $1,000; designhotels.com.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Thai Modern', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Phuket (Thailand)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-18T13:01:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Magazine', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/73dcef91-6c2e-554b-8f11-ab4eccfa2f23', 'word_count': 60, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73dcef91-6c2e-554b-8f11-ab4eccfa2f23'}, {'abstract': 'The Times has done some great work on the issue of poverty. But is it enough, given the depth of the problem?', 'web_url': 'https://publiceditor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/18/a-new-focus-on-poverty-raises-a-question-about-times-coverage/', 'snippet': 'The Times has done some great work on the issue of poverty. But is it enough, given the depth of the problem?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Poverty was in the news last week, with the coverage of Pope Francis’ attention to poor people worldwide, particularly those in his home country of Argentina. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Focus on Poverty Raises a Question About Times Coverage', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poverty', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-18T13:05:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaret Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/159af2b3-be6a-5565-b8e9-749cfbfc00bf', 'word_count': 723, 'uri': 'nyt://article/159af2b3-be6a-5565-b8e9-749cfbfc00bf'}, {'abstract': 'Just as pressure was easing on Europe’s financial sector, the situation in Cyprus has created chaos, sending bank shares tumbling and raising concerns that other institutions could face similar problems.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/03/18/cyprus-bailout-puts-new-pressure-on-european-banks/', 'snippet': 'Just as pressure was easing on Europe’s financial sector, the situation in Cyprus has created chaos, sending bank shares tumbling and raising concerns that other institutions could face similar problems.', 'lead_paragraph': '12:14 p.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cyprus Bailout Puts New Pressure on Europe’s Banks', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-18T13:07:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/508253a2-9c5f-5179-87b8-cb582c401acb', 'word_count': 906, 'uri': 'nyt://article/508253a2-9c5f-5179-87b8-cb582c401acb'}, {'abstract': 'The decision to unwind ST-Ericsson brings a measure of finality to an attempt to build a European semiconductor business to compete with American and Asian market leaders.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/19/technology/ericsson-and-st-microelectronics-to-dissolve-venture.html', 'snippet': 'The decision to unwind ST-Ericsson brings a measure of finality to an attempt to build a European semiconductor business to compete with American and Asian market leaders.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — Ericsson and STMicroelectronics announced plans on Monday to dissolve their unprofitable four-year-old Swiss venture, ST-Ericsson, a move that may eliminate 1,600 jobs worldwide.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/business/Ericsson/Ericsson-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 432, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/19/business/Ericsson/Ericsson-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 432}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/business/Ericsson/Ericsson-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 737, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/business/Ericsson/Ericsson-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1474, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/business/Ericsson/Ericsson-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/19/business/Ericsson/Ericsson-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/business/Ericsson/Ericsson-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ericsson and ST Microelectronics to Dissolve Venture', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ericsson and Partner Will End a Chip Venture in Europe', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Brien, Kevin J", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Telefonaktiebolaget L M Ericsson', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Chips', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'STMicroelectronics NV', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-18T13:07:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': "By Kevin J. O'Brien", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': "O'Brien", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b17f5401-cf98-58d7-9edd-2495ed1f2941', 'word_count': 606, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b17f5401-cf98-58d7-9edd-2495ed1f2941'}, {'abstract': 'The Senate report and hearing on JPMorgan Chase’s $6 billion trading loss provides a portrait of a bank that went right to the edge of acceptable practices, and may have even stepped over the line.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/03/18/senate-report-on-jpmorgan-loss-may-provide-fresh-evidence/', 'snippet': 'The Senate report and hearing on JPMorgan Chase’s $6 billion trading loss provides a portrait of a bank that went right to the edge of acceptable practices, and may have even stepped over the line.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Senate report and hearing on JPMorgan Chase’s multibillion-dollar trading loss provides a portrait of a bank that went right to the edge of acceptable practices, and may have even stepped over the line. The questions now are what type of enforcement action the bank could face, and whether any individuals will be ensnared by the case.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Senate Report on JPMorgan Loss May Provide Fresh Evidence', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dimon, James', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Levin, Carl M', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JPMorgan Chase & Company', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-18T13:07:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter J. Henning', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Henning', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/20a6c4b2-6ee3-51ca-a033-e4ac707df321', 'word_count': 1128, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20a6c4b2-6ee3-51ca-a033-e4ac707df321'}, {'abstract': 'The Justice Department investigates claims of bribery at The Wall Street Journal, Barry Diller’s Aereo could change the game in television, and the case of Matthew Keys highlights problems with hacking laws.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/18/the-breakfast-meeting-bribery-inquiry-at-the-journal-and-taking-aim-at-cable-tv/', 'snippet': 'The Justice Department investigates claims of bribery at The Wall Street Journal, Barry Diller’s Aereo could change the game in television, and the case of Matthew Keys highlights problems with hacking laws.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A United States government inquiry into News Corporation broadened last year after the Justice Department investigated claims that Wall Street Journal employees in China bribed local officials with gifts in exchange for information, Christine Haughney writes. The Journal broke the news of the investigation on Sunday. Paula Keve, a spokeswoman for The Journal, said that the company was conducting its own investigation and had found no evidence of impropriety. The bribery accusations came out of a broader investigation into News Corporation’s practices, and Ms. Keve suggested that the claims had been made to discredit The Journal’s reporting.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting: Bribery Inquiry at The Journal, and Taking Aim at Cable TV', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-18T13:19:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel E. Slotnik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Slotnik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8df63d85-b6c8-5234-bee3-bb26ab337fe4', 'word_count': 616, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8df63d85-b6c8-5234-bee3-bb26ab337fe4'}, {'abstract': 'What is it about bankers and island nations?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/18/island-nightmares/', 'snippet': 'What is it about bankers and island nations?', 'lead_paragraph': 'What is it about islands around Europe’s periphery? Is there some peculiar psychological thing about proximity plus the illusion of isolation that makes them turn themselves into havens for runaway banks? Inquiring minds want to know.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Island Nightmares', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-18T13:25:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f68eaaa3-fceb-5b91-a07f-2d1dd11d29ca', 'word_count': 516, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f68eaaa3-fceb-5b91-a07f-2d1dd11d29ca'}, {'abstract': 'Hopeful signs coming out of the Big Ten? A North Carolina-Kansas matchup? One thing is certain: Kentucky will not be around to defend its title.', 'web_url': 'https://thequad.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/18/leading-off-selection-science-or-a-dartboard/', 'snippet': 'Hopeful signs coming out of the Big Ten? A North Carolina-Kansas matchup? One thing is certain: Kentucky will not be around to defend its title.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Normally, one of the best things about N.C.A.A. tournament week is its\xa0 democracy. No, not every one of the tournament’s 68 teams has an equal chance to win the title, but every single person in your circle of acquaintances has a roughly equal chance to win your N.C.A.A. pool. Because no matter how much the rabid basketball fans think they know about R.P.I. and strength of schedule and just how well Coach A does against Coach K, once the tournament starts, all that knowledge has as much to do with picking winners as it does forecasting an election in Burma. The bloke who picks against Notre Dame because it wore those horrific lime green jerseys in the Big East tournament? Our money’s on him.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/sports/ncaabasketball/19leadingpic/19leadingpic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 876, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/19/sports/ncaabasketball/19leadingpic/19leadingpic-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 876}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/sports/ncaabasketball/19leadingpic/19leadingpic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 702, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/sports/ncaabasketball/19leadingpic/19leadingpic-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1403, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/sports/ncaabasketball/19leadingpic/19leadingpic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/19/sports/ncaabasketball/19leadingpic/19leadingpic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/sports/ncaabasketball/19leadingpic/19leadingpic-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Leading Off: Selection Science or a Dartboard?', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Atlantic Ten Conference', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Big East Conference', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Big Ten Conference', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Iowa State University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'James Madison University', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Collegiate Athletic Assn', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Arizona', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Kentucky', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Notre Dame', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-18T13:36:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/752544a9-36dc-52ea-b9ff-40d257d07ac7', 'word_count': 636, 'uri': 'nyt://article/752544a9-36dc-52ea-b9ff-40d257d07ac7'}, {'abstract': 'Parents cite safety concerns in their decisions not to seek out the HPV vaccine, but unspoken factors like convenience may also get in the way.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/18/resistance-to-hpv-vaccines-needs-new-solutions/', 'snippet': 'Parents cite safety concerns in their decisions not to seek out the HPV vaccine, but unspoken factors like convenience may also get in the way.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Centers for Disease Control and Prevention recommend three vaccinations for preteens and teenagers: a booster for tetanus toxoid, diphtheria toxoid and acellular pertussis vaccine (Tdap) given at 11-12 years; quadrivalent meningococcal conjugate vaccine (MCV4), with a first dose at 11-12 and a follow-up at 16-18; and human papillomavirus vaccine (HPV), given in three doses over a six-month period to boys and girls 11-12.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Resistance to HPV Vaccines Needs New Solutions', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-18T13:44:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0f6bf5f-edd3-590f-b939-17724ed95556', 'word_count': 932, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0f6bf5f-edd3-590f-b939-17724ed95556'}, {'abstract': 'The Royal Bank of Canada has hired Michal Katz and Michael Carter as co-heads of its United States technology investment banking group, and Erik-Jaap Molenaar as a technology deal maker.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/03/18/royal-bank-of-canada-hires-new-co-heads-of-u-s-technology-banking/', 'snippet': 'The Royal Bank of Canada has hired Michal Katz and Michael Carter as co-heads of its United States technology investment banking group, and Erik-Jaap Molenaar as a technology deal maker.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Royal Bank of Canada said on Monday that it had hired Michal Katz and Michael Carter as co-heads of its United States technology investment banking group. The bank also hired Erik-Jaap Molenaar as a managing director in technology mergers and acquisitions. All three come from Barclays, and had previously worked at Lehman Brothers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Royal Bank of Canada Hires Co-Heads of U.S. Technology Banking', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Royal Bank of Canada', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-18T13:54:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9ec39f2-c2f4-554c-a27d-7cbcc1aab3e5', 'word_count': 54, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9ec39f2-c2f4-554c-a27d-7cbcc1aab3e5'}, {'abstract': 'Building Blocks: In a $9.8 million renovation project, the 47-year-old Queens Central Library in Jamaica is being transformed into a more appealing space.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/18/queens-central-library-opens-wider/', 'snippet': 'Building Blocks: In a $9.8 million renovation project, the 47-year-old Queens Central Library in Jamaica is being transformed into a more appealing space.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s a mystery at first. The youngsters on the computers in the children’s center adjoining the Queens Central Library appear to be squatting on floor cushions, but their legs are nowhere to be seen. In a moment, it grows clear. They’re seated at shallow wells scooped into the floor so there’s no danger of falling off their chairs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/11/blogs/20130307QueensPublicEmbed3/20130307QueensPublicEmbed3-a