Lloyd C. Blankfein, the chief executive of Goldman Sachs, has gained a daughter-in-law.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Blankfein Wedding', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blankfein, Lloyd C', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-18T14:23:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0f94185d-f1de-5ebb-9ee8-ecd892f13408', 'word_count': 284, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0f94185d-f1de-5ebb-9ee8-ecd892f13408'}, {'abstract': 'For women with ectopic pregnancies, surgery to remove a fallopian tube did not affect the ability to become pregnant later any more than more conservative treatments for the condition.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/18/ectopic-pregnancy-treatments-preserve-fertility/', 'snippet': 'For women with ectopic pregnancies, surgery to remove a fallopian tube did not affect the ability to become pregnant later any more than more conservative treatments for the condition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Each of the three main treatments for ectopic pregnancy — a condition in which a fetus develops outside the uterus, often in the fallopian tube — appears to be equally effective in preserving a women’s ability to become pregnant in the future, a new study found.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/02/health/well_childbirth/well_childbirth-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 214, 'width': 215, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/02/health/well_childbirth/well_childbirth-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 214, 'width': 215, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/02/health/well_childbirth/well_childbirth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/07/02/health/well_childbirth/well_childbirth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/02/health/well_childbirth/well_childbirth-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ectopic Pregnancy Treatments Preserve Fertility', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pregnancy and Childbirth', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surgery and Surgeons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-18T14:25:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Bakalar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bakalar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a3698df-c74f-5dda-8fe3-4d79059d7d92', 'word_count': 252, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a3698df-c74f-5dda-8fe3-4d79059d7d92'}, {'abstract': 'Louisville is the nominal favorite to win the tournament despite its tough draw, according to the FiveThirtyEight forecast. Still, it has only a 23 percent chance of doing so, just ahead of Indiana at 20 percent.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/18/parity-in-n-c-a-a-means-no-commanding-favorite/', 'snippet': 'Louisville is the nominal favorite to win the tournament despite its tough draw, according to the FiveThirtyEight forecast. Still, it has only a 23 percent chance of doing so, just ahead of Indiana at 20 percent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even before the N.C.A.A. men’s basketball tournament bracket was announced on Sunday, there was plenty of discussion about how much parity there was in this year’s field. The chatter only increased after Louisville, the No. 1 overall seed, was placed in a brutally tough Midwest region that also includes Duke and Michigan State.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Parity in N.C.A.A. Means No Commanding Favorite', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On the Road to a Championship, the Journey Counts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-18T14:26:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c389f217-8d7e-5094-8301-71937cab781a', 'word_count': 1489, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c389f217-8d7e-5094-8301-71937cab781a'}, {'abstract': 'A new book reminds us that accessible homes can also be beautiful.', 'web_url': 'https://newoldage.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/18/the-unobstructed-home/', 'snippet': 'A new book reminds us that accessible homes can also be beautiful.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The houses photographed for Deborah Pierce’s book, “The Accessible Home: Designing for All Ages & Abilities,” look so inviting that I want to move in. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Unobstructed Home', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elder Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Home Repairs and Improvements', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-18T14:42:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paula Span', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paula', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Span', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5522818d-c103-592f-88a9-4ece0ceb73a2', 'word_count': 574, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5522818d-c103-592f-88a9-4ece0ceb73a2'}, {'abstract': 'This hearty, high-protein combination shows up in countless cuisines – including Persian cooking, which inspired several of this week’s dishes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/18/health/beans-and-greens-a-power-couple-recipes-for-health.html', 'snippet': 'This hearty, high-protein combination shows up in countless cuisines – including Persian cooking, which inspired several of this week’s dishes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you’ve been a longtime follower of Recipes for Health, you know how much I like combining beans and greens. They make a good, nourishing couple and every peasant cuisine in the world seems to know this. It’s so easy to put together a hearty, high-protein one-dish meal rich in vitamins and minerals with these two foods as the focus.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/science/18recipehealth/18recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 386, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/19/science/18recipehealth/18recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 386}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/science/18recipehealth/18recipehealth-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 659, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/science/18recipehealth/18recipehealth-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1317, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/science/18recipehealth/18recipehealth-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/19/science/18recipehealth/18recipehealth-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/science/18recipehealth/18recipehealth-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Beans and Greens: A Power Couple', 'kicker': 'Recipes for Health', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beans', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-18T14:51:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martha Rose Shulman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martha', 'middlename': 'Rose', 'lastname': 'Shulman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'recipe', '_id': 'nyt://article/c67b9378-151a-532b-8935-ca68320abbcd', 'word_count': 931, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c67b9378-151a-532b-8935-ca68320abbcd'}, {'abstract': 'Why is the Small Business Administration asking General Electric to participate in small-business discussions?', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/18/a-small-business-office-is-accused-of-advocating-for-big-business/', 'snippet': 'Why is the Small Business Administration asking General Electric to participate in small-business discussions?', 'lead_paragraph': 'For decades, the Office of Advocacy, a bureau within the Small Business Administration, has worked behind the scenes to soften the impact of federal regulations on small companies. It is charged with, among other responsibilities, representing “the views and interests of small businesses before other federal agencies.” To learn how regulatory policies might affect small businesses, the office regularly convenes round-table discussions with its constituents.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Small-Business Office Is Accused of Advocating for Big Business', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN CHEMISTRY COUNCIL', 'ran