 official authority, not a random soldier.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week, The Times will feature reflections on the 10th anniversary of the invasion. We invite anyone who was directly affected by the invasion to submit their essays via atwar@nytimes.com. Please keep pieces to 500 words. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How One Soldier Learned the Iraq War Was On', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003-11)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Missiles and Missile Defense Systems', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blitzer, Wolf', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Marine Corps', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kuwait', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-18T19:17:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Don Gomez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Don', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gomez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8b56a77-edc0-5b55-8d33-e803250010ec', 'word_count': 1051, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8b56a77-edc0-5b55-8d33-e803250010ec'}, {'abstract': 'After eight years of marriage and two kids, my husband and I are fighting over whether or not to have more children — and our battles are revealing bigger divisions.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/18/i-want-more-children-he-doesnt/', 'snippet': 'After eight years of marriage and two kids, my husband and I are fighting over whether or not to have more children — and our battles are revealing bigger divisions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When we were first married, my husband and I talked about “the big stuff.” We discussed religion and politics; we respected the differences in our opinions. We both wanted to raise children in New York City and remain united against the suburbs. With no red flags in sight, we began our union with confidence.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'I Want More Children; He Doesn’t', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pregnancy and Childbirth', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-18T19:17:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carinn Jade', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carinn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jade', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b937c614-b8c4-50e2-a444-fe244af3da73', 'word_count': 777, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b937c614-b8c4-50e2-a444-fe244af3da73'}, {'abstract': 'Some surgeons say anterior hip replacements, in which the incision is made at the front of the hip instead of through the buttocks or the side, result in decreased pain and faster recovery.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/18/faster-recovery-from-hip-surgery/', 'snippet': 'Some surgeons say anterior hip replacements, in which the incision is made at the front of the hip instead of through the buttocks or the side, result in decreased pain and faster recovery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Larry Kufel had always been an active man, tall and rangy, who worke