{'main': 'Bancroft Prize Awarded to Two Historians', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bancroft Prizes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Columbia University', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-18T19:25:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Schuessler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schuessler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/767a2d3b-827d-5e80-8127-2261a8781133', 'word_count': 112, 'uri': 'nyt://article/767a2d3b-827d-5e80-8127-2261a8781133'}, {'abstract': 'The crisis in Cyprus highlights the need for common European regimes on deposit insurance and on winding down failing banks, the author writes.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/03/18/the-lesson-from-cyprus/', 'snippet': 'The crisis in Cyprus highlights the need for common European regimes on deposit insurance and on winding down failing banks, the author writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Cyprus fiasco sets a high bar for the euro zone’s new banking union. The new superregulator might not have been able to stop the blowup, or to avoid losses for insured depositors. The clear lesson from the mess is the need for a procedure to wind down failing banks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Lesson From Cyprus', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deposit Insurance', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Monetary Union', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cyprus', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-18T19:25:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Unmack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Unmack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a15e0fa0-73b2-5029-9560-dc3984ee2941', 'word_count': 377, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a15e0fa0-73b2-5029-9560-dc3984ee2941'}, {'abstract': 'New Mexico won both the regular season and conference tournaments in the Mountain West, so why does no one know what to expect in the N.C.A.A. tournament?', 'web_url': 'https://thequad.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/18/what-to-make-of-new-mexico/', 'snippet': 'New Mexico won both the regular season and conference tournaments in the Mountain West, so why does no one know what to expect in the N.C.A.A. tournament?', 'lead_paragraph': 'We know what you are thinking. You do not know what to make of New Mexico. Overrated? Underrated? Final Four sleeper? Disappointing early exiter? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What to Make of New Mexico', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-18T19:29:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Branch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Branch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a49caa4f-ac4e-5084-bd15-5a56fcb9fcb3', 'word_count': 742, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a49caa4f-ac4e-5084-bd15-5a56fcb9fcb3'}, {'abstract': 'The bureau said it believed it had figured out who pulled off a famous theft of 13 works of art, valued at up to $500 million, from Boston’s Isabella Stewart Gardner Museum.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/19/us/fbi-says-it-has-clues-in-1990-isabella-stewart-gardner-museum-art-heist.html', 'snippet': 'The bureau said it believed it had figured out who pulled off a famous theft of 13 works of art, valued at up to $500 million, from Boston’s Isabella Stewart Gardner Museum.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was one of the most brazen art thefts in history. Two thieves, posing as police officers, prevailed on the night watchman at Boston’s Isabella Stewart Gardner Museum to let them in. After tying him up, and a leisurely 81 minutes, they walked out with 13 works of art and into the annals of one of the world’s most infamous unsolved crimes.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/18/us/stolen-works-slide-Z8QN-copy/stolen-works-slide-Z8QN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/18/us/stolen-works-slide-Z8QN-copy/stolen-works-slide-Z8QN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/18/us/stolen-works-slide-Z8QN-copy/stolen-works-slide-Z8QN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 649, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/18/us/stolen-works-slide-Z8QN-copy/stolen-works-slide-Z8QN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1297, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/18/us/stolen-works-slide-Z8QN-copy/stolen-works-slide-Z8QN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/18/us/stolen-works-slide-Z8QN-copy/stolen-works-slide-Z8QN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/18/us/stolen-works-slide-Z8QN-copy/stolen-works-slide-Z8QN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Effort in Boston to Catch 1990 Art Thieves', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A New Effort in Boston To Catch 1990 Art Thieves', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gardner, Isabella Stewart, Museum', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Investigation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-18T19:34:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katharine Q. Seelye and Tom Mashberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katharine', 'middlename': 'Q.', 'lastname': 'Seelye', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mashberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8baafd