s', 'value': 'Assn of Zoos & Aquariums', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Scripps Institution of Oceanography', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADULT EDUCATION', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-18T20:44:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Hanc', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hanc', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c21377ed-87f3-5562-b735-0f8827a4fa25', 'word_count': 1114, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c21377ed-87f3-5562-b735-0f8827a4fa25'}, {'abstract': 'The travel business has job openings — it added more jobs in 2012 than many other industries — and offers training through colleges and professional organizations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/19/education/travel-industry-offers-education-and-has-job-openings.html', 'snippet': 'The travel business has job openings — it added more jobs in 2012 than many other industries — and offers training through colleges and professional organizations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JOHN LINDER had a career as a senior human resources manager, but he wanted something more. “It was a good job, but I didn’t want to be in an office anymore or in a corporate environment,” he said. He also did not want extensive schooling, since he already had a master’s degree. \xa0He loved to travel, and knew his strong people skills would translate well. His answer: a two-week immersion course at the International Tour Management Institute. ', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/education/TRAVEL/TRAVEL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 405, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/19/education/TRAVEL/TRAVEL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 405}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/education/TRAVEL/TRAVEL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 691, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/education/TRAVEL/TRAVEL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1383, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/education/TRAVEL/TRAVEL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/19/education/TRAVEL/TRAVEL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/education/TRAVEL/TRAVEL-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Tourism, Classes Can Open Doors', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Tourism, Classes Can Open Doors', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Careers and Professions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mohn, Tanya', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hotels and Travel Lodgings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vocational Training', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-18T20:44:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tanya Mohn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tanya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mohn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/162dfaae-d575-5e7e-b083-1275202b6263', 'word_count': 775, 'uri': 'nyt://article/162dfaae-d575-5e7e-b083-1275202b6263'}, {'abstract': 'Professional schools are not traditionally thought of as places to go for the mere joy of it, but some are returning later in life to study business and law for a love of learning.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/19/education/back-on-campus-to-experience-road-not-taken.html', 'snippet': 'Professional schools are not traditionally thought of as places to go for the mere joy of it, but some are returning later in life to study business and law for a love of learning.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ADITI ROY wasn’t looking to become an entrepreneur or head to Wall Street or move up the corporate totem pole like most of her compatriots in the University of Pennsylvania’s Wharton School executive M.B.A. program. She was the morning news anchor for WCAU-TV, the NBC affiliate in Philadelphia, and already had a stint as West Coast correspondent for the network.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/education/WHY1/WHY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/19/education/WHY1/WHY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/education/WHY1/WHY1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type':