y.html', 'snippet': 'As employers demand more skills, many people are turning to online certificate programs to acquire a specific expertise that can lead them to a job or a promotion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AS employers demand skills and more skills, many people are turning to online certificate programs to acquire a specific expertise that can lead them to a job or a promotion — or, sometimes, simply to ensure that they hang on to their current position.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/education/CERTIFY/CERTIFY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/19/education/CERTIFY/CERTIFY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/education/CERTIFY/CERTIFY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/education/CERTIFY/CERTIFY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/education/CERTIFY/CERTIFY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/19/education/CERTIFY/CERTIFY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/education/CERTIFY/CERTIFY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Online Certificate Programs at Colleges and Universities Gain Popularity', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A New Order, From Inexpensive and Online ...', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Learning', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Olson, Elizabeth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Careers and Professions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vocational Training', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-18T20:45:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth Olson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Olson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bec8446c-f428-52d6-b182-63b3933e73c1', 'word_count': 912, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bec8446c-f428-52d6-b182-63b3933e73c1'}, {'abstract': 'Credits and deductions can help a taxpayer meet the costs of continuing education. Eligibility depends on income, how tuition is paid and the type of student.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/19/education/tax-code-helps-continuing-education-students-with-costs.html', 'snippet': 'Credits and deductions can help a taxpayer meet the costs of continuing education. Eligibility depends on income, how tuition is paid and the type of student.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROCCO ABBATEMARCO, 42, a middle school teacher from New York City, recently moved to Portland, Me., where he landed a teaching spot at a youth correctional facility. His new job required that he become certified in special education. To do so, Mr. Abbatemarco is taking accredited online courses, studying in the evening and on weekends. ', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Those Returning to School Can Find Help in the Tax Code', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Those Returning to School Can Find Help in the Tax Code', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Credits, Deductions and Exemptions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADULT EDUCATION', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Internal Revenue Service', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-18T20:45:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Walecia Konrad', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Walecia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Konrad', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4416075d-e105-503d-a348-daab625927b4', 'word_count': 1033, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4416075d-e105-503d-a348-daab625927b4'}, {'abstract': 'Elite universities are joining in, but the massive online open courses, known as MOOCs, threaten to poach paying students from other institutions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/19/education/colleges-assess-cost-of-free-online-only-courses.html', 'snippet': 'Elite universities are joining in, but the massive online open courses, known as MOOCs, threaten to poach paying students from other institutions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VIRGINIA M. ROMETTY, the chief executive of I.B.M., recently urged her employees to take 40 hours of continuing education this year. The company would not reimburse tuition, but would pay for expenses, like textbooks. ', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Colleges Assess Cost of Free Online-Only Courses', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '... To Free and Online', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Learning', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADULT EDUCATION', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Coursera Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'EdX', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Udacity', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-18T20:45:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Wallis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wallis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa6a5887-8382-5b67-b670-df0e33bd09c3', 'word_count': 1141, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa6a5887-8382-5b67-b670-df0e33bd09c3'}, {'abstract': 'More colleges are offering entrepreneurship programs as a way to help people get their businesses off the ground.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/19/education/entrepreneurship-certificates-give-small-businesses-a-lift.html', 'snippet': 'More colleges are offering entrepreneurship programs as a way to help people get their businesses off the ground.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THEY’RE called entrepreneurship or small-business certificates, and they don’t carry the cachet or the credit of an M.B.A. But they take far less time to obtain, and they cost less, too. More colleges are offering them as a way to help people get their businesses off the 