None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0691dc48-b9a6-5551-a768-00fea7ab3662', 'word_count': 523, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0691dc48-b9a6-5551-a768-00fea7ab3662'}, {'abstract': 'The land out here is a series of characters to me, as mysterious and alluring as any people I might invent on the page.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/18/oh-california/', 'snippet': 'The land out here is a series of characters to me, as mysterious and alluring as any people I might invent on the page.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Of all the things I’ve been called in my time, the one that surprises me the most is “California Writer.” When I hear that, I look over my shoulder, certain that the phrase must apply to the writer behind me or to my left. It’s the way I feel when I am addressed by my husband’s last name. It takes me a moment to realize his mother is not in the room.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Oh, California', 'kicker': 'Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-19T00:20:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marisa Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/31ec6ea7-4554-51b7-8b14-db3f450d318d', 'word_count': 1061, 'uri': 'nyt://article/31ec6ea7-4554-51b7-8b14-db3f450d318d'}, {'abstract': 'The 1 percent drop in drug spending was partly a sign of the rising use of generics, but experts warn that the high cost of specialty medicines could reverse the downturn.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/19/business/use-of-generics-produces-an-unusual-drop-in-drug-spending.html', 'snippet': 'The 1 percent drop in drug spending was partly a sign of the rising use of generics, but experts warn that the high cost of specialty medicines could reverse the downturn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Spending on prescription drugs nationwide has been slowing for years because of the increasingly widespread use of low-cost generics. But in 2012, something unheard-of happened: money spent on prescription drugs actually dropped.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/business/Drug/Drug-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/19/business/Drug/Drug-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/business/Drug/Drug-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/business/Drug/Drug-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/business/Drug/Drug-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/19/business/Drug/Drug-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/business/Drug/Drug-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Drug Costs Dropped in 2012, but Rises Loom', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Drug Costs Dropped in 2012, But Rises Loom', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thomas, Katie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'IMS Health', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Generic Brands and Products', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-19T00:22:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katie Thomas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thomas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/af8722d7-dcb0-5ea8-b268-4512ddbfd092', 'word_count': 1288, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af8722d7-dcb0-5ea8-b268-4512ddbfd092'}, {'abstract': 'Phil Hughes pitched in a simulated game, throwing off a mound for the first time since being shut down Feb. 18 because of a bulging disk.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/18/hughes-says-his-back-feels-good-after-throwing-off-mound/', 'snippet': 'Phil Hughes pitched in a simulated game, throwing off a mound for the first time since being shut down Feb. 18 because of a bulging disk.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TAMPA, Fla. — Tucked away in the corner of the Yankees’ minor league facility, on a day off for the team, three players who are key to the Yankees’ hopes this season toiled in relative obscurity Monday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hughes Is Hit by Grounder in Return, but Says He’s Fine', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hughes Works Off Mound', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hughes, Phil', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pettitte, Andy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rivera, Mariano', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-19T00:25:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Kerasotis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kerasotis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/17ce991e-0e76-539d-9677-8660b3849385', 'word_count': 514, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17ce991e-0e76-539d-9677-8660b3849385'}, {'abstract': 'Tiger Woods and Lindsey Vonn confirmed that they are dating, uniting one of the world’s best golfers with one of the world’s best ski racers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/19/sports/golf/tiger-woods-and-lindsey-vonn-confirm-that-they-are-dating.html', 'snippet': 'Tiger Woods and Lindsey Vonn confirmed that they are dating, uniting one of the world’s best golfers with one of the world’s best ski racers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With eerily similar announcements to a combined Facebook and Twitter audience of nearly 6.5 million, Tiger Woods and Lindsey Vonn confirmed Monday that they are dating, then asked for privacy because they want to live, in Woods’s words, “as an ordinary couple.”', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/sports/COUPLEvignette/COUPLEvignette-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 910, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/19/sports/COUPLEvignette/COUPLEvignette-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 910}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/sports/COUPLEvignette/COUPLEvignette-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 676, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/sports/COUPLEvignette/COUPLEvignette-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1351, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/sports/COUPLEvignette/COUPLEvignette-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/19/sports/COUPLEvignette/COUPLEvignette-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/sports/COUPLEvignette/COUPLEvignette-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A New First Couple in Sports: Woods and Vonn', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Nascent Power Couple For Sports', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skiing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woods, Tiger', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vonn, Lindsey', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dating and Courtship', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-19T00:26:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Pennington', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pennington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f066e2d-4b1e-53a6-8d99-f05b6ab00df5', 'word_count': 1017, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f066e2d-4b1e-53a6-8d99-f05b6ab00df5'}, {'abstract': 'Negotiators at the United Nations began a final round of talks on Monday aimed at completing a treaty to regulate the international trade in conventional weapons.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/19/world/negotiators-for-arms-trade-treaty-discuss-regulation-of-ammunition.html', 'snippet': 'Negotiators at the United Nations began a final round of talks on Monday aimed at completing a treaty to regulate the international trade in conventional weapons.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Negotiators at the United Nations began a final round of talks on Monday aimed at completing a treaty to regulate the international trade in conventional weapons. Objections by the United States and other major weapons exporters prevented an agreement. The United Nations secretary general, Ban Ki-moon, lamented what he called the lack of regulatory controls for the import and export of conventional weapons, asking why “there are common standards for the global trade in armchairs but not the global trade in arms.” One of the most contentious issues was whether ammunition should be included in the scope of the treaty. Anna McDonald, a representative of Oxfam, which is pushing for strong treaty, said her group wanted strict and specific language that would regulate ammunition. Thomas Mason, a representative of the World Forum on Shooting Activities, a group that represents firearms makers and users, said the sheer volume of ammunition produced made such monitoring impractical.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/world/BRIEFS/BRIEFS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 469, 'width': 306, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/world/BRIEFS/BRIEFS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 469, 'width': 306, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/world/BRIEFS/BRIEFS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/19/world/BRIEFS/BRIEFS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/world/BRIEFS/BRIEFS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Negotiators for Arms Trade Treaty Discuss Regulation of Ammunition', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | United Nations', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Negotiators for Arms Trade Treaty Discuss Regulation of Ammunition', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ban Ki-moon', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Firearms', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Arms Trade', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-19T00:31:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/820a62dc-6ca6-5804-be08-f9fe34065b7c', 'word_count': 154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/820a62dc-6ca6-5804-be08-f9fe34065b7c'}, {'abstract': 'The number of dead pigs found in the river near Shanghai rose to more than 13,000 over the weekend.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/19/world/asia/china-more-pigs-found-in-river.html', 'snippet': 'The number of dead pigs found in the river near Shanghai rose to more than 13,000 over the weekend.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The number of dead pigs found in a river near Shanghai rose to more than 13,000 over the weekend. Last Friday, the figure stood at about 7,500. The authorities, who are in the middle of a weeklong effort to collect the carcasses, are still trying to determine how the pigs died and why they ended up in the Huangpu River, which winds through Shanghai. The government has insisted that there is no evidence of an epidemic and that the food supply is safe. City officials also say the river meets national water quality standards. The authorities say they believe that many of the pigs came from the nearby city of Jiaxing, in Zhejiang Province, where there are major pig farms. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China: More Pigs Found in River', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China: More Pigs Found in River', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 