g damage to confidence in banks in other euro-zone countries.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/19/opinion/taxing-bank-depositors-in-cyprus.html', 'snippet': 'Europe’s bailout plan for the island is needlessly harsh and could do lasting damage to confidence in banks in other euro-zone countries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A European plan could force Cyprus to tax bank depositors as a condition of a bailout in a way that would unfairly punish savers and could do lasting damage to confidence in banks in other euro-zone countries in financial crisis. The country’s leaders have a chance to change the agreement and should do so.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Taxing Savers in Cyprus', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Taxing Savers in Cyprus', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cyprus', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Monetary Fund', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-19T01:00:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/92cc96f5-63a1-578e-baf9-69094fd5b879', 'word_count': 520, 'uri': 'nyt://article/92cc96f5-63a1-578e-baf9-69094fd5b879'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Mandal recounts the horrors of living inside Delhi’s Tihar jail after being wrongly implicated in a rape case.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/18/a-conversation-with-former-tihar-inmate-niranjan-kumar-mandal/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Mandal recounts the horrors of living inside Delhi’s Tihar jail after being wrongly implicated in a rape case.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI — The death of Ram Singh, one of the six defendants in the Delhi gang rape case who was found hanged in his cell, has raised speculation about its cause and questions about the management of Tihar Jail. While the post-mortem report suggested suicide, Mr. Singh’s parents contend that the police murdered him, in part because both his arms were damaged from previous accidents.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/18/world/asia/18-Tihar-inmate-IndiaInk/18-Tihar-inmate-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 668, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/18/world/asia/18-Tihar-inmate-IndiaInk/18-Tihar-inmate-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 668}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/18/world/asia/18-Tihar-inmate-IndiaInk/18-Tihar-inmate-IndiaInk-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 921, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/18/world/asia/18-Tihar-inmate-IndiaInk/18-Tihar-inmate-IndiaInk-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1841, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/18/world/asia/18-Tihar-inmate-IndiaInk/18-Tihar-inmate-IndiaInk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/18/world/asia/18-Tihar-inmate-IndiaInk/18-Tihar-inmate-IndiaInk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/18/world/asia/18-Tihar-inmate-IndiaInk/18-Tihar-inmate-IndiaInk-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Conversation With: Former Tihar Inmate Niranjan Kumar Mandal', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tihar Jail', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Delhi (India)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-19T01:00:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Betwa Sharma', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Betwa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sharma', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d51078a-3265-56d8-a31c-bc4dcda7c30d', 'word_count': 1311, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d51078a-3265-56d8-a31c-bc4dcda7c30d'}, {'abstract': 'A town’s new law reads like an imitation of the physical act it is trying to prevent.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/18/the-andes-chronicles-a-ban-on-hydraulic-fracturing/', 'snippet': 'A town’s new law reads like an imitation of the physical act it is trying to prevent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Once or twice a year I bring news from the small Catskills town of Andes, and usually the news concerns the ongoing battle to preserve the town’s rural character in the face of incursions from entrepreneurial energy companies. A few years back Andes passed an ordinance banning wind turbines. Late last month the town board passed a law prohibiting heavy industry. The intended target of the law was hydraulic fracturing, or fracking, the technique by which natural gas is extracted from underground rock formations that have been subjected to the high velocity impact of chemically laced water. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Andes Chronicles: A Ban on Hydraulic Fracturing', 'kicker': 'Stanley Fish', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hydraulic Fracturing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rural Areas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Catskills (NYS Area)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-19T01:00:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stanley Fish', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stanley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fish', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7244764c-4e5f-57db-a76d-8ab596188a51', 'word_count': 880, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7244764c-4e5f-57db-a76d-8ab596188a51'}, {'abstract': 'Stacy Lewis became the seventh woman to ascend to No. 1 in the world rankings and the second American. Pressures aside, Lewis said she planned to continue to have fun.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/19/sports/golf/ranked-no-1-stacy-lewis-keeps-expectations-in-check.html', 'snippet': 'Stacy Lewis became the seventh woman to ascend to No. 1 in the world rankings and the second American. Pressures aside, Lewis said she planned to continue to have fun.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PHOENIX — As a teenager, Stacy Lewis spent 18 hours a day wearing a back brace to cope with scoliosis. That was hard. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/sports/Y-GOLF/Y-GOLF-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 789, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/19/sports/Y-GOLF/Y-GOLF-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 789}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/sports/Y-GOLF/Y-GOLF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 779, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/sports/Y-GOLF/Y-GOLF-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1558, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/sports/Y-GOLF/Y-GOLF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/19/sports/Y-GOLF/Y-GOLF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/sports/Y-GOLF/Y-GOLF-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ranked No. 1, Lewis Keeps Expectations in Check', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ranked No. 1, Lewis Keeps Expectations in Check', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lewis, Stacy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ladies Professional Golf Assn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-19T01:02:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d68b3804-7f7e-553c-abcb-8e6f52786f72', 'word_count': 757, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d68b3804-7f7e-553c-abcb-8e6f52786f72'}, {'abstract': 'A special counsel’s letter to the White House detailed complaints on missed diagnoses, poor sterilization and understaffing at a Department of Veterans Affairs medical center in Jackson, Miss.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/19/us/whistle-blower-complaints-at-veterans-hospital-in-mississippi.html', 'snippet': 'A special counsel’s letter to the White House detailed complaints on missed diagnoses, poor sterilization and understaffing at a Department of Veterans Affairs medical center in Jackson, Miss.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — In an unusually strong letter sent to the White House on Monday, the office that handles complaints from federal whistle-blowers says it has found a pattern of problems at a Department of Veterans Affairs medical center in Jackson, Miss., that raises serious questions about the hospital’s management practices.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Pattern of Problems at a Hospital for Veterans', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Pattern Of Problems At Hospital For Veterans', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Office of Special Counsel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dao, James', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Veterans Affairs Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jackson (Miss)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Montgomery, G V (Sonny), Veteran Affairs Medical Center', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Whistle-Blowers', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-19T01:09:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Dao', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dao', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a5df8b5-76e3-5446-9d1f-9ee597f1e8ba', 'word_count': 1114, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a5df8b5-76e3-5446-9d1f-9ee597f1e8ba'}, {'abstract': 'For Pope Francis to change the Vatican, he must tame a hierarchy whose branches are run like medieval fiefs and whose supplicants vie for access and influence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/19/world/europe/pope-francis-faces-an-entrenched-curia.html', 'snippet': 'For Pope Francis to change the Vatican, he must tame a hierarchy whose branches are run like medieval fiefs and whose supplicants vie for access and influence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VATICAN CITY — An Italian industrialist tried to curry favor by donating $100,000 worth of truffles. A Mercedes-Benz executive hoped for an audience to suggest improvements to the Popemobile. But in the final years of the papacy of Benedict XVI, others sent very different messages, too, desperate for the pope’s ear.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/world/JP-CURIA/JP-CURIA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/19/world/JP-CURIA/JP-CURIA-articleLarge.jpg', '