As lower-cost generic drugs have become more widely prescribed, the dollar amount spent on drugs fell last year for the first time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As lower-cost generic drugs have become more widely prescribed, the dollar amount spent on drugs fell last year for the first time.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Some, Spending Less on Drugs', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-19T02:22:49+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business Day', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/f46907f2-234b-58b6-96fe-aa0f6b5064b0', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/f46907f2-234b-58b6-96fe-aa0f6b5064b0'}, {'abstract': 'Dr. Kermit Gosnell, who operated a women’s health clinic in West Philadelphia, is accused of performing illegal late-term abortions and killing seven viable fetuses.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/19/us/philadelphia-abortion-doctors-murder-trial-opens.html', 'snippet': 'Dr. Kermit Gosnell, who operated a women’s health clinic in West Philadelphia, is accused of performing illegal late-term abortions and killing seven viable fetuses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PHILADELPHIA — In opening statements in court on Monday, prosecutors charged that a doctor who operated a women’s health clinic here killed seven viable fetuses by plunging scissors into their necks and “snipping” their spinal cords and was also responsible for the death of a pregnant woman in his care. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/us/ABORTION/ABORTION-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 733, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'art