: 'Marc Staal watched from a Madison Square Garden luxury box, attending his first game since taking a puck near the right eye in a frightening accident March 5. Staal did not speak to reporters, but obviously liked what he saw — a 2-1 shootout victory for the Rangers over the Carolina Hurricanes and his brothers Eric and Jordan on Monday night.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/sports/RANGERS/RANGERS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 459, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/19/sports/RANGERS/RANGERS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 459}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/sports/RANGERS/RANGERS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 783, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/sports/RANGERS/RANGERS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1566, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/sports/RANGERS/RANGERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/19/sports/RANGERS/RANGERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/sports/RANGERS/RANGERS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rangers Manage to Break Losing Streak, if Not Their Scoring Struggles', 'kicker': 'Rangers 2, Hurricanes 1 (SO)', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rangers Manage to Break Losing Streak, if Not Their Scoring Struggles', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klein, Jeff Z', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carolina Hurricanes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Rangers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Staal, Eric', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Staal, Jordan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Staal, Marc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-19T04:36:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8cfddd6e-54cf-50ad-ac5a-8aa4749987b6', 'word_count': 654, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8cfddd6e-54cf-50ad-ac5a-8aa4749987b6'}, {'abstract': 'Coach Jurgen Klinsmann has had to piece together a roster light on experience for two World Cup qualifiers after his team was hit hard by injuries.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/19/sports/soccer/united-states-faces-important-world-cup-qualifiers-with-a-thin-roster.html', 'snippet': 'Coach Jurgen Klinsmann has had to piece together a roster light on experience for two World Cup qualifiers after his team was hit hard by injuries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When United States national team Coach Jurgen Klinsmann called in attacking threats like Jozy Altidore, Herculez Gomez and Clint Dempsey for his latest roster, it was surely done with the hope that the United States would be able to score often in its two coming World Cup qualifying matches. Given the injuries and illness that have racked Klinsmann’s group of defenders, he could hardly be blamed for thinking he will need as many goals as possible.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/sports/soccer/19soccer1-img/19soccer1-img-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 405, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/19/sports/soccer/19soccer1-img/19soccer1-img-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 405}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/sports/soccer/19soccer1-img/19soccer1-img-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 691, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/sports/soccer/19soccer1-img/19soccer1-img-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1382, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/sports/soccer/19soccer1-img/19soccer1-img-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/19/sports/soccer/19soccer1-img/19soccer1-img-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/sports/soccer/19soccer1-img/19soccer1-img-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'United States Facing Two Qualifying Games With Thin Roster', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'United States Facing Two Qualifying Games With Thin Roster', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "United States Men's National Soccer Team", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Altidore, Jozy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klinsmann, Jurgen', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gomez, Herculez', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dempsey, Clint', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Donovan, Landon', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bocanegra, Carlos', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-19T04:53:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Borden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e62bf38d-b834-55d0-8363-f3aef6902670', 'word_count': 758, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e62bf38d-b834-55d0-8363-f3aef6902670'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/19/arts/television/whats-on-tuesday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '8 P.M. (ABC) SPLASH The Olympic gold medalist Greg Louganis, above, will tutor 10 celebrities — among them, Kareem Abdul-Jabbar, Louie Anderson, Drake Bell, Keshia Knight Pulliam and Kendra Wilkinson — in the art of diving before they try to flip, twist and spin off a regulation platform and springboard in this new competition series. The diver David Boudia and the director of the United States team, Steve Foley, will critique each dive. Chuy Bravo, Rory Bushfield, Nicole Eggert, Ndamukong Suh and Katherine Webb round out the roster of competitors; Joey Lawrence and Charissa Thompson host.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Tuesday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-19T05:00:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/122741ca-bf39-55d5-8443-5e2fd3b2b8c2', 'word_count': 714, 'uri': 'nyt://article/122741ca-bf39-55d5-8443-5e2fd3b2b8c2'}, {'abstract': 'The Dominicans defeated the Netherlands, setting up a matchup with Puerto Rico in the World Baseball Classic final.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/19/sports/baseball/dominican-republic-beats-the-netherlands-and-advances-to-world-baseball-classic-final.html', 'snippet': 'The Dominicans defeated the Netherlands, setting up a matchup with Puerto Rico in the World Baseball Classic final.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO — No team has gone undefeated in a World Baseball Classic. The Japanese won it in 2006 and 2009 while losing three games the first time and two the second. Now, the Dominican Republic will take an unblemished record into the final game on Tuesday at AT&T Park.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/sports/BATS/BATS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 451, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/19/spor