rt: Cypriot Bank Deposits', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-19T12:05:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ffbaa512-591d-5f9b-acff-eedb3873b588', 'word_count': 95, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ffbaa512-591d-5f9b-acff-eedb3873b588'}, {'abstract': 'Nothing will shake the right-wing faith.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/19/the-dunning-kruger-madoff-effect/', 'snippet': 'Nothing will shake the right-wing faith.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Via Mark Thoma, Hale Stewart is bemused by John Hinderaker of PowerLine. As Stewart notes, Hinderaker begins by asserting that everyone knows that an economic crisis is coming — which apparently means everyone he talks to — then rolls out just about every one of the myths that have been proved wrong again and again by events, from the looming debt crisis to the imminent takeoff of inflation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Dunning-Kruger-Madoff Effect', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-19T12:07:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ffaef846-2759-5930-9235-65bbb824a593', 'word_count': 354, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ffaef846-2759-5930-9235-65bbb824a593'}, {'abstract': 'Musicians and artists often transcend their nations, borrowing from others’ cultures and making new hybrids', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/19/the-mumbainew-york-photo-project-music-and-dance/', 'snippet': 'Musicians and artists often transcend their nations, borrowing from others’ cultures and making new hybrids', 'lead_paragraph': 'The grand cities of Mumbai and New York differ from each other in a million ways, but are brought together by a few common strands – their entrepreneurial spirit, their dynamic “always on-the-go” nature, their lively sidewalks, their gorgeous coastlines, the diversity of their residents who bring unique culture and religion and their vibrant music scene. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Mumbai/New York Photo Project: Music and Dance', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AILEY, ALVIN, AMERICAN DANCE THEATER', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mumbai (India)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-19T12:09:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nisha Sondhe and Neha Thirani Bagri', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nisha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sondhe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'repo