 each day, an estimated 2,793 people have died as a result of gun violence since December 14, 2012. The recorded death toll of the Sept. 11 attacks stands at 2,752.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Gun Report: March 19, 2013', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALBUQUERQUE (NM)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beaumont (Tex)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indiana', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lawrence (Mass)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mobile (Ala)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Carolina', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oklahoma City (Okla)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-19T15:17:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Mascia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mascia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f18ed305-dca6-5a63-b6d4-7337c472ddc3', 'word_count': 754, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f18ed305-dca6-5a63-b6d4-7337c472ddc3'}, {'abstract': 'Part of the beauty of travel, stylistically speaking, is letting go of the restraints of the everyday for a more carefree look.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/19/wanderlust-in-repose/', 'snippet': 'Part of the beauty of travel, stylistically speaking, is letting go of the restraints of the everyday for a more carefree look.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Part of the beauty of travel, stylistically speaking, is letting go of the restraints of the everyday for a more carefree look.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wanderlust in Repose', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-19T15:30:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Magazine', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca8724eb-506e-5fce-9428-761a9d539359', 'word_count': 26, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca8724eb-506e-5fce-9428-761a9d539359'}, {'abstract': 'An artist in Southern California who runs his own branding and design consulting company happens to have a thing for restaurants.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/19/posters-for-chefs-the-new-rock-stars/', 'snippet': 'An artist in Southern California who runs his own branding and design consulting company happens to have a thing for restaurants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Whether we’re talking about San Francisco in the 1960s, during the early years of the Grateful Dead and Jefferson Airplane, or the alternative-rock scene that produced bands like Superchunk, Soundgarden and Pavement in the 1980s and ’90s, rock music has long been a fertile breeding ground for visual art. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Posters for Chefs, the New Rock Stars', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chefs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Posters', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davis, Stuart', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goin, Suzanne', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Soundgarden', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-19T15:30:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Gordinier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gordinier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b53a5df3-3ef2-5647-b760-bf7d4557d61d', 'word_count': 367, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b53a5df3-3ef2-5647-b760-bf7d4557d61d'}, {'abstract': 'The Miami Heat have won 23 games in a row, an accomplishment that is overshadowed by the N.C.A.A. tournaments — and Tiger and Lindsey.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/20/sports/a-streak-that-doesnt-grab-the-spotlight.html', 'snippet': 'The Miami Heat have won 23 games in a row, an accomplishment that is overshadowed by the N.C.A.A. tournaments — and Tiger and Lindsey.', 'lead_paragraph': 'About the only thing you can fault the Miami Heat on these days is their lousy timing. Yes, the Heat’s 23-game winning streak is one to behold, no matter the time of year and yes, it certainly is a reason to tune in to games when the regular season usually turns to unwatchable mush. But there is so much out there clamoring for fans’ attention these days, the Heat are struggling to get the hype machine pointed squarely in their direction.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/20/sports/20le