: 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/20/education/activists-at-colleges-network-to-fight-sexual-assault.html', 'snippet': 'Campaigns against sexual assault on campuses have connected people who, while sometimes seeking advice elsewhere, have largely learned from one another.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Frustrated and angry over the handling of sexual assault cases at Occidental College in Los Angeles, a group of students and faculty members recently decided to take the matter to the federal government as a civil rights case. Few people had explored this legal terrain, so the Occidental group reached out to women at the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill, who had filed a similar complaint — which this month prompted a federal investigation — for insights on how to press their case.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/20/education/20network-cnd1/20network-cnd1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 424, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/20/education/20network-cnd1/20network-cnd1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 424}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/20/education/20network-cnd1/20network-cnd1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 723, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/20/education/20network-cnd1/20network-cnd1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1447, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/20/education/20network-cnd1/20network-cnd1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/20/education/20network-cnd1/20network-cnd1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/20/education/20network-cnd1/20network-cnd1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'College Groups Connect to Fight Sexual Assault', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'College Groups Connect To Fight Sexual Assault', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Title IX (Gender Discrimination Legislation)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sexual Harassment', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occidental College', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of North Carolina', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMHERST COLLEGE', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yale University', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-19T18:22:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Pérez-Peña', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pérez-Peña', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c4e4f88-095a-5a47-80ce-44c062a24d95', 'word_count': 1017, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c4e4f88-095a-5a47-80ce-44c062a24d95'}, {'abstract': 'The organizers of the European Fine Art Fair are in talks with Sotheby’s about holding a high-end art and antiques fair in China.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/19/european-art-fair-may-join-with-sothebys-for-chinese-sales/', 'snippet': 'The organizers of the European Fine Art Fair are in talks with Sotheby’s about holding a high-end art and antiques fair in China.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In what might seem like a pairing of competitive bedfellows, the organizers of the European Fine Art Fair – that 10-day event going on through Sunday in Maastricht, the Netherlands – announced on Tuesday that they were in talks with Sotheby’s about holding a high-end art and antiques fair in China. The new event, which would be called Tefaf Beijing 2014, would be “planned as a collaboration between Maastricht, the Netherlands-based event, and Sotheby’s recently forged joined venture with China’s state-owned Beijing Ge-Hua Cultural Development Group,’’ the European Fine Art Fair said in an e-mail.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'European Art Fair May Join With Sotheby’s for Chinese Sales', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Fine Art Fair', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Sotheby's", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-19T18:32:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Vogel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vogel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7cf362bc-51c8-5c89-b648-168adedef555', 'word_count': 211, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7cf362bc-51c8-5c89-b648-168adedef555'}, {'abstract': 'Brooklyn prosecutors cited reckless behavior in bringing second-degree manslaughter charges against Julio Acevedo.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/20/nyregion/charges-upgraded-in-brooklyn-crash-that-killed-couple.html', 'snippet': 'Brooklyn prosecutors cited reckless behavior in bringing second-degree manslaughter charges against Julio Acevedo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A grand jury has indicted the driver accused in a fatal hit-and-run crash this month on new charges of second-degree manslaughter, the Brooklyn district attorney said on Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Charges Upgraded in Hit-Run Crash That Killed Couple', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Charges Are Upgraded in Crash That Killed Couple', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Acevedo, Julio', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Glauber, Nathan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Glauber, Raizy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hit-and-Run Drivers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-19T18:33:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. David Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9bffafc-29f9-52d9-8978-8fe51c97294f', 'word_count': 457, 'uri': 'nyt: