 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pat Borzi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pat', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borzi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ddc5719-becd-52d4-bcb0-06516f5bfc7d', 'word_count': 1032, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ddc5719-becd-52d4-bcb0-06516f5bfc7d'}, {'abstract': 'The Massachusetts Institute of Technology announced on Tuesday it would release documents related to the case against Aaron Swartz, the Internet activist who committed suicide.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/20/us/massachusetts-mit-will-release-documents-in-hacking-case.html', 'snippet': 'The Massachusetts Institute of Technology announced on Tuesday it would release documents related to the case against Aaron Swartz, the Internet activist who committed suicide.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Massachusetts Institute of Technology on Tuesday announced that it would release documents related to the case against Aaron Swartz, the Internet activist who committed suicide in January, about a month before he was to go to trial on charges that he illegally downloaded academic articles from the university’s computer network. In a letter to the M.I.T. community, the university president, L. Rafael Reif, said lawyers for Mr. Swartz had requested in federal court that the institution make evidence related to the case public. Mr. Reif said M.I.T. planned to release those documents, with some information redacted, when it completed an investigation led by a computer science professor, Hal Abelson, into the university’s role in the case. Professor Abelson said in late January that he hoped to complete the investigation within a few weeks. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Massachusetts: M.I.T. Will Release Documents in Hacking Case', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | New England', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Massachusetts: M.I.T. Will Release Documents In Hacking Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Swartz, Aaron (1986-2013)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bidgood, Jess', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Massachusetts Institute of Technology', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberattacks and Hackers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suicides and Suicide Attempts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Massachusetts', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-19T23:50:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jess Bidgood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jess', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bidgood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/493ee661-63d0-51c8-a170-3ee59b0957af', 'word_count': 134, 'uri': 'nyt://article/493ee661-63d0-51c8-a170-3ee59b0957af'}, {'abstract': 'A defiant 18-year-old was sentenced Tuesday to spend the rest of his life in prison for a 2012 shooting at a high school cafeteria in Chardon, where he killed three students and wounded three others.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/20/us/ohio-teenage-killer-gets-life.html', 'snippet': 'A defiant 18-year-old was sentenced Tuesday to spend the rest of his life in prison for a 2012 shooting at a high school cafeteria in Chardon, where he killed three students and wounded three others.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A defiant 18-year-old was sentenced Tuesday to spend the rest of his life in prison for a 2012 shooting at a high school cafeteria in Chardon, where he killed three students and wounded three others. Wearing a T-shirt with the word “killer” printed on it, T. J. Lane directed an obscene statement and gesture toward family members of the shooting victims when asked for a statement. He pleaded guilty last month to three counts of aggravated murder, two counts of attempted aggravated murder and one count of assault. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ohio: Teenage Killer Gets Life', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Midwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ohio: Teenage Killer Gets Life', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lane, T J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bidgood, Jess', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'School Shootings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chardon (Ohio)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-19T23:54:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jess Bidgood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jess', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bidgood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/70eead5e-1277-5a33-845b-3dd670ac098b', 'word_count': 88, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70eead5e-1277-5a33-845b-3dd670ac098b'}, {'abstract': 'Malala Yousafzai, the 15-year-old Pakistani campaigner for girls’ education who was gravely wounded by the Taliban in October, is back in school for the first time since the attack.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/20/world/europe/britain-girl-shot-by-taliban-returns-to-the-classroom.html', 'snippet': 'Malala Yousafzai, the 15-year-old Pakistani campaigner for girls’ education who was gravely wounded by the Taliban in October, is back in school for the first time since the attack.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Malala Yousafzai, the 15-year-old Pakistani campaigner for girls’ education who was gravely wounded by the Taliban in October, is back in school for the first time since the attack, according to a statement by her family. Ms. Yousafzai, shown with her father, is now enrolled full time at Edgbaston, a private girls’ high school in Birmingham, England, where her family now lives and where she underwent extensive medical treatment in recent months. “I miss my classmates from Pakistan very much, but I am looking forward to meeting my teachers and making new friends here in Birmingham,” she was quoted as saying in the statement. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/20/world/BRIEFS/BRIEFS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 880, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/20/world/BRIEFS/BRIEFS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 880}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/20/world/BRIEFS/BRIEFS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 699, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/20/world/BRIEFS/BRIEFS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1397, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/20/world/BRIEFS/BRIEFS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legac