ey are taking the fight to neighboring countries, especially Syria.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/20/opinion/iraq-a-school-for-terrorists-thanks-to-america.html', 'snippet': 'Qaeda-affiliated militants drawn to Iraq since 2003 have been battle-tested. They are taking the fight to neighboring countries, especially Syria.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IRAQ, President George W. Bush said in 2003, was a “central front” in the war on terrorism. He was wrong, but prescient. Iraq has become a front for militant extremism — a front the United States created.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iraq: Where Terrorists Go to School', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iraq: A School for Terrorists, Thanks to America', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003-11)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-20T01:11:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jessica Stern', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jessica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stern', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1b8ebb5-2f7c-5180-9ecd-70feeea499ab', 'word_count': 937, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1b8ebb5-2f7c-5180-9ecd-70feeea499ab'}, {'abstract': 'Rafe al-Essawi, until recently Iraq’s finance minister and one of the highest-ranking Sunni politicians, is now on the run from the Shiite-led government.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/20/world/middleeast/fading-hopes-of-unity-in-iraq-as-sectarian-tensions-rise.html', 'snippet': 'Rafe al-Essawi, until recently Iraq’s finance minister and one of the highest-ranking Sunni politicians, is now on the run from the Shiite-led government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RAMADI, Iraq — As Rafe al-Essawi, the embattled Sunni leader, sped south on a desert highway last week to attend the funeral of a political ally who was assassinated, his cellphone rang with a warning: Up ahead, Iraqi soldiers, backed by two helicopters hovering overhead, planned to arrest him.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/20/world/JP-IRAQ-2/JP-IRAQ-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/20/world/JP-IRAQ-2/JP-IRAQ-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/20/world/JP-IRAQ-2/JP-IRAQ-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/20/world/JP-IRAQ-2/JP-IRAQ-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/20/world/JP-IRAQ-2/JP-IRAQ-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/20/world/JP-IRAQ-2/JP-IRAQ-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/20/world/JP-IRAQ-2/JP-IRAQ-2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sectarian Strains Pit Some Iraqis Against Their Own Leaders', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sectarian Split Again Imperils Future of Iraq', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Essawi, Rafe al', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gordon, Michael R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sunni Muslims', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Arango, Tim', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shiite Muslims', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maliki, Nuri Kamal al-', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ANBAR PROVINCE (IRAQ)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-20T01:15:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Arango and Michael R. Gordon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Arango', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Gordon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c403469-eab6-532e-9bef-cf2264eb4b15', 'word_count': 1112, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c403469-eab6-532e-9bef-cf2264eb4b15'}, {'abstract': 'Dr. Ruddle, one of the first scientists to map genes’ locations on specific human chromosomes, helped lay the groundwork for the Human Genome Project.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/20/science/francis-ruddle-who-led-transgenic-research-dies-at-83.html', 'snippet': 'Dr. Ruddle, one of the first scientists to map genes’ locations on specific human chromosomes, helped lay the groundwork for the Human Genome Project.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Francis Ruddle, a Yale University geneticist who plumbed the DNA of mice and men, and from whose laboratory sprang the first transgenic mammal — a mouse with added foreign DNA — died on March 10 in New Haven. He was 83.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/20/us/RUDDLE-obit/RUDDLE-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/20/us/RUDDLE-obit/RUDDLE-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 480}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/20/us/RUDDLE-obit/RUDDLE-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/20/us/RUDDLE-obit/RUDDLE-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1638, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/20/us/RUDDLE-obit/RUDDLE-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/20/us/RUDDLE-obit/RUDDLE-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/20/us/RUDDLE-obit/RUDDLE-obit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Francis Ruddle, Who Led Transgenic Research, Dies at 83', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Francis Ruddle, 83, Is Dead; Led Transgenic Research', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fox, Margalit', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ruddle, Francis H (1929-2013)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetic Engineering', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yale University', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mice', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-20T01:15:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margalit Fox', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margalit', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fox', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/58fafa64-ff66-5d77-a457-39430e73c579', 'word_count': 811, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58fafa64-ff66-5d77-a457-39430e73c579'}, {'abstract': 'The producer of Monster Energy will no longer be required to tell federal regulators about reports potentially linking its products to deaths and injuries.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/20/business/in-a-new-aisle-energy-drinks-sidestep-rules.html', 'snippet': 'The producer of Monster Energy will no longer be required to tell federal regulators about reports potentially linking its products to deaths and injuries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fans of Monster Energy, the popular high-caffeine energy drink, may not notice the change: its ingredients will be the same and its familiar label bearing a green, clawlike monogram will change only slightly. But the drink’s maker has decided after a decade of selling it as a dietary supplement to market it as a beverage, a switch that will bring significant changes in how it is regulated.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/20/business/MONSTER-1/MONSTER-1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/20/business/MONSTER-1/MONSTER-1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/20/business/MONSTER-1/MONSTER-1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 631, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/20/business/MONSTER-1/MONSTER-1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1262, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/20/business/MONSTER-1/MONSTER-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/20/business/MONSTER-1/MONSTER-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/20/business/MONSTER-1/MONSTER-1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In a New Aisle, Energy Drinks Sidestep Some Rules', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In a New Aisle, Energy Drinks Sidestep Rules', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Energy and Sports Drinks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Monster Beverage Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rockstar Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Caffeine', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beverages', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dietary Supplements and Herbal Remedies', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-20T01:16:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Barry Meier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Barry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Meier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9014f0a-ed66-5d2e-8683-9f10cdd464b2', 'word_count': 1388, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9014f0a-ed66-5d2e-8683-9f10cdd464b2'}, {'abstract': 'Iraq might seem to have been the last place in the Middle East we should have tried to help establish a democracy, but it was the most important.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/20/opinion/friedman-democrats-dragons-or-drones.html', 'snippet': 'Iraq might seem to have been the last place in the Middle East we should have tried to help establish a democracy, but it was the most important.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On this 10th anniversary of the U.S. invasion of Iraq, three things are clear. First, whatever happens in Iraq, we overpaid for it in lives and treasure and focus. Second, you can overpay for something decent and you can overpay for total junk. What exactly we overpaid for in Iraq is not yet clear and will be decided by Iraqis. Third, as much as we’d prefer to forget about Iraq, what happens there matters more than ever for the Middle East.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Democrats, Dragons or Drones?', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Democrats, Dragons Or Drones?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Friedman, Thomas L', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003-11)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-20T01:21:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas L. Friedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Friedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b710d51-ce7c-565e-92be-1602b128f291', 'word_count': 879, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b710d51-ce7c-565e-92be-1602b128f291'}, {'abstract': 'An ill-conceived war continues to affect American policy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/20/opinion/ten-years-after-the-iraq-war-began.html', 'snippet': 'An ill-conceived war continues to affect American policy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ten years after it began, the Iraq war still haunts the United States in the nearly 4,500 troops who died there; the more than 30,000 American wounded who have come home; the more than $2 trillion spent on combat operations and reconstruction, which inflated the deficit; and in the lessons learned about the limits of American leadership and power.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ten Years After', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ten Years After', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003-11)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, George W', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wolfowitz, Paul D', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-20T01:23:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/2556476c-1696-5172-a27f-0275866664fc', 'word_count': 756, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2556476c-1696-5172-a27f-0275866664fc'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Marder may not have gotten a lot of the glory for helping bring down a Red-baiting Senator Joe McCarthy, but he deserves much of the credit, colleagues said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/20/us/murrey-marder-reporter-who-took-on-joe-mccarthy-dies-at-93.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Marder may not have gotten a lot of the glory for helping bring down a Red-baiting Senator Joe McCarthy, but he deserves much of the credit, colleagues said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'By certain journalistic lights, the reporter Murrey Marder was an editor’s nightmare. He wrote slowly and squeezed against deadlines. He debated with editors. His articles were long, often complicated and never laid claim to stylish writing.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/20/us/MARDER-obit/MARDER-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 640, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/20/us/MARDER-obit/MARDER-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 640}}, {'rank': 0, 