dnesday, Mar. 20, 2013', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-20T01:44:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a6569a3-2799-5ce5-983d-1bdcc118f1d6', 'word_count': 46, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a6569a3-2799-5ce5-983d-1bdcc118f1d6'}, {'abstract': 'The Supreme Court heard arguments Tuesday on whether a drug maker could be held responsible for severe injuries caused by its generic pain pill.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/20/business/justices-explore-fine-line-on-generic-drug-injuries.html', 'snippet': 'The Supreme Court heard arguments Tuesday on whether a drug maker could be held responsible for severe injuries caused by its generic pain pill.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — In 2010, a New Hampshire jury awarded Karen Bartlett $21 million for the ordeal she endured from taking a generic pain pill for an aching shoulder. It caused two-thirds of her skin to slough off, damaged her lungs and esophagus and rendered her legally blind.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/20/business/BIZCOURT/BIZCOURT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 368, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/20/business/BIZCOURT/BIZCOURT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 368}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/20/business/BIZCOURT/BIZCOURT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 629, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': N