: 1224, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4b9f6bc8-490a-5f87-a8f1-79d99c316427'}, {'abstract': 'Can you calculate the number of first-time college students who did not graduate after six years?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/20/test-yourself-math-march-20-2013/', 'snippet': 'Can you calculate the number of first-time college students who did not graduate after six years?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Test your math skills with this question created by Scott Matthews at Math for America from the Economix blog post “Only Half of First-Time College Students Graduate in 6 Years.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Test Yourself | Math, March 20, 2013', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-20T08:24:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4228610-aa3e-5e7a-8a72-80099e28a204', 'word_count': 58, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4228610-aa3e-5e7a-8a72-80099e28a204'}, {'abstract': 'Revelers gathered along Fifth Avenue on Saturday to view the St. Patrick’s Day parade, and Nicole Bengiveno was in their midst, on assignment, snapping away.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/20/seeing-the-surrealness-of-st-pattys-day/', 'snippet': 'Revelers gathered along Fifth Avenue on Saturday to view the St. Patrick’s Day parade, and Nicole Bengiveno was in their midst, on assignment, snapping away.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I love surreal-ness,” said Nicole Bengiveno, staff photographer of The New York Times, who photographed the St. Patrick’s Day parade in New York on Saturday. “You have men in skirts, you have people with shamrocks on their faces — I kept snapping pictures of people with these funny hats and green hair. Because they’re just really in the spirit.” Followed by the freelance videographer Elaisha Stokes, Ms. Bengiveno demonstrates how, for the parade-going photographer, it is helpful to be drawn to strangeness. After all, if you have photographed as many parades as she has, an eye for the uncommon can be a gift. Likewise, a knack for sticking to the sidelines. “I like to stay around the edges,” Ms. Bengiveno said. “I like the idea of being invisible.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Parading on the Edges', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parades', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "St Patrick's Day", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-20T09:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e494565a-4c46-553e-9354-2fae2e8f69ac', 'word_count': 139, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e494565a-4c46-553e-9354-2fae2e8f69ac'}, {'abstract': 'What kinds of things do you throw away in a typical week?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/20/do-you-ever-feel-guilty-about-what-or-how-much-you-throw-away/', 'snippet': 'What kinds of things do you throw away in a typical week?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Americans throw away hundreds of millions of tons of trash every year. We throw away spoiled food, old sneakers, unwanted pianos and bulky televisions. That’s a lot of garbage. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/19/us/WASTE-LN/WASTE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 