om/2013/03/20/how-to-live-in-assisted-living/', 'snippet': 'Martin Bayne, an advocate for people in assisted living, describes his perfect living arrangement: ‘We want you busy, productive, happy.’', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sometimes Martin Bayne speaks in little more than a whisper, like many people with advanced Parkinson’s disease. But his voice has a way of carrying.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Live in Assisted Living', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elder Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nursing Homes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-20T10:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judith Graham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Graham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe48efe9-3bcd-5beb-a440-4d69d66cfa74', 'word_count': 1338, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe48efe9-3bcd-5beb-a440-4d69d66cfa74'}, {'abstract': 'Forms of debt forgiveness can make collection more efficient but run the risk of debtors’ gaming the system, an economist writes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/20/forgiveness-formulas/', 'snippet': 'Forms of debt forgiveness can make collection more efficient but run the risk of debtors’ gaming the system, an economist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Casey B. Mulligan is an economics professor at the University of Chicago. He is the author of “The Redistribution Recession: How Labor Market Distortions Contracted the Economy.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Forgiveness Formulas',