xchange Commission', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Romania', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-20T11:30:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf0e96fd-b284-526b-8b8b-1534fcaf2bea', 'word_count': 350, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf0e96fd-b284-526b-8b8b-1534fcaf2bea'}, {'abstract': 'JPMorgan Chase is making changes to its policy on Internet-based payday lenders. | John C. Malone is moving to re-enter the cable business. | Federal authorities are scrutinizing Microsoft’s involvement with companies and officials accused of paying bribes overseas. | Bill Gross is auctioning off some rare stamps.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/03/20/jpmorgans-new-policy-on-payday-lenders/', 'snippet': 'JPMorgan Chase is making changes to its policy on Internet-based payday lenders. | John C. Malone is moving to re-enter the cable business. | Federal authorities are scrutinizing Microsoft’s involvement with companies and officials accused of payi...', 'lead_paragraph': 'JPMorgan Chase is moving to protect customers whose accounts are tapped by Internet-based payday lenders, planning to give those customers more power to stop withdrawals and close their accounts, Jessica Silver-Greenberg reports in DealBook. Under the changes, to be announced on Wednesday, JPMorgan is also limiting the fees it charges customers when the withdrawals trigger penalties.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'JPMorgan’s New Policy on Payday Lenders', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-20T11:38:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/81b5a9bf-cdd2-544c-a59f-681196196b8a', 'word_count': 1724, 'uri': 'nyt://article/81b5a9bf-cdd2-544c-a59f-681196196b8a'}, {'abstract': 'In his new collection of essays, Mr. Hemon writes about growing up in Sarajevo and his life in Chicago.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/20/waiting-for-catastrophes-aleksandar-hemon-talks-about-the-book-of-my-lives/', 'snippet': 'In his new collection of essays, Mr. Hemon writes about growing up in Sarajevo and his life in Chicago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1992, Aleksandar Hemon was visiting Chicago when war broke out in his home country, Bosnia. Chicago became his adopted home, and he soon became a highly praised writer of fiction. In 2004, he received a MacArthur “genius” grant. Mr. Hemon’s new book, “The Book of My Lives,” collects nonfiction pieces about his upbringing in Sarajevo and his life in America. In a recent e-mail interview, Mr. Hemon discussed displacement, visiting Sarajevo now, the purpose of art and more. Below are edited excerpts from the conversation:', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/20/books/20hemon/20hemon-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 815, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/20/books/20hemon/20hemon-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 815}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/20/books/20hemon/20hemon-jumbo.jpg', '