hreatened Wildlife', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endangered and Extinct Species', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poaching (Wildlife)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Convention on International Trade in Endangered Species', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bangkok (Thailand)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cameroon', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chad', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-20T13:43:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bettina Wassener', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bettina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wassener', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3008aab8-5676-540a-b8e8-bb29ee22298a', 'word_count': 415, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3008aab8-5676-540a-b8e8-bb29ee22298a'}, {'abstract': 'The season’s seven episodes averaged 11.5 million viewers a week, PBS said after it received updated Nielsen numbers that included digital video recorder playback.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/20/downton-season-3-sets-pbs-record/', 'snippet': 'The season’s seven episodes averaged 11.5 million viewers a week, PBS said after it received updated Nielsen numbers that included digital video recorder playback.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The third season of “Downton Abbey” was even more popular than previously believed. The season’s seven episodes averaged 11.5 million viewers a week, PBS said Tuesday after it received updated Nielsen numbers that included digital video recorder playbacks. Earlier numbers suggested that seven million to eight million viewers had tuned in for each episode. The total audience — up about 65 percent from the second season — makes the third season of “Downton” the most popular drama ever televised by PBS. The show’s online viewership was counted separately. But there, too, a record was set: The public broadcaster said there were 900,000 video streams on the “Masterpiece” Web site the day after the Season 3 finale, the most for the site.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Downton’ Season 3 Sets PBS Record', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Downton’ Season 3 Sets PBS Record', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-20T14:02:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a1362f6-345c-5df7-9fb6-65f783060204', 'word_count': 121, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a1362f6-345c-5df7-9fb6-65f783060204'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/20/what-were-reading-653/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Southern Foodways Alliance: It must be spring: Hansen’s Sno-Bliz in New Orleans has started serving sno-balls again. — Julia Moskin', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-20T14:04:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk