0', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Dunlap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Dunlap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8267d2a1-173d-566e-a3dc-1bd139fa755f', 'word_count': 524, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8267d2a1-173d-566e-a3dc-1bd139fa755f'}, {'abstract': 'In-flight allergy reactions to tree nuts and peanuts have been reported by only small numbers of passengers, and scientists are uncertain whether dust from the nuts poses serious airborne risks to travelers, but many allergy sufferers take a pro-active stance, a new study indicates.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/20/wisdom-from-flyers-with-nut-allergies/', 'snippet': 'In-flight allergy reactions to tree nuts and peanuts have been reported by only small numbers of passengers, and scientists are uncertain whether dust from the nuts poses serious airborne risks to travelers, but many allergy sufferers take a pro-a...', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Roxanne Palin of Manhattan travels by plane with her family, some of whom are allergic to tree nuts or peanuts, she has a standing battle plan. She books flights in advance so that the three with allergies can sit together, and makes sure they bring their own food and beverages. She swabs their seats and table trays with alcohol pads or baby wipes. She packs eight doses of self-injectable epinephrine, including back-ups, in case any of them has an allergic reaction.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/science/16wellpeanut/16wellpeanut-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 484, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/16/science/16wellpeanut/16wellpeanut-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 484}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/science/16wellpeanut/16wellpeanut-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 825, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/science/16wellpeanut/16wellpeanut-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1376, 'width': 1707, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/science/16wellpeanut/16wellpeanut-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/16/science/16wellpeanut/16wellpeanut-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/16/science/16wellpeanut/16wellpeanut-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Wisdom From Flyers With Nut Allergies', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALLERGIES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Epinephrine (Drug)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Peanuts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-20T14:53:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jan Hoffman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoffman', 'qualifier': None, 'tit