'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flegenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/604ee4f9-76a4-5a76-8a99-eec6308cf026', 'word_count': 1183, 'uri': 'nyt://article/604ee4f9-76a4-5a76-8a99-eec6308cf026'}, {'abstract': 'Hugh Martin’s war began while he was watching television in a friend’s living room, showing off his military knowledge. In less than a year, he was in Iraq himself.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/20/longing-for-the-test-of-war-as-a-young-man/', 'snippet': 'Hugh Martin’s war began while he was watching television in a friend’s living room, showing off his military knowledge. In less than a year, he was in Iraq himself.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The war began for me while I was sitting on a couch in a living room. Like many people, I watched it all commence on television. At a friend’s house on campus, I sat with a few college friends and drank Bud Ice from bottles. We weren’t drinking beer because of the war; we were drinking simply because, being in college, it was something we often did. White smoke from an explosion would burst up from the cityscape of Baghdad as the sound echoed through the dark. Yellow tracers from antiaircraft fire sprayed randomly into the sky. The ticker on the bottom of the screen euphemistically summarized what was happening (while adding some alliteration and a subtle rhyme): “Large explosion rocks Iraq’s capital.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Longing for the Test of War as a Young Man', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'n