haheed: The Dream and Death of Benazir Bhutto,” a one-woman show written and performed by Anna Khaja at the Culture Project, explores the assassinated prime minister of Pakistan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A modernizing democrat or a “kleptocrat in a Hermès scarf”? Pakistan’s “daughter of destiny” (the title of her autobiography) or puppet of the West? That Benazir Bhutto, a two-time prime minister of Pakistan educated at Harvard and Oxford, contained not merely multitudes but multitudes of contradictions, would seem to be the premise of the uneven one-woman show “Shaheed: The Dream and Death of Benazir Bhutto,” written and performed by Anna Khaja at the Culture Project. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/20/theater/20shaheed-web/20shaheed-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/20/theater/20shaheed-web/20shaheed-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/20/theater/20shaheed-web/20shaheed-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/20/theater/20shaheed-web/20shaheed-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1200, 'width': 1800, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/20/theater/20shaheed-web/20shaheed-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/20/theater/20shaheed-web/20shaheed-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/20/theater/20shaheed-web/20shaheed-web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Many Strands Make Up One Woman', 'kicker': 'Theater Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'One Woman and Her Multitudes of Contradictions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bhutto, Benazir', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Culture Project', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Khaja, Anna', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Michele, Heather', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-20T18:34:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Saltz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saltz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/179cadaf-5997-5f66-997f-6dac65e618d1', 'word_count': 439, 'uri': 'nyt://article/179cadaf-5997-5f66-997f-6dac65e618d1'}, {'abstract': 'Derek Jeter received a cortisone shot after complaining of ankle stiffness, and General Manager Brian Cashman acknowledged he could begin the season on the disabled list.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/20/yankees-say-jeter-may-not-be-ready-for-opener/', 'snippet': 'Derek Jeter received a cortisone shot after complaining of ankle stiffness, and General Manager Brian Cashman acknowledged he could begin the season on the disabled list.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TAMPA, Fla. — It’s Derek Jeter, so people automatically assume he will exceed normal standards. But it is possible that not even Jeter will be able to make the Yankees’ opening day lineup less than sixth months after fracturing his left ankle and needing surgery to repair it.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yankees Say Jeter May Not Be Ready for Opener', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Yankees Say Jeter May Not Be Ready for Opener', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jeter, Derek', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-20T18:34:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Kerasotis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kerasotis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9dbdf002-996c-5555-a1bd-b6840a00d0bb', 'word_count': 652, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9dbdf002-996c-5555-a1bd-b6840a00d0bb'}, {'abstract': 'Giants Coach Tom Coughlin once tried to hire Chip Kelly, the new coach of the Eagles, but was turned down.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/20/chip-kelly-could-have-been-a-giant/', 'snippet': 'Giants Coach Tom Coughlin once tried to hire Chip Kelly, the new coach of the Eagles, but was turned down.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PHOENIX — Keep this in mind when the Giants and Eagles play: Giants Coach Tom Coughlin tried to hire new Eagles Coach Chip Kelly as a quality control coach not that long ago and was turned down. Kelly was the offensive coordinator at the University of New Hampshire, early in his meteoric rise, when the Giants came calling in 2006. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/sports/football/22kelly/22kelly-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 416, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/22/sports/football/22kelly/22kelly-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 416}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/sports/football/22kelly/22kelly-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 710, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/sports/football/22kelly/22kelly-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1421, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/sports/football/22kelly/22kelly-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/22/sports/football/22kelly/22kelly-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/sports/football/22kelly/22kelly-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Chip Kelly Could Have Been a Giant', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coaches and Managers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coughlin, Tom', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kelly, Chip', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Philadelphia Eagles', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of New Hampshire', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-20T18:39:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judy Battista', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Battista', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad33ed53-89a4-579f-b414-c342c2b31c62', 'word_count': 294, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad33ed53-89a4-579f-b414-c342c2b31c62'}, {'abstract': 'Lawmakers love to talk about cutting spending. They just don’t like to do it.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/20/nimby-deficit-hawks/', 'snippet': 'Lawmakers love to talk about cutting spending. They just don’t like to do it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jerry Moran often repeated the Republican party’s magical incantation when he was running for senator from Kansas in 2010: “We don’t have a revenue problem – we have a spending problem.” After he was elected, he continued the drumbeat, and supported using the debt ceiling as a threat to enact more budget cuts. He opposed the 2011 budget deal that led to the sequester, not because he was against the sequester but because it didn’t cut spending enough.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'NIMBY Deficit Hawks', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budget Control Act (2011)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'nam