2013/03/21/health/parental-study-shows-rise-in-autism-spectrum-cases.html', 'snippet': 'The chances of a school-aged child receiving a diagnosis rose 72 percent in 2011-12 from 2007, but most of the increase was because of previously undiagnosed cases, a report said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The likelihood of a school-aged American child receiving a diagnosis of autism, Asperger syndrome or a related developmental disorder increased 72 percent in 2011-12 from 2007, according to an analysis of a phone survey of parents released Wednesday by the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention and the Health Resources and Services Administration.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Parental Study Shows Rise in Autism Spectrum Cases', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Parental Study Shows Rise In Autism Spectrum Cases', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hoffman, Jan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Autism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Centers for Disease Control and Prevention', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Asperger's Syndrome", 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-20T23:37:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jan Hoffman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoffman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0219af55-0372-5d61-bc40-0117a32d6f38', 'word_count': 641, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0219af55-0372-5d61-bc40-0117a32d6f38'}, {'abstract': 'Ahead of renovations, a look at the interior workings of the Metropolitan Opera.', 'web_ur