s.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A War, Before and After, Part 5', 'kicker': 'Home Fires', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003-11)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterans', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Marine Corps', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-21T01:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Josiah White and Maurice Decaul', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Josiah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'White', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Maurice', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Decaul', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab2a7f35-443e-5f0f-8516-3c07eaf1cfb7', 'word_count': 1093, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab2a7f35-443e-5f0f-8516-3c07eaf1cfb7'}, {'abstract': 'As the Supreme Court prepares to take up the question of same-sex marriage, it seems worth remembering how much has changed without the Supreme Court’s ever addressing the issue directly.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/20/wedding-bells/', 'snippet': 'As the Supreme Court prepares to take up the question of same-sex marriage, it seems worth remembering how much has changed without the Supreme Court’s ever addressing the issue directly.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I was at the Library of Congress the other day, doing some research in Justice Harry A. Blackmun’s collected papers there (an amazing gift that keeps on giving to anyone interested in the history of the Supreme Court in the last three decades of the 20th century). Thinking about the same-sex marriage cases that the court will hear next week, it occurred to me to see whether Justice Blackmun, who annotated nearly every piece of paper that came across his desk, had recorded any thoughts about a case that arrived at the court in 1971, Baker v. Nelson.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wedding Bells', 'kicker': 'Linda Greenhouse', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitution (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Referendums', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baker, Jack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blackmun, Harry A', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kennedy, Anthony M', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Civil Liberties Union', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Minnesota', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-21T01:00:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Linda Greenhouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Linda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenhouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/19f4c08b-97f9-575c-a991-886811ea4380', 'word_count': 1651, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19f4c08b-97f9-575c-a991-886811ea4380'}, {'abstract': 'The budget cuts known as the sequester now threaten basic health care for two million American Indians.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/21/opinion/the-sequester-hits-the-indian-health-service.html', 'snippet': 'The budget cuts known as the sequester now threaten basic health care for two million American Indians.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Congressional Republicans who brought us the mindless budget cuts known as the sequester have shown remarkable indifference to life-sustaining government services, American jobs and other programs. So what do they make of the country’s commitments to American Indians, its longstanding obligations to tribal governments under the Constitution and treaties dating back centuries?', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Sequester Hits the Reservation', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Sequester Hits the Reservation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Native Americans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indian Health Service', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-21T01:00:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3a93bcd-0b44-5925-8593-ba6bd20fd845', 'word_count': 495, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3a93bcd-0b44-5925-8593-ba6bd20fd845'}, {'abstract': 'How did Dr. Sexton lose the confidence of so many faculty members? By ignoring us.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/21/opinion/the-war-at-nyu.html', 'snippet': 'How did Dr. Sexton lose the confidence of so many faculty members? By ignoring us.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAST week the faculty of arts and science of New York University approved a no-confidence resolution against the university’s president, John Sexton. I had introduced the resolution in December, and in the ensuing months it generated one of the largest campus debates in recent memory. The final no-confidence vote, the first in N.Y.U. history, was decisive: 298 to 224. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The War in Washington Square', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The War in Washington Square', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sexton, John E', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lew, Jacob J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington Square Park (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-21T01:00:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Goodwin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goodwin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e771be7-e813-538a-97d6-866326dd223f', 'word_count': 727, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e771be7-e813-538a-97d6-866326dd223f'}, {'abstract': 'The financial regulator can — and should — force corporations to disclose their political donations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/21/opinion/companies-show-us-the-money.html', 'snippet': 'The financial regulator can — and should — force corporations to disclose their political donations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ON Tuesday, the Senate Banking Committee gave Mary Jo White, President Obama’s choice to lead the Securities and Exchange Commission, a rousing show of support, voting 21 to 1 to send her nomination to the full Senate for a vote. Ms. White, who is likely to be confirmed as the S.E.C. chairwoman, will need that bipartisan backing as she takes on a host of challenges at the nation’s top financial regulator.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Companies: Show Us the Money', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributors', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Companies: Show Us The Money', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'White, Mary Jo', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corporations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-21T01:00:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas P. DiNapoli and Bill de Blasio', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': 'P.', 'lastname': 'DiNapoli', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'de Blasio', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9703e9e-30b2-536f-bdf5-2091f639820a', 'word_count': 775, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9703e9e-30b2-536f-bdf5-2091f639820a'}, {'abstract': 'Many jobs today require technology skills, and job seekers who don’t go online miss opportunities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/21/business/a-campaign-to-help-people-learn-internet-skills.html', 'snippet': 'Many jobs today require technology skills, and job seekers who don’t go online miss opportunities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE Advertising Council and Connect2Compete, a nonprofit group whose goal is to eliminate the digital divide in the United States, are introducing a public service campaign to help those who are not digitally literate find free training to obtain these skills.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/21/business/media/21adco/21adco-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 405, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/21/business/media/21adco/21adco-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 405}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/21/business/media/21adco/21adco-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 540, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/21/business/media/21adco/21adco-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 540, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/21/business/media/21adco/21adco-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnai