ts', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Sandomir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sandomir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/55fd73aa-030b-5c4d-bb59-d92c81114ea7', 'word_count': 674, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55fd73aa-030b-5c4d-bb59-d92c81114ea7'}, {'abstract': 'Louisville will play at Rupp Arena, but it will not face Kentucky, which lost on Tuesday night in the first round of the N.I.T.', 'web_url': 'https://thequad.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/20/louisville-starting-its-run-in-the-home-of-its-rival/', 'snippet': 'Louisville will play at Rupp Arena, but it will not face Kentucky, which lost on Tuesday night in the first round of the N.I.T.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LEXINGTON, Ky. — The question about Kentucky was posed thus to Peyton Siva, the superlative senior point guard for Louisville: “Is there part of you that kind of takes a little satisfaction — not only are you guys the No. 1 seed, but you are playing here, and they’re not even in the N.I.T. anymore?”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/sports/ncaabasketball/22siva/22siva-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 860, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/22/sports/ncaabasketball/22siva/22siva-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 860}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/sports/ncaabasketball/22siva/22siva-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 715, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/sports/ncaabasket