alifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/a30fdeda-e60a-5be6-941c-024ae8a5e490', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/a30fdeda-e60a-5be6-941c-024ae8a5e490'}, {'abstract': 'Hanna Rosin boldly allowed her 2-year-old unfettered access to an iPad for six weeks. It’s not an experiment I’ll duplicate.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/21/parents-of-the-touch-screen-generation-dont-free-your-ipad-yet/', 'snippet': 'Hanna Rosin boldly allowed her 2-year-old unfettered access to an iPad for six weeks. It’s not an experiment I’ll duplicate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every weekend morning, one or the other of my younger children appears early. He or she creeps to the side of my bed, and for a brief moment, I can feel the child’s thoughtful, assessing gaze, but I don’t move. There is usually a pause. Waking Mommy can be a dangerous proposition. But it’s worth it for the prize. “Mommy,” the child whispers, “can I have your iPad?”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/10/12/style/motherlode-doll-picture/motherlode-doll-picture-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 753, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/10/12/style/motherlode-doll-picture/motherlode-doll-picture-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1506, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/10/12/style/motherlode-doll-picture/motherlode-doll-picture-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/10/12/style/mo