 dozens of terrorist bombings. He was later convicted of murder.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Paul Rose, a strident Quebec separatist leader who in October 1970 helped kidnap and, he claimed, strangle a provincial official, inflaming a crisis that pitted terrorists against the Canadian prime minister, Pierre Trudeau, died March 14 in Montreal. He was 69.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/21/world/ROSE-OBIT/ROSE-OBIT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 919, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/21/world/ROSE-OBIT/ROSE-OBIT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 919}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/21/world/ROSE-OBIT/ROSE-OBIT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 669, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/21/world/ROSE-OBIT/ROSE-OBIT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1338, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/21/world/ROSE-OBIT/ROSE-OBIT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/21/world/ROSE-OBIT/ROSE-OBIT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/21/world/ROSE-OBIT/ROSE-OBIT-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Paul Rose, Quebec Separatist Involved in a Kidnapping and Murder, Dies at 69', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Paul Rose, Quebec Separatist Leader, Dies at 69', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rose, Paul (1943-2013)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-21T14:43:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Douglas Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Douglas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/64fb37da-9d9d-540a-92be-192aad532477', 'word_count': 888, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64fb37da-9d9d-540a-92be-192aad532477'}, {'abstract': 'Tina Fey stars as an admissions officer at Princeton in “Admission,” a comedy directed by Paul Weitz.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/22/movies/admission-starring-tina-fey-directed-by-paul-weitz.html', 'snippet': 'Tina Fey stars as an admissions officer at Princeton in “Admission,” a comedy directed by Paul Weitz.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The timing of “Admission,” Paul Weitz’s new comedy, is either clever or cruel — perhaps both. In the next few weeks, word will go forth from colleges across the land about who is in and who is out, as the American higher-education-industrial complex enacts its own Darwinian version of “Project Runway.” As the father of a high school junior, paying my tithe to the test prep gods while preparing to sacrifice most of my worldly goods on the altar of the liberal arts, I can’t tell if I’m part of the intended audience, or if the ratings board should issue a special warning for sensitive parents like me. How could anyone make light of the brutal, capricious system by which our young people are judged and sorted?', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'She’s Not Impressed? Then You’re Not In', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'She’s Not Impressed? Then You’re Not In', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Admission (Movie)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tomlin, Lily', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fey, Tina', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weitz, Paul', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rudd, Paul', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-21T14:51:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f6fe39b-591e-5e5e-b2fc-89597a6ec40f', 'word_count': 971, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f6fe39b-591e-5e5e-b2fc-89597a6ec40f'}, {'abstract': 'The artist will create an installation along a river consisting of 1,000 tents.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/21/ai-weiwei-to-let-1000-tents-bloom-in-germany/', 'snippet': 'The artist will create an installation along a river consisting of 1,000 tents.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Chinese artist Ai Weiwei plans to create a major installation at a festival in Germany this summer consisting of 1,000 tents set up along the Emscher River, the BBC reported.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ai Weiwei to Let 1,000 Tents Bloom in Germany', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, '