g', 'height': 475, 'width': 720, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/21/magazine/video-met-timelapse-copy/video-met-timelapse-copy-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 475, 'width': 720, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/21/magazine/video-met-timelapse-copy/video-met-timelapse-copy-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/21/magazine/video-met-timelapse-copy/video-met-timelapse-copy-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/21/magazine/video-met-timelapse-copy/video-met-timelapse-copy-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Scenes From Two Days at the Met', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-21T15:02:13+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'Stephen Mallon and Catriona Stuart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mallon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Catriona', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stuart', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/a5f44622-12ac-5399-9ef6-5d3c2529e91d', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/a5f44622-12ac-5399-9ef6-5d3c2529e91d'}, {'abstract': 'What it takes to run the Metropolitan Opera.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/24/magazine/the-epic-ups-and-downs-of-peter-gelb.html', 'snippet': 'What it takes to run the Metropolitan Opera.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most mornings Peter Gelb, the 59-year-old general manager of the world’s most prominent opera company, rises between 4 a.m. and 5 a.m. The elegant Upper West Side duplex he shares with his wife is four blocks from Lincoln Center. He puts on a bathrobe and pads downstairs to the kitchen, where he turns on his La Pavoni espresso machine with the hand-levered piston that allows him to feel, amid all he can’t control at the Metropolitan Opera, that he can at least control the quality of his coffee. He fixes a skim-milk cappuccino with two shots of espresso, eats a banana and then sits down in his home office, where the walls are decorated with autographed scores by Verdi, Puccini and Shostakovich and the shelves are filled with hundreds of CDs, including some by his great-uncle, the renowned violinist Jascha Heifetz. Gelb himself has no particular musical gift, but his ability to remain alert while attending 280 or so opera performances and rehearsals a year on apparently very little sleep qualifies him as a virtuoso of some sort.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/magazine/24gelb1/mag-24Gelb-t_CA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 742, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/24/magazine/24gelb1/mag-24Gelb-t_CA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 742}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/magazine/24gelb1/24gelb1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 761, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/magazine/24gelb1/24gelb1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1559, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/magazine/24gelb1/mag-24Gelb-t_CA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/24/magazine/24gelb1/mag-24Gelb-t_CA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/magazine/24gelb1/mag-24Gelb-t_CA1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Epic Ups and Downs of Peter Gelb', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Operatic Reign of Peter Gelb', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Chip', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gelb, Peter', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-21T15:03:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chip Brown', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brown', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8296a643-ee66-58b6-bff4-3903f96cb81e', 'word_count': 7269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8296a643-ee66-58b6-bff4-3903f96cb81e'}, {'abstract': 'The men were said to use others’ self-immolation deaths for publicity purposes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/22/world/asia/3-tibetans-sentenced-in-immolation-cases.html', 'snippet': 'The men were said to use others’ self-immolation deaths for publicity purposes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — Three Tibetans from Qinghai Province have been given prison sentences for “inciting state secession,” according to a statement on an official provincial Web site. On Monday, a court in Haidong Prefecture sentenced the Tibetans — Kalsang Dhondup, Jigme Thabkey and Lobsang — to terms of six, five and four years, respectively. The online announcement said that the men used self-immolations by Tibetans for publicity purposes and circulated texts and photographs related to Tibetan independence, spreading “bad influence locally and internationally.” Since 2009, at least 109 Tibetans have set fire to themselves to protest Chinese rule, and most have died. To deter the act, Chinese officials are trying to prosecute people associated with those who commit self-immolation. Tibetans opposed to Chinese rule say those who self-immolated did it out of frustration with Chinese policies.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '3 Tibetans Sentenced in Immolation Cases', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China: Punishments for Tibetan Protests', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immolation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tibet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-21T15:04:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/699e6c66-b5cb-5a45-b4e7-cc020e08097e', 'word_count': 135, 'uri': 'nyt://article/699e6c66-b5cb-5a45-b4e7-cc020e08097e'}, {'abstract': 'Underdogs will, as usual, wreck a lot of N.C.A.A. tournament brackets. But no one, not even a fan on the court, seems able to stop the Miami Heat.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/22/sports/you-wont-win-but-the-heat-probably-will.html', 'snippet': 'Underdogs will, as usual, wreck a lot of N.C.A.A. tournament brackets. But no one, not even a fan on the court, seems able to stop the Miami Heat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is officially underdog day (Part 1), when America is united in rooting for a bunch of guys we have never heard of toiling for a university we cannot find on a map, the only acceptable exception being when that bunch of guys can totally ruin your bracket. (And even then, expect office ridicule if you start rooting loudly for Duke.) Because we are all about the underdog, the Round of 64 in the N.C.A.A. men’s basketball tournament tapping into that vein in our national character. Hey, back in 1776, England was the big-money team with the overpaid coach and look what we did then. That was our first 3-pointer at the buzzer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/sports/basketball/22leadingpic/22leadingpic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 454, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/22/sports/basketball/22leadingpic/22leadingpic-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 454}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/sports/basketball/22leadingpic/22leadingpic-jumbo.jpg', '