en Syria and South Korea will not go off as planned in Seoul on Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/21/south-korea-shuts-door-on-syria-match/', 'snippet': 'The planned closed-door exhibition match between Syria and South Korea will not go off as planned in Seoul on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is hard to imagine in the midst of the bloody Syrian conflict anything happening other than the daily task of survival. Yet despite the descent into chaos, the Syrian national team has remained intact, escaping the implosion of its country.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Door Shut on South Korea-Syria Match', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-21T15:48:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roy Ghim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ghim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aade7a86-dda1-51a5-ade0-153dd7cbde2e', 'word_count': 526, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aade7a86-dda1-51a5-ade0-153dd7cbde2e'}, {'abstract': 'Nearly two-thirds of Americans favor giving illegal immigrants an opportunity for legal status, according to a poll by the Public Religion Research Institute and the Brookings Institution.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/22/us/broad-support-for-path-to-citizenship-poll-finds.html', 'snippet': 'Nearly two-thirds of Americans favor giving illegal immigrants an opportunity for legal status, according to a poll by the Public Religion Research Institute and the Brookings Institution.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nearly two-thirds of Americans favor giving illegal immigrants in the country an opportunity for legal status with a path to citizenship, according to a poll published Thursday by the Public Religion Research Institute and the Brookings Institution. Support for an earned path to citizenship for those immigrants came from 71 percent of Democrats and also a majority, 53 percent, of Republicans, the poll found.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Path to Citizenship for Immigrants Draws Support Across Party Lines, Survey Finds', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Path to Citizenship for Immigrants Draws Support Across Party Lines, Survey Finds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Preston, Julia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigrants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Citizenship and Naturalization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brookings Institution', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-21T15:51:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d872fc2c-c90e-501d-b852-9a5178fdd7fb', 'word_count': 844, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d872fc2c-c90e-501d-b852-9a5178fdd7fb'}, {'abstract': 'Readers respond to a recent review of Sheryl Sandberg’s “Lean In.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/24/books/review/lean-in.html', 'snippet': 'Readers respond to a recent review of Sheryl Sandberg’s “Lean In.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Lean In’', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Lean In’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-21T15:56:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/5589c2bf-cac4-5ac4-8585-6da1e7dffd95', 'word_count': 749, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5589c2bf-cac4-5ac4-8585-6da1e7dffd95'}, {'abstract': 'There is a downside to working from home: chores.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/21/my-new-office-a-parking-spot/', 'snippet': 'There is a downside to working from home: chores.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before my fiancé, James, and I bought our first car, we discussed money, fantasy vacation homes, insurance, pleather, climate control, climate change and unborn children. But perhaps more important was what we didn’t discuss. And that was parking. We spent about 30 seconds on it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'My New Office: A Parking Space', 'kicker': 'Townies', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parking', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-21T16:00:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Sarkissian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sarkissian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/09051bed-145d-5c6d-9159-f374d387137a', 'word_count': 993, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09051bed-145d-5c6d-9159-f374d387137a'}, {'abstract': 'As it approved legislation to pay for federal spending through September, the Republican-led House also passed a blueprint for a smaller government.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/22/us/politics/house-passes-plan-to-avert-federal-shutdown.html', 'snippet': 'As it approved legislation to pay for federal spending through September, the Republican-led House also passed a blueprint for a smaller government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The House gave final approval on Thursday to legislation to keep government financed through September, and it also passed a Republican blueprint that enshrined the party’s vision of a balanced budget that would substantially shrink spending, privatize Medicare and rewrite the tax code to make it simpler.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/us/BUDGET-1/BUDGET-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 367, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/22/us/BUDGET-1/BUDGET-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 367}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/us/BUDGET-1/BUDGET-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 626, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/us/BUDGET-1/BUDGET-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1252, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/us/BUDGET-1/BUDGET-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/22/us/BUDGET-1/BUDGET-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/us/BUDGET-1/BUDGET-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'House Passes Money Bill and Budget Blueprint', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'House Passes Money Bill and Budget Blueprint', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-21T16:01:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Weisman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weisman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4906630-a9c3-57f6-955f-5fc79cb716c5', 'word_count': 951, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4906630-a9c3-57f6-955f-5fc79cb716c5'}, {'abstract': 'Sally Jewell, the chief executive of Recreational Equipment Inc., won approval of the Senate Energy and Natural Resources Committee by a large bipartisan margin.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/22/us/senate-panel-approves-sally-jewell-for-interior-dept-post.html', 'snippet': 'Sally Jewell, the chief executive of Recreational Equipment Inc., won approval of the Senate Energy and Natural Resources Committee by a large bipartisan margin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON – President Obama’s nominee to lead the Interior Department, Sally Jewell, cleared her first hurdle on the way to confirmation on Thursday, winning approval of the Senate Energy and Natural Resources Committee by a large bipartisan margin.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Senate Panel Approves Obama’s Choice for Interior Dept.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Interior Nominee Clears Committee', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Broder, John M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jewell, Sally', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Interior Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-21T16:04:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By John M. Broder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d964b6ad-6622-525d-a4cd-436c80eb5eab', 'word_count': 469, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d964b6ad-6622-525d-a4cd-436c80eb5eab'}, {'abstract': 'Tom Clements, the slain head of the Colorado prison system, reminded me how and why prisons matter.', 'web_url': 'https://bruni.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/21/redemptions-advocate/', 'snippet': 'Tom Clements, the slain head of the Colorado prison system, reminded me how and why prisons matter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most Americans don’t think or talk much about the way prisons in this country are funded or run. We want a vague, blanket assurance that our politicians and their appointees are being tough on crime. We pay attention to verdicts and to sentences but not to what happens afterward, to the experience that a convicted criminal has over the years before he or she most likely reenters society. We forget—or we simply don’t bother to recognize—that the nature of this experience has an effect on whether the criminal breaks the law again. We want to feel safe, and yet we’re utterly uneducated about, and inattentive to, a part of our criminal justice system that in fact has enormous bearing on our safety.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Redemption’s Advocate', 'kicker': 'Frank Bruni', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clements, Tom (1954-2013)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colorado', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-21T16:06:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Frank Bruni', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Frank', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bruni', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/578a5a7e-6013-528f-916e-5842974b42fc', 'word_count': 1211, 'uri': 'nyt://article/578a5a7e-6013-528f-916e-5842974b42fc'}, {'abstract': 'Following is a complete transcript of President Obama’s remarks in Jerusalem on March 21, 2013', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/22/world/middleeast/transcript-of-obamas-speech-in-israel.html', 'snippet': 'Following is a complete transcript of President Obama’s remarks in Jerusalem on March 21, 2013', 'lead_paragraph': 'Following is a complete transcript of President Obama’s remarks in Jerusalem on March 21, 2013. (Transcript courtesy of Federal News Service).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Transcript of Obama’s Speech in Israel', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Speeches and Statements', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-21T16:11:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Text', '_id': 'nyt://article/78ed9419-19d1-5459-9725-e3076ff12bbb', 'word_count': 5654, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78ed9419-19d1-5459-9725-e3076ff12bbb'}, {'abstract': 'Patrick Healy interviewed the composer Tim Minchin about the challenges of bringing Roald Dahl’s work to Broadway.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/theater/100000002125855/matilda-comes-to-broadway.html', 'snippet': 'Patrick Healy interviewed the composer Tim Minchin about the challenges of bringing Roald Dahl’s work to Broadway.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Patrick Healy interviewed the composer Tim Minchin about the challenges of bringing Roald Dahl’s work to Broadway.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/20/arts/video-minchin-matilda-musical/video-minchin-matilda-musical-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/20/arts/vide