ias-in-auto-loans/', 'snippet': 'The Consumer Financial Protection Bureau takes on auto dealers and lenders who are engaging in discriminatory lending practices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Consumer Financial Protection Bureau laid out its authority over auto lenders on Thursday and warned them to comply with fair lending requirements. The agency said that it was issuing the new instructions in response to discriminatory practices that resulted in Hispanic and black borrowers’ illegally being charged higher rates than whites for auto loans. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Consumer Agency Warns Lenders on Bias in Auto Loans', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cordray, Richard', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consumer Financial Protection Bureau', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-21T18:49:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nadia Taha', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nadia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taha', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fba06b99-e645-57b5-b89c-ad213b738eb9', 'word_count': 291, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fba06b99-e645-57b5-b89c-ad213b738eb9'}, {'abstract': 'Long-haul truck drivers who drink coffee or other caffeinated drinks are significantly less likely to have an accident than their uncaffeinated peers, a new study found.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/21/caffeine-may-boost-driver-safety/', 'snippet': 'Long-haul truc