Terry Gilliam and Jimmy Page. In addition to supplying great books, the store became a go-to destination for royalty-free images pulled from Victorian-era women’s magazines or 19th-century garden manuals that artists could incorporate into their work. For those who considered the shop a trove of ready-made inspiration, the news that it will close at the end of the month comes as a huge shock. “The Charing Cross Road area of London has changed from a haven for small shops to an area for mainstream brands and fashion,” the store’s manager Tim Matthews wrote in an e-mail. “Beyond that, though, image resources are increasingly found online and Dover Publications are moving steadily into that world.” Among the brilliant, obscure volumes that made up the shop’s stock in trade were Gustave Doré’s illustrations of London; Jan Vredeman De Vries’s book of 16th-century architectural engravings, “Studies in Perspective”; and Jim Harner’s collection of 1,000 black-and-white animal drawings.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Endnotes | The Dover Bookshop', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dover Publications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-21T19:00:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Azadeh Ensha', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Azadeh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ensha', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/578175b2-67c3-56cf-a4c7-7e6c5571dd84', 'word_count': 181, 'uri': 'nyt://article/578175b2-67c3-56cf-a4c7-7e6c5571dd84'}, {'abstract': 'Israeli politicians have tried and failed to convince President Obama to release Jonathan Pollard, a former United States Navy intelligence analyst serving a life term in a North Carolina prison for spying for Israel. Now it is Miss Israel’s turn.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/21/israeli-beauty-queen-next-in-line-to-press-obama-to-release-spy/', 'snippet': 'Israeli politicians have tried and failed to convince President Obama to release Jonathan Pollard, a former United States Navy intelligence analyst serving a life term in a North Carolina prison for spying for Israel. Now it is Miss Israel’s turn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last Updated, Friday, 9:19 a.m. As my colleague Isabel Kershner explained, Israeli politicians have taken turns this week pressing President Obama to release Jonathan Pollard, a former United States Navy intelligence analyst serving a life term in a North Carolina prison for spying for Israel. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Israeli Beauty Queen Next in Line to Press Obama to Release Spy', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage and Intelligence Services', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pollard, Jonathan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Navy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-21T19:08:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/73c77f25-290a-5710-a5f2-d1329b7bfa29', 'word_count': 827, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73c77f25-290a-5710-a5f2-d1329b7bfa29'}, {'abstract': 'Cooper-Moore and Lonnie Holley will perform in conjunction with the “Blues for Smoke” exhibition at the Whitney Museum of American Art.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/22/arts/a-jazz-pairing-that-plays-outside-the-lines.html', 'snippet': 'Cooper-Moore and Lonnie Holley will perform in conjunction with the “Blues for Smoke” exhibition at the Whitney Museum of American Art.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Miser moved to New York in the mid-1990s mostly for love, it’s true, but also because of a growing interest in avant-garde jazz. And at the time, it was still possible to catch a pioneer like Cecil Taylor, Anthony Braxton or even Ornette Coleman in an intimate setting somewhere in downtown Manhattan. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Jazz Pairing That Plays Outside the Lines', 'kicker': 'Weekend Miser', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Jazz Pairing That Plays Outside the Lines', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-21T19:09:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By A. C. Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c62d86c-5884-5340-958b-dfbcc15206e1', 'word_count': 430, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c62d86c-5884-5340-958b-dfbcc15206e1'}, {'abstract': 'A column about LED light bulbs generated a lot of reader e-mail, probably because LED represents change. And change is always scary. David Pogue addresses some reader concerns.', 'web_url': 'https://pogue.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/21/addressing-fears-about-led-light-bulbs/', 'snippet': 'A column about LED light bulbs generated a lot of reader e-mail, probably because LED represents change. And change is always scary. David Pogue addresses some reader concerns.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In my Times column Thursday, I reviewed a new generation of LED light bulbs. They last 25 times as long as regular bulbs, use maybe one-eighth the electricity, work with dimmers, turn on instantly to full brightness and remain cool to the touch. A big drawback has always been cost, but now, I noted, the prices have fallen.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Addressing Fears About LED Light Bulbs', 'kicker': 'Pogue&#039;s Posts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Light Bulbs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electronics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Light-Emitting Diodes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-21T19:15:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Pogue', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogue', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5cf1f0b-911d-5d54-b508-1d386ed776e0', 'word_count': 969, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5cf1f0b-911d-5d54-b508-1d386ed776e0'}, {'abstract': 'The cleric, Mohammad Said Ramada al-Bouti, was the most important religious figure to be killed so far in the Syrian civil war.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/22/world/middleeast/senior-pro-assad-sunni-imam-in-syria-is-assassinated.html', 'snippet': 'The cleric, Mohammad Said Ramada al-Bouti, was the most important religious figure to be killed so far in the Syrian civil war.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — A large explosion killed at least 42 people inside a central Damascus mosque on Thursday, including the top Sunni cleric in Syria, one of the major remaining Sunni supporters of President Bashar al-Assad’s embattled government in the civil war.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/world/22syriaweb1/22syriaweb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 361, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/22/world/22syriaweb1/22syriaweb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 361}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/world/22syriaweb1/22syriaweb1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 616, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/world/22syriaweb1/22syriaweb1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1232, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/world/22syriaweb1/22syriaweb1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/22/world/22syriaweb1/22syriaweb1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/world/22syriaweb1/22syriaweb1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subTy