en)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Iona College', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Collegiate Athletic Assn', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ohio State University', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-21T19:27:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Jordan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jordan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dfb71580-7d50-5af5-a55a-16a5d58e6bbc', 'word_count': 680, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dfb71580-7d50-5af5-a55a-16a5d58e6bbc'}, {'abstract': 'With the sale to the Russian oil giant, BP aimed to resolve one of two problems that have clouded its future and depressed its stock price.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/22/business/global/rosneft-finalizes-acquisition-of-tnk-bp.html', 'snippet': 'With the sale to the Russian oil giant, BP aimed to resolve one of two problems that have clouded its future and depressed its stock price.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — BP, the British oil company, said on Thursday that it had completed the sale of its 50 percent stake in the Russian affiliate TNK-BP. In a series of transactions, BP will receive about $12.5 billion in cash and will own 19.75 percent of Rosneft, the largest Russian oil company. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rosneft Completes Acquisition of TNK-BP', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'BP Completes Deal With Rosneft', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rosneft', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TNK-BP', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BP Plc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-21T19:31:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stanley Reed', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stanley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/746da8fe-06d9-5716-bf31-e2d1034e0b74', 'word_count': 574, 'uri': 'nyt://article/746da8fe-06d9-5716-bf31-e2d1034e0b74'}, {'abstract': 'Europe’s losses from a Cypriot banking collapse would be minimal compared with the havoc that a Greek exit would have created.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/22/business/global/a-cyprexit-might-not-hurt-euro-zone-much.html', 'snippet': 'Europe’s losses from a Cypriot banking collapse would be minimal compared with the havoc that a Greek exit would have created.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Cyprus exit from the euro union, if it comes to that, would have a devastating effect on the country’s citizens, who are among the most indebted in the euro zone. And for European unity and diplomacy, the Cyprus debacle has already been at least a short-term disaster.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Euro Zone, a Cyprus Exit Would Have Little Impact', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Exit From the Euro by CyprusWould Hurt Its Citizens, but Little Affect Europe', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subjec