}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/arts/22SIDEBAR/22SIDEBAR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/22/arts/22SIDEBAR/22SIDEBAR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/arts/22SIDEBAR/22SIDEBAR-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'His Work Is the Cat’s Meow', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'His Work Is the Cat’s Meow', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tribeca Performing Arts Center', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-21T21:50:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kim Palchikoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Palchikoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/01fb9a91-31b2-5fab-b2e8-a230351983ee', 'word_count': 604, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01fb9a91-31b2-5fab-b2e8-a230351983ee'}, {'abstract': 'Timberlake’s latest album delivers its artistry through its familiarity.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/21/justin-timberlake-keeps-it-retro/', 'snippet': 'Timberlake’s latest album delivers its artistry through its familiarity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In pop music, hindsight is the key to relevance. There is the Warholian logic to the iTunes chart: the artist who appropriates a particular time period with the most cunning and skill feels the freshest. The Los Angeles-based musical duo Rhye have received critical acclaim recently for evoking the early-‘80s-era “quiet storm” of Sade. Azealia Banks channels the 1990s with her best Crystal Waters imitation with about the same success as Lady Gaga’s echoing of Blond Ambition-era Madonna. (Remember that?) The moody atmosphere of Drake’s oeuvre picks up the pieces that Aaliyah left behind in 2001. And the dance-pop white noise that inhabits the radio today is, of course, a rehash of the Euro-pop and rave culture of yesteryear that Daft Punk helped foster. The French D.J. duo, who recently signed to Columbia and have a new album coming out in time for summer, are said to be working with the funk legend Niles Rodgers for their anticipated new release, situating themselves comfortably in the 1970s disco revival moment that has become a staple of underground night-life culture in Paris, London and New York.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Justin Timberlake Keeps it Retro', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'AALIYAH', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Banks, Azealia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lady Gaga', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Timbaland', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Timberlake, Justin', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-21T21:55:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Hawgood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hawgood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/05def65d-ada7-582f-afe0-14b2d96fa6f6', 'word_count': 684, 'uri': 'nyt://article/05def65d-ada7-582f-afe0-14b2d96fa6f6'}, {'abstract': 'A concert at Symphony Space on Friday organized by the saxophonist Joe Lovano and the guitarist Bill Frisell will celebrate the influence of their former band mate, the drummer Paul Motian.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/22/arts/music/paul-motian-tribute-at-symphony-space.html', 'snippet': 'A concert at Symphony Space on Friday organized by the saxophonist Joe Lovano and the guitarist Bill Frisell will celebrate the influence of their former band mate, the drummer Paul Motian.', 'lead_paragraph': '“We are going to play one more song,” Reid Anderson, the bassist in the Bad Plus, told an overflow crowd in a large tent at the most recent Newport Jazz Festival. “It’s another Paul Motian song, because we love Paul so much, and his music means so much to us.” This statement met with a rumble of approval — a lot of “yeahs” punctuated the applause — as the band, joined for the occasion by the guitarist Bill Frisell, ventured on.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/arts/22MOTIAN_SPAN/22MOTIAN_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 376, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/22/arts/22MOTIAN_SPAN/22MOTIAN_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 376}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/arts/22MOTIAN_SPAN/22MOTIAN_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 642, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/arts/22MOTIAN_SPAN/22MOTIAN_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1284, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/arts/22MOTIAN_SPAN/22MOTIAN_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/22/arts/22MOTIAN_SPAN/22MOTIAN_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/arts/22MOTIAN_SPAN/22MOTIAN_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tribute to a Drummer Who Moved Jazz On', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tribute to a Drummer Who Moved Jazz On', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Symphony Space', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Motian, Paul', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Frisell, Bill', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lovano, Joe', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-21T21:56:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Chinen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chinen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c9a3c56-3b13-504f-8d97-99d1b1cd0b22', 'word_count': 1190, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c9a3c56-3b13-504f-8d97-99d1b1cd0b22'}, {'abstract': 'Two Bronx graffiti artists go on a daylong quest to finance an ambitious project: the tagging of a big plastic apple at Citi Field.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/22/movies/gimme-the-loot-directed-by-adam-leon.html', 'snippet': 'Two Bronx graffiti artists go on a daylong quest to finance an ambitious project: the tagging of a big plastic apple at Citi Field.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Gimme the Loot,” Adam Leon’s loose and rambunctious debut feature, tells the tale of two young artists scrambling to kick-start an ambitious project. Or, if you prefer, it follows a pair of vandals through a day of improvised criminality. Really, though, it’s both: a celebration of outlaw creativity and entrepreneurial gumption.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Larceny for the Sake of Art', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Larceny For the Sake Of Art', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leon, Adam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-21T21:57:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/6db97a2d-4b5f-574f-846c-f00d70acde72', 'word_count': 376, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6db97a2d-4b5f-574f-846c-f00d70acde72'}, {'abstract': 'The long-gone Biltmore Hotel was the linchpin of Terminal City, now the focus of redevelopment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/24/realestate/a-long-gone-rendezvous-with-1000-rooms.html', 'snippet': 'The long-gone Biltmore Hotel was the linchpin of Terminal City, now the focus of redevelopment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Whether you think of them as quotidian, or “soaring masonry facades enlivened by decorative details,” as does the New York Landmarks Conservancy, the network of 1910s and 1920s building