op of other renovations it says are necessary since Congress has decided to keep it open indefinitely.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON – The United States Southern Command has requested $49 million to build a new prison building at Guantánamo Bay, Cuba, for “special” detainees on top of other renovations it says are necessary since Congress has decided to keep it open indefinitely. That brings the potential taxpayer bill for upgrading the deteriorating facilities to an estimated $195.7 million, the military said on Thursday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Money Requested for New Prison at Guantánamo', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September 11 (2001)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kelly, John F', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mohammed, Khalid Shaikh', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central Intelligence Agency', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cuba', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guantanamo Bay Naval Base (Cuba)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-21T22:32:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5934cd5d-640f-50a7-9416-209a13e17023', 'word_count': 402, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5934cd5d-640f-50a7-9416-209a13e17023'}, {'abstract': 'The Ringling Brothers and Barnum & Bailey Circus has a new show at Barclays Center in Brooklyn.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2013/