e contrast between fast-moving technology and slow-moving laws was on full display on Wednesday at a hearing of the Senate Judiciary Committee on domestic use of drones. The issue was not arming them, because the Federal Aviation Administration bans weaponizing civil aircraft. (Several senators asked about drones outfitted with weapons, though, including nonlethal options like tear gas or stun grenades.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/21/technology/21bits-wald/21bits-wald-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 271, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/21/technology/21bits-wald/21bits-wald-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 271}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/21/technology/21bits-wald/21bits-wald-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 462, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/21/technology/21bits-wald/21bits-wald-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 924, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/21/technology/21bits-wald/21bits-wald-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/21/technology/21bits-wald/21bits-wald-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/21/technology/21bits-wald/21bits-wald-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Drone Cameras May Be High Worry, but They’re Not High Tech', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-21T23:47:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ed2c91b-a41e-58f1-894d-c9885cb39677', 'word_count': 548, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ed2c91b-a41e-58f1-894d-c9885cb39677'}, {'abstract': 'Lockheed Martin will make commercial use of quantum computing, which could solve some business and science problems millions of times faster than can be done today.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/22/technology/testing-a-new-class-of-speedy-computer.html', 'snippet': 'Lockheed Martin will make commercial use of quantum computing, which could solve some business and science problems millions of times faster than can be done today.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VANCOUVER, British Columbia — Our digital age is all about bits, those precise ones and zeros that are the stuff of modern computer code.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/business/QUANTUM/QUANTUM-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/22/business/QUANTUM/QUANTUM-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/business/QUANTUM/QUANTUM-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 631, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name'