 would face a formal investigation into whether he abused the frailty of Liliane Bettencourt, 90, the heiress to the L’Oréal fortune and France’s richest woman, to get funds for his 2007 presidential campaign. Mr. Sarkozy has denied accepting illegal campaign funds from Ms. Bettencourt, either personally or through his party treasurer at the time, Éric Woerth, as alleged by her former butler. Mr. Sarkozy’s lawyer, Thierry Herzog, called the judge’s decision, which indicates that the judge believes that Mr. Sarkozy probably committed a crime, “incoherent” and “unjust.” The lawyer said he would appeal. The ruling does not necessarily mean that Mr. Sarkozy, who lost his re-election bid last May and with it his presidential immunity from prosecution, will stand trial. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'France: Sarkozy Faces Investigation', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'France: Sarkozy Faces Investigation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Erlanger, Steven', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sarkozy, Nicolas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bettencourt, Liliane', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "L'Oreal SA", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-21T23:54:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Erlanger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erlanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/42b7e1f1-5dce-54b9-868d-78913cdfb673', 'word_count': 129, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42b7e1f1-5dce-54b9-868d-78913cdfb673'}, {'abstract': 'Notre Dame will play the last game in the tournament’s second round. Until then, there’s nothing to do but wait.', 'web_url': 'https://thequad.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/21/notre-dame-sits-and-waits/', 'snippet': 'Notre Dame will play the last game in the tournament’s second round. Until then, there’s nothing to do but wait.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DAYTON, Ohio — Notre Dame arrived here Wednesday night and practiced early Thursday evening, just as the action in the N.C.A.A. tournament was getting good. During team stretches in their locker room, they had the television set tuned to the final moments of the St. Mary’s-Memphis game, and they stole more than a few glances at it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Notre Dame Sits and Waits', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball (College)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'NCAA Basketball Championships (Men)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Notre Dame', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-21T23:58:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zach Schonbrun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zach', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schonbrun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1992ebb5-58e9-5fb4-9a78-60332c36fc32', 'word_count': 339, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1992ebb5-58e9-5fb4-9a78-60332c36fc32'}, {'abstract': 'Many of the potters at the Mud, Sweat and Tears Pottery studio in Clinton work in demanding professions, and the pottery seems to play a therapeutic role.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/24/nyregion/mud-sweat-and-tears-pottery-studio-offers-a-form-of-therapy.html', 'snippet': 'Many of the potters at the Mud, Sweat and Tears Pottery studio in Clinton work in demanding professions, and the pottery seems to play a therapeutic role.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A corner storefront glows warmly on a winter night. Inside, a stool and a friendly proprietor beckon. This is a place where you could spend a few hours, or wile away the decades, watch Hell’s Kitchen become Clinton. ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/nyregion/24JOINT1_SPAN/24JOINT1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/24/nyregion/24JOINT1_SPAN/24JOINT1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/nyregion/24JOINT1_SPAN/24JOINT1_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/nyregion/24JOINT1_SPAN/24JOINT1_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/nyregion/24JOINT1_SPAN/24JOINT1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/24/nyregion/24JOINT1_SPAN/24JOINT1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/nyregion/24JOINT1_SPAN/24JOINT1_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Where Dirty Hands Act as Therapy', 'kicker': 'Neighborhood Joint', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Where Dirty Hands Act as Therapy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ceramics and Pottery', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, Ji Hyun', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': "Hell's Kitchen (Manhattan, NY)", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mud, Sweat and Tears Pottery (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-22T00:07:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ji Hyun Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ji', 'middlename': 'Hyun', 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/006d05ac-3dae-5208-94d5-6f5dd5712064', 'word_count': 615, 'uri': 'nyt://article/006d05ac-3dae-5208-94d5-6f5dd5712064'}, {'abstract': 'In their latest video, the activists of Cairo’s Mosireen film collective argue that violent resistance to an unreformed police force is not only justified, but also necessary.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/21/egyptian-activists-defend-use-of-force-against-an-unreformed-police-force/', 'snippet': 'In their latest video, the activists of Cairo’s Mosireen film collective argue that violent resistance to an unreformed police force is not only justified, but also necessary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In their latest video, “Why Riot?,” the activists of Cairo’s Mosireen film collective argue that violent resistance to an unreformed police force is not only justified, but also necessary. They write, by way of introduction to the film: “Two years after the start of the January 25 revolution we still riot because the ruling elite still exploit us, because the police still torture, maim and kill us and none of them are brought to justice.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egyptian Activists Defend ‘Riots’ Against an Unreformed Police Force', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cairo (Egypt)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-22T00:09:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/22d9de0d-0fd3-55fd-9c71-e1af849e29de', 'word_count': 172, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22d9de0d-0fd3-55fd-9c71-e1af849e29de'}, {'abstract': 'A 30-foot-tall rainbow sculpture in downtown Warsaw has been set on fire four times since June, with opponents outraged at what they say is its pro-gay-rights message.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/22/world/europe/in-warsaw-rainbow-sculpture-draws-attacks.html', 'snippet': 'A 30-foot-tall rainbow sculpture in downtown Warsaw has been set on fire four times since June, with opponents outraged at what they say is its pro-gay-rights message.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WARSAW — The 30-foot-tall rainbow sculpture in downtown Savior Square here is looking somewhat the worse for wear these days, half covered in patches of artificial flowers and half bare from being set on fire. What was intended as a work of public art without an overt political message beyond the need for inclusiveness, according to the artist behind it, has instead become part of a culture war over homosexuality that has been brewing in one of Europe’s most Catholic countries.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/world/0322WARSAWsub/0322WARSAWsub-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 476, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/22/world/0322WARSAWsub/0322WARSAWsub-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 476}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/world/0322WARSAWsub/0322WARSAWsub-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 813, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/world/0322WARSAWsub/0322WARSAWsub-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1626, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/world/0322WARSAWsub/0322WARSAWsub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/22/world/0322WARSAWsub/0322WARSAWsub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/world/0322WARSAWsub/0322WARSAWsub-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rainbow Becomes a Prism to View Gay Rights', 'kicker': 'Warsaw Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rainbow Becomes a Prism to View Gay Rights', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Warsaw (Poland)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vandalism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Poland', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-22T00:16:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hanna Kozlowska', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hanna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozlowska', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/25e65f0a-f639-5376-852a-50a3a3c34375', 'word_count': 1113, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25e65f0a-f639-5376-852a-50a3a3c34375'}, {'abstract': 'Dish, Tex., got its name as part of a deal with the Dish Network satellite TV service. But the town is not exactly TV land, and the arrangement did not turn the place into a household name.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/22/us/texas-town-called-dish-has-an-identity-problem.html', 'snippet': 'Dish, Tex., got its name as part of a deal with the Dish Network satellite TV service. But the town is not exactly TV land, and the arrangement did not turn the place into a household name.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DISH, Tex. — In this rural North Texas town, it is no coincidence that residents of Dish watch Dish.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The Ne