res on April 1. The role was handed to Johan Santana at the start of camp, but Santana has not pitched a single game during spring training because of shoulder fatigue.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Niese Will Pitch the Mets’ Opener', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Niese Gets Opener', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Niese, Jon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santana, Johan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-22T00:34:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Keh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ed1207b-595d-5584-850c-b0d250084e31', 'word_count': 91, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ed1207b-595d-5584-850c-b0d250084e31'}, {'abstract': '“Leonie,” a biopic, stars Emily Mortimer in the story of Isamu Noguchi’s mother.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/22/movies/leonie-the-story-of-isamu-noguchis-mother.html', 'snippet': '“Leonie,” a biopic, stars Emily Mortimer in the story of Isamu Noguchi’s mother.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Who is Leonie Gilmour and why does she rank her own biopic? For the writers of “Leonie,” Hisako Matsui (who also directed) and David Wiener, the short answer is that she’s the mother of the sculptor Isamu Noguchi. And the long answer is this plodding film.Leonie (Emily Mortimer, who against all odds creates a credible character) meets and falls in love with a Japanese poet, Yone Noguchi, who is living in New York. She becomes his editor, lover and the mother of his child. For some reason — motivations in “Leonie” are either murky or too neatly explained — he dumps her when she’s pregnant and moves back to Japan. She joins him there, but their relationship is over, and she strikes out on her own.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/arts/22RDP_LEONIE_SPAN/22RDP_LEONIE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 387, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/22/arts/22RDP_LEONIE_SPAN/22RDP_LEONIE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 387}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/arts/22RDP_LEONIE_SPAN/22RDP_LEONIE_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 661, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/arts/22RDP_LEONIE_SPAN/22RDP_LEONIE_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1321, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/arts/22RDP_LEONIE_SPAN/22RDP_LEONIE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/22/arts/22RDP_LEONIE_SPAN/22RDP_LEONIE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/arts/22RDP_LEONIE_SPAN/22RDP_LEONIE_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Free S