serve’s monetary policies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/22/movies/silver-circle-directed-by-pasha-roberts.html', 'snippet': '“Silver Circle,” directed by Pasha Roberts, is set in a post-apocalyptic world brought on by the Federal Reserve’s monetary policies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The animated “Silver Circle” is set in a dystopian Washington in 2019, when the Federal Reserve Police, in riot gear, are forcibly seizing houses from homeowners when they refuse to sell them to the government. At the same time, inflation runs amok, and working-class people turn to an underground economy, using silver for money. Society’s ills, you see, stem from all that paper money circulating.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/arts/22RDP_SILVER_SPAN/22RDP_SILVER_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 274, 'width': 500, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/arts/22RDP_SILVER_SPAN/22RDP_SILVER_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 274, 'width': 500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/arts/22RDP_SILVER_SPAN/22RDP_SILVER_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/22/arts/22RDP_SILVER_SPAN/22RDP_SILVER_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/arts/22RDP_SILVER_SPAN/22RDP_SILVER_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Apocalypse Fed', 'kicker': 'Movie Review ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Silver Circle', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roberts, Pasha', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-22T01:11:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Webster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Webster', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c3dd0cbd-c746-57b9-bc27-f66586fc2a05', 'word_count': 247, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c3dd0cbd-c746-57b9-bc27-f66586fc2a05'}, {'abstract': 'The Supreme Court correctly slapped down a law that could squeeze far more money from beneficiaries than they actually owe.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/22/opinion/north-carolina-overreaches.html', 'snippet': 'The Supreme Court correctly slapped down a law that could squeeze far more money from beneficiaries than they actually owe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Under the federal Medicaid statute, states must seek reimbursement for medical expenses if the beneficiary also receives money from an insurance company or another third party. This week, the Supreme Court correctly slapped down a North Carolina law that could squeeze far more from beneficiaries than they actually owe. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'North Carolina Overreaches', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'North Carolina Overreaches', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value':