pulation studies responds to two news articles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Church and the Poor', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Church and the Poor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Control and Family Planning', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Francis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philippines', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-22T01:27:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/546fa929-bce2-5709-ba0e-0fb181b8d2fa', 'word_count': 142, 'uri': 'nyt://article/546fa929-bce2-5709-ba0e-0fb181b8d2fa'}, {'abstract': 'A suit says people tied to an anti-aging clinic hurt the sport by supplying drugs. It could also provide a way for Major League Baseball to pursue suspected dopers who haven’t tested positive.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/22/sports/baseball/major-league-baseball-is-said-to-be-suing-people-linked-to-florida-anti-aging-clinic.html', 'snippet': 'A suit says people tied to an anti-aging clinic hurt the sport by supplying drugs. It could also provide a way for Major League Baseball to pursue suspected dopers who haven’t tested positive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Limited by their inability to compel people to cooperate with their investigators, Major League Baseball officials will open a new front in their battle against doping. They plan to file a lawsuit on Friday against a number of people connected to a South Florida anti-aging clinic, alleging that the individuals damaged the sport by providing some of the game’s biggest stars with performance-enhancing drugs, according to two people briefed on the matter.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Baseball Said to Be Suing People Linked to Florida Clinic', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Baseball Is Said to Be Suing People Linked to Florida Clinic', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schmidt, Michael S', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Biogenesis of America LLC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Major League Baseball', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doping (Sports)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bosch, Anthony', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-22T01:27:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael S. Schmidt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Schmidt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/202e32ba-7426-5448-a0b4-fde2b7e67445', 'word_count': 813, 'uri': 'nyt://article/202e32ba-7426-5448-a0b4-fde2b7e67445'}, {'abstract': 'Arrests based on the open display of marijuana are a tumorous outgrowth of the stop-and-frisk practices and are now broadly recognized as scandalous. Yet they remain out of control.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/22/nyregion/out-of-one-gram-of-marijuana-a-manufactured-misdemeanor.html', 'snippet': 'Arrests based on the open display of marijuana are a tumorous outgrowth of the stop-and-frisk practices and are now broadly recognized as scandalous. Yet they remain out of control.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For marijuana smokers in the right neighborhoods, there is no need to go out for supplies. A dealer-businessman will come right to the door, sit at the dining room table and open a box that looks as if it could be used to display herbal tea choices in restaurants. This particular case, however, is used to show varieties of cannabis — weed — and the businessman will annotate the flavor and potency of his offerings. Bought and smoked behind closed doors, the pot in such transactions has almost no risk of attracting attention from law enforcement. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/nyregion/about-1/about-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 798, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/22/nyregion/about-1/about-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 798}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/nyregion/about-1/about-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 770, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/nyregion/about-1/about-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1540, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/nyregion/about-1/about-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/22/nyregion/about-1/about-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'cred