umbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Home-Court Feeling for 2 Kansas Teams', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball (College)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kansas State University', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Kansas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kansas City (Mo)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-22T02:00:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pat Borzi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pat', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borzi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/341b406a-5a73-5028-80ac-8bce50c24239', 'word_count': 382, 'uri': 'nyt://article/341b406a-5a73-5028-80ac-8bce50c24239'}, {'abstract': 'Friday fun with Tim Croce.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/21/not-in-eine-million-jahre/', 'snippet': 'Friday fun with Tim Croce.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRIDAY’S PUZZLE — This is the first time in my own solving history that I can honestly say that I was stumped by the entire top third of a puzzle. It’s O.K.; I eventually finished, but I had to work my way back up, and even then, there were quite a few things I didn’t know (I’m looking at you, OTOMIS) or were fooled by in the cluing. If anyone else had a similar experience, this must be Friday, and this must be a Tim Croce puzzle.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Not in Eine Million Jahre', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-22T02:00:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6278aa3-c373-5318-9644-baae5147f17d', 'word_count': 439, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6278aa3-c373-5318-9644-baae5147f17d'}, {'abstract': '“Hands on a Hardbody,” on Broadway at the Brooks Atkinson Theater, is a musical with a handmade feel and a bluesy-country-rock vibe about Texans vying to win a truck.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/22/theater/reviews/hands-on-a-hardbody-at-the-brooks-atkinson-theater.html', 'snippet': '“Hands on a Hardbody,” on Broadway at the Brooks Atkinson Theater, is a musical with a handmade feel and a bluesy-country-rock vibe about Texans vying to win a truck.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You can hear the sound of America singing in “Hands on a Hardbody,” the daring new musical that opened at the Brooks Atkinson Theater on Thursday night. With a bravado to match the gumption of its characters, a hard-pressed bunch of Texans hoping to beat the odds and win a truck in a grueling contest, this new show drives onto the Broadway lot without the high-gloss blandishments that adorn most big musicals: glittering sets and costumes, high-kicking chorines, megawatt star turns. Instead it concentrates its energies on giving voice to a story of average people fighting to hold onto hope in the face of fierce economic headwinds and bad breaks, not to mention buckling knees. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/arts/22HANDS_SPAN/22HANDS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'c