int_headline': 'Davidson Grants Marquette Last-Second Reprieve', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'NCAA Basketball Championships (Men)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Marquette University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Davidson College', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Butler University', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bucknell University', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Buzz', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball (College)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-22T02:34:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8bec97a6-7417-5a9f-8b88-45c6ea917235', 'word_count': 771, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8bec97a6-7417-5a9f-8b88-45c6ea917235'}, {'abstract': 'Over the last two years, it has appeared only in men, believed to be contracted through anonymous sexual encounters with other men. But health officials fear an outbreak.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/22/nyregion/city-health-officials-warn-some-men-on-lethal-strain-of-meningitis.html', 'snippet': 'Over the last two years, it has appeared only in men, believed to be contracted through anonymous sexual encounters with other men. But health officials fear an outbreak.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is a variant of a disease that can go from a fever and headache to a galloping rash and then to death within hours — so quickly that some victims have been found dead in bed before they could even get to a doctor. Over the last two years, it has appeared only among men, and they often got it, health officials say, through anonymous sexual encounters with other men found through Internet chat rooms or digital apps or at parties, making it all but impossible to trace the path of infection.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'City Health Officials Warn Some Men on Lethal Strain of Meningitis', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'City Health Officials Warn Some Men on Lethal Strain of Meningitis', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Meningitis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-22T02:35:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anemona Hartocollis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anemona', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hartocollis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/292848ce-d437-5d88-9627-bd01b85d1a91', 'word_count': 591, 'uri': 'nyt://article/292848ce-d437-5d88-9627-bd01b85d1a91'}, {'abstract': 'Unlike in previous years, there was no growth in the number of commuting cyclists in the typical riding season in 2012 in New York, but officials highlighted an increase in off-season ridership.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/22/nyregion/commuter-cycling-in-new-york-stays-flat-in-2012.html', 'snippet': 'Unlike in previous years, there was no growth in the number of commuting cyclists in the typical riding season in 2012 in New York, but officials highlighted an increase in off-season ridership.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After years of growth in bike ridership, commuter cycling in New York remained flat in 2012 during the typical riding season, according to counts conducted by the city at six commuter locations last year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Commuter Cycling Stays Flat in ’12', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Commuter Cycling Stays Flat in ’12', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bicycles and Bicycling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Commuting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Transportation Department (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-22T02:35:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Flegenheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flegenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b5d2e13c-b5aa-586a-a467-24f02d6159cb', 'word_count': 420, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5d2e13c-b5aa-586a-a467-24f02d6159cb'}, {'abstract': 'Cuomo administration officials denied that the tax break was written with “The Tonight Show” in mind.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/22/nyregion/cuomo-drafts-a-tax-break-for-talk-shows-that-return-to-new-york.html', 'snippet': 'Cuomo administration officials denied that the tax break was written with “The Tonight Show” in mind.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALBANY — The new state budget has a gift for NBC. A tax credit aimed at variety and talk shows, included in the new budget plan, will be an added incentive for NBC as it plots to relocate “The Tonight Show” to New York City. On Wednesday, The New York Times reported that the network plans to have Jimmy Fallon take over for Jay Leno next year. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'pri