n has gotten plenty of attention ahead of Friday’s game against Wisconsin, but the Badgers have their own charismatic star: Mike Bruesewitz.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KANSAS CITY, Mo. — Even before the Marshall Henderson Traveling Salvation Show rolled into the Sprint Center on Thursday, Henderson, Mississippi’s shooting guard/provocateur, pulled innocent bystanders into his uncomfortable orbit via Twitter. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/sports/kansas/kansas-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/22/sports/kansas/kansas-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 480}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/sports/kansas/kansas-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 820, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/sports/kansas/kansas-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1639, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/sports/kansas/kansas-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/22/sports/kansas/kansas-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/sports/kansas/kansas-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Big Talk and Large Hair for Colorful Opponents Ole Miss and Wisconsin', 'kicker': 'West Region', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Big Talk and Large Hair For Colorful Opponents', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Borzi, Pat', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'NCAA Basketball Championships (Men)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball (College)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Wisconsin-Madison', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Mississippi', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Henderson, Marshall', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bruesewitz, Mike', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-22T03:21:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pat Borzi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pat', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borzi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/29c9664a-411e-55ea-95c8-7ba10aace7b6', 'word_count': 844, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29c9664a-411e-55ea-95c8-7ba10aace7b6'}, {'abstract': 'After weathering large cuts in 2011 and facing new ones, Texas school administrators say they are running out of cost-saving options to maintain services that receive federal money.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/22/education/special-education-programs-brace-for-possible-cuts.html', 'snippet': 'After weathering large cuts in 2011 and facing new ones, Texas school administrators say they are running out of cost-saving options to maintain services that receive federal money.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Aurora Ford, a fifth-grader with Down syndrome, needs regular speech classes and occupational therapy, services that are guaranteed under the Individuals With Disabilities Education Act. But looming federal financing cuts could affect Aurora and her peers, because they might mean bigger classes and fewer teachers next year.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Special-Education Programs Steel Themselves as Cuts Loom', 'kicker': 'The Texas Tribune', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Special-Education Programs Steel Themselves as Cuts Loom', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Special Education', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Aid (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-22T03:22:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elena Schneider', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schneider', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7892eb6f-b76b-5777-8446-81d4591b29e2', 'word_count': 516, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7892eb6f-b76b-5777-8446-81d4591b29e2'}, {'abstract': 'Terrysa Guerra, a Democratic strategist, is viewed by some in the party as a rare weapon for progressives in a conservative stronghold.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/22/us/politics/terrysa-guerra-a-democratic-strategist-in-cowboy-boots.html', 'snippet': 'Terrysa Guerra, a Democratic strategist, is viewed by some in the party as a rare weapon for progressives in a conservative stronghold.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It seemed like a chore at the time to Terrysa Guerra. In 2001, on a fun-filled afternoon on South Padre Island while on a spring break, her grandfather ordered her to drive 20 mile