0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/100cce12-2cbc-566d-a8e9-55d6e68ab2a6'}, {'abstract': 'Israel’s apology for errors in a 2010 raid on a ship bound for Gaza thawed relations with Turkey and gave President Obama a solid achievement as he closed out his Middle East visit.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/23/world/middleeast/president-obama-israel.html', 'snippet': 'Israel’s apology for errors in a 2010 raid on a ship bound for Gaza thawed relations with Turkey and gave President Obama a solid achievement as he closed out his Middle East visit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — Under persistent prodding from President Obama, Israel and Turkey resolved a bitter three-year dispute on Friday with a diplomatic thaw that will help a fragile region confront Syria’s civil war, while handing the president a solid accomplishment as he closed out his visit to the Middle East.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With Obama as Broker, Israelis and Turkey End Dispute', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With Obama as Broker, Israelis and Turkey End Dispute Over Ship Raid', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rudoren, Jodi', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Landler, Mark', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Erdogan, Recep Tayyip', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Netanyahu, Benjamin', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Free Gaza Movement', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-22T09:42:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jodi Rudoren and Mark Landler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jodi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rudoren', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/91c0df18-6cb0-586e-842d-35fc28da8d29', 'word_count': 1360, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91c0df18-6cb0-586e-842d-35fc28da8d29'}, {'abstract': 'The Ford Mark IV that Dan Gurney and A.J. Foyt drove to a historic victory at the 1967 24 Hours of Le Mans will be undergoing “conservation.”', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/22/preserving-a-famous-american-racecar/', 'snippet': 'The Ford Mark IV that Dan Gurney and A.J. Foyt drove to a historic victory at the 1967 24 Hours of Le Mans will be undergoing “conservation.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Ford Mark IV GT40 that Dan Gurney and A.J. Foyt drove to a historic victory at the 1967 24 Hours of Le Mans is going to be making a maintenance pit stop at Mr. Gurney’s All American Racers shop in California. The swoopy red sports car belongs to the Henry Ford Museum in Dearborn, Mich., but made several appearances in Europe last year to commemorate the 45th anniversary of its Le Mans triumph. That tour of the continent proved somewhat taxing, and the car was slightly damaged, so the museum has asked the Gurney shop to perform a conservation — a process that will ensure the car’s condition is the same as it was at the end of the race.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Preserving a Famous American Racecar', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Le Mans Auto Race', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restoration and Renovation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ferrari SpA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ford Motor Co', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ford, Henry, Museum', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-22T10:00:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Stenquist', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stenquist', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/14347e9b-70f9-53b8-8e7c-ade10545571b', 'word_count': 626, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14347e9b-70f9-53b8-8e7c-ade10545571b'}, {'abstract': 'Political news from today’s Times, plus a look at what’s happening in Washington.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/22/the-early-word-nudge-2/', 'snippet': 'Political news from today’s Times, plus a look at what’s happening in Washington.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Today’s Times:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Early Word: Nudge', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-22T10:00:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emmarie Huetteman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emmarie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Huetteman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': No