ead_paragraph': 'O.K., O.K. So you probably didn’t pick Harvard on Thursday night. Or Wichita State. But you had Oregon’s upset, right? And Cal? … Well, fine, but a lot of people disrespect the Pac-12, so your bracket is probably still alive in the office pool and you need to keep up with Friday’s action. Zach Hillesland, Mike Huguenin and Times editors and reporters will supply updates from around the country.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Highlights and Analysis: N.C.A.A. Tournament, Round of 64, Day 2', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'NCAA Basketball Championships (Men)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-22T13:57:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd6ba152-c630-561c-84b5-efa1ea383a9b', 'word_count': 9802, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd6ba152-c630-561c-84b5-efa1ea383a9b'}, {'abstract': 'The new chief executive of the Royal Opera House is Alex Beard, the deputy director of the four Tate museums.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/22/new-chief-of-royal-opera-is-a-manager-not-an-artist/', 'snippet': 'The new chief executive of the Royal Opera House is Alex Beard, the deputy director of the four Tate museums.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON—When it was announced in November that Tony Hall, the chief executive of the Royal Opera House, would leave in April to run the BBC, speculation about who would replace him was immediately rife. Mr. Hall is a hard act to follow. In the 12 years that he has run the opera house, he has transformed it from an institution beset by a succession of artistic directors, funding problems and a reputation for elitest money-wasting, to a model of balanced budgets, expanded access and artistic stability.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/blogs/22rdv-sulcas-art/22rdv-sulcas-art-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 361, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/22/blogs/22rdv-sulcas-art/22rdv-sulcas-art-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 361}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/blogs/22rdv-sulcas-art/22rdv-sulcas-art-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 615, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/blogs/22rdv-sulcas-art/22rdv-sulcas-art-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1231, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/blogs/22rdv-sulcas-art/22rdv-sulcas-art-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/22/blogs/22rdv-sulcas-art/22rdv-sulcas-art-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/blogs/22rdv-sulcas-art/22rdv-sulcas-art-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Chief of Royal Opera Is a Manager, Not an Artist', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beard, Alex', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hall, Tony (1951- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Royal Opera House', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-22T14:00:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roslyn Suclas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roslyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Suclas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e64d95a-ef61-56f3-8ed5-50850b443986', 'word_count': 615, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e64d95a-ef61-56f3-8ed5-50850b443986'}, {'abstract': 'Julius Genachowski’s resignation raises a thorny issue for President Obama: whether it will be possible to keep the Internet free and open to businesses and users.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/23/business/fcc-chairman-announces-resignation.html', 'snippet': 'Julius Genachowski’s resignation raises a thorny issue for President Obama: whether it will be possible to keep the Internet free and open to businesses and users.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The resignation on Friday of Julius Genachowskiafter four years as chairman of the Federal Communications Commission again raises a thorny issue forPresident Obama: whether it will be possible to get the F.C.C. or Congress to help him fulfill a campaign promise to guarantee that the Internet remains free and open to businesses and users.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/23/business/23fcc2/23fcc2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/23/business/23fcc2/23fcc2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/23/business/23fcc2/23fcc2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/23/business/23fcc2/23fcc2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/23/business/23fcc2/23fcc2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/23/business/23fcc2/23fcc2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/23/business/23fcc2/23fcc2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Backer of an Open Internet Steps Down as F.C.C. Chief', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Backer of an Open Internet Steps Down as F.C.C. Chief', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Communications Commission', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wyatt, Edward', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Genachowski, Julius', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Net Neutrality', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-22T14:01:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wyatt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wyatt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d0683a8-fcdd-5034-a66f-4bbd9b41cc26', 'word_count': 1144, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d0683a8-fcdd-5034-a66f-4bbd9b41cc26'}, {'abstract': 'To celebrate the centennial of the famous train station, students from the Ailey School of the Alvin Ailey American Dance Theater will (literally) be horsing around in Nick Cave’s Soundsuits next week.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/22/galloping-through-grand-central/', 'snippet': 'To celebrate the centennial of the famous train station, students from the Ailey School of the Alvin Ailey American Dance Theater will (literally) be horsing around in Nick Cave’s Soundsuits next week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The sight of 30 multicolored horses galloping through Grand Central Terminal would give pause to even the most jaded New Yorker. But don’t worry; you won’t be imagining things. From March 25 to March 31, at 11 a.m. and 2 p.m. each day, a group of students from the Ailey School of the Alvin Ailey American Dance Theater will put on horse costumes — which are actually the artist Nick Cave’s famous mixed-media Soundsuits — and move through the space, either as a herd or in smaller groups. The project, “HEARD NY,” which Cave has done in collaboration with the Chicago choreographer William Gill, is presented by Creative Time and MTA Arts for Transit to celebrate Grand Central’s centennial. Between performances, the Soundsuits will be on display in the terminal’s Vanderbilt Hall for closer inspection. The video above offers a glimpse of the dancers rehearsing on-site, as well as the reactions of passers-by.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Galloping Through Grand Central', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grand Central Terminal (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cave, Nick (1959- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AILEY, ALVIN, AMERICAN DANCE THEATER', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Creative Time', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-22T14:03:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pilar Viladas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pilar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Viladas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c915d6dd-6d37-55b6-aefa-47ba4ca87f5c', 'word_count': 153, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c915d6dd-6d37-55b6-aefa-47ba4ca87f5c'}, {'abstract': 'Misconceptions surround the practice of mindfulness, which is part meditation and part a greater awareness of the things around you.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/23/your-money/mindfulness-requires-practice-and-purpose.html', 'snippet': 'Misconceptions surround the practice of mindfulness, which is part meditation and part a greater awareness of the things around you.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LIKE most people, I have my share of tension and anxiety. And I’m happy to find ways to cope that don’t involve illegal drugs. So when the term mindfulness began cropping up everywhere, I became intrigued.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption'