cials-release-details-of-plan-to-building-near-housing-projects/', 'snippet': 'New York City Housing Authority officials have faced criticism that they had not disclosed enough information about a proposal to lease lands for private development at eight Manhattan projects.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One public housing project, Frederick Douglass Houses on the Upper West Side, could eventually add as many as three apartment buildings — with a total of 794 units — on what are now parking spaces on its grounds. Another project, Alfred E. Smith Houses, could see as many as 1,151 apartments rise on a single parcel of land by the East River.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Officials Release Details of Plan to Build Near Housing Projects', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public and Subsidized Housing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Housing Authority (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-22T16:15:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mireya Navarro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mireya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Navarro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c957cb03-326f-5941-82b0-f313d7613efa', 'word_count': 256, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c957cb03-326f-5941-82b0-f313d7613efa'}, {'abstract': 'With a new duets album out, Emmylou Harris talks about four decades of singing and the reinventions and tradeoffs along the way.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/22/booming/a-full-circle-for-emmylou-harris.html', 'snippet': 'With a new duets album out, Emmylou Harris talks about four decades of singing and the reinventions and tradeoffs along the way.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In her four-decade career, Emmylou Harris has earned a dozen Grammy Awards and a spot in the Country Music Hall of Fame. Her long list of collaborators includes Gram Parsons, Bob Dylan, Roy Orbison, George Jones, Willie Nelson, Neil Young, Dolly Parton, Linda Ronstadt and Rodney Crowell, an old friend and former band mate with whom she has just released a duets album, “Old Yellow Moon.”', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/booming/22midlife-booming-harris3/22midlife-booming-harris3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 446, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/22/booming/22midlife-booming-harris3/22midlife-booming-harris3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 446}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/booming/22midlife-booming-harris3/22midlife-booming-harris3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 761, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/booming/22midlife-booming-harris3/22midlife-booming-harris3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1181, 'width': 1589, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/booming/22midlife-booming-harris3/22midlife-booming-harris3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/22/booming/22midlife-booming-harris3/22midlife-booming-harris3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/booming/22midlife-booming-harris3/22midlife-booming-harris3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Full Circle for Emmylou Harris', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Emmylou Harris: Music, the Road and Her Hair', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Anderman, Joan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baby Boomers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harris, Emmylou', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Country Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Age, Chronological', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Creativity', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-22T16:15:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Booming', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joan Anderman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Anderman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/289fd84f-b0c5-5917-a63d-a712218017ae', 'word_count': 2110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/289fd84f-b0c5-5917-a63d-a712218017ae'}, {'abstract': 'In a new video series, Coach features its spring collection of handbags and accessories in a series of videos that brings together young and old fashion icons to discuss what style means today.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/22/style-coaches/', 'snippet': 'In a new video series, Coach features its spring collection of handbags and accessories in a series of videos that brings together young and old fashion icons to discuss what style means today.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a new digital project called “Generations of Style,” Coach features its spring collection of handbags and accessories in a series of videos that brings together young and old fashion icons to discuss what style means today. Ari Seth Cohen, the 31-year-old behind Advanced Style, orchestrated the one-on-one conversations between fashion bloggers in their 20s and women ranging in age from 65 to 92. “I love these intergenerational projects that bring younger people into the same environment as older people to discuss things that they can both relate to and really show that there is a lot that they can learn from each other,” he says. In one of the flicks, Cohen captures Leandra Medine (“Man Repeller”) playing dress up with the Off Broadway Boutique owner Lynn Dell and saying, “I can’t wait to turn 80!”', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Style Coaches', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stylish Talk', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Handbags and Purses', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Coach Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-22T16:17:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alainna Lexie Beddie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alainna', 'middlename': 'Lexie', 'lastname': 'Beddie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e267cacd-f7b7-59c9-b515-78df106f713c', 'word_count': 183, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e267cacd-f7b7-59c9-b515-78df106f713c'}, {'abstract': 'In Guyana, a place that was once denuded regains some of its former wildness — with the help of some who used to strip it.', 'web_url': 'https://scientistatwork.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/22/in-guyana-wildlife-makes-a-slow-return/', 'snippet': 'In Guyana, a place that was once denuded regains some of its former wildness — with the help of some who used to strip it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dr. Lesley de Souza, a research biologist at John G. Shedd Aquarium, writes from Guyana, where she studies the region’s rich aquatic wildlife, including the arapaima, one of the largest freshwater fishes in the world.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/science/saw-desouza-4-3/saw-desouza-4-3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1000, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/22/science/saw-desouza-4-3/saw-desouza-4-3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1000}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/science/saw-desouza-4-3/saw-desouza-4-3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 615, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/science/saw-desouza-4-3/saw-desouza-4-3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1229, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/science/saw-desouza-4-3/saw-desouza-4-3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/22/science/saw-desouza-4-3/saw-desouza-4-3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/science/saw-desouza-4-3/saw-desouza-4-3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Guyana, Wildlife Makes a Slow Return', 'kicker': 'Scientist at Work', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conservation of Resources', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sustainable Living', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guyana', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-22T16:21:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lesley de Souza', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lesley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'de Souza', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/75be3665-5216-5899-bfa5-ed87c6613eda', 'word_count': 614, 'uri': 'nyt://article/75be3665-5216-5899-bfa5-ed87c6613eda'}, {'abstract': 'A commercial that is to begin running on Friday features several of Major League Baseball’s youngest stars who will help promote the game and Opening Day 2013.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/22/m-l-b-turns-to-young-stars-to-reach-new-fans/', 'snippet': 'A commercial that is to begin running on Friday features several of Major League Baseball’s youngest stars who will help promote the game and Opening Day 2013.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Trout, Harper, Posey, McCutchen and Price. Sounds like an advertising agency, or a law firm. Actually, the names are those of several of the young stars who will be the face of the effort from Major League Baseball to promote Opening Day 2013.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'M.L.B. Turns to Young Stars to Reach New Fans', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'co