hioned capitalism with crowd-funding principles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The other day you may have read about Patrick Robinson, the former Gap creative director, who is producing a new line, Paskho, with money he hopes to raise on Kickstarter. Among crowd-funding sites, Kickstarter is the largest, with more 30,000 projects financed and $300 million in pledges. A virtue of these sites is that for a small sum an investor can feel included in the creative process, whether it’s a film or an amazing sweatshirt. If the project is successful, investors receive a reward or privilege.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Funding Site to Designers: Leave the Business End to Us', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-22T16:33:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b60ad704-6124-5cd8-995c-2a67da09fea0', 'word_count': 668, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b60ad704-6124-5cd8-995c-2a67da09fea0'}, {'abstract': 'The Metropolitan section is introducing a Q. and A. series with New Yorkers whose behind-the-scenes jobs help keep the city humming. First up: Jeffrey Tascarella.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/22/questions-for-the-nomads-general-manager/', 'snippet': 'The Metropolitan section is introducing a Q. and A. series with New Yorkers whose behind-the-scenes jobs help keep the city humming. First up: Jeffrey Tascarella.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Next Sunday, the Metropolitan section will introduce a Q. and A. series with New Yorkers whose behind-the-scenes jobs — from the service industry to city government — help keep the city humming. ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Questions for the NoMad’s General Manager', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': "Questions For the Nomad's Manager", 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'NoMad (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-22T16:35:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Kramer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kramer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c15332c4-8b53-5741-a7ee-27da793020e0', 'word_count': 121, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c15332c4-8b53-5741-a7ee-27da793020e0'}, {'abstract': 'There are no good alternatives, the author contends. But the longer it takes for Cyprus to recognize how bleak its situation is, the greater the damage.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/03/22/why-cyprus-will-pay-dearly/', 'snippet': 'There are no good alternatives, the author contends. But the longer it takes for Cyprus to recognize how bleak its situation is, the greater the damage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cyprus will pay dearly for its sins. The Mediterranean island has committed many follies over the years — and is still making mistakes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Cyprus Will Pay Dearly', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Euro (Currency)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pensions and Retirement Plans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Anastasiades, Nicos', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Merkel, Angela', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cyprus Popular Bank', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Central Bank', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Monetary Union', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cyprus', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-22T16:35:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hugo Dixon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hugo', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dixon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/52a14d81-5e03-5b63-af11-3155296dd52b', 'word_count': 933, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52a14d81-5e03-5b63-af11-3155296dd52b'}, {'abstract': 'The story of Lyman Hapgood, a Boston abolitionist who gave the poet his first job in the capital.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/22/walt-whitmans-boss/', 'snippet': 'The story of Lyman Hapgood, a Boston abolitionist who gave the poet his first job in the capital.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the morning of March 20, 1863, Walt Whitman sat at his desk in a bustling office building in Washington and penned a letter to friends. At one point, he gazed out of his fifth-floor window at the wartime capital. After a long pause he resumed writing and described the vista.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Walt Whitman’s Boss', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Whitman, Walt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-22T16:35:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ronald S. Coddington', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ronald', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Coddington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/97797a8f-50fc-546a-83d4-3e0efaa76a27', 'word_count': 1815, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97797a8f-50fc-546a-83d4-3e0efaa76a27'}, {'abstract': 'Few holidays present more obstacles to vegan diners than Passover, which imposes a daunting set of dietary restrictions.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/22/a-vegan-passover/', 'snippet': 'Few holidays present more obstacles to vegan diners than Passover, which imposes a daunting set of dietary restrictions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Holidays are often a challenge for vegans, who eschew all animal foods. But few holidays present more obstacles to vegan diners than Passover, which imposes a daunting set of dietary restrictions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/23/science/23wellseder/23wellseder-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 365, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/23/science/23wellseder/23wellseder-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 365}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/23/science/23wellseder/23wellseder-jumbo.jpg', '