eywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-22T18:00:37+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Booming', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/040fcdf3-a580-54f3-9a3d-738ec270c59c', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/040fcdf3-a580-54f3-9a3d-738ec270c59c'}, {'abstract': 'In the Colchagua and Millahue Valleys, about two hours from Santiago, wineries are hoping to lure sophisticated visitors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/24/travel/among-chiles-vines-villas-and-views.html', 'snippet': 'In the Colchagua and Millahue Valleys, about two hours from Santiago, wineries are hoping to lure sophisticated visitors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From my horse-top perch, I could view seemingly endless rows of green vines, stretching out across a wide valley floor. To the west, sharp mountains rose behind a glassy emerald lake reflecting slow-moving clouds; a family of herons roosted by the water. Other than the winemaker who rode next to me, a few workers, hundreds of cattle, those herons and millions of precious grapes, I was alone on this 11,000-acre Chilean estate.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/travel/24OVERNIGHTER_SPAN/24OVERNIGHTER_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/24/travel/24OVERNIGHTER_SPAN/24OVERNIGHTER_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/travel/24OVERNIGHTER_SPAN/24OVERNIGHTER_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/travel/24OVERNIGHTER_SPAN/24OVERNIGHTER_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/travel/24OVERNIGHTER_SPAN/24OVERNIGHTER_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/24/travel/24OVERNIGHTER_SPAN/24OVERNIGHTER_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/travel/24OVERNIGHTER_SPAN/24OVERNIGHTER_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Among the Vines in Chile, Villas and Views', 'kicker': 'Overnighter ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Among the Vines, Villas and Views', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cohane, Ondine', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chile', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-22T18:04:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ondine Cohane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ondine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/deefd4a8-2e7c-509c-a85a-f57cdec02f5e', 'word_count': 1330, 'uri': 'nyt://article/deefd4a8-2e7c-509c-a85a-f57cdec02f5e'}, {'abstract': 'Head to the heel of Italy’s boot in the colder months and you’ll find smaller crowds, lower prices and tastier food.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/24/travel/winter-not-summer-is-prime-in-puglia.html', 'snippet': 'Head to the heel of Italy’s boot in the colder months and you’ll find smaller crowds, lower prices and tastier food.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Disappointment swept across the table. Daniela, our waitress, with tight jeans and dyed pink hair, hovered over our table, shaking her head. “I trying to warn you,” she scolded. There were dozens of bowls of antipasto unfinished, many of them untouched. She just shook her head some more. “I leaving and you eating. Now.” With a nod that smacked of finality, she turned and sashayed back to the kitchen.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/travel/24-journeys-farm/24-journeys-farm-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/24/travel/24-journeys-farm/24-journeys-farm-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/travel/24-journeys-farm/24-journeys-farm-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/travel/24-journeys-farm/24-journeys-farm-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/travel/24-journeys-farm/24-journeys-farm-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/24/travel/24-journeys-farm/24-journeys-farm-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/travel/24-journeys-farm/24-journeys-farm-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Winter Is Prime in Puglia', 'kicker': 'Journeys', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Winter, Not Summer, Is Prime in Puglia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pergament, Danielle', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Apulia (Italy)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-22T18:05:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Danielle Pergament', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Danielle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pergament', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d80c5de-f567-5439-b8bd-03119db821c5', 'word_count': 1759, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d80c5de-f567-5439-b8bd-03119db821c5'}, {'abstract': 'Forget Art Basel. My Miami is a place of fruit stands, fritters, airboat rides and a serene hotel on Ocean Drive.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/24/travel/miami-my-way.html', 'snippet': 'Forget Art Basel. My Miami is a place of fruit stands, fritters, airboat rides and a serene hotel on Ocean Drive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We stood on the Everglades boardwalk, an hour south of Miami Beach, squinting in the sun, looking like fools. He was as white as milk and as gangly as Napoleon Dynamite, with a gaudy beach towel we’d bought at a\xa0Woolworth’s tied around his neck. I was dressed head-to-toe in discount specials: a bright orange cover-up and plastic sandals three sizes too big. As we stood in our absurd get-ups, marring the blue-skied Florida backdrop, he told me I looked like a Dreamsicle.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/travel/24SUB2COVER/24SUB2COVER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/24/travel/24SUB2COVER/24SUB2COVER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/travel/24SUB2COVER/24SUB2COVER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/travel/24SUB2COVER/24SUB2COVER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/travel/24SUB2COVER/24SUB2COVER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/24/travel/24SUB2COVER/24SUB2COVER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/travel/24SUB2COVER/24SUB2COVER-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Miami, My Way', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Miami, My Way', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schillinger, Liesl', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Miami Beach (Fla)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wynwood (Miami, Fla)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Everglades (Fla)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Miami (Fla)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-22T18:06:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liesl Schillinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liesl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schillinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7898ac58-e6ed-5414-bb52-25b5ba7ac607', 'word_count': 3138, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7898ac58-e6ed-5414-bb52-25b5ba7ac607'}, {'abstract': 'Brian S. Brown has become the nation’s leading opponent of gay marriage. Now, his views are set for the ultimate American test: a Supreme Court hearing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/23/us/politics/brian-brown-fights-same-sex-marriage-with-zeal-and-strategy.html', 'snippet': 'Brian S. Brown has become the nation’s leading opponent of gay marriage. Now, his views are set for the ultimate American test: a Supreme Court hearing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — As gay couples fight for the right to wed, a little-known but determined force is working to stop them: Brian S. Brown, a 39-year-old father of eight who has raised millions of dollars from religious conservatives — especially his fellow Roman Catholics — to become the nation’s leading opponent of same-sex marriage.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': '