label before he ever played a gig, Mr. Moon was noticed by Jack White, who released his single “Railroad Track” and took him on tour in England last year. His debut album, “Here’s Willy Moon,” 12 propulsive songs that total less than 29 minutes, will be out April 2 on Cherrytree/Island; thanks to its use in an iPod commercial his single “Yeah Yeah,” which borrowed a Wu-Tang Clan sample, has already made the charts.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/arts/24SNAPSHOT_SPAN/24SNAPSHOT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 740, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/24/arts/24SNAPSHOT_SPAN/24SNAPSHOT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 740}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/arts/24SNAPSHOT_SPAN/24SNAPSHOT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 830, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/arts/24SNAPSHOT_SPAN/24SNAPSHOT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1660, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/arts/24SNAPSHOT_SPAN/24SNAPSHOT_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/24/arts/24SNAPSHOT_SPAN/24SNAPSHOT_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/arts/24SNAPSHOT_SPAN/24SNAPSHOT_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thum