ef executive, in the face of calls from some investors that the two jobs be split.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'JPMorgan Board Confirms Dual Role for Dimon', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'JPMorgan Board Confirms Dual Role for Top Executive', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boards of Directors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Compensation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cavanagh, Michael J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dimon, James', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Raymond, Lee R', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN FEDERATION OF STATE, COUNTY AND MUNICIPAL EMPLOYEES', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JPMorgan Chase & Company', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-22T20:44:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jessica Silver-Greenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jessica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver-Greenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e69c86b5-a410-50cf-a77e-ae10bd274e9d', 'word_count': 462, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e69c86b5-a410-50cf-a77e-ae10bd274e9d'}, {'abstract': 'On “Twain” and other albums the singer Rebecca Martin blurs the lines between jazz and other vocal styles.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/24/arts/music/rebecca-martins-voice-leaps-between-genres.html', 'snippet': 'On “Twain” and other albums the singer Rebecca Martin blurs the lines between jazz and other vocal styles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KINGSTON, N.Y. — Rebecca Martin and Larry Grenadier live in a house on a hill in this weathered Hudson Valley city, some 90 miles upriver from Manhattan. At a glance, their sturdy Victorian doesn’t seem like the obvious hub of a small-batch initiative to redraw contemporary jazz singing. During one recent visit, there was snow on the ground and soup on the stove, and their 7-year-old son, Charlie, was home from school.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/arts/24MARTIN1_SPAN/24MARTIN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/24/arts/24MARTIN1_SPAN/24MARTIN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/arts/24MARTIN1_SPAN/24MARTIN1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/arts/24MARTIN1_SPAN/24MARTIN1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/arts/24MARTIN1_SPAN/24MARTIN1_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/24/arts/24MARTIN1_SPAN/24MARTIN1_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/arts/24MARTIN1_SPAN/24M