ame': 'New Cars', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/c2994df9-3e6e-572a-8e6a-5cde601456e7', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/c2994df9-3e6e-572a-8e6a-5cde601456e7'}, {'abstract': 'The caregiving is over, but instead of being relieved, I feel worse.', 'web_url': 'https://newoldage.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/22/suddenly-theyre-all-gone/', 'snippet': 'The caregiving is over, but instead of being relieved, I feel worse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Caring for the old is just like parenting an infant, only on really bad acid. It’s all there: the head-spinning exhaustion, the fractured brain, the demands and smells. Only this time with the knowledge that it won’t get better. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Suddenly, They’re All Gone', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Suddenly, They’re All Gone', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elder Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-22T21:33:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Mithers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mithers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f598feaf-53d2-5744-9692-d7653e980b5a', 'word_count': 1779, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f598feaf-53d2-5744-9692-d7653e980b5a'}, {'abstract': 'Use a colorful combination of currants, golden raisins, dried apricots and dried cranberries to make this year’s holiday Easter bread something special.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/27/dining/dressing-up-bread-for-easter.html', 'snippet': 'Use a colorful combination of currants, golden raisins, dried apricots and dried cranberries to make this year’s holiday Easter bread something special.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THESE DAYS WE ARE constantly surrounded by sweet baked goods, but once upon a time they were really considered quite special. Daily bread was usually brown and meant for sustenance; only for holidays, Easter in particular, was it rich and extravagant, made with fancy white flour, milk, butter and eggs, and studded with candied fruit.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/27/dining/27KITCH1_SPAN/27KITCH1_SPAN-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/27/dining/27KITCH1_SPAN/27KITCH1_SPAN-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/27/dining/27KITCH1_SPAN/27KITCH1_SPAN-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/27/dining/27KITCH1_SPAN/27KITCH1_SPAN-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/27/dining/27KITCH1_SPAN/27KITCH1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/27/dining/27KITCH1_SPAN/27KITCH1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'cr