of last year, tracks the car and monitors the driver.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Far too often, drivers of older vehicles try to add the services available in new Internet-connected cars by balancing smartphones in their laps. But smartphones — aside from the obvious distraction they present — cannot do things like monitor the car’s location when someone else is using it or send a maintenance reminder based on miles traveled.', 'print_section': 'AU', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Plug and Play for Internet Connections', 'kicker': 'Technology', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Plug and Play For Internet Connections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Audiovox Corporation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-22T21:45:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Automobiles', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By John R. Quain', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Quain', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/78657c53-540b-58da-a911-e44798254fc4', 'word_count': 367, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78657c53-540b-58da-a911-e44798254fc4'}, {'abstract': 'The 24-year-old student from Israel’s Arab minority who interrupted President Obama’s speech in Jerusalem on Thursday explained his comments and why he said them in an interview on Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/22/arab-student-explains-why-he-heckled-obama-in-jerusalem/', 'snippet': 'The 24-year-old student from Israel’s Arab minority who interrupted President Obama’s speech in Jerusalem on Thursday explained his comments and why he said them in an interview on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 24-year-old student from Israe