unt': 596, 'uri': 'nyt://article/321bb158-5f55-59d9-b79a-d05c64efa15e'}, {'abstract': 'Blogger and activist Yoani Sánchez regularly condemns the Cuban regime from her home in Havana. On her first trip abroad in nearly a decade, she also called for an end to the American embargo.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/world/americas/100000002133249/cuban-dissident-calls-to-end-embargo.html', 'snippet': 'Blogger and activist Yoani Sánchez regularly condemns the Cuban regime from her home in Havana. On her first trip abroad in nearly a decade, she also called for an end to the American embargo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Blogger and activist Yoani Sánchez regularly condemns the Cuban regime from her home in Havana. On her first trip abroad in nearly a decade, she also called for an end to the American embargo.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/world/video-yoani/video-yoani-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/22/world/video-yoani/video-yoani-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/world/video-yoani/video-yoani-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 507, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/world/video-yoani/video-yoani-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 507, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/world/video-yoani/video-yoani-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/22/world/video-yoani/video-yoani-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/22/world/video-yoani/video-yoani-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cuban Dissident Calls to End Embargo', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cuba', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-22T21:58:52+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'Emily B. Hager and Axel Gerdau', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/bec5c832-06aa-5520-8e34-61cc8916915e', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/bec5c832-06aa-5520-8e34-61cc8916915e'}, {'abstract': 'Travel is about seeing new things, and also familiar things in a new way.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/22/cultural-capital/', 'snippet': 'Travel is about seeing new things, and also familiar things in a new way.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This issue starts off in America, or at least an idea of America. Brooklyn, N.Y., has, as we all know, become a bastion of handcrafted, locally sourced, small-scale-production everything, from bikes to beer. The irony is that this passion for authenticity, diversity and a longing for realness have now turned what was once just a borough into a global brand, one that is vigorously being exported around the world: France, Russia, the United Arab Emirates. The local has gone global, or in other words, anti-homogenization is itself now being homogenized: In Paris you find food trucks, in Gorky Park a snack kiosk called Williamsburg, there is a Brooklyn Diner in Dubai, and even the native beer, Brooklyn Brewery, is planning an outpost in Stockholm — how local is that? When a value system based on unscalability starts to scale, it may be time to turn to other locales for a sense of uniqueness and locally grown culture.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cultural Capital', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-22T22:00:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deborah Needleman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deborah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Needleman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d70f91ab-a93a-5f19-b282-3b15423a5095', 'word_count': 436, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d70f91ab-a93a-5f19-b282-3b15423a5095'}, {'abstract': 'New on DVD: the comedies of Bert Wheeler and Robert Woolsey.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/24/movies/homevideo/new-dvds-wheeler-and-woolseys-rko-comedy-classics.html', 'snippet': 'New on DVD: the comedies of Bert Wheeler and Robert Woolsey.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERT WHEELER and Robert Woolsey made 21 feature films together (and a couple separately) between 1929 and 1937. They were one of the most popular comedy teams of a decade that knew several great ones, and yet today they are almost unknown, except to cinephiles who make a habit of exploring the uncharted overnight territory of the Turner Classic Movies channel.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit