: '“America and Beyond” is the theme of the spring travel issue of T. Start off locally with “Modernism Is the Message,” a look at fashion’s new minimalism, as seen through the eyes of the photographer Mario Sorrenti. Then read Simon Romero’s piece on how São Paulo, Brazil’s largest city, is being redefined. There’s also a report on Seoul, the South Korean capital that is becoming the fashionable intrigue of the Far East, and an essay on the exportation of Brooklyn, which has transformed the borough from landmass into global phenomenon. As you hopscotch around the globe, don’t forget to read Alexandra Marshall’s dispatch on the young chefs revolutionizing Paris, Christian Louboutin’s travel diary of his visit to the Marrakesh film festival or “Matches as Memories,” which rounds up the perfect hotel souvenirs that may also be the most anachronistic: matchbooks.See more from the issue >>', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'T Spring Travel 2013', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-22T23:00:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Editors', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/23b61990-e548-5850-beff-5d41c0bec999', 'word_count': 145, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23b61990-e548-5850-beff-5d41c0bec999'}, {'abstract': 'Neil deGrasse Tyson, the director of the Hayden Planetarium, credits Ann Druyan, widow of Carl Sagan, as the main creative force behind a new version of the show.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/23/opinion/creating-cosmos.html', 'snippet': 'Neil deGrasse Tyson, the director of the Hayden Planetarium, credits Ann Druyan, widow of Carl Sagan, a