aufman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/47c8d8ec-927d-568b-83f1-436f9db2e317', 'word_count': 741, 'uri': 'nyt://article/47c8d8ec-927d-568b-83f1-436f9db2e317'}, {'abstract': 'Michael Krancer, the state environment secretary, will step down next month to return to private law practice, Gov. Tom Corbett said Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/23/us/pennsylvanias-environment-secretary-resigns.html', 'snippet': 'Michael Krancer, the state environment secretary, will step down next month to return to private law practice, Gov. Tom Corbett said Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Michael Krancer, the state environment secretary, will step down next month to return to private law practice, Gov. Tom Corbett said Friday. Since taking office in January 2011, Mr. Krancer, 55, has been accused by environmentalists of lax regulation of Pennsylvania’s booming oil and gas industry, and of reporting incomplete results of water tests from private wells near gas sites. Mr. Corbett, a Republican, praised Mr. Krancer’s efforts to stop gas companies from sending wastewater to treatment plants that were not equipped to process it, as well as his role in keeping open three refineries that were in danger of being closed. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pennsylvania: Environment Secretary Resigns', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Mid-Atlantic', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pennsylvania: Environment Secretary Resigns', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Krancer, Michael', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hurdle, Jon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], '