ernment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sebelius, Kathleen', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kaiser Family Foundation', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-23T00:42:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Pear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pear', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad77ae41-be98-509c-9fd1-33776e56e9f4', 'word_count': 894, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad77ae41-be98-509c-9fd1-33776e56e9f4'}, {'abstract': 'A takeout stand that was transformed into a lively full-scale restaurant is buoyed by its chef, who balances the traditional and the inventive.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/24/nyregion/a-review-of-riviera-maya-mexican-cuisine-in-bogota.html', 'snippet': 'A takeout stand that was transformed into a lively full-scale restaurant is buoyed by its chef, who balances the traditional and the inventive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The last great Mexican meal I ate was in 2004, at La Super-Rica Taqueria in Santa Barbara, Calif., whose most famous patron was Julia Child. The lines were endless. ', 'print_section': 'NJ', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/nyregion/24DINENJ02/24DINENJ02-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/24/nyregion/24DINENJ02/24DINENJ02-a