are in New Haven, has been known for its striking onyx bar and inventive cocktails. Now, with the help of a new chef, it is quietly reinventing itself as a first-class restaurant. John Ginnetti, who owns 116 Crown with his wife, Danielle, said he knew it would be a challenge: “When you walk in, there’s this giant glowing bar. We knew that would work against us as a dinner place.”', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/nyregion/24SUBDINECT02/SUB-24-DINE-CT-02-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/24/nyregion/24SUBDINECT02/SUB-24-DINE-CT-02-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/nyregion/24SUBDINECT02/SUB-24-DINE-CT-02-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/nyregion/24SUBDINECT02/SUB-24-DINE-CT-02-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/nyregion/24SUBDINECT02/SUB-24-DINE-CT-02-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/24/nyregion/24SUBDINECT02/SUB-24-DINE-CT-02-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/nyregion/24SUBDINECT02/SUB-24-DINE-CT-02-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 't