ce as much as its food.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/24/nyregion/a-review-of-mint-premium-foods-in-tarrytown.html', 'snippet': 'The pleasures at Mint, which began life as a gourmet food shop, reside in its ambience as much as its food.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mint Premium Foods began life as a gourmet food shop, and when entering the Tarrytown restaurant one is met by a display case containing huge chunks of delicious cheese, bowls of salty, fragrant olives and shelves of imported sauces, pastas and crackers. If you’re lucky, the elegant proprietor, Hassan Jarane, will offer you a slice of Pickwick Cheddar with caramelized onion, a pesto basil Gouda or a subtle truffle cheese from Tuscany.', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/nyregion/24DINEWE3/24-DINE-WE-03-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/24/nyregion/24DINEWE3/24-DINE-WE-03-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/nyregion/24DINEWE3/24-DINE-WE-03-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/nyregion/24DINEWE3/24-DINE-WE-03-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/nyregion/24DINEWE3/24-DINE-WE-03-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/24/nyregion/24DINEWE3/24-DINE-WE-03-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/nyregion/24DINEWE3/24-DINE-WE-03-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Beyond the Cheese, a Quirky World of Flavors', 'kicker': 'Westchester Dining | Tarrytown', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Beyond the Cheese, a Quirky World of Flavors', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tarrytown (NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mint Premium Foods (Tarrytown, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-23T01:42:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily DeNitto', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'DeNitto', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0ae042e-3d56-5011-aed5-f8ffe1fc40ab', 'word_count': 697, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0ae042e-3d56-5011-aed5-f8ffe1fc40ab'}, {'abstract': 'Testimony in a stop-and-frisk trial has pointed to disturbing conduct by the police command.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/23/opinion/walking-while-black-in-new-york.html', 'snippet': 'Testimony in a stop-and-frisk trial has pointed to disturbing conduct by the police command.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York City Police Department has a long history of violating constitutional rights by stopping, questioning or frisking people on the streets without legal justification. The city has steadfastly denied that the detentions — made under its increasingly unpopular stop-and-frisk program — have been based on race. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Walking While Black in New York', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Walking While Black in New York', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search and Seizure', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fourth Amendment (US Constitution)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Serrano, Pedro', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Polanco, Adhyl', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCormack, Christopher', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-23T01:47:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/2902d5bd-26f6-5044-9392-053499869d39', 'word_count': 377, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2902d5bd-26f6-5044-9392-053499869d39'}, {'abstract': 'Bird life continues at Jamaica Bay Wildlife Refuge after Hurricane Sandy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/23/opinion/watchman-at-the-waters-edge.html', 'snippet': 'Bird life continues at Jamaica Bay Wildlife Refuge after Hurricane Sandy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two bird-watchers moved camera-ready through the Jamaica Bay Wildlife Refuge last week, grateful that the first ospreys had arrived at their familiar nests after flying 2,600 miles from winter roosts in South America. The fish hawks hungrily plied the bay’s resources as jetliners traversed the horizon across the way at Kennedy Airport. But the birders were more intent on investigating worrisome breaches in the refuge’s earthen walls caused by Hurricane Sandy. Would that affect the comings and goings this year of the multitudes of aquatic and meadow birds that favor the 13,000-acre preserve?', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Watchman at the Water’s Edge', 'kicker': 'Editorial | The City Life', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Watchman at the Water’s Edge', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jamaica Bay Wildlife Refuge (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-23T01:47:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Francis X. Clines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Francis', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Clines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ec111a3-1cca-534a-ba0f-2cee2f2553d3', 'word_count': 343, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ec111a3-1cca-534a-ba0f-2cee2f2553d3'}, {'abstract': 'A vote is scheduled for one of the most important measures to reduce gun violence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/23/opinion/keep-guns-out-of-criminal-hands.html', 'snippet': 'A vote is scheduled for one of the most important measures to reduce gun violence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Senate, at long last, will take up a package of gun-control measures when it returns from recess next month. On Thursday, the majority leader, Harry Reid, announced that one of those measures will require almost all gun buyers to undergo a background check. This is a vital step that would help keep guns out of the wrong hands, and it deserves far more bipartisan support than it has received.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Keep Guns Out of Criminal Hands', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Keep Guns Out of Criminal Hands', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Rifle Assn', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-23T01:47:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/e27b7fc4-4db8-5935-9384-e130ea5a4d53', 'word_count': 517, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e27b7fc4-4db8-5935-9384-e130ea5a4d53'}, {'abstract': 'At President Obama’s urging, Israel and Turkey have chosen a wiser course and restored diplomatic relations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/23/opinion/overdue-reconciliation.html', 'snippet': 'At President Obama’s urging, Israel and Turkey have chosen a wiser course and restored diplomatic relations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama concluded a successful visit to Israel on Friday by helping broker an end to the self-defeating standoff between two American allies, Israel and Turkey. The breakthrough is a credit to both prime ministers, Benjamin Netanyahu of Israel and Recep Tayyip Erdogan of Turkey, but it is also a sign that Mr. Obama, criticized as “leading from behind” on foreign policy, is prepared to engage more directly in international affairs.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Overdue Reconciliation', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Overdue Reconciliation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Free Gaza Movement', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-23T01:47:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/cecffdc6-7898-5a12-b84d-75bc186cb00d', 'word_count': 311, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cecffdc6-7898-5a12-b84d-75bc186cb00d'}, {'abstract': 'In its first trip to the N.C.A.A. tournament, 15th-seeded Florida Gulf Coast defeated Georgetown, a perennial power and No. 2 seed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/23/sports/ncaabasketball/florida-gulf-coast-stuns-second-seeded-georgetown-in-ncaa-opener.html', 'snippet': 'In its first trip to the N.C.A.A. tournament, 15th-seeded Florida Gulf Coast defeated Georgetown, a perennial power and No. 2 seed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PHILADELPHIA — The final two and a half minutes were, in Andy Enfield’s estimation, the longest two and a half minutes of his life. The game could not end soon enough, not with the way Georgetown was making 3-pointers and