 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-23T02:00:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a41a08a-3001-587e-8b55-fdb5b0c9ba81', 'word_count': 215, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a41a08a-3001-587e-8b55-fdb5b0c9ba81'}, {'abstract': 'The author responds to readers’ theories on whether consciousness can be explained by science.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/22/mary-and-the-zombies-consciousness-revisited/', 'snippet': 'The author responds to readers’ theories on whether consciousness can be explained by science.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thanks to the nearly 800 readers who submitted comments on last week’s column, “Mary and the Zombies: Can Science Explain Consciousness?”\xa0 Together they produced over 100,000 words (a good sized book).\xa0 The column summarized two widely discussed arguments against understanding consciousness as entirely physical: the Mary Argument and the Zombie Argument.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mary and the Zombies: Consciousness Revisited', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-23T02:00:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gary Gutting', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gutting', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7744ed3e-9640-5a56-aece-be0d6c531d3a', 'word_count': 1882, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7744ed3e-9640-5a56-aece-be0d6c531d3a'}, {'abstract': 'A measure allowing the public to decide whether the State Constitution should assert that life begins at conception will appear on next year’s ballot.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/23/us/north-dakota-allows-vote-on-strict-abortion-limit.html', 'snippet': 'A measure allowing the public to decide whether the State Constitution should assert that life begins at conception will appear on next year’s ballot.', 'lead_paragraph': 'North Dakota lawmakers passed a resolution on Friday to allow the public to decide whether the State Constitution should assert that life begins at conception, a move that would essentially ban all abortions in the state.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'North Dakota to Put End to Abortions on the Ballot', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'North Dakota To Put End To Abortions On the Ballot', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Dakota', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Roe v Wade (Supreme Court Decision)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitutional Amendments', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-23T02:01:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Eligon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eligon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/445a8654-66ab-51b3-95b2-4f8f51c83553', 'word_count': 388, 'uri': 'nyt://article/445a8654-66ab-51b3-95b2-4f8f51c83553'}, {'abstract': 'A special prosecutor in Iceland issued indictments this week against the chief executives and 14 other employees of two banks whose spectacular collapse in 2008 sent the Icelandic economy into a tailspin.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/23/world/europe/iceland-prosecutor-issues-charges-over-collapse-of-2-banks-in-2008.html', 'snippet': 'A special prosecutor in Iceland issued indictments this week against the chief executives and 14 other employees of two banks whose spectacular collapse in 2008 sent the Icelandic economy into a tailspin.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A special prosecutor in Iceland issued indictments this week against the chief executives and 14 other employees of two banks whose spectacular collapse during the financial crisis of 2008 sent the Icelandic economy into a tailspin. In one of the world’s most ambitious prosecutions stemming from the crisis, the 16 people are being charged with manipulating the financial markets and with putting their institutions in jeopardy by flouting internal rules. Among other things, the indictment says they issued loans to friendly companies that in turn used the loans to buy shares in the banks, elevating their stock prices. The people charged could face up to six years in prison if convicted. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iceland: Prosecutor Issues Charges Over Collapse of 2 Banks in 2008', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iceland: Prosecutor Issues Charges Over Collapse of 2 Banks in 2008', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iceland', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lyall, Sarah', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Special Prosecutors (Ind