 armed America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Today, Joe is devoting his column to smart gun technology, which includes biometric gun locks that ensure only a gun’s owner can fire it. States including New Jersey and California would like to make “gun personalization” technology, as it is called, required for all legally owned firearms. Many Second Amendment absolutists believe that any refinement to current gun laws is an infringement on their rights. “Why should legal gun owners suffer background checks when such a small percentage of people use guns to kill?” they ask.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Gun Report: March 23, 2013', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kansas City (Mo)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Las Vegas (Nev)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Montgomery (Ala)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Carolina', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philadelphia (Pa)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Seattle (Wash)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-23T14:30:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Mascia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mascia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ecabade3-57bd-54d6-b29e-e2bd5003e4a1', 'word_count': 1061, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ecabade3-57bd-54d6-b29