apologize for supporting a war that’s responsible for liberalism’s current political and cultural ascendance.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/ross-douthat/ross-douthat-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/ross-douthat/ross-douthat-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/ross-douthat/ross-douthat-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/ross-douthat/ross-douthat-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/ross-douthat/ross-douthat-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/ross-douthat/ross-douthat-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/ross-douthat/ross-douthat-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Obama Era, Brought to You by the Iraq War', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Obama Era, Brought to You by the Iraq War', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, George W', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Douthat, Ross G', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003-11)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Liberalism (US Politics)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-23T17:26:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3ff10d9-af7e-5ba9-b4ea-5e03e03ed102', 'word_count': 782, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3ff10d9-af7e-5ba9-b4ea-5e03e03ed102'}, {'abstract': 'Shane Battier, one of the Miami Heat’s stalwarts during their current 25-game win streak, also contributed significantly to lengthy victory stretches with the Duke Blue Devils and the Houston Rockets.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/23/where-battier-goes-winning-streaks-follow/', 'snippet': 'Shane Battier, one of the Miami Heat’s stalwarts during their current 25-game win streak, also contributed significantly to lengthy victory stretches with the Duke Blue Devils and the Houston Rockets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The question of whether it is better to be loved or hated may never be answered satisfactorily, but when it comes to Shane Battier, there is no need to choose. He is loved and hated with equal passion, based almost entirely on how one feels about Duke basketball.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Where Battier Goes, Winning Streaks Follow', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Where Battier Goes, Winning Streaks Follow ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Battier, Shane', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Duke University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Houston Rockets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-23T17:26:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Hoffman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoffman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3351482-baf8-5019-a50f-38c032e3db06', 'word_count': 883, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3351482-baf8-5019-a50f-38c032e3db06'}, {'abstract': 'The rape and murder of a young woman in New Delhi last year may have been a tipping point in a long struggle.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/24/opinion/sunday/in-india-womens-issues-are-finally-out-front.html', 'snippet': 'The rape and murder of a young woman in New Delhi last year may have been a tipping point in a long struggle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Having recently returned to the United States from a four-year assignment in India, I’m often asked about events in that country. And so it was with the brutal rape and murder of a 23-year-old student in New Delhi in December that set off big protests across India and was covered widely around the world. Why has this particular rape inspired so much outrage, people ask, when sexual violence is, sadly, so pervasive and commonplace there?', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/sunday-review/24editorial/24editorial-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/24/sunday-review/24editorial/24editorial-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/sunday-review/24editorial/24editorial-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/sunday-review/24editorial/24editorial-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/sunday-review/24editorial/24editorial-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/24/sunday-review/24editorial/24editorial-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/sunday-review/24editorial/24editorial-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In India, Women’s Issues Are Finally Out Front', 'kicker': 'Editorial | Sunday Observer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In India, Women’s Issues Are Finally Out Front', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bajaj, Vikas', 'rank': 1, '