2012)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public Editor (Times Column)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-23T17:35:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaret Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/2535feeb-36b3-53b0-b370-223b7c08b2f5', 'word_count': 1062, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2535feeb-36b3-53b0-b370-223b7c08b2f5'}, {'abstract': 'Political attacks ignore the considerable benefits delivered to millions of people since the law’s enactment three years ago.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/24/opinion/sunday/report-card-on-health-care-reform.html', 'snippet': 'Political attacks ignore the considerable benefits delivered to millions of people since the law’s enactment three years ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Republican leaders in Congress regularly denounce the 2010 Affordable Care Act and vow to block money to carry it out or even to repeal it. Those political attacks ignore the considerable benefits delivered to millions of people since the law’s enactment three years ago Saturday. The main elements of the law do not kick in until Jan. 1, 2014, when many millions of uninsured people will gain coverage. Yet it has already thrown a lifeline to people at high risk of losing insurance or being uninsured, including young adults and people with chronic health problems, and it has made a start toward reforming the costly, dysfunctional American health care system. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Report Card on Health Care Reform', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Report Card on Health Care Reform', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reform and Reorganization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Preventive Medicine', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-23T17:36:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1118198-d0ad-528f-95d1-5412794b2943', 'word_count': 837, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1118198-d0ad-528f-95d1-5412794b2943'}, {'abstract': 'Imprisonment rates continue to decrease, but more states need reforms to keep the population and cost down.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/24/opinion/sunday/shrinking-prisons-saving-billions.html', 'snippet': 'Imprisonment rates continue to decrease, but more states need reforms to keep the population and cost down.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The mandatory sentencing craze that gripped the country four decades ago drove up the state prison population sevenfold — from under 200,000 in the early 1970s to about 1.4 million today — and pushed costs beyond $50 billion a year. Until recently, it seemed that the numbers would keep growing. But thanks to reforms in more than half the states, the prison census has edged down slightly — by just under 2 percent — since 2009. A new analysis by the Pew Charitable Trusts shows that the decline would have been considerably larger had the other states not been pulling in the opposite direction.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shrinking Prisons, Saving Billions', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Shrinking Prisons, Saving Billions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mandatory Sentencing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-23T17:36:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/d59245c8-7f46-5edc-827c-d8bea64de64e', 'word_count': 375, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d59245c8-7f46-5edc-827c-d8bea64de64e'}, {'abstract': 'The justices should be as dubious about distinctions based on sexual orientation as on gender.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/24/opinion/sunday/heightened-scrutiny-of-proposition-8-and-doma.html', 'snippet': 'The justices should be as dubious about distinctions based on sexual orientation as on gender.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the central questions in the two gay marriage cases to be argued before the Supreme Court this week is whether gays and lesbians are a protected class under the Constitution. Under longstanding principles, government actions that fall heavily on “discrete and insular minorities” historically subject to prejudice and stigma are to be given particular scrutiny. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Heightened Scrutiny', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Heightened Scrutiny', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense of Marriage Act (1996)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-23T17:36:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/5cfcb4d1-dc03-5281-b006-7a31e8f14060', 'word_count': 497, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5cfcb4d1-dc03-5281-b006-7a31e8f14060'}, {'abstract': 'Marketers want us to believe that we can perfect our lives by perfecting our homes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/24/opinion/sunday/unhappy-clean-house.html', 'snippet': 'Marketers want us to believe that we can perfect our lives by perfecting our homes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'London', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/sunday-review/24SPRING/24SPRING-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 391, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/24/sunday-review/24SPRING/24SPRING-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 391}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/24/sunday-review/24SPRING/24SPRING-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 667, 'width': 1024, 's