the choreographer’s career, concluded Sunday at the David H. Koch Theater.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/25/arts/dance/paul-taylor-dance-company-at-david-h-koch-theater.html', 'snippet': 'A three-week visit by the Paul Taylor Dance Company, encompassing works spanning the choreographer’s career, concluded Sunday at the David H. Koch Theater.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Who in the world is Paul Taylor? Every year this impossible question comes around with the New York season of his dance company; this year’s, a three-week affair at the David H. Koch Theater, ended on Sunday.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/25/arts/PAULTAYLOR/PAULTAYLOR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 342, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/25/arts/PAULTAYLOR/PAULTAYLOR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 342}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/25/arts/PAULTAYLOR/PAULTAYLOR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 584, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/25/arts/PAULTAYLOR/PAULTAYLOR-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1169, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/25/arts/PAULTAYLOR/PAULTAYLOR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/25/arts/PAULTAYLOR/PAULTAYLOR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/25/arts/PAULTAYLOR/PAULTAYLOR-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pushing and Pulling Between Opposites to Zones in Between', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pushing and Pulling Between Opposites to Zones in Between', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taylor, Paul, Dance Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-24T21:41:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/53004804-3a58-5ba1-aa79-9c5468dfb0be', 'word_count': 1094, 'uri': 'nyt://article/53004804-3a58-5ba1-aa79-9c5468dfb0be'}, {'abstract': '“Planetarium” combined a string quartet and a chaotic, multimedia spectacle at the Brooklyn Academy of Music.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/25/arts/music/planetarium-at-brooklyn-academy-of-music.html', 'snippet': '“Planetarium” combined a string quartet and a chaotic, multimedia spectacle at the Brooklyn Academy of Music.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Toward the end of the first half of Friday evening’s performance of “Planetarium” at the Brooklyn Academy of Music, during a string quartet arrangement of a song called “Year of the Boar” by the singer-songwriter Sufjan Stevens, the violinist Ben Russell let loose with a wild riff. His finger slithered up and down the fingerboard producing electric guitarlike squeals while the other members of the quartet — Nadia Sirota (viola), Clarice Jensen (cello) and Rob Moose (violin) — provided an accompaniment of crunchy rhythmic chords that were subtly amplified and altered through giant speakers on each side of the stage.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/25/arts/PLANET/PLANET-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/25/arts/PLANET/PLANET-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/25/arts/PLANET/PLANET-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/25/arts/PLANET/PLANET-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/25/arts/PLANET/PLANET-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/25/arts/PLANET/PLANET-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/25/arts/PLANET/PLANET-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Spectacle With Something for Everyone, Even Poor Neglected Pluto', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Spectacle With Something for Everyone, Even Poor Neglected Pluto', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'da Fonseca-Wollheim, Corinna', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Muhly, Nico', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stevens, Sufjan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dessner, Bryce', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sirota, Nadia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jensen, Clarice', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Academy of Music', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-24T21:49:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Corinna da Fonseca-Wollheim', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/a07d5884-3616-55f9-b26d-4ac7097604b2', 'word_count': 522, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a07d5884-3616-55f9-b26d-4ac7097604b2'}, {'abstract': '“Seven Words” mingles art by Ofri Cnaani, music by the Salzburg Chamber Soloists, and the collection of the Metropolitan Museum of Art.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/25/arts/music/seven-words-with-ofri-cnaani-at-the-met-museum.html', 'snippet': '“Seven Words” mingles art by Ofri Cnaani, music by the Salzburg Chamber Soloists, and the collection of the Metropolitan Museum of Art.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the first full season she has planned as the general manager of concerts and lectures at the Metropolitan Museum of Art, Limor Tomer has tried to link music programs to the museum’s exhibitions and collections. A concert on Friday night put that goal into practice. The Salzburg Chamber Soloists performed Haydn’s ruminative masterpiece “The Seven Last Words of Christ on the Cross,” an hourlong work in nine movements, including seven slow movements called sonatas that reflect the final phrases Jesus spoke during the Crucifixion.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/25/arts/words/words-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 391, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/25/arts/words/words-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 391}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/25/arts/words/words-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 667, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/25/arts/words/words-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1333, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/25/arts/words/words-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/25/arts/words/words-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/25/arts/words/words-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Art Adds a Dimension to Biblically Inspired Melody', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Art Adds a Dimension to Biblically Inspired Melody', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tommasini, Anthony', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'r