l', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Barry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ddf1ae5f-a1c4-5895-84e9-bc1db33848d6', 'word_count': 1304, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ddf1ae5f-a1c4-5895-84e9-bc1db33848d6'}, {'abstract': 'The American Dance Festival has announced the 80th edition of its summer season, from June 13 to July 27 in Durham, N.C., and New York City.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/25/arts/dance/american-dance-festival-unveils-summer-season.html', 'snippet': 'The American Dance Festival has announced the 80th edition of its summer season, from June 13 to July 27 in Durham, N.C., and New York City.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The American Dance Festival has announced the 80th edition of its summer season, from June 13 to July 27 in Durham, N.C., and New York City. The festival is to feature nine world premieres, including two by the dance troupe Pilobolus. The first is a collaboration with the choreographer Trish Sie set to original music by the Nortec Collective Presents Bostich + Fussible, a Latin fusion group. The second will highlight the illusionists Penn and Teller. Another world premiere is to be Twyla Tharp’s 130th work, which she has created for American Dance Festival students and set to a score by the music producer David Kahne. The festival is to include 47 performances by 25 companies, including Shen Wei Dance Arts, Paul Taylor Dance Company, Trisha Brown Dance Company, the Brenda Angiel Aerial Dance Company from Argentina, Mark Haim, Kyle Abraham/Abraham.In.Motion and Faye Driscoll. Among those presenting for the first time at the festival are Camille A. Brown & Dancers, the 605 Collective from Canada and Ponydance from Ireland. The festival plans to start a social-media campaign in honor of its anniversary, called “80 Years — 80 Stories,” in early May.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'American Dance Festival Unveils Summer Season', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'American Dance Festival Unveils Summer Season', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AMERICAN DANCE FESTIVAL', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-24T22:25:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Nicole Higgins DeSmet', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicole', 'middlename': 'Higgins', 'lastname': 'DeSmet', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/0dee0e69-8083-59df-91d7-c2041f2fff50', 'word_count': 191, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0dee0e69-8083-59df-91d7-c2041f2fff50'}, {'abstract': 'A victory would be Tiger Woods’s record-tying eighth at the Arnold Palmer Invitational, but weather problems have forced him to wait.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/25/sports/golf/with-tiger-woods-leading-weather-delays-arnold-palmer-final-round.html', 'snippet': 'A victory would be Tiger Woods’s record-tying eighth at the Arnold Palmer Invitational, but weather problems have forced him to wait.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ORLANDO, Fla. — After Tiger Woods birdied the second hole to increase his lead at the Arnold Palmer Invitational to three strokes, it seemed that only an act of nature could prevent him from winning his 77th PGA Tour title, and his record-tying eighth in a single tournament. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/