, 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Bonds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Credits, Deductions and Exemptions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-24T22:58:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/3590d242-4bba-5f50-8fbf-8aa1da910461', 'word_count': 344, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3590d242-4bba-5f50-8fbf-8aa1da910461'}, {'abstract': 'Zainab al-Khawaja, a human rights activist in Bahrain, writes a letter from prison about why she is on a hunger strike and how Martin Luther King Jr. guides her acts of civil disobedience.', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/24/a-letter-from-a-political-prisoner-on-hunger-strike-in-bahrain/', 'snippet': 'Zainab al-Khawaja, a human rights activist in Bahrain, writes a letter from prison about why she is on a hunger strike and how Martin Luther King Jr. guides her acts of civil disobedience.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This is a letter that Zainab al-Khawaja, a human rights activist and political prisoner in Bahrain, wrote from jail. I wrote about her in a column examining the regime’s repression of protesters. The United States is a leading backer of the Bahrain government and sells it weapons. Zainab went on a hunger strike recently, after being denied family visits in jail. – Nicholas D. Kristof ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why I am on Hunger Strike in Bahrain', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-24T23:16:32+0000', 'document_type': 'art