best known for its traffic, warehouses and airport access.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/25/us/miami-herald-prepares-to-leave-bastion-on-the-bay.html', 'snippet': 'In June, The Herald will leave its longtime home on Biscayne Bay for Doral, a small city best known for its traffic, warehouses and airport access.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MIAMI — One Herald Plaza rises like a boxy behemoth on Biscayne Bay, an industrial-looking rectangle that is not so easy to like but hard to ignore. A fitting trait, it turns out, for a daily newspaper.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/25/us/HERALD-1/HERALD-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 282, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/25/us/HERALD-1/HERALD-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 282}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/25/us/HERALD-1/HERALD-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 482, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/25/us/HERALD-1/HERALD-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 963, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/25/us/HERALD-1/HERALD-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/25/us/HERALD-1/HERALD-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/25/us/HERALD-1/HERALD-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'No Longer Will News Lap at Miami Herald’s Door', 'kicker': 'Reporter’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Longer Will News Lap At Miami Herald’s Door', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Alvarez, Lizette', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Herald', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Relocation of Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Doral (Fla)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Miami (Fla)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'McClatchy Company', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Genting Group', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-25T00:52:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lizette Alvarez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lizette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alvarez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0bf51c1b-4dad-53eb-b039-13030d999288', 'word_count': 952, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0bf51c1b-4dad-53eb-b039-13030d999288'}, {'abstract': 'Secretary of State John Kerry urged the government to make public the results of an investigation of what happened to Sombath Somphone, an American-educated agricultural specialist.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/25/world/asia/kerry-appeals-to-laos-in-case-of-a-missing-man.html', 'snippet': 'Secretary of State John Kerry urged the government to make public the results of an investigation of what happened to Sombath Somphone, an American-educated agricultural specialist.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VIENTIANE, Laos — On the 100th day since the disappearance of a prominent American-educated Laotian agriculture specialist, Secretary of State John Kerry on Monday urged the government here to make public the results of an investigation into what had happened to him, and to return him to his family.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kerry Appeals to Laos in Case of a Missing Man', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Kerry Appeals to Laos Officials to Share Information About Man Missing Since December', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perlez, Jane', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Laos', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sombath Somphone', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Missing Persons', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kerry, John', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-25T00:55:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane Perlez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Perlez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3de616c3-9065-568c-b684-2729f83882b6', 'word_count': 847, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3de616c3-9065-568c-b684-2729f83882b6'}, {'abstract': 'Philadelphia Magazine’s article “Being White in Philly” provoked a rebuke from the mayor, angry comments and the threat of a boycott, as well as a sales bump.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/24/being-white-in-philly-article-brings-an-outcry/', 'snippet': 'Philadelphia Magazine’s article “Being White in Philly” provoked a rebuke from the mayor, angry comments and the threat of a boycott, as well as a sales bump.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Few subjects appear to provoke from readers as much debate, and anger, as race does. Since Philadelphia Magazine published its article “Being White in Philly: Whites, race, class, and the things that never get said” in late February, it has drawn a public rebuke by the city’s mayor, the threat of a boycott by the local African-American Chamber of Commerce and at least two forums where the magazine’s editor and the article’s writer answered angry questions.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Magazine Article on Race Sets Off an Outcry', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Magazine Article on Race Sets Off an Outcry', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Magazines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Philadelphia (Magazine)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philadelphia (Pa)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-25T00:58:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Haughney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haughney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5cf0cb8-e370-5a5b-aafc-38b6d8ccfcd3', 'word_count': 458, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5cf0cb8-e370-5a5b-aafc-38b6d8ccfcd3'}, {'abstract': 'Cuts to the Census Bureau’s budget will create a big information gap.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/25/opinion/census-budget-cuts-show-willful-ignorance.html', 'snippet': 'Cuts to the Census Bureau’s budget will create a big information gap.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Automatic spending cuts are a mindless way to budget, and they will leave the nation in the dark. Here’s how: Under the cuts, the Census Bureau budget will be $845 million, well below the Obama administration’s $970 million request. That will force the bureau to delay completion of the Economic Census, an immense survey done every five years that provides the benchmark measurements for economic growth and other vital indicators, including inflation and productivity. Without such data, policy makers, business leaders, investors, economists and social researchers will be at a disadvantage. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Willful Ignorance', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Willful Ignorance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Census', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Census Bureau', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-25T01:00:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/2bba048e-6cf1-5296-b3f7-c5c5f798fb74', 'word_count': 300, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2bba048e-6cf1-5296-b3f7-c5c5f798fb74'}, {'abstract': 'People whose credit history was damaged in the recession should not be shut out of the job market.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/25/opinion/the-credit-history-pariah-class.html', 'snippet': 'People whose credit history was damaged in the recession should not be shut out of the job market.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Research has shown that someone with a poor credit history is not automatically a poor job prospect. Nevertheless, millions of Americans who have emerged from the recession with medical debts or a record of late payments are at risk of being denied jobs by companies that use credit histories to screen applicants. Several states have placed limits on this practice. But until the federal government engages the issue more aggressively, employers will consign otherwise qualified applicants to a kind of pariah class that gets shut out of the job market. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Credit-History Pariah Class', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Credit-History Pariah Class', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Scores', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-25T01:02:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e61d0c0-7593-51e0-8ca4-2861eecc6203', 'word_count': 410, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e61d0c0-7593-51e0-8ca4-2861eecc6203'}, {'abstract': 'As inequality has risen in the developed world, many governments have been dismantling — not increasing — estate taxes. In the United States, it took national wartime mobilization to create the political conditions that made progressive estate taxation possible.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/24/is-the-estate-tax-doomed/', 'snippet': 'As inequality has risen in the developed world, many governments have been dismantling — not increasing — estate taxes. In the United States, it took national wartime mobilization to create the political conditions that made progressive estate tax...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Under the deal struck by President Obama and Congress to avert the “fiscal cliff,” the estate tax — long targeted for elimination by Republicans — survived, but in a substantially diminished form.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Is the Estate Tax Doomed?', 'kicker': 'The Great Divide', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inheritance and Estate Taxes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wills and Estates', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-25T01:03:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kenneth F. Scheve Jr. and David Stasavage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kenneth', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Scheve', 'qualifier': 'Jr.', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stasavage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1eb63d1-e87e-54a5-bb6e-f5157e143c1a', 'word_count': 1728, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1eb63d1-e87e-54a5-bb6e-f5157e143c1a'}, {'abstract': 'It is still unclear how Boris A. Berezovsky died, but what is certain is that a humiliating court ruling last August helped to drive the exiled oligarch into despair.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/25/world/europe/for-homesick-russian-tycoon-instant-of-ruin-came-in-court.html', 'snippet': 'It is still unclear how Boris A. Berezovsky died, but what is certain is that a humiliating court ruling last August helped to drive the exiled oligarch into despair.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The moment of ruin for Boris A. Berezovsky, the exiled Russian oligarch who was found dead on Saturday outside London, came not when he fell out with the Kremlin, or when his latest long-term relationship broke up, or even when Russia sentenced him to prison in absentia.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/25/world/JP-BEREZOVSKY/JP-BEREZOVSKY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 361, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/25/world/JP-BEREZOVSKY/JP-BEREZOVSKY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 361}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/25/world/JP-BEREZOVSKY/JP-BEREZOVSKY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 616, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/25/world/JP-BEREZOVSKY/JP-BEREZOVSKY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1231, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/25/world/JP-BEREZOVSKY/JP-BEREZOVSKY-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/25/world/JP-BEREZOVSKY/JP-BEREZOVSKY-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/