media. Enjoy!', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/25/10-ways-to-teach-the-joys-of-spring/', 'snippet': 'Ideas for teaching 10 seasonal subjects, from poetry and baseball to Earth Day and April Fool’s, all via Times articles, essays, and multimedia. Enjoy!', 'lead_paragraph': 'Visit the City Room blog’s 2012 Spring Time series, which tracked the season in a patch of Staten Island forest. Above, photographs show the changes from Week 1 to Week 14. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/20/dining/20HAM_SPAN-LN/20HAM-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/20/dining/20HAM_SPAN-LN/20HAM-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/20/dining/20HAM_SPAN-LN/20HAM-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/20/dining/20HAM_SPAN-LN/20HAM-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/20/dining/20HAM_SPAN-LN/20HAM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/20/dining/20HAM_SPAN-LN/20HAM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/20/dining/20HAM_SPAN-LN/20HAM-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '10 Ways to Teach the Joys of Spring', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Spring (Season)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-25T12:43:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5855d064-6e1b-559c-bb12-aff6119a8386', 'word_count': 1020, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5855d064-6e1b-559c-bb12-aff6119a8386'}, {'abstract': 'Rupert Murdoch will have to wrangle with regulators once again if he tries to buy The Los Angeles Times, Steve Harvey has become a daytime TV standout and NBC is risking one of its rare high points in the ratings by replacing Jay Leno on “Tonight” with Jimmy Fallon.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/25/the-breakfast-meeting-murdoch-weighs-a-newspaper-deal-and-steve-harvey-surprises-daytime-tv/', 'snippet': 'Rupert Murdoch will have to wrangle with regulators once again if he tries to buy The Los Angeles Times, Steve Harvey has become a daytime TV standout and NBC is risking one of its rare high points in the ratings by replacing Jay Leno on “Tonight”...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rupert Murdoch finds himself in a familiar predicament as he considers a bid for The Los Angeles Times: awaiting rule changes from the government, Amy Chozick reports. Mr. Murdoch has increased his lobbying efforts to revise a media ownership rule that prevents companies from owning both television stations and newspapers in the same local market (News Corporation owns KTTV and KCOP in the Los Angeles area). Mr. Murdoch has given mixed signals about his interest in The Los Angeles Times, which the Tribune Company plans to sell. The resignation last week of the Federal Communications Commission chairman, Julius Genachowski, could further slow the process. Mr. Genachowski had proposed allowing a rule change to allow a single company to own both a TV station and newspaper in a top-20 market provided the station was not in the top four in audience size.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting: Murdoch Weighs a Newspaper Deal and Steve Harvey Surprises Daytime TV', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-25T12:52:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel E. Slotnik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Slotnik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/43015bb6-2d5f-55aa-a47b-7d2c7fe11307', 'word_count': 643, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43015bb6-2d5f-55aa-a47b-7d2c7fe11307'}, {'abstract': 'On bad punditry.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/25/ego-image-and-sin/', 'snippet': 'On bad punditry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The excellent Kathleen Geier — give this woman a bigger job! — has a terrific piece on pundit sins in the runup to the Iraq war, which has applicability to lots of other issues too.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ego, Image, and Sin', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-25T12:55:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'