2-a507-e52b51b7c167'}, {'abstract': 'Ten of the 11 teams our model initially gave the greatest chance of winning the tournament have survived to the Round of 16. But their odds have changed based on their margins of victory so far and the teams they are most likely to face.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/25/evaluating-the-odds-for-florida-gulf-coast-and-the-rest-of-the-final-16-teams/', 'snippet': 'Ten of the 11 teams our model initially gave the greatest chance of winning the tournament have survived to the Round of 16. But their odds have changed based on their margins of victory so far and the teams they are most likely to face.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The story of the N.C.A.A. men’s basketball tournament is Florida Gulf Coast University, which on Sunday became the first No. 15 seed ever to reach the Round of 16, despite having become a full Division I member only last season. Just how unlikely was its accomplishment? Does the team have a chance of advancing much further? And what about the other teams in the Round of 16?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Evaluating the Odds for Florida Gulf Coast and the Rest of the Final 16 Teams', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-25T14:16:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/03215a4e-1a7b-576c-ac58-f24d494b331b', 'word_count': 2887, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03215a4e-1a7b-576c-ac58-f24d494b331b'}, {'abstract': 'Cyprus secures a bailout deal. | Banks lose a loophole | An F.C.C. shift may thwart a Murdoch media deal. | Buyers Circle Marks & Spencer as takeover target | A buyer is found for Blockbuster’s British unit.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/03/25/rival-bids-for-dell/', 'snippet': 'Cyprus secures a bailout deal. | Banks lose a loophole | An F.C.C. shift may thwart a Murdoch media deal. | Buyers Circle Marks & Spencer as takeover target | A buyer is found for Blockbuster’s British unit.', 'lead_paragraph': ' \xa0|\xa0 RIVAL BIDS FOR DELL The bidding war for Dell is heating up. The computer maker confirmed on Monday that it had received preliminary takeover proposals by the private equity giant Blackstone Group and the investor Carl C. Icahn. As expected, the company’s special committee determined that “both proposals could reasonably be expected to result in superior proposals” and intended to keep negotiating with Blackstone and Mr. Icahn, DealBook’s Michael J. de la Merced reports.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rival Bids for Dell', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-25T14:16:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a40a0914-bbd2-5397-b004-eeaaf1dc42fc', 'word_count': 1130, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a40a0914-bbd2-5397-b004-eeaaf1dc42fc'}, {'abstract': 'Flu vaccination is recommended for people with asthma, yet most people with the disease do not get vaccinated, in part over unfounded worries that the shot itself can worsen asthma and provoke attacks.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/25/really-the-claim-the-flu-shot-can-worsen-asthma/', '