8c6c5c8a49'}, {'abstract': 'The justices accepted a case on a state voter initiative even as they weighed a challenge to the University of Texas’ race-conscious admissions program.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/26/us/justices-take-new-case-on-affirmative-action.html', 'snippet': 'The justices accepted a case on a state voter initiative even as they weighed a challenge to the University of Texas’ race-conscious admissions program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Supreme Court on Monday added a new affirmative action case to its docket. It is already considering a major challenge to the University of Texas’ race-conscious admissions program.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Supreme Court Takes New Case on Affirmative Action, From Michigan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Supreme Court Takes New Case on Affirmative Action, From Michigan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AFFIRMATIVE ACTION', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Michigan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADMISSIONS STANDARDS', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-25T14:41:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Liptak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Liptak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a887ad89-1835-56d0-b0e1-35de745edbc4', 'word_count': 585, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a887ad89-1835-56d0-b0e1-35de745edbc4'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/25/what-were-reading-656/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Atlantic: Behold: the radish as an aphrodisiac (and you thought you were tired of reading about root vegetables). — Melissa Clark', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-25T14:44:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1be3573a-71f0-5a44-bec0-e0b3899463f5', 'word_count': 583, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1be3573a-71f0-5a44-bec0-e0b3899463f5'}, {'abstract': 'Check back here for the most recent sentence, and tweet your idea for the next sentence using the hashtag #NYTMagStory.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/25/write-a-short-story-with-kate-atkinson/', 'snippet': 'Check back here for the most recent sentence, and tweet your idea for the next sentence using the hashtag #NYTMagStory.', 'lead_paragraph': '1:39 p.m. | Updated  Read the full story below.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Write a Short Story With Kate Atkinson!', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Atkinson, Kate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-25T14:45:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Samantha Henig', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Samantha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Henig', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/50dde062-2362-509c-90df-d1c5990577ec', 'word_count': 172, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50dde062-2362-509c-90df-d1c5990577ec'}, {'abstract': 'Tracking a single number — whether it’s how much you save each month or how much your investments are worth — may be a subtle nudge to improving your finances.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/25/tracking-your-finances-one-number-at-a-time/', 'snippet': 'Tracking a single number — whether it’s how much you save each month or how much your investments are worth — may be a subtle nudge to improving your finances.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I think it’s true that if I want to improve my performance in something, I need to measure and track it. As Thomas Monson, an author and president of the Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints, said: “When performance is measured, performance improves. When performance is measured and reported back, the rate of improvement accelerates.”', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tracking Your Finances, One Number at a Time', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'One Number at a Time', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-25T14:51:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By CARL RICHARDS', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'RICHARDS', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/288f13d8-98d8-5144-8e9c-0d4e98e2daf7', 'word_count': 755, 'uri': 'nyt://article/288f13d8-98d8-5144-8e9c-0d4e98e2daf7'}, {'abstract': 'Contrary to his critics, and despite greatly expanding executive powers, the president was pragmatic and respectful of individual liberties.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/25/was-lincoln-a-tyrant/', 'snippet': 'Contrary to his critics, and despite greatly expanding executive powers, the president was pragmatic and respectful of individual liberties.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Abraham Lincoln took office in March 1861, the executive branch was small and relatively limited in its power. By the time of his assassination, he had claimed more prerogatives than any president before him, and the executive branch had grown enormously. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Was Lincoln a Tyrant?', 'kicker': 'Opinionator', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitution (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Draft and Recruitment (Military)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidents and Presidency (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lincoln, Abraham', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-25T14:57:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer L. Weber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Weber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/37695a2c-dd59-52ac-b033-66d9a4afcfc8', 'word_count': 1581, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37695a2c-dd59-52ac-b033-66d9a4afcfc8'}, {'abstract': 'In death as in life, Boris A. Berezovsky, the former tycoon who amassed billions of dollars and enormous political influence in post-Soviet Russia, remained true to Winston Churchill’s depiction of his land as the supreme enigma.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/25/in-death-as-in-life-berezovsky-remains-a-puzzle/', 'snippet': 'In death as in life, Boris A. Berezovsky, the former tycoon who amassed billions of dollars and enormous political influence in post-Soviet Russia, remained true to Winston Churchill’s depiction of his land as the supreme enigma.', 'lead_paragraph': ' In death as in life, Boris A. Berezovsky, the former tycoon who amassed billions of dollars and enormous political influence in post-Soviet Russia, remained true to Winston Churchill’s depiction of his land as the supreme enigma.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Death as in Life, Berezovsky Remains a Puzzle', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABRAMOVICH, ROMAN A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berezovsky, Boris A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Litvinenko, Marina', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'KGB', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-25T15:00:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Cowell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cowell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf3aff2a-414b-53d1-ac7f-52958e5e927e', 'word_count': 335, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf3aff2a-414b-53d1-ac7f-52958e5e927e'}, {'abstract': 'Every merchant services application I have seen has required a Social Security number and demanded that all card transactions be backstopped by my own assets. My house, my car and my savings are all up for grabs if things go wrong.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/25/what-you-need-to-know-about-credit-card-processing/', 'snippet': 'Every merchant services application I have seen has required a Social Security number and demanded that all card transactions be backstopped by my own assets. My house, my car and my savings are all up for grabs if things go wrong.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Starting on Tuesday morning, I am going to publish a series of posts about my search for an honest and affordable processor of credit card transactions. It was not an easy search, but I learned a lot — much of which I never wanted to know but some of which I think may be helpful to other business owners.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What You Need to Know About Credit Card Processing', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Cards', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Downs, Paul', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN EXPRESS COMPANY', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MasterCard Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Paul Downs Cabinetmakers', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Visa Inc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-25T15:00:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Downs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Downs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/885a33d5-6d4d-53fa-8eb4-c5894692dca4', 'word_count': 1276, 'uri': 'nyt://article/885a33d5-6d4d-53fa-8eb4-c5894692dca4'}, {'abstract': 'Sandwiches can provide a great way to get more vegetables into your diet.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/25/health/tomato-kale-and-mozzarella-sandwich-with-parsley-pesto.html', 'snippet': 'Sandwiches can provide a great way to get more vegetables into your diet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Health professionals, scientists, and chefs all agree that the American diet is short on vegetables. They are working together to address the problem, which is at the heart of the health and obesity crisis facing our country. A couple of weeks ago I brought you burgers that were made with a mix of meat and vegetables. What I didn’t talk about was how you could build on that burger, with layers of different lettuces, tomatoes, peppers, onions, pickles and even cooked greens.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/23/science/25recipehealth/25recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/23/science/25recipehealth/25recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/23/science/25recipehealth/25recipehealth-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/23/science/25recipehealth/25recipehealth-