l', 'snippet': 'The authors Flynt Leverett and Hillary Mann Leverett respond to a recent review of their book “Going to Tehran.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Going to Tehran’', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Going To Tehran’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-25T15:13:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6891674-065e-5bc2-a989-714e5bc94e45', 'word_count': 1052, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6891674-065e-5bc2-a989-714e5bc94e45'}, {'abstract': 'When did I lose the power to declare “family time”?', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/25/know-when-to-hold-em-making-family-time-work-for-teens/', 'snippet': 'When did I lose the power to declare “family time”?', 'lead_paragraph': 'When my children were little, it was easy to create connected family time. I called it incubation, when we’d shut out the rest of the world and go off on our own, just the kids and my husband and me. We’d make a plan, pack up some snacks, load everyone in the car or strollers, and head out to some near or far-off state park or nature area, where we could run, play, climb and be as loud as a family of six people is sometimes wont to be.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Know When to Hold ’Em: Making Family Time Work for Teens', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teenagers and Adolescence', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-25T15:13:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bernadette Noll', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bernadette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Noll', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a630faf1-6990-597d-8ee0-4123bb60a78e', 'word_count': 645, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a630faf1-6990-597d-8ee0-4123bb60a78e'}, {'abstract': 'It would also be possible, Nissan said, for the driver to think the vehicle was in “Park” when it was in a gear that could allow it to roll away.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/25/nissan-recalls-nv-commercial-vans-for-transmission-shifter/', 'snippet': 'It would also be possible, Nissan said, for the driver to think the vehicle was in “Park” when it was in a gear that could allow it to roll away.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nissan is recalling all the NV commercial vans it built for the last two years because of a problem with the automatic transmission shifter, according to a report from the automaker posted on the Web site of the National Highway Traffic Safety Administration.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nissan Recalls NV Commercial Vans for Transmission Shifter', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recalls and Bans of Products', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vans', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Highway Traffic Safety Administration