', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/26/nyregion/former-village-dispensary-must-untangle-restrictions.html', 'snippet': 'The Northern Dispensary in Manhattan’s Greenwich Village has sat empty for decades, thanks to its owners’ quirks and a staggering set of deed restrictions on its use.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The corner of Christopher Street and Waverly Place, in the heart of Greenwich Village, is one of the most sought after slices of Manhattan. The stoops are tidy, the restaurants are lavish and a town house down the block sold last year for $11.5 million.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/26/nyregion/26appraisal_cnd/26appraisal_cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/26/nyregion/26appraisal_cnd/26appraisal_cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/26/nyregion/26appraisal_cnd/26appraisal_cnd-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/26/nyregion/26appraisal_cnd/26appraisal_cnd-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/26/nyregion/26appraisal_cnd/26appraisal_cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/26/nyregion/26appraisal_cnd/26appraisal_cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/26/nyregion/26appraisal_cnd/26appraisal_cnd-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At High-Priced Corner, a Building Forlorn', 'kicker': 'The Appraisal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Desolate Building At a High-Priced Corner', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Zoning', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greenwich Village (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-25T15:23:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth A. Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/20ea80bb-1271-55c3-b38e-efa377fa5023', 'word_count': 1135, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20ea80bb-1271-55c3-b38e-efa377fa5023'}, {'abstract': 'News organizations should evaluate the motivations of parents who want to take their child’s story public.', 'web_url': 'https://publiceditor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/25/anna-quindlen-and-andrew-solomon/', 'snippet': 'News organizations should evaluate the motivations of parents who want to take their child’s story public.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My blog post last week – about Coy Mathis, the 6-year-old transgender Colorado child – drew some strong responses from readers. On Twitter, I immediately heard from those who sharply questioned my suggestion that “the willingness of the child” be considered, along with parental approval, in deciding to name her and use photographs of her. As many of these critics (some of whom were parents) noted, young children are willing to do many things they might regret later; they don’t have the maturity to know how their actions will play out.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Anna Quindlen and Andrew Solomon Join Discussion About Media and Transgender Children', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transgender and Transsexual', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-25T15:24:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaret Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/01ad8b82-96dc-5d47-8eab-2269c7740bdc', 'word_count': 937, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01ad8b82-96dc-5d47-8eab-2269c7740bdc'}, {'abstract': 'A life-size cutout of a traffic policeman in Bangalore, Karnataka.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/25/image-of-the-day-march-25/', 'snippet': 'A life-size cutout of a traffic policeman in Bangalore, Karnataka.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/25/world/asia/25-POD-Bangalore-IndiaInk/25-POD-Bangalore-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 392, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/25/world/asia/25-POD-Bangalore-IndiaInk/25-POD-Bangalore-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 392}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url'