dös was one of the most extraordinary mathematicians of the last century. Celebrate the 100th anniversary of his birth with two puzzles, including a challenge from a longtime collaborator, Ronald Graham.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/25/erdos/', 'snippet': 'Paul Erdös was one of the most extraordinary mathematicians of the last century. Celebrate the 100th anniversary of his birth with two puzzles, including a challenge from a longtime collaborator, Ronald Graham.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week we celebrate the life of\xa0the most published mathematician in history, Paul Erdos (AIR-dosh), who was born 100 years ago on March 26. Dr.\xa0Erdos, who has been called the world’s greatest problem poser and solver, collaborated with over 500 mathematicians before his death in 1996.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/23/crosswords/Erdos0/Erdos0-jumbo.png', 'height': 480, 'width': 480, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/23/crosswords/Erdos0/Erdos0-superJumbo.png', 'height': 480, 'width': 480, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/23/crosswords/Erdos0/Erdos0-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/23/crosswords/Erdos0/Erdos0-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/23/crosswords/Erdos0/Erdos0-thumbLarge-v2.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Improbable Life of Paul Erdős', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mathematics', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Puzzles', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Heiligman, Deborah', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pham, LeUyen', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York University', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of California, San Diego', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Budapest (Hungary)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-25T16:00:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gary Antonick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Antonick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0f51001f-31ff-531b-9d2a-fba60dddb936', 'word_count': 3979, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0f51001f-31ff-531b-9d2a-fba60dddb936'}, {'abstract': 'Standard Chartered learned the hard way that prosecutors take deferred prosecution agreements quite seriously, when the government forced the chairman to retract his statements on the settlement.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/03/25/sending-a-message-for-backpedaling-on-settlements/', 'snippet': 'Standard Chartered learned the hard way that prosecutors take deferred prosecution agreements quite seriously, when the government forced the chairman to retract his statements on the settlement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When a company accepts a deferred prosecution agreement to resolve a criminal investigation, one requirement is that it cannot backtrack on an admission of guilt. Standard Chartered learned the hard way that prosecutors take these agreements quite seriously when an executive tries to soft-pedal any corporate wrongdoing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sending a Message for Backpedaling on Settlements', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Standard Chartered Bank PLC', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-25T16:19:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter J. Henning', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Henning', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/02f7b5bb-b518-56b9-b0a3-d59b994194c0', 'word_count': 882, 'uri': 'nyt://article/02f7b5bb-b518-56b9-b0a3-d59b994194c0'}, {'abstract': 'The new BioShock Infinite, from the Irrational video game studio, takes place in a 1912 dystopian environment loaded with period detail.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/26/arts/video-games/bioshock-infinite-irrationals-new-video-game.html', 'snippet': 'The new BioShock Infinite, from the Irrational video game studio, takes place in a 1912 dystopian environment loaded with period detail.', 'lead_paragraph': 'During the long development of BioShock Infinite — the first release by the Massachusetts studio Irrational Games since the original BioShock transfixed players more