'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1eda5754-213d-56c1-8a2a-99d13cd8f1bc', 'word_count': 1056, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1eda5754-213d-56c1-8a2a-99d13cd8f1bc'}, {'abstract': 'Episode 10 recap, “House of Card”: After Frank Underwood is clobbered by the president for getting the vote count wrong, he realizes that Congress is not the house he needs to get in order. Ashley Parker and David Carr tease apart the episode.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/25/house-of-cards-episode-10-the-recap-frank-forgets-how-to-count-and-peter-tumbles/', 'snippet': 'Episode 10 recap, “House of Card”: After Frank Underwood is clobbered by the president for getting the vote count wrong, he realizes that Congress is not the house he needs to get in order. Ashley Parker and David Carr tease apart the episode.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We are now officially headed toward end-of-season recess on “House of Cards” and Ashley Parker and David Carr take a look at episode 10. If you like reading their take on the political and media dimensions of the rest of the season, you can find episode one, two,three, four, five, six,seven , eight or nine here. Spoilers are thicker than plots on “House of Cards,” so consider yourself warned.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '“House of Cards” Episode 10, the Recap: Frank Forgets How to Count and Peter Tumbles', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-25T17:09:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Carr and Ashley Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8467a3ed-1914-551e-bc85-93d0b64b3214', 'word_count': 1251, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8467a3ed-1914-551e-bc85-93d0b64b3214'}, {'abstract': 'President Xi Jinping defended China’s economic stake in many African countries during a speech in Tanzania, and promised aid in an effort to counter fears over competitive Chinese companies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/26/world/asia/chinese-leader-xi-jinping-offers-africa-assurance-and-aid.html', 'snippet': 'President Xi Jinping defended China’s economic stake in many African countries during a speech in Tanzania, and promised aid in an effort to counter fears over competitive Chinese companies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — China’s new president, Xi Jinping, sought to assure African countries on Monday that his government would heed complaints that relentlessly competitive Chinese companies were suffocating African efforts to nurture industry and jobs, and he promised aid, scholarships and technology transfers in an effort to counter those fears.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/26/world/CHINA/CHINA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/26/world/CHINA/CHINA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/26/world/CHINA/CHINA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'ju