b0d56419-a0a6-589a-9030-d6cf83b2a880', 'word_count': 727, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0d56419-a0a6-589a-9030-d6cf83b2a880'}, {'abstract': 'Paul Caine joined Dial Global, New York, as chief executive. Mr. Caine had been executive vice president and president for advertising at Time Inc., New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/25/business/media/accounts-and-people-of-note-in-the-advertising-industry.html', 'snippet': 'Paul Caine joined Dial Global, New York, as chief executive. Mr. Caine had been executive vice president and president for advertising at Time Inc., New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Paul Caine joined Dial Global, New York, a radio syndication company, as chief executive. He succeeds Spencer Brown, who is leaving, the company said. Mr. Caine had been executive vice president and president for advertising, as well as chief revenue officer, at Time Inc., New York, part of Time Warner. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Accounts and People of Note in the Advertising Industry', 'kicker': 'Webdenda', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Webdenda', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public Relations and Publicity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-25T17:12:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2be6ae94-4b31-591b-b96e-792bac4239f3', 'word_count': 1110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2be6ae94-4b31-591b-b96e-792bac4239f3'}, {'abstract': 'The artistic director of Playwrights Horizons sent an e-mail to subscribers explaining the company’s decision to produce Annie Baker’s play “The Flick,” which has been embraced by critics but has prompted threats of subscriber cancellations.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/25/the-flick-prompts-an-explanation-from-playwrights-horizons/', 'snippet': 'The artistic director of Playwrights Horizons sent an e-mail to subscribers explaining the company’s decision to produce Annie Baker’s play “The Flick,” which has been embraced by critics but has prompted threats of subscriber cancellations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The artistic director of Playwrights Horizons, a leading Off Broadway company that produces new American plays, took the unusual step on Saturday of e-mailing 3,000 of the theater’s subscribers to explain his decision to produce Annie Baker’s new play “The Flick,” whose three-hour length and periods of long silence have infuriated some audience members.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/25/arts/25artsbeat-flick/25artsbeat-flick-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 403, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/25/arts/25artsbeat-flick/25artsbeat-flick-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 403}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/25/arts/25artsbeat-flick/25artsbeat-flick-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 688, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/25/arts/25artsbeat-flick/25artsbeat-flick-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1376, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/25/arts/25artsbeat-flick/25artsbeat-flick-thumbStandard.jpg',