'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6cf22040-fc18-5011-aa15-e2aa328dfe64', 'word_count': 155, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6cf22040-fc18-5011-aa15-e2aa328dfe64'}, {'abstract': 'Using Google’s enormous Ngram database, researchers at three British universities tracked the use of “mood” words over the 20th century.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/25/fold-up-your-handkerchiefs-books-have-gotten-less-emotional-study-says/', 'snippet': 'Using Google’s enormous Ngram database, researchers at three British universities tracked the use of “mood” words over the 20th century.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you find you’re crying less while reading and throwing fewer books across the room, there may be a good reason. English-language books became steadily less “emotional” over the 20th century, according to a new study crunching billions of words via Google’s Ngram database.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fold Up Your Handkerchiefs: Books Have Gotten Less ‘Emotional,’ Study Says', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emotions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'PLoS One (Journal)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-25T19:13:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Schuessler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schuessler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/61721549-05d2-5a86-a37e-f7c795d5c6dd', 'word_count':