'_id': 'nyt://article/30c2d236-41f3-562b-b2d4-87ab956acd18', 'word_count': 675, 'uri': 'nyt://article/30c2d236-41f3-562b-b2d4-87ab956acd18'}, {'abstract': 'Studies suggest surprisingly few patients receive evidence-based treatments like cognitive behavioral therapy, which have been shown to be effective.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/25/looking-for-evidence-that-therapy-works/', 'snippet': 'Studies suggest surprisingly few patients receive evidence-based treatments like cognitive behavioral therapy, which have been shown to be effective.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mental-health care has come a long way since the remedy of choice was trepanation — drilling holes into the skull to release “evil spirits.” Over the last 30 years, treatments like cognitive-behavioral therapy, dialectical behavior therapy and family-based treatment have been shown effective for ailments ranging from anxiety and depression to post-traumatic stress disorder and eating disorders.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/26/science/26CONS_SPAN/26CONS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 375, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/26/science/26CONS_SPAN/26CONS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 375}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/26/science/26CONS_SPAN/26CONS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 640, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/26/science/26CONS_SPAN/26CONS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1113, 'width': 1780, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'ty