ind Your Flippers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Go Find Your Flippers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-25T20:04:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Finn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Finn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c264fc4-b37d-59c5-8060-bb3255d640a1', 'word_count': 395, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c264fc4-b37d-59c5-8060-bb3255d640a1'}, {'abstract': 'An official military count said that 28 detainees were refusing food, up from 26 on Friday, but prisoners and their lawyers said that tally was short.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/26/us/guantanamo-hunger-strike-appears-to-widen.html', 'snippet': 'An official military count said that 28 detainees were refusing food, up from 26 on Friday, but prisoners and their lawyers said that tally was short.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A  hunger strike among detainees at Guantánamo Bay, Cuba, who have been imprisoned by the United States military without trial — some for more than a decade — is continuing to grow, although there is sharp disagreement between the military and lawyers for the detainees about how many are participating.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/26/us/GITMO/GITMO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 385, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/26/us/GITMO/GITMO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 385}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/26/us/GITMO/GITMO-jumbo.jpg', '