': 'nyt://article/71878a83-390b-5c01-b4d3-3d41871d60a7', 'word_count': 519, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71878a83-390b-5c01-b4d3-3d41871d60a7'}, {'abstract': 'Every day, humans generate two to three pints of saliva, which comes in two varieties, with heroic attributes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/26/health/the-mouths-guard.html', 'snippet': 'Every day, humans generate two to three pints of saliva, which comes in two varieties, with heroic attributes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Humans secrete two kinds of saliva, stimulated and unstimulated, no more alike than most siblings. The prettier child is stimulated saliva. It comes from the parotid glands, between cheek and ear. When a plate of spaghetti carbonara makes your mouth water, that’s stimulated saliva. It makes up 70 to 90 percent of the two to three pints of saliva each of us generates daily. Stimulated saliva looks, tastes and flows like water — it is, in fact, 99 percent water with some proteins and minerals. Each person’s saliva contains minerals in unique proportions.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/26/science/26SALI/26SALI-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 813, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/26/science/26SALI/26SALI-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 813}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/26/science/26SALI/26SALI-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 757, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/26/science/26SALI/26SALI-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1513, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnai