: 'By Karen Barrow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barrow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/35631f31-33a0-5c9c-a74d-4e4bcd261823', 'word_count': 54, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35631f31-33a0-5c9c-a74d-4e4bcd261823'}, {'abstract': 'To combat and correct stressed-out skin, Kiehl’s launched an exclusive service and a line of products.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/25/vain-glorious-kiehls-stress-relief/', 'snippet': 'To combat and correct stressed-out skin, Kiehl’s launched an exclusive service and a line of products.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Stress. Our bodies are engineered to cope with a certain amount comfortably, but sustained, intense stress is an entirely different matter. It can negatively impact our minds, our hearts, and our body’s largest organ, skin. “Its effects are particularly harsh, causing premature aging and advancing the symptoms of every common skin condition from sensitive skin to eczema and psoriasis,” says Dr. Cynthia Ackrill, a fellow at the American Institute of Stress. ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vain Glorious | Kiehl’s Stress Relief', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Vain Glorious: Relief at the Spa, Then One to Go', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Kiehl's", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-25T21:00:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katie Chang', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type