sors — are a new disruptive force in education. Leading universities have scrambled to join or offer alternatives like edX, a collaboration of the Massachusetts Institute of Technology, Harvard University and others.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Beware of the High Cost of ‘Free’ Online Courses', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Learning', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cusumano, Michael A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sloan School of Management', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-25T21:04:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Lohr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lohr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5727c58f-39bc-59b2-a835-84558ecc68ab', 'word_count': 606, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5727c58f-39bc-59b2-a835-84558ecc68ab'}, {'abstract': '“Life After Life,” the latest novel by Kate Atkinson, depicts a woman who appears in contradictory versions of similar events.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/26/books/life-after-life-a-novel-by-kate-atkinson.html', 'snippet': '“Life After Life,” the latest novel by Kate Atkinson, depicts a woman who appears in contradictory versions of similar events.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the midst of a secret love affair, Ursula Todd discovers that she is an excellent liar. The same can be said admiringly of Kate Atkinson, whose latest novel, “Life After Life,” is her very best. Ms. Atkinson’s wide-ranging body of work includes several novels that resemble mysteries, but she has never had the narrowly deductive mind to suit that genre. “Life After Life” is a big book that defies logic, chronology and even history in ways that underscore its author’s fully untethered imagination. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/26/arts/BOOK/BOOK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 789, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/26/arts/BOOK/BOOK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 789}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/26/arts/BOOK/BOOK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 779, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/26/arts/BOOK/BOOK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1557, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/26/arts/BOOK/BOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/26/arts/BOOK/BOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/26/arts/BOOK/BOOK-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Different Versions of a Life, All Lived', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Different Versions Of a Life, All Lived', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Life After Life (Book)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Atkinson, Kate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}