: 'nyt://article/40d73ffe-bb99-572c-99a3-15954ce5dc72'}, {'abstract': 'One of the pleasures and privileges of theatergoing in London — in addition to those little wooden spoonlets that come with the interval ice cream – is the beauty of the printed theater program. Granted, they’re not free.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/26/see-the-play-dont-miss-the-program/', 'snippet': 'One of the pleasures and privileges of theatergoing in London — in addition to those little wooden spoonlets that come with the interval ice cream – is the beauty of the printed theater program. Granted, they’re not free.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — One of the pleasures and privileges of theatergoing in London — in addition to those little wooden spoonlets that come with the interval ice cream — is the beauty of the printed theater program. Rather than the advertising-heavy publications of many cities, particularly New York, chock-full of fluffy profiles of the newest musical star and features on the favorite Thai restaurant of a chorus member of “Wicked,” a London theater program is often a quick study guide — a cheat sheet for the high-brow pop quiz of theater about to unfold. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/26/arts/rdv26-programs/rdv26-programs-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 395, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/26/arts/rdv26-programs/rdv26-programs-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 395}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/26/arts/rdv26-programs/rdv26-programs-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 569, 'width': 864, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/26/arts/rdv26-programs/