': 'By Carlos Puig', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carlos', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Puig', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5193026d-be6d-5754-a84e-9ebc124385d6', 'word_count': 444, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5193026d-be6d-5754-a84e-9ebc124385d6'}, {'abstract': 'The battle over Dell suggests that investors today may be slightly less short-term greedy than previous generations. | A collection of internal e-mails at the law firm DLA Piper could reinforce a perception that law firms inflate bills. | Puerto Rico is fashioning a new identity for itself as a tax haven. | A report says that the board of Hulu has approached potential buyers.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/03/26/in-dell-shifting-attitude-toward-buyouts/', 'snippet': 'The battle over Dell suggests that investors today may be slightly less short-term greedy than previous generations. | A collection of internal e-mails at the law firm DLA Piper could reinforce a perception that law firms inflate bills. | Puerto R...', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN DELL OFFERS, SHIFTING ATTITUDE TOWARD BUYOUTS \xa0|\xa0 The battle over Dell puts into focus the question of whether management-led buyouts are in shareholders’ best interests, and it reflects a shifting ethos on Wall Street, “one that might be slightly less short-term greedy than that of previous generations,” Andrew Ross Sorkin writes in the DealBook column. “It appears that some shareholders of companies involved in buyouts would prefer to ride a wave of gains alongside the buyout kings rather than cash out immediately.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Dell, Shifting Attitude Toward Buyouts', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-26T11:40:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/78ae6320-3fb8-5de0-8ad3-fd69201c7240', 'word_count': 1796, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78ae6320-3fb8-5de0-8ad3-fd69201c7240'}, {'abstract': 'Don’t worry: the nagging and fault-finding proceed as usual in the “In a Word” section below. But first, a small and subjective sampling of sparkling prose from recent editions. Nominations are always welcome.', 'web_url': 'https://afterdeadline.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/26/bright-passages-14/', 'snippet': 'Don’t worry: the nagging and fault-finding proceed as usual in the “In a Word” section below. But first, a small and subjective sampling of sparkling prose from recent editions. Nominations are always welcome.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Don’t worry: the fault-finding proceeds as usual in the “In a Word” section below. But first, a small and subjective sampling of sparkling prose from recent editions. Nominations are always welcome.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bright Passages', 'kicker': 'After Deadline', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-26T12:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Times Topics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Philip B. Corbett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Philip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c3b15619-dc6a-58fd-8a1d-0bb40ad01959', 'word_count': 1627, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c3b15619-dc6a-58fd-8a1d-0bb40ad01959'}, {'abstract': 'The actress plays Queen Margaret in a scene from Shakespeare’s “Henry VI, Part III,” from her show “Women of Will.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/26/in-performance-tina-packer-of-women-of-will/', 'snippet': 'The actress plays Queen Margaret in a scene from Shakespeare’s “Henry VI, Part III,” from her show “Women of Will.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In “Women of Will” the actress Tina Packer, the founder and former artistic director of Shakespeare & Company in Lenox, Mass., explores Shakespeare’s heroines. In this excerpt from “Henry VI, Part III,” Ms. Packer plays Queen Margaret of Anjou, who has captured the Duke of York and is about to have him killed for usurping the English crown for his children, even though Margaret’s children are the rightful heirs. The show, which also stars Nigel Gore, continues through June 2 at the Gym at Judson Memorial Church.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Performance: Tina Packer of ‘Women of Will’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Packer, Tina', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shakespeare, William', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-26T12:00:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa0b137c-b792-58d2-b83a-1ce6661caf76', 'word_count': 137, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa0b137c-b792-58d2-b83a-1ce6661caf76'}, {'abstract': 'A summary of what’s on today’s editorial page.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/26/opinion-report-anthony-lewis/', 'snippet': 'A summary of what’s on today’s editorial page.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From the editorial page', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Opinion Report: Anthony Lewis', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-26T12:06:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fecd2591-0475-5581-a95d-64d76e8e5330', 'word_count': 80, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fecd2591-0475-5581-a95d-64d76e8e5330'}, {'abstract': 'As the Supreme Court weighed a challenge to California’s ban on same-sex marriage, the weight of the decision that the justices will make was felt in thousands of communities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/27/us/crowds-camp-out-for-supreme-court-reward.html', 'snippet': 'As the Supreme Court weighed a challenge to California’s ban on same-sex marriage, the weight of the decision that the justices will make was felt in thousands of communities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'COLUMBIA, S.C. — Most United States Supreme Court cases, however significant, pass largely unnoticed when they are argued. But the opening of hearings over the legal definition of marriage was a cultural moment that brought America to its front porch.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/27/us/SCENE-1/SCENE-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 408, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/27/us/SCENE-1/SCENE-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeh