{'abstract': 'The Lede is following the Supreme Court hearing on Tuesday, the first of two days of arguments related to same-sex marriage.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/26/latest-updates-on-supreme-court-same-sex-marriage-hearing/', 'snippet': 'The Lede is following the Supreme Court hearing on Tuesday, the first of two days of arguments related to same-sex marriage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'That’s a wrap for today, but we’ll be back on Wednesday with live updates from the oral arguments as the high court weighs the Defense of Marriage Act. For now, The Times’s Adam Liptak and Scott Shane report that the justices might be nervous about acting too quickly on gay marriage, and Jeremy Peters writes about the people who waited for days to witness the discussion. Don’t want the argument to end? Room for Debate has a discussion about whether gay marriage is best left to the courts or to states.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'March 26 Updates on Supreme Court Same-Sex Marriage Hearing', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-26T13:53:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3be8b495-15c7-522f-baa5-455e59510e1e', 'word_count': 3027, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3be8b495-15c7-522f-baa5-455e59510e1e'}, {'abstract': 'Pitcher Pedro Feliciano, who will not begin the season with the Mets, said he would remain with the organization. Las Vegas is a likely destination.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/26/feliciano-will-stay-with-mets/', 'snippet': 'Pitcher Pedro Feliciano, who will not begin the season with the Mets, said he would remain with the organization. Las Vegas is a likely destination.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PORT ST. LUCIE, Fla. — One day after it appeared he would seek a new employer, Pedro Feliciano, one of the last links to the Mets’ playoff run in 2006, said he would stay with the team somewhere in the organization.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Feliciano Will Stay With Mets', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'den Dekker, Matt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Feliciano, Pedro', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Horwitz, Jay', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-26T14:07:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dddba676-21c3-5a44-a41c-9d128f9f5df2', 'word_count': 238, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dddba676-21c3-5a44-a41c-9d128f9f5df2'}, {'abstract': 'Support for same-sex marriage is increasing, but is it doing so at a faster rate than in the past? How much of the shift is because of generational turnover? And how many states would approve same-sex marriage today?', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/26/how-opinion-on-same-sex-marriage-is-changing-and-what-it-means/', 'snippet': 'Support for same-sex marriage is increasing, but is it doing so at a faster rate than in the past? How much of the shift is because of generational turnover? And how many states would approve same-sex marriage today?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Supreme Court will hear arguments this week on two cases related to same-sex marriage, the first involving a California referendum that barred gay marriage, the other involving a federal law that prevents the government from recognizing same-sex unions. A variety of outcomes are possible, but it seems prudent to take stock of public opinion on same-sex marriage before the decisions come down. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Opinion on Same-Sex Marriage Is Changing, and What It Means', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-26T14:10:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4dfd36a8-c09a-5986-93d7-cdd568b5fafb', 'word_count': 2189, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4dfd36a8-c09a-5986-93d7-cdd568b5fafb'}, {'abstract': 'A renowned art collector, Steven Cohen has bought Picasso’s “Le Rêve” from the casino owner Stephen A. Wynn for $155 million. It is at least the second $100 million-plus acquisition of art by Mr. Cohen in the last two years.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/03/26/for-cohen-a-big-art-deal/', 'snippet': 'A renowned art collector, Steven Cohen has bought Picasso’s “Le Rêve” from the casino owner Stephen A. Wynn for $155 million. It is at least the second $100 million-plus acquisition of art by Mr. Cohen in the last two years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Less than two weeks after SAC Capital Advisors, the hedge fund owned by the billionaire trader Steven A. Cohen, agreed to pay the government $616 million to settle accusations of insider trading, Mr. Cohen has decided to buy a little something for himself.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '$616 Million Poorer, Hedge Fund Owner Still Buys Art', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '$616 Million Poorer, Hedge Fund Owner Still Buys Art', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hedge Funds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cohen, Steven A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Picasso, Pablo', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walter, Marie-Therese', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wynn, Stephen A', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'SAC Capital Advisors', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-26T14:17:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Vogel and Peter Lattman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vogel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/02a853b2-7f83-5887-95d4-7c03ca5cbed7', 'word_count': 1022, 'uri': 'nyt://article/02a853b2-7f83-5887-95d4-7c03ca5cbed7'}, {'abstract': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/26/the-gun-report-march-26-2013/', 'snippet': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every day we cite gun death statistics culled by Slate, which has been publishing the number of gun deaths since the Newtown massacre last December. Slate’s initiative was prompted in part by the fact that the F.B.I. statistics on gun deaths are woefully outdated, and that there is a void that needs to be filled: no research organization is even trying to “create a real-time chronicle of the death attributable to guns in the United States,” as Slate puts it. How does Slate compile its information? It uses crowdsourcing techniques, relying especially on a Twitter feed, @GunDeaths, which is run by an anonymous researcher who has been tweeting every reported gun death he can find since the mass shooting in Aurora.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Gun Report: March 26, 2013', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hartford (Conn)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oklahoma', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sandy Springs (Ga)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Toledo (Ohio)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (State)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-26T14:30:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Mascia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mascia', 'qualifier': None, 'title':