‘da Funk,” is the director of “Lucky Guy,” opening at the Broadhurst Theater on April 1. It is the last play Nora Ephron wrote before her death last year, and stars Tom Hanks as Mike McAlary, the Pulitzer Prize-winning newspaper journalist who covered the police beat in New York in the 1980s and ’90s. A resident of the city during those years, Wolfe was drawn to the pulse of Ephron’s script and the challenge of recreating such a dynamic time in New York’s history.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Talking Talent | George C. Wolfe', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Talking Talent: George C. Wolfe', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wolfe, George C', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Lucky Guy (Play)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-26T15:58:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lauren Tabach-Bank', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lauren', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tabach-Bank', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/81b675c7-c596-5153-9528-5eb8290c152e', 'word_count': 1536, 'uri': 'nyt://article/81b675c7-c596-5153-9528-5eb8290c152e'}, {'abstract': 'The enormous festival of food, drink and music in Brooklyn’s Prospect Park will be held over three days this year, May 17 to 19.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/26/the-googamooga-festival-will-return-in-may/', 'snippet': 'The enormous festival of food, drink and music in Brooklyn’s Prospect Park will be held over three days this year, May 17 to 19.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Great GoogaMooga festival of food, drink and music in Prospect Park, which drew thousands of people to its first outing last spring, will return. And there will be improvements to the festival, where general admission attendees complained last year of hourlong waits for food, drinks and bathrooms at the two-day event. Those who bought $250 tickets for Extra Mooga, the V.I.P. section of the festival, received refunds after organizers acknowledged that the experience was not commensurate with the price tag. (General admission tickets were, and will remain, free for Saturday and Sunday.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The GoogaMooga Festival Will Return in May', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Prospect Park (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-26T16:00:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b19f90b1-f095-56d3-90e2-41b8164cfa4d', 'word_count': 519, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b19f90b1-f095-56d3-90e2-41b8164cfa4d'}, {'abstract': 'When I hear about a tragedy caused by a moment of parental carelessness — a hot car, an unlocked pool gate — I don’t judge the parents. I was lucky.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/26/a-narrow-escape-and-lasting-guilt/', 'snippet': 'When I hear about a tragedy caused by a moment of parental carelessness — a hot car, an unlocked pool gate — I don’t judge the parents. I was lucky.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I was a new mom at 36, and there was a lot about motherhood that terrified me. I had no experience with infants, nor did my husband,\xa0 Michael. As happy as we were to be expecting, I was filled with fear and trepidation. How on earth would I know what to do?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Narrow Escape, and Lasting Guilt', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies and Infants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Falls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-26T16:04:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexandra Cantor Owens', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexandra', 'middlename': 'Cantor', 'lastname': 'Owens', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6eb04a4e-dbcf-534d-b384-0bec761c06b7', 'word_count': 733, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6eb04a4e-dbcf-534d-b384-0bec761c06b7'}, {'abstract': 'Books about bullying, for youngsters and adults, are now so numerous they are a genre in themselves.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/27/books/bullying-becomes-hot-and-profitable-topic-for-publishers.html', 'snippet': 'Books about bullying, for youngsters and adults, are now so numerous they are a genre in themselves.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nobody likes a bully — but these days the book industry loves having them to kick around.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/27/arts/BULLY/BULLY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 933, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/27/arts/BULLY/BULLY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 933}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption