paragraph': 'To compare the challenges faced by the Issue Project Room, an experimental music collective in Brooklyn, to Homer’s Odyssey might be a stretch, but the challenges faced by the group certainly have all the trappings of an ancient tragedy. The recent performance of “November” — a five-hour piano performance written by Dennis Johnson — was yet another triumph for the organization, which has oscillated between progress and defeat for nearly a decade.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After a Series of Setbacks, a Music Collective Reopens Its Doors', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Issue Project Room', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Downtown Brooklyn (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-26T16:37:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Colin Weatherby', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Colin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weatherby', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f94482d9-a196-5f43-9bcd-7fe0e74d2f83', 'word_count': 381, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f94482d9-a196-5f43-9bcd-7fe0e74d2f83'}, {'abstract': 'The former governor of Florida indicates that he has not yet evolved on the issue of gay marriage.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/26/as-supreme-court-deliberates-jeb-bush-speaks/', 'snippet': 'The former governor of Florida indicates that he has not yet evolved on the issue of gay marriage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Quite a few Republicans have been announcing new stages in their “evolution” on same-sex marriage, which is being debated in the Supreme Court today and tomorrow. Senator Rob Portman of Ohio said earlier this month that he was prompted to reverse his position when he learned his son was gay – after a two-year period of reflection that included having his name floated as a potential running mate for Mitt Romney, a staunch opponent of gay marriage.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Supreme Court Deliberates, Jeb Bush Speaks', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, Jeb', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Portman, Rob', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Warner, Mark R', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-26T16:40:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f319e745-6518-536f-9819-4f17a2e23a48', 'word_count': 376, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f319e745-6518-536f-9819-4f17a2e23a48'}, {'abstract': 'Hearing the band America in the music of Band of Horses.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/26/booming/if-you-like-horse-with-no-name-try-band-of-horses.html', 'snippet': 'Hearing the band America in the music of Band of Horses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Each week, Val Haller, a music-obsessed baby boomer and the founder of the Web site Valslist.com, matches tracks from her generation to those of her 20-something sons’ generation. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [