enetics Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-26T17:30:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Pollack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pollack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/362841ec-aaea-50d3-aa8e-e65e679b8dba', 'word_count': 1371, 'uri': 'nyt://article/362841ec-aaea-50d3-aa8e-e65e679b8dba'}, {'abstract': 'The parent company of IKEA and Marriott International announced this month that they are teaming up to create Moxy, a chain of budget hotels across Europe.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/26/hotel-partners-strange-bedfellows/', 'snippet': 'The parent company of IKEA and Marriott International announced this month that they are teaming up to create Moxy, a chain of budget hotels across Europe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The parent company of the design-driven furniture maker IKEA and the untrendy Marriott International announced this month that they are teaming up to create Moxy, a chain of budget hotels across Europe, news that strikes many travelers as an odd coupling. (And inspires questions, like, will you have to put together your nightside table with an Allen wrench?)', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hotel Partners, Strange Bedfellows', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hotel Partners, Strange Bedfellows', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-26T17:30:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elaine Glusac', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elaine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Glusac', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a2d5aa0-4060-5e0d-9dc8-fcc12a9df312', 'word_count': 228, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a2d5aa0-4060-5e0d-9dc8-fcc12a9df312'}, {'abstract': 'George Soros, the billionaire financier and philanthropist, has pledged $1 million to the NAACP Legal Defense and Educational Fund.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/26/soros-to-give-1-million-to-naacp-legal-fund/', 'snippet': 'George Soros, the billionaire financier and philanthropist, has pledged $1 million to the NAACP Legal Defense and Educational Fund.', 'lead_paragraph': 'George Soros, the billionaire financier and philanthropist, has pledged $1 million to the NAACP Legal Defense and Educational Fund, the country’s leading civil rights legal advocacy group, officials there said Tuesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Soros to Give $1 Million to NAACP Legal Fund', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights and Liberties', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voter Registration and Requirements', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Soros, George', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Assn for the Advancement of Colored People', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Open Society Foundations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-26T17:33:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Confessore', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Confessore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8fee3d9-c68f-5933-a88d-2f8f52b757d7', 'word_count': 255, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8fee3d9-c68f-5933-a88d-2f8f52b757d7'}, {'abstract': 'What makes these squid fritters unusual is that they are sizzled like pancakes, rather than deep-fried.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/27/dining/pairing-island-flavor-with-amber-ales.html', 'snippet': 'What makes these squid fritters unusual is that they are sizzled like pancakes, rather than deep-fried.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Assuming the occasion does not demand fancy fare, there is very little you can’t enjoy with American amber ales. I proved that at a recent Sunday lunch. We had just spent a long weekend at the home of friends in the Grenadines, where Venita Alexander, an accomplished local cook who adds island flavor to some of her meals, made an impossible quantity of conch fritters for lunch one day. We ate them all with Hairoun, the local lager, but it could just as well have been an American amber ale. What made her fritters unusual was that she didn’t deep-fry them; rather, she used much less oil to sizzle them like pancakes. I stole her idea, replacing the conch with more easily obtained squid and adding beer (instead of milk) to my batter. FLORENCE FABRICANT', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/27/dining/27PAIR_SPAN/27PAIR_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/27/dining/27PAIR_SPAN/27PAIR_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/27/dining/27PAIR_SPAN/27PAIR_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/27/dining/27PAIR_SPAN/27PAIR_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/27/dining/27PAIR_SPAN/27PAIR_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/27/dining/27PAIR_SPAN/27PAIR_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/27/dining/27PAIR_SPAN/27PAIR_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sampling Island Flavor With Amber Ales', 'kicker': 'Pairings', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Squid', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-26T17:41:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d3f8022-02e3-5b26-84e1-366a8ae29a73', 'word_count': 135, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d3f8022-02e3-5b26-84e1-366a8ae29a73'}, {'abstract': 'Elysia Borowy-Reeder will take over at the Museum of Contemporary Art Detroit.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/26/detroits-contemporary-art-museum-finally-has-a-new-director/', 'snippet': 'Elysia Borowy-Reeder will take over at the Museum of Contemporary Art Detroit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Detroit might not be doing so well – it was placed this month under the control of an emergency manager as it tries to stave off financial default. But its contemporary-art scene is thriving and on Tuesday the Museum of Contemporary Art Detroit announced that it had selected a new director after more than a year and a half without a permanent leader. Elysia Borowy-Reeder, who was most recently the director of the Contemporary Art Museum in Raleigh, N.C., where she focused on strengthening that museum’s education programs, will take over in early April.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Detroit’s Contemporary Art Museum Finally Has a New Director', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Detroit (Mich)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-26T17:44:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randy Kennedy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kennedy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/210d492b-c0db-5c0b-8841-a3e9b0135af3', 'word_count': 190, 'uri': 'nyt://article/210d492b-c0db-5c0b-8841-a3e9b0135af3'}, {'abstract': 'Some consumers see long-term care insurance as a way to help them stay out of a nursing home and in their own homes longer.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/26/buyers-of-long-term-care-insurance-prefer-home-care/', 'snippet': 'Some consumers see long-term care insurance as a way to help them stay out of a nursing home and in their own homes longer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Long-term care insurance, which can help cover the cost of extended care if you’re unable to care for yourself, is something no one really wants to think about. It’s a product you buy, after all, in the hope that you will never have to use it. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Buyers of Long-Term Care Insurance Prefer Home Care', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elder Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Home Health Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Long-Term Care Insurance', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nursing Homes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-26T17:46:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc7fd041-7244-57b8-9e8f-2399ce7a8b64', 'word_count': 383, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc7fd041-7244-57b8-9e8f-2399ce7a8b64'}, {'abstract': 'Rachel Shein, owner of Baked in the Sun, responds to reader comments from last week’s case study.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/26/bakery-owner-talks-about-coping-with-health-insurance-changes/', 'snippet': 'Rachel Shein, owner of Baked in the Sun, responds to reader comments from last week’s case study.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week, we published a case study about Baked in the Sun, a wholesale bakery and distributor that is trying to decide how best to comply with the Affordable Care Act. Starting in January, the new law requires businesses with 50 or more full-time employees to offer health insurance or pay a penalty. Owned by Rachel Shein and Steve Pilarski, husband and wife, the company employs nearly 100 workers to bake and deliver freshly made pastries to coffee shops, hospitals and hotels in Southern California.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bakery Owner Talks About Coping With Health Insurance Changes', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Providing Health Insurance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bakeries and Baked Products', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-26T18:00:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Weed', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d3a0e09-9091-5678-ad9e-f62e2343c09c', 'word_count': 876, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d3a0e09-9091-5678-ad9e-f62e2343c09c'}, {'abstract': 'The American mobile carrier, which has struggled against rivals like AT&T and Verizon, will offer the iPhone 5 and other top smartphones without locking in customers for two years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/27/technology/t-mobile-unveils-aggressive-phone-pricing-with-no-contracts.html', 'snippet': 'The American mobile carrier, which has struggled against rivals like AT&T and Verizon, will offer the iPhone 5 and other top smartphones without locking in customers for two years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'T-Mobile USA, long trailing its rivals in the cellphone industry, is trying to catch up by changing the conversation: it is selling the iPhone cheaper than the competition, and most important, customers would not have to sign a contract.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/27/business/PHONE/PHONE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 347, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/27/business/PHONE/PHONE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 347}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/27/business/PHONE/PHONE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 593, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/27/business/PHONE/PHONE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1186, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'T-Mobile Shakes Up Its Service', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'T-Mobile Shakes Up Its Service', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chen, Brian X', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cellular Telephones', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'T-Mobile', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-26T18:04:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian X. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': 'X.', 'las