ues in the Israeli-Palestinian conflict.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/27/world/BRIEFS-2/BRIEFS-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 533, 'width': 348, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/27/world/BRIEFS-2/BRIEFS-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 533, 'width': 348, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/27/world/BRIEFS-2/BRIEFS-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/27/world/BRIEFS-2/BRIEFS-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/27/world/BRIEFS-2/BRIEFS-2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Qatar Proposes $1 Billion Jerusalem Heritage Fund', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Qatar: Fund Proposed to Protect \r\nJerusalem’s Arab Heritage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thani, Hamad bin Khalifa al-', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Droubi, Hala', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jerusalem (Israel)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Qatar', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARAB LEAGUE', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-26T18:43:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hala Droubi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hala', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Droubi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/78868945-e85d-5fd1-802a-52d9ffd616a3', 'word_count': 469, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78868945-e85d-5fd1-802a-52d9ffd616a3'}, {'abstract': 'The players remaining in free agency have their flaws, but there are still a lot of good buys on the market.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/26/n-f-l-free-agents-who-are-still-worth-signing/', 'snippet': 'The players remaining in free agency have their flaws, but there are still a lot of good buys on the market.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It has been an unusually soft free-agent market this year. There could be multiple reasons for that: the salary cap’s lack of growth, a deep pool of draft prospects at the same positions that are deep in free agency (defensive end, for example), a subtle leaguewide shift in the way free agents are viewed, perhaps. Whatever the case, it’s left a lot of really good buys on the market. True, every unsigned veteran has a flaw or two. (After all, there’s a reason he’s still unsigned.) But a lot of these players still have valuable attributes that can fill an important niche for a team. These unsigned veterans should not be viewed in terms of what they once were; they should be viewed in terms of what they are now. Here are 10 who are worth signing:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/27/sports/football/27abraham/27abraham-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 