rganization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/314f4ec6-1408-537f-8139-50ebd02edbd4', 'word_count': 1314, 'uri': 'nyt://article/314f4ec6-1408-537f-8139-50ebd02edbd4'}, {'abstract': 'In “Welcome to the Punch” a group of thieves is joined in the uninhabited night by a cop, who, from the looks it, is angry, determined and terminally alone.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/27/movies/welcome-to-the-punch-from-eran-creevy.html', 'snippet': 'In “Welcome to the Punch” a group of thieves is joined in the uninhabited night by a cop, who, from the looks it, is angry, determined and terminally alone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Watching “Welcome to the Punch” I kept hoping for clowns, the inflatable kind that you sock in the head and that bounce back again and again — or maybe a couple of pugilists with tragic faces and Michelangelo musculature. While this curiously titled, intently self-serious British cops-and-robbers showdown doesn’t feature any clowns, it does include plenty of mano-a-mano action and a clutch of presumably unintended laughs. This isn’t a warning. It’s a recommendation.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/27/arts/27WELCOME/27WELCOME-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 347, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/27/arts/27WELCOME/27WELCOME-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 347}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/27/arts/27WELCOME/27WELCOME-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 591, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/27/arts/27WELCOME/27WELCOME-superJumbo.jpg', 'heigh