son': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e15fbcf9-d33d-50d2-8fb1-43af7842ca82', 'word_count': 915, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e15fbcf9-d33d-50d2-8fb1-43af7842ca82'}, {'abstract': 'A widespread practice by lenders of buying often-costly insurance for mortgaged property and billing the owner is under scrutiny.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/27/business/economy/regulators-review-costs-of-force-placed-insurance.html', 'snippet': 'A widespread practice by lenders of buying often-costly insurance for mortgaged property and billing the owner is under scrutiny.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Among the conditions imposed on most people who borrow money to buy a house, maintaining property insurance is one of the most common. If a borrower lets such a policy lapse, the lender will often protect its investment by purchasing a policy and billing the homeowner for it.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Mortgage Practice Gets a Closer Look by Regulators', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Mortgage Practice Gets A Closer Look By Regulators', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wyatt, Edward', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insurance', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgages', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Housing Finance Agency', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-26T23:24:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edwa