news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By David M. Herszenhorn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f27ddca6-96fe-59c8-96d0-1e3e048409bf', 'word_count': 891, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f27ddca6-96fe-59c8-96d0-1e3e048409bf'}, {'abstract': 'Derek Jeter said he was disappointed to open the season on the disabled list but that he intends to start for the bulk of the season.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/27/sports/baseball/injured-jeter-says-he-will-still-be-an-every-day-shortstop.html', 'snippet': 'Derek Jeter said he was disappointed to open the season on the disabled list but that he intends to start for the bulk of the season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TAMPA, Fla. — Derek Jeter finally acknowledged the sobering reality Tuesday that he will start the season on the disabled list, forcing him to miss his first opening day game since 2001.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jeter Confirms Stint on Disabled List', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jeter Confirms Stint on D.L.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jeter, Derek', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Waldstein, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-27T01:26:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Web Log', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ce50a32-5c6b-58fc-acd5-73a11c6ba0cd', 'word_count': 216, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ce50a32-5c6b-58fc-acd5-73a11c6ba0cd'}, {'abstract': 'There is a strong argument for everyone doing more to end the Syrian civil war, but satisfactory answers are needed first to some crucial questions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/27/opinion/friedman-cautions-curves-ahead.html', 'snippet': 'There is a strong argument for everyone doing more to end the Syrian civil war, but satisfactory answers are needed first to some crucial questions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are mounting reports that the U.S. is getting more deeply involved in supporting the Syrian rebels trying to topple President Bashar al-Assad. There is a strong argument for everyone doing more to end the Syrian civil war before the Syrian state totally collapses and before its sectarian venom and refugees further destabilize Lebanon, Iraq and Jordan. But I hope that before President Obama gets more deeply involved in Syria, he gets satisfactory answers to the following questions:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': 