ay. After five years of pre-eminence, the Boston Celtics have at least earned a withholding of judgment until the games really matter.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/27/sports/KNICKS/KNICKS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 421, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/27/sports/KNICKS/KNICKS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 421}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/27/sports/KNICKS/KNICKS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 718, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/27/sports/KNICKS/KNICKS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1436, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/27/sports/KNICKS/KNICKS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/27/sports/KNICKS/KNICKS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/27/sports/KNICKS/KNICKS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Knicks Poised to Take Celtics’ Crown ', 'kicker': 'Knicks 100, Celtics 85', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Knicks Poised to Take Celtics’ Crown', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beck, Howard', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Celtics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, J R', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANTHONY, CARMELO', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-27T02:28:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Howard Beck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Howard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f62a2e64-dd92-5c3a-9d68-56e21da5f0e8', 'word_count': 923, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f62a2e64-dd92-5c3a-9d68-56e21da5f0e8'}, {'abstract': 'The new judge in the trial of James (Whitey) Bulger, the Boston gangster, said that the trial would begin on June 10.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/27/us/massachusetts-bulger-trial-will-proceed-on-schedule.html', 'snippet': 'The new judge in the trial of James (Whitey) Bulger, the Boston gangster, said that the trial would begin on June 10.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The new judge in the trial of James (Whitey) Bulger, the Boston gangster, held her first hearing with lawyers for Mr. Bulger and government prosecutors on Tuesday, and said that the trial would begin on June 10, as scheduled by her predecessor. The new judge, Denise J. Casper of Federal District Court, was assigned the case this month after an appeals court removed Judge Richard G. Stearns because his previous career as a federal prosecutor was found by a federal appeals court to feed the perception of bias in his handling of the case. Mr. Bulger faces a sweeping racketeering indictment that charges him with involvement in 19 murders. Lawyers on both sides of the case said Tuesday that they expect the trial to last through the summer. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Massachusetts: Bulger Trial Will Proceed on Schedule', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | New England', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Massachusetts: Bulger Trial Will Proceed On Schedule', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bidgood, Jess', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bulger, James J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Racketeering and Racketeers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Casper, Denise J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Massachusetts', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Crime', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-27T02:34:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jess Bidgood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jess', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bidgood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/977613f7-986e-5551-b2d4-69d55fe754c3', 'word_count': 128, 'uri': 'nyt://article/977613f7-986e-5551-b2d4-69d55fe754c3'}, {'abstract': 'The state Supreme Court ruled on Tuesday that a two-year-old school voucher program allowing low- and middle-income families to use public funds to attend private schools was constitutional.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/27/us/indiana-voucher-program-ruled-constitutional.html', 'snippet': 'The state Supreme Court ruled on Tuesday that a two-year-old school voucher program allowing low- and middle-income families to use public funds to attend private schools was constitutional.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Indiana Supreme Court ruled on Tuesday that the state’s two-year-old school voucher program allowing low- and middle-income families to use public funds to attend private schools was constitutional. In a 5-to-0 decision, the court said that the voucher program did not violate the state’s prohibition against using state funds to benefit religious institutions because the primary beneficiaries of the vouchers were the families who used them. Since the state legislature enacted the voucher program, about 9,000 families have taken advantage, and the vast majority are sending their children to parochial schools. Glenda Ritz, Indiana superintendent of public instruction, said she was disappointed in the court’s decision. “I personally believe that public dollars should go to public schools,” she said in a statement. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Indiana: Voucher Program Ruled Constitutional', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Midwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Indiana: Voucher Program Ruled Constitutional', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indiana', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vouchers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private and Sectarian Schools', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Supreme Courts (State)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-27T02:34:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Motoko Rich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Motoko', 'middlename': None