e70076a', 'word_count': 605, 'uri': 'nyt://article/259c5799-adf2-5d27-a33f-94d99e70076a'}, {'abstract': 'BMW has ambitions for the power plant; plug-in hybrid applications are only one approach.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/27/bmw-thinks-small-with-a-3-cylinder-engine/', 'snippet': 'BMW has ambitions for the power plant; plug-in hybrid applications are only one approach.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The hatchback looked like a production Euro-spec 1 Series BMW. On the roads around company headquarters in Woodcliff Lake, N.J., it drove like one, too. But the car is a work in progress, a prototype powered by BMW’s new 1.5-liter 3-cylinder gasoline engine, which next year will go into the i8 plug-in hybrid.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'BMW Thinks Small With a 3-Cylinder Engine', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Engines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York International Auto Show', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bayerische Motorenwerke AG', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-27T04:01:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Motavalli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Motavalli', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d80ed3d6-dc10-59ae-a822-0eaca7e28cc9', 'word_count': 364, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d80ed3d6-dc10-59ae-a822-0eaca7e28cc9'}, {'abstract': 'This word has appeared in 236 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/27/word-of-the-day-pithy/', 'snippet': 'This word has appeared in 236 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'pithy •\\ˈpi-the\\• adjective', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Word of the Day | pithy', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-27T04:03:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/39d97644-0cc7-52e8-80e3-8889fa4c6457', 'word_count': 198, 'uri': 'nyt://article/39d97644-0cc7-52e8-80e3-8889fa4c6457'}, {'abstract': 'The United States earned a vital, and somewhat surprising, point in World Cup qualifying by playing a scoreless draw with Mexico at the Azteca on Tuesday night.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/27/sports/soccer/for-us-tie-in-mexico-feels-a-lot-like-victory.html', 'snippet': 'The United States earned a vital, and somewhat surprising, point in World Cup qualifying by playing a scoreless draw with Mexico at the Azteca on Tuesday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MEXICO CITY — It is one thing to defeat Mexico at Estadio Azteca in a friendly match, as the United States did last summer. It is something much more vital and rewarding to forge a tie in a World Cup qualifying match, as the Americans did with a 0-0 draw on Tuesday night.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/27/sports/SOCCER/SOCCER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 389, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/27/sports/SOCCER/SOCCER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 389}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/