, 'lastname': 'Longman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2579a5c-3d28-5afe-b61b-45b282ed9360', 'word_count': 1314, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2579a5c-3d28-5afe-b61b-45b282ed9360'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/27/arts/television/whats-on-wednesday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '2:15 P.M. (Comedy Central) POOTIE TANG (2001) Lance Crouther is Pootie Tang, a modern-day renaissance man whose talent, we’re told, in the fields of music, film, martial arts and pottery are exceeded only by his skills in crime fighting, in this comedy written and directed by Louis C. K. Pootie Tang uses these powers for good, battling drug dealers and corporations with the support of his friends, J. B. (Chris Rock), Trucky (J B Smoove) and Biggie Shorty (Wanda Sykes). “\xa0‘Pootie Tang’ may be raw and slovenly — hey, it often is raw and slovenly — but it succeeds as a laugh getter because of the spot on satirical notes,” Elvis Mitchell wrote in The New York Times. “You might say that the movie walks it like it talks it; I’m not sure what Pootie would say.” (Above, from left, Mr. Rock, Mr. Smoove, Mr. Crouther and Mario Joyner.)', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Wednesday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s on Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-27T05:00:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/2696c461-e346-5bd2-abd1-4a159c9fc187', 'word_count': 760, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2696c461-e346-5bd2-abd1-4a159c9fc187'}, {'abstract': 'The collapse of a deal to sell two Taiwan newspapers to pro-Beijing investors sets off speculation about what killed the purchase.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/27/as-media-deal-in-taiwan-collapses-political-fallout-lingers/', 'snippet': 'The collapse of a deal to sell two Taiwan newspapers to pro-Beijing investors sets off speculation about what killed the purchase.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — Today was the deadline for two liberal publications in Taiwan to be sold off to investors who favor stronger ties with mainland China, a deal that alarmed many in Taiwan who are suspicious of the current government’s warming ties with Beijing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/27/global-home/27rdv-nextmedia/27rdv-nextmedia-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 365, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/27/global-home/27rdv-nextmedia/27rdv-nextmedia-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 365}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/27/global-home/27rdv-nextmedia/27rdv-nextmedia-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 624, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/27/global-home/27rdv-nextmedia/27rdv-nextmedia-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1247, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/27/global-home/27rdv-nextmedia/27rdv-nextmedia-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 7