s was experiencing a sales slump. We were about to come out of it, but I didn’t know that at that time. Cash was tight, and the prospect of saving money on my credit card processing was very attractive.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'My Search for a Credit Card Processor, Part 2', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Cards', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Paul Downs Cabinetmakers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-27T11:00:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Downs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Downs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e51e636-1719-529c-904a-a502c9778d92', 'word_count': 1097, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e51e636-1719-529c-904a-a502c9778d92'}, {'abstract': 'The organizational psychologist Adam Grant argues that the key to hyperefficiency is tirelessly helping others.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/31/magazine/is-giving-the-secret-to-getting-ahead.html', 'snippet': 'The organizational psychologist Adam Grant argues that the key to hyperefficiency is tirelessly helping others.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Editor’s note: We’re resurfacing this 2013 magazine article to remind you that\xa0tirelessly helping others could be the key to hyperefficiency.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Is Giving the Secret to Getting Ahead?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Saintly Way To Succeed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grant, Adam M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Altruism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Give and Take: A Revolutionary Approach to Success (Book)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Productivity', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychology and Psychologists', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-27T11:01:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susan Dominus', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dominus', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a019aa59-feb9-5378-8839-2ebd2c1355c4', 'word_count': 6228, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a019aa59-feb9-5378-8839-2ebd2c1355c4'}, {'abstract': 'A squabble between a group fighting spam and a Dutch company that hosts Web sites said to be sending spam has escalated into one of the largest computer attacks on the Internet, causing widespread congestion and jamming crucial infrastructure around the world, John Markoff and Nicole Perlroth write on Wednesday in The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/27/daily-report-dispute-on-spam-stirs-big-assault-on-the-internet/', 'snippet': 'A squabble between a group fighting spam and a Dutch company that hosts Web sites said to be sending spam has escalated into one of the largest computer attacks on the Internet, causing widespread congestion and jamming crucial infrastructure arou...', 'lead_paragraph': 'A squabble between a group fighting spam and a Dutch company that hosts Web sites said to be sending spam has escalated into one of the largest computer attacks on the Internet, causing widespread congestion and jamming crucial infrastructure around the world, John Markoff and Nicole Perlroth write on Wednesday in The New York Times.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-jumbo-v6.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-superJumbo-v3.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbLarge-v5.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Daily Report: Dispute on Spam Stirs Big Assault on the Internet', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Spam (Electronic)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-27T11:07:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cfc0933b-76ec-5a96-b43b-fc324f1f2f0d', 'word_count': 392, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cfc0933b-76ec-5a96-b43b-fc324f1f2f0d'}, {'abstract': 'The Bank of England said the new cash reserves were needed to protect against instability in the world’s financial industry.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/03/27/regulators-find-british-banks-must-raise-38-billion/', 'snippet': 'The Bank of England said the new cash reserves were needed to protect against instability in the world’s financial industry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — British banks must raise a combined £25 billion, or $38 billion, in new capital by the end of the year to protect against future financial shocks, according to a report on Wednesday from the country’s authorities.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'British Banks Told to Raise $38 Billion in Capital', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'British Banks Told to Raise $38 Billion in New Capital', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, Mervyn A', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bank of England', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-27T11:09:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2070de11-5786-5806-9ca1-39074962e57a', 'word_count': 785, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2070de11-5786-5806-9ca1-39074962e57a'}, {'abstract': 'Even in LA.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/27/subways-pay/', 'snippet': 'Even in LA.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here’s an interesting new working paper: Subways, Strikes, and Slowdowns. Unfortunately, there doesn’t seem to be an ungated version. But here’s the summary: the author argues that mass transit has a significant impact in reducing traffic congestion, even when it carries only a small fraction of commuters. Why? Because commuters who take mass transit are, very disproportionately, people who would otherwise be driving on the most congested routes. So even the small number of people taken off the roads has a surprisingly large effect in reducing travel delays.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Subways Pay', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-27T11:10:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': '