ead_paragraph': 'PORTLAND, Me. — Most Americans have never heard of Mary Bonauto. But inside the tightknit world of gay legal advocacy, Ms. Bonauto is a quiet celebrity — a lawyer and mother of twins who some say is almost single-handedly responsible for the same-sex marriage cases now pending before the Supreme Court.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/28/us/28bonauto-cnd/28bonauto-cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/28/us/28bonauto-cnd/28bonauto-cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/28/us/28bonauto-cnd/28bonauto-cnd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/28/us/28bonauto-cnd/28bonauto-cnd-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/28/us/28bonauto-cnd/28bonauto-cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/28/us/28bonauto-cnd/28bonauto-cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/28/us/28bonauto-cnd/28bonauto-cnd-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Fight for Marriage Rights, ‘She’s Our Thurgood Marshall’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Fight for Marriage Rights, ‘She’s Our Thurgood Marshall’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bonauto, Mary', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense of Marriage Act (1996)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gay and Lesbian Advocates and Defenders (GLAD)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wolfson, Evan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-27T12:56:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sheryl Gay Stolberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sheryl', 'middlename': 'Gay', 'lastname': 'Stolberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/80be98e5-3df1-52c8-ae74-6f8838d2561a', 'word_count': 1253, 'uri': 'nyt://article/80be98e5-3df1-52c8-ae74-6f8838d2561a'}, {'abstract': 'How conveying that good behavior is the social norm can change how people drink, recycle and even pay their taxes.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/27/the-destructive-influence-of-imaginary-peers/', 'snippet': 'How conveying that good behavior is the social norm can change how people drink, recycle and even pay their taxes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We humans irrationally think we’re rational.\xa0We think that we decide how to behave by weighing the pros and cons. In reality, the strongest influence on our decisions is the example of the people around us — even, oddly enough, when they are imaginary.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Destructive Influence of Imaginary Peers', 'kicker': 'Fixes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alcohol Abuse', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Northern Illinois University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Opower', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-27T13:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tina Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b87f5c8-5575-5aa8-833b-86b759ba3ae2', 'word_count': 1864, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b87f5c8-5575-5aa8-833b-86b759ba3ae2'}, {'abstract': 'Cloud computing and mobility have brought to the fore an unexpected strategic asset from the humanities: design. A start-up called Tidemark, which sells cloud-based business analytics software, has introduced a series of planning features designed to speed forecasting and decision making.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/27/designing-big-data-that-works/', 'snippet': 'Cloud computing and mobility have brought to the fore an unexpected strategic asset from the humanities: design. A start-up called Tidemark, which sells cloud-based business analytics software, has introduced a series of planning features designed...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Whether the move is from mainframes to minicomputers, or from there to personal computers and servers, and now to mobile devices and cloud computing, we are witnessing one grand process of moving machine intelligence closer to the people on the front lines, even as the computing at the center gets more powerful.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarg