ominance and protectionism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In his book “No Ancient Wisdom, No Followers,” the author James McGregor delivers a sharp critique of China’s recent development path, and what he calls “authoritarian capitalism.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Limits of China’s Market Model', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Protectionism (Trade)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Trade Organization', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-27T14:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Barboza', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barboza', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0de3b540-d4a9-5af3-b5c9-2c78b312788e', 'word_count': 1068, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0de3b540-d4a9-5af3-b5c9-2c78b312788e'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/27/what-were-reading-658/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Saveur: A look at the history of Easter candy, from chocolate bunnies to marshmallow peeps. — Melissa Clark', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-27T14:18:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c90f958b-1dd7-58a3-a131-43c1f18ccf60', 'word_count': 460, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c90f958b-1dd7-58a3-a131-43c1f18ccf60'}, {'abstract': 'Wanelo, a social shopping site that has a strong appeal among the youngs, reveals some new data and information about its service, which is steadily gaining traction online.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/27/wanelo-social-commerce-site-picks-up-speed/', 'snippet': 'Wanelo, a social shopping site that has a strong appeal among the youngs, reveals some new data and information about its service, which is steadily gaining traction online.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wanelo, the social shopping site that resembles a well-designed window display, is quickly gaining fans online, \xa0despite being largely under the mainstream radar.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/27/technology/27bits-wanelo/27bits-wanelo-articleLarge.png', 'height': 277, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/27/technology/27bits-wanelo/27bits-wanelo-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 277}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/27/technology/27bits-wanelo/27bits-wanelo-jumbo.png', 'height': 472, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/27/technology/27bits-wanelo/27