and even small business start-ups. But gun research?\xa0Given the lack of federal funds available for such research, why not?\xa0(A quick reminder: In 1996, the National Rifle Association lobbied Congress to cut all funding to the Center for Disease Control for gun-related research.)\xa0That hasn’t stopped researchers at the University of Alabama at Birmingham, however.\xa0Last year, a U.A.B. study found that increased gun background checks correlate with fewer homicides and suicides. The study concluded that more comprehensive background checks at the state level may reduce firearm deaths, but “more research is needed.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Gun Report: March 27, 2013', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beaumont (Tex)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Idaho', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Maine', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mississippi', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Carolina', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oakland (Calif)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philadelphia (Pa)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tulsa (Okla)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-27T14:27:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Mascia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mascia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2cd07943-2808-5d4e-b2bd-5dc1b2d5b47b', 'word_count': 964, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2cd07943-2808-5d4e-b2bd-5dc1b2d5b47b'}, {'abstract': 'In interfaith marriages, children are more likely to adopt the religion of their mother.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/27/easter-vs-passover-in-interfaith-marriages-moms-faith-wins-out/', 'snippet': 'In interfaith marriages, children are more likely to adopt the religion of their mother.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I never thought of myself as part of an interfaith marriage — more of a faith/no-faith marriage. I am a Conservative Jew and my husband is a former Jehovah’s Witness, now an “aspiring atheist.” I told him on our first date that our children would be raised Jewish — indeed that they would go to Jewish day school. A little forward, perhaps, but I had friends who spent years arguing over faith until they finally decided their relationship just wasn’t going anywhere. And I had friends who wanted to expose kids to “a little bit of both” and then let them decide. Bringing up children as Unitarians or Jews for Jesus wasn’t in the cards for me.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Easter vs. Passover: In Interfaith Marriages, Mom’s Faith Wins Out', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Passover', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-27T14:38:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Naomi Schaefer Riley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Naomi', 'middlename': 'Schaefer', 'lastname': 'Riley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f3b43bf-5939-5932-b172-75b820c34e3a', 'word_count': 905, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f3b43bf-5939-5932-b172-75b820c34e3a'}, {'abstract': 'Two people were arrested in East Harlem this month and accused of running numbers. But what exactly do the numbers mean?', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/27/on-illegal-betting-slips-a-three-digit-mystery/', 'snippet': 'Two people were arrested in East Harlem this month and accused of running numbers. But what exactly do the numbers mean?', 'lead_paragraph': 'So what do all those numbers in a so-called numbers-running racket mean, anyway? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/28/nyregion/27cityroom-crimescene/27cityroom-crimescene-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 661, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/28/nyregion/27cityroom-crimescene/27cityroom-crimescene-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 661}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/28/nyregion/27cityroom-crimescene/27cityroom-crimescene-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 930, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/28/nyregion/27cityroom-crimescene/27cityroom-crimescene-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1880, 'width': 1706, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/28/nyregion/27cityroom-crimescene/27cityroom-crimescene-