ne}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/77a2488c-2dff-5f9d-903a-0a3f349e04df', 'word_count': 315, 'uri': 'nyt://article/77a2488c-2dff-5f9d-903a-0a3f349e04df'}, {'abstract': 'More than $200 million will be wagered in Nevada sports books on the N.C.A.A. men’s college basketball tournament, a sum double that bet on the Super Bowl.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/28/sports/more-states-look-to-get-in-the-sports-betting-game.html', 'snippet': 'More than $200 million will be wagered in Nevada sports books on the N.C.A.A. men’s college basketball tournament, a sum double that bet on the Super Bowl.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAS VEGAS — It is a lucrative time of year for Nevada, where more than $200 million will be wagered in sports books on the N.C.A.A. men’s basketball tournament, a pot of money that has budget-crunched states across the country pushing for a piece of the action despite strong opposition from the N.C.A.A. and professional sports leagues. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cash-Hungry States Eye Sports Betting, to Leagues’ Dismay', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Needy States Weigh Sport Betting As Leagues Line Up Against It', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gambling', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'NCAA Basketball Championships (Men)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball (College)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Athletics and Sports', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nevada', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-27T15:26:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Drape', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Drape', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/63254b3c-a605-5c7f-9827-626a47df1c7d', 'word_count': 1056, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63254b3c-a605-5c7f-9827-626a47df1c7d'}, {'abstract': 'A release of records shed light on the behavior of Jared L. Loughner, who killed 6 people and wounded 13 in Tucson, including former Representative Gabrielle Giffords.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/28/us/documents-2011-tucson-shooting-case-gabrielle-giffords.html', 'snippet': 'A release of records shed light on the behavior of Jared L. Loughner, who killed 6 people and wounded 13 in Tucson, including former Representative Gabrielle Giffords.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TUCSON — The parents of Jared L. Loughner, the man who killed six people and wounded 13 others during a meet-and-greet event hosted by former Representative Gabrielle Giffords in 2011, told the authorities after the mass shooting that they had become so concerned about their son’s strange behavior in the previous months that they had taken away his shotgun, insisted he get psychological counseling and had even begun to disable his car so that he could not go out at night, according to thousands of pages of documents related to the case released Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/28/us/28giffords-web/28giffords-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/28/us/28giffords-web/28giffords-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 750}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'i