on': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/66399bb4-a760-5d74-af11-2da0cbd18ac4', 'word_count': 717, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66399bb4-a760-5d74-af11-2da0cbd18ac4'}, {'abstract': 'The president designated five new national monuments, but overall he’s been more than generous to oil interests.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/27/obamas-public-lands-record/', 'snippet': 'The president designated five new national monuments, but overall he’s been more than generous to oil interests.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama’s decision to designate five new national monuments is a warm farewell present to the outgoing Interior secretary, Ken Salazar, who has been trying without great success to get Mr. Obama to protect more public lands from development. It also makes a nice welcoming gift for Sally Jewell, the presumed incoming secretary, whose life will be much happier if the President continues along this path. But environmentalists are not dancing in the streets, at least not yet. Conservation issues still do not loom large in this White House, and the lands Mr. Obama has protected over the course of his administration are small change compared to the efforts of his recent predecessors.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama’s Public Lands Record', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Land Use Policies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Parks, Monuments and Seashores', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wilderness Areas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Bill', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-27T15:38:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 