20d470-329e-564d-bece-681581801e8c'}, {'abstract': 'Sustainable doesn’t need to be boring. Popupshop has created swimsuits with tropical themes for children aged 2 to 10.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/27/sweet-suits/', 'snippet': 'Sustainable doesn’t need to be boring. Popupshop has created swimsuits with tropical themes for children aged 2 to 10.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The motivation behind the sustainable clothing line Popupshop is clear: create simple, chic, wearable and environmentally defensible garments for women and children. The usual pieces are mostly neutral and work well as basics for everyday mixing and matching. It may be easy to outfit children aged 2 to 10 in a uniform of mostly beige and navy blue, but Popupshop is changing things this season with little swimsuits covered in colorful, tropical birds, nuzzling zebras and dancing flamingos (in the same organic and sustainably sourced cotton it has used in the past). Cotton tees, leggings, jumpers and rompers are also available in bright animal prints, and range from $38 to $78 at Sweet William LTD, the children’s clothing store in downtown Manhattan and Williamsburg, Brooklyn. Popupshop fits right in with the store’s stock of other ethically responsible, and mostly independent, brands.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sweet Suits', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Williamsburg (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-27T19:00:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erika Allen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erika', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Allen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organ