}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c32ba9e1-f189-560c-abc1-eb4a84e9e8e7', 'word_count': 647, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c32ba9e1-f189-560c-abc1-eb4a84e9e8e7'}, {'abstract': 'Opening a 30th-anniversary program at the Joyce Theater, the Bill T. Jones/Arnie Zane Dance Company invoked the deaths of two dancers in a signature watery work.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/28/arts/dance/bill-t-jones-arnie-zane-at-the-joyce-theater.html', 'snippet': 'Opening a 30th-anniversary program at the Joyce Theater, the Bill T. Jones/Arnie Zane Dance Company invoked the deaths of two dancers in a signature watery work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Tuesday the Bill T. Jones/Arnie Zane Dance Company began a two-week 30th-anniversary season at the Joyce Theater. After the performance the audience members applauded enthusiastically, but Mr. Jones quieted them with the pall of death. He spoke of Mr. Zane, his former partner, who died of AIDS in 1988, and of Demian Acquavella, a company member who died of AIDS in 1990. “There are ghosts in this piece,” he said, twice. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/28/arts/BILLTJONES/BILLTJONES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 394, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/28/arts/BILLTJONES/BILLTJONES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 394}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/28/arts/BILLTJONES/BILLTJONES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 673, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/28/arts/BILLTJONES/BILLTJONES-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1345, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'sup