, 'snippet': 'In conjunction with the New York auto show, Porsche celebrated half a century of its 911 sports car at a beer garden in the meatpacking district of Manhattan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Not many car companies are associated with a single automobile. Fewer still continue to produce the very car that made the marque. So the 50th birthday of the Porsche 911 is definitely noteworthy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/27/automobiles/wheels-porsche911/wheels-porsche911-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/27/automobiles/wheels-porsche911/wheels-porsche911-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/27/automobiles/wheels-porsche911/wheels-porsche911-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/27/automobiles/wheels-porsche911/wheels-porsche911-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/27/automobiles/wheels-porsche911/wheels-porsche911-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/27/automobiles/wheels-porsche911/wheels-porsche911-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/27/automobiles/wheels-porsche911/wheels-porsche911-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Nifty 50th for the Porsche 911', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-27T21:21:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By John R. Quain', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Quain', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/377ceb7c-1362-541e-a3d5-285bc44e643f', 'word_count': 783, 'uri': 'nyt://article/377ceb7c-1362-541e-a3d5-285bc44e643f'}, {'abstract': 'A scene from "Evil Dead," directed by Fede Alvarez.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/movies/100000002141575/clip-evil-dead.html', 'snippet': 'A scene from "Evil Dead," directed by Fede Alvarez.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A scene from "Evil Dead," directed by Fede Alvarez.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/27/arts/video-evil-dead-clip/video-evil-dead-clip-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/27/arts/video-evil-dead-clip/video-evil-dead-clip-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/27/arts/video-evil-dead-clip/video-evil-dead-clip-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/27/arts/video-evil-dead-clip/video-evil-dead-clip-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/27/arts/video-evil-dead-clip/video-evil-dead-clip-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': "Clip: 'Evil Dead'", 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-27T21:25:41+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'TriStar Pictures', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tristar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pictures', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/625498e4-6d28-512e-9a94-1e01d3a7ab4b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/625498e4-6d28-512e-9a94-1e01d3a7ab4b'}, {'abstract': 'Got that covered.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/27/on-mundell-fleming-very-wonkish/', 'snippet': 'Got that covered.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Aha. I see that Simon Wren-Lewis is on a campaign against the use of the Mundell-Fleming model, a simple international macroeconomic extension of IS-LM analysis, because of the way it handles the relationship between interest rates and exchange rates. And it’s true that the simplest version of Mundell-Fleming assumes that interest rates are equalized by capital flows, taking no account of expectations of future exchange rate changes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Mundell-Fleming (Very Wonkish)', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-27T21:27:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'rol