 York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/28/garden/28CURR3/28CURR3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/28/garden/28CURR3/28CURR3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/28/garden/28CURR3/28CURR3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/28/garden/28CURR3/28CURR3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/28/garden/28CURR3/28CURR3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/28/garden/28CURR3/28CURR3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/28/garden/28CURR3/28CURR3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Within a Sconce, Reflections of Infinity', 'kicker': 'Currents | Lighting', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Within a Sconce, Reflections of Infinity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lighting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McKeough, Tim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-27T22:19:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim McKeough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McKeough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aac8c812-2fb3-543d-962b-2173b252de57', 'word_count': 116, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aac8c812-2fb3-543d-962b-2173b252de57'}, {'abstract': 'A D.I.Y. kit for carving your own rubber stamps.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/28/garden/a-diy-kit-for-carving-your-own-rubber-stamps.html', 'snippet': 'A D.I.Y. kit for carving your own rubber stamps.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You have to root a little for Yellow Owl Workshop, a San Francisco company that makes beautiful paper products in this paperless age. Their newest offering is the Carve-A-Stamp-Kit, a D.I.Y. set for creating ink stamps to adorn thank-you cards or envelopes. The $28 kit includes a rubber stamp block, a carving tool, an ink pad, tracing paper and 25 designs (or create your own).', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/28/garden/28CURR1/28CURR1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 610, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/28/garden/28CURR1/28CURR1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 610}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/28/garden/28CURR1/28CURR1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1008, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/28/garden/28CURR1/28CURR1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1276, 'width': 1256, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'cred