 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-27T23:25:30+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Fashion & Style', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/eae05e07-2c28-5313-bcfa-2f87c878ff34', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/eae05e07-2c28-5313-bcfa-2f87c878ff34'}, {'abstract': 'Yankees pitcher Phil Hughes will begin the season on the 15-day disabled list, Manager Joe Girardi said, and may not start until April 11, or even later.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/28/sports/baseball/phil-hughes-is-set-for-dl.html', 'snippet': 'Yankees pitcher Phil Hughes will begin the season on the 15-day disabled list, Manager Joe Girardi said, and may not start until April 11, or even later.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Yankees pitcher Phil Hughes will begin the season on the 15-day disabled list, Manager Joe Girardi said, and may not start until April 11, or even later. Hughes pitched in a minor league game Wednesday and threw 81 pitches, but it was only his second spring game. He had to take two weeks off earlier in spring training because of a back problem that slowed his progress and arm conditioning. Until Hughes comes back, the Yankee rotation will consist of C. C. Sabathia, Andy Pettitte, Hiroki Kuroda, Ivan Nova and David Phelps. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hughes Is Set for D.L.', 'kicker': 'Sports Briefing | Baseball', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hughes Is Set for D.L.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-27T23:25:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/e581856e-8dc0-52d5-8d83-c6983ab2ff9e', 'word_count': 92, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e581856e-8dc0-52d5-8d83-c6983ab2ff9e'}, {'abstract': 'Just as the Whole Foods Markets have helped make over Americans’ diets, the chain’s Whole Body shops are laying claim to their complexions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/28/fashion/at-whole-body-shops-natural-beauty-products.html', 'snippet': 'Just as the Whole Foods Markets have helped make over Americans’ diets, the chain’s Whole Body shops are laying claim to their complexions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Shortly after New York Fashion Week, I stood with my umbrella dripping on the concrete floor of Whole Body, the health and beauty department of the Whole Foods Market in Chelsea. After days of Champagne and late nights, the thought of rejuvenating with natural beauty products had conjured visions of “Sound of Music” bliss, but the aisles were jammed with more labels and products than I could easily navigate. ', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/28/fashion/28SKIN_SPAN/28SKIN_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/28/fashion/28SKIN_SPAN/28SKIN_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/28/fashion/28SKIN_SPAN/28SKIN_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/28/fashion/28SKIN_SPAN/28SKIN_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'w