 three centuries, breaking up with the United Kingdom will be complicated.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Scottish voters will decide on Sept. 18, 2014, whether Scotland should remain part of the United Kingdom or become an independent nation. After more than three centuries of political union, breaking up would be complicated. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Vote on Scottish Independence', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Vote on Scottish Independence', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Scotland', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Referendums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Salmond, Alex', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cameron, David', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-28T01:15:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d41fa3c-52e1-55ac-a194-86f03c0de14e', 'word_count': 346, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d41fa3c-52e1-55ac-a194-86f03c0de14e'}, {'abstract': 'New York City should create the position of inspector general to strengthen supervision and accountability of its police department.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/28/opinion/the-new-york-city-police-need-a-monitor.html', 'snippet': 'New York City should create the position of inspector general to strengthen supervision and accountability of its police department.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mayor Michael Bloomberg of New York and Commissioner Raymond Kelly are apoplectic about a bill pending in the City Council that would create the position of inspector general, an official with broad powers to review the policies of the nation’s largest police department. Given the department’s long history of episodic misconduct, the idea is one whose time has clearly come. The City Council should press ahead with the bill and be prepared to override a veto by the mayor. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Monitoring New York City’s Police', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Monitoring New York City’s Police', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inspectors General', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kelly, Raymond W', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-28T01:19:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/0921c63f-071a-509b-855e-49b7901a93d7', 'word_count': 385, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0921c63f-071a-509b-855e-49b7901a93d7'}, {'abstract': 'Why did an encounter between a man with Down syndrome and three off-duty county sheriff’s deputies at a movie theater have to turn deadly?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/28/opinion/down-syndrome-and-a-death.html', 'snippet': 'Why did an encounter between a man with Down syndrome and three off-duty county sheriff’s deputies at a movie theater have to turn deadly?', 'lead_paragraph': 'A grand jury in Frederick County, Md., decided last week not to bring criminal charges in the death of Robert Ethan Saylor, a 26-year-old man with Down syndrome who was killed in a struggle with three off-duty county sheriff’s deputies at a movie theater in January. Advocates for people with intellectual disabilities are bewildered and furious, and it is easy to see why. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Down Syndrome and a Death', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Down Syndrome and a Death', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Down Syndrome', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saylor, Robert Ethan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality and Misconduct', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-28T01:22:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/88b4ba61-7084-54a2-9bd3-bc0376182a56', 'word_count': 338, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88b4ba61-7084-54a2-9bd3-bc0376182a56'}, {'abstract': 'A majority of justices seem doubtful that this antigay law has any legitimate purpose.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/28/opinion/the-indefensible-marriage-act.html', 'snippet': 'A majority of justices seem doubtful that this antigay law has any legitimate purpose.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The discrimination embedded in the Defense of Marriage Act is precise yet sweeping. The 1996 statute defines marriage as the union of a man and a woman, and applies that definition to about 1,100 federal laws and programs. One of its many discriminatory results is that same-sex couples are prohibited from collecting many federal benefits available to other couples. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Indefensible Marriage Act', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Indefensible Marriage Act', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense of Marriage Act (1996)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-28T01:22:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc5bd89f-f52b-5dd6-adf5-14fbda911f72', 'word_count': 531, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc5bd89f-f52b-5dd6-adf5-14fbda911f72'}, {'abstract': 'Lawyers for James E. Holmes, charged in the Aurora theater massacre, signaled in court filings Wednesday they would let their client plead guilty if he was spared the death penalty.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/28/us/defense-in-aurora-massacre-seeks-plea-deal.html', 'snippet': 'Lawyers for James E. Holmes, charged in the Aurora theater massacre, signaled in court filings Wednesday they would let their client plead guilty if he was spared the death penalty.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CENTENNIAL, Colo. — Defense lawyers for James E. Holmes, who is charged with killing 12 people and wounding dozens more at an Aurora, Colo., movie theater last summer, signaled in court filings on Wednesday that they were willing to have Mr. Holmes plead guilty if he was spared the death penalty. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 