n of Croats and Muslims, many of whom were beaten, tortured, raped or otherwise abused in as many as 50 wartime detention centers run by Bosnian Serbs. The judges said that many civilians were killed or died from hunger, illness and mistreatment during the campaign to create zones for Serbs only in Bosnia. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hague: 2 Serb Police Chiefs Convicted', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hague: 2 Serb Police Chiefs Convicted', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Simons, Marlise', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bosnia and Herzegovina', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zupljanin, Stojan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stanisic, Mico', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-28T01:33:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marlise Simons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marlise', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Simons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/01b6e005-876f-5dbc-a55d-9fadfc6fcfef', 'word_count': 123, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01b6e005-876f-5dbc-a55d-9fadfc6fcfef'}, {'abstract': 'Buckingham Palace has released details of a mid-May trip by Prince Harry, which will include a visit to storm-damaged parts of the New Jersey coast and to a polo match in Greenwich.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/28/nyregion/prince-harry-to-visit-connecticut-and-new-jersey.html', 'snippet'