ch.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TAMPA, Fla. — Derek Jeter is eligible to come off the 15-day disabled list April 6, but at the rate he is going, that date would be a very difficult target to reach.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Resting Ankle, Jeter Faces Long Road Back', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jeter, Derek', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-28T03:10:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d33d78cb-4622-5dc9-ba19-0916873e4aa8', 'word_count': 186, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d33d78cb-4622-5dc9-ba19-0916873e4aa8'}, {'abstract': 'The perfect boomer’s Camaro, summoning the spirit of the first-generation model, right down to its Z-slash-28 logo.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/27/distant-replay-chevy-revives-the-z28-camaro/', 'snippet': 'The perfect boomer’s Camaro, summoning the spirit of the first-generation model, right down to its Z-slash-28 logo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Introduced on Wednesday, March 27: 2014 Chevrolet Camaro Z/28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Distant Replay: Chevy Revives the Z/28 Camaro', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chevrolet Division of General Motors Corp', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-28T03:12:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jerry Garrett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jerry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garrett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/38093f1d-c8ac-59e3-a643-a0b7b5a18abe', 'word_count': 329, 'uri': 'nyt://article/38093f1d-c8ac-59e3-a643-a0b7b5a18abe'}, {'abstract': 'The Pittsburgh Penguins go into Thursday’s game against the Winnipeg Jets with 13 straight victories, tied for the fifth-longest winning streak in N.H.L. history.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/27/close-wins-set-penguins-apart/', 'snippet': 'The Pittsburgh Penguins go into Thursday’s game against the Winnipeg Jets with 13 straight victories, tied for the fifth-longest winning streak in N.H.L. history.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Pittsburgh Penguins go into Thursday’s game against the Winnipeg Jets with 13 straight victories, tied for the fifth-longest winning streak in N.H.L. history. The Penguins, who lead the Eastern Conference with 52 points, have not lost in March, their last defeat coming Feb. 28 at Carolina. Pittsburgh has outscored opponents by 47-26 during the streak, but nine of the victories have been by a single goal, including two wins in overtime and one in a shootout. Below, a look at the longest N.H.L. winning streaks, including one-goal games. (The N.H.L. introduced an overtime period for regular-season games in the 1983-84 season and started the shootout in the 2005-6 season.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Close Wins Set Penguins Apart', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'HOCKEY, ICE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pittsburgh Penguins', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-28T0