: 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/27/27-game-streak-for-heat-50-1-shot/', 'snippet': 'The math shows that the chance of such a streak by a team with the winning percentage of the Heat is only 2 percent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'They lost Wednesday night to the Chicago Bulls, but the Miami Heat still put an impressive 27-game winning streak in the books, the second longest in N.B.A. history. Just how unlikely is such a streak?', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '27-Game Streak? For Heat, 50-1 Shot', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Heat, 27-Gamer A 50-1 Shot', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mathematics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-28T03:54:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Victor Mather', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Victor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mather', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0e4af4e-7f43-56b2-9724-5d3825e90ad8', 'word_count': 476, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0e4af4e-7f43-56b2-9724-5d3825e90ad8'}, {'abstract': 'The aftereffects of cancer and its treatments challenge our perceptions of beauty, as captured in the photos and documentary of “The Scar Project.”', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/28/living-with-cancer-the-scar-project/', 'snippet': 'The aftereffects of cancer and its treatments challenge our perceptions of beauty, as captured in the photos and documentary of “The Scar Project.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the documentary “Baring it All,” a young woman declares, “The scar represents everything I’ve been through. I’m proud of what I’ve been through.” The film focuses on the fashion photographer David Jay, who created a pictorial series about breast cancer called “The Scar Project.”', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Living With Cancer: The Scar Project', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Facing Their Scars, Head-On', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-28T04:01:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susan Gubar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gubar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba8aa765-88f1-57c6-b128-8732efed186f', 'word_count': 732, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba8aa765-88f1-57c6-b128-8732efed186f'}, {'abstract': 'This word has appeared in 29 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/28/word-of-the-day-mimicry/', 'snippet': 'This word has appeared in 29 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'mimicry •\\ˈmi-mi-kre\\• noun', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Word of the Day | mimicry', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-28T04:05:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c300db38-f974-5288-bbe6-f4520ee75bc9', 'word_count': 155, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c300db38-f974-5288-bbe6-f4520ee75bc9'}, {'abstract': 'After years of contentious contract negotiations and holdouts, Osi Umenyiora, 