ount': 120, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89ebb576-1bd1-5b34-bde7-5fe9c31f37be'}, {'abstract': 'Does BRICS increasingly challenge the world financial order as it forges more definite goals and measures, and is it a place to be for a strong Asian economy like Indonesia?', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/28/first-bric-then-brics-now-bricsi-the-world-financial-orders-challenge/', 'snippet': 'Does BRICS increasingly challenge the world financial order as it forges more definite goals and measures, and is it a place to be for a strong Asian economy like Indonesia?', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — First it was called BRIC, a group of emerging economies thought up in 2001 by a Goldman Sachs economist, Jim O’Neill, made up of Brazil, Russia, India and China. Then it acquired an “s” for South Africa and become BRICS. Now there’s talk of Indonesia, which has a strongly growing economy, maybe wanting in: BRICSI, anyone?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/28/world/asia/28BRICSrdv/28BRICSrdv-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 385, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/28/world/asia/28BRICSrdv/28BRICSrdv-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 385}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/28/world/asia/28BRICSrdv/28BRICSrdv-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 657, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/28/world/asia/28BRICSrdv/28BRICSrdv-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1314, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/28/world/asia/28