-a-movement-its-the-muslim-brotherhood/', 'snippet': 'A legal battle over the official status of Egypt’s main political group brings out the worst of all sides.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — The feints and pretenses of Egypt’s post-revolutionary politics have been dizzying, but the situation in which the Muslim Brotherhood finds itself these days may be the most puzzling yet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'It’s a Charity! It’s a Movement! It’s the Muslim Brotherhood!', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morsi, Mohamed', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muslim Brotherhood (Egypt)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-28T10:53:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Issandr El Amrani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Issandr', 'middlename': 'El', 'lastname': 'Amrani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/60a34e57-3397-5448-805e-020329a1645f', 'word_count': 596, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60a34e57-3397-5448-805e-020329a1645f'}, {'abstract': 'When I reviewed the WorldPay agreement, I was most interested in seeing what it said about reserve accounts, and I found the relevant language easily. It was quite unsettling. WorldPay could take money straight out of my bank accounts any time it wanted without notice.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/28/my-search-for-a-credit-card-processor-part-3/', 'snippet': 'When I reviewed the WorldPay agreement, I was most interested in seeing what it said about reserve accounts, and I found the relevant language easily. It was quite unsettling. WorldPay could take money straight out of my bank accounts any time it ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Wednesday’s post, I wrote about my decision not to accept the credit card processing offer I had received from Emerald World. That left me at PNC, where I had my business accounts and where I now understood that I was probably paying more than necessary for card processing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'My Search for a Credit Card Processor, Part 3', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Cards', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Paul Downs Cabinetmakers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wells Fargo & Company', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-28T11:00:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Downs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Downs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/93e1eb90-80db-5bfb-b7b4-6654b854c9d6', 'word_count': 1682, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93e1eb90-80db-5bfb-b7b4-6654b854c9d6'}, {'abstract': 'Seven people were killed at a nondescript nursing school in Oakland one year ago. Should it matter that the shooter was a Korean immigrant? It does to Koreans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/31/magazine/should-it-matter-that-the-shooter-at-oikos-university-was-korean.html', 'snippet': 'Seven people were killed at a nondescript nursing school in Oakland one year ago. Should it matter that the shooter was a Korean immigrant? It does to Koreans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On April 2 last year, a 43-year-old former nursing student named One L. Goh walked into Oikos University in Oakland, Calif., with a .45-caliber handgun. He killed six people and wounded three others, then exited the building and shot and killed Tshering Bhutia, a former classmate, in the school’s parking lot. Goh then climbed into Bhutia’s car and drove to a Safeway in the nearby city of Alameda, where he ultimately surrendered to police.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '32', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/31/magazine/31oikos1/mag-31Oikos-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 445, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/31/magazine/31oikos1/mag-31Oikos-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 445}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/31/magazine/31oikos1/mag-31Oikos-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 759, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/31/magazine/31oikos1/mag-31Oikos-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1112, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/31/magazine/31oikos1/mag-31Oikos-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/31/magazine/31oikos1/mag-31Oikos-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jp