ntial Center in Newark, Taylor Swift was unflappable, even in the midst of a mishap, with a voice stronger and sturdier than it’s ever been.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/29/arts/music/in-an-arena-performance-taylor-swifts-nerves-of-steel.html', 'snippet': 'At a king-size spectacle at the Prudential Center in Newark, Taylor Swift was unflappable, even in the midst of a mishap, with a voice stronger and sturdier than it’s ever been.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEWARK — An arena show, for all the planning that goes into it, is still a tightrope walk — there is nowhere to hide once the lights go up. So when things began to go wrong for Taylor Swift about midway through her Wednesday night concert at the Prudential Center here, the question wasn’t whether she’d sweat, but if it would show.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/28/arts/28swift-1/28swift-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 421, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/28/arts/28swift-1/28swift-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 421}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/28/arts/28swift-1/28swift-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 718, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/28/arts/28swift-1/28swift-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1436, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/28/arts/28swift-1/28swift-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/28/arts/28swift-1/28swift-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/28/arts/28swift-1/28swift-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Losing Her Audio, but Never Her Nerve', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Losing Her Audio, But Never Her Nerve', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Swift, Taylor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-28T13:34:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/83386fea-b4e2-5bf8-9ce5-0c5b1e73e592', 'word_count': 939, 'uri': 'nyt://article/83386fea-b4e2-5bf8-9ce5-0c5b1e73e592'}, {'abstract': 'NBC reportedly called Anderson Cooper about hosting “Today,” the head of Hearst Corporation will step down and Weight Watchers found spokeswoman Ana Gasteyer on Twitter.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/28/the-breakfast-meeting-nbc-calls-cooper-about-today-and-hearst-chief-to-step-down/', 'snippet': 'NBC reportedly called Anderson Cooper about hosting “Today,” the head of Hearst Corporation will step down and Weight Watchers found spokeswoman Ana Gasteyer on Twitter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Reports of a surprising phone call from an NBC executive to CNN’s Anderson Cooper have fueled speculation about possible succession plans for Matt Lauer, the co-host of the “Today” show, which has had slumping ratings, Brian Stelter writes. NBC tried to quell the rumors, but three television industry insiders confirmed that Mr. Cooper was asked this month whether he would consider hosting “Today.” It is unclear whether Mr. Cooper might be interested in moving from “Anderson Cooper 360,” his nightly program on CNN, to a morning show on NBC, but rumors of the call come as NBC is finalizing plans to have Jimmy Fallon replace Jay Leno on “The Tonight Show.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting: NBC Calls Cooper About ‘Today’ and Hearst Chief to Step Down', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-28T13:41:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel E. Slotnik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Slotnik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e6cdf4ec-21f2-55b7-836a-e3968686e93a', 'word_count': 556, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e6cdf4ec-21f2-55b7-836a-e3968686e93a'}, {'abstract': 'How to buy and install an electric generator, living the bed-and-breakfast dream, a slimmer keyboard for the iPad and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/28/thursday-reading-how-to-buy-and-install-a-generator/', 'snippet': 'How to buy and install an electric generator, living the bed-and-breakfast dream, a slimmer keyboard for the iPad and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Thursday Reading: How to Buy and Install a Generator', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-28T13:48:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/10f5fb58-9b28-5320-a530-0b008c8c3597', 'word_count': 87, 'uri': 'nyt://article/10f5fb58-9b28-5320-a530-0b008c8c3597'}, {'abstract': 'E-mail messages that claim to be from the Internal Revenue Service asking for personal information are probably phishing scams.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/28/tip-of-the-week-beware-of-tax-season-scams/', 'snippet': 'E-mail messages that claim to be from the Internal Revenue Service asking for personal information are probably phishing scams.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The deadline for filing federal (and many state) tax returns is just a few weeks away, so the level of scam e-mail messages claiming to be from the Internal Revenue Service are likely to increase in the coming days. Remember, the I.R.S. does not initially contact taxpayers by e-mail or text message to request PIN codes, Social Security numbers or other financial data. Do not click on any Web links or open attachments included with these types of messages because you could inadvertently install malicious software on the computer. You can report suspicious mail by forwarding the messages to phishing@irs.gov and the agency’s site has a page with additional safety information. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tip of the Week: Beware of Tax Season Scams', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'na