+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/f4aba53d-3c86-5801-9304-181a213fa0c1', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/f4aba53d-3c86-5801-9304-181a213fa0c1'}, {'abstract': 'The Heat’s run is over, but the N.C.A.A. tournament offers plenty of colorful characters and storylines of its own.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/29/sports/one-streak-ends-16-are-on-the-line.html', 'snippet': 'The Heat’s run is over, but the N.C.A.A. tournament offers plenty of colorful characters and storylines of its own.', 'lead_paragraph': "Now that the Miami Heat’s winning streak has fizzled to an unsatisfying end, we can all go back to contemplating the N.C.A.A. tournaments’ rounds of 16 or contemplating an imminent baseball season or watching “Iron Chef” reruns or whatever else usually fills the time between spring supposedly starting and when it really starts. It was nice that the N.B.A.'s ludicrously long regular season threw in a reason to watch its most tortured portion for awhile — it was no Linsanity, but still — and now it has passed into instant history. Now the Heat can claim the streak was never really important and you can all push the pause button on your attention spans until the playoffs.", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/29/sports/basketball/29leadingpic/29leadingpic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/29/sports/basketball/29leadingpic/29leadingpic-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/29/sports/basketball/29leadingpic/29leadingpic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'w