'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c952cbb8-949b-5e57-91e9-8df17d82329e', 'word_count': 572, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c952cbb8-949b-5e57-91e9-8df17d82329e'}, {'abstract': 'By 1863, antislavery had become the driving spirit for many soldiers from the northern Midwest.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/28/mitchel-thompsons-war/', 'snippet': 'By 1863, antislavery had become the driving spirit for many soldiers from the northern Midwest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Aug. 1, 1860, an article in the Chicago Tribune proclaimed, “Great doings in Warren County.” The reporter recounted the immense surge in political support for the Republican presidential candidate, Abraham Lincoln, in the northwest farm regions. At a flagpole raising near Monmouth, pro-Lincoln speakers fulminated by the hour to “enthusiastic shouts” from a large crowd. In neighboring Henderson County a flood of 5,000 people, including hundreds arriving by steamboat from Iowa, crowded into Oquawka for a Republican rally later that month.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mitchel Thompson’s War', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Illinois', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-28T14:58:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By C Kay Larson', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f1a5666-cfa8-5b18-a1c4-3e9fa7e882a0', 'word_count': 1434, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f1a5666-cfa8-5b18-a1c4-3e9fa