dangerous incidents aboard international cruise ships.” (Below, the Carnival Triumph is pulled into port at the Alabama Cruise Terminal in Mobile last month, after a fire disabled the ship, stranding 4,200 people onboard.) The guidelines, for passengers on cruise ships, even ones registered in foreign countries, are modeled on those in the airline passenger bill of rights that is currently law. They include access to backup generators, staff members traed in emergency and evacuation procedures, and full refunds for cruises abruptly canceled because of mechanical failures, plus three other guidelines.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'If Something Goes Wrong', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cruises: If Something Goes Wrong', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cruises', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-28T17:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tanya Mohn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tanya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mohn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8479e8c4-8c37-5d63-9a36-370fb96f329c', 'word_count': 116, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8479e8c4-8c37-5d63-9a36-370fb96f329c'}, {'abstract': 'Police list assorted ammunition and weapons, and a spreadsheet of mass killings, found in the home of Adam Lanza, perhaps providing a peek inside a troubled mind.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/nyregion/100000002143125/secrets-in-newtown.html', 'snippet': 'Police list assorted ammunition and weapons, and a spreadsheet of mass killings, found in the home of Adam Lanza, perhaps providing a peek inside a troubled mi