in of Myanmar said Thursday that he was prepared to use force to quell the religious rioting that has shaken his country, answering calls even from longtime democracy advocates for more forceful security measures.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/29/world/myanmar/myanmar-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 365, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/29/world/myanmar/myanmar-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 365}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/29/world/myanmar/myanmar-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 623, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/29/world/myanmar/myanmar-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1245, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/29/world/myanmar/myanmar-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/29/world/myanmar/myanmar-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/29/world/myanmar/myanmar-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Myanmar’s Leader Says He May Use Force to Halt Deadly Rioting', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Myanmar’s Leader Says He May Use Force to Halt Deadly Rioting', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fuller, Thomas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rohingya (Ethnic Group)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thein Sein', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Myanmar', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Buddhism', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-28T18:39:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Fuller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fuller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/317bab12-7079-5ea4-ad7a-03919aa3bd96', 'word_count': 689, 'uri': 'nyt://article/317bab12-7079-5ea4-ad7a-03919aa3bd96'}, {'abstract': 'J.R. Smith has rarely shown the consistency that he has exhibited during the Knicks’ six-game winning streak. He’s scoring more and shooting better.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/28/knicks-hot-streak-coincides-with-smiths/', 'snippet': 'J.R. Smith has rarely shown the consistency that he has exhibited during the Knicks’ six-game winning streak. He’s scoring more and shooting better.', 'lead_paragraph': 'J. R. Smith has always had a knack for making it look easy, if only for brief periods. Throughout his career, Smith’s game has been defined by exquisite exhibitions of skill and athleticism mixed with equal measures of average play. Catch the right five minutes, and if you knew nothing else about the N.B.A., you would swear he was the greatest player on earth. Watch the wrong quarter or half, and you wouldn’t remember his name.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Knicks’ Wild Thing Settles Into Groove at the Right Time', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Knicks’ Backcourt Comes to the Forefront at the Right Time', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, J R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-28T18:40:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Beckley Mason', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Beckley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mason', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d767c67-3278-5b45-b808-8960705309bd', 'word_count': 817, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d767c67-3278-5b45-b808-8960705309bd'}, {'abstract': 'The 113th Congress is the third consecutive legislative session to experience an unusually high number of Senate retirements. Those retirements have combined with defeats at the ballot box to create the largest turnover in the Senate in nearly 40 years.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/28/retirements-contributing-to-largest-senate-turnover-in-decades/', 'snippet': 'The 113th Congress is the third consecutive legislative session to experience an unusually high number of Senate retirements. Those retirements have combined with defeats at the ballot box to create the largest turnover in the Senate in nearly 40 ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The announcement on Tuesday by Senator Tim Johnson, Democrat of South Dakota, that he will not run for re-election in 2014 brings the total number of senators who have retired or resigned in the 113th Congress to eight.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Retirements Contributing to Largest Senate Turnover in Decades', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-28T18:42:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Micah Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Micah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1065bcbe-4524-541a-9b81-774dc6642b96', 'word_count': 577, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1065bcbe-4524-541a-9b81-774dc6642b96'}, {'abstract': 'A view of the day in sports, including gymnastics and horse racing in Dubai, and Maria Sharapova reaching a final in Key Biscayne, Fla.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2013/03/28/sports/20130328PHOTOREPLAY.html', 'snippet': 'A view of the day in sports, including gymnastics and horse racing in Dubai, and Maria Sharapova reaching a final in Key Biscayne, Fla.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A view of the day in sports, including gymnastics and horse racing in Dubai, and Maria Sharapova reaching a final in Key Biscayne, Fla.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/28/sports/20130328PHOTOREPLAY-slide-LHSH/20130328PHOTOREPLAY-slide-LHSH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 394, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/28/sports/20130328PHOTOREPLAY-slide-LHSH/20130328PHOTOREPLAY-slide-LHSH-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 394}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/28/sports/20130328PHOTOREPLAY-slide-LHSH/20130328PHOTOREPLAY-slide-LHSH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 673, 'width': 1024, 'subTyp