s', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-28T18:53:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Gough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/49c0ad7c-15b4-59b2-93cb-bce2d9c535e8', 'word_count': 1048, 'uri': 'nyt://article/49c0ad7c-15b4-59b2-93cb-bce2d9c535e8'}, {'abstract': 'The festival, at the home of the academy (known familiarly as BAAD), will include the film “Lucky.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/29/arts/baadass-womens-festival-at-bronx-academy-of-arts-and-dance.html', 'snippet': 'The festival, at the home of the academy (known familiarly as BAAD), will include the film “Lucky.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Whether or not the Bronx Academy of Arts and Dance’s annual BAADass Women’s Festival is a conscious homage to Melvin Van Peebles’s classic blaxploitation film “Sweet Sweetback’s Baadasssss Song,” it, too, comments on social injustice with seriousness and humor.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'BAADass Women’s Festival at Bronx Academy of Arts and Dance', 'kicker': 'Weekend Miser', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bronx Academy of Arts and Dance', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-28T19:05:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By A. C. Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/53ce6078-e8a6-56ab-b255-6fd1feabba0d', 'word_count': 419, 'uri': 'nyt://article/53ce6078-e8a6-56ab-b255-6fd1feabba0d'}, {'abstract': 'James Magnuson’s next novel, “Famous Writers I Have Known,” will feature a character inspired by the best-selling author James Michener.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/28/michener-center-director-to-mold-its-namesake-into-fiction/', 'snippet': 'James Magnuson’s next novel, “Famous Writers I Have Known,” will feature a character inspired by the best-selling author James Michener.', 'lead_paragraph': 'James Magnuson, who has been the director of the Michener Center for Writers at the University of Texas at Austin since 1994, will bring some of his experience with boldface names to his next novel. The book, “Famous Writers I Have Known,” was recently acquired by the publishing house W. W. Norton & Company.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Michener Center Director To Mold Its Namesake Into Fiction', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Magnuson, James', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Michener, James', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-28T19:06:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/11dafe89-0730-51dd-9d1a-7cf2040827a7', 'word_count': 356, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11dafe89-0730-51dd-9d1a-7cf2040827a7'}, {'abstract': 'A besieged commission, accused of bungling presidential voting this month, said that nullifying it over a few irregularities would be a mistake.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/29/world/africa/kenyan-panel-warns-against-nullifying-election.html', 'snippet': 'A besieged commission, accused of bungling presidential voting this month, said that nullifying it over a few irregularities would be a mistake.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NAIROBI, Kenya — Kenya’s besieged election commission, accused of bungling the recent presidential vote, fired back in court on Thursday, with its lawyers dismissing the allegations as “reckless, misguided and without regard for the truth” and saying that even if there were a few irregularities here and there, canceling the entire election and calling for a new one would be even worse.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kenyan Officials Advise Against Calling New Election Despite a Vote’s Flaws', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Kenyan Officials Advise Against Calling New Election Despite a Vote’s Flaws', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gettleman, Jeffrey', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kenya', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kenyatta, Uhuru Muigai', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Odinga, Raila', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-28T19:12:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeffrey Gettleman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeffrey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gettleman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3660604-0bff-5720-b31f-5995241ecc76', 'word_count': 726, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3660604-0bff-5720-b31f-5995241ecc76'}, {'abstract': 'A new legislative proposal seeks to streamline tax rules for flow-through entities, including S corporations, but it is unclear how much most small businesses will benefit from the changes.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/28/house-republicans-try-to-simplify-small-business-taxes/', 'snippet': 'A new legislative proposal seeks to streamline tax rules for flow-through entities, including S corporations, but it is unclear how much most small businesses will benefit from the changes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This month, Republicans in Congress unveiled proposals to radically remake the way many small businesses are taxed. As with many radical Republican proposals, this one from the House Ways and Means Committee chairman, David Camp, furthers a partisan agenda — if implemented, it would almost certainly reduce revenue to the federal government. But it also wins praise from independent tax experts for repairing what they call a body of law almost too complicated to comply with or to enforce.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'House Republicans Try to Simplify Small-Business Taxes', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corporate Taxes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-28T19:18:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robb Mandelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mandelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7194f005-2541-53ff-abe6-29f43577471f', 'word_count': 981, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7194f005-2541-53ff-abe6-29f43577471f'}, {'abstract': 'Over a period of three years, two independent filmmakers shot 400 hours of footage of the Olympic gold medalist Missy Franklin.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/29/sports/catching-missy-franklin-a-champion-swimmer-on-film.html', 'snippet': 'Over a period of three years, two independent filmmakers shot 400 hours of footage of the Olympic gold medalist Missy Franklin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Of the 400 hours of footage that the independent filmmakers Grant Barbeito and Christo Brock gathered on the swimming champion Missy Franklin and her training partner Kara Lynn Joyce, one scene stands out as their favorite. It was not from any of Franklin’s four gold medal swims at the Olympics, but from the 2012 Colorado state high school championships several months before her breakout performance in London. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/29/sports/29missy1/29missy1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/29/sports/29missy1/29missy1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/29/sports/29missy1/29missy1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/29/sports/29missy1/29missy1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, '