r,” directed by Gilles Bourdos, tells the story of this Impressionist painter’s last model, who became the wife of his son Jean, the film director.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I refuse to paint the world black,” declares Pierre-Auguste Renoir (the great French actor Michel Bouquet) in “Renoir,” Gilles Bourdos’s compassionate late-life portrait of this French Impressionist painter, infirm with rheumatoid arthritis. “A painting should be something pleasant and cheerful,” he adds. “There are enough disagreeable things in life. I don’t need to paint more.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Muse to the Father, and a Wife to the Son', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Muse to the Father, and a Wife to the Son', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Renoir, Pierre Auguste', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bourdos, Gilles', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bouquet, Michel', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Theret, Christa', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Doret, Thomas', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rottiers, Vincent', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-28T20:59:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/a70551f6-593f-5ef4-80d1-bfd0183f8d53', 'word_count': 736, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a70551f6-593f-5ef4-80d1-bfd0183f8d53'}, {'abstract': 'Cyprus would be better off now had huge amounts of money not flowed into its banks in 2008 and 2009.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/29/business/cyprus-capital-controls-come-years-after-they-were-needed.html', 'snippet': 'Cyprus would be better off now had huge amounts of money not flowed into its banks in 2008 and 2009.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Capital controls came to Cyprus this week, a few years after they should have arrived — when it needed controls to stem the flow of hot money into the country’s banks.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/04/19/business/norris-75-standardinline/norris-75-standardinline-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2010/04/19/business/norris-75-standardinline/norris-75-standardinline-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Controls on Capital Come Late to Cyprus', 'kicker': 'High & Low Finance', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Controls on Capital Come Late to Cyprus', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cyprus', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-28T21:01:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Floyd Norris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Floyd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Norris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/116e13c8-e7b4-5a33-be5c-2953a5eb8fdf', 'word_count': 1399, 'uri': 'nyt://article/116e13c8-e7b4-5a33-be5c-2953a5eb8fdf'}, {'abstract': 'If you had Google Glass, what would your children do with it?', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/28/if-children-had-google-glass/', 'snippet': 'If you had Google Glass, what would your children do with it?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Would you buy Google Glass? How about a 3-D printer? I would (and, in the case of the 3-D printer, I have). Of course, I’m a sucker for being an earlier adopter, and the first to get my hands on new things. I’d be tinkering with this stuff even if I wasn’t a parent — but my children give me an excuse to indulge in my (expensive) hobby. I want to expose them to new technologies while they’re still new, and before we’ve had a chance to figure out how they fit into our lives.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/28/style/motherlode-glass/motherlode-glass-jumbo.png', 'height': 315, 'width': 581, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/28/style/motherlode-glass/motherlode-glass-superJumbo.png', 'height': 315, 'width': 581, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/28/style/motherlode-glass/motherlode-glass-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/28/style/motherlode-glass/motherlode-glass-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/28/style/motherlode-glass/motherlode-glass-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headl