'value': 'BANG & OLUFSEN', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-28T21:03:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72274b1b-b4d4-5581-8472-4fc1bb2e3d3c', 'word_count': 159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72274b1b-b4d4-5581-8472-4fc1bb2e3d3c'}, {'abstract': 'An exhibition on the Pre-Raphaelites at the National Gallery of Art makes the case that their movement was avant-garde.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/29/arts/design/pre-raphaelites-at-national-gallery-of-art.html', 'snippet': 'An exhibition on the Pre-Raphaelites at the National Gallery of Art makes the case that their movement was avant-garde.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — If “Pre-Raphaelites: Victorian Art and Design” at the National Gallery of Art were a theme-park ride, you would be strenuously exhorted to buckle up and hold on tight. Devoted to England’s ever-popular mid-19th-century art movement, the Pre-Raphaelite Brotherhood, and its followers, this exhibition is full of jolts and thrills that feel intense but never go very deep.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/29/arts/29SUB-PRERAPH-1_SPAN/29SUB-PRERAPH-1_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/29/arts/29SUB-PRERAPH-1_SPAN/29SUB-PRERAPH-1_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/29/arts/29SUB-PRERAPH-1_SPAN/29SUB-PRERAPH-1_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype