e': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/f58edc03-8849-5231-9cef-38aaf0c71396', 'word_count': 258, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f58edc03-8849-5231-9cef-38aaf0c71396'}, {'abstract': 'In Newtown, officials are listening to the veterans of past tragedies before disbursing the donations that poured in.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/29/opinion/wealth-that-comes-of-tragedy-in-newtown-conn.html', 'snippet': 'In Newtown, officials are listening to the veterans of past tragedies before disbursing the donations that poured in.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No one should envy the civic leaders of Newtown, Conn., as they attempt to bring order and transparency to distributing most of the $15 million in donations that has poured into town since the Sandy Hook Elementary School massacre of 20 children and six adults last December. The money was given through 40 ad hoc groups, many of them pursuing separate causes from helping families to building a local memorial, even an angel atop the town flagpole. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wealth That Comes of Tragedy', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wealth That Comes of Tragedy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newtown, Conn, Shooting (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Newtown (Conn)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-29T01:03:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/43058900-e0f7-5b9d-ae3c-cd2499ac16a6', 'word_count': 346, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43058900-e0f7-5b9d-ae3c-cd2499ac16a6'}, {'abstract': 'The increase in sexual assaults against women dehumanizes and demeans all Egyptians.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/29/opinion/terror-in-tahrir-square.html', 'snippet': 'The increase in sexual assaults against women dehumanizes and demeans all Egyptians.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cairo’s Tahrir Square once symbolized the hope Egyptians felt when they overthrew Hosni Mubarak and began building a democracy. But this iconic rallying point for protesters has today also come to symbolize the terror and contempt women increasingly face since the Muslim Brotherhood came to power and the country descended into turmoil.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Terror in Tahrir Square', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Terror in Tahrir Square', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tahrir Square (Cairo)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-29T01:03:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/6162fade-a31f-5907-a716-305d27b17259', 'word_count': 437, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6162fade-a31f-5907-a716-305d27b17259'}, {'abstract':