ursday for the first time since ending his self-imposed sabbatical from soccer, talked about a return to the game, to the national team and about the reactions of others to his difficult “mental place.”', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/29/donovan-speaks-about-a-national-team-return-and-more/', 'snippet': 'Landon Donovan, speaking with reporters Thursday for the first time since ending his self-imposed sabbatical from soccer, talked about a return to the game, to the national team and about the reactions of others to his difficult “mental place.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Landon Donovan spoke with reporters on Thursday for the first time since announcing he would return to Major League Soccer’s Los Angeles Galaxy this week. Sam Borden’s article for The Times dealt mostly with the one question on the mind of most fans when he walked away from the game after winning last year’s M.L.S. title: is he planning to return to the United States national team?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Donovan Speaks About a National Team Return, and More', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Donovan, Landon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Galaxy (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-29T04:14:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Das', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Das', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f01a61d-bb3c-578d-a8e4-63cda4b1f284', 'word_count': 807, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f01a61d-bb3c-578d-a8e4-63cda4b1f284'}, {'abstract': 'Water lines break in Hoboken.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/29/from-todays-paper-water-line-break-and-flood-homes-in-hoboken/', 'snippet': 'Water lines break in Hoboken.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Workers at Willow Avenue and 8th Street in Hoboken, N.J., the site of one of two water line breaks just a few blocks apart. The other was at Willow and 14th. Many in the city lost water pressure, and an advisory was issued warning residents to boil water.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From Today’s Paper: Water Line Break and Flood Homes in Hoboken', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-29T04:54:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7cf03364-563e-5dd7-99fa-5467f7268608', 'word_count': 48, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7cf03364-563e-5dd7-99fa-5467f7268608'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/29/arts/television/whats-on-friday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '11:30 A.M. (AMC) HACKERS (1995) Two New York high school students (played by Angelina Jolie and Jonny Lee Miller) use their hacking skills for mischiefmaking until they stumble upon a corporate extortion scheme and are charged for computer crimes they did not commit. Only through copious in-line skating, frenzied typing and obsolete tech lingo can their names be cleared. Janet Maslin, writing in The New York Times about this ’90s time capsule directed by Iain Softley, said, “A lot of attention has gone into the film’s video games, computer imagery and costumes, to the point where simply watching these artifacts is half the fun.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Friday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-29T05:00:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/cdd85ffb-fd65-5abb-a32e-ccec1f2064e1', 'word_count': 743, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cdd85ffb-fd65-5abb-a32e-ccec1f2064e1'}, {'abstract': 'A mother recalls a long-ago morning in a family where an autistic child pushes against the world, and everyone must cope.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/31/booming/a-time-as-fleeting-as-waxwings.html', 'snippet': 'A mother recalls a long-ago morning in a family where an autistic child pushes against the world, and everyone must cope.', 'lead_paragraph': ' I wrote this piece about six years ago, thinking back on a particular morning and piecing together the events of that day through old e-mails. I am 55 now and divorced, and think wistfully about the brief constellation that was our family. Studies of divorce rates among parents of autistic children contradict one another, citing rates as low as 24 percent and as high as 80 percent. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/31/booming/31mystory-booming-autism/31mystory-booming-autism-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 374, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/31/booming/31mystory-booming-autism/31mystory-booming-autism-