me': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2e31fb5-5542-572d-96ad-646089bdf0c4', 'word_count': 287, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d2e31fb5-5542-572d-96ad-646089bdf0c4'}, {'abstract': 'President Thein Sein claims security forces refrained from intervening to stop recent violence against Muslims to protect Myanmar’s democratic transition. Not so.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/29/violence-against-muslims-in-meiktila-myanmar/', 'snippet': 'President Thein Sein claims security forces refrained from intervening to stop recent violence against Muslims to protect Myanmar’s democratic transition. Not so.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MEIKTILA, Myanmar — Not one bullet was fired, not one smoke bomb was dropped as scores of Muslims were attacked and some were burnt alive in Myanmar last week. The security forces just looked on. In a country where they routinely use brute force against political dissidents, villagers who protest land grabs and even monks, their passivity was sadly revealing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kristallnacht in Myanmar', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Buddhism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Religion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reform and Reorganization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion and Belief', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Meiktila (Myanmar)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-29T14:23:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Swe Win', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Swe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Win', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6d70274-99cb-517a-b77d-9586ec37486a', 'word_count': 786, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6d70274-99cb-517a-b77d-9586ec37486a'}, {'abstract': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/29/the-gun-report-march-29-2013/', 'snippet': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There was a lot of gun news yesterday. An inventory of Adam Lanza’a possessions was released by police. According to the Times, they included “several firearms, more than 1,600 rounds of ammunition, 11 knives, a starter pistol, a bayonet, 3 samurai swords,” as well as “photographs of what appeared to be a corpse smeared in blood and covered in plastic, as well as a newspaper clipping that chronicled a vicious shooting at Northern Illinois University.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Gun Report: March 29, 2013', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-29T14:30:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Nocera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nocera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5174ef51-0568-55e6-ba9b-2935afc0df32', 'word_count': 803, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5174ef51-0568-55e6-ba9b-2935afc0df32'}, {'abstract': 'When John Swan and Sarah Masel searched for a rental apartment to share, a usable living room was a priority.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/31/realestate/we-do-not-want-to-go-home-again.html', 'snippet': 'When John Swan and Sarah Masel searched for a rental apartment to share, a usable living room was a priority.', 'lead_paragraph': 'John Swan was acutely aware of what his apartment on the Upper East Side lacked — a living room. ', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/31/realestate/31HUNT4_SPAN/Hunt4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 441, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/31/realestate/31HUNT4_SPAN/Hunt4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 441}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/31/realestate/31HUNT4_SPAN/Hunt4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 752, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/31/realestate/31HUNT4_SPAN/Hunt4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1504, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/31/realestate/31HUNT4_SPAN/Hunt4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/31/realestate/31HUNT4_SPAN/Hunt4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/31/realestate/31HUNT4_SPAN/Hunt4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'We Do Not Want to Go Home Again', 'kicker': 'The Hunt', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'We Do Not Want to Go Home Again', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cohen, Joyce', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'SoHo (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Village (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Upper East Side (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Meatpacking District (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-29T14:31:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joyce Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joyce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7921050-772c-5dd6-b5ed-e4b6cf0cb623', 'word_count': 973, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7921050-772c-5dd6-b5ed-e4b6cf0cb623'}, {'abstract': 'A new biography of Karl Marx emphasizes his responses to events, not his body of ideas.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/31/books/review/karl-marx-by-jonathan-sperber.html', 'snippet': 'A new biography of Karl Marx emphasizes his responses to events, not his body of ideas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Karl Marx depicted in Jonathan Sperber’s absorbing, meticulously researched biography will be unnervingly familiar to anyone who has had even the most fleeting acquaintance with radical politics. Here is a man never more passionate than when attacking his own side, saddled with perennial money problems and still reliant on his parents for cash, constantly plotting new, world-changing ventures yet having trouble with both deadlines and personal hygiene, living in rooms that some might call bohemian, others plain “slummy,” and who can be maddeningly inconsistent when not lapsing into elaborate flights of theory and unintelligible abstraction. ', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/31/books/review/31FREEDLAND/31FREEDLAND-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 536, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/31/books/review/31FREEDLAND/31FREEDLAND-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 536}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/31/books/review/31FREEDLAND/31FREEDLAND-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 915, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/31/books/review/31FREEDLAND/31FREEDLAND-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1830, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/31/books/review/31FREEDLAND/31FREEDLAND-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/31/books/review/31FREEDLAND/31FREEDLAND-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/31/books/review/31FREEDLAND/31FREEDLAND-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Man of His Time', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Man of His Time', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Freedland, Jonathan', 'rank': 2,