amp-by-richard-hell.html', 'snippet': 'The rocker and frontman for the Voidoids ruminates on his life, loves and his rift with a collaborator.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Richard Hell was partly responsible for the phenomenon of punk, a visionary whose style Malcolm McLaren imported to England and impressed upon his pet project, the Sex Pistols, who popularized and cashed in on Hell’s spiky hair, torn clothes and audacious attitude — embodied in his seminal record of 1977, “Blank Generation.” In his new autobiography, “I Dreamed I Was a Very Clean Tramp,” Hell admits to resenting the Sex Pistols for failing to acknowledge how much they lifted from him. But in a moment that speaks to this punk-icon-turned-accomplished-writer’s commitment to an objective distance from himself, he rhetorically asks, “How many kids were going to get excited about calling themselves ‘blank’? The concept of ‘anarchy’ was just as disgusted and contrary but a lot more fun.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/31/books/review/31KUSHNER/31KUSHNER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 379, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/31/books/review/31KUSHNER/31KUSHNER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 379}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/31/books/review/31KUSHNER/31KUSHNER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 647, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/31/books/review/31KUSHNER/31KUSHNER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1293, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/31/books/review/31KUSHNER/31KUSHNER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/31/books/review/31KUSHNER/31KUSHNER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/31/books/review/31KUSHNER/31KUSHNER-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Prince of Punk', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Prince of Punk', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kushner, Rachel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hell, Richard', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Television (Music Group)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-29T14:45:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Kushner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kushner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/21bb2e51-e231-5d99-b266-0f1e08181d7d', 'word_count': 1008, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21bb2e51-e231-5d99-b266-0f1e08181d7d'}, {'abstract': 'This biography reveals a fiercely determined activist behind the mild-mannered lady in a hat.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/31/books/review/the-rebellious-life-of-mrs-rosa-parks-by-jeanne-theoharis.html', 'snippet': 'This biography reveals a fiercely determined activist behind the mild-mannered lady in a hat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Beautiful Rosa Parks sits alone in the Montgomery, Ala., city bus she desegregated, an image endlessly replicated, most recently on an American postage stamp issued in February to commemorate Black History Month and what would have been Parks’s 100th birthday. By the time she died in 2005, Parks had become an American saint. President Bill Clinton gave her a Medal of Freedom in 1996; Congress awarded her a Gold Medal in 1999 (passed nearly unanimously — only Representative Ron Paul of Texas dissented); and after her death, her body lay in the Capitol Rotunda. She was the first woman to be so honored, and the first black woman to have a statue in her likeness placed in the National Statuary Hall of the Capitol. It was unveiled this year and positioned, House Speaker John Boehner pointed out, “right in the gaze” of Jefferson Davis, president of the \xadConfederacy. ', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/31/books/review/31PAINTER/31PAINTER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 638, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/31/books/review/31PAINTER/31PAINTER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 638}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/31/books/review/31PAINTER/31PAINTER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 963, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/31/books/review/31PAINTER/31PAINTER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1925, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/31/books/review/31PAINTER/31PAINTER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/31/books/review/31PAINTER/31PAINTER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/31/books/review/31PAINTER/31PAINTER-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mother of the Movement', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mother of the Movement', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Rebellious Life of Mrs. Rosa Parks (Book)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Theoharis, Jeanne', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Parks, Rosa', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights and Liberties', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-29T14:46:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nell Irvin Painter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nell', 'middlename': 'Irvin', 'lastname': 'Painter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/11657a58-eb4c-5373-a578-376cdd032797', 'word_count': 1153, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11657a58-eb4c-5373-a578-376cdd032797'}, {'abstract': 'Some Democrats aren’t giving up.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/29/what-now-for-gun-control/', 'snippet': 'Some Democrats aren’t giving up.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Senate Majority Leader Harry Reid and other Democratic leaders in Congress folded their tents on comprehensive gun control fast — dropping a ban on assault weapons and limits on the size of magazines as they watered down the “official” bill that will hit the Senate floor.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Now for Gun Control?', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newtown, Conn, Shooting (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-29T14:46:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe3d9046-8dea-51ee-b392-a4a8dc31c331', 'word_count': 445, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe3d9046-8dea-51ee-b392-a4a8dc31c331'}, {'abstract': 'Alexander Stille looks at the discordant strains of his parents’ marriage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/31/books/review/the-force-of-things-by-alexander-stille.html', 'snippet': 'Alexander Stille looks at the discordant strains of his parents’ marriage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s tempting to invest the remnants of the past — the letters, the heirlooms, the junk — with tremendous explanatory power, especially when the stuff is your family’s. The cliché about the dustbin of history is almost too apt when Alexander Stille walks into his aunt Lally’s apartment. Buried in the stacks of clothes, receipts, lottery tickets and old balls of yarn, there are fantastic photographs, a letter from the proto-Fascist poet Gabriele d’Annunzio and all the living room furniture Lally’s parents had taken with them when the family fled Russia for Italy and then Italy for the United States. ', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/31/books/review/0331-Thomas/0331-Thomas-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 481, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/31/books/review/0331-Thomas/0331-Thomas-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 481}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/31/books/review/0331-Thomas/0331-Thomas-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 820, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/31/books/review/0331-Thomas/0331-Thomas-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1047, 'width': 1307, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/31/books/review/0331-Thomas/0331-Thomas-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/31/books/review/0331-Thomas/0331-Thomas-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/31/books/review/0331-Thomas/0331-Thomas-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When Worlds Collide', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When Worlds Collide', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stille, Alexander', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject',