, 'word_count': 826, 'uri': 'nyt://article/909e3bca-1df4-55e4-a003-4abf408a149f'}, {'abstract': 'The new investigation was prompted by six reports from owners that a rear control arm failed, apparently because of corrosion.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/29/safety-agency-opens-inquiry-on-hyundai-sonata-suspension-failures/', 'snippet': 'The new investigation was prompted by six reports from owners that a rear control arm failed, apparently because of corrosion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Almost four years after Hyundai had to recall about 600,000 vehicles for corrosion problems, the National Highway Traffic Safety Administration has started investigating possible corrosion-related rear suspension failures on an estimated 393,000 2006-8 Hyundai Sonatas, according to a report posted on Friday on the agency Web site.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Safety Agency Opens Inquiry on Hyundai Sonata Suspension Failures', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recalls and Bans of Products', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hyundai Motor Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Highway Traffic Safety Administration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-29T15:36:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca9edc2c-f4f0-54ad-8b22-bf41675568c5', 'w