ord_count': 701, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fdbc34da-656d-5341-8daf-7ca472e0d9e2'}, {'abstract': 'President Mahmoud Abbas of the Palestinian Authority pardoned Mamdouh Hamamreh, who officers said portrayed Mr. Abbas as a traitor on Facebook.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/30/world/middleeast/mahmoud-abbas-pardons-palestinian-journalist.html', 'snippet': 'President Mahmoud Abbas of the Palestinian Authority pardoned Mamdouh Hamamreh, who officers said portrayed Mr. Abbas as a traitor on Facebook.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The president of the Palestinian Authority, Mahmoud Abbas, has pardoned a Palestinian journalist whose one-year prison sentence for insulting him on Facebook was upheld by a West Bank appeals court on Thursday, the president’s legal adviser said in a statement. The journalist, Mamdouh Hamamreh, was arrested in 2009 after Palestinian intelligence officers said they saw a photograph portraying Mr. Abbas as a traitor on Mr. Hamamreh’s Facebook page. The Palestinian Center for Development and Media Freedoms, a nongovernmental organization based in the West Bank, said that Mr. Hamamreh was not the person who had posted the photograph, nor did he share or “like” it. The president’s legal adviser said that Mr. Abbas respected freedom of opinion and expression and that he had not personally filed a complaint against the journalist.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Abbas Pardons Journalist Sentenced for Insulting Him', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'West Bank: Journalist Jailed Over Insult Is Pardoned', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABBAS, MAHMOUD', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Palestinian Authority', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hamamreh, Mamdouh', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-29T16:10:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Isabel Kershner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kershner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3598a433-d640-5cc8-a184-1b3c32811fb2', 'word_count': 130, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3598a433-d640-5cc8-a184-1b3c32811fb2'}, {'abstract': 'Doctors and lawyers are big earners and smart people, but that does not necessarily mean they’re the best financial decision-makers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/30/your-money/money-advice-for-doctors-and-lawyers.html', 'snippet': 'Doctors and lawyers are big earners and smart people, but that does not necessarily mean they’re the best financial decision-makers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN most places in America, doctors and lawyers are at the top of the career pyramid. They’re often the top earners in town. And they usually live in the nicest neighborhoods and drive expensive cars. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/30/your-money/30wealth/30wealth-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/30/your-money/30wealth/30wealth-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image