 those who leased or bought Ford vehicles manufactured from 2002 to 2010.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/29/suit-claims-ford-failed-to-protect-vehicles-from-unintended-acceleration/', 'snippet': 'The suit asks to represent those who leased or bought Ford vehicles manufactured from 2002 to 2010.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A class-action suit filed against the Ford Motor Company on Thursday asserted that the automaker knew its vehicles were “vulnerable to sudden unintended acceleration events,” but failed to equip them with a system so that the brake pedal would always overrule the gas pedal.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Suit Claims Ford Failed to Protect Vehicles From Unintended Acceleration', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ford Motor Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-29T16:58:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c3286b2e-ffdc-5c3a-9e41-80ff64659d26', 'word_count': 279, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c3286b2e-ffdc-5c3a-9e41-80ff64659d26'}, {'abstract': 'Suddenly, Florida Gulf Coast has become a popular pick to keep its N.C.A.A. tournament upset streak going, this time against Florida.', 'web_url': 'https://thequad.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/29/florida-gulf-coast-from-plucky-underdog-to-chic-pick/', 'snippet': 'Suddenly, Florida Gulf Coast has become a popular pick to keep its N.C.A.A. tournament upset streak going, this time against Florida.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ESPN analysts Digger Phelps and Bruce Pearl have picked Florida Gulf Coast to beat Florida. They did so matter-of-factly, too, like a 15th seed knocking off a No. 3 in the round of 16 is as common as pouring milk on cereal.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Florida Gulf Coast, From Plucky Underdog to Chic Pick', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball (College)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Florida Gulf Coast University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Florida', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-29T16:59:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Spousta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Spousta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/339a494b-bbcc-536c-b6df-de49f128bcd7', 'word_count': 341, 'uri': 'nyt://article/339a494b-bbcc-536c-b6df-de49f128bcd7'}, {'abstract': 'A weekly capsule of events around the globe curated by our writers and editors.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/29/calendar-coming-events-in-paris-scotland-and-new-york-city/', 'snippet': 'A weekly capsule of events around the globe curated by our writers and editors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Paris Haute Couture, Paris There’s vintage, and then there’s historic couture. This show of 100 dresses is the latter. The selection from the Musée Galliera collection — from late-19th-century Worth evening gowns (a 1925 Jean Patou dress is shown right) to an intricately embroidered outfit by John Galliano for Christian Dior — is on view at Paris’s City Hall through July 6.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Calendar: Coming Events in Paris, Scotland and New York City', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Calendar', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-29T17:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/00b8fc97-7daf-5e78-92bc-ea4d03eb93a2', 'word_count': 171, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00b8fc97-7daf-5e78-92bc-ea4d03eb93a2'}, {'abstract': 'Kenya’s Supreme Court released results from a recount in the presidential election that Uhuru Kenyatta won, narrowly avoiding a runoff and clinching the presidency by a few thousand ballots.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/30/world/africa/voting-irregularities-in-kenya-election-are-confirmed.html', 'snippet': 'Kenya’s Supreme Court released results from a recount in the presidential election that Uhuru Kenyatta won, narrowly avoiding a runoff and clinching the presidency by a few thousand ballots.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NAIROBI, Kenya — The landmark legal challenge to Kenya’s presidential election wrapped up on Friday, and the last bits of evidence confirmed what many had suspected from the beginning: there were definitely voting irregularities, but were they big enough to change the outcome?', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/30/world/kenya/kenya-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 357, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/30/world/kenya/kenya-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 357}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/30/world/kenya/kenya-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 609, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/30/world/kenya/kenya-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1217, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/30/world/kenya/kenya-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/30/world/kenya/kenya-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/30/world/kenya/kenya-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Voting Irregularities in Kenya Election Are Confirmed, Adding Fuel to Dispute', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Voting Irregularities in Kenya Election Are Confirmed, Adding Fuel to Dispute', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kenya', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gettleman, Jeffrey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kenyatta, Uhuru Muigai', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Odinga, Raila', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-29T17:01:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeffrey Gettleman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeffrey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gettleman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/92a8d206-d30e-500a-862f-4009a0541d3a', 'word_count': 544, 'uri': 'nyt://article/92a8d206-d30e-500a-862f-4009a0541d3a'}, {'abstract': 'Sara Schechner and Kenneth Launie bonded over a shared love of science and history.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/31/fashion/weddings/sara-schechner-kenneth-launie-vows.html', 'snippet': 'Sara Schechner and Kenneth Launie bonded over a shared love of science and history.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the call came in April 2004, it was hard for Kenneth Launie to contain his enthusiasm. An amateur collector and restorer of telescopes, he had seen the instrument before, but only behind the glare of a glass case at Harvard. Then, out of nowhere, came the offer: Bring your white gloves and your screwdriver, and take apart the telescope that had been used by John Winthrop, a Harvard professor and descendant of the Massachusetts Bay Colony founder, to observe the transit of Venus in 1769. ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/31/fashion/weddings/31VOWS1/31VOWS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 436, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/31/fashion/weddings/31VOWS1/31VOWS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 436}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/31/fashion/weddings/31VOWS1/31VOWS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 745, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'super