//takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/29/syria-iran-and-the-n-r-a-versus-everybody/', 'snippet': 'The treaty to regulate global trade in conventional weapons is essential. But a few pariah states, plus a few interest groups, don’t like it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was always wishful thinking to expect that all of the United Nations’ 193 member states would approve the treaty regulating global trade in conventional weapons that was negotiated in New York this week. But the conclusion reached on Thursday was stark: On one side, opposing the new pact, were three of the world’s pariah states – Syria, Iran and North Korea. On the other side, favoring the new pact, was … everybody else.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Syria, Iran and the N.R.A. Versus Everybody', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARMS CONTROL AND LIMITATION AND DISARMAMENT', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Arms Trade', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-29T17:48:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Giacomo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Giacomo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/332f085b-d424-59b4-b7be-5ce55659985f', 'word_count': 465, 'uri': 'nyt://article/332f085b-d424-59b4-b7be-5ce55659985f'}, {'abstract': 'Images of Hollywood actors in non-English films.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2013/03/31/movies/20130331_FOREIGN.html', 'snippet': 'Images of Hollywood actors in non-English films.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Images of Hollywood actors in non-English films.', 'source': 'The N