ract': 'Alice Cooper, Robbie Krieger and others perform at a benefit concert for a rock ‘n’ roll academy.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/29/some-veteran-rockers-help-to-pass-the-torch/', 'snippet': 'Alice Cooper, Robbie Krieger and others perform at a benefit concert for a rock ‘n’ roll academy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With Alice Cooper approximating Jim Morrison’s trademark alternation of growling intensity and meditative sultriness, and Robby Krieger reprising his vintage guitar solos, a starry band dominated by glam-metal veterans worked their way through the Doors classics “Back Door Man” and “Break On Through (To the Other Side)” on Thursday evening in Sioux Falls, S.D., as part of a concert to benefit the city’s new Brennan Rock & Roll Academy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Some Veteran Rockers Help to Pass the Torch', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bach, Sebastian', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cooper, Alice', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Singer, Eric (1958- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boys and Girls Clubs of America', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Doors, The', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kiss (Music Group)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Motley Crue', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Dakota', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-29T18:00:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed648fe1-cb01-52b1-849f-a5f2ba59a976', 'word_count': 323, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed648fe1-cb01-52b1-849f-a5f2ba59a976'}, {'abstract': 'In its latest collaboration with Vans, Kenzo takes leopard and floral cues from Thailand.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/29/fresh-kicks/', 'snippet': 'In its latest collaboration with Vans, Kenzo takes leopard and floral cues from Thailand.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Vans, a favorite of surfers and skaters, goes for an Asian punk brightly colored look this season. The Kenzo designers Humberto Leon and Carol Lim emblazoned the canvas kicks with motifs culled from their spring 2013 collection, which was inspired by a trip to Thailand. While the collection’s colorful leopard spots and bursts of floral prints may be a challenge to pull off on a head-to-toe look, the exuberant pops of pattern on these Vans feel just right. $125; openingceremony.us (beginning Monday).', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fresh Kicks', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fresh Kicks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-29T18:00:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maura Egan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maura', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Egan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e84a639a-4d3f-521e-a601-808bdf6ce169', 'word_count': 82, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e84a639a-4d3f-521e-a601-808bdf6ce169'}, {'abstract': 'Food-related events around New York.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/29/weekend-fare-135/', 'snippet': 'Food-related events around New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While many Easter workshops may be for children, Neuhaus, the luxury Belgian chocolatier at 500 Madison Avenue in Midtown, is offering one for adults, from 7 to 9 p.m. Friday and 9 to 11 a.m. Saturday. Guests will decorate their own chocolate Easter egg shells and choose pralines to take home in a houndstooth-wrapped package. The class is $75 a person and includes all materials and beverages. Call (212) 644-4490 to make a reservation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Weekend Fare', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-29T18:09:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bao Ong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bao', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0afef0cc-4574-5ec0-9111-bde836db3a5f', 'word_count': 400, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0afef0cc-4574-5ec0-9111-bde836db3a5f'}, {'abstract': '“Earth 2″ chronicles a parallel world in which Batman, Superman and Wonder Woman have died.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/29/graphic-books-best-sellers-earth-2-at-no-1/', 'snippet': '“Earth 2″ chronicles a parallel world in which Batman, Superman and Wonder Woman have died.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is an embarrassment of riches on our hardcover and paperback graphic books best-seller lists this week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/29/books/29earth2/29earth2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 396, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'su