{'firstname': 'Liam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/66140789-72d6-55ed-b35d-d77c62961ab1', 'word_count': 815, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66140789-72d6-55ed-b35d-d77c62961ab1'}, {'abstract': 'At Saigonese, traditional Vietnamese dishes are offered in large portions for the health and taste conscious, with seasoning that is unlikely to offend.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/31/nyregion/a-review-of-saigonese-in-hartsdale.html', 'snippet': 'At Saigonese, traditional Vietnamese dishes are offered in large portions for the health and taste conscious, with seasoning that is unlikely to offend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Traditional Vietnamese cuisine has the reputation of being one of the healthiest in the world. Considering in the growing popularity of foods that are not only tasty, but also healthful, Saigonese could not have arrived in Hartsdale at a better time. Cooking in this restaurant’s kitchen is about quick preparations of fresh ingredients with masses of dewy herbs (parsley, mint, sweet basil and cilantro). Few items are deep fried. ', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/31/nyregion/31DINEWE3/31DINEWE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/31/nyregion/31DINEWE3/31DINEWE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/31/nyregion/31DINEWE3/31DINEWE3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type':