nization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': "O'Brien", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6661a1d-97cb-5fa9-ad63-2c7399945580', 'word_count': 1164, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6661a1d-97cb-5fa9-ad63-2c7399945580'}, {'abstract': 'Alarmed by injuries and an aging roster, some Yankees fans believe they are already in the same boat as Mets fans, dreading the season to come.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/30/sports/baseball/some-yankees-fans-have-gnawing-feeling-that-all-is-not-well.html', 'snippet': 'Alarmed by injuries and an aging roster, some Yankees fans believe they are already in the same boat as Mets fans, dreading the season to come.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is little that screams the words “damage” and “control” like a typically news-media-shy baseball owner suddenly making the rounds of sports talk radio and opening his door to quotation-hungry reporters. In a spate of recent interviews, Hal Steinbrenner, the Yankees’ managing general partner, has given his personal assurance that his franchise remains committed to “fielding a championship-caliber team every year.”', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Some Yankees Fans Have Gnawing Feeling That All Is Not Well', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Gnawing Feeling That All Is Not Well', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Steinbrenner, George M 3d', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rodriguez, Alex', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Steinbrenner, Hal', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-30T02:08:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harvey Araton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harvey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Araton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/69eb2d30-53c3-5649-9c56-306e13d57e97', 'word_count': 1386, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69eb2d30-53c3-5649-9c56-306e13d57e97'}, {'abstract': 'City officials said those in hotels were mostly poor, with no home to return to or not enough income to qualify for available apartments.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/30/nyregion/relying-on-hotel-rooms-for-thousands-who-were-uprooted-by-hurricane.html', 'snippet': 'City officials said those in hotels were mostly poor, with no home to return to or not enough income to qualify for available apartments.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Five months after Hurricane Sandy, more than 2,000 people who were displaced by the storm remain in hotels in New York City, leading some officials to acknowledge that the city had not been prepared for the challenges in finding them housing.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/30/nyregion/sandy/sandy-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/30/nyregion/sandy/sandy-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/30/nyregion/sandy/sandy-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'su