rganization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/18779468-8aa6-564e-8943-ad0c95ee3119', 'word_count': 594, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18779468-8aa6-564e-8943-ad0c95ee3119'}, {'abstract': 'A Brooklyn federal court judge has ruled against two lawyers who brought forth lawsuits claiming that businesses had violated the Americans with Disabilities Act.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/30/nyregion/judge-rebukes-lawyers-profiting-from-us-disability-law.html', 'snippet': 'A Brooklyn federal court judge has ruled against two lawyers who brought forth lawsuits claiming that businesses had violated the Americans with Disabilities Act.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The lawyers drafted the lawsuits by the dozens, claiming that local businesses had violated federal law by not providing access to people with disabilities — and generating thousands of dollars per case in legal fees for themselves. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Judge Rebukes 2 Lawyers Profiting From U.S. Disability Law', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Judge Rebukes 2 Lawyers Profiting From U.S. Disability Law', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Secret, Mosi', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AMERICANS WITH DISABILITIES ACT', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disabilities', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legal Profession', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-30T02:24:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mosi Secret', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mosi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Secret', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/717a5cda-4fa8-592b-9b92-c0a0eabb2e8a', 'word_count': 729, 'uri': 'nyt://article/717a5cda-4fa8-592b-9b92-c0a0eabb2e8a'}, {'abstract': 'Volunteers have collected 78 bodies from the streets of Bangui, Central African Republic’s capital, since rebels seized control of the city last week, the Central African Red Cross reported.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/30/world/africa/central-african-republic-bodies-found-in-the-capital.html', 'snippet': 'Volunteers have collected 78 bodies from the streets of Bangui, Central African Republic’s capital, since rebels seized control of the city last week, the Central African Red Cross reported.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Volunteers have collected 78 bodies from the streets of Bangui, the capital of the Central African Republic, since rebel fighters seized control of the city last week, the Central African Red Cross reported Friday. Many of the bodies lacked identification documents, a Red Cross official told Agence France-Presse, and other medical officials said it was not immediately clear whether the dead were rebels, government soldiers, foreign soldiers or civilians. Hospitals in the capital are overflowing with rebels and others wounded in the fighting, above, officials said. A loose coalition of armed groups from the country’s northeast ousted President François Bozizé on Sunday; the rebels, who are reported to have child soldiers among their ranks, accused Mr. Bozizé of breaching the terms of a January peace deal. He first fled to Cameroon but has since requested refuge in Benin, news reports said Friday. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/30/world/briefs-