nd have elected to postpone the change until 2014, when it becomes mandatory, the Education Ministry confirmed Friday. The ministry estimated that the plan would affect fewer than 25 percent of France’s nearly six million public school children ages 3 to 11 in the coming school year. But several large cities, including Paris, will begin the half-day in September. For more than a century, the French school schedule has been punctuated by a midweek break, originally created for catechism studies. The new plan, which has drawn opposition from teachers and parents, calls for three hours of class time on Wednesdays while reducing the regular school day — which typically runs from 8:30 a.m. to at least 4 p.m. — by 45 minutes. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'France: Most Cities Postpone Plan for New School Hours', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'France: Most Cities Postpone Plan for New School Hours', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-30T02:29:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicola Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicola', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/69a55f5d-9fb7-5dcc-b267-fc77b4a27c18', 'word_count': 144, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69a55f5d-9fb7-5dcc-b267-fc77b4a27c18'}, {'abstract': 'Vernon Reid, guitarist in the band Living Colour, usually rises before the rest of his family and tries to catch up with his favorite podcasts; he calls them a kind of rebirth of radio.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/31/nyregion/vernon-reid-savors-the-mellower-music-of-home.html', 'snippet': 'Vernon Reid, guitarist in the band Living Colour, usually rises before the rest of his family and tries to catch up with his favorite podcasts; he calls them a kind of rebirth of radio.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Vernon Reid, guitarist in the band Living Colour, became a rock star, he bought a Victorian house in the St. George neighborhood on Staten Island. Now, as the band celebrates the 25th anniversary of its breakthrough album, “Vivid” — which the group will play at Irving Plaza on April 6 — Mr. Reid, 54, still enjoys the neighborhood’s mix of Fort Greene-style diversity with a maritime vibe. A composer as well as a musician, he lives with his wife, Gabri Christa Reid, 49, a choreographer and filmmaker, and their daughter, Idea Viola Reid, 9. They have three cats. ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/31/nyregion/31ROUTINE1_SPAN/31ROUTINE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/31/nyregion/31ROUTINE1_SPAN/31ROUTINE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/31/nyregion/31ROUTINE1_SPAN/31ROUTINE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/31/nyregion/31ROUTINE1_SPAN/31ROUTINE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/31/nyregion/31ROUTINE1_SPAN