, and cyberattacks target companies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEWS Sven Olaf Kamphuis calls himself the “minister of telecommunications and foreign affairs for the Republic of CyberBunker.” Others see him as the Prince of Spam. Mr. Kamphuis, who is actually Dutch, is at the heart of an international investigation into one of the biggest cyberattacks identified by the authorities. Because of his outspoken position in a loose federation of hackers, the authorities in the Netherlands and several other countries are examining what role he or the Internet companies he runs played in snarling traffic on the Web this week. Eric Pfanner and Kevin J. O’Brien report.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/30/business/Irelandhome2/Irelandhome2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 373, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/30/business/Irelandhome2/Irelandhome2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 373}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/30/business/Irelandhome2/Irelandhome2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 636, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/30/business/Irelandhome2/Irelandhome2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1272, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/30/business/Irelandhome2/Irelandhome2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/30/business/Irelandhome2/Irelandhome2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/30/business/Irelandhome2/Irelandhome2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'IHT Quick Read: March 30', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-30T04:36:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By The International Herald Tribune', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The International Herald Tribune'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d480ad5e-f0fc-59f3-88aa-51a0ce456de9', 'word_count': 511, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d480ad5e-f0fc-59f3-88aa-51a0ce456de9'}, {'abstract': 'The Yankees and the Mets both have their problems and that is something that is reflected in the market for ticket.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/30/sports/baseball/status-of-yankees-and-mets-may-affect-ticket-sales-of-openers.html', 'snippet': 'The Yankees and the Mets both have their problems and that is something that is reflected in the market for ticket.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The local forecast on Monday calls for a high near 60 degrees with a mix of sun and clouds. Not bad for fans heading to Yankee Stadium and Citi Field as the Yankees and the Mets open their seasons simultaneously in New York for the first time. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Injuries May Affect Ticket Sales of Openers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Injuries May Affect Ticket Sales Of Openers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ticket Scalping', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-30T04:36:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/20f5e044-d3bb-5f26-b20e-19e361722b40', 'word_count': 633, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20f5e044-d3bb-5f26-b20e-19e361722b40'}, {'abstract': 'The second-seeded Blue Devils used stout defense, Seth Curry’s 3-point touch and a second-half run to top No. 3 Michigan State.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/30/sports/ncaabasketball/with-second-half-run-duke-pushes-out-michigan-state.html', 'snippet': 'The second-seeded Blue Devils used stout defense, Seth Curry’s 3-point touch and a second-half run to top No. 3 Michigan State.', 'lead_paragraph': 'INDIANAPOLIS — Steven Izzo called it right. Two weeks ago, Steven, the 13-year-old son of Michigan State Coach Tom Izzo, sidestepped family loyalty and picked Duke to defeat the Spartans in his N.C.A.A. tournament bracket. The Blue Devils validated his nerve Friday night by sending the Izzos home.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/30/sports/jpDUKE/jpDUKE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 487, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/30/sports/jpDUKE/jpDUKE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 487}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/30/sports/jpDUKE/jpDUKE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 831, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/30/sports/jpDUKE/jpDUKE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1662, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/30/sports/jpDUKE/jpDUKE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/30/sports/jpDUKE/jpDUKE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/30/sports/jpDUKE/jpDUKE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Duke Pushes Out Michigan State', 'kicker': 'Midwest: Duke 71, Michigan State 61', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With Second-Half Run, Duke Moves to Round of 8', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'NCAA Basketball Championships (Men)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball (College)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Duke University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Michigan State University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Curry, Seth (1990- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-30T04:47:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pat Borzi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pat', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borzi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dcfb4f7f-e3b5-582e-9267-599742c3473f', 'word_count': 798, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dcfb4f7f-e3b5-582e-9267-599742c3473f'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/30/arts/television/whats-on-saturday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '8 P.M. (HBO) SNOW WHITE AND THE HUNTSMAN (2012) Kristen Stewart, above, is Snow White, who seeks to usurp the evil queen Ravenna (Charlize Theron) with the help of the Huntsman (Chris Hemsworth) and a specific number of dwarfs (played by Ian McShane, Ray Winstone and Bob Hoskins, among others) in this darkened adaptation of the Brothers Grimm fairy tale, directed by Rupert Sanders. Writing in The New York Times, A. O. Scott said: “There is nothing cute about this movie. And that feels right. There is something exciting about how seriously ‘Snow White and the Huntsman’ takes its themes.” He added that Ms. Stewart’s Snow White was “part of an interesting new breed of warrior princesses — Katniss Everdeen is their current leader — whose ascendance reflects the convergence of commercial calculations and cultural longings. Long may they reign.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Saturday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s on Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-30T05:00:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a5bdf8e-7b8c-5d18-b7a0-67c29d223195', 'word_count': 757, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a5bdf8e-7b8c-5d18-b7a0-67c29d223195'}, {'abstract': 'The Nuggets scored the game’s first 21 fast-break points en route to their 18th straight victory at the Pepsi Center, where Denver is 33-3, the best home record in the league.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/30/sports/basketball/nets-fade-and-fall-in-denver.html', 'snippet': 'The Nuggets scored the game’s first 21 fast-break points en route to their 18th straight victory at the Pepsi Center, where Denver is 33-3, the best home record in the league.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DENVER — The Nets’ bid to ensure a winning road record for the first time since entering the N.B.A. in 1976 came up well short against the Denver Nuggets’ home dominance on Friday night. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/30/sports/basketball/30nets1-img/30nets1-img-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 520, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/30/sports/basketball/30nets1-img/30nets1-img-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 520}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/30/sports/basketball/30nets1-img/30nets1-img-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 887, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/30/sports/basketball/30nets1-img/30nets1-img-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1774, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/30/sports/basketball/30nets1-img/30nets1-img-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/30/sports/