ust budgets, not online courses, are the best answer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/31/opinion/sunday/resurrecting-californias-public-universities.html', 'snippet': 'More robust budgets, not online courses, are the best answer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even before the recession hit, the public colleges and universities that educate more than 70 percent of the nation’s students were suffering from dwindling state revenue. Their response, not surprisingly, was to raise tuition, slash course offerings and, in some cases, freeze or even reduce student enrollment. The damage was acute in California, whose once-glorious system of higher education effectively cannibalized itself, shutting out a growing number of well-qualified students. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Resurrecting California’s Public Universities', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Resurrecting California’s Public Universities', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Learning', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Public Policy Institute of California', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of California', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'California State University', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-30T16:26:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board