27-game win streak. They dominated the Hornets, with James’s grabbing 36 points.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW ORLEANS — If LeBron James seemed bothered by the lapse of Miami’s 27-game winning streak or the hard fouls — physical and verbal — he had absorbed in recent days, it was not apparent Friday morning. His hunger for victory or reprisal seemed outweighed at the moment by his hunger for lunch.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/31/sports/dog-dress-HEAT/dog-dress-HEAT-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 384, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/31/sports/dog-dress-HEAT/dog-dress-HEAT-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 384}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/31/sports/dog-dress-HEAT/dog-dress-HEAT-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 656, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/31/sports/dog-dress-HEAT/dog-dress-HEAT-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1312, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/31/sports/dog-dress-HEAT/dog-dress-HEAT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/31/sports/dog-dress-HEAT/dog-dress-HEAT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/31/sports/dog-dress-HEAT/dog-dress-HEAT-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Heat’s Streak May Be Over, but Show Rolls On', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Streak May Be Over, But Drama Continues', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Heat', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, LeBron', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Bulls', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Orleans Hornets', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-30T16:27:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeré Longman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeré', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Longman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d57aed1-eaf6-548e-9b25-1c231becc091', 'word_count': 1172, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d57aed1-eaf6-548e-9b25-1c231becc091'}, {'abstract': 'We like to believe that our principles are rooted in conviction. But much research shows that they often prove to be finicky, inconsistent intuitions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/31/opinion/sunday/how-firm-are-our-principles.html', 'snippet': 'We like to believe that our principles are rooted in conviction. But much research shows that they often prove to be finicky, inconsistent intuitions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MORAL quandaries often pit concerns about principles against concerns about practical consequences. Should we ban assault rifles and large sodas, restricting people’s liberties for the sake of physical health and safety? Should we allow drone killings or torture, if violating one person’s rights could save a thousand lives?', 'print_section