es” — the education world and the business world, the people who teach our kids and the people who give them jobs. Wagner’s argument in his book “Creating Innovators: The Making of Young People Who Will Change the World” is that our K-12 and college tracks are not consistently “adding the value and teaching the skills that matter most in the marketplace.” ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thu