://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/30/king-cottons-long-shadow/', 'snippet': 'Slavery was crucial to the development of global capitalism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last month, researchers at University College London made public a database that describes in illuminating detail one of the largest government bailouts in modern history. In 1833, Britain paid 20 million pounds to compensate 3,000 Caribbean slaveholders for the emancipation of their slaves. The payments constituted about 40 percent of total governmental expenditures that year. Conversation about the database in Britain centered on the recipients of these reparations for slaveholders, among them the ancestors of George Orwell, Graham Greene and David Cameron.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'King Cotton’s Long Shadow', 'kicker': 'The Great Divide', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'King Cotton’s Long Shadow', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Slavery', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Southern States (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-30T17:42:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Walter Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Walter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9fb98cdc-7cfe-5c48-8611-7ad9b57c62c0', 'word_count': 1073, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9fb98cdc-7cfe-5c48-8611-7ad9b57c62c0'}, {'abstract': 'The Mariners’ $10 million scoreboard and the Astros’ new look are among the new things to watch for this season.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/31/sports/baseball/whats-new-beyond-box-score-including-william-howard-taft.html', 'snippet': 'The Mariners’ $10 million scoreboard and the Astros’ new look are among the new things to watch for this season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We know this baseball season will have breakout stars we never expected, injuries we never saw coming and — based on last year — about 100 no-hitters and perfect games. That all involves players. Here are nine new things to watch on the periphery of the game.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/31/sports/baseball/31funstuff2-img/31funstuff2-img-articleLarge.png', 'height': 1084, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/31/sports/baseball/31funstuff2-img/31funstuff2-img-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1084}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/31/sports/baseball/31funstuff2-img/31funstuff2-img-jumbo.png', 'height': 1024, 'width': 567, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/31/sports/baseball/31funstuff2-img/31funstuff2-img-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1518, 'width': 840, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/31/sports/baseball/31funstuff2-img/31funstuff2-img-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/31/sports/baseball/31funstuff2-img/31funstuff2-img-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/31/sports/baseball/31funstuff2-img/31funstuff2-img-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Introducing a Repurposed President and a Revamped Star', 'kicker': 'Beyond the Box Score', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Introducing a Repurposed President and a Revamped Star', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kepner, Tyler', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stadiums and Arenas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Dodgers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dodger Stadium', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Seattle Mariners', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Houston Astros', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-30T17:47:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7fe532f-a9e6-5f2f-8041-ef1eb4eb883f', 'word_count': 614, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7fe532f-a9e6-5f2f-8041-ef1eb4eb883f'}, {'abstract': 'The problem with attempts to “bury” technology is that they embody an amoral and unsustainable vision.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/31/opinion/sunday/morozov-machines-of-laughter-and-forgetting.html', 'snippet': 'The problem with attempts to “bury” technology is that they embody an amoral and unsustainable vision.', 'lead_paragraph': 'UNTIL very recently, technology had a clear, if boring, purpose: by taking care of the Little Things, it enabled us, its human masters, to focus on the Big Things. “Unless there are slaves to do the ugly, horrible, uninteresting work, culture and contemplation become almost impossible,” proclaimed that noted connoisseur of contemplation Oscar Wilde. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/09/opinion/morozov/morozov-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 833, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/09/opinion/morozov/morozov-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 833}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/09/opinion/morozov/morozov-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 739, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/09/opinion/morozov/morozov-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1477, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/09/opinion/morozov/morozov-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/09/opinion/morozov/morozov-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/09/opinion/morozov/morozov-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Machines of Laughter and Forgetting', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Guest Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Machines of Laughter and Forgetting', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morozov, Evgeny', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Home Appliances', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-30T17:56:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Evgeny Morozov', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Evgeny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Morozov', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/68284dfd-2795-537e-b085-ac40d8abc9ea', 'word_count': 832, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68284dfd-2795-537e-b085-ac40d8abc9ea'}, {'abstract': 'The location of an infamous massacre in 1890, and a violent standoff in 1973, has again become the subject of introspection and dispute.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/31/us/wounded-knee-site-for-sale-stirring-controversy.html', 'snippet': 'The location of an infamous massacre in 1890, and a violent standoff in 1973, has again become the subject of introspection and dispute.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WOUNDED KNEE, S.D. — Ever since American soldiers massacred men, women and children here more than a century ago in the last major bloodshed of the American Indian wars, this haun