teachings?', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/30/on-being-catholic/', 'snippet': 'Can reflective and honest intellectuals actually believe in the church’s teachings?', 'lead_paragraph': 'An old friend and mentor of mine, Ernan McMullin, was a philosopher of science widely respected in his discipline.\xa0 He was also a Catholic priest.\xa0 I don’t know how many times fellow philosophers at professional meetings drew me aside and asked, “Does Ernan really believe that stuff?”\xa0 (He did.) Amid all the serious and generally respectful coverage of the papal resignation and the election of a new pope, I often detect an undertone of this same puzzlement.\xa0 Can reflective and honest intellectuals actually believe that stuff?', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Being Catholic', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On Being Catholic', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Easter and Holy Week', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-30T19:07:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gary Gutting', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gutting', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71429f2d-0046-51ac-aff8-efabfcc06714', 'word_count': 1392, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71429f2d-0046-51ac-aff8-efabfcc06714'}, {'abstract': 'Why “that was an epic fail” sounds so good and also so annoying.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/30/those-irritating-verbs-as-nouns/', 'snippet': 'Why “that was an epic fail” sounds so good and also so annoying.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Do you have a solve for this problem?” “Let’s all focus on the build.” “That’s the take-away from today’s seminar.” Or, to quote a song that was recently a No. 1 hit in Britain, “Would you let me see beneath your beautiful?”', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Those Irritating Verbs-as-Nouns', 'kicker': 'Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Those Irritating Verbs-as-Nouns', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grammar', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reading and Writing Skills', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-30T19:09:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Henry Hitchings', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Henry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hitchings', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/68dbbd77-d8a5-564f-a38a-6b317667a0a8', 'word_count': 893, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68dbbd77-d8a5-564f-a38a-6b317667a0a8'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Ramone defined the role of record producer as being roughly equivalent to that of a movie director.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/03/31/arts/music/phil-ramone-record-producer-and-winner-of-14-grammys-dies-at-79.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Ramone defined the role of record producer as being roughly equivalent to that of a movie director.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Phil Ramone, a prolific record producer and engineer who worked with some of the biggest music stars of the last 50 years, including Ray Charles, Frank Sinatra, Paul Simon, Billy Joel and Barbra Streisand, died on Saturday in Manhattan. He was 79. (Though it was widely reported that he was 72, public records and his family confirm that he was born on Jan. 5, 1934.)