ns', 'value': 'Rutenberg, Jim', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-31T13:32:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By The International Herald Tribune', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The International Herald Tribune'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3f71954-ad40-566a-a037-4621dc87205a', 'word_count': 30, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3f71954-ad40-566a-a037-4621dc87205a'}, {'abstract': 'In search of the origins of obtuseness.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/31/the-ecb-and-the-austerity-trap/', 'snippet': 'In search of the origins of obtuseness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Simon Wren-Lewis tries to show some sympathy for the devil: he tries to get into the mindset of European officials who defend austerity. And he gets at an important point in the process, although he may let the austerians off too lightly.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The ECB and the Austerity Trap', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-03-31T13:56:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/73ff19f4-c440-5e04-a8f4-0a87a59e1bf1', 'word_count': 714, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73ff19f4-c440-5e04-a8f4-0a87a59e1bf1'}, {'abstract': 'As several of the senators taking part in a bipartisan effort to overhaul to the nation’s immigration laws appeared on the Sunday talk shows to sound an optimistic note, Senator Marco Rubio, a Republican member of the group, sounded a strongly worded note of caution.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/03/31/rubio-calls-reports-of-immigration-deal-premature/', 'snippet': 'As several of the senators taking part in a bipartisan effort to overhaul to the nation’s immigration laws appeared on the Sunday talk shows to sound an optimistic note, Senator Marco Rubio, a Republican member of the group, sounded a strongly wor...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Read an updated version of this post.12:45 p.m. | Updated As several of the senators taking part in a bipartisan effort to overhaul to the nation’s immigration laws appeared on the Sunday talk shows to sound an optimistic note, Senator Marco Rubio, Republican of Florida and a member of the group, offered a strongly worded note of caution. In a statement released by his office\xa0 on Sunday, the headline — in all capital letters — read: “No Final Agreement on Immigration Legislation Yet.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Word of Caution From Rubio on Immigration', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rubio, Marco', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate Committee on the Judiciary', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-31T14:03:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d8e9c5f-2520-533c-9511-61ae67463533', 'word_count': 802, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d8e9c5f-2520-533c-9511-61ae67463533'}, {'abstract': 'Chart shows the total credit market of the United States as a percent of G.D.P.', 'web_url': 'https://