r, which is expected to supply 50 to 80 percent of Israel’s natural gas needs over the next 10 years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — Israel moved closer to its goal of energy independence on Sunday as natural gas from a large offshore field began flowing into the country, a harbinger of important change that will benefit the country strategically and economically, officials said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Israel Taps an Offshore Natural Gas Field', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Israel Taps an Offshore Natural Gas Field', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Natural Gas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Netanyahu, Benjamin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Offshore Drilling and Exploration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Peres, Shimon', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mediterranean Sea', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-31T18:19:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Isabel Kershner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kershner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/85fa3427-9eeb-5bb3-bc20-51310dec3d26', 'word_count': 558, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85fa3427-9eeb-5bb3-bc20-51310dec3d26'}, {'abstract': 'American TV has a long tradition of imitating foreign shows, and the fall season may include several new forms of flattery, with “Friends and Family,” “Pulling,” “Rake,” “Second Sight” and “Spy.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/01/arts/television/new-american-versions-of-foreign-tv-shows-are-in-the-works.html', 'snippet': 'American TV has a long tradition of imitating foreign shows, and the fall season may include several new forms of flattery, with “Friends and Family,” “Pulling,” “Rake,” “Second Sight” and “Spy.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ideas may not fall out of trees, but they do come in the mail from Sydney and Tel Aviv. Of the 100 or so pilot episodes being shot as candidates for the broadcast television networks’ fall lineups, at least a dozen are based on shows from Argentina, Australia, Britain or Israel.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/01/arts/foreign-1/foreign-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 244, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/01/arts/foreign-1/foreign-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 244}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/01/arts/foreign-1/foreign-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 416, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/01/arts/foreign-1/foreign-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 759, 'width': 1870, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/01/arts/foreign-1/foreign-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/01/arts/foreign-1/foreign-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'c