d-39c5-548e-a9fd-feafaa7e2ebd'}, {'abstract': 'The Australian singer Nick Cave, backed by an ensemble including Sharon Van Etten at the Beacon Theater, offered a set spanning his 30-year career.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/01/arts/music/nick-cave-and-the-bad-seeds-at-the-beacon-theater.html', 'snippet': 'The Australian singer Nick Cave, backed by an ensemble including Sharon Van Etten at the Beacon Theater, offered a set spanning his 30-year career.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Visions of murder, catastrophe, transfiguration and desperate love issued from the Beacon Theater stage on Friday night, set to dirges, stomps and inexorable crescendos. Nick Cave and the Bad Seeds — along with a string ensemble, the backup singers Sharon Van Etten (who opened the concert) and Shilpa Ray, and a youth choir, the Harlem Voices — were midway through a sold-out three-night stand. Songs from their new album, “Push the Sky Away” (Bad Seed Ltd.), started and ended the set. In between they revisited material recorded over the last three decades. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/01/arts/cave/cave-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/01/arts/cave/cave-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/01/arts/cave/cave-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 511, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/01/arts/cave/cave-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1023, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None