a-a-bollywood-disco-remake.html', 'snippet': '“Himmatwala” is a remake of a Bollywood disco film from 30 years ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In its first scene, set at the Funkytown Disco in Bombay — year: 1983 — “Himmatwala” loads on the period markers, with quick nods to Michael Jackson, Madonna and, of course, the reign of disco in a song-and-dance number (called “Thank God It’s Friday,” no less) full of flashing lights and silver-clad hoofers. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/01/arts/himma/himma-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 387, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/01/arts/himma/himma-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 387}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/01/arts/himma/himma-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 661, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/01/arts/himma/himma-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1321, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/01/arts/himma/himma-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/01/arts/himma/himma-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/01/arts/himma/himma-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Disco and Villains in 1983 Bollywood', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Disco and Villains in 1983 Bollywood', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-03-31T21:18:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Saltz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saltz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/1def9148-2520-580f-b16e-6bd9b802e7ac', 'word_count': 270, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1def9148-2520-580f-b16e-6bd9b802e7ac'}, {'abstract': 'The Moving Sidewalks reunited for their first gig in nearly 44 years on Saturday night at B. B. King Blues Club and Grill.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/01/arts/music/the-moving-sidewalks-at-b-b-king-blues-club-and-grill.html', 'snippet': 'The Moving Sidewalks reunited for their first gig in nearly 44 years on Saturday night at B. B. King Blues Club and Grill.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Moving Sidewalks, in their first gig in nearly 44 years on Saturday night at B. B. King Blues Club and Grill, played some pretty nice gear for a band that never had a national hit. Tube amplifiers by Magnatone, the recently revived pre-’70s American brand, handsome in design, broad and deep in sound; custom-made Telecaster-like guitars with psychedelic blob patterns swirling on a small screen underneath the strings, as if iPads had been built into the instruments’ bodies.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/01/arts/sub-moving/sub-moving-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 409, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': '